const STW_ID_CONTENT={"Chat with people in Taiwan and words like 'yī jiān èr gù,' 'guīmáo,' or 'túchuí' suddenly pop up—not in your dictionary, yet everyone uses them naturally. These are proverbs and slang born from Taiwanese life, and learning them instantly makes your speech sound more 'local.' Let's look at some common ones, with their meanings and when to use them.":"Mengobrol dengan orang Taiwan, kata-kata seperti 'yī jiān èr gù', 'guīmáo', atau 'túchuí' tiba-tiba muncul—tak ada di kamusmu, namun semua orang memakainya dengan wajar. Ini adalah peribahasa dan bahasa gaul yang lahir dari kehidupan Taiwan, dan mempelajarinya seketika membuat tutur katamu terdengar lebih 'lokal'. Mari kita lihat beberapa yang umum, beserta arti dan kapan menggunakannya.","Taiwanese proverbs and slang are packed with everyday wisdom. Expressions like '一兼二顧' and '凸槌' rarely appear in textbook examples, yet you'll hear them constantly in daily conversation. That's exactly why using them naturally gives a strong 'I actually live in Taiwan' vibe. But note that '龜毛' and '鴨霸' judge someone's character, so saying them to a person's face can sting—it's safest to use them jokingly among close friends.":"Peribahasa dan bahasa gaul Taiwan penuh dengan kearifan hidup sehari-hari. Ungkapan seperti '一兼二顧' dan '凸槌' jarang muncul dalam contoh buku pelajaran, tetapi kamu akan terus mendengarnya dalam percakapan sehari-hari. Justru itulah memakainya dengan wajar memberi kesan kuat 'saya benar-benar tinggal di Taiwan'. Tetapi perhatikan bahwa '龜毛' dan '鴨霸' menilai karakter seseorang, jadi mengatakannya langsung di depan orang bisa menyakiti—paling aman memakainya untuk bercanda di antara teman dekat.","Let's start with one everyone hears: '一兼二顧' (yī jiān èr gù). It means 'doing one thing while also taking care of another'—in other words, 'killing two birds with one stone.' Taiwanese love it for describing a smart, economical arrangement. For example: 'I caught a concert while I was in Japan for a business trip—truly two birds with one stone.' Or a mom exercising while binge-watching a drama might say smugly, 'See, two things at once, how great.' It carries a thrifty, time-savvy philosophy of life.":"Mari mulai dengan satu yang sering didengar semua orang: '一兼二顧' (yī jiān èr gù). Artinya 'mengerjakan satu hal sekaligus mengurus hal lain'—dengan kata lain, 'sekali dayung dua tiga pulau terlampaui'. Orang Taiwan gemar memakainya untuk menggambarkan pengaturan yang cerdas dan hemat. Misalnya: 'Saya sekalian nonton konser waktu dinas ke Jepang—benar-benar sekali dayung dua pulau'. Atau seorang ibu yang berolahraga sambil maraton drama mungkin berkata bangga, 'Tuh, dua hal sekaligus, hebat kan.' Ia mengandung filosofi hidup yang hemat dan pandai memanfaatkan waktu.","Taiwanese internet slang largely forms in three patterns: (1) number puns like '484 = 是不是'; (2) homophone swaps like '森77 = 生氣氣'; and (3) phonetic loans like '迷因 = meme.' These emerge from PTT (Taiwan's huge bulletin board), Dcard, and various social media, spreading in a flash. Since slang changes fast, there's no need to memorize it all. Ask a Taiwanese friend 'What does this mean?' and they'll usually be delighted to explain—which itself makes a great conversation starter.":"Bahasa gaul internet Taiwan sebagian besar terbentuk dalam tiga pola: (1) pelesetan angka seperti '484 = 是不是'; (2) penggantian homofon seperti '森77 = 生氣氣'; dan (3) pinjaman bunyi seperti '迷因 = meme'. Semua ini muncul dari PTT (papan buletin raksasa Taiwan), Dcard, dan berbagai media sosial, lalu menyebar dalam sekejap. Karena bahasa gaul berubah cepat, tak perlu menghafal semuanya. Tanyakan pada teman Taiwan 'Ini artinya apa?' dan biasanya mereka dengan senang hati menjelaskan—yang justru menjadi pembuka obrolan yang bagus.","Finally, we can't skip '迷因' (míyīn), the phonetic rendering of English 'meme'—the funny images, videos, and jokes that go viral online. A photo with a hilarious caption, a wildly remixed short clip—any of it can be a meme. Taiwan's meme culture is highly developed, often blending current events and homophones, with humor that's fast and local. Getting the memes is almost like receiving the younger generation's passport. These slang words change fast—new ones pop up, old ones fade—but it's exactly this rapid renewal that keeps language forever fresh and fun.":"Terakhir, kita tak boleh melewatkan '迷因' (míyīn), transliterasi bunyi dari kata Inggris 'meme'—gambar, video, dan lelucon lucu yang viral di internet. Sebuah foto dengan takarir kocak, klip pendek yang di-remix habis-habisan—semuanya bisa jadi meme. Budaya meme Taiwan sangat berkembang, sering memadukan peristiwa terkini dan homofon, dengan humor yang cepat dan lokal. Memahami meme hampir seperti menerima paspor generasi muda. Kata-kata gaul ini berubah cepat—yang baru bermunculan, yang lama memudar—tetapi justru pembaruan yang kilat inilah yang membuat bahasa selamanya segar dan menyenangkan.","The language understood most widely in Taiwan is Huayu (Guoyu, Mandarin)—at school, at government offices, on the news, at work, it's all you need to get by. Taiwanese Mandarin has also absorbed words from Japanese brought in during the colonial era (such as 'biàndāng,' from bentō) and, more recently, English mixed into everyday speech (like 'zhège case'), so tracing its words reveals Taiwan's history. Taiwan's language keeps blending and changing at this very moment.":"Bahasa yang paling luas dipahami di Taiwan adalah Huayu (Guoyu, bahasa Mandarin)—di sekolah, kantor pemerintah, berita, maupun tempat kerja, cukup bahasa ini untuk hidup sehari-hari. Mandarin Taiwan juga menyerap kata-kata dari bahasa Jepang yang masuk pada era kolonial (seperti 'biàndāng', dari bentō) dan, belakangan ini, bahasa Inggris yang diselipkan dalam percakapan sehari-hari (seperti 'zhège case'), sehingga menelusuri kata-katanya akan memperlihatkan sejarah Taiwan. Bahasa di Taiwan terus berbaur dan berubah tepat pada saat ini.","The most charming thing about how Taiwanese people speak is the ability to \"switch.\" One and the same person might speak Taiwanese to elders, Guoyu to colleagues, and toss in a few English words with children—mixing three languages in a single sentence is nothing unusual. For example: \"I'll tell you about this case in the afternoon, OK?\" This natural mixing is called \"code-switching\" in linguistics. It's not a sign of poor command, but the Taiwanese knack for flexibly choosing the most fitting language for the person and the situation.":"Hal paling memikat dari cara orang Taiwan berbicara adalah kemampuan untuk \"beralih\". Satu orang yang sama bisa berbahasa Taiwan kepada orang tua, Guoyu kepada rekan kerja, dan menyelipkan beberapa kata bahasa Inggris dengan anak-anak—mencampur tiga bahasa dalam satu kalimat bukanlah hal aneh. Misalnya: \"Soal case ini nanti sore aku ceritakan, OK?\" Pencampuran alami ini dalam linguistik disebut \"alih kode\" (code-switching). Ini bukan tanda penguasaan yang buruk, melainkan kepiawaian orang Taiwan dalam secara luwes memilih bahasa yang paling pas untuk orang dan situasinya.","For foreigners hoping to fit into Taiwan, there's no need to rush to learn every language from the start. Master Guoyu first, and you can communicate anywhere on the island; stay a while longer and you'll naturally begin to understand the market auntie's accent and all kinds of local expressions. When Taiwanese people see a foreigner making the effort to fit into local life, they're usually both surprised and delighted. Here language is not just a tool for communication but a bond of identity, memory, and emotion—the more voices you listen to, the better you'll understand this island.":"Bagi orang asing yang berharap membaur di Taiwan, tak perlu terburu-buru mempelajari setiap bahasa sejak awal. Kuasai Guoyu lebih dulu, dan kamu bisa berkomunikasi di mana pun di pulau ini; tinggal lebih lama sedikit dan kamu akan secara alami mulai memahami logat si ibu penjual di pasar dan berbagai ungkapan setempat. Ketika orang Taiwan melihat orang asing berusaha membaur dengan kehidupan setempat, mereka biasanya sekaligus terkejut dan senang. Di sini bahasa bukan sekadar alat komunikasi melainkan ikatan identitas, kenangan, dan emosi—semakin banyak suara yang kamu dengarkan, semakin baik kamu memahami pulau ini.","At rechao joints, the rallying cry 'gan la' inevitably appears once people are tipsy—it's the standard signal for 'drink it dry!' Taiwan also punishes drunk driving (jiujia) very harshly, so after drinking, the norm is to call a 'designated driver' (daijia) or head home by taxi or MRT. That's exactly why everyone can enjoy barhopping worry-free. For non-drinkers, there's also the kind custom of 'joining with tea' instead of alcohol.":"Di kedai rechao, seruan 'gan la' pasti muncul begitu orang-orang mulai mabuk ringan—itulah aba-aba standar untuk 'minum sampai habis!' Taiwan juga menghukum mengemudi dalam keadaan mabuk (jiujia) dengan sangat berat, jadi setelah minum, kebiasaannya adalah memanggil 'sopir pengganti' (daijia) atau pulang naik taksi atau MRT. Justru karena itulah semua orang bisa menikmati barhopping tanpa khawatir. Bagi yang tidak minum alkohol, ada juga kebiasaan baik 'ikut dengan teh' sebagai ganti minuman keras.","The soul of rechao, besides the food, is 'Taiwan Beer.' It's the island's most classic brand, chilled ice-cold, and paired with stir-fried clams, popcorn chicken, three-cup chicken, and fried rice for the most authentic combo. Everyone chats while they 'ganbei' (bottoms up), clinking glasses and shouting 'Gan la!'—meaning 'drink it all.' This unfussy atmosphere of big bites and big gulps is exactly how Taiwanese relax and bond.":"Jiwa dari rechao, selain makanannya, adalah 'Taiwan Beer'. Ini merek paling klasik di pulau tersebut, didinginkan hingga sedingin es, dan dipadukan dengan kerang tumis, ayam popcorn, ayam tiga cawan, dan nasi goreng untuk kombinasi paling autentik. Semua orang mengobrol sambil 'ganbei' (habiskan sampai tandas), mengadu gelas dan berteriak 'Gan la!'—artinya 'minum sampai habis'. Suasana santai makan banyak dan minum banyak inilah cara orang Taiwan bersantai dan mempererat hubungan.","Walk through Taiwan and you'll find small shops and workshops packed along every street—the morning-market lunchbox stand, the back-alley machine shop, the night-market stall—most of them small businesses run by families. In Taiwan, a boss is often called 'tóujiā,' and the wish to 'one day have a shop of my own' runs deep in many Taiwanese hearts. Let's look at the entrepreneurial DNA that supports Taiwan's economy from the ground up.":"Berjalanlah menyusuri Taiwan dan kamu akan menemukan toko kecil dan bengkel berjejal di setiap jalan—lapak nasi kotak di pasar pagi, bengkel mesin di gang belakang, gerai di pasar malam—sebagian besar adalah usaha kecil yang dijalankan keluarga. Di Taiwan, bos sering disebut 'tóujiā', dan keinginan untuk 'suatu hari punya toko sendiri' tertanam dalam di hati banyak orang Taiwan. Mari kita lihat DNA kewirausahaan yang menopang ekonomi Taiwan dari akar rumput.","'Tóujiā' (boss, shop owner) shows up often in everyday talk. Haggling at a market or stall, a customer calling out 'Tóujiā, make it a bit cheaper!' is a classic exchange. Many Taiwanese SMEs are family-run; during the boom of the 1960s–80s, people spoke of 'the living room as the factory,' when whole families stayed up through the night making goods for export. This grassroots entrepreneurial power is the force that pushed Taiwan into being a land of 'MIT' (Made in Taiwan).":"'Tóujiā' (bos, pemilik toko) sering muncul dalam percakapan sehari-hari. Saat menawar di pasar atau lapak, pelanggan yang berseru 'Tóujiā, kurangi sedikit dong!' adalah dialog klasik. Banyak UKM Taiwan dikelola keluarga; pada masa keemasan 1960-an–80-an, orang bicara tentang 'ruang tamu sebagai pabrik', ketika seisi keluarga begadang semalaman membuat barang untuk ekspor. Kekuatan kewirausahaan akar rumput inilah yang mendorong Taiwan menjadi negeri 'MIT' (Made in Taiwan).","boss, business owner":"bos, pemilik usaha","to make it; rise to success":"berhasil; meraih sukses","Taiwan has a vivid saying: 'grease-stained hands become the boss' (hēishǒu biàn tóujiā). 'Heishou'—literally 'black hands'—refers to skilled workers who repair cars or do machine work, their hands coated in grease in the factory; 'tóujiā' means 'boss.' The saying tells the story of an apprentice who starts at the bottom and, relying on solid skills and years of hard graft, finally opens a shop and becomes the boss. Such legends of turning one's life around by hand abound among Taiwan's older generation.":"Taiwan punya pepatah yang gamblang: 'tangan berlumur oli menjadi bos' (hēishǒu biàn tóujiā). 'Heishou'—harfiahnya 'tangan hitam'—merujuk pada pekerja terampil yang memperbaiki mobil atau menggarap mesin, tangannya berlumur oli di pabrik; 'tóujiā' berarti 'bos'. Pepatah ini mengisahkan seorang murid magang yang memulai dari bawah dan, dengan mengandalkan keterampilan yang mumpuni serta bertahun-tahun kerja keras, akhirnya membuka toko dan menjadi bos. Legenda mengubah nasib dengan tangan sendiri seperti ini bertaburan di kalangan generasi tua Taiwan.","For many Taiwanese, 'being the boss' is not just about making money—it's a life goal and a bone-deep value. They'd rather be their own tóujiā and toil a bit harder than spend a lifetime working for someone else; this mindset makes Taiwanese especially willing to take the risk of starting a business. Even just taking over a tiny drink shop or a food truck, or renting a stall at the night market, many people want to taste what it's like to 'run your own business.' This unyielding spirit of wanting to make it big is precisely the 'boss spirit' (tóujiā jingshen).":"Bagi banyak orang Taiwan, 'menjadi bos' bukan sekadar soal menghasilkan uang—melainkan tujuan hidup dan nilai yang mendarah daging. Mereka lebih memilih menjadi tóujiā sendiri dan bekerja sedikit lebih keras daripada seumur hidup bekerja untuk orang lain; pola pikir ini membuat orang Taiwan sangat berani mengambil risiko memulai usaha. Bahkan hanya dengan mengambil alih kedai minuman kecil atau gerobak makanan, atau menyewa lapak di pasar malam, banyak orang ingin merasakan bagaimana rasanya 'menjalankan usaha sendiri'. Semangat pantang menyerah yang ingin sukses besar inilah yang disebut 'semangat bos' (tóujiā jīngshén).","aunt (maternal); auntie":"bibi (dari pihak ibu); tante","This is my aunt.":"Ini bibi saya.","uncle (father's younger brother)":"paman (adik laki-laki ayah)","My uncle is coming to my place tomorrow.":"Besok paman saya akan datang ke tempat saya.","grandfather (maternal)":"kakek (dari pihak ibu)","My grandfather lives in Tainan.":"Kakek saya tinggal di Tainan.","grandmother (maternal)":"nenek (dari pihak ibu)","My grandmother cooks very well.":"Nenek saya sangat pandai memasak.","boy; guy":"anak laki-laki; cowok","That guy is my classmate.":"Cowok itu teman sekelas saya.","girl":"anak perempuan; cewek","There are ten girls in our class.":"Ada sepuluh anak perempuan di kelas kami.","colleague; coworker":"rekan kerja; kolega","He is my colleague.":"Dia rekan kerja saya.","body; health":"badan; kesehatan","I'm not feeling well today.":"Hari ini saya kurang enak badan.","belly; stomach":"perut","I'm hungry.":"Saya lapar.","teeth":"gigi","Brush your teeth after eating.":"Sikat gigi setelah makan.","color":"warna","What color do you like?":"Kamu suka warna apa?","pink":"merah muda","Her phone is pink.":"Ponselnya berwarna merah muda.","gray":"abu-abu","I bought a gray piece of clothing.":"Saya membeli sepotong pakaian berwarna abu-abu.","orange (color)":"oranye (warna)","What is this orange fruit?":"Buah berwarna oranye ini buah apa?","to sleep":"tidur","I go to bed at eleven every night.":"Setiap malam saya tidur jam sebelas.","to get up":"bangun tidur","I get up at six thirty in the morning.":"Saya bangun jam setengah tujuh pagi.","to give":"memberi","This is for you.":"Ini untukmu.","to stand":"berdiri","Please don't stand in the doorway.":"Tolong jangan berdiri di depan pintu.","to wear (clothes, shoes)":"memakai (baju, sepatu)","It's cold today, dress warmly.":"Hari ini dingin, pakailah baju yang hangat.","to sing":"menyanyi","She loves singing.":"Dia suka menyanyi.","to rest":"beristirahat","Rest a bit when you're tired.":"Kalau lelah, istirahatlah sebentar.","to need":"membutuhkan; perlu","Do you need help?":"Apakah kamu perlu bantuan?","to go to work":"pergi bekerja","I have to work tomorrow.":"Besok saya harus bekerja.","to get off work":"pulang kerja","I get off work at six.":"Saya pulang kerja jam enam.","to think; to feel":"berpikir; merasa","I think it's very pretty here.":"Menurut saya di sini sangat indah.","to start; to begin":"mulai","What time does the movie start?":"Jam berapa filmnya mulai?","few; little":"sedikit","There are few customers today.":"Hari ini pelanggannya sedikit.","old (of things)":"lama; usang (untuk benda)","This phone is too old.":"Ponsel ini terlalu tua.","difficult; hard":"sulit; susah","This character is hard to write.":"Karakter ini sulit ditulis.","easy":"mudah; gampang","This question is easy.":"Soal ini mudah.","clean":"bersih","This restaurant is very clean.":"Restoran ini sangat bersih.","dirty":"kotor","Your shoes are so dirty.":"Sepatumu kotor sekali.","comfortable":"nyaman","This bed is very comfortable.":"Kasur ini sangat nyaman.","cute":"lucu; imut","Your cat is so cute!":"Kucingmu lucu sekali!","summer":"musim panas","Summer in Taiwan is hot and humid.":"Musim panas di Taiwan panas dan lembap.","winter":"musim dingin","Winters in Taipei are often rainy.":"Musim dingin di Taipei sering hujan.","hour":"jam (durasi)","I waited for an hour.":"Saya menunggu selama satu jam.","before; in the past":"dulu; di masa lalu","I used to live in Japan.":"Dulu saya pernah tinggal di Jepang.","after; later":"setelah itu; nanti","After eating I'll rest.":"Setelah makan saya akan beristirahat.","weather":"cuaca","How's the weather today?":"Bagaimana cuaca hari ini?","to rain":"hujan","It's raining, let's take a taxi.":"Sedang hujan, ayo naik taksi.","wind":"angin","It's very windy today.":"Hari ini anginnya kencang sekali.","cloud":"awan","There are no clouds today; the weather is nice.":"Hari ini tidak ada awan, cuacanya bagus.","typhoon":"topan; taifun","There's a typhoon tomorrow, so no work.":"Besok ada topan, jadi libur kerja.","meat":"daging","I don't eat meat.":"Saya tidak makan daging.","lunchbox; bento":"kotak makan; bento","I bought a lunchbox at noon.":"Siang tadi saya membeli kotak makan.","pineapple":"nanas","Taiwanese pineapples are very sweet.":"Nanas Taiwan sangat manis.","tomato":"tomat","I like eating tomatoes.":"Saya suka makan tomat.","ice cream":"es krim","I love ice cream most in summer.":"Di musim panas saya paling suka es krim.","dessert; sweets":"makanan penutup; makanan manis","I still want dessert after the meal.":"Setelah makan saya masih ingin makanan penutup.","Taiwanese salty crispy chicken":"ayam goreng renyah gurih khas Taiwan","I want salty crispy chicken tonight.":"Malam ini saya ingin makan ayam goreng renyah gurih.","room":"kamar","My room is small.":"Kamar saya kecil.","market":"pasar","Mom goes to the market to buy groceries in the morning.":"Pagi hari ibu pergi ke pasar untuk belanja.","kitchen":"dapur","Dad is cooking in the kitchen.":"Ayah sedang memasak di dapur.","office":"kantor","My office is on the third floor.":"Kantor saya di lantai tiga.","nearby; vicinity":"sekitar; dekat sini","Is there a convenience store nearby?":"Apakah ada minimarket di sekitar sini?","house":"rumah","This house is very beautiful.":"Rumah ini sangat indah.","(measure word for flat objects)":"(kata bantu bilangan untuk benda pipih)","I want to buy two HSR tickets.":"Saya ingin membeli dua tiket kereta cepat.","(measure word for clothes, matters)":"(kata bantu bilangan untuk pakaian, urusan)","How much is this piece of clothing?":"Berapa harga pakaian ini?","pair (of)":"pasang (sepasang)","I want to buy a pair of shoes.":"Saya ingin membeli sepasang sepatu.","bowl (of)":"mangkuk (semangkuk)","Boss, I'd like a bowl of noodles.":"Bos, saya mau semangkuk mi.","front; ahead":"depan; di depan","The station is right ahead.":"Stasiunnya tepat di depan.","back; behind":"belakang; di belakang","The restroom is behind the restaurant.":"Toilet ada di belakang restoran.","inside":"di dalam","It's dark inside the room.":"Di dalam kamar gelap.","outside":"di luar","It's raining outside.":"Di luar sedang hujan.","beside; next to":"di samping; di sebelah","The bank is next to the post office.":"Bank itu di sebelah kantor pos.","mobile phone":"ponsel; HP","My phone is out of battery.":"Ponsel saya kehabisan baterai.","computer":"komputer","I work on a computer.":"Saya bekerja dengan komputer.","television; TV":"televisi; TV","I like watching TV in the evening.":"Saya suka menonton TV di malam hari.","clothes":"pakaian; baju","These clothes are very pretty.":"Baju ini sangat cantik.","shoes":"sepatu","Take off your shoes before entering.":"Lepaskan sepatu sebelum masuk.","wife; Mrs.":"istri; Nyonya","Mr. Chen's wife is a teacher.":"Istri Tuan Chen adalah seorang guru.","child":"anak (kecil)","There are many children in the park.":"Ada banyak anak-anak di taman.","driver":"sopir; pengemudi","The taxi driver is very kind.":"Sopir taksi itu sangat baik.","finger":"jari","My finger hurts a little.":"Jari saya agak sakit.","leg":"kaki (tungkai)","After walking all day, my legs are sore.":"Setelah berjalan seharian, kaki saya pegal.","back (body)":"punggung","His back hurts a lot.":"Punggungnya sangat sakit.","skin":"kulit","In summer, skin gets tanned easily.":"Di musim panas kulit mudah menjadi gelap terbakar matahari.","brown":"cokelat","I bought a pair of brown shoes.":"Saya membeli sepasang sepatu berwarna cokelat.","purple":"ungu","She likes purple clothes.":"Dia suka baju berwarna ungu.","zero":"nol","There are two zeros in my phone number.":"Ada dua angka nol di nomor telepon saya.","half":"setengah","It is half past three now.":"Sekarang jam setengah empat.","(measure word for round things)":"(kata bantu bilangan untuk benda bulat)","I want to buy three apples.":"Saya ingin membeli tiga buah apel.","kind; type":"jenis; macam","This shop has many kinds of drinks.":"Toko ini punya banyak jenis minuman.","(measure word for dishes/plates)":"(kata bantu bilangan untuk hidangan/piring)","I ordered a plate of fried rice.":"Saya memesan sepiring nasi goreng.","to return":"kembali; pulang","I will go home after work.":"Setelah kerja saya akan pulang ke rumah.","to introduce":"memperkenalkan","Let me introduce you; this is my colleague.":"Mari saya perkenalkan, ini rekan kerja saya.","to stroll; to browse (shops)":"jalan-jalan; keliling (toko)","On weekends I like to stroll around the night market.":"Di akhir pekan saya suka jalan-jalan di pasar malam.","fried rice":"nasi goreng","The egg fried rice here is delicious.":"Nasi goreng telur di sini enak.","plain white rice":"nasi putih","I would like a bowl of white rice.":"Saya mau semangkuk nasi putih.","sandwich":"roti lapis; sandwich","The sandwiches at the breakfast shop are cheap.":"Sandwich di kedai sarapan murah.","hamburger":"hamburger; burger","My younger brother likes hamburgers the most.":"Adik laki-laki saya paling suka burger.","candy":"permen","Children love eating candy.":"Anak-anak suka makan permen.","shrimp":"udang","This dish has a lot of shrimp.":"Hidangan ini banyak udangnya.","spicy; hot":"pedas","Is this salt-and-pepper chicken too spicy?":"Apakah ayam goreng gurih ini terlalu pedas?","recently; lately":"akhir-akhir ini; belakangan ini","How have you been lately?":"Bagaimana kabarmu belakangan ini?","midnight; late at night":"tengah malam; larut malam","He often works until midnight.":"Dia sering bekerja sampai tengah malam.","usually; normally":"biasanya","I usually eat sandwiches from the breakfast shop.":"Saya biasanya makan sandwich dari kedai sarapan.","good morning":"selamat pagi","Good morning, the weather is really nice today.":"Selamat pagi, hari ini cuacanya bagus sekali.","good night":"selamat malam (mau tidur)","I'm going to sleep now, good night.":"Saya mau tidur sekarang, selamat malam.","to welcome":"menyambut","Welcome! (to a shop)":"Selamat datang!","please; to invite":"silakan; mengundang","Please sit down and have some tea.":"Silakan duduk dan minum teh.","congratulations":"selamat (ucapan)","Congratulations on finding a new job!":"Selamat atas pekerjaan barumu!","no problem":"tidak masalah","Leave this to me, no problem.":"Serahkan ini pada saya, tidak masalah.","correct; right; yes":"benar; betul; ya","You're right; taking the MRT is faster.":"Kamu benar, naik MRT lebih cepat.","come on; keep it up; cheer on":"ayo; semangat","You have an exam tomorrow, good luck!":"Besok kamu ujian, semangat ya!","wrong; mistaken":"salah; keliru","Sorry, I took the wrong way.":"Maaf, saya salah jalan.","the same":"sama","These two shirts are the same color.":"Kedua baju ini warnanya sama.","famous":"terkenal","This night market is very famous.":"Pasar malam ini sangat terkenal.","really; truly":"sungguh; benar-benar","This bowl of beef noodles is really delicious.":"Semangkuk mi sapi ini benar-benar enak.","sofa; couch":"sofa","Dad is sitting on the sofa watching TV.":"Ayah sedang duduk di sofa menonton TV.","mirror":"cermin","She is putting on makeup in front of the mirror.":"Dia sedang berdandan di depan cermin.","wallet; purse":"dompet","My wallet is in my bag.":"Dompet saya ada di dalam tas.","plate; dish":"piring","Please get me a plate.":"Tolong ambilkan saya sebuah piring.","chopsticks":"sumpit","I'm not very good at using chopsticks.":"Saya kurang mahir memakai sumpit.","spoon":"sendok","Use a spoon to drink soup.":"Gunakan sendok untuk minum sup.","electric light; lamp":"lampu","Remember to turn off the light before going out.":"Ingat matikan lampu sebelum keluar.","movie theater; cinema":"bioskop","We go to the cinema to watch a movie.":"Kami pergi ke bioskop untuk menonton film.","pharmacy; drugstore":"apotek","The pharmacy is right next to the convenience store.":"Apotek itu tepat di sebelah minimarket.","breakfast shop":"kedai sarapan","I often buy egg pancakes at the breakfast shop.":"Saya sering membeli dadar telur di kedai sarapan.","parking lot":"tempat parkir","The parking lot is in the basement of the department store.":"Tempat parkir ada di basement pusat perbelanjaan.","hat; cap":"topi","The sun is strong, so wear a hat.":"Mataharinya terik, pakailah topi.","socks":"kaus kaki","I bought three pairs of socks.":"Saya membeli tiga pasang kaus kaki.","coat; jacket":"jaket; mantel","It's cold outside; put on a jacket.":"Di luar dingin, pakailah jaket.","I; me":"saya; aku","I am Japanese.":"Saya orang Jepang.","you":"kamu","Are you a student?":"Apakah kamu seorang pelajar?","you (polite)":"Anda (sopan)","Hello, may I ask your surname?":"Halo, boleh saya tahu marga Anda?","he; him":"dia (laki-laki)","He is my friend.":"Dia teman saya.","she; her":"dia (perempuan)","She is Taiwanese.":"Dia orang Taiwan.","we; us":"kami; kita","We go to the night market together.":"Kami pergi ke pasar malam bersama-sama.","everyone":"semua orang","Hello, everyone!":"Halo semuanya!","person; people":"orang","There are many people at the night market.":"Ada banyak orang di pasar malam.","friend":"teman","I go eat with my friend.":"Saya pergi makan bersama teman.","name":"nama","What is your name?":"Siapa namamu?","Mr.; husband":"Tuan; suami","Mr. Tanaka is Japanese.":"Tuan Tanaka orang Jepang.","Miss; Ms.":"Nona; Ibu (panggilan wanita)","Miss Lin works at a bank.":"Nona Lin bekerja di bank.","family (members)":"keluarga (anggota keluarga)","My family has four people.":"Keluarga saya berjumlah empat orang.","dad; father":"ayah; papa","My dad works every day.":"Ayah saya bekerja setiap hari.","mom; mother":"ibu; mama","The food my mom makes is delicious.":"Masakan ibu saya enak.","older brother":"kakak laki-laki","My older brother lives in Taipei.":"Kakak laki-laki saya tinggal di Taipei.","older sister":"kakak perempuan","My older sister loves coffee.":"Kakak perempuan saya suka kopi.","younger brother":"adik laki-laki","My younger brother is ten this year.":"Adik laki-laki saya tahun ini berumur sepuluh tahun.","younger sister":"adik perempuan","My younger sister is learning Japanese.":"Adik perempuan saya sedang belajar bahasa Jepang.","teacher":"guru","Teacher Wang teaches Chinese.":"Guru Wang mengajar bahasa Mandarin.","student":"pelajar; siswa","I am a university student.":"Saya seorang mahasiswa.","doctor":"dokter","He is a doctor at the hospital.":"Dia seorang dokter di rumah sakit.","engineer":"insinyur; teknisi","I am a front-end engineer.":"Saya seorang insinyur front-end.","Taiwan":"Taiwan","I really like Taiwan.":"Saya sangat suka Taiwan.","Japan":"Jepang","I come from Japan.":"Saya berasal dari Jepang.","Taipei":"Taipei","Taipei 101 is very tall.":"Taipei 101 sangat tinggi.","home; house":"rumah","I want to go home.":"Saya ingin pulang ke rumah.","school":"sekolah","The school is next to the MRT station.":"Sekolah itu di sebelah stasiun MRT.","company":"perusahaan","I work at a company in Taipei.":"Saya bekerja di sebuah perusahaan di Taipei.","hospital":"rumah sakit","The hospital is across from the bank.":"Rumah sakit itu di seberang bank.","bank":"bank","What time does the bank open?":"Jam berapa bank buka?","restaurant":"restoran","This restaurant is very famous.":"Restoran ini sangat terkenal.","night market":"pasar malam","In the evening we go to the night market for snacks.":"Malam hari kami pergi ke pasar malam untuk jajan.","convenience store":"minimarket","Convenience stores are open 24 hours.":"Minimarket buka 24 jam.","toilet; restroom":"toilet; kamar kecil","Excuse me, where is the restroom?":"Permisi, di mana toiletnya?","MRT (Taipei metro)":"MRT (kereta bawah tanah Taipei)","I take the MRT to work every day.":"Setiap hari saya naik MRT untuk bekerja.","(city) bus":"bus (kota)","Does this bus go to Taipei Main Station?":"Apakah bus ini menuju Stasiun Utama Taipei?","train":"kereta api","We take the train to Hualien.":"Kami naik kereta api ke Hualien.","HSR (high-speed rail)":"HSR (kereta cepat)","It takes two hours to Kaohsiung by HSR.":"Dengan HSR ke Kaohsiung memakan waktu dua jam.","scooter; motorbike":"sepeda motor; skuter","There are many scooters in Taiwan.":"Di Taiwan banyak sekali sepeda motor.","taxi":"taksi","Let's take a taxi to the airport.":"Ayo naik taksi ke bandara.","station; stop":"stasiun; halte","The station is very close to here.":"Stasiunnya sangat dekat dari sini.","airport":"bandara","Taoyuan Airport is very big.":"Bandara Taoyuan sangat besar.","water":"air","Please give me a glass of water.":"Tolong beri saya segelas air.","tea":"teh","Taiwanese tea is very famous.":"Teh Taiwan sangat terkenal.","coffee":"kopi","I drink coffee every morning.":"Setiap pagi saya minum kopi.","bubble milk tea":"teh susu mutiara (bubble tea)","One bubble tea, half sugar, less ice.":"Satu bubble tea, gula setengah, es sedikit.","beer":"bir","Two bottles of Taiwan Beer, please.":"Tolong dua botol Bir Taiwan.","rice; meal":"nasi; makan","Have you eaten?":"Apakah kamu sudah makan?","noodles":"mi","Beef noodles are a famous Taiwanese dish.":"Mi sapi adalah hidangan Taiwan yang terkenal.","soup dumplings":"xiao long bao (pangsit sup)","Let's order a basket of soup dumplings.":"Ayo pesan satu keranjang xiao long bao.","braised pork rice":"nasi babi kecap (lu rou fan)","Boss, one bowl of braised pork rice.":"Bos, satu mangkuk nasi babi kecap.","fruit":"buah","Taiwanese fruit is cheap and delicious.":"Buah Taiwan murah dan enak.","mango":"mangga","In summer you have to eat mango shaved ice!":"Di musim panas wajib makan es serut mangga!","breakfast":"sarapan","Taiwanese often buy breakfast at breakfast shops.":"Orang Taiwan sering membeli sarapan di kedai sarapan.","dinner":"makan malam","What do you want for dinner tonight?":"Malam ini kamu ingin makan apa?","today":"hari ini","The weather is nice today.":"Hari ini cuacanya bagus.","tomorrow":"besok","See you tomorrow!":"Sampai jumpa besok!","yesterday":"kemarin","I went to the Palace Museum yesterday.":"Kemarin saya pergi ke Museum Istana Nasional.","now":"sekarang","What time is it now?":"Sekarang jam berapa?","morning":"pagi","I get up at seven in the morning.":"Saya bangun jam tujuh pagi.","evening; night":"malam","Shall we go to the night market tonight?":"Malam ini kita pergi ke pasar malam, yuk?","week":"minggu (pekan)","Are you free on Saturday?":"Apakah kamu ada waktu hari Sabtu?","time":"waktu","I don't have time today.":"Hari ini saya tidak punya waktu.","o'clock":"pukul (jam)","Let's meet at the station at three.":"Jam tiga kita bertemu di stasiun.","one":"satu","I'd like one coffee.":"Saya mau satu kopi.","two (before measure words)":"dua (sebelum kata bantu bilangan)","I have two younger sisters.":"Saya punya dua adik perempuan.","three":"tiga","I've been learning Chinese for three months.":"Saya sudah belajar bahasa Mandarin selama tiga bulan.","ten":"sepuluh","This is ten dollars (NTD).":"Ini sepuluh dolar (NTD).","hundred":"ratus","That's 350 dollars in total.":"Totalnya 350 dolar.","money":"uang","How much is this?":"Ini berapa harganya?","dollar (colloquial)":"dolar (bahasa sehari-hari)","Bubble tea is fifty dollars a cup.":"Bubble tea lima puluh dolar per gelas.","(general measure word)":"(kata bantu bilangan umum)","Give me one soup dumpling.":"Beri saya satu xiao long bao.","cup of; glass of":"gelas; cangkir","Two iced milk teas, please.":"Tolong dua teh susu dingin.","to be":"adalah","I am an engineer.":"Saya seorang insinyur.","to have; there is":"punya; ada","Do you have an EasyCard?":"Apakah kamu punya EasyCard?","to go":"pergi","I'm going to Tainan tomorrow.":"Besok saya pergi ke Tainan.","to come":"datang","Welcome to Taiwan!":"Selamat datang di Taiwan!","to eat":"makan","What do you want to eat?":"Kamu ingin makan apa?","to drink":"minum","I don't drink coffee; I drink tea.":"Saya tidak minum kopi, saya minum teh.","to buy":"membeli","I want to buy an EasyCard.":"Saya ingin membeli EasyCard.","to look; to read; to watch":"melihat; membaca; menonton","I like watching movies.":"Saya suka menonton film.","to listen":"mendengar; mendengarkan","I listen to Chinese podcasts every day.":"Setiap hari saya mendengarkan podcast bahasa Mandarin.","to speak; to say":"berbicara; mengatakan","Please speak a little slower.":"Tolong bicara sedikit lebih pelan.","to write":"menulis","Traditional characters are hard to write.":"Aksara tradisional sulit ditulis.","to learn; to study":"belajar","I'm learning Taiwanese Mandarin.":"Saya sedang belajar bahasa Mandarin Taiwan.","to work; job":"bekerja; pekerjaan","I work in Japan.":"Saya bekerja di Jepang.","to like":"menyukai","I really like Taiwan's night markets.":"Saya sangat suka pasar malam Taiwan.","to want; will":"mau; ingin; akan","I want this one.":"Saya mau yang ini.","to want to; to think":"ingin; berpikir","I want to visit Jiufen.":"Saya ingin mengunjungi Jiufen.","can; will":"bisa; dapat","I can speak a little Chinese.":"Saya bisa berbicara sedikit bahasa Mandarin.","may; can":"boleh; bisa","Can I pay by card?":"Apakah saya boleh bayar dengan kartu?","to know":"tahu; mengetahui","I don't know how to get there.":"Saya tidak tahu cara ke sana.","to live; to stay":"tinggal; menginap","Where do you live?":"Kamu tinggal di mana?","good":"baik; bagus","OK, no problem!":"Oke, tidak masalah!","big":"besar","This bowl of noodles is huge!":"Semangkuk mi ini besar sekali!","small":"kecil","I'll take the small size.":"Saya ambil ukuran kecil.","many; much":"banyak","Taipei has many cafes.":"Taipei punya banyak kafe.","expensive":"mahal","Too expensive! Can you make it cheaper?":"Terlalu mahal! Bisa lebih murah tidak?","cheap":"murah","Things at the night market are cheap.":"Barang-barang di pasar malam murah.","delicious (food)":"enak (makanan)","This is super delicious!":"Ini enak sekali!","delicious (drink)":"enak (minuman)","This shop's milk tea is really good.":"Teh susu toko ini benar-benar enak.","pretty; beautiful":"cantik; indah","The scenery at Sun Moon Lake is beautiful.":"Pemandangan di Danau Matahari Bulan sangat indah.","hot":"panas","Summer in Taiwan is very hot.":"Musim panas di Taiwan sangat panas.","cold":"dingin","It's a bit cold today.":"Hari ini agak dingin.","busy":"sibuk","I've been very busy lately.":"Belakangan ini saya sangat sibuk.","tired":"lelah; capek","I walked all day today; I'm so tired.":"Hari ini saya berjalan seharian, capek sekali.","happy":"senang; gembira","I'm happy to meet you.":"Saya senang bertemu denganmu.","near; close":"dekat","The MRT station is very close to the hotel.":"Stasiun MRT sangat dekat dengan hotel.","far":"jauh","Is Jiufen far from Taipei?":"Apakah Jiufen jauh dari Taipei?","what":"apa","What is this?":"Ini apa?","who":"siapa","Who is that person?":"Siapa orang itu?","where":"di mana; ke mana","Where do you want to go?":"Kamu mau pergi ke mana?","how many (small numbers)":"berapa (jumlah kecil)","How many people (in your party)?":"Berapa orang (rombongan Anda)?","how much; how many":"berapa banyak","How much is the monthly rent?":"Berapa uang sewa per bulan?","how; why":"bagaimana; mengapa","How do you read this character?":"Bagaimana cara membaca karakter ini?","this":"ini","This is my EasyCard.":"Ini EasyCard saya.","that":"itu","What snack is that?":"Jajanan itu apa?","hello":"halo","Hello, I'm Yamada.":"Halo, saya Yamada.","thank you":"terima kasih","Thanks for your help!":"Terima kasih atas bantuannya!","you're welcome":"sama-sama","You're welcome, it was nothing.":"Sama-sama, bukan apa-apa kok.","sorry":"maaf","Sorry, I'm late.":"Maaf, saya terlambat.","excuse me; sorry (very common in Taiwan)":"permisi; maaf (sangat umum di Taiwan)","Excuse me, coming through.":"Permisi, numpang lewat.","it's OK; no problem":"tidak apa-apa; tidak masalah","It's fine, take your time.":"Tidak apa-apa, santai saja.","goodbye":"selamat tinggal; sampai jumpa","Bye, see you next time!":"Dah, sampai jumpa lain kali!","excuse me, may I ask...":"permisi, boleh saya bertanya...","Excuse me, may I sit here?":"Permisi, boleh saya duduk di sini?","boss; shopkeeper (used to address staff)":"bos; pemilik toko (untuk memanggil pelayan)","Boss, how much is this?":"Bos, ini berapa harganya?","four":"empat","There are four people in our family.":"Keluarga kami berjumlah empat orang.","five":"lima","I get off work at five.":"Saya pulang kerja jam lima.","six":"enam","I get up at six in the morning.":"Saya bangun jam enam pagi.","seven":"tujuh","It is seven thirty now.":"Sekarang jam setengah delapan.","eight":"delapan","This coffee is eighty NT dollars.":"Kopi ini delapan puluh dolar NT.","nine":"sembilan","I have a meeting at nine.":"Jam sembilan saya ada rapat.","thousand":"ribu","This piece of clothing is one thousand NT dollars.":"Pakaian ini seribu dolar NT.","ten thousand":"sepuluh ribu","This phone is twenty thousand NT dollars.":"Ponsel ini dua puluh ribu dolar NT.","measure word for animals":"kata bantu bilangan untuk hewan","I have a cat at home.":"Di rumah saya ada seekor kucing.","measure word for books":"kata bantu bilangan untuk buku","I bought three books.":"Saya membeli tiga buah buku.","Monday":"hari Senin","I have to work on Monday.":"Hari Senin saya harus bekerja.","Sunday":"hari Minggu","I rest at home on Sunday.":"Hari Minggu saya beristirahat di rumah.","month":"bulan","A year has twelve months.":"Satu tahun ada dua belas bulan.","day of the month; number":"tanggal; nomor","Today is July fifth.":"Hari ini tanggal lima Juli.","birthday":"ulang tahun","My birthday is March tenth.":"Ulang tahun saya tanggal sepuluh Maret.","red":"merah","I like red clothes.":"Saya suka baju berwarna merah.","blue":"biru","His scooter is blue.":"Sepeda motornya berwarna biru.","white":"putih","I want to buy white shoes.":"Saya ingin membeli sepatu putih.","black":"hitam","This cat is black.":"Kucing ini berwarna hitam.","green":"hijau","I like green the most.":"Saya paling suka warna hijau.","yellow":"kuning","Taxis in Taiwan are yellow.":"Taksi di Taiwan berwarna kuning.","head":"kepala","My head hurts a little today.":"Hari ini kepala saya agak sakit.","hand":"tangan","His hands are very big.":"Tangannya besar sekali.","foot; leg":"kaki","After walking all day, my feet really hurt.":"Setelah berjalan seharian, kaki saya sakit sekali.","eye":"mata","Her eyes are very pretty.":"Matanya sangat indah.","ear":"telinga","My ear does not feel very well.":"Telinga saya terasa kurang enak.","mouth":"mulut","The doctor said: please open your mouth.":"Dokter berkata: tolong buka mulut Anda.","dog":"anjing","I take my dog to the park every day.":"Setiap hari saya membawa anjing saya ke taman.","cat":"kucing","My cat loves sleeping.":"Kucing saya suka tidur.","bird":"burung","There are many birds in the park.":"Ada banyak burung di taman.","fish":"ikan","I want to eat fish for dinner.":"Untuk makan malam saya ingin makan ikan.","chicken (meat)":"daging ayam","I would like a chicken bento.":"Saya mau satu bento ayam.","pork":"daging babi","The pork at this shop is delicious.":"Daging babi di toko ini enak.","beef":"daging sapi","I do not eat beef.":"Saya tidak makan daging sapi.","egg":"telur","I ate two eggs for breakfast.":"Untuk sarapan saya makan dua butir telur.","bread":"roti","I bought bread this morning.":"Tadi pagi saya membeli roti.","soup":"sup","This soup is very tasty.":"Sup ini sangat enak.","juice":"jus","Boss, I would like a glass of juice.":"Bos, saya mau segelas jus.","milk":"susu","I drink milk every morning.":"Saya minum susu setiap pagi.","cola":"cola","He does not drink coffee, only cola.":"Dia tidak minum kopi, hanya cola.","ice (cubes)":"es (batu)","Please do not add ice, thank you.":"Tolong jangan pakai es, terima kasih.","park":"taman","I take a walk in the park in the morning.":"Pagi hari saya berjalan-jalan di taman.","library":"perpustakaan","I often go to the library to read.":"Saya sering pergi ke perpustakaan untuk membaca.","post office":"kantor pos","I am going to the post office to mail something.":"Saya pergi ke kantor pos untuk mengirim sesuatu.","supermarket":"supermarket","Mom buys fruit at the supermarket.":"Ibu membeli buah di supermarket.","hotel":"hotel","We are staying at a hotel in Taipei.":"Kami menginap di hotel di Taipei.","classroom":"ruang kelas","The students are all in the classroom.":"Para siswa semuanya ada di ruang kelas.","university":"universitas","He studies Chinese at university.":"Dia belajar bahasa Mandarin di universitas.","table; desk":"meja","There is a cup of tea on the table.":"Di atas meja ada secangkir teh.","chair":"kursi","This chair is very comfortable.":"Kursi ini sangat nyaman.","bed":"tempat tidur","There is a bed in my room.":"Di kamar saya ada tempat tidur.","door; gate":"pintu; gerbang","Please close the door, thank you.":"Tolong tutup pintunya, terima kasih.","window":"jendela","The window in the room is very big.":"Jendela di kamar itu sangat besar.","book":"buku","I am reading a Japanese book.":"Saya sedang membaca buku berbahasa Jepang.","pen":"pena","Could you lend me a pen?":"Bisakah kamu meminjamkan saya pena?","umbrella":"payung","It is raining outside; you should take an umbrella.":"Di luar sedang hujan, sebaiknya kamu membawa payung.","glasses":"kacamata","My glasses are gone!":"Kacamata saya hilang!","grandfather (paternal)":"kakek (dari pihak ayah)","Grandpa is eighty years old this year.":"Tahun ini kakek berusia delapan puluh tahun.","grandmother (paternal)":"nenek (dari pihak ayah)","Grandma goes to the park every morning.":"Nenek pergi ke taman setiap pagi.","son":"anak laki-laki","His son is five years old this year.":"Tahun ini anak laki-lakinya berusia lima tahun.","daughter":"anak perempuan","Her daughter is a university student.":"Anak perempuannya adalah seorang mahasiswa.","to open; to turn on":"membuka; menyalakan","It is so hot; I turned on the air conditioner.":"Panas sekali, saya menyalakan AC.","to close; to turn off":"menutup; mematikan","Turn off the air conditioner before going out.":"Matikan AC sebelum keluar.","to sit; to take (transport)":"duduk; naik (kendaraan)","to walk; to go":"berjalan; pergi","The station is close; let's walk there.":"Stasiunnya dekat, ayo kita jalan kaki ke sana.","to take; to hold":"mengambil; memegang","This is heavy; let me carry it for you.":"Ini berat, biar saya bawakan untukmu.","to use":"memakai; menggunakan","May I use your pen for a moment?":"Boleh saya pakai pena kamu sebentar?","to do; to make":"melakukan; membuat","This is a dish my mom made.":"Ini masakan yang dibuat ibu saya.","to play; to have fun":"bermain; bersenang-senang","Let's go have fun in Tainan this weekend!":"Akhir pekan ini ayo kita main ke Tainan!","to ask":"bertanya","If you don't know, you can ask the teacher.":"Kalau tidak tahu, kamu bisa bertanya kepada guru.","to wash":"mencuci","Wash your hands before eating.":"Cuci tangan sebelum makan.","to look for":"mencari","I am looking for my phone.":"Saya sedang mencari ponsel saya.","to teach":"mengajar","Can you teach me how to make this dish?":"Bisakah kamu mengajari saya cara membuat masakan ini?","to know (a person); to meet":"mengenal (seseorang); berkenalan","Nice to meet you!":"Senang berkenalan dengan Anda!","tall; high":"tinggi","long":"panjang","Her hair is very long.":"Rambutnya sangat panjang.","short (length)":"pendek","These pants are too short.":"Celana ini terlalu pendek.","fast":"cepat","The high-speed rail is fast; it arrives in an hour and a half.":"Kereta cepat sangat cepat, satu setengah jam sudah sampai.","slow":"lambat; pelan","Sorry, please speak a little more slowly.":"Maaf, tolong bicara sedikit lebih pelan.","new":"baru","I bought a new phone.":"Saya membeli ponsel baru.","early":"awal; pagi","I need to get up a bit earlier tomorrow.":"Besok saya harus bangun sedikit lebih awal.","late":"terlambat; larut","It is very late now; I am going to sleep.":"Sekarang sudah larut, saya mau tidur.","morning; a.m.":"pagi; a.m.","I have Chinese class in the morning.":"Pagi hari saya ada kelas bahasa Mandarin.","afternoon; p.m.":"sore; p.m.","Let's go shopping this afternoon.":"Sore ini ayo kita pergi berbelanja.","weekend":"akhir pekan","I want to go hiking this weekend.":"Akhir pekan ini saya ingin mendaki gunung.","every day":"setiap hari","I drink a cup of coffee every day.":"Saya minum secangkir kopi setiap hari.","year":"tahun","I have been in Taiwan for a year.":"Saya sudah setahun tinggal di Taiwan.","oneself":"diri sendiri","I live by myself.":"Saya tinggal sendiri.","together":"bersama-sama","Let's go eat together!":"Ayo kita makan bersama!","thing; stuff":"barang; benda","I am going to the supermarket to buy some things.":"Saya pergi ke supermarket untuk membeli beberapa barang.","measure word for long thin things":"kata bantu bilangan untuk benda panjang dan tipis","I bought a fish.":"Saya membeli seekor ikan.","measure word for people (polite)":"kata bantu bilangan untuk orang (sopan)","How many people, please?":"Berapa orang, ya?","measure word for machines":"kata bantu bilangan untuk mesin","There are two computers in my home.":"Di rumah saya ada dua komputer.","time (occurrence)":"kali","I have been to Tainan once.":"Saya pernah ke Tainan satu kali.","years old":"tahun (usia)","I am twenty-five this year.":"Tahun ini saya berusia dua puluh lima tahun.","some; a few":"beberapa; sedikit","I bought some fruit.":"Saya membeli beberapa buah.","sugar":"gula","Do you want sugar in your coffee?":"Apakah kopimu mau pakai gula?","salt":"garam","Please give me a little salt.":"Tolong beri saya sedikit garam.","oil":"minyak","My mom uses a lot of oil when cooking.":"Ibu saya memakai banyak minyak saat memasak.","soy sauce":"kecap asin","Please give me some soy sauce.":"Tolong beri saya sedikit kecap asin.","boiled dumpling":"pangsit rebus","The dumplings at this shop are delicious.":"Pangsit di toko ini enak.","steamed bun":"bakpao","I ate two steamed buns for breakfast.":"Saya makan dua bakpao untuk sarapan.","tofu":"tahu","There is tofu in this soup.":"Di dalam sup ini ada tahu.","green vegetables":"sayuran hijau","Boss, I would like a plate of greens.":"Bos, saya mau sepiring sayuran hijau.","apple":"apel","I eat an apple every day.":"Saya makan sebuah apel setiap hari.","banana":"pisang","Bananas in Taiwan are very cheap.":"Pisang di Taiwan sangat murah.","watermelon":"semangka","This watermelon is very sweet.":"Semangka ini sangat manis.","fork":"garpu","I want a fork, not chopsticks.":"Saya mau garpu, bukan sumpit.","luggage":"koper; bagasi","My luggage is very heavy.":"Koper saya sangat berat.","telephone":"telepon","What is your phone number?":"Berapa nomor teleponmu?","photo":"foto","This photo is very beautiful.":"Foto ini sangat indah.","newspaper":"koran","Grandpa reads the newspaper every morning.":"Kakek membaca koran setiap pagi.","magazine":"majalah","I bought a magazine at the convenience store.":"Saya membeli majalah di minimarket.","envelope":"amplop","I want to buy envelopes and stamps.":"Saya mau membeli amplop dan perangko.","stamp":"perangko","This stamp is very cute.":"Perangko ini sangat lucu.","box":"kotak","What is in the box?":"Apa isi kotak itu?","bottle":"botol","There is a bottle on the table.":"Di atas meja ada sebuah botol.","cup; glass":"cangkir; gelas","This cup is mine.":"Cangkir ini milik saya.","noon":"tengah hari; siang","I eat a lunch box at noon.":"Siang hari saya makan nasi kotak.","minute":"menit","It takes ten minutes from my home to the station.":"Dari rumah saya ke stasiun butuh sepuluh menit.","face":"wajah","I wash my face every morning.":"Saya mencuci muka setiap pagi.","skirt":"rok","She is wearing a white skirt today.":"Hari ini dia memakai rok putih.","nose":"hidung","I have a cold and my nose feels uncomfortable.":"Saya sedang pilek dan hidung saya terasa tidak nyaman.","hair":"rambut","sun":"matahari","The sun has come out.":"Matahari sudah muncul.","moon":"bulan","The moon is very beautiful tonight.":"Malam ini bulannya sangat indah.","star":"bintang","You can see many stars on the mountain.":"Di gunung kamu bisa melihat banyak bintang.","sky":"langit","The sky is very blue today.":"Hari ini langitnya sangat biru.","mountain":"gunung","Taiwan has many high mountains.":"Taiwan memiliki banyak gunung tinggi.","sea":"laut","We are going to see the sea this weekend.":"Akhir pekan ini kami akan pergi melihat laut.","river":"sungai","There is a park beside the river.":"Di tepi sungai ada sebuah taman.","tree":"pohon","There are many trees in the park.":"Di taman ada banyak pohon.","flower":"bunga","These flowers are very beautiful.":"Bunga-bunga ini sangat indah.","grass":"rumput","The cat is sleeping on the grass.":"Kucing itu sedang tidur di atas rumput.","airplane":"pesawat terbang","I go to Japan by plane.":"Saya pergi ke Jepang naik pesawat.","bicycle":"sepeda","I ride a bicycle to work every day.":"Saya naik sepeda ke kantor setiap hari.","car; vehicle":"mobil; kendaraan","There are many cars on the road.":"Di jalan ada banyak mobil.","to wait":"menunggu","Please wait for me for five minutes.":"Tolong tunggu saya lima menit.","to help":"membantu","Can you help me carry this?":"Bisakah kamu membantu saya membawa ini?","to sell":"menjual","This shop sells fruit.":"Toko ini menjual buah.","to rent":"menyewa","I rent a place in Taipei.":"Saya menyewa tempat tinggal di Taipei.","to fly":"terbang","Birds are flying in the sky.":"Burung-burung terbang di langit.","to jump":"melompat","The cat jumped onto the table.":"Kucing itu melompat ke atas meja.","to draw; to paint":"menggambar; melukis","My younger sister is very good at drawing.":"Adik perempuan saya sangat pandai menggambar.","to push":"mendorong","Push this door, do not pull it.":"Dorong pintu ini, jangan ditarik.","to pull":"menarik","My younger brother pulls my hand.":"Adik laki-laki saya menarik tangan saya.","to hug; to hold":"memeluk; menggendong","The mother is holding the baby.":"Ibu itu sedang menggendong bayi.","to take off":"melepas (pakaian)","You need to take off your shoes when entering.":"Kamu harus melepas sepatu saat masuk.","to wear (glasses, hat)":"memakai (kacamata, topi)","He is wearing glasses today.":"Hari ini dia memakai kacamata.","dry":"kering","The clothes are not dry yet.":"Pakaiannya belum kering.","wet":"basah","It rained and my shoes got wet.":"Hujan turun dan sepatu saya jadi basah.","bright":"terang","This room is very bright.":"Ruangan ini sangat terang.","dark":"gelap","The room is too dark.":"Ruangan ini terlalu gelap.","full":"penuh","The cup is full.":"Cangkirnya sudah penuh.","empty":"kosong","The bottle is empty.":"Botolnya kosong.","light (weight)":"ringan","This bag is very light.":"Tas ini sangat ringan.","heavy":"berat","The luggage is too heavy.":"Kopernya terlalu berat.","thick":"tebal","This book is very thick.":"Buku ini sangat tebal.","thin (flat things)":"tipis","This coat is too thin.":"Jaket ini terlalu tipis.","round":"bulat","The moon is round and bright.":"Bulannya bulat dan terang.","square":"persegi","This table is square.":"Meja ini berbentuk persegi.","watch":"jam tangan","This watch is very expensive.":"Jam tangan ini sangat mahal.","left side":"sebelah kiri","The convenience store is on the left of the bank.":"Minimarket itu ada di sebelah kiri bank.","right side":"sebelah kanan","The restroom is on the right.":"Toilet ada di sebelah kanan.","on top; above":"di atas","The book is on the table.":"Buku itu ada di atas meja.","below; underneath":"di bawah","The cat is under the chair.":"Kucing itu ada di bawah kursi.","here":"di sini","Please wait here for a moment.":"Tolong tunggu di sini sebentar.","there":"di sana","The station is over there.":"Stasiunnya ada di sana.","just now":"barusan; tadi","Someone called you just now.":"Tadi ada yang meneleponmu.","road; street":"jalan","Be careful when crossing the road.":"Hati-hati saat menyeberang jalan.","intersection":"persimpangan","Turn right at the next intersection.":"Belok kanan di persimpangan berikutnya.","classmate":"teman sekelas","He is my university classmate.":"Dia teman sekelas saya di universitas.","fat; chubby":"gemuk","I have gained weight recently.":"Akhir-akhir ini saya jadi gemuk.","thin; slim":"kurus","He eats a lot but is very thin.":"Dia makan banyak tapi sangat kurus.","guest; customer":"tamu; pelanggan","There are many customers in the shop today.":"Hari ini banyak pelanggan di toko.","female boss; boss's wife":"pemilik toko wanita; istri bos","The boss's wife gave me a cup of tea.":"Istri bos memberi saya secangkir teh.","child; kid":"anak-anak","baby":"bayi","The baby is sleeping.":"Bayi itu sedang tidur.","to go online":"berselancar internet; online","I go online every night.":"Saya online setiap malam.","to play ball":"bermain bola","I play ball with my friends on weekends.":"Akhir pekan saya bermain bola dengan teman-teman.","to run; to jog":"berlari; jogging","I go jogging in the park in the morning.":"Pagi hari saya jogging di taman.","to take a walk":"berjalan-jalan","We take a walk after dinner.":"Setelah makan malam kami berjalan-jalan.","to order food":"memesan makanan","Are you ready to order?":"Apakah Anda sudah siap memesan?","to take out (food)":"bawa pulang (makanan)","One bubble tea, to go.":"Satu teh boba, bawa pulang.","movie":"film","We are going to see a movie tonight.":"Malam ini kami akan menonton film.","music":"musik","I like listening to music.":"Saya suka mendengarkan musik.","cake":"kue","We eat cake on birthdays.":"Saat ulang tahun kita makan kue.","place":"tempat","Taiwan is a very beautiful place.":"Taiwan adalah tempat yang sangat indah.","spring":"musim semi","The flowers in spring are very beautiful.":"Bunga di musim semi sangat indah.","autumn; fall":"musim gugur","Autumn is neither hot nor cold.":"Musim gugur tidak panas dan tidak dingin.","cheap; inexpensive":"murah","The fruit here is fresh and cheap.":"Buah di sini segar dan murah.","This jacket is too expensive—can you give me a bit of a discount?":"Jaket ini terlalu mahal—bisakah diberi sedikit diskon?","On my way home from work I stop by the supermarket for dinner groceries.":"Dalam perjalanan pulang kerja saya mampir ke supermarket untuk membeli bahan makan malam.","market (esp. traditional market)":"pasar (terutama pasar tradisional)","Grandma is used to going to the traditional market in the morning.":"Nenek terbiasa pergi ke pasar tradisional pada pagi hari.","boss; shop owner":"bos; pemilik toko","There are especially many customers in the shop today.":"Hari ini pelanggan di toko sangat banyak.","to line up; to queue":"mengantre","This fried-chicken stand is so famous you have to queue half an hour.":"Kedai ayam goreng ini begitu terkenal sampai harus mengantre setengah jam.","cash":"uang tunai","This eatery takes cash only—no cards.":"Warung makan ini hanya menerima uang tunai—tidak menerima kartu.","size":"ukuran","These shoes don't come in my size—do you have one size up?":"Sepatu ini tidak ada ukuran saya—apakah ada yang satu ukuran lebih besar?","bus":"bus","It's more convenient to take the bus there.":"Lebih praktis naik bus ke sana.","MRT (Taiwan's metro)":"MRT (kereta metro Taiwan)","Taipei's MRT is very clean; eating on board is not allowed.":"MRT Taipei sangat bersih; makan di dalam kereta tidak diperbolehkan.","I take the train to Hualien—you can see the ocean the whole way.":"Saya naik kereta ke Hualien—sepanjang jalan bisa melihat laut.","HSR (Taiwan High Speed Rail)":"HSR (Kereta Cepat Taiwan)","It's only an hour and a half from Taipei to Kaohsiung by HSR.":"Dari Taipei ke Kaohsiung hanya satu setengah jam dengan HSR.","It's late—let's call a taxi to get home.":"Sudah larut—ayo kita panggil taksi untuk pulang.","scooter; motorbike (most common in Taiwan)":"sepeda motor; skuter (paling umum di Taiwan)","In Taiwan, lots of people commute by scooter.":"Di Taiwan, banyak orang pergi kerja naik sepeda motor.","to walk (on foot)":"berjalan kaki","It's close—just a five-minute walk.":"Dekat kok—hanya lima menit jalan kaki.","to get on/in (a vehicle)":"naik (kendaraan)","Tap your card when you board, and again when you get off.":"Tempelkan kartu saat naik, dan tempelkan lagi saat turun.","to get off (a vehicle)":"turun (dari kendaraan)","I'm getting off at the next stop, so goodbye for now.":"Saya turun di halte berikutnya, jadi sampai jumpa dulu.","to park (a vehicle)":"memarkir (kendaraan)","Parking is hard around here—let's just take the MRT.":"Susah cari parkir di sekitar sini—kita naik MRT saja.","to get lost":"tersesat","It's my first time here, so I use my phone's navigation to avoid getting lost.":"Ini pertama kali saya ke sini, jadi saya pakai navigasi ponsel agar tidak tersesat.","to be late":"terlambat","There's traffic, so I might be ten minutes late.":"Jalanan macet, jadi saya mungkin terlambat sepuluh menit.","He felt ill yesterday and was taken to the hospital.":"Kemarin dia merasa tidak enak badan dan dibawa ke rumah sakit.","clinic":"klinik","For a mild cold, a nearby clinic is enough—no need to go to a big hospital.":"Untuk pilek ringan, klinik terdekat sudah cukup—tidak perlu ke rumah sakit besar.","I worked overtime until late today—I'm so tired.":"Hari ini saya lembur sampai larut—lelah sekali.","to get an injection/shot":"disuntik","The kid is scared of shots and keeps crying.":"Anak itu takut disuntik dan terus menangis.","to examine; to check":"memeriksa","The doctor said further tests are needed to find the cause.":"Dokter mengatakan perlu pemeriksaan lebih lanjut untuk menemukan penyebabnya.","to have diarrhea":"diare; mencret","I ate something bad yesterday and have had diarrhea all day.":"Kemarin saya makan sesuatu yang tidak baik dan diare seharian.","living room":"ruang tamu","In the evening the whole family likes watching TV together in the living room.":"Pada malam hari seluruh keluarga suka menonton TV bersama di ruang tamu.","This studio's kitchen is tiny—you can only cook simple things.":"Dapur studio ini sangat kecil—hanya bisa memasak hal-hal sederhana.","Excuse me, where's the restroom?":"Permisi, di mana toiletnya?","bathroom":"kamar mandi","The bathroom light is broken—I need to tell the landlord.":"Lampu kamar mandi rusak—saya harus memberi tahu pemilik rumah.","balcony":"balkon","I hung the clothes on the balcony and they dried quickly.":"Saya menjemur pakaian di balkon dan cepat kering.","The weather's nice—open the window to let some air in.":"Cuacanya bagus—buka jendela agar udara masuk.","deposit (security)":"uang jaminan; deposit","When renting, you usually pay two months' deposit up front.":"Saat menyewa, biasanya membayar uang jaminan dua bulan di muka.","to have a power outage":"mati listrik","The power sometimes goes out on typhoon days—remember to have a flashlight ready.":"Saat hari topan kadang mati listrik—ingat siapkan senter.","salary; pay":"gaji","This job is tough, but the pay is decent.":"Pekerjaan ini berat, tapi gajinya lumayan.","to work overtime":"lembur","Work's been busy lately—I have to work overtime almost every day.":"Akhir-akhir ini pekerjaan sibuk—saya harus lembur hampir setiap hari.","job interview":"wawancara kerja","I have an important interview next week.":"Minggu depan saya ada wawancara penting.","business card":"kartu nama","Here's my business card—contact me if anything comes up.":"Ini kartu nama saya—hubungi saya jika ada sesuatu.","client; customer (business)":"klien; pelanggan (bisnis)","This afternoon I'm meeting an important client.":"Sore ini saya akan bertemu dengan klien penting.","hard; toilsome; (thanks for) your hard work":"susah payah; (terima kasih atas) kerja kerasmu","You worked hard today—head home and rest early.":"Kamu sudah bekerja keras hari ini—pulanglah dan istirahat lebih awal.","happy; glad":"senang; gembira","I'm really happy I got to see you today.":"Saya sangat senang bisa bertemu denganmu hari ini.","happy (also in greetings)":"bahagia (juga dalam ucapan selamat)","Happy birthday to you!":"Selamat ulang tahun untukmu!","satisfied; pleased":"puas","The customer is very satisfied with the service this time.":"Pelanggan sangat puas dengan layanan kali ini.","to be moved; touched":"terharu; tersentuh","Everyone celebrated my birthday—I was so touched.":"Semua orang merayakan ulang tahun saya—saya sangat terharu.","to regret":"menyesal","I really regret not learning Chinese sooner.":"Saya benar-benar menyesal tidak belajar bahasa Mandarin lebih awal.","to dislike; annoying":"tidak suka; menyebalkan","What I hate most is having to go out on rainy days.":"Yang paling saya benci adalah harus keluar saat hari hujan.","relaxed; easy; light":"santai; ringan","After the exam, I finally feel relaxed.":"Setelah ujian, akhirnya saya merasa lega.","to bring; to take (along)":"membawa","Before you go out, remember to bring an umbrella and your EasyCard.":"Sebelum keluar, ingat bawa payung dan kartu EasyCard-mu.","The movie starts at seven—let's go a bit early.":"Filmnya mulai jam tujuh—ayo kita berangkat lebih awal.","to end; to finish":"berakhir; selesai","After the meeting ends, let's grab a meal together.":"Setelah rapat selesai, ayo kita makan bersama.","to decide":"memutuskan","I've decided to take the N2 exam next year.":"Saya sudah memutuskan untuk mengikuti ujian N2 tahun depan.","If you need help, just let me know anytime.":"Kalau butuh bantuan, beri tahu saya kapan saja.","to agree":"setuju","Does everyone agree with this plan?":"Apakah semua orang setuju dengan rencana ini?","to complete; to finish":"menyelesaikan","I absolutely have to finish this report today.":"Hari ini saya harus benar-benar menyelesaikan laporan ini.","to go out; to leave home":"keluar rumah","I'm about to be late, so I'm heading out right now.":"Saya hampir terlambat, jadi saya berangkat sekarang.","to go home":"pulang ke rumah","It's so late—be careful going home by yourself.":"Sudah larut sekali—hati-hati pulang sendiri.","to chat":"mengobrol","Let's find a café, sit down, and chat.":"Ayo cari kafe, duduk, dan mengobrol.","What have you been busy with lately? Haven't seen you in ages.":"Akhir-akhir ini kamu sibuk apa? Sudah lama tidak bertemu.","important":"penting","This matter is very important—you must remember it.":"Hal ini sangat penting—kamu harus mengingatnya.","You look really pretty in that skirt today.":"Kamu terlihat sangat cantik dengan rok itu hari ini.","fresh":"segar","The fish at this seafood restaurant is very fresh.":"Ikan di restoran seafood ini sangat segar.","lively; bustling":"ramai; meriah","The night market in the evening is lively and fun.":"Pasar malam di malam hari ramai dan menyenangkan.","so; therefore":"jadi; oleh karena itu","It rained hard today, so I didn't go hiking.":"Hari ini hujan deras, jadi saya tidak jadi mendaki gunung.","because":"karena","Because of the traffic, I was late.":"Karena macet, saya terlambat.","although; even though":"meskipun; walaupun","Even though it's cold, I still want to go out for a walk.":"Meskipun dingin, saya tetap ingin keluar berjalan-jalan.","moreover; and also":"lagipula; dan juga","The food here is tasty, and it's cheap too.":"Makanan di sini enak, dan juga murah.","if":"jika; kalau","If the weather's nice tomorrow, we'll go to the beach.":"Kalau besok cuacanya bagus, kita akan pergi ke pantai.","Want to go eat hot pot together this weekend?":"Mau makan hot pot bareng akhir pekan ini?","finally; at last":"akhirnya","After a whole month of being busy, I can finally rest this weekend.":"Setelah sibuk sebulan penuh, akhirnya saya bisa istirahat akhir pekan ini.","flight":"penerbangan","My flight takes off at three in the afternoon.":"Penerbangan saya lepas landas jam tiga sore.","to go abroad":"pergi ke luar negeri","The first time I went abroad was to Japan.":"Pertama kali saya ke luar negeri adalah ke Jepang.","seat":"tempat duduk","Are there still window seats on the high-speed rail?":"Apakah masih ada tempat duduk dekat jendela di kereta cepat?","EasyCard (Taiwan transit card)":"EasyCard (kartu transportasi Taiwan)","Taking the bus with an EasyCard is cheaper.":"Naik bus dengan EasyCard lebih murah.","to top up (a card)":"mengisi ulang (kartu)","My EasyCard is empty, so I'll top it up at the convenience store.":"EasyCard saya kosong, jadi saya akan mengisinya di minimarket.","to transfer (flights)":"transit (penerbangan)","To get to Europe you transfer once in Hong Kong.":"Untuk ke Eropa kamu transit sekali di Hong Kong.","round trip":"pulang pergi","How much is a round-trip ticket from Taipei to Taichung?":"Berapa harga tiket pulang pergi dari Taipei ke Taichung?","to book a ticket":"memesan tiket","Book high-speed rail tickets early for long weekends.":"Pesan tiket kereta cepat lebih awal untuk libur panjang.","ticket machine":"mesin tiket","You can also top up your EasyCard at the MRT station's ticket machine.":"Kamu juga bisa mengisi ulang EasyCard di mesin tiket stasiun MRT.","to check out; to pay the bill":"membayar; membayar tagihan","I'd like to check out—can I pay by card?":"Saya mau membayar—boleh bayar pakai kartu?","ATM":"ATM","There's usually an ATM inside a convenience store.":"Biasanya ada ATM di dalam minimarket.","to save money":"menabung","I save a little money each month for traveling.":"Setiap bulan saya menabung sedikit uang untuk berlibur.","to earn money":"menghasilkan uang","He earns money with a part-time job while studying.":"Dia menghasilkan uang dengan kerja paruh waktu sambil kuliah.","to spend money":"menghabiskan uang","It's easy to spend a lot of money at a night market.":"Mudah menghabiskan banyak uang di pasar malam.","special price; sale":"harga spesial; obral","This jacket is on special now for only 500 dollars.":"Jaket ini sedang obral hanya 500 dolar Taiwan.","to do earlier; ahead of time":"melakukan lebih awal; sebelumnya","With the typhoon coming, the company let everyone leave work early.":"Karena topan akan datang, perusahaan mengizinkan semua orang pulang kerja lebih awal.","to make it in time":"sempat; keburu","If we leave now we can still catch the last train.":"Kalau kita berangkat sekarang masih bisa mengejar kereta terakhir.","holiday; day off":"hari libur","Tourist spots are especially crowded on holidays.":"Tempat wisata sangat ramai pada hari libur.","weekday":"hari kerja; hari biasa","There are fewer people at the hot spring on weekdays.":"Pada hari biasa pengunjung pemandian air panas lebih sedikit.","mood; feelings":"suasana hati; perasaan","Listening to music puts me in a better mood.":"Mendengarkan musik membuat suasana hati saya lebih baik.","I'm glad to meet you.":"Saya senang bertemu dengan Anda.","to thank; to be grateful":"berterima kasih; bersyukur","Thank you so much for your help during this time.":"Terima kasih banyak atas bantuanmu selama ini.","lonely":"kesepian","Being alone abroad, you can't help feeling lonely.":"Sendirian di luar negeri, tak terhindarkan merasa kesepian.","to relax":"bersantai; rileks","Take a hot spring and relax properly.":"Berendam di pemandian air panas dan bersantailah dengan baik.","textbook":"buku pelajaran","I forgot my textbook—can I look at yours?":"Saya lupa membawa buku pelajaran—boleh saya lihat punyamu?","semester":"semester","I signed up for five courses this semester.":"Semester ini saya mendaftar lima mata kuliah.","tuition":"biaya kuliah; uang sekolah","Tuition at Taiwan's public universities isn't too expensive.":"Biaya kuliah di universitas negeri Taiwan tidak terlalu mahal.","to pass (an exam)":"lulus (ujian)","You need sixty to pass this exam.":"Kamu perlu nilai enam puluh untuk lulus ujian ini.","to attend cram school":"ikut bimbingan belajar; les","Many Taiwanese students go to cram school after school.":"Banyak siswa Taiwan pergi les setelah sekolah.","club (student society)":"klub (perkumpulan mahasiswa)","In college I joined the guitar club.":"Saat kuliah saya bergabung dengan klub gitar.","score; grade":"nilai; skor","This score improved a lot compared to last time.":"Nilai kali ini meningkat banyak dibandingkan sebelumnya.","to photocopy":"memfotokopi","Please photocopy this document ten times.":"Tolong fotokopi dokumen ini sepuluh kali.","occupation; profession":"pekerjaan; profesi","May I ask what your occupation is?":"Boleh saya tahu apa pekerjaan Anda?","exhibition":"pameran","The Palace Museum has a famous exhibition right now.":"Museum Istana Nasional sedang mengadakan pameran terkenal saat ini.","to camp":"berkemah","We plan to go camping in the mountains this weekend.":"Kami berencana pergi berkemah di gunung akhir pekan ini.","to have a picnic":"piknik","The weather's so nice, it's perfect for a picnic in the park.":"Cuacanya sangat bagus, cocok untuk piknik di taman.","My younger sister loves to draw.":"Adik perempuan saya sangat suka menggambar.","to collect":"mengoleksi; mengumpulkan","He likes collecting souvenirs from different places.":"Dia suka mengoleksi suvenir dari berbagai tempat.","performance; to perform":"pertunjukan; tampil","There's a street performer's show in the square.":"Ada pertunjukan seniman jalanan di alun-alun.","to be hospitalized":"dirawat di rumah sakit","He was seriously ill and hospitalized for a week.":"Dia sakit parah dan dirawat di rumah sakit selama seminggu.","to have heatstroke":"kena sengatan panas; heatstroke","Staying outside too long in summer easily causes heatstroke.":"Terlalu lama berada di luar saat musim panas mudah menyebabkan sengatan panas.","sleep":"tidur","Not getting enough sleep is bad for your health.":"Kurang tidur buruk bagi kesehatan.","to get vaccinated":"divaksinasi","I'll get vaccinated before going abroad.":"Saya akan divaksinasi sebelum pergi ke luar negeri.","to reserve a table":"memesan meja; reservasi meja","This restaurant is popular, so it's best to reserve a table first.":"Restoran ini populer, jadi sebaiknya pesan meja terlebih dahulu.","to dine in":"makan di tempat","Will you dine in or take out?":"Anda mau makan di tempat atau bawa pulang?","waiter; server":"pelayan","I asked the server for another pair of chopsticks.":"Saya meminta pelayan sepasang sumpit lagi.","salty":"asin","This dish is a little too salty for me.":"Masakan ini sedikit terlalu asin bagi saya.","bitter":"pahit","This coffee has no sugar and tastes bitter.":"Kopi ini tanpa gula dan rasanya pahit.","flavor; taste preference":"rasa; selera","Bubble milk tea comes in many flavors to choose from.":"Teh susu boba tersedia dalam banyak rasa untuk dipilih.","to pack up (leftovers)":"membungkus (sisa makanan) untuk dibawa pulang","You can pack up what you can't finish and take it home.":"Yang tidak habis bisa dibungkus dan dibawa pulang.","ingredients":"bahan makanan","This shop emphasizes using fresh ingredients.":"Toko ini mengutamakan penggunaan bahan yang segar.","scarf":"syal","It's colder up in the mountains, so bring a scarf.":"Di gunung lebih dingin, jadi bawalah syal.","to try on (clothes)":"mencoba (pakaian)","Can I try this one on?":"Boleh saya coba yang ini?","What's the weather like tomorrow?":"Bagaimana cuaca besok?","It often rains in Taipei in winter.":"Di Taipei sering hujan pada musim dingin.","A typhoon is coming; tomorrow might be a typhoon day off.":"Topan akan datang; besok mungkin libur karena topan.","Taiwanese summers are hot and humid.":"Musim panas di Taiwan panas dan lembap.","In winter everyone loves hot pot.":"Saat musim dingin semua orang suka makan hot pot.","How have you been feeling lately?":"Bagaimana kondisi badanmu akhir-akhir ini?","to catch a cold":"masuk angin; kena flu","I caught a cold and want to take today off.":"Saya kena flu dan ingin izin tidak masuk hari ini.","to have a fever":"demam","He has a fever—take him to the doctor quickly.":"Dia demam—cepat bawa ke dokter.","to have a headache":"sakit kepala","I've had a headache since morning.":"Saya sakit kepala sejak pagi.","medicine":"obat","Take this medicine three times a day.":"Minum obat ini tiga kali sehari.","to register (at a clinic)":"mendaftar (di klinik)","I'd like to register—how long is the wait?":"Saya mau mendaftar—berapa lama harus menunggu?","NHI card (Taiwan health insurance)":"kartu NHI (asuransi kesehatan Taiwan)","Bring your NHI card when you see a doctor.":"Bawalah kartu NHI-mu saat pergi ke dokter.","I get up at six thirty every day.":"Saya bangun pukul setengah tujuh setiap hari.","I went to bed too late last night.":"Semalam saya tidur terlalu larut.","to take a bath/shower":"mandi","I shower right after exercising.":"Saya mandi langsung setelah berolahraga.","to clean (a room)":"membersihkan (kamar)","I'm going to clean my room this weekend.":"Akhir pekan ini saya akan membersihkan kamar.","to do laundry":"mencuci pakaian","There's a laundromat near my place, so doing laundry is easy.":"Ada binatu dekat tempat saya, jadi mencuci pakaian mudah.","garbage (read lèsè in Taiwan)":"sampah (di Taiwan dibaca lèsè)","Garbage must be sorted—you can't just toss it.":"Sampah harus dipilah—tidak boleh dibuang sembarangan.","garbage truck (plays music in Taiwan)":"truk sampah (memutar musik di Taiwan)","The garbage truck is here! Run after it!":"Truk sampah datang! Ayo kejar!","air conditioner":"AC; pendingin ruangan","So hot—can we turn on the AC?":"Panas sekali—boleh nyalakan AC?","My room isn't big, but it's comfortable.":"Kamar saya tidak besar, tapi nyaman.","landlord":"pemilik rumah; tuan tanah","My landlord is nice and even fixes things.":"Pemilik rumah saya baik dan bahkan memperbaiki barang-barang.","rent":"uang sewa","Rent in Taipei keeps getting more expensive.":"Uang sewa di Taipei terus semakin mahal.","to move (house)":"pindah rumah","I'm moving to Taichung next month.":"Bulan depan saya akan pindah ke Taichung.","I start work at nine every day.":"Setiap hari saya mulai bekerja jam sembilan.","Want to grab dinner after work?":"Mau makan malam bareng setelah pulang kerja?","to take leave":"mengambil cuti","I'm taking leave tomorrow to go back to Japan.":"Besok saya cuti untuk pulang ke Jepang.","to have a meeting":"rapat","We have a meeting at 2 p.m.":"Kita ada rapat jam 2 siang.","coworker":"rekan kerja","My coworkers are all friendly.":"Rekan-rekan kerja saya semuanya ramah.","to exercise; sports":"berolahraga; olahraga","What exercise do you usually do?":"Kamu biasanya olahraga apa?","to swim":"berenang","I often go swimming in summer.":"Saat musim panas saya sering berenang.","to hike; to climb a mountain":"mendaki gunung","Let's hike Elephant Mountain this weekend and see Taipei 101.":"Akhir pekan ini yuk mendaki Gunung Gajah dan melihat Taipei 101.","Taiwanese people love singing at KTV.":"Orang Taiwan suka menyanyi di KTV.","to take photos":"memotret","The view here is beautiful—let's take photos!":"Pemandangan di sini indah, ayo foto-foto!","to travel":"berwisata","I want to travel to Taitung.":"Saya ingin berwisata ke Taitung.","to go window shopping; stroll around":"jalan-jalan lihat-lihat toko","She loves shopping in Ximending on weekends.":"Akhir pekan dia suka belanja di Ximending.","Can I try on this piece of clothing?":"Boleh saya coba baju ini?","pants; trousers":"celana","Do you have these pants in a bigger size?":"Celana ini ada ukuran yang lebih besar?","I want to buy a pair of sneakers.":"Saya mau beli sepasang sepatu kets.","receipt (Taiwan's receipts double as lottery tickets!)":"struk (struk di Taiwan juga bisa untuk undian!)","Print the receipt? — Save it to my e-carrier, thanks.":"Struknya dicetak? — Simpan ke carrier elektronik saya saja, terima kasih.","to turn left":"belok kiri","Turn left at the next intersection and you're there.":"Belok kiri di persimpangan berikutnya, sudah sampai.","to turn right":"belok kanan","Driver, please turn right at the next light.":"Pak sopir, tolong belok kanan di lampu berikutnya.","Are there any good restaurants nearby?":"Ada restoran enak di dekat sini?","across from; opposite":"di seberang","The pharmacy is right across from the convenience store.":"Apoteknya tepat di seberang minimarket.","sad":"sedih","I was very sad to hear this news.":"Saya sangat sedih mendengar kabar ini.","angry; to get angry":"marah","Don't be angry—he didn't do it on purpose.":"Jangan marah, dia tidak sengaja kok.","nervous":"gugup","I have an interview tomorrow and I'm so nervous.":"Besok saya wawancara jadi sangat gugup.","afraid; scared":"takut","I'm terrified of cockroaches.":"Saya takut sekali sama kecoak.","bored; boring":"bosan; membosankan","It's boring at home—let's go out for a walk.":"Bosan di rumah, ayo keluar jalan-jalan.","interesting; fun":"menarik; seru","Learning Chinese is more fun than I expected.":"Belajar bahasa Mandarin lebih seru dari yang saya kira.","to make a phone call":"menelepon","I'll call you in a bit.":"Nanti saya telepon kamu.","to meet (in person)":"bertemu (langsung)","We haven't met in ages!":"Sudah lama sekali kita tidak bertemu!","to forget":"lupa","Oops, I forgot to bring my EasyCard.":"Aduh, saya lupa bawa kartu EasyCard.","to remember":"ingat","Remember to bring your passport tomorrow!":"Ingat bawa paspor besok ya!","to prepare":"mempersiapkan","I'm preparing for next week's exam.":"Saya sedang mempersiapkan ujian minggu depan.","to practice":"berlatih","I practice speaking Chinese ten minutes a day.":"Setiap hari saya berlatih berbicara bahasa Mandarin sepuluh menit.","to rest (read xiūxí in Taiwan)":"beristirahat (di Taiwan dibaca xiūxí)","We've walked all day—let's take a break.":"Sudah jalan seharian, ayo istirahat sebentar.","convenient":"praktis; nyaman","Transportation in Taipei is very convenient.":"Transportasi di Taipei sangat praktis.","This sofa is really comfortable to sit on.":"Sofa ini nyaman sekali kalau diduduki.","quiet":"tenang","You must keep quiet in the library.":"Di perpustakaan harus tetap tenang.","This restaurant is clean and tasty.":"Restoran ini bersih dan enak.","simple; easy":"sederhana; mudah","This dish is easy to make.":"Masakan ini mudah dibuat.","I used to live in Osaka.":"Dulu saya pernah tinggal di Osaka.","after; from now on":"setelah; mulai sekarang","Let's get bubble tea after class.":"Setelah kelas ayo beli teh boba.","right away":"segera","Wait for me—I'll be right there!":"Tunggu ya, saya segera datang!","already":"sudah","It's already midnight—go to bed!":"Sudah tengah malam, tidur sana!","cellphone":"ponsel","My computer has been acting weird lately.":"Akhir-akhir ini komputer saya sering aneh.","sunny day":"hari cerah","It's a rare sunny day—let's take a walk in the riverside park.":"Jarang-jarang cuaca cerah, ayo jalan-jalan di taman tepi sungai.","cloudy day":"hari mendung","It's cloudy today—it looks like it's about to rain.":"Hari ini mendung, sepertinya mau hujan.","The wind is so strong today my hat blew away.":"Hari ini anginnya kencang sekali sampai topi saya terbang.","There isn't a single cloud in the sky—what great weather.":"Langit tanpa awan sedikit pun, cuacanya bagus sekali.","to snow":"turun salju","It rarely snows in Taipei; you can only see snow on Hehuanshan.":"Di Taipei jarang turun salju, salju hanya bisa dilihat di Gunung Hehuan.","temperature (weather)":"suhu (cuaca)","It'll only be ten degrees tomorrow, so dress warmly.":"Besok cuma sepuluh derajat, pakai baju yang hangat ya.","east":"timur","The sun rises in the east.":"Matahari terbit di timur.","west":"barat","There's a famous noodle shop on the west side of the station.":"Di sebelah barat stasiun ada kedai mi yang terkenal.","south":"selatan","The weather in southern Taiwan is hotter than in the north.":"Cuaca di Taiwan bagian selatan lebih panas daripada di utara.","north":"utara","Drive north for an hour and you'll reach Keelung.":"Berkendara ke utara satu jam sampai di Keelung.","front; in front":"depan","The convenience store is just ahead—two minutes on foot.":"Minimarket ada tepat di depan, jalan kaki dua menit.","There's a small park behind my house.":"Di belakang rumah saya ada taman kecil.","It's too hot outside—let's go inside where there's AC.":"Di luar panas sekali, ayo masuk ke dalam yang ada AC.","It's raining outside—remember to bring an umbrella.":"Di luar sedang hujan, ingat bawa payung.","There's a great bubble tea shop next to the MRT station.":"Di sebelah stasiun MRT ada kedai teh boba yang enak.","middle; between":"di tengah; di antara","I'm sitting between the two of them.":"Saya duduk di antara mereka berdua.","downstairs":"lantai bawah","There's a convenience store right downstairs from my place—super convenient.":"Tepat di lantai bawah tempat saya ada minimarket, praktis sekali.","to attend class":"masuk kelas","I go to Chinese class every Saturday morning.":"Setiap Sabtu pagi saya masuk kelas bahasa Mandarin.","to finish class":"selesai kelas","After class, let's go get fried chicken together.":"Setelah kelas, ayo makan ayam goreng bareng.","exam; test":"ujian","There's an exam next week, so I need to prepare well.":"Minggu depan ada ujian jadi saya harus persiapan dengan baik.","grades; results":"nilai; hasil","My grades on this exam were much better than last time.":"Nilai ujian saya kali ini jauh lebih baik dari sebelumnya.","homework":"pekerjaan rumah","The homework the teacher assigned today is a bit much.":"PR yang diberikan guru hari ini agak banyak.","to graduate":"lulus (dari sekolah)","I came to Taiwan to work right after graduating from university.":"Begitu lulus kuliah saya langsung ke Taiwan untuk bekerja.","summer vacation":"liburan musim panas","Do you have any plans for summer vacation?":"Sudah ada rencana untuk liburan musim panas?","winter vacation":"liburan musim dingin","I want to go back to Japan to see my family during winter vacation.":"Saat liburan musim dingin saya ingin pulang ke Jepang menemui keluarga.","to ask for advice":"meminta pendapat; bertanya","Excuse me, may I ask you a question?":"Permisi, boleh saya bertanya satu hal?","to get sick":"jatuh sakit","He got sick and didn't come to work today.":"Dia sakit jadi hari ini tidak masuk kerja.","to get injured":"terluka; cedera","He got injured while playing basketball.":"Dia cedera saat main basket.","nurse":"perawat","The nurse asked me to wait outside for a moment.":"Perawat menyuruh saya menunggu di luar sebentar.","tooth":"gigi","My tooth hurts so much—I have to see a dentist.":"Gigi saya sakit sekali, harus ke dokter gigi.","I'm starving—let's go eat.":"Saya lapar sekali, ayo makan.","to take a day off":"mengambil libur sehari","I'm taking time off next week and want to visit Tainan.":"Minggu depan saya ambil libur, mau jalan-jalan ke Tainan.","to worry":"khawatir","My mom worries a lot about me living abroad alone.":"Ibu saya sangat khawatir saya tinggal sendirian di luar negeri.","to hope":"berharap","I hope it doesn't rain tomorrow.":"Saya berharap besok tidak hujan.","I think this place has the best beef noodles.":"Menurut saya mi daging sapi di sini paling enak.","to believe":"percaya","I believe you can definitely do it.":"Saya percaya kamu pasti bisa.","to be at ease; to relax":"tenang; lega","Don't worry—just leave this to me.":"Tenang saja, urusan ini serahkan pada saya.","to joke":"bercanda","Don't be mad—I was just joking.":"Jangan marah, saya cuma bercanda.","to participate":"ikut serta","Do you want to join this weekend's language exchange event?":"Kamu mau ikut acara pertukaran bahasa akhir pekan ini?","to invite":"mengundang","My coworker invited me to have dinner at his place.":"Rekan kerja saya mengundang saya makan malam di rumahnya.","to choose":"memilih","There are too many flavors—I don't know which to choose.":"Rasanya terlalu banyak, saya bingung mau pilih yang mana.","to give (a gift); to see someone off":"memberi (hadiah); mengantar","For my friend's birthday, I gave her a box of pineapple cakes.":"Untuk ulang tahun teman, saya memberinya sekotak kue nanas.","to return (something)":"mengembalikan (sesuatu)","I finished this book—I'll return it to you tomorrow.":"Buku ini sudah selesai saya baca, besok saya kembalikan.","to borrow; to lend":"meminjam; meminjamkan","I forgot to bring a pen—could you lend me one?":"Saya lupa bawa pulpen, boleh pinjam satu?","to change; to exchange":"menukar","This shirt is too small—I'd like to exchange it for a bigger one.":"Baju ini terlalu kecil, saya mau tukar dengan ukuran lebih besar.","to repair":"memperbaiki","The AC broke; the landlord said he'll get someone to fix it tomorrow.":"AC-nya rusak, pemilik kos bilang besok akan panggil orang untuk memperbaikinya.","to depart":"berangkat","We're leaving for Kenting at seven tomorrow morning.":"Besok jam tujuh pagi kita berangkat ke Kenting.","to pick someone up; to answer (a call)":"menjemput; menerima (telepon)","I'm going to the airport this afternoon to pick up a friend.":"Sore ini saya ke bandara menjemput teman.","to mail; to send":"mengirim (pos)","I want to mail a package to Japan—how do I get to the post office?":"Saya mau kirim paket ke Jepang, bagaimana cara ke kantor pos?","to receive":"menerima","I just received your message.":"Saya baru saja menerima pesanmu.","to throw away; to lose":"membuang; menghilangkan","Are you going to throw away these old clothes?":"Baju-baju lama ini mau kamu buang?","to take care of":"merawat; mengurus","Thank you for taking care of me during this time.":"Terima kasih sudah mengurus saya selama ini.","to make an appointment; to ask out":"membuat janji; mengajak","We agreed to meet at the MRT station at two on Saturday afternoon.":"Kami berjanji bertemu di stasiun MRT jam dua siang Sabtu.","key":"kunci","Oh no, I left my keys at home.":"Gawat, kunci saya tertinggal di rumah.","credit card":"kartu kredit","Excuse me, can I pay by credit card?":"Permisi, boleh bayar pakai kartu kredit?","package; parcel":"paket","Your package arrived; it's at the convenience store downstairs.":"Paketmu sudah datang, ada di minimarket lantai bawah.","gift":"hadiah","This is a small gift I brought back from Japan.":"Ini hadiah kecil yang saya bawa dari Jepang.","platform (station)":"peron (stasiun)","The train to Taichung is on platform two.":"Kereta ke Taichung ada di peron dua.","train/bus ticket":"tiket kereta/bus","HSR tickets for long weekends are hard to get—book early.":"Tiket kereta cepat saat libur panjang sulit didapat, pesan lebih awal.","driver's license":"SIM","I want to get a scooter license—riding is more convenient in Taiwan.":"Saya mau bikin SIM motor, di Taiwan naik motor lebih praktis.","address":"alamat","Please write your address here.":"Silakan tulis alamat Anda di sini.","elevator":"lift","The elevator is broken, so we have to take the stairs.":"Liftnya rusak, jadi harus lewat tangga.","stairs":"tangga","For my health, I take the stairs up every day.":"Demi kesehatan, setiap hari saya naik lewat tangga.","refrigerator":"kulkas","There's still fruit from yesterday in the fridge.":"Di kulkas masih ada buah dari kemarin.","washing machine":"mesin cuci","The room I rent doesn't have a washing machine.":"Kamar yang saya sewa tidak ada mesin cuci.","television":"televisi","I rarely watch TV; I watch videos on my phone instead.":"Saya jarang menonton TV, lebih sering menonton video di ponsel.","Your cat is way too cute!":"Kucingmu lucu banget!","smart; clever":"pintar","This kid is really smart and learns everything quickly.":"Anak ini benar-benar pintar, belajar apa pun cepat.","serious; earnest":"serius; sungguh-sungguh","He works very earnestly, and everyone likes him.":"Dia bekerja dengan sungguh-sungguh, semua orang menyukainya.","hardworking; to work hard":"rajin; berusaha keras","To pass the proficiency test, I study hard every day.":"Agar lulus tes kemahiran, setiap hari saya belajar dengan giat.","healthy":"sehat","Drinking less bubble tea is healthier for you.":"Mengurangi minum teh boba lebih sehat untukmu.","dangerous":"berbahaya","Riding a scooter without a helmet is very dangerous.":"Naik motor tanpa helm sangat berbahaya.","safe":"aman","In Taiwan it's safe to walk alone even at night.":"Di Taiwan, berjalan sendirian di malam hari pun aman.","troublesome; to trouble someone":"merepotkan; merepotkan orang","Applying for a visa is a bit of a hassle—you need lots of documents.":"Mengurus visa agak merepotkan, perlu banyak dokumen.","strange; weird":"aneh","Weird—where did my EasyCard go?":"Aneh, ke mana kartu EasyCard saya?","young":"muda","Many young people like living downtown.":"Banyak anak muda suka tinggal di pusat kota.","often":"sering","I often have lunch at the buffet-style eatery near my office.":"Saya sering makan siang di kedai prasmanan dekat kantor.","sometimes":"kadang-kadang","Sometimes I cook for myself, and sometimes I order delivery.":"Kadang saya masak sendiri, kadang pesan antar.","suddenly":"tiba-tiba","It was sunny just now, and suddenly it started pouring.":"Tadi masih cerah, tiba-tiba hujan deras.","continuously; all along":"terus-menerus; dari tadi","He has been waiting for your call the whole time.":"Dia terus menunggu teleponmu dari tadi.","almost; about the same":"hampir; kurang lebih","I've been in Taiwan for about two years.":"Saya sudah kurang lebih dua tahun di Taiwan.","What did you just say? I didn't hear clearly.":"Kamu tadi bilang apa? Saya kurang jelas mendengarnya.","later; afterwards":"kemudian; setelahnya","We planned to go to the night market, but later it rained so we didn't.":"Kami berencana ke pasar malam, tapi kemudian hujan jadi batal.","menu":"menu","Excuse me, could I see the menu?":"Permisi, boleh lihat menunya?","taste; smell":"rasa; aroma","The flavor of this shop's braised snacks is totally different from Japan's.":"Rasa makanan rebusan kedai ini benar-benar beda dengan di Jepang.","sweet":"manis","I always order bubble tea half-sweet; full sugar is too sweet.":"Saya selalu pesan teh boba setengah gula, gula penuh terlalu manis.","sour":"asam","This lemon juice is so sour—could you add a little sugar?":"Jus lemon ini asam sekali, bisa tambah sedikit gula?","full (after eating)":"kenyang","I'm so full I don't even need dinner.":"Saya kenyang sekali sampai tidak perlu makan malam.","hungry":"lapar","I'm starving—let's grab something to eat first.":"Saya lapar sekali, ayo cari makan dulu.","thirsty":"haus","Hiking made me so thirsty—I'm going to buy a bottle of water.":"Mendaki membuat saya haus sekali, saya mau beli sebotol air.","to ride (a bike/scooter)":"mengendarai (sepeda/motor)","I ride my scooter to work every day.":"Setiap hari saya naik motor ke tempat kerja.","to drive a car":"menyetir mobil","This weekend we're driving to Yilan for fun.":"Akhir pekan ini kami menyetir ke Yilan untuk jalan-jalan.","gas station":"SPBU","There's a gas station ahead—let's fill up first.":"Di depan ada SPBU, kita isi bensin dulu.","traffic light":"lampu lalu lintas","Turn right at the traffic light and you're there.":"Belok kanan di lampu lalu lintas, sudah sampai.","route":"rute","This bus route passes by the night market.":"Rute bus ini melewati pasar malam.","to transfer (trains/buses)":"berpindah (kereta/bus)","To get to Tamsui, transfer at Taipei Main Station.":"Untuk ke Tamsui, pindah kereta di Stasiun Utama Taipei.","timetable":"jadwal","Check the train timetable first.":"Cek dulu jadwal keretanya.","to be delayed (train, flight)":"terlambat; delay (kereta, penerbangan)","The train was delayed twenty minutes today.":"Hari ini keretanya delay dua puluh menit.","to be stuck in traffic":"terjebak macet","The highway always jams at rush hour.":"Jalan tol selalu macet saat jam sibuk.","passport":"paspor","Check your passport before going abroad.":"Periksa paspor sebelum pergi ke luar negeri.","visa":"visa","You need to get a visa before working in Japan.":"Kamu harus mengurus visa sebelum bekerja di Jepang.","scenery":"pemandangan","The scenery in Hualien is really beautiful.":"Pemandangan di Hualien benar-benar indah.","local specialty":"makanan/produk khas daerah","Pineapple cakes are a famous Taiwanese specialty.":"Kue nanas adalah oleh-oleh khas Taiwan yang terkenal.","souvenir":"oleh-oleh","I want to buy some souvenirs for my friends.":"Saya mau beli oleh-oleh untuk teman-teman.","tour guide":"pemandu wisata","The tour guide took us to many places.":"Pemandu wisata mengajak kami ke banyak tempat.","hot spring":"pemandian air panas","Nothing beats soaking in a hot spring in winter.":"Tidak ada yang mengalahkan berendam air panas di musim dingin.","to type":"mengetik","He types very fast.":"Dia mengetik dengan sangat cepat.","to reply":"membalas","I've been too busy to reply to his message.":"Saya terlalu sibuk jadi belum membalas pesannya.","to be marked as read (message)":"sudah dibaca (pesan)","He read my message but didn't reply—I'm a bit sad.":"Dia sudah membaca pesan saya tapi tidak membalas, saya agak sedih.","sticker (in messaging apps)":"stiker (di aplikasi pesan)","This sticker is so cute—where did you buy it?":"Stiker ini lucu sekali, kamu beli di mana?","to video call":"panggilan video","I video call my family every week.":"Setiap minggu saya video call dengan keluarga.","charger":"charger","Oh no, I forgot to bring my charger.":"Aduh, saya lupa bawa charger.","Bluetooth":"Bluetooth","My earphones connect to my phone via Bluetooth.":"Earphone saya terhubung ke ponsel lewat Bluetooth.","hot pot":"hot pot; steamboat","Cold weather is perfect for hot pot.":"Cuaca dingin paling pas untuk makan hot pot.","barbecue; grilled food":"barbeku; makanan panggang","Everyone has barbecue during the Mid-Autumn Festival.":"Saat Festival Pertengahan Musim Gugur, semua orang barbeku.","boxed lunch; bento":"nasi kotak; bento","I often buy a pork chop bento for lunch.":"Saya sering beli nasi kotak dengan chop babi untuk makan siang.","drink; beverage":"minuman","Want me to grab you a drink while I'm at it?":"Sekalian saya belikan minuman untukmu, mau?","Have you decided? Let's order.":"Sudah pilih? Ayo pesan.","free of charge":"gratis","This place offers free soup refills.":"Tempat ini menyediakan tambah kuah gratis.","to treat; on the house":"traktir; dari pihak toko","The owner said this side dish is on the house.":"Pemiliknya bilang lauk ini gratis dari toko.","self-serve cafeteria; buffet":"kantin prasmanan; bufet","The cafeteria near my office is cheap and tasty.":"Kantin prasmanan dekat kantor saya murah dan enak.","late-night snack":"camilan tengah malam","Let's grab a late-night snack after overtime!":"Setelah lembur, ayo cari makan tengah malam!","dessert":"hidangan penutup","There's always room for dessert after a meal.":"Setelah makan selalu ada ruang untuk hidangan penutup.","cookie; cracker":"biskuit; kue kering","All the cookies in the office got eaten.":"Biskuit di kantor sudah habis dimakan semua.","chocolate":"cokelat","He gave me a box of chocolates on Valentine's Day.":"Saat Hari Valentine dia memberi saya sekotak cokelat.","Summer calls for ice cream!":"Musim panas paling pas makan es krim!","to feel dizzy":"merasa pusing","I feel a bit dizzy and want to sit down and rest.":"Saya agak pusing, mau duduk istirahat sebentar.","to feel nauseous":"merasa mual","The boat ride made me feel so nauseous.":"Naik perahu membuat saya sangat mual.","to be allergic":"alergi","I'm allergic to seafood, so I can't eat shrimp.":"Saya alergi makanan laut jadi tidak bisa makan udang.","to sneeze":"bersin","He's been sneezing nonstop since a moment ago.":"Dari tadi dia bersin terus-menerus.","to cough":"batuk","I've been coughing for a week and it's still not better.":"Sudah seminggu saya batuk dan belum sembuh juga.","to have a runny nose":"pilek; ingusan","My nose keeps running—it might be allergies.":"Hidung saya terus meler, mungkin alergi.","to see a dentist":"ke dokter gigi","I'm going to the dentist tomorrow afternoon.":"Besok sore saya ke dokter gigi.","body temperature":"suhu tubuh","The nurse took my temperature first.":"Perawat mengukur suhu tubuh saya dulu.","to cook (a meal)":"memasak","I like cooking for myself on weekends.":"Saya suka memasak sendiri saat akhir pekan.","to wash the dishes":"mencuci piring","It's your turn to do the dishes today.":"Hari ini giliranmu mencuci piring.","to wipe":"mengelap","The table is dirty—let me wipe it.":"Mejanya kotor, biar saya lap.","to sweep":"menyapu","The floor is covered in hair—sweep it up.":"Lantainya penuh rambut, sapu ya.","to mop the floor":"mengepel lantai","I'll mop after I finish sweeping.":"Setelah menyapu saya akan mengepel.","to hang laundry":"menjemur cucian","It's about to rain—let's hang the laundry inside.":"Sebentar lagi hujan, ayo jemur cucian di dalam.","to tidy up; to organize":"merapikan; menata","You have to organize your things before moving.":"Sebelum pindah kamu harus menata barang-barang.","to clean up; to pack up":"membereskan","Remember to clear the table after eating.":"Setelah makan ingat membereskan meja.","to pay":"membayar","I'll pay today—you treated last time.":"Hari ini saya yang bayar, kemarin kan kamu yang traktir.","to give change":"memberi kembalian","Excuse me, I think you gave me the wrong change.":"Permisi, sepertinya kembaliannya salah.","small change; coins":"uang receh; koin","I don't have change—can I pay by card?":"Saya tidak punya uang receh, boleh bayar pakai kartu?","banknote; bill":"uang kertas","This machine doesn't accept 1000-dollar bills.":"Mesin ini tidak menerima uang 1000 dolar.","to raise prices":"menaikkan harga","This shop's braised pork rice went up in price again.":"Nasi babi kecap kedai ini naik harga lagi.","to give a discount":"memberi diskon","These shoes are 20% off right now.":"Sepatu ini sedang diskon 20%.","free shipping":"gratis ongkir","Spend 500 or more and shipping is free.":"Belanja 500 atau lebih, ongkirnya gratis.","to be out of stock":"stok habis","Sorry, this color is out of stock.":"Maaf, warna ini stoknya habis.","to refund":"mengembalikan uang; refund","The item was broken, so the shop agreed to refund me.":"Barangnya rusak, jadi toko setuju me-refund uang saya.","date (romantic)":"kencan","They went to a movie on their first date.":"Pada kencan pertama mereka menonton film.","to get married":"menikah","They've dated five years and are getting married next year.":"Mereka sudah pacaran lima tahun dan tahun depan menikah.","boyfriend":"pacar (laki-laki)","Her boyfriend is a great cook.":"Pacar dia pandai memasak.","girlfriend":"pacar (perempuan)","I want to bring my girlfriend home to meet my parents.":"Saya ingin membawa pacar saya ke rumah menemui orang tua.","married couple":"pasangan suami istri","This couple opened a breakfast shop together.":"Pasangan ini bersama-sama membuka kedai sarapan.","to break up":"putus","I heard they broke up last month.":"Katanya bulan lalu mereka putus.","to be homesick":"rindu kampung halaman","I get especially homesick around Lunar New Year.":"Menjelang Tahun Baru Imlek saya sangat rindu kampung halaman.","very; extremely":"sangat; amat","This movie is extremely good.":"Film ini bagus sekali.","especially":"terutama","Tainan's street food is especially famous.":"Jajanan Tainan terutama sangat terkenal.","relatively; comparatively":"relatif; agak","Evening high-speed rail tickets are relatively cheap.":"Tiket kereta cepat malam hari relatif murah.","even more":"lebih lagi","Mangoes taste even better in summer.":"Mangga terasa lebih enak lagi di musim panas.","the most":"paling","Fried chicken cutlet is my favorite at the night market.":"Di pasar malam saya paling suka ayam goreng fillet.","too (excessively)":"terlalu","This jacket is too expensive—I can't afford it.":"Jaket ini terlalu mahal, saya tidak sanggup beli.","really":"sungguh; benar-benar","This shop's bubble tea is really good.":"Teh boba kedai ini benar-benar enak.","to seem; as if":"sepertinya; seakan","It seems to be raining outside—take an umbrella.":"Sepertinya di luar hujan, bawa payung.","should; ought to":"seharusnya; sebaiknya","You have a cold—you should sleep early.":"Kamu sedang flu, sebaiknya tidur lebih awal.","maybe; possibly":"mungkin","He may have already left work.":"Mungkin dia sudah pulang kerja.","of course":"tentu saja","'Are you coming along?' 'Of course!'":"\"Kamu ikut?\" \"Tentu saja!\"","definitely; surely":"pasti","If you come to Taiwan, I'll definitely take you to a night market.":"Kalau kamu datang ke Taiwan, saya pasti akan mengajakmu ke pasar malam.","to review (lessons)":"mengulang pelajaran","You should review well before the exam.":"Sebelum ujian sebaiknya kamu mengulang pelajaran dengan baik.","to preview (lessons)":"mempelajari materi terlebih dulu","The teacher asked us to preview Lesson 5 first.":"Guru menyuruh kami mempelajari Pelajaran 5 terlebih dulu.","to sign up; to register":"mendaftar","I signed up for next month's Chinese proficiency test.":"Saya sudah mendaftar tes kemahiran bahasa Mandarin bulan depan.","to leave early (work/school)":"pulang lebih awal (kerja/sekolah)","I'm not feeling well today and want to ask my manager to leave early.":"Hari ini saya kurang enak badan, mau minta izin atasan untuk pulang lebih awal.","to celebrate":"merayakan","Let's go have a feast to celebrate your promotion!":"Ayo makan enak untuk merayakan promosimu!","to visit (someone)":"mengunjungi (seseorang)","We're visiting Grandpa and Grandma for Lunar New Year.":"Saat Imlek kami mengunjungi kakek dan nenek.","to take (transport)":"naik (transportasi)","to give someone a ride":"memberi tumpangan","It's raining—let me give you a ride home on my scooter.":"Hujan nih, biar saya antar kamu pulang naik motor.","to accompany":"menemani","Can you come with me to the doctor tomorrow?":"Besok bisa temani saya ke dokter?","to wake someone up":"membangunkan","Remember to wake me up at seven tomorrow.":"Besok jam tujuh ingat bangunkan saya ya.","to urge; to rush someone":"mendesak; menyuruh cepat","Stop rushing me—I'm almost done!":"Jangan buru-buru terus, sebentar lagi selesai!","toilet paper; tissue":"tisu toilet; tisu","The bathroom is out of toilet paper—grab me a pack.":"Tisu di kamar mandi habis, ambilkan saya satu bungkus.","to deliver food; food delivery":"mengantar makanan; pesan-antar makanan","I'm feeling lazy today—let's order delivery.":"Hari ini saya malas, ayo pesan antar makanan saja.","slippers; flip-flops":"sandal; sandal jepit","In Taiwan, many people go out in flip-flops.":"Di Taiwan, banyak orang keluar rumah pakai sandal jepit.","to brush one's teeth":"menyikat gigi","You must brush your teeth before bed.":"Sebelum tidur harus menyikat gigi.","towel":"handuk","Wipe your sweat with a towel after exercising.":"Setelah olahraga lap keringat dengan handuk.","quilt; comforter":"selimut","It's getting cold—time to bring out the thick quilt.":"Cuaca mulai dingin, saatnya keluarkan selimut tebal.","toothbrush":"sikat gigi","My toothbrush is old—time to get a new one.":"Sikat gigi saya sudah usang, saatnya beli yang baru.","raincoat":"jas hujan","Wear a raincoat when it rains while riding a scooter.":"Kalau hujan saat naik motor, pakai jas hujan.","pillow":"bantal","This pillow is too high—I can't get used to it.":"Bantal ini terlalu tinggi, saya tidak terbiasa.","meeting":"rapat","For the three o'clock meeting, could you prepare the slides for me first?":"Untuk rapat jam tiga, bisa siapkan slide-nya untuk saya dulu?","My colleagues often invite me out for a late-night snack after work.":"Rekan-rekan kerja sering mengajak saya makan tengah malam sepulang kerja.","to ask for leave":"meminta izin/cuti","I want to take leave tomorrow to see a doctor, so I need to tell my manager first.":"Besok saya mau izin ke dokter, jadi harus memberitahu atasan dulu.","on time; punctual":"tepat waktu","Taiwan's high-speed rail is almost always on time and rarely delayed.":"Kereta cepat Taiwan hampir selalu tepat waktu dan jarang delay.","sales performance":"kinerja penjualan","This quarter's sales performance beat the target, so the boss decided to give out bonuses.":"Kinerja penjualan kuartal ini melampaui target, jadi bos memutuskan memberi bonus.","position; post":"posisi; jabatan","This position requires frequent business trips—is that acceptable to you?":"Posisi ini sering dinas ke luar kota, apakah kamu bisa menerimanya?","order (purchase)":"pesanan","There are especially many orders this month, and everyone is swamped.":"Bulan ini pesanan sangat banyak, semua orang kewalahan.","to develop":"mengembangkan","The company is developing a Chinese-learning app for foreigners.":"Perusahaan sedang mengembangkan aplikasi belajar bahasa Mandarin untuk orang asing.","to train":"melatih; memberi pelatihan","New hires receive basic training in their first week.":"Karyawan baru mendapat pelatihan dasar di minggu pertama.","attendance (at work)":"kehadiran (kerja)","Company policy says attendance records are calculated by the clock-in system.":"Menurut aturan perusahaan, catatan kehadiran dihitung lewat sistem absen.","society":"masyarakat","When I first entered society, I knew nothing and made plenty of blunders.":"Saat pertama terjun ke masyarakat kerja, saya tidak tahu apa-apa dan banyak salah.","economy":"ekonomi","The economy isn't great lately, so many people are reluctant to change jobs.":"Belakangan ekonomi kurang baik, jadi banyak orang enggan pindah kerja.","politics":"politik","When chatting with people you don't know well, it's best not to talk politics.":"Saat mengobrol dengan orang yang belum akrab, sebaiknya jangan bahas politik.","law":"hukum","If you have questions before signing, ask a friend who knows the law.":"Kalau ada pertanyaan sebelum tanda tangan, tanyakan pada teman yang paham hukum.","election":"pemilu","During Taiwan's elections, candidates' flags are everywhere on the streets.":"Saat pemilu di Taiwan, bendera para kandidat ada di mana-mana di jalan.","tax":"pajak","May is tax-filing season every year, so don't forget to pay your taxes.":"Setiap Mei adalah musim lapor pajak, jangan lupa bayar pajak.","population":"populasi; penduduk","Taipei has a large population, and the MRT is packed during rush hour.":"Populasi Taipei besar, MRT penuh sesak saat jam sibuk.","culture":"budaya","Night-market culture is one of the things foreigners most want to experience in Taiwan.":"Budaya pasar malam adalah salah satu hal yang paling ingin dialami orang asing di Taiwan.","tradition; traditional":"tradisi; tradisional","Gathering around the hot pot at New Year is a tradition Taiwanese people value.":"Berkumpul mengelilingi hot pot saat Tahun Baru adalah tradisi yang dijunjung orang Taiwan.","environmental protection":"pelestarian lingkungan","For the sake of the environment, many people now bring their own cups when buying drinks.":"Demi lingkungan, kini banyak orang membawa gelas sendiri saat membeli minuman.","nervous; tense":"gugup; tegang","Presenting in Chinese for the first time, I was so nervous my hands kept shaking.":"Presentasi dalam bahasa Mandarin untuk pertama kalinya, saya gugup sampai tangan gemetar.","excited":"bersemangat; gembira","When he heard he could be posted to Taiwan, he was so excited he couldn't sleep all night.":"Mendengar bisa ditugaskan ke Taiwan, dia sangat bersemangat sampai semalaman tak bisa tidur.","to feel wronged":"merasa disalahkan; merasa tak adil","It clearly wasn't his fault, yet the manager scolded him, and he felt wronged.":"Jelas-jelas bukan salahnya, tapi atasan memarahinya, dia merasa tak adil.","to be reluctant to part with":"berat hati meninggalkan","After living in Taiwan for five years, I really can't bear to leave and go home.":"Setelah lima tahun tinggal di Taiwan, saya benar-benar berat hati untuk pulang.","to be deeply grateful":"sangat berterima kasih","When I first came to Taiwan, my landlord helped me a lot, and I'm still grateful.":"Waktu baru datang ke Taiwan, pemilik kos banyak membantu saya, dan saya masih berterima kasih.","worry; trouble":"kekhawatiran; kegundahan","Money worries are what keep you up at night the most.":"Masalah uang adalah yang paling membuat orang tak bisa tidur.","to look forward to":"menantikan","I'm really looking forward to this company trip—I heard we're going to Kenting.":"Saya sangat menantikan wisata perusahaan kali ini, katanya ke Kenting.","to cherish; to treasure":"menghargai; menyayangi","Making such good friends abroad is something to truly cherish.":"Mendapat teman sebaik itu di luar negeri adalah hal yang patut disyukuri.","to feel sorry for; to ache for":"iba; kasihan","Seeing him work overtime until midnight every day, his mother aches for him.":"Melihat dia lembur sampai tengah malam setiap hari, ibunya merasa iba.","to hesitate":"ragu-ragu","I hesitated over this coat for a long time but ended up buying it.":"Saya ragu-ragu lama sekali soal mantel ini tapi akhirnya tetap membelinya.","viewpoint; perspective":"sudut pandang","From the boss's viewpoint, doing it this way really does save money.":"Dari sudut pandang bos, cara ini memang lebih menghemat uang.","standpoint; stance":"posisi; pendirian","Thinking from the client's standpoint, it's normal for them to make such demands.":"Kalau dilihat dari posisi klien, wajar mereka mengajukan permintaan seperti itu.","to approve; to be in favor":"menyetujui; mendukung","I'm in favor of switching to remote work—it saves commuting time.":"Saya setuju beralih ke kerja jarak jauh, menghemat waktu perjalanan.","to question; to challenge":"mempertanyakan; menyanggah","He questioned at the meeting whether this figure had been miscalculated.":"Dalam rapat, dia mempertanyakan apakah angka ini salah hitung.","to judge; to determine":"menilai; menentukan","How to handle this matter is left to your own judgment.":"Bagaimana menangani hal ini terserah pada penilaianmu sendiri.","comment; review":"ulasan; komentar","Online reviews of this movie are polarized—some love it, some trash it.":"Ulasan film ini di internet terbelah dua, ada yang memuji ada yang mencela.","to analyze":"menganalisis","Analyze the pros and cons of these two plans before deciding.":"Analisis dulu kelebihan dan kekurangan kedua rencana ini sebelum memutuskan.","to supplement; to add":"menambahkan; melengkapi","I agree with everything he just said; I only want to add one point.":"Saya setuju dengan semua yang dia katakan tadi, saya hanya ingin menambahkan satu poin.","to consider":"mempertimbangkan","I'm still considering whether to take this job.":"Saya masih mempertimbangkan apakah akan mengambil pekerjaan ini.","to handle; to deal with":"menangani; mengurus","I'll handle the customer complaint—you go do something else first.":"Keluhan pelanggan biar saya yang tangani, kamu urus hal lain dulu.","to arrange":"mengatur; menjadwalkan","I've arranged for you to meet the client next Tuesday.":"Saya sudah menjadwalkan kamu bertemu klien Selasa depan.","to grasp; to master":"menguasai","Once you grasp a few common sentence patterns, ordering food isn't hard.":"Begitu menguasai beberapa pola kalimat umum, memesan makanan tidak sulit.","to accumulate":"mengumpulkan; menumpuk","Experience builds up slowly—don't rush.":"Pengalaman terkumpul sedikit demi sedikit, jangan terburu-buru.","to cultivate; to develop":"menumbuhkan; membina","Cultivating a reading habit from childhood really helps with learning languages.":"Menumbuhkan kebiasaan membaca sejak kecil sangat membantu dalam belajar bahasa.","to overcome":"mengatasi","At first I was afraid to speak Chinese, but I gradually got over it.":"Awalnya saya takut berbicara bahasa Mandarin, tapi lama-lama bisa mengatasinya.","to avoid":"menghindari","To avoid traffic, I always leave half an hour early.":"Untuk menghindari macet, saya selalu berangkat setengah jam lebih awal.","to overlook; to neglect":"mengabaikan","When you're busy with work, it's easy to neglect your own health.":"Saat sibuk bekerja, mudah sekali mengabaikan kesehatan sendiri.","to maintain; to keep":"mempertahankan; menjaga","Even after changing jobs, I still want to maintain my exercise habit.":"Meski sudah pindah kerja, saya tetap ingin menjaga kebiasaan berolahraga.","to achieve; to reach":"mencapai","After several discussions, both sides finally reached a consensus.":"Setelah beberapa kali berdiskusi, kedua pihak akhirnya mencapai kesepakatan.","to face; to confront":"menghadapi","No matter how hard the problem, you have to face it—running away is useless.":"Sesulit apa pun masalahnya, kamu harus menghadapinya, lari tidak ada gunanya.","to bear; to take on":"menanggung; memikul","We made this decision together, so we should bear the responsibility together.":"Keputusan ini kita buat bersama, jadi kita harus menanggung tanggung jawabnya bersama.","proactive; positive":"proaktif; positif","He's very proactive at work and takes the initiative on everything.":"Dia sangat proaktif dalam bekerja dan selalu berinisiatif dalam segala hal.","passive; negative":"pasif; negatif","He has consistently had a passive attitude toward this plan.":"Dia selalu bersikap negatif terhadap rencana ini.","cautious; careful":"hati-hati; berhati-hati","You must be more cautious when signing a big contract like this.":"Menandatangani kontrak besar seperti ini harus lebih berhati-hati.","optimistic":"optimis","Even though things aren't going well, she stays optimistic.":"Meskipun keadaan tidak lancar, dia tetap optimis.","pessimistic":"pesimis","Don't be so pessimistic—things won't necessarily turn out that bad.":"Jangan terlalu pesimis, keadaannya belum tentu seburuk itu.","active; on one's own initiative":"aktif; atas inisiatif sendiri","If there's something you don't understand, ask on your own initiative—don't be shy.":"Kalau ada yang tidak dimengerti, tanyalah atas inisiatif sendiri, jangan malu.","passive":"pasif","He's rather passive by nature, so others usually have to speak up first.":"Sifatnya cenderung pasif, jadi biasanya orang lain yang harus bicara duluan.","obvious; clear":"jelas; nyata","After using this method, the effect was very obvious.":"Setelah memakai metode ini, hasilnya sangat jelas.","complicated; complex":"rumit; kompleks","The application process is a bit complicated—I'll walk you through it step by step.":"Proses pendaftarannya agak rumit, biar saya pandu langkah demi langkah.","simple; pure":"sederhana; murni","The matter is actually quite simple—you're overthinking it.":"Masalahnya sebenarnya sederhana, kamu terlalu banyak berpikir.","casually; whatever":"terserah; sembarang","Anything's fine to eat—you decide, I'm easy.":"Makan apa saja boleh, kamu putuskan, saya terserah.","Halfway through the meeting, he suddenly said he was quitting.":"Di tengah rapat, dia tiba-tiba bilang mau berhenti kerja.","gradually":"lambat laun; perlahan-lahan","After living here a year, I gradually got used to life in Taiwan.":"Setelah setahun tinggal di sini, saya perlahan-lahan terbiasa dengan hidup di Taiwan.","specially; on purpose (for a reason)":"khusus; sengaja (untuk suatu tujuan)","He came all the way up from Kaohsiung to Taipei just to celebrate my birthday.":"Dia jauh-jauh datang dari Kaohsiung ke Taipei hanya untuk merayakan ulang tahunku.","it's a deal; that's settled":"sepakat begitu; sudah diputuskan","We'll go to Tainan together next month—it's a deal!":"Bulan depan kita pergi ke Tainan bareng ya—sepakat!","in a total mess":"berantakan total","The room is a total mess—tidy it up quickly before the guests arrive.":"Kamarnya berantakan total—cepat rapikan sebelum tamu datang.","so-so; sloppy":"biasa saja; asal-asalan","\"Your Chinese is great!\" \"Not really, just so-so.\"":"\"Bahasa Mandarinmu bagus banget!\" \"Enggak juga, biasa saja kok.\"","exactly the same; identical":"sama persis; identik","These two bags look exactly the same, but the prices are very different.":"Kedua tas ini terlihat sama persis, tapi harganya sangat berbeda.","to give up halfway":"menyerah di tengah jalan","With languages, the worst thing is giving up halfway—you must keep at it.":"Dalam belajar bahasa, yang paling buruk adalah menyerah di tengah jalan—harus tekun terus.","to kill two birds with one stone":"sekali mendayung dua tiga pulau terlampaui","Walking to work saves money and gives you exercise—killing two birds with one stone.":"Jalan kaki ke kantor hemat uang sekaligus olahraga—sekali mendayung dua tiga pulau terlampaui.","to go all out; to give it one's all":"berjuang sekuat tenaga; mengerahkan segalanya","I will definitely give it my all in this competition.":"Dalam kompetisi ini aku pasti akan berjuang sekuat tenaga.","although":"meskipun","Although the work is tiring, I really like my coworkers.":"Meskipun pekerjaannya melelahkan, aku sangat suka rekan-rekan kerjaku.","but; however":"tapi; namun","The stuff at this shop is good, but it's a little pricey.":"Barang di toko ini bagus, tapi agak mahal.","therefore; as a result":"oleh karena itu; akibatnya","His Chinese improved fast, and as a result he was quickly promoted.":"Bahasa Mandarinnya cepat meningkat, akibatnya dia cepat dipromosikan.","and so; thereupon":"maka; lalu","It rained heavily that day, so we canceled our outing plan.":"Hari itu hujan deras, maka kami membatalkan rencana jalan-jalan.","since; now that":"karena sudah; berhubung","Since you're already here, stay and have a meal with us.":"Berhubung kamu sudah di sini, tinggallah dan makan bersama kami.","otherwise; or else":"kalau tidak; jika tidak","Leave early, otherwise you'll definitely be late.":"Berangkat lebih awal, kalau tidak kamu pasti akan terlambat.","even; to the point that":"sampai-sampai; bahkan","He was so busy he didn't even eat lunch—he even forgot to drink water.":"Dia sibuk sampai-sampai tidak makan siang—bahkan lupa minum air.","on the contrary; instead":"sebaliknya; malah","After taking the medicine I didn't get better—on the contrary, I felt worse.":"Setelah minum obat aku tidak membaik—sebaliknya malah terasa lebih parah.","volunteer":"relawan","She volunteers at the animal shelter every weekend.":"Setiap akhir pekan dia menjadi relawan di penampungan hewan.","to donate money":"menyumbang uang","Many people donated money for the disaster area, hoping to help.":"Banyak orang menyumbang uang untuk daerah bencana, berharap bisa membantu.","poor; poverty":"miskin; kemiskinan","This organization is dedicated to helping poor families.":"Organisasi ini berdedikasi membantu keluarga miskin.","live streaming":"siaran langsung; live streaming","This shop does a live stream every night to sell fruit.":"Toko ini setiap malam melakukan siaran langsung untuk menjual buah.","post (social media)":"unggahan; postingan","Her post yesterday was shared by a lot of people.":"Unggahannya kemarin dibagikan oleh banyak orang.","to like (a post)":"menyukai; memberi like","If you like this video, remember to give it a like.":"Kalau suka video ini, jangan lupa beri like.","to leave a comment":"meninggalkan komentar","If you have any questions, leave a comment below and ask me.":"Kalau ada pertanyaan, tinggalkan komentar di bawah dan tanyakan padaku.","to block":"memblokir","He kept sending ads, so I had no choice but to block him.":"Dia terus mengirim iklan, jadi terpaksa aku memblokirnya.","virus":"virus","Don't click random links—your computer might get a virus.":"Jangan sembarangan klik tautan—komputermu bisa kena virus.","social media; online community":"media sosial; komunitas daring","Nowadays many small shops rely on social media to promote themselves.":"Sekarang banyak toko kecil mengandalkan media sosial untuk berpromosi.","platform":"platform","This platform lets creators earn a bit of income.":"Platform ini memungkinkan kreator memperoleh sedikit penghasilan.","to take a screenshot":"mengambil tangkapan layar","Take a screenshot of the conversation and send it to me so I can look.":"Ambil tangkapan layar percakapannya lalu kirim ke aku supaya bisa kulihat.","to follow (an account)":"mengikuti; follow","I follow several accounts that introduce Taiwanese food.":"Aku mengikuti beberapa akun yang memperkenalkan kuliner Taiwan.","smart (device)":"pintar; cerdas","Nowadays you can even control the lights at home with a smartphone.":"Sekarang bahkan bisa mengontrol lampu di rumah dengan ponsel pintar.","warming":"pemanasan","Global warming is making summers hotter and hotter.":"Pemanasan global membuat musim panas semakin panas.","earthquake":"gempa bumi","The earthquake just now shook me awake from my sleep.":"Gempa tadi mengguncangku sampai terbangun dari tidur.","symptom":"gejala","If the symptoms don't improve, you'd better see a doctor.":"Kalau gejalanya tidak membaik, sebaiknya periksa ke dokter.","to be infected":"terinfeksi","If a wound isn't treated properly, it easily gets infected.":"Kalau luka tidak dirawat dengan benar, mudah terinfeksi.","to treat; treatment":"mengobati; pengobatan","This illness can be cured if treated early.":"Penyakit ini bisa sembuh jika diobati sejak dini.","medication; drug":"obat","This medication must be taken according to the doctor's instructions.":"Obat ini harus diminum sesuai petunjuk dokter.","side effect":"efek samping","A side effect of this medicine is that it makes you drowsy.":"Efek samping obat ini adalah membuat mengantuk.","emergency room":"ruang gawat darurat","His stomach hurt unbearably at midnight, so he had to go to the ER.":"Perutnya sakit tak tertahankan tengah malam, jadi dia harus ke ruang gawat darurat.","surgery; operation":"operasi; pembedahan","The doctor said this surgery is simple, so there's no need to worry too much.":"Dokter bilang operasi ini sederhana, jadi tidak perlu terlalu khawatir.","depressed; gloomy":"depresi; murung","Prolonged high stress can make a person become depressed.":"Stres tinggi yang berkepanjangan bisa membuat seseorang menjadi depresi.","anxious":"cemas; gelisah","Before exams I always feel anxious and can't sleep well.":"Sebelum ujian aku selalu merasa cemas dan tidak bisa tidur nyenyak.","team":"tim","Our team collaborated well and finished quickly.":"Tim kami bekerja sama dengan baik dan cepat selesai.","project":"proyek","There are only two weeks left before this project's deadline.":"Proyek ini tinggal dua minggu lagi sebelum tenggat waktunya.","presentation; slides":"presentasi; slide","I have to give a presentation to the client tomorrow, so I need to practice once more tonight.":"Besok aku harus presentasi ke klien, jadi malam ini perlu berlatih sekali lagi.","career":"karier","This job is very helpful for my career development.":"Pekerjaan ini sangat membantu perkembangan karierku.","social engagement (for work)":"jamuan sosial (untuk pekerjaan)","He has a lot of work-related social engagements and often gets home late.":"Dia banyak jamuan sosial terkait pekerjaan dan sering pulang larut.","planning; proposal":"perencanaan; proposal","The planning for this event was handled by her.":"Perencanaan acara ini ditangani olehnya.","savings; deposit":"tabungan; simpanan","I use my monthly savings to pay the rent.":"Aku memakai tabungan bulananku untuk membayar sewa.","interest (on money)":"bunga (uang)","This bank's fixed-deposit interest is relatively high.":"Bunga deposito berjangka bank ini relatif tinggi.","to manage finances":"mengelola keuangan","You should learn how to manage your finances while you're young.":"Sebaiknya belajar mengelola keuangan sejak masih muda.","reporter; journalist":"reporter; wartawan","Many reporters came to the scene to cover this incident.":"Banyak reporter datang ke lokasi untuk meliput kejadian ini.","to interview; to cover (news)":"mewawancarai; meliput","This boss rarely gives interviews to the media.":"Bos ini jarang memberikan wawancara kepada media.","advertisement":"iklan","This ad is very creative and leaves a deep impression.":"Iklan ini sangat kreatif dan meninggalkan kesan mendalam.","channel":"kanal; channel","That channel I often watch has uploaded a new video again.":"Kanal yang sering kutonton itu mengunggah video baru lagi.","program; show":"acara; program","This show introduced street food from all over Taiwan.":"Acara ini memperkenalkan jajanan kaki lima dari seluruh Taiwan.","audience; viewers":"penonton; pemirsa","As soon as the performance ended, the audience stood up and applauded.":"Begitu pertunjukan berakhir, penonton berdiri dan bertepuk tangan.","headline; top news":"berita utama; headline","This event made the headlines of all the major news outlets today.":"Peristiwa ini menjadi berita utama di semua media besar hari ini.","emotion; mood":"emosi; suasana hati","He controls his emotions well and rarely gets angry.":"Dia pandai mengendalikan emosi dan jarang marah.","temper":"temperamen; watak","He has a bit of a temper, so be careful with what you say.":"Dia agak temperamental, jadi hati-hati dengan ucapanmu.","to rely on; depend on":"bergantung pada; mengandalkan","Modern people rely on their phones more and more.":"Orang zaman sekarang semakin bergantung pada ponsel.","considerate; thoughtful":"penuh perhatian; pengertian","He is very considerate and always remembers what I like.":"Dia sangat penuh perhatian dan selalu ingat apa yang kusukai.","to date; go out with":"berpacaran; berkencan","They've been dating for three years and plan to get married soon.":"Mereka sudah berpacaran tiga tahun dan berencana segera menikah.","to accompany; be with":"menemani; mendampingi","For the elderly, companionship matters more than gifts.":"Bagi orang tua, kebersamaan lebih berarti daripada hadiah.","to listen attentively":"mendengarkan dengan saksama","Sometimes what a friend needs is just someone willing to listen.":"Terkadang yang dibutuhkan seorang teman hanyalah seseorang yang mau mendengarkan.","frank; to be honest":"terus terang; sejujurnya","Frankly speaking, I think this plan is a bit difficult.":"Terus terang, menurutku rencana ini agak sulit.","to control":"mengendalikan","When losing weight, you need to control your diet well.":"Saat menurunkan berat badan, kamu perlu mengendalikan pola makan dengan baik.","to establish; build":"membangun; membina","Trust is something that needs to be built slowly over time.":"Kepercayaan adalah sesuatu yang perlu dibangun perlahan seiring waktu.","to recover; restore":"pulih; memulihkan","Rest well for a few days and your body will recover quickly.":"Istirahatlah beberapa hari dengan baik, tubuhmu akan cepat pulih.","strict":"ketat; tegas","This teacher is strict with students but very popular.":"Guru ini tegas terhadap murid tapi sangat disukai.","reasonable":"wajar; masuk akal","This shop's prices are reasonable and the goods are good too.":"Harga di toko ini wajar dan barangnya juga bagus.","detailed":"terperinci; detail","Please explain in detail how to use this feature.":"Tolong jelaskan secara terperinci cara memakai fitur ini.","rapid; swift":"cepat; gesit","The fire brigade swiftly rushed to the scene to put out the fire.":"Pemadam kebakaran dengan cepat bergegas ke lokasi untuk memadamkan api.","I have to work overtime until nine every day this week.":"Minggu ini setiap hari aku harus lembur sampai jam sembilan.","Sorry, traffic was bad and I'm late.":"Maaf, lalu lintasnya macet jadi aku terlambat.","report":"laporan","I have to hand this report to my manager tomorrow morning.":"Besok pagi aku harus menyerahkan laporan ini ke manajerku.","resume; CV":"resume; CV","I sent my resume to three companies.":"Aku mengirimkan resume ke tiga perusahaan.","interview":"wawancara","Tomorrow's interview makes me so nervous.":"Wawancara besok membuatku sangat gugup.","salary":"gaji","Rent in Taipei is too expensive; half my salary goes to housing.":"Sewa di Taipei terlalu mahal; setengah gajiku habis untuk tempat tinggal.","supervisor; manager":"atasan; manajer","My supervisor is really nice and often teaches me a lot.":"Atasanku sangat baik dan sering mengajariku banyak hal.","progress; schedule":"kemajuan; jadwal","The project is a bit behind schedule.":"Proyeknya sedikit terlambat dari jadwal.","to go on a business trip":"melakukan perjalanan dinas","He has to go to Kaohsiung on business twice this month.":"Bulan ini dia harus melakukan perjalanan dinas ke Kaohsiung dua kali.","to be in charge of":"bertanggung jawab atas","I am in charge of this project, so ask me if you have questions.":"Aku yang menangani proyek ini, jadi tanyakan padaku kalau ada pertanyaan.","client; customer":"klien; pelanggan","We are meeting the client this afternoon—are the materials ready?":"Sore ini kita bertemu klien—apakah materinya sudah siap?","performance":"kinerja","His performance this year has been great, and the manager is very satisfied.":"Kinerjanya tahun ini sangat bagus, dan manajer sangat puas.","Everyone agrees with this plan, so let's go with it.":"Semua orang setuju dengan rencana ini, jadi mari kita jalankan.","to oppose":"menentang","I am against overtime culture; after work you should go home and rest.":"Aku menentang budaya lembur; setelah kerja seharusnya pulang dan istirahat.","to suggest":"menyarankan","I suggest you check the reviews online before buying.":"Aku sarankan kamu cek ulasan online dulu sebelum membeli.","to discuss":"membahas; berdiskusi","Let's discuss this matter at the meeting.":"Mari kita bahas hal ini di rapat.","I have decided to keep working in Taiwan next year.":"Aku sudah memutuskan untuk terus bekerja di Taiwan tahun depan.","opinion":"pendapat","Does anyone have opinions about this plan?":"Apakah ada yang punya pendapat tentang rencana ini?","to communicate":"berkomunikasi","If there is a problem, just say it—good communication prevents misunderstandings.":"Kalau ada masalah, katakan saja—komunikasi yang baik mencegah kesalahpahaman.","to explain":"menjelaskan","Could you explain it one more time? I still don't quite get it.":"Bisa dijelaskan sekali lagi? Aku masih belum begitu paham.","to complain":"mengeluh","He often complains that his salary is too low, but he doesn't want to change jobs either.":"Dia sering mengeluh gajinya terlalu rendah, tapi juga tidak mau pindah kerja.","to refuse":"menolak","If you don't want to go, just say no directly.":"Kalau tidak mau ikut, tolak saja langsung.","internet":"internet","The internet at this cafe is fast—great for working.":"Internet di kafe ini cepat—cocok untuk bekerja.","to download":"mengunduh; download","Download this app first; it is really handy for ordering delivery.":"Unduh dulu aplikasi ini; sangat praktis untuk memesan makanan antar.","account":"akun","I forgot my account, so I had to register a new one.":"Aku lupa akunku, jadi terpaksa mendaftar yang baru.","password":"kata sandi","Don't make your password too simple—it is risky.":"Jangan buat kata sandi terlalu sederhana—berisiko.","website":"situs web","You can check the weather around Taiwan on this website.":"Kamu bisa cek cuaca di seluruh Taiwan di situs web ini.","data; materials":"data; materi","Remember to print out the materials before the meeting.":"Ingat cetak materinya sebelum rapat.","to update":"memperbarui; update","After the update, my phone became easier to use.":"Setelah diperbarui, ponselku jadi lebih mudah dipakai.","screen":"layar","After staring at a screen all day, my eyes are so sore.":"Setelah menatap layar seharian, mataku terasa perih sekali.","message":"pesan","I just sent you a message—did you see it?":"Aku baru saja mengirimimu pesan—apakah kamu melihatnya?","to shop online":"belanja online","I love shopping online because things arrive the next day.":"Aku suka belanja online karena barangnya sampai keesokan harinya.","relationship":"hubungan","I have a good relationship with my coworkers.":"Aku punya hubungan baik dengan rekan-rekan kerja.","misunderstanding":"kesalahpahaman","It is just a misunderstanding; once we clear it up, it will be fine.":"Ini cuma kesalahpahaman; begitu diperjelas, semuanya beres.","to apologize":"meminta maaf","It was my fault—I apologize.":"Ini salahku—aku minta maaf.","to trust":"memercayai","Trust takes time to build.":"Kepercayaan butuh waktu untuk dibangun.","to quarrel":"bertengkar","They had a fight yesterday, and today they are ignoring each other.":"Kemarin mereka bertengkar, hari ini saling mendiamkan.","to forgive":"memaafkan","He has already apologized, so forgive him.":"Dia sudah minta maaf, jadi maafkanlah dia.","personality":"kepribadian","She has a cheerful personality, and everyone likes her.":"Dia berkepribadian ceria, dan semua orang menyukainya.","to get along":"akur; cocok bergaul","My Taiwanese coworkers are easy to get along with; I got used to things quickly.":"Rekan-rekan kerja Taiwan-ku mudah diajak akur; aku cepat terbiasa.","habit":"kebiasaan","I have developed the habit of getting up early to exercise.":"Aku sudah membentuk kebiasaan bangun pagi untuk berolahraga.","environment":"lingkungan","The work environment at this company is quite good.":"Lingkungan kerja di perusahaan ini cukup bagus.","opportunity":"kesempatan","If I get the chance, I would like to live in Tainan for a while.":"Kalau ada kesempatan, aku ingin tinggal di Tainan untuk sementara.","to affect; to influence":"memengaruhi","Staying up late affects your work the next day.":"Begadang memengaruhi pekerjaanmu keesokan harinya.","attitude":"sikap","He has a serious work attitude, and everyone trusts him.":"Dia bersikap serius dalam bekerja, dan semua orang memercayainya.","goal":"tujuan; target","My goal this year is to master Chinese.":"Targetku tahun ini adalah menguasai bahasa Mandarin.","pressure; stress":"tekanan; stres","Work has been so stressful lately; on weekends I just want to sleep at home.":"Belakangan ini pekerjaan sangat menekan; akhir pekan aku hanya ingin tidur di rumah.","experience":"pengalaman","This work experience helped me a lot.":"Pengalaman kerja ini sangat membantuku.","situation":"situasi; keadaan","How is the situation now? Do you need any help?":"Bagaimana situasinya sekarang? Butuh bantuan?","condition":"kondisi; syarat","The conditions of this job are good, except that it requires shift work.":"Kondisi pekerjaan ini bagus, hanya saja harus kerja shift.","result":"hasil","I won't know the interview result until next week.":"Aku baru akan tahu hasil wawancaranya minggu depan.","cause; reason":"penyebab; alasan","No one knows the reason he suddenly quit.":"Tidak ada yang tahu alasan dia tiba-tiba berhenti kerja.","method; way":"metode; cara","The best way to learn a language is to use it every day.":"Cara terbaik belajar bahasa adalah menggunakannya setiap hari.","ability":"kemampuan","Her Chinese ability is much better than mine.":"Kemampuan bahasa Mandarinnya jauh lebih baik daripadaku.","In the end, I chose to stay and work in Taipei.":"Pada akhirnya, aku memilih tetap tinggal dan bekerja di Taipei.","to change":"berubah; mengubah","My life has changed a lot since coming to Taiwan.":"Hidupku banyak berubah sejak datang ke Taiwan.","to succeed":"berhasil; sukses","As long as you don't give up, you will succeed someday.":"Selama kamu tidak menyerah, suatu hari kamu pasti akan sukses.","to fail":"gagal","It is okay to fail—just try again.":"Gagal itu tidak apa-apa—coba lagi saja.","Taiwan's tech industry has developed rapidly in recent years.":"Industri teknologi Taiwan berkembang pesat beberapa tahun terakhir.","to adapt":"beradaptasi; menyesuaikan diri","Taiwan's summers are really hot; it took me a long time to adapt.":"Musim panas di Taiwan sangat panas; aku butuh waktu lama untuk beradaptasi.","smooth; without a hitch":"lancar; tanpa hambatan","Good luck with your interview!":"Semoga wawancaramu lancar!","Rent in central Taipei goes up year after year.":"Sewa di pusat Taipei naik dari tahun ke tahun.","National Health Insurance (Taiwan)":"Asuransi Kesehatan Nasional (Taiwan)","With NHI, seeing a doctor only costs about NT$150.":"Dengan Asuransi Kesehatan Nasional, berobat hanya sekitar NT$150.","to clock in/out; to check in":"absen masuk/keluar","At our company, we have to clock in and out.":"Di perusahaan kami, kami harus absen masuk dan keluar.","to work in shifts":"kerja bergantian shift","Convenience store jobs require shift work, sometimes overnight shifts.":"Pekerjaan di minimarket harus kerja shift, kadang shift malam.","deposit":"uang jaminan; deposit","Renting a place usually requires a two-month deposit.":"Menyewa tempat biasanya butuh uang jaminan dua bulan.","contract":"kontrak","Read the contents carefully before signing a contract.":"Baca isinya dengan teliti sebelum menandatangani kontrak.","to stay up late":"begadang","I stayed up late finishing a report—so sleepy.":"Aku begadang menyelesaikan laporan—ngantuk sekali.","to pay a bill/fee":"membayar tagihan","You can pay utility bills right at the convenience store.":"Kamu bisa membayar tagihan utilitas langsung di minimarket.","burden":"beban","Rent in Taipei is a heavy burden for young people.":"Sewa di Taipei adalah beban berat bagi anak muda.","promotion":"promosi jabatan","He works hard, and this year he finally got promoted to manager.":"Dia bekerja keras, dan tahun ini akhirnya dipromosikan menjadi manajer.","bonus":"bonus","The company made money this year, so the year-end bonus should be good.":"Perusahaan untung tahun ini, jadi bonus akhir tahun mestinya lumayan.","department":"departemen; divisi","I am transferring to another department next month.":"Bulan depan aku pindah ke departemen lain.","to sign one's name":"menandatangani nama","Please sign at the bottom of this document.":"Silakan tanda tangani di bagian bawah dokumen ini.","Remember to exchange business cards with the client when you first meet.":"Ingat bertukar kartu nama dengan klien saat pertama kali bertemu.","folder":"folder; map","All the contracts are in that blue folder on the desktop.":"Semua kontrak ada di dalam map biru di atas meja itu.","schedule; itinerary":"jadwal; agenda","The manager's schedule is completely full this week.":"Jadwal manajer minggu ini penuh sekali.","efficiency":"efisiensi","Too many meetings in the morning hurt work efficiency.":"Terlalu banyak rapat di pagi hari menurunkan efisiensi kerja.","responsibility":"tanggung jawab","This mistake is not your responsibility alone, so don't blame yourself too much.":"Kesalahan ini bukan tanggung jawabmu sendiri, jadi jangan terlalu menyalahkan diri.","to cooperate":"bekerja sama","Our company is working with a Japanese company to develop a new product.":"Perusahaan kami bekerja sama dengan perusahaan Jepang untuk mengembangkan produk baru.","to negotiate":"bernegosiasi","We are leaving this price negotiation with the supplier to an experienced colleague.":"Negosiasi harga dengan pemasok kali ini kami serahkan kepada rekan yang berpengalaman.","program (computer)":"program (komputer)","He studies programming at home every night.":"Setiap malam dia belajar pemrograman di rumah.","software":"perangkat lunak","Company rules say you cannot install software from unknown sources on your computer.":"Aturan perusahaan melarang memasang perangkat lunak dari sumber tak dikenal di komputer.","system":"sistem","The company's leave system is acting up today—I can't log in at all.":"Sistem cuti perusahaan bermasalah hari ini—aku sama sekali tidak bisa masuk.","information":"informasi","There is a lot of information online, but not all of it is true.":"Ada banyak informasi di internet, tapi tidak semuanya benar.","file":"berkas; file","This file is too big to send.":"Berkas ini terlalu besar untuk dikirim.","to back up (data)":"mencadangkan (data)","Remember to back up important data first, or you'll lose it if the computer breaks.":"Ingat cadangkan data penting dulu, kalau tidak, hilang saat komputer rusak.","to log in":"masuk; login","You need to log in as a member first to see the discounted price.":"Kamu harus login sebagai anggota dulu untuk melihat harga diskon.","to log out":"keluar; logout","After using a public computer, be sure to log out.":"Setelah memakai komputer umum, pastikan logout.","to connect (online)":"terhubung (daring)","The video meeting keeps failing to connect—it might be a network issue.":"Rapat video terus gagal terhubung—mungkin masalah jaringan.","to crash; to freeze (computer)":"hang; macet (komputer)","My computer crashed halfway through writing the report—I almost cried.":"Komputerku hang di tengah menulis laporan—hampir menangis.","to charge (a battery)":"mengisi daya","My phone is almost dead—can I charge it here?":"Ponselku hampir mati—boleh mengisi daya di sini?","earphones; headphones":"earphone; headphone","Please wear earphones when watching videos on the MRT.":"Harap pakai earphone saat menonton video di MRT.","to envy; to admire":"iri; kagum","He gets to work from home—I really envy him.":"Dia bisa kerja dari rumah—aku benar-benar iri.","I really regret not making myself clear yesterday.":"Aku benar-benar menyesal tidak menjelaskan dengan jelas kemarin.","to be moved; touching":"terharu; mengharukan","My coworkers secretly threw me a birthday celebration—I was so touched.":"Rekan-rekan kerjaku diam-diam mengadakan perayaan ulang tahun untukku—aku sangat terharu.","disappointed":"kecewa","This restaurant has great reviews, but the food was a bit disappointing.":"Restoran ini ulasannya bagus, tapi makanannya agak mengecewakan.","proud; arrogant":"bangga; sombong","Your parents must be so proud that you won this award.":"Orang tuamu pasti sangat bangga kamu memenangkan penghargaan ini.","Spending the New Year alone abroad, it's hard not to feel lonely.":"Merayakan Tahun Baru sendirian di luar negeri, sulit untuk tidak merasa kesepian.","to miss (someone/something)":"merindukan","Even after living in Taiwan for a long time, I still miss the taste of home.":"Meski sudah lama tinggal di Taiwan, aku masih merindukan cita rasa kampung halaman.","to admire":"mengagumi","He works while preparing for exams—I really admire him.":"Dia bekerja sambil mempersiapkan ujian—aku benar-benar mengaguminya.","cannot stand":"tidak tahan","I really can't stand summer without air conditioning.":"Aku benar-benar tidak tahan musim panas tanpa AC.","satisfied":"puas","The client is very satisfied with this design and wants to keep working together.":"Klien sangat puas dengan desain ini dan ingin terus bekerja sama.","to make an appointment/reservation":"membuat janji/reservasi","This restaurant is really popular—you need to book a week ahead.":"Restoran ini sangat populer—kamu harus reservasi seminggu sebelumnya.","to cancel":"membatalkan","Tomorrow's event has been canceled because of the typhoon.":"Acara besok dibatalkan karena topan.","to queue; to line up":"mengantre","You have to line up for half an hour every day at this fried chicken stand.":"Kios ayam goreng ini setiap hari harus mengantre setengah jam.","special offer; discount":"penawaran khusus; diskon","This credit card gives you a discount on the MRT.":"Kartu kredit ini memberi diskon untuk MRT.","discount":"potongan harga; diskon","The anniversary sale discounts are huge, so lots of people rush to the department store.":"Diskon obral ulang tahun sangat besar, jadi banyak orang berbondong-bondong ke mal.","to collect points":"mengumpulkan poin","You can collect points buying coffee at the convenience store and redeem a free cup.":"Beli kopi di minimarket bisa mengumpulkan poin dan menukarnya dengan segelas gratis.","member":"anggota; member","Members get 10% off—would you like to sign up?":"Anggota dapat diskon 10%—apakah kamu mau mendaftar?","receipt":"struk; kuitansi","Keep your receipts from the business trip so you can claim expenses when you return.":"Simpan struk perjalanan dinasmu supaya bisa mengklaim biaya setelah kembali.","to return goods":"mengembalikan barang","If clothes bought online don't fit, you can return them within seven days.":"Kalau baju yang dibeli online tidak pas, bisa dikembalikan dalam tujuh hari.","warranty":"garansi","This laptop is still under warranty, so it can be repaired for free.":"Laptop ini masih bergaransi, jadi bisa diperbaiki gratis.","home delivery":"pengiriman ke rumah","I have anything too heavy delivered to my home.":"Barang yang terlalu berat kukirim ke rumah saja.","in passing; while at it":"sekalian","If you're going to the convenience store, grab me a bottle of water while you're at it.":"Kalau kamu ke minimarket, sekalian belikan aku sebotol air ya.","on purpose":"sengaja","He didn't do it on purpose, so don't be angry.":"Dia tidak sengaja melakukannya, jadi jangan marah.","rare; hard to come by":"langka; jarang ada","It's rare to get a long weekend—let's go to Tainan for a few days.":"Jarang-jarang dapat libur panjang—ayo ke Tainan beberapa hari.","fortunately":"untungnya","Luckily I brought an umbrella, or I would have been soaked.":"Untungnya aku bawa payung, kalau tidak pasti basah kuyup.","unexpectedly; to one's surprise":"tak disangka; ternyata","He has only studied Chinese for a year, yet surprisingly he can already hold meetings with clients.":"Dia baru belajar bahasa Mandarin setahun, tapi tak disangka sudah bisa rapat dengan klien.","at least":"setidaknya; paling tidak","It takes at least an hour from the airport to downtown.":"Dari bandara ke pusat kota butuh setidaknya satu jam.","actually":"sebenarnya","Everyone thinks he is Taiwanese, but actually he is Japanese.":"Semua mengira dia orang Taiwan, padahal sebenarnya dia orang Jepang.","as expected":"ternyata benar; sesuai dugaan","Everyone online said this place was delicious, and sure enough, it lived up to its reputation.":"Semua orang di internet bilang tempat ini enak, dan ternyata benar sesuai reputasinya.","as much as possible":"sebisa mungkin","I will try my best to have the materials ready by Friday.":"Aku akan berusaha sebisa mungkin menyiapkan materinya sebelum Jumat.","gathering; get-together":"kumpul-kumpul; pertemuan","There is a class reunion this Saturday—are you coming?":"Sabtu ini ada reuni kelas—kamu datang?","After work I often go chat with coworkers at a cafe.":"Setelah kerja aku sering mengobrol dengan rekan kerja di kafe.","to wish someone well":"mendoakan kebahagiaan","A coworker is getting married, and everyone wishes them the best.":"Seorang rekan kerja akan menikah, dan semua mendoakan kebahagiaannya.","to comfort":"menghibur","She failed the interview and is upset—let's go comfort her.":"Dia gagal wawancara dan sedang sedih—ayo kita hibur dia.","to encourage":"menyemangati; mendorong","Our manager often encourages us to come up with new ideas.":"Manajer kami sering mendorong kami untuk memunculkan ide baru.","to criticize":"mengkritik","Rather than criticizing others, it's better to do your own work well first.":"Daripada mengkritik orang lain, lebih baik kerjakan dulu tugasmu sendiri dengan baik.","to praise":"memuji","The client praised our service for being fast and excellent.":"Klien memuji layanan kami yang cepat dan sangat baik.","memory":"kenangan; ingatan","My memory of coming to Taiwan for the first time is still vivid.":"Kenanganku pertama kali datang ke Taiwan masih sangat jelas.","impression":"kesan","First impressions matter a lot in an interview.":"Kesan pertama sangat penting dalam wawancara.","idea; thought":"ide; gagasan","If you have a better idea, feel free to bring it up in the meeting.":"Kalau punya ide yang lebih baik, silakan sampaikan di rapat.","feeling":"perasaan; firasat","I have a feeling this project will go smoothly.":"Aku punya firasat proyek ini akan berjalan lancar.","concept; mindset":"konsep; pola pikir","Each generation has a different mindset about work.":"Setiap generasi punya pola pikir yang berbeda tentang pekerjaan.","common sense":"akal sehat; hal umum","Not eating on the MRT is basic common sense in Taiwan.":"Tidak makan di MRT adalah hal umum yang mendasar di Taiwan.","regulation; rule":"peraturan; aturan","According to company rules, leave must be requested one day in advance.":"Menurut peraturan perusahaan, cuti harus diajukan satu hari sebelumnya.","standard":"standar; kriteria","Everyone has different standards for choosing a place—for me, transportation matters most.":"Setiap orang punya kriteria berbeda dalam memilih tempat tinggal—bagiku, transportasi paling penting.","scope; range":"cakupan; lingkup","This exam covers lessons five through eight.":"Ujian ini mencakup pelajaran lima sampai delapan.","degree; level":"tingkat; taraf","My Chinese is about intermediate level—I still need more practice.":"Bahasa Mandarinku sekitar tingkat menengah—masih perlu lebih banyak latihan.","purpose; goal":"tujuan","The purpose of this business trip is to visit new clients.":"Tujuan perjalanan dinas ini adalah mengunjungi klien baru.","process":"proses","The process of learning a language is tough, but it's worth it.":"Proses belajar bahasa itu berat, tapi sepadan.","content":"isi; konten","Please read the contract carefully before signing.":"Harap baca isi kontrak dengan teliti sebelum menandatangani.","key point":"poin utama; inti","Meeting time is limited, so let's get straight to the point.":"Waktu rapat terbatas, jadi langsung ke poin utama saja.","details":"rincian; detail","The overall direction is fine—let's confirm the details by email.":"Arah besarnya sudah oke—rinciannya kita konfirmasi lewat email.","strength; advantage":"kelebihan; keunggulan","The advantage of living in Taipei is convenient transportation—you can get anywhere fast.":"Keunggulan tinggal di Taipei adalah transportasi yang praktis—ke mana pun cepat.","weakness; drawback":"kelemahan; kekurangan","The only drawback of this apartment is that it's a bit far from the MRT station.":"Satu-satunya kekurangan apartemen ini adalah agak jauh dari stasiun MRT.","to respect":"menghormati","Everyone makes different choices, and we should respect each other.":"Setiap orang membuat pilihan berbeda, dan kita harus saling menghormati.","confidence":"rasa percaya diri","Practice a few more times and you will feel more confident.":"Berlatihlah beberapa kali lagi dan kamu akan lebih percaya diri.","to express":"mengungkapkan; mengekspresikan","Expressing my opinions in Chinese is still a bit hard for me.":"Mengungkapkan pendapat dalam bahasa Mandarin masih agak sulit bagiku.","to apply for a job":"melamar pekerjaan","Last month I applied for an engineer position at a startup.":"Bulan lalu aku melamar posisi insinyur di sebuah startup.","to hire; to admit":"merekrut; menerima","Congratulations, you got the job! You start next Monday.":"Selamat, kamu diterima! Kamu mulai kerja Senin depan.","to resign; to quit a job":"mengundurkan diri; berhenti kerja","He felt the work stress was too much, so he decided to quit and rest for a while.":"Dia merasa tekanan kerjanya terlalu besar, jadi memutuskan berhenti dan istirahat sebentar.","to switch jobs; to job-hop":"pindah kerja; ganti pekerjaan","I heard he switched to another company and got a thirty percent raise.":"Kudengar dia pindah ke perusahaan lain dan gajinya naik tiga puluh persen.","to intern":"magang","She interned at a design company for half a year in college.":"Dia magang di perusahaan desain selama setengah tahun saat kuliah.","part-time job":"kerja paruh waktu","Besides his full-time job, he also works part-time at night.":"Selain pekerjaan tetapnya, dia juga kerja paruh waktu di malam hari.","full-time position":"posisi penuh waktu","After two years of part-time work, I finally found a full-time job.":"Setelah dua tahun kerja paruh waktu, akhirnya aku menemukan pekerjaan penuh waktu.","pay and benefits; treatment":"gaji dan tunjangan; fasilitas","This company offers good pay and benefits, including company trips.":"Perusahaan ini menawarkan gaji dan tunjangan yang baik, termasuk tamasya perusahaan.","to get a raise":"naik gaji","I have worked here for two years and want to talk to my manager about a raise.":"Aku sudah bekerja di sini dua tahun dan ingin bicara ke manajer soal kenaikan gaji.","to retire":"pensiun","My dad is retiring next year and plans to move back to the countryside.":"Ayahku pensiun tahun depan dan berencana pindah kembali ke desa.","utility bills (water and electricity)":"tagihan air dan listrik","Does the rent for this place include utilities?":"Apakah sewa tempat ini sudah termasuk tagihan air dan listrik?","gas":"gas","Remember to check that the gas is turned off before you go out.":"Ingat periksa apakah gas sudah dimatikan sebelum keluar rumah.","management fee":"biaya pengelolaan","This building charges a monthly management fee of two thousand NT dollars.":"Gedung ini mengenakan biaya pengelolaan dua ribu dolar NT per bulan.","top floor; rooftop":"lantai teratas; rooftop","Top-floor rooms get really hot in summer, so the rent is cheaper.":"Kamar di lantai teratas sangat panas saat musim panas, jadi sewanya lebih murah.","room with shared bathroom":"kamar dengan kamar mandi bersama","With a yafang you share the bathroom with others, so I would rather rent a studio.":"Kamar seperti ini harus berbagi kamar mandi dengan orang lain, jadi aku lebih baik menyewa studio.","studio with private bathroom":"studio dengan kamar mandi dalam","I rented a small studio near my office; it is only a ten-minute walk away.":"Aku menyewa studio kecil dekat kantor; hanya sepuluh menit jalan kaki.","furniture":"perabot; furnitur","This place comes furnished, so you can move right in.":"Tempat ini sudah dilengkapi perabot, jadi bisa langsung ditempati.","interior decoration":"dekorasi interior","This cafe's interior design is very distinctive, and many people come to take photos.":"Desain interior kafe ini sangat khas, banyak orang datang untuk berfoto.","neighbor":"tetangga","My neighbor is very kind and often shares fruit with me.":"Tetanggaku sangat baik dan sering berbagi buah denganku.","to lose weight; to diet":"menurunkan berat badan; diet","I am on a diet lately, so I only eat salad for dinner.":"Belakangan ini aku sedang diet, jadi makan malam hanya makan salad.","to work out":"berolahraga; nge-gym","He works out at the gym three times a week.":"Dia nge-gym tiga kali seminggu.","nutrition":"nutrisi; gizi","If you eat boxed meals every day, you won't get enough nutrition—eat more vegetables.":"Kalau setiap hari makan nasi kotak, nutrisimu kurang—perbanyak makan sayur.","to have insomnia":"mengalami insomnia; susah tidur","I often cannot sleep lately; maybe it is because of too much work stress.":"Belakangan ini aku sering susah tidur; mungkin karena tekanan kerja yang terlalu besar.","fatigued; tired":"lelah; letih","Driving too long makes you fatigued, so remember to take breaks.":"Menyetir terlalu lama membuat lelah, jadi ingat untuk beristirahat.","physical checkup":"pemeriksaan kesehatan","The company arranges a free physical checkup every year.":"Perusahaan mengadakan pemeriksaan kesehatan gratis setiap tahun.","to see a doctor; to have a consultation":"berobat; konsultasi ke dokter","At this clinic you have to register online first before seeing the doctor.":"Di klinik ini kamu harus mendaftar online dulu sebelum berobat.","news":"berita","Every morning I watch the news while eating breakfast.":"Setiap pagi aku menonton berita sambil sarapan.","government":"pemerintah","The government recently launched a new rental subsidy.":"Pemerintah baru-baru ini meluncurkan subsidi sewa yang baru.","police":"polisi","The wallet is gone—let's go ask at the nearby police station first.":"Dompetnya hilang—ayo tanya dulu ke kantor polisi terdekat.","fire fighting; fire safety":"pemadaman kebakaran; keselamatan kebakaran","The building conducts a fire safety inspection once a year.":"Gedung ini melakukan inspeksi keselamatan kebakaran setahun sekali.","ticket; fine notice":"surat tilang; denda","I parked my scooter illegally and got a six-hundred-dollar ticket.":"Aku memarkir motor sembarangan dan kena tilang enam ratus dolar.","car accident":"kecelakaan lalu lintas","It looks like there was a car accident ahead—no wonder traffic is so bad.":"Sepertinya ada kecelakaan di depan—pantas saja macet parah.","accident; unexpected event":"kecelakaan; kejadian tak terduga","Wear a helmet when riding—it protects you if an accident happens.":"Pakai helm saat berkendara—melindungimu kalau terjadi kecelakaan.","insurance":"asuransi","Before traveling abroad, it is best to buy travel insurance first.":"Sebelum bepergian ke luar negeri, sebaiknya beli asuransi perjalanan dulu.","news; information":"kabar; informasi","Everyone was surprised to hear the news that the company is moving.":"Semua orang terkejut mendengar kabar bahwa perusahaan akan pindah.","to commute":"berkomuter; pulang pergi kerja","I commute by MRT every day; it takes about forty minutes.":"Setiap hari aku pulang pergi kerja naik MRT; butuh sekitar empat puluh menit.","to think; to believe":"berpendapat; menganggap","I don't think remote work is necessarily less efficient.":"Aku tidak berpendapat kerja jarak jauh pasti kurang efisien.","to advocate; to maintain":"menganjurkan; berpandangan","He maintains that meetings should not last more than an hour.":"Dia berpandangan bahwa rapat tidak boleh berlangsung lebih dari satu jam.","to doubt; to suspect":"meragukan; mencurigai","This price is suspiciously cheap; I suspect it is fake.":"Harga ini murah mencurigakan; aku curiga ini palsu.","to confirm; to be sure":"memastikan; mengonfirmasi","Confirm the meeting time and place once more before setting out.":"Konfirmasikan sekali lagi waktu dan tempat rapat sebelum berangkat.","to deny":"menyangkal","He denied saying that, but everyone heard it.":"Dia menyangkal mengatakan itu, tapi semua orang mendengarnya.","to admit; to acknowledge":"mengakui","If you make a mistake, admit it and then find a way to fix it.":"Kalau berbuat salah, akui lalu cari cara memperbaikinya.","to emphasize":"menekankan","The manager keeps emphasizing that the deadline cannot be pushed back again.":"Manajer terus menekankan bahwa tenggat waktu tidak bisa diundur lagi.","to remind":"mengingatkan","Thanks for reminding me—I almost forgot about tomorrow's meeting.":"Terima kasih sudah mengingatkan—aku hampir lupa rapat besok.","situation; condition":"keadaan; kondisi","The system is unstable today and often fails to connect.":"Sistem hari ini tidak stabil dan sering gagal terhubung.","probability; chance":"kemungkinan; probabilitas","The forecast says there is an eighty percent chance of rain tomorrow.":"Prakiraan cuaca bilang besok ada delapan puluh persen kemungkinan hujan.","style":"gaya","Every designer has a different style—which one do you prefer?":"Setiap desainer punya gaya berbeda—kamu lebih suka yang mana?","atmosphere":"suasana","This restaurant has a great atmosphere—perfect for a date.":"Restoran ini suasananya bagus—cocok sekali untuk kencan.","popular; trendy":"populer; sedang tren","This song is really popular lately—you hear it everywhere.":"Lagu ini sedang sangat populer belakangan ini—di mana-mana terdengar.","topic (of conversation)":"topik (obrolan)","When chatting with coworkers, food is the safest topic.":"Saat mengobrol dengan rekan kerja, makanan adalah topik yang paling aman.","due to; owing to":"karena; akibat","Due to days of heavy rain, the event had to be postponed.":"Karena hujan deras berhari-hari, acaranya terpaksa ditunda.","despite; even though":"meskipun; walaupun","Despite encountering many difficulties, he insisted on finishing the project.":"Meskipun menghadapi banyak kesulitan, dia bersikeras menyelesaikan proyeknya.","therefore; hence":"oleh sebab itu; maka dari itu","This road is under construction, therefore please take an alternate route.":"Jalan ini sedang dalam perbaikan, oleh sebab itu harap ambil jalur lain.","however; nevertheless":"namun demikian; meski begitu","This method sounds ideal; however, it is not easy to carry out in practice.":"Metode ini terdengar ideal; namun demikian, tidak mudah dilaksanakan dalam praktik.","besides; in addition":"selain itu; di samping itu","This job pays well; in addition, it has a solid training system.":"Pekerjaan ini bergaji baik; selain itu, ada sistem pelatihan yang solid.","in short; in a word":"singkatnya; pendeknya","In short, it still comes down to how the boss finally decides.":"Singkatnya, semuanya tetap bergantung pada keputusan akhir bos.","in other words":"dengan kata lain","He didn't give a direct answer; in other words, he isn't really willing to help.":"Dia tidak menjawab langsung; dengan kata lain, dia tidak benar-benar mau membantu.","and then; thereby":"lalu; dengan demikian","Exercising more can build up your stamina and thereby improve work efficiency.":"Lebih banyak berolahraga bisa meningkatkan stamina dan dengan demikian menaikkan efisiensi kerja.","You'd better set off now, otherwise you'll definitely be late.":"Sebaiknya kamu berangkat sekarang, kalau tidak pasti terlambat.","even if; even though":"sekalipun; kendati","Even if he is very busy, he makes time to have dinner with his family.":"Sekalipun sangat sibuk, dia menyempatkan makan malam bersama keluarga.","Cycling to work saves money and gives you exercise—truly killing two birds with one stone.":"Bersepeda ke kantor hemat uang sekaligus olahraga—benar-benar sekali mendayung dua tiga pulau terlampaui.","to constantly strive for improvement":"terus berupaya meningkatkan diri","This old shop constantly strives to improve its quality—no wonder business is so good.":"Toko lama ini terus berupaya meningkatkan kualitasnya—pantas saja usahanya laris.","to proceed step by step":"melangkah setahap demi setahap","Learning a language should proceed step by step; you can't memorize too many words at once.":"Belajar bahasa harus setahap demi setahap; jangan menghafal terlalu banyak kata sekaligus.","to go all out; to give one's all":"berjuang mati-matian; mengerahkan segenap tenaga","No matter the outcome, I will give it my all.":"Apa pun hasilnya, aku akan berjuang mati-matian.","to get twice the result with half the effort":"hasil berlipat ganda dengan usaha separuh","With the right tools, you can get twice the result with half the effort.":"Dengan alat yang tepat, kamu bisa mendapat hasil berlipat ganda dengan usaha separuh.","to be at a loss what to do":"kebingungan tak tahu harus berbuat apa","Hearing this sudden news, she was at a loss for a moment.":"Mendengar kabar mendadak ini, dia sejenak kebingungan tak tahu harus berbuat apa.","to play a decisive role; pivotal":"memainkan peran penentu; sangat menentukan","TSMC plays a pivotal role in the global semiconductor industry.":"TSMC memainkan peran penentu dalam industri semikonduktor global.","widely known; a household name":"dikenal luas; terkenal di mana-mana","This singer is practically a household name in Taiwan.":"Penyanyi ini hampir dikenal semua orang di Taiwan.","to rank among the top":"selalu menempati peringkat teratas","He ranks among the top in every exam and is a model student in the teachers' eyes.":"Dia selalu menempati peringkat teratas di setiap ujian dan menjadi murid teladan di mata para guru.","to be down-to-earth; to work steadily":"membumi; bekerja dengan mantap dan tekun","Rather than aiming too high, it's better to stay down-to-earth and do the task at hand well.":"Daripada bercita-cita terlalu tinggi, lebih baik membumi dan mengerjakan tugas di depan mata dengan baik.","to think over carefully; deliberate":"mempertimbangkan dengan matang","This is a decision I made after careful deliberation, so I won't regret it.":"Ini keputusan yang kubuat setelah dipertimbangkan dengan matang, jadi aku tidak akan menyesal.","to have the opposite effect; backfire":"menjadi kontraproduktif; berbalik merugikan","Being too strict with children can sometimes backfire.":"Terlalu keras terhadap anak terkadang justru berbalik merugikan.","Meetings that run too long actually lower the whole team's efficiency.":"Rapat yang berlangsung terlalu lama justru menurunkan efisiensi seluruh tim.","performance; results":"kinerja; hasil","The company distributes year-end bonuses based on individual performance.":"Perusahaan membagikan bonus akhir tahun berdasarkan kinerja masing-masing individu.","résumé; CV":"resume; CV","Before submitting your résumé, remember to tailor it to the position.":"Sebelum mengirim resume, ingat untuk menyesuaikannya dengan posisi yang dilamar.","He has an interview at a tech company tomorrow and is too nervous to sleep.":"Besok dia ada wawancara di perusahaan teknologi dan gugup sampai tidak bisa tidur.","to negotiate; negotiation":"bernegosiasi; negosiasi","After many rounds of negotiation, the two sides finally reached an agreement.":"Setelah beberapa putaran negosiasi, kedua pihak akhirnya mencapai kesepakatan.","Before signing a contract, be sure to read every clause carefully.":"Sebelum menandatangani kontrak, pastikan membaca setiap klausul dengan cermat.","This client is very demanding, so you'll need to put in extra care.":"Klien ini sangat menuntut, jadi Anda perlu ekstra hati-hati.","department; division":"departemen; divisi","This project requires several departments to work together.":"Proyek ini memerlukan kerja sama beberapa departemen.","promotion (in job)":"promosi (jabatan)","This company's promotion path is transparent—work hard and you'll have a chance.":"Jalur promosi di perusahaan ini transparan—kerja keras dan Anda akan punya kesempatan.","to resign; to leave a job":"mengundurkan diri; berhenti kerja","He decided to resign and pursue what he truly wants to do.":"Dia memutuskan berhenti kerja untuk mengejar apa yang benar-benar ingin dilakukannya.","to apply (for a job)":"melamar (pekerjaan)","I'd like to apply for this position, but I'm not sure if I have a chance.":"Saya ingin melamar posisi ini, tapi tidak yakin apakah punya peluang.","to admit; to hire":"menerima; mempekerjakan","Congratulations, you've been hired—you can report to work next Monday.":"Selamat, Anda diterima—Anda bisa mulai bekerja Senin depan.","He's going to Japan on a business trip next week, for about a week.":"Minggu depan dia akan dinas ke Jepang, sekitar seminggu.","business performance; sales":"kinerja bisnis; penjualan","This year's sales grew by twenty percent compared with last year.":"Penjualan tahun ini tumbuh dua puluh persen dibanding tahun lalu.","decision-making; policy decision":"pengambilan keputusan; keputusan kebijakan","Important decisions should be based on sufficient data.":"Keputusan penting harus didasarkan pada data yang memadai.","to coordinate; to mediate":"mengoordinasi; menengahi","Someone needs to step in and mediate this, or it will only get worse.":"Seseorang perlu turun tangan menengahi ini, kalau tidak akan makin buruk.","benefit; effectiveness":"manfaat; efektivitas","Whether this ad spending is worthwhile depends on the actual benefit.":"Apakah pengeluaran iklan ini sepadan tergantung pada manfaat nyatanya.","If you have any issues, feel free to raise them directly with your supervisor.":"Jika ada masalah, silakan sampaikan langsung kepada atasan Anda.","political party":"partai politik","Taiwan has several major political parties, each with different ideals.":"Taiwan memiliki beberapa partai politik besar, masing-masing dengan ideal yang berbeda.","democracy":"demokrasi","The value of democracy lies in everyone being able to express their views.":"Nilai demokrasi terletak pada setiap orang bisa menyampaikan pandangannya.","freedom; liberty":"kebebasan","Freedom of speech is an important foundation of a democratic society.":"Kebebasan berpendapat adalah fondasi penting masyarakat demokratis.","constitution":"konstitusi","People's fundamental rights are protected by the constitution.":"Hak-hak dasar rakyat dilindungi oleh konstitusi.","official; officer":"pejabat","This official apologized to the public for a verbal blunder.":"Pejabat ini meminta maaf kepada publik karena keceplosan bicara.","to protest":"memprotes; berunjuk rasa","Over a hundred people gathered in front of city hall to protest.":"Lebih dari seratus orang berkumpul di depan balai kota untuk berunjuk rasa.","to go on strike":"mogok kerja","To fight for fair wages, the union decided to go on strike.":"Untuk memperjuangkan upah yang adil, serikat pekerja memutuskan mogok kerja.","agreement; accord":"perjanjian; kesepakatan","After several rounds of talks, the two countries finally signed a trade agreement.":"Setelah beberapa putaran perundingan, kedua negara akhirnya menandatangani perjanjian dagang.","diplomacy; foreign affairs":"diplomasi; urusan luar negeri","This visit is highly significant for the two countries' diplomatic relations.":"Kunjungan ini sangat penting bagi hubungan diplomatik kedua negara.","trade":"perdagangan","Trade between these two countries is quite frequent.":"Perdagangan antara kedua negara ini cukup sering.","to export; export":"mengekspor; ekspor","Taiwan's fruit is exported in large quantities to Japan and Southeast Asia.":"Buah Taiwan diekspor dalam jumlah besar ke Jepang dan Asia Tenggara.","to import; import":"mengimpor; impor","Most of these goods are imported from abroad, so they cost more.":"Sebagian besar barang ini diimpor dari luar negeri, jadi harganya lebih mahal.","supply chain":"rantai pasok","The pandemic disrupted the global supply chain, forcing many factories to halt production.":"Pandemi mengganggu rantai pasok global, memaksa banyak pabrik menghentikan produksi.","public finance; fiscal":"keuangan publik; fiskal","A local government's fiscal condition directly affects public infrastructure.":"Kondisi fiskal pemerintah daerah langsung memengaruhi infrastruktur publik.","sovereignty":"kedaulatan","Safeguarding national sovereignty is an important responsibility of the government.":"Menjaga kedaulatan negara adalah tanggung jawab penting pemerintah.","globalization":"globalisasi","Globalization has made economic ties among countries much closer.":"Globalisasi membuat keterkaitan ekonomi antarnegara jauh lebih erat.","domestic demand":"permintaan domestik","The government rolled out stimulus measures in hopes of boosting domestic demand.":"Pemerintah meluncurkan langkah stimulus dengan harapan mendorong permintaan domestik.","councilor; legislator":"anggota dewan; legislator","This legislator has long paid attention to workers' rights issues.":"Legislator ini sudah lama menaruh perhatian pada isu hak pekerja.","concept; notion; mindset":"konsep; pola pikir","The older generation and young people have very different money-management mindsets.":"Generasi tua dan anak muda memiliki pola pikir mengelola uang yang sangat berbeda.","values; sense of values":"nilai; sistem nilai","Their values were too different, so in the end they broke up.":"Nilai-nilai mereka terlalu berbeda, sehingga akhirnya putus.","stance; position":"sikap; posisi","On this issue, the company's position has always been clear.":"Mengenai isu ini, sikap perusahaan selalu jelas.","From the consumer's perspective, this price is still on the high side.":"Dari sudut pandang konsumen, harga ini masih tergolong mahal.","factor":"faktor","There are many factors that affect a person's success.":"Ada banyak faktor yang memengaruhi kesuksesan seseorang.","premise; prerequisite":"premis; prasyarat","Only on the premise of guaranteed quality will we consider lowering the price.":"Hanya dengan prasyarat kualitas terjamin, kami akan mempertimbangkan menurunkan harga.","basis; grounds":"dasar; landasan","Do you have any basis for saying that?":"Apakah kamu punya dasar untuk mengatakan itu?","principle":"prinsip","One should have principles and not compromise on everything.":"Seseorang harus punya prinsip dan tidak berkompromi dalam segala hal.","field; domain":"bidang; ranah","He has been studying the field of artificial intelligence for over a decade.":"Dia telah meneliti bidang kecerdasan buatan selama lebih dari sepuluh tahun.","aspect; level":"aspek; tingkatan","This issue must be discussed from both economic and social aspects.":"Masalah ini harus dibahas dari aspek ekonomi maupun sosial.","mechanism":"mekanisme","The company has set up a complete mechanism for handling customer complaints.":"Perusahaan telah menyiapkan mekanisme lengkap untuk menangani keluhan pelanggan.","model; pattern; mode":"model; pola; mode","This startup has adopted a brand-new business model.":"Startup ini mengadopsi model bisnis yang benar-benar baru.","structure":"struktur","Taiwan's population structure is changing rapidly.":"Struktur populasi Taiwan berubah dengan cepat.","consensus":"konsensus","After discussion, everyone finally reached a consensus on this direction.":"Setelah berdiskusi, semua orang akhirnya mencapai konsensus mengenai arah ini.","to explore; to examine (a topic)":"menjajaki; mengkaji (suatu topik)","This lecture mainly explores the problem of internet addiction among teenagers.":"Ceramah ini terutama mengkaji masalah kecanduan internet di kalangan remaja.","to assess; to evaluate":"menilai; mengevaluasi","Before investing, you must first assess the risks.":"Sebelum berinvestasi, Anda harus menilai risikonya terlebih dahulu.","to implement; to put into practice":"menerapkan; melaksanakan","No matter how good a policy is, it's meaningless if it isn't implemented.":"Sebagus apa pun sebuah kebijakan, tidak ada artinya jika tidak dilaksanakan.","to promote; to popularize":"mempromosikan; memasyarakatkan","The government is working hard to promote local culture among young people.":"Pemerintah berupaya keras mempromosikan budaya lokal di kalangan anak muda.","to implement; to put into effect":"memberlakukan; menjalankan","The new garbage-sorting rules will be implemented starting next month.":"Aturan pemilahan sampah yang baru akan diberlakukan mulai bulan depan.","to grasp; to master; to have a firm hold on":"menguasai; memahami betul","To stay competitive in the workplace, you must master key skills.":"Untuk tetap kompetitif di tempat kerja, Anda harus menguasai keterampilan kunci.","to present; to show; to display":"menyajikan; menampilkan","This report clearly presents the sales trend using charts.":"Laporan ini menyajikan tren penjualan dengan jelas menggunakan grafik.","to formulate; to draw up (rules, laws)":"menyusun; merumuskan (aturan, undang-undang)","The company formulated new management rules for remote work.":"Perusahaan menyusun aturan pengelolaan baru untuk kerja jarak jauh.","to call on; to appeal":"menyerukan; mengimbau","Environmental groups are calling on everyone to reduce the use of disposable tableware.":"Kelompok lingkungan menyerukan agar semua orang mengurangi penggunaan peralatan makan sekali pakai.","to question; to challenge; to cast doubt on":"mempertanyakan; meragukan","Many people are questioning the fairness of this policy.":"Banyak orang mempertanyakan keadilan kebijakan ini.","to respond to; to cope with":"menanggapi; mengatasi","To cope with the declining birthrate, schools have introduced many new measures.":"Untuk mengatasi penurunan angka kelahiran, sekolah menerapkan banyak langkah baru.","to alleviate; to ease":"meringankan; meredakan","This subsidy can, to some extent, ease the public's financial pressure.":"Subsidi ini sampai batas tertentu dapat meringankan tekanan finansial masyarakat.","remarkable; notable":"mencolok; menonjol","Over the past half year, his Chinese has made remarkable progress.":"Selama setengah tahun terakhir, bahasa Mandarinnya mengalami kemajuan yang menonjol.","huge; enormous":"besar; sangat besar","This project requires enormous funding and manpower.":"Proyek ini memerlukan dana dan tenaga kerja yang sangat besar.","comprehensive; well-established":"lengkap; memadai","The public facilities in this community are quite comprehensive.":"Fasilitas umum di lingkungan ini cukup lengkap.","diverse; pluralistic":"beragam; majemuk","This school offers a diverse range of courses for students to choose freely.":"Sekolah ini menawarkan beragam mata pelajaran agar siswa bebas memilih.","objective":"objektif","When commenting on something, it's best to maintain an objective attitude.":"Saat mengomentari sesuatu, sebaiknya bersikap objektif.","sufficient; full; ample":"cukup; memadai","Before presenting, you must be fully prepared.":"Sebelum presentasi, Anda harus benar-benar siap.","financing":"pendanaan; pembiayaan","This startup successfully secured a huge round of financing.":"Startup ini berhasil mendapatkan putaran pendanaan yang besar.","funds; capital":"dana; modal","Due to insufficient funds, the project had to be suspended.":"Karena dana tidak mencukupi, proyek terpaksa dihentikan sementara.","asset":"aset","Real estate is his most important asset.":"Properti adalah aset terpentingnya.","debt; liability":"utang; kewajiban","This company's liabilities have already exceeded its assets.":"Kewajiban perusahaan ini sudah melebihi asetnya.","to go bankrupt":"bangkrut","Poor management ultimately drove this old store to declare bankruptcy.":"Pengelolaan yang buruk akhirnya membuat toko lama ini menyatakan bangkrut.","to monopolize":"memonopoli","The government legislated to prevent big corporations from monopolizing the market.":"Pemerintah membuat undang-undang untuk mencegah korporasi besar memonopoli pasar.","to merge and acquire (M&A)":"merger dan akuisisi (M&A)","The merger of these two tech companies has drawn high market attention.":"Merger kedua perusahaan teknologi ini menarik perhatian besar pasar.","to start a business":"memulai usaha","He quit his job and decided to start his own business.":"Dia berhenti kerja dan memutuskan memulai usahanya sendiri.","marketing":"pemasaran","A successful marketing strategy made this product an instant hit.":"Strategi pemasaran yang sukses membuat produk ini langsung laris.","inventory; stock":"persediaan; stok","To clear out inventory, the store launched a big sale.":"Untuk menghabiskan stok, toko mengadakan diskon besar-besaran.","demand; need":"permintaan; kebutuhan","After the pandemic, demand for remote-work equipment surged.":"Setelah pandemi, permintaan perlengkapan kerja jarak jauh melonjak.","interest rate":"suku bunga","The central bank decided to keep the current interest rate unchanged.":"Bank sentral memutuskan mempertahankan suku bunga saat ini.","reward; return":"imbalan; pengembalian","High-risk investments are often accompanied by high returns.":"Investasi berisiko tinggi sering disertai imbal hasil yang tinggi.","earnings; returns":"pendapatan; hasil investasi","This fund's returns last year were quite substantial.":"Hasil investasi dana ini tahun lalu cukup besar.","distribution channel":"saluran distribusi","This brand opened up the youth market through online channels.":"Merek ini membuka pasar anak muda melalui saluran daring.","to be in power; to govern":"berkuasa; memerintah","This party has been in power for eight consecutive years.":"Partai ini telah berkuasa selama delapan tahun berturut-turut.","regime; political power":"rezim; kekuasaan politik","The election results will determine whether there is a change of regime.":"Hasil pemilu akan menentukan apakah terjadi pergantian rezim.","cabinet":"kabinet","The newly appointed premier is in the process of forming his cabinet.":"Perdana menteri yang baru diangkat sedang menyusun kabinetnya.","to legislate; legislation":"membuat undang-undang; legislasi","Many citizens are urging the government to legislate quickly to protect workers' rights.":"Banyak warga mendesak pemerintah segera membuat undang-undang untuk melindungi hak pekerja.","to vote (on a motion)":"memberikan suara (atas suatu mosi)","This bill will be sent to the legislature for a vote next week.":"RUU ini akan dikirim ke lembaga legislatif untuk dipungut suara minggu depan.","referendum":"referendum","This issue was ultimately decided by a nationwide referendum.":"Isu ini akhirnya diputuskan melalui referendum nasional.","opinion poll":"jajak pendapat","The latest poll shows this candidate leading in support.":"Jajak pendapat terbaru menunjukkan kandidat ini unggul dalam dukungan.","to sanction; sanctions":"menjatuhkan sanksi; sanksi","Several countries announced economic sanctions against that country.":"Beberapa negara mengumumkan sanksi ekonomi terhadap negara itu.","situation (political/military)":"situasi (politik/militer)","Experts are closely watching changes in the international situation.":"Para pakar mencermati perubahan situasi internasional dengan saksama.","alliance; league":"aliansi; persekutuan","These companies formed an alliance to jointly develop new technology.":"Perusahaan-perusahaan ini membentuk aliansi untuk bersama-sama mengembangkan teknologi baru.","turbulent; unstable":"bergejolak; tidak stabil","The war plunged the entire region into turmoil.":"Perang membuat seluruh kawasan itu bergejolak.","summit":"konferensi tingkat tinggi","More than a hundred national leaders attended this climate summit.":"Lebih dari seratus pemimpin negara menghadiri KTT iklim ini.","lawsuit; litigation":"gugatan; litigasi","The two sides waged a three-year lawsuit over this debt.":"Kedua pihak berperkara selama tiga tahun atas utang ini.","verdict; ruling":"putusan; vonis","The court's verdict sparked wide public discussion.":"Putusan pengadilan itu memicu diskusi luas di masyarakat.","to compensate; compensation":"memberi ganti rugi; kompensasi","The manufacturer must compensate consumers for their losses.":"Produsen harus memberi ganti rugi atas kerugian konsumen.","to break the law; illegal":"melanggar hukum; ilegal","Dumping waste at will is an illegal act.":"Membuang limbah sembarangan adalah tindakan yang melanggar hukum.","to prosecute; to indict":"menuntut; mendakwa","Prosecutors indicted the official on corruption charges.":"Jaksa mendakwa pejabat itu atas tuduhan korupsi.","to guarantee; to safeguard":"menjamin; melindungi","This law aims to safeguard the basic rights of disadvantaged groups.":"Undang-undang ini bertujuan melindungi hak dasar kelompok rentan.","to authorize; to license":"memberi wewenang; melisensikan","This game is an officially licensed version.":"Gim ini adalah versi berlisensi resmi.","evidence":"bukti","The police have obtained sufficient evidence.":"Polisi telah memperoleh bukti yang cukup.","laws and regulations":"peraturan perundang-undangan","Businesses must comply with the relevant food safety regulations.":"Pelaku usaha harus mematuhi peraturan keamanan pangan yang terkait.","philosophy; ideal":"filosofi; ideal","This company's management philosophy is integrity and innovation.":"Filosofi manajemen perusahaan ini adalah integritas dan inovasi.","indicator; benchmark":"indikator; tolok ukur","The unemployment rate is one of the key indicators for measuring the economy.":"Tingkat pengangguran adalah salah satu indikator kunci untuk mengukur ekonomi.","core":"inti","Technological R&D is this company's core competitiveness.":"Penelitian dan pengembangan teknologi adalah daya saing inti perusahaan ini.","way; approach; channel":"cara; pendekatan; jalur","Education is the most effective way to reduce the wealth gap.":"Pendidikan adalah cara paling efektif untuk mengurangi kesenjangan kekayaan.","characteristic; feature":"ciri; karakteristik","The most obvious feature of this plant is its heart-shaped leaves.":"Ciri paling menonjol tanaman ini adalah daunnya yang berbentuk hati.","meaning; significance":"makna; arti penting","This collaboration holds great significance for both sides.":"Kerja sama ini memiliki arti penting yang besar bagi kedua pihak.","to explore":"menjelajahi; mengeksplorasi","Humanity has never stopped exploring the mysteries of the universe.":"Umat manusia tidak pernah berhenti menjelajahi misteri alam semesta.","to clarify; to sort out":"menjernihkan; menguraikan","We need to first clarify the whole sequence of events.":"Kita perlu terlebih dahulu menguraikan seluruh rangkaian kejadiannya.","to define; to delimit":"mendefinisikan; membatasi","It is hard to legally define responsibility for this kind of behavior.":"Sulit mendefinisikan tanggung jawab hukum atas perilaku semacam ini.","to cover; to encompass":"mencakup; meliputi","This report covers statistical data from the past ten years.":"Laporan ini mencakup data statistik sepuluh tahun terakhir.","to attend to both; to balance":"menyeimbangkan; mengurus keduanya","How to balance work and family is a dilemma for many people.":"Bagaimana menyeimbangkan pekerjaan dan keluarga adalah dilema bagi banyak orang.","to endow; to grant":"menganugerahkan; memberikan","The constitution grants the people the right to freedom of speech.":"Konstitusi memberikan rakyat hak atas kebebasan berpendapat.","to plan; to map out":"merencanakan; merancang","The city government is planning a new metro line.":"Pemerintah kota sedang merencanakan jalur kereta bawah tanah baru.","to strengthen; to reinforce":"memperkuat; meningkatkan","The government decided to strengthen border quarantine measures.":"Pemerintah memutuskan memperkuat langkah karantina di perbatasan.","to promote; to push forward":"mendorong; menggalakkan","This organization has long promoted the idea of gender equality.":"Organisasi ini sudah lama menggalakkan gagasan kesetaraan gender.","to involve; to relate to":"melibatkan; berkaitan dengan","This case involves a huge sum of money.":"Kasus ini melibatkan uang dalam jumlah besar.","to measure; to weigh up":"mengukur; menimbang","By what standard should we measure a person's success?":"Dengan standar apa kita mengukur kesuksesan seseorang?","let alone; much less":"apalagi; jangankan","Even experts can't solve it, let alone us.":"Pakar saja tidak bisa menyelesaikannya, apalagi kita.","conversely; on the contrary":"sebaliknya","Moderate exercise benefits health; conversely, excessive exercise is harmful.":"Olahraga secukupnya bermanfaat bagi kesehatan; sebaliknya, olahraga berlebihan merugikan.","by this means; to take this opportunity":"dengan cara itu; memanfaatkan kesempatan itu","The company holds seminars to thereby improve employees' professional skills.":"Perusahaan mengadakan seminar untuk dengan begitu meningkatkan keterampilan profesional karyawan.","if; supposing":"jika; seandainya","If it rains heavily tomorrow, the event will be postponed by a week.":"Jika besok hujan deras, acara akan ditunda seminggu.","only (by/if)":"hanya (jika/dengan)","Only if everyone works together can we improve environmental problems.":"Hanya jika semua orang bekerja sama, kita dapat memperbaiki masalah lingkungan.","once; in case":"begitu; seandainya","Once trust is lost, it is very hard to win back.":"Begitu kepercayaan hilang, sangat sulit untuk merebutnya kembali.","such as; for example":"seperti; misalnya","Many industries, such as tourism and catering, were all hit hard.":"Banyak industri, seperti pariwisata dan kuliner, semuanya terpukul keras.","by every possible means":"dengan segala cara","He tried by every possible means to save this relationship.":"Dia berusaha dengan segala cara untuk menyelamatkan hubungan ini.","unprecedented":"belum pernah terjadi sebelumnya","This pandemic brought unprecedented challenges to the whole world.":"Pandemi ini membawa tantangan yang belum pernah terjadi sebelumnya bagi seluruh dunia.","as everyone knows":"seperti yang diketahui semua orang","As everyone knows, Taiwan's night market culture is very famous.":"Seperti yang diketahui semua orang, budaya pasar malam Taiwan sangat terkenal.","largely the same with minor differences":"pada dasarnya sama dengan sedikit perbedaan","These companies' products are actually much the same.":"Produk perusahaan-perusahaan ini sebenarnya hampir sama saja.","once in a lifetime; extremely rare":"sekali seumur hidup; sangat langka","This is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity; don't miss it.":"Ini kesempatan sekali seumur hidup; jangan sampai terlewat.","clear at a glance":"jelas dalam sekali pandang","Presenting the data in charts makes it clear at a glance.":"Menyajikan data dalam grafik membuatnya jelas dalam sekali pandang.","to research and develop (R&D)":"meneliti dan mengembangkan (litbang/R&D)","This company invests heavily in R&D every year.":"Perusahaan ini berinvestasi besar dalam litbang setiap tahun.","innovation; to innovate":"inovasi; berinovasi","Constant innovation is the key to a company's survival.":"Inovasi terus-menerus adalah kunci kelangsungan hidup sebuah perusahaan.","to break through; breakthrough":"menerobos; terobosan","The research team achieved a major breakthrough in cancer treatment.":"Tim peneliti mencapai terobosan besar dalam pengobatan kanker.","chip (semiconductor)":"cip (semikonduktor)","Chips made in Taiwan supply many major tech companies worldwide.":"Cip buatan Taiwan memasok banyak perusahaan teknologi besar di seluruh dunia.","data":"data","The company analyzes consumer behavior through big data.":"Perusahaan menganalisis perilaku konsumen melalui data besar.","the cloud (computing)":"awan (komputasi)","These files are all backed up in the cloud, so there's no fear of losing them.":"Berkas-berkas ini semuanya dicadangkan di awan, jadi tak perlu takut hilang.","patent":"paten","This technology has already been patented.":"Teknologi ini sudah dipatenkan.","satellite":"satelit","This satellite will be responsible for monitoring global climate change.":"Satelit ini akan bertugas memantau perubahan iklim global.","heritage; inheritance":"warisan; pusaka","This ancient city is listed as a world cultural heritage site.":"Kota kuno ini terdaftar sebagai situs warisan budaya dunia.","historic site; monument":"situs bersejarah; monumen","The government is spending funds to restore these precious historic sites.":"Pemerintah mengeluarkan dana untuk memugar situs-situs bersejarah yang berharga ini.","to symbolize; symbol":"melambangkan; simbol","This bridge symbolizes the friendship between the peoples of the two places.":"Jembatan ini melambangkan persahabatan antara masyarakat kedua tempat.","to blend; to fuse":"memadukan; menyatukan","This dish cleverly blends Taiwanese and Japanese flavors.":"Hidangan ini dengan cerdik memadukan cita rasa Taiwan dan Jepang.","faith; belief":"keyakinan; kepercayaan","Religious faith plays an important role in life in Taiwan.":"Keyakinan agama memainkan peran penting dalam kehidupan di Taiwan.","policy":"kebijakan","The government rolled out a new childcare policy.":"Pemerintah meluncurkan kebijakan pengasuhan anak yang baru.","news report; coverage":"berita; liputan","This report drew the attention of the general public.":"Liputan ini menarik perhatian masyarakat luas.","incident; event":"insiden; peristiwa","The police are investigating this food safety incident.":"Polisi sedang menyelidiki insiden keamanan pangan ini.","to investigate; survey":"menyelidiki; survei","According to the latest survey, over sixty percent of the public support this policy.":"Menurut survei terbaru, lebih dari enam puluh persen masyarakat mendukung kebijakan ini.","trend":"tren","Remote work has already become a global trend.":"Kerja jarak jauh sudah menjadi tren global.","public opinion":"opini publik","This decision sparked strong criticism from public opinion.":"Keputusan ini memicu kritik keras dari opini publik.","media":"media","All the major media outlets covered this press conference.":"Semua media besar meliput konferensi pers ini.","phenomenon":"fenomena","Late marriage has become a common social phenomenon in Taiwan.":"Menikah terlambat telah menjadi fenomena sosial yang umum di Taiwan.","crisis":"krisis","The company is facing a serious financial crisis.":"Perusahaan sedang menghadapi krisis keuangan yang serius.","issue; topic":"isu; topik","Environmental issues are receiving more and more attention from young people.":"Isu lingkungan semakin mendapat perhatian dari kaum muda.","the public; the people":"publik; masyarakat","Many members of the public came to the scene to express their dissatisfaction.":"Banyak anggota masyarakat datang ke lokasi untuk menyatakan ketidakpuasan.","to announce":"mengumumkan","The government announced that the minimum wage will be raised next year.":"Pemerintah mengumumkan bahwa upah minimum akan dinaikkan tahun depan.","Taiwan's population has seen negative growth for several years in a row.":"Populasi Taiwan mengalami pertumbuhan negatif beberapa tahun berturut-turut.","to age (population, etc.)":"menua (populasi, dll.)","Population aging brings many challenges to society.":"Penuaan populasi membawa banyak tantangan bagi masyarakat.","gap; disparity":"kesenjangan; jurang","The education gap between urban and rural areas is growing wider.":"Kesenjangan pendidikan antara kota dan desa semakin melebar.","ethnic group; community":"kelompok etnis; komunitas","Taiwan is a society of diverse ethnic groups.":"Taiwan adalah masyarakat dengan beragam kelompok etnis.","welfare; benefits":"kesejahteraan; tunjangan","The employee benefits this company offers are quite good.":"Tunjangan karyawan yang ditawarkan perusahaan ini cukup baik.","declining birthrate":"penurunan angka kelahiran","The declining birthrate has left many schools facing closure.":"Penurunan angka kelahiran membuat banyak sekolah terancam tutup.","to be unemployed":"menganggur","After being unemployed for half a year, he finally found a new job.":"Setelah menganggur setengah tahun, akhirnya dia mendapat pekerjaan baru.","to discriminate; discrimination":"mendiskriminasi; diskriminasi","No form of discrimination should be tolerated.":"Segala bentuk diskriminasi tidak boleh ditoleransi.","equal; equality":"setara; kesetaraan","Everyone should enjoy equal educational opportunities.":"Setiap orang seharusnya menikmati kesempatan pendidikan yang setara.","system; institution":"sistem; institusi","The company recently revised its leave system.":"Perusahaan baru-baru ini merevisi sistem cutinya.","to immigrate; immigrant":"berimigrasi; imigran","More and more young people are considering emigrating abroad.":"Semakin banyak anak muda mempertimbangkan untuk beremigrasi ke luar negeri.","generation":"generasi","Different generations have very different views on work.":"Generasi yang berbeda memiliki pandangan yang sangat berbeda tentang pekerjaan.","to invest; investment":"berinvestasi; investasi","Before investing in stocks, you should do your homework first.":"Sebelum berinvestasi saham, sebaiknya lakukan riset dulu.","cost":"biaya","Rising raw material prices have greatly increased production costs.":"Naiknya harga bahan baku sangat meningkatkan biaya produksi.","profit":"keuntungan; laba","The profit on this product is actually not high.":"Keuntungan dari produk ini sebenarnya tidak tinggi.","This company plans to enter the Southeast Asian market.":"Perusahaan ini berencana masuk ke pasar Asia Tenggara.","brand":"merek","This Taiwanese brand is becoming more and more famous internationally.":"Merek Taiwan ini semakin terkenal di kancah internasional.","to compete; competition":"bersaing; persaingan","Competition in the hand-shaken drink market is extremely fierce.":"Persaingan di pasar minuman kocok (bubble tea) sangat sengit.","enterprise; company":"perusahaan; badan usaha","Many companies are starting to pay attention to employees' mental health.":"Banyak perusahaan mulai memperhatikan kesehatan mental karyawan.","to run; to manage (a business)":"menjalankan; mengelola (usaha)","He has been running this restaurant for twenty years.":"Dia sudah menjalankan restoran ini selama dua puluh tahun.","to consume; consumption":"mengonsumsi; konsumsi","Young people's consumption habits are very different from the previous generation's.":"Kebiasaan konsumsi anak muda sangat berbeda dari generasi sebelumnya.","industry":"industri","Semiconductors are one of Taiwan's most important industries.":"Semikonduktor adalah salah satu industri terpenting Taiwan.","revenue":"pendapatan; omzet","The company's revenue this year hit a record high.":"Pendapatan perusahaan tahun ini mencapai rekor tertinggi.","prices (of goods)":"harga (barang)","Prices keep rising, but salaries have not been adjusted accordingly.":"Harga terus naik, tetapi gaji tidak ikut disesuaikan.","salary; wages":"gaji; upah","The salary for this job is a bit higher than the market rate.":"Gaji pekerjaan ini sedikit lebih tinggi daripada rata-rata pasar.","economic conditions; business climate":"kondisi ekonomi; iklim usaha","With the economy in a slump, many shops can no longer stay afloat.":"Dengan ekonomi yang lesu, banyak toko tak lagi mampu bertahan.","pollution":"polusi; pencemaran","Wastewater discharged by factories has caused river pollution.":"Air limbah yang dibuang pabrik telah mencemari sungai.","climate":"iklim","Climate change has affected agricultural production worldwide.":"Perubahan iklim telah memengaruhi produksi pertanian di seluruh dunia.","energy (resources)":"energi (sumber daya)","The government is promoting the development of renewable energy.":"Pemerintah sedang mendorong pengembangan energi terbarukan.","to recycle":"mendaur ulang","These plastic bottles can be recycled and reused.":"Botol-botol plastik ini bisa didaur ulang dan digunakan kembali.","Bringing your own shopping bag is the simplest eco-friendly action.":"Membawa tas belanja sendiri adalah aksi ramah lingkungan yang paling sederhana.","resources":"sumber daya","The earth's resources are limited, so we should cherish them.":"Sumber daya bumi terbatas, jadi kita harus menghargainya.","ecology; ecosystem":"ekologi; ekosistem","Overdevelopment has destroyed the local ecosystem.":"Pembangunan berlebihan telah merusak ekosistem setempat.","to emit; to discharge":"mengemisi; membuang","Countries have pledged to reduce carbon dioxide emissions.":"Berbagai negara berjanji mengurangi emisi karbon dioksida.","to save energy":"menghemat energi","This type of air conditioner is very energy-efficient.":"AC jenis ini sangat hemat energi.","disaster":"bencana","The damage caused by the typhoon was worse than expected.":"Kerusakan akibat topan lebih parah dari perkiraan.","The public's attitude toward this policy is gradually changing.":"Sikap masyarakat terhadap kebijakan ini perlahan berubah.","obviously; evidently":"jelas; nyata","He is obviously not ready to accept this outcome yet.":"Dia jelas belum siap menerima hasil ini.","substantially; by a large margin":"secara signifikan; jauh","This company's stock price fell sharply.":"Harga saham perusahaan ini turun tajam.","relatively":"relatif","Compared with the city center, the rent here is relatively cheap.":"Dibandingkan pusat kota, sewa di sini relatif murah.","the whole; overall":"keseluruhan; secara umum","Overall, this event was a great success.":"Secara keseluruhan, acara ini sangat sukses.","common; widespread":"umum; meluas","Overtime is a very common phenomenon in this industry.":"Lembur adalah fenomena yang sangat umum di industri ini.","The difference between these two proposals is very obvious.":"Perbedaan antara kedua proposal ini sangat jelas.","to continue; sustained":"berlanjut; berkelanjutan","Housing prices keep rising, and young people are increasingly unable to afford them.":"Harga rumah terus naik, dan anak muda semakin tidak mampu membelinya.","roughly; more or less":"kira-kira; kurang lebih","I have roughly gone through the report, and there are no major issues.":"Saya sudah membaca laporannya secara garis besar, tidak ada masalah besar.","even; so much so that":"bahkan; sampai-sampai","He is so busy that he doesn't even have time for lunch.":"Dia sibuk sampai-sampai tidak sempat makan siang.","after all":"lagi pula; bagaimanapun","After all, he is still new, so let's give him a bit more time.":"Lagi pula dia masih baru, jadi beri dia sedikit lebih banyak waktu.","hard to avoid; inevitably":"tak terhindarkan; mau tak mau","It's your first time presenting on stage, so being nervous is inevitable.":"Ini pertama kalinya kamu presentasi di panggung, jadi gugup itu tak terhindarkan.","to reflect":"mencerminkan","This film reflects the problems of modern society.":"Film ini mencerminkan masalah-masalah masyarakat modern.","in a mess; chaotic":"berantakan; kacau","His desk is always a complete mess.":"Mejanya selalu berantakan total.","exactly the same":"sama persis","These twins look exactly the same.":"Anak kembar ini terlihat sama persis.","unbelievable; incredible":"sulit dipercaya; luar biasa","He actually finished all the work in three days—it's simply unbelievable.":"Dia benar-benar menyelesaikan semua pekerjaan dalam tiga hari—sungguh sulit dipercaya.","baffling; inexplicable":"membingungkan; tak masuk akal","He suddenly lost his temper at me, and I found it completely baffling.":"Dia tiba-tiba marah kepadaku, dan aku benar-benar bingung.","a matter of course; taken for granted":"hal yang wajar; dianggap sudah semestinya","Don't take other people's help for granted.":"Jangan menganggap bantuan orang lain sebagai hal yang sudah semestinya.","Since you have started, don't give up halfway.":"Karena sudah memulai, jangan menyerah di tengah jalan.","supply falls short of demand":"pasokan tak memenuhi permintaan","This product is so popular that supply has never kept up with demand.":"Produk ini begitu laris sampai pasokan tak pernah cukup memenuhi permintaan.","changing rapidly day by day":"berubah pesat dari hari ke hari","Technology advances rapidly, so we must keep learning.":"Teknologi maju dengan pesat, jadi kita harus terus belajar.","can hardly wait":"tak sabar menunggu","Everyone can hardly wait to find out the result of the competition.":"Semua orang tak sabar ingin tahu hasil pertandingannya.","Voter turnout in this election hit a new high in recent years.":"Tingkat partisipasi pemilih dalam pemilu ini mencapai rekor tertinggi dalam beberapa tahun terakhir.","to vote":"memberikan suara; mencoblos","Many people working away from home made a special trip back to vote.":"Banyak orang yang bekerja jauh dari rumah sengaja pulang untuk mencoblos.","If an employer fails to pay wages as required, they are breaking the law.":"Jika pemberi kerja tidak membayar upah sebagaimana mestinya, itu melanggar hukum.","right":"hak","Workers have the legal right to take paid annual leave.":"Pekerja memiliki hak hukum untuk mengambil cuti tahunan berbayar.","obligation; duty":"kewajiban","Paying taxes is an obligation every citizen must fulfill.":"Membayar pajak adalah kewajiban yang harus dipenuhi setiap warga negara.","norm; regulation":"norma; peraturan","The government is drafting new food safety regulations.":"Pemerintah sedang menyusun peraturan keamanan pangan yang baru.","fine; penalty":"denda; sanksi","Illegal parking can result in a fine of up to 2,400 NT dollars.":"Parkir ilegal dapat dikenai denda hingga 2.400 dolar Taiwan.","academic degree":"gelar akademik","He studied while working and finally earned a master's degree.":"Dia kuliah sambil bekerja dan akhirnya meraih gelar master.","educational background":"latar belakang pendidikan","This job values experience; educational background is not the main point.":"Pekerjaan ini mengutamakan pengalaman; latar belakang pendidikan bukan poin utama.","profession; specialty":"profesi; keahlian","Cross-disciplinary learning can make your expertise more competitive.":"Belajar lintas disiplin dapat membuat keahlian Anda lebih kompetitif.","to train; training":"melatih; pelatihan","The company offers thorough pre-job training, so newcomers need not worry.":"Perusahaan menyediakan pelatihan pra-kerja yang menyeluruh, jadi karyawan baru tak perlu khawatir.","literacy; cultivation":"literasi; kecakapan","Media literacy education helps students tell fake news apart.":"Pendidikan literasi media membantu siswa membedakan berita palsu.","diploma":"ijazah","More and more people believe ability matters more than a diploma.":"Semakin banyak orang percaya kemampuan lebih penting daripada ijazah.","vaccine":"vaksin","Health authorities urge the public to get their flu vaccine as soon as possible.":"Otoritas kesehatan mengimbau masyarakat segera mendapatkan vaksin flu.","epidemic prevention":"pencegahan wabah","During the epidemic prevention period, everyone developed the habit of washing hands frequently.":"Selama masa pencegahan wabah, semua orang membiasakan diri sering mencuci tangan.","to care for; care":"merawat; perawatan","Many families feel great pressure from caring for their elderly parents.":"Banyak keluarga merasa sangat tertekan karena harus merawat orang tua yang lanjut usia.","long-term care":"perawatan jangka panjang","Population aging is rapidly increasing the demand for long-term care.":"Penuaan populasi dengan cepat meningkatkan kebutuhan akan perawatan jangka panjang.","medical care":"layanan medis; pelayanan kesehatan","The quality of medical care in Taiwan is quite well known internationally.":"Kualitas layanan medis di Taiwan cukup terkenal di dunia internasional.","psychology; mental state":"psikologi; kondisi mental","Society is paying more and more attention to office workers' mental health.":"Masyarakat semakin memperhatikan kesehatan mental para pekerja kantoran.","inflation":"inflasi","Inflationary pressure has noticeably raised people's cost of living.":"Tekanan inflasi jelas menaikkan biaya hidup masyarakat.","exchange rate":"nilai tukar","The weak yen exchange rate is drawing large numbers of Taiwanese tourists to Japan.":"Nilai tukar yen yang lemah menarik banyak wisatawan Taiwan ke Jepang.","stock; share":"saham","The stock market has been very volatile lately, making investors quite nervous.":"Pasar saham belakangan sangat bergejolak, membuat para investor cukup cemas.","loan":"pinjaman","The couple is carrying a thirty-year home loan.":"Pasangan ini menanggung pinjaman rumah berjangka tiga puluh tahun.","budget":"anggaran","The council cut next year's tourism budget.":"Dewan memangkas anggaran pariwisata tahun depan.","May is tax season in Taiwan, so remember to file your income tax on time.":"Bulan Mei adalah musim pajak di Taiwan, jadi ingat untuk melaporkan pajak penghasilan tepat waktu.","subsidy":"subsidi","The government provides rent subsidies to ease the burden on young people.":"Pemerintah memberikan subsidi sewa untuk meringankan beban anak muda.","allowance; benefit":"tunjangan","The company pays its expatriate employees an overseas allowance every month.":"Perusahaan membayar tunjangan luar negeri kepada karyawan ekspatriatnya setiap bulan.","artificial intelligence":"kecerdasan buatan","Artificial intelligence is changing the way every industry works.":"Kecerdasan buatan sedang mengubah cara kerja setiap industri.","algorithm":"algoritma","Social media algorithms decide what content you get to see.":"Algoritma media sosial menentukan konten apa yang bisa Anda lihat.","privacy":"privasi","People are increasingly concerned about the protection of personal data and privacy.":"Orang semakin peduli terhadap perlindungan data pribadi dan privasi.","to scam; fraud":"menipu; penipuan","Police remind the public to beware of scams disguised as investment offers.":"Polisi mengingatkan masyarakat untuk mewaspadai penipuan yang menyamar sebagai tawaran investasi.","disinformation; fake news":"disinformasi; berita palsu","During elections, there is especially a lot of disinformation online.":"Selama pemilu, disinformasi di internet sangat banyak.","digital":"digital","Many traditional industries are undergoing digital transformation.":"Banyak industri tradisional sedang menjalani transformasi digital.","to enhance; to raise":"meningkatkan","The company introduced new equipment in hopes of raising production efficiency.":"Perusahaan memperkenalkan peralatan baru dengan harapan meningkatkan efisiensi produksi.","to promote; to facilitate":"mendorong; memfasilitasi","The purpose of this event is to promote cultural exchange between the two countries.":"Tujuan acara ini adalah mendorong pertukaran budaya antara kedua negara.","to lead to; to result in":"menyebabkan; berujung pada","Long-term lack of sleep may lead to reduced concentration.":"Kurang tidur dalam jangka panjang dapat menyebabkan penurunan konsentrasi.","to cause; to bring about":"menimbulkan; mengakibatkan","The heavy rain caused serious damage in the southern region.":"Hujan lebat menimbulkan kerusakan serius di wilayah selatan.","To avoid misunderstandings, it is best to confirm important matters in writing.":"Untuk menghindari kesalahpahaman, sebaiknya konfirmasikan hal-hal penting secara tertulis.","to maintain":"mempertahankan; menjaga","The central bank decided to keep interest rates unchanged.":"Bank sentral memutuskan mempertahankan suku bunga tidak berubah.","to expand":"memperluas; mengembangkan","This chain store plans to expand its business scale next year.":"Toko waralaba ini berencana memperluas skala usahanya tahun depan.","to narrow; to reduce":"mempersempit; mengurangi","The government hopes to narrow the urban-rural gap through subsidies.":"Pemerintah berharap mempersempit kesenjangan kota-desa melalui subsidi.","to improve":"memperbaiki; meningkatkan","The new traffic measures have clearly improved rush-hour congestion.":"Langkah lalu lintas yang baru jelas memperbaiki kemacetan pada jam sibuk.","to worsen; to deteriorate":"memburuk; merosot","If not handled in time, relations between the two countries may keep deteriorating.":"Jika tidak ditangani tepat waktu, hubungan kedua negara bisa terus memburuk.","Many people are so busy with work that they neglect their own health.":"Banyak orang begitu sibuk bekerja sampai mengabaikan kesehatan mereka sendiri.","to value; to attach importance to":"menghargai; menaruh perhatian pada","This company attaches great importance to employees' work-life balance.":"Perusahaan ini sangat menghargai keseimbangan kerja dan kehidupan karyawannya.","to face; to be confronted with":"menghadapi","Many traditional bookstores are facing the challenge of business difficulties.":"Banyak toko buku tradisional menghadapi tantangan kesulitan usaha.","Once you overcome the language barrier, living abroad becomes much easier.":"Begitu Anda mengatasi hambatan bahasa, hidup di luar negeri menjadi jauh lebih mudah.","serious; severe":"serius; parah","The labor shortage is especially serious in the restaurant industry.":"Kekurangan tenaga kerja sangat parah di industri restoran.","major; significant":"besar; signifikan","This ruling has major significance for society.":"Putusan ini memiliki arti penting yang besar bagi masyarakat.","key; crux":"kunci; inti persoalan","Whether a company can retain talent is the key to its success or failure.":"Apakah perusahaan mampu mempertahankan talenta adalah kunci keberhasilan atau kegagalannya.","urgent; pressing":"mendesak","The need for medical resources in remote areas is quite pressing.":"Kebutuhan sumber daya medis di daerah terpencil cukup mendesak.","Experts are optimistic about the economy's performance in the second half of the year.":"Para pakar optimistis terhadap kinerja ekonomi pada paruh kedua tahun ini.","Facing high housing prices, many young people feel pessimistic about buying a home.":"Menghadapi harga rumah yang tinggi, banyak anak muda merasa pesimis untuk membeli rumah.","stable":"stabil","Rather than a high salary, he wants a stable job.":"Daripada gaji tinggi, dia menginginkan pekerjaan yang stabil.","drastic; intense":"drastis; ekstrem","With drastic temperature changes, the public is reminded to keep warm.":"Dengan perubahan suhu yang ekstrem, masyarakat diimbau menjaga kehangatan tubuh.","to keep pace with the times":"mengikuti perkembangan zaman","Regulations must also keep pace with the times to address problems brought by new technology.":"Peraturan juga harus mengikuti perkembangan zaman untuk mengatasi masalah yang dibawa teknologi baru.","supply exceeds demand":"pasokan melebihi permintaan","In some areas, the housing market is already showing signs of oversupply.":"Di beberapa daerah, pasar perumahan sudah menunjukkan tanda-tanda kelebihan pasokan.","to emerge one after another":"bermunculan silih berganti","New scam tactics keep emerging one after another, so the public must stay alert.":"Modus penipuan baru terus bermunculan, jadi masyarakat harus tetap waspada.","to be closely related":"berkaitan erat","Exchange rate fluctuations are closely related to our daily lives.":"Fluktuasi nilai tukar berkaitan erat dengan kehidupan sehari-hari kita.","to live up to one's name":"sesuai dengan namanya; tidak mengecewakan reputasinya","Tainan truly lives up to its name as a food capital, with local snacks everywhere.":"Tainan benar-benar layak menyandang julukan kota kuliner, jajanan lokal ada di mana-mana.","essence; nature":"esensi; hakikat","Don't be misled by surface phenomena—see the essence of the problem clearly.":"Jangan tertipu oleh fenomena permukaan—lihat dengan jelas hakikat masalahnya.","connotation; substance":"kandungan makna; substansi","This brand cares not only about appearance but also about cultural substance.":"Merek ini tidak hanya peduli pada tampilan tetapi juga pada substansi budaya.","A declining birthrate has become a social phenomenon many countries face together.":"Penurunan angka kelahiran telah menjadi fenomena sosial yang dihadapi bersama oleh banyak negara.","Remote work has already become an irreversible trend.":"Kerja jarak jauh sudah menjadi tren yang tak bisa dibalikkan.","The company lacks an effective communication mechanism, so information often fails to get through.":"Perusahaan tidak memiliki mekanisme komunikasi yang efektif, sehingga informasi sering tidak tersampaikan.","framework":"kerangka","Only by breaking out of the existing framework can you come up with innovative solutions.":"Hanya dengan keluar dari kerangka yang ada, Anda bisa menemukan solusi yang inovatif.","criterion; guideline":"kriteria; pedoman","Honesty is this company's most fundamental code of conduct.":"Kejujuran adalah pedoman perilaku paling mendasar perusahaan ini.","norm; standard":"norma; standar","After the new law took effect, businesses' operations came under stricter norms.":"Setelah undang-undang baru berlaku, operasi bisnis diatur oleh norma yang lebih ketat.","vision":"visi","A leader must be able to paint a clear vision of the future for the team.":"Seorang pemimpin harus mampu menggambarkan visi masa depan yang jelas bagi timnya.","purpose; tenet":"tujuan; asas","The purpose of establishing this association is to promote local culture.":"Tujuan didirikannya asosiasi ini adalah untuk mempromosikan budaya lokal.","On this controversy, the government has yet to make its position clear.":"Mengenai kontroversi ini, pemerintah belum memperjelas sikapnya.","After repeated discussion, the participants finally forged a consensus.":"Setelah berkali-kali berdiskusi, para peserta akhirnya membentuk konsensus.","divergence; disagreement":"perbedaan pendapat; ketidaksepakatan","The two sides still have major disagreements over key conditions.":"Kedua pihak masih memiliki perbedaan pendapat yang besar mengenai syarat-syarat utama.","gap; discrepancy":"kesenjangan; ketimpangan","The gap between ideals and reality often leaves young people feeling frustrated.":"Kesenjangan antara ideal dan kenyataan sering membuat anak muda merasa frustrasi.","hub; pivot":"pusat; simpul","Taoyuan Airport is a major international transport hub for Taiwan.":"Bandara Taoyuan adalah simpul transportasi internasional utama bagi Taiwan.","lifeblood; lifeline":"urat nadi; tumpuan kehidupan","The semiconductor industry can be called the lifeblood of Taiwan's economy.":"Industri semikonduktor bisa disebut sebagai urat nadi ekonomi Taiwan.","The incident sparked a strong public backlash online.":"Insiden ini memicu reaksi keras dari publik di internet.","malpractice; drawback":"penyimpangan; kelemahan","Poorly designed systems often give rise to all kinds of malpractice.":"Sistem yang dirancang buruk sering menimbulkan berbagai penyimpangan.","to expose; to disclose":"membongkar; mengungkap","This report exposed the hidden truths behind the food factory.":"Liputan ini membongkar kebenaran tersembunyi di balik pabrik makanan itu.","to lay (a foundation)":"meletakkan (fondasi)","These years of effort laid the foundation for his later success.":"Bertahun-tahun usaha ini meletakkan fondasi bagi kesuksesannya kemudian.","to establish; to set up":"menegakkan; membangun","This athlete set an excellent example for the younger generation.":"Atlet ini menjadi teladan yang luar biasa bagi generasi muda.","to uphold; to adhere to":"menjunjung; berpegang teguh pada","He has always upheld his original intention of serving others.":"Ia selalu memegang teguh niat awalnya untuk melayani orang lain.","to carry through; to implement fully":"menjalankan hingga tuntas; melaksanakan sepenuhnya","A policy must be carried through to the end so it isn't abandoned halfway.":"Sebuah kebijakan harus dijalankan hingga tuntas agar tidak ditinggalkan di tengah jalan.","to put into practice; to implement":"menerapkan; melaksanakan","Even the finest ideals are just empty talk if they can't be put into practice.":"Sebagus apa pun cita-citanya, jika tidak bisa diterapkan maka hanya menjadi omong kosong.","to advocate; to promote":"menganjurkan; mempromosikan","This organization has long advocated the idea of gender equality.":"Organisasi ini sudah lama menganjurkan gagasan kesetaraan gender.","to appeal; to call on":"menyerukan; mengimbau","Experts are calling on the public to reduce the use of single-use plastics.":"Para ahli menyerukan agar masyarakat mengurangi penggunaan plastik sekali pakai.","to follow; to abide by":"mengikuti; mematuhi","Construction must follow the relevant safety regulations.":"Pembangunan harus mematuhi peraturan keselamatan yang berlaku.","to check and balance":"saling mengawasi dan mengimbangi","The separation of powers aims to have branches check one another and prevent overconcentration of power.":"Pemisahan kekuasaan bertujuan agar cabang-cabang saling mengawasi dan mencegah pemusatan kekuasaan yang berlebihan.","to check; to hold in check":"menahan; mengekang","The existence of an opposition party effectively holds those in power in check.":"Keberadaan partai oposisi secara efektif mengekang mereka yang berkuasa.","to defend; to safeguard":"membela; menjaga","Journalists have a responsibility to defend freedom of speech.":"Wartawan memiliki tanggung jawab untuk membela kebebasan berbicara.","to maintain; to hold together":"memelihara; menjaga tetap utuh","No matter how far apart we are, I want to work at maintaining this friendship.":"Sejauh apa pun kita terpisah, aku ingin berusaha menjaga persahabatan ini.","to continue; to carry on":"melanjutkan; meneruskan","This traditional craft needs someone to carry it on.":"Kerajinan tradisional ini membutuhkan seseorang untuk meneruskannya.","to derive; to give rise to":"menimbulkan; melahirkan","The rise of new technology has also given rise to many unprecedented problems.":"Kemunculan teknologi baru juga menimbulkan banyak masalah yang belum pernah ada sebelumnya.","to evolve; to develop":"berevolusi; berkembang","This fishing village gradually evolved into a popular tourist destination.":"Desa nelayan ini perlahan berkembang menjadi destinasi wisata yang populer.","to sprout; to arise (an idea)":"muncul; timbul (suatu gagasan)","Seeing the plight of the disaster victims, he began to feel the urge to volunteer.":"Melihat penderitaan para korban bencana, ia mulai merasa terdorong untuk menjadi relawan.","to spread; to sprawl":"menyebar; merambat","Rumors spread rapidly on social media and are hard to control.":"Rumor menyebar dengan cepat di media sosial dan sulit dikendalikan.","to permeate; to pervade":"meresap; memenuhi","After the rain, the forest is filled with the fresh scent of earth.":"Setelah hujan, hutan dipenuhi aroma tanah yang segar.","to create; to achieve":"menciptakan; meraih","This team achieved a record of three consecutive championships.":"Tim ini menciptakan rekor tiga kali juara berturut-turut.","to hold in high esteem":"sangat menghargai; menjunjung tinggi","This director's works are highly esteemed by film critics.":"Karya-karya sutradara ini sangat dihargai oleh para kritikus film.","to attack (verbally); to lash out at":"menyerang (dengan kata-kata); melontarkan kecaman","As soon as the policy was announced, it drew fierce criticism from all quarters.":"Begitu kebijakan itu diumumkan, ia langsung menuai kritik keras dari berbagai pihak.","to condemn; to denounce":"mengutuk; mengecam","The international community unanimously condemns such acts of violence.":"Komunitas internasional dengan bulat mengutuk tindakan kekerasan semacam itu.","to consult; to confer":"berunding; berkonsultasi","The two countries are holding intensive consultations on tariff issues.":"Kedua negara sedang melakukan konsultasi intensif mengenai masalah tarif.","to lobby; to canvass":"melobi; menggalang dukungan","Businesses are actively lobbying legislators to support the amendment.":"Kalangan bisnis aktif melobi anggota legislatif untuk mendukung amandemen tersebut.","to restrict; to constrain":"membatasi; mengekang","Insufficient funding has constrained the progress of this research.":"Pendanaan yang tidak mencukupi telah menghambat kemajuan penelitian ini.","to resist; to withstand":"melawan; menahan","The thick city walls enabled the ancient city to withstand invasion by enemies.":"Tembok kota yang tebal memungkinkan kota kuno itu menahan serbuan musuh.","to deduce; to interpret (a performance)":"menafsirkan; membawakan (suatu penampilan)","This singer reinterpreted the old song with a gentle voice.":"Penyanyi ini membawakan ulang lagu lama itu dengan suara yang lembut.","appeal; core message":"pesan utama; inti pesan","This ad's appeal is clear—it emphasizes being healthy and natural.":"Pesan iklan ini jelas—menekankan pada kesehatan dan kealamian.","to emphasize; to focus on":"menekankan; berfokus pada","This course places special emphasis on developing speaking ability.":"Kursus ini secara khusus menekankan pengembangan kemampuan berbicara.","far-reaching; profound":"berjangkauan luas; mendalam","This teacher has had a far-reaching influence on my whole life.":"Guru ini memberikan pengaruh yang mendalam bagi seluruh hidup saya.","deep; profound":"dalam; mendalam","His eyes are deep, as if hiding many stories.":"Matanya dalam, seolah menyembunyikan banyak kisah.","meticulous; thorough":"teliti; menyeluruh","After a meticulous investigation, the truth of the case finally came to light.":"Setelah penyelidikan yang teliti, kebenaran kasus itu akhirnya terungkap.","rigorous; precise":"cermat; tepat","The attitude toward scientific research must be rigorous, with no room for sloppiness.":"Sikap terhadap penelitian ilmiah harus cermat, tanpa ada kelonggaran untuk kecerobohan.","incisive; penetrating":"tajam; menusuk","His analysis of the current situation is incisive and admirable.":"Analisisnya tentang situasi saat ini tajam dan mengagumkan.","consummate; superb":"sempurna; luar biasa","This old craftsman's carving skills are truly superb.":"Keterampilan mengukir pengrajin tua ini benar-benar luar biasa.","outstanding; excellent":"menonjol; unggul","Her outstanding academic achievements have earned international recognition.":"Prestasi akademiknya yang menonjol telah mendapat pengakuan internasional.","remarkable; significant":"signifikan; nyata","The new teaching method led to a significant improvement in students' grades.":"Metode pengajaran baru menghasilkan peningkatan nilai siswa yang signifikan.","subtle; delicate":"halus; peka","After this incident, the relationship between the two became somewhat delicate.":"Setelah kejadian ini, hubungan antara keduanya menjadi agak peka.","ambiguous; equivocal":"ambigu; mendua","His answer was ambiguous, making it hard to tell what he really thinks.":"Jawabannya ambigu, sehingga sulit menebak apa yang sebenarnya ia pikirkan.","reserved; implicit":"tertutup; tersirat","Emotional expression in Eastern cultures tends to be more reserved.":"Ungkapan emosi dalam budaya Timur cenderung lebih tertutup.","sharp; incisive":"tajam; jitu","The host's questions were so sharp that the guest could barely keep up.":"Pertanyaan pembawa acara begitu tajam sampai tamu nyaris tak mampu mengimbanginya.","tactful; harmonious":"bijaksana; harmonis","She handles things tactfully and rarely comes into conflict with others.":"Ia menangani berbagai hal dengan bijaksana dan jarang berselisih dengan orang lain.","tactful; euphemistic":"halus; taktis","When turning someone down, a more tactful tone is less likely to hurt feelings.":"Saat menolak seseorang, nada yang lebih halus cenderung tidak menyakiti perasaan.","circuitous; roundabout":"berbelit-belit; berputar-putar","Rather than dropping roundabout hints, it's better to state the problem directly.":"Daripada memberi isyarat berbelit-belit, lebih baik menyatakan masalahnya secara langsung.","admittedly; indeed":"memang; diakui","Admittedly, this method carries risk, but it's worth a try.":"Memang metode ini berisiko, tetapi patut dicoba.","admittedly; it is true that":"memang benar bahwa; diakui bahwa","Talent is admittedly important, but acquired effort is even more indispensable.":"Bakat memang penting, tetapi usaha yang diperoleh lewat kerja keras justru lebih tak tergantikan.","Even if countless difficulties lie ahead, he will never shrink back.":"Meski di depan ada kesulitan yang tak terhitung, ia tak akan pernah surut.","First understand the other party's needs, and then propose a suitable plan.":"Pahami dulu kebutuhan pihak lain, baru ajukan rencana yang sesuai.","thus; thereby":"dengan demikian; sehingga","They improved the workflow and thereby greatly boosted efficiency.":"Mereka memperbaiki alur kerja dan dengan demikian meningkatkan efisiensi secara drastis.","up to now; to date":"hingga kini; sampai saat ini","To this day, this mystery still has no definitive answer.":"Hingga kini, misteri ini masih belum memiliki jawaban pasti.","for the time being; tentatively":"untuk sementara; buat sementara","Let's set aside whether this is true for now and first think about how to respond.":"Untuk sementara kesampingkan dulu apakah ini benar, dan pikirkan dulu cara menanggapinya.","to persevere; to keep at it":"gigih; bertahan terus","The key to exercise is perseverance, not a momentary burst of enthusiasm.":"Kunci berolahraga adalah kegigihan, bukan semangat sesaat.","to consider carefully; to deliberate":"mempertimbangkan masak-masak; menimbang","This is a decision made after careful deliberation, and I won't regret it.":"Ini adalah keputusan yang diambil setelah pertimbangan matang, dan aku tak akan menyesalinya.","to hit the nail on the head":"tepat mengena pada intinya","He pointed out the flaw in the entire plan with pinpoint accuracy.":"Ia menunjukkan kelemahan seluruh rencana itu dengan sangat jitu.","vividly and thoroughly; to the fullest":"secara hidup dan tuntas; sampai ke akar-akarnya","This novel portrays human greed vividly and to the fullest.":"Novel ini menggambarkan keserakahan manusia secara hidup dan tuntas.","icing on the cake":"melengkapi yang sudah baik; kian sempurna","This dessert is already great, and pairing it with this tea is the icing on the cake.":"Pencuci mulut ini sudah enak, dan dipadukan dengan teh ini membuatnya makin sempurna.","to provide timely help":"memberi bantuan tepat pada waktunya","When I was at my hardest, he provided timely help by lending me money.":"Saat aku paling kesulitan, ia memberi bantuan tepat waktu dengan meminjamiku uang.","to adapt to local conditions":"menyesuaikan dengan kondisi setempat","Policies should be adapted to local conditions, not applied uniformly.":"Kebijakan sebaiknya disesuaikan dengan kondisi setempat, bukan diterapkan secara seragam.","As everyone knows, Taiwan's night-market culture is very famous.":"Seperti diketahui semua orang, budaya pasar malam Taiwan sangat terkenal.","true to its name; worthy of the name":"sesuai dengan namanya; pantas menyandang namanya","With its picturesque scenery, this place is a paradise worthy of the name.":"Dengan pemandangan seindah lukisan, tempat ini benar-benar surga yang pantas menyandang namanya.","it goes without saying":"tak perlu dikatakan lagi; sudah jelas","The importance of health goes without saying, yet it is often overlooked.":"Pentingnya kesehatan tak perlu dikatakan lagi, namun sering diabaikan.","to play a decisive/pivotal role":"memainkan peran yang menentukan/kunci","He is a pivotal figure in the company; no decision can be made without him.":"Ia adalah tokoh kunci di perusahaan; tak ada keputusan yang bisa dibuat tanpanya.","deep-rooted; deeply ingrained":"berakar kuat; tertanam dalam","Such notions of favoring sons over daughters remain deeply ingrained in some places.":"Anggapan mengutamakan anak laki-laki atas perempuan seperti itu masih tertanam kuat di beberapa tempat.","Eating habits are closely related to health, so one cannot be careless about them.":"Kebiasaan makan berkaitan erat dengan kesehatan, jadi tidak boleh disepelekan.","to emerge endlessly; to keep cropping up":"bermunculan tanpa henti; terus bermunculan","Scam tactics have been cropping up endlessly lately, so the public must stay vigilant.":"Belakangan ini modus penipuan terus bermunculan, jadi masyarakat harus tetap waspada.","to increase day by day":"meningkat dari hari ke hari","As online shopping becomes widespread, demand for logistics keeps growing by the day.":"Seiring meluasnya belanja daring, permintaan logistik terus meningkat dari hari ke hari.","indispensable":"tak tergantikan; sangat diperlukan","The smartphone has become an indispensable tool in modern life.":"Ponsel pintar telah menjadi alat yang tak tergantikan dalam kehidupan modern.","to master thoroughly by integrating knowledge":"menguasai secara menyeluruh dengan mengintegrasikan pengetahuan","Rote memorization is useless; only by mastering it thoroughly can you truly say you've learned it.":"Menghafal mentah-mentah tak berguna; hanya dengan menguasainya secara menyeluruh kamu benar-benar bisa disebut telah memahaminya.","to complete in one go; done in one breath":"menyelesaikan dalam satu tarikan napas; sekali jadi","This essay was written in one flowing stretch and reads very smoothly.":"Esai ini ditulis dalam satu tarikan napas dan sangat lancar dibaca.","to be richly endowed by nature":"dianugerahi alam secara melimpah","This land is richly blessed by nature and is very well suited to growing high-mountain tea.":"Tanah ini dianugerahi alam secara melimpah dan sangat cocok untuk menanam teh pegunungan tinggi.","Since you've decided to do it, don't give up halfway.":"Karena kamu sudah memutuskan untuk melakukannya, jangan menyerah di tengah jalan.","proposition; topic":"proposisi; topik","This paper attempts to answer an age-old philosophical proposition.":"Makalah ini berupaya menjawab sebuah proposisi filsafat yang sudah lama ada.","paradigm; role model":"teladan; panutan","His rigorous scholarly attitude is a true paradigm for younger generations.":"Sikap ilmiahnya yang cermat merupakan teladan sejati bagi generasi muda.","guiding principles; platform":"asas panduan; landasan","This document establishes the guiding principles for the organization's next decade.":"Dokumen ini menetapkan asas panduan bagi organisasi untuk sepuluh tahun ke depan.","blueprint":"cetak biru","The government has drawn a grand blueprint for the city's long-term development.":"Pemerintah telah menyusun cetak biru besar untuk pembangunan jangka panjang kota tersebut.","aspect; dimension":"aspek; dimensi","Evaluating a policy requires considering multiple aspects such as the economic and social.":"Menilai suatu kebijakan memerlukan pertimbangan berbagai aspek seperti ekonomi dan sosial.","element; factor":"unsur; faktor","Trust is the most crucial element in sustaining long-term cooperation.":"Kepercayaan adalah unsur paling penting dalam mempertahankan kerja sama jangka panjang.","incentive; inducement":"insentif; pendorong","Without sufficient incentives, it is hard to attract firms to invest in R&D.":"Tanpa insentif yang memadai, sulit menarik perusahaan untuk berinvestasi dalam litbang.","cause; underlying reason":"sebab; alasan yang mendasari","The research team is exploring the underlying causes of this phenomenon.":"Tim peneliti sedang menyelidiki sebab-sebab mendasar dari fenomena ini.","origin; source":"asal-usul; sumber","The origin of this traditional festival can be traced back over a thousand years.":"Asal-usul festival tradisional ini dapat ditelusuri hingga lebih dari seribu tahun lalu.","root; root cause":"akar; akar penyebab","To solve the problem, you must first identify its root cause.":"Untuk menyelesaikan masalah, kamu harus terlebih dahulu menemukan akar penyebabnya.","sign; omen":"tanda; pertanda","Various signs indicate that the economy is showing symptoms of recovery.":"Berbagai tanda menunjukkan bahwa ekonomi mulai memperlihatkan gejala pemulihan.","situation; posture":"situasi; posisi","The two companies present a posture of intense competition in the market.":"Kedua perusahaan menunjukkan posisi persaingan sengit di pasar.","trend; direction":"tren; arah","Analysts are closely watching the direction of next year's market.":"Para analis mencermati dengan saksama arah pasar tahun depan.","benchmark; standard":"tolok ukur; standar","This survey uses last year's data as the benchmark for comparison.":"Survei ini menggunakan data tahun lalu sebagai tolok ukur perbandingan.","standard; guiding principle":"acuan; asas penuntun","Many creators revere this master's works as their guiding standard.":"Banyak kreator mengagungkan karya-karya maestro ini sebagai acuan penuntun mereka.","chasm; wide gap":"jurang; kesenjangan lebar","The spread of technology has ironically created a new chasm between generations.":"Penyebaran teknologi, ironisnya, justru menciptakan jurang baru antargenerasi.","estrangement; barrier":"keterasingan; penghalang","Years of misunderstanding created a deep estrangement between the two.":"Bertahun-tahun salah paham menciptakan keterasingan yang dalam di antara keduanya.","barrier; protective shield":"penghalang; tameng pelindung","This forest is a natural barrier against strong winds.":"Hutan ini adalah penghalang alami terhadap angin kencang.","constraint; bondage":"belenggu; ikatan","She longs to break free from the constraints of traditional ideas and live as herself.":"Ia mendambakan untuk lepas dari belenggu gagasan tradisional dan hidup sebagai dirinya sendiri.","shackles; fetters":"belenggu; rantai","A rigid system has become the shackles of innovation.":"Sistem yang kaku telah menjadi belenggu bagi inovasi.","appearance; look":"wajah; rupa","This documentary authentically portrays the town's changing appearance over decades.":"Film dokumenter ini menggambarkan secara autentik perubahan wajah kota itu selama beberapa dekade.","normal state; the norm":"kondisi normal; hal yang lumrah","Remote work has gradually become the norm since the pandemic.":"Kerja jarak jauh perlahan menjadi hal yang lumrah sejak pandemi.","law (scientific)":"hukum (ilmiah)","Newton's laws of motion laid the foundation of classical physics.":"Hukum gerak Newton meletakkan dasar bagi fisika klasik.","theorem":"teorema","The proof of this theorem is rather intricate.":"Pembuktian teorema ini cukup rumit.","general rule; general principle":"kaidah umum; prinsip umum","This is only a general rule; actual cases still require individual judgment.":"Ini hanya kaidah umum; kasus nyata tetap memerlukan penilaian tersendiri.","paradigm":"paradigma","The rise of AI is transforming the thinking paradigm of the entire industry.":"Kebangkitan AI sedang mengubah paradigma berpikir seluruh industri.","extent; magnitude":"tingkat; besaran","The magnitude of this year's price increase exceeded everyone's expectations.":"Besaran kenaikan harga tahun ini melampaui perkiraan semua orang.","measure; scale; standard":"ukuran; tolok; standar","Everyone applies a somewhat different measure when judging a work's merit.":"Setiap orang menerapkan ukuran yang agak berbeda saat menilai kualitas sebuah karya.","link; segment (of a process)":"mata rantai; tahapan (dari suatu proses)","Every link in the production process must be error-free.":"Setiap mata rantai dalam proses produksi harus bebas dari kesalahan.","foresight; forward-looking vision":"kejelian ke depan; visi yang berpandangan jauh","This plan is quite forward-looking, anticipating the needs of the next thirty years.":"Rencana ini cukup berpandangan jauh, mengantisipasi kebutuhan tiga puluh tahun ke depan.","hidden danger; latent hazard":"bahaya tersembunyi; ancaman laten","This old building harbors quite a few hidden safety hazards.":"Bangunan tua ini menyimpan cukup banyak bahaya keselamatan yang tersembunyi.","basis to rely on; guiding aim":"landasan berpijak; tujuan penuntun","This firm always makes customer needs the guiding aim of all its decisions.":"Perusahaan ini selalu menjadikan kebutuhan pelanggan sebagai tujuan penuntun bagi semua keputusannya.","demarcation; dividing line":"batas; garis pemisah","As technology advances, the demarcation between disciplines grows ever blurrier.":"Seiring kemajuan teknologi, batas antardisiplin ilmu semakin kabur.","to confirm; to corroborate":"memastikan; menguatkan","The experimental results neatly corroborated his earlier hypothesis.":"Hasil eksperimen dengan rapi menguatkan hipotesisnya yang terdahulu.","to argue; to demonstrate":"berargumen; membuktikan","The author demonstrated his viewpoint with a wealth of historical materials.":"Penulis membuktikan pandangannya dengan sejumlah besar bahan sejarah.","to sum up; to attribute to":"menyimpulkan; menisbatkan pada","He attributed this failure to inadequate preparation.":"Ia menisbatkan kegagalan ini pada persiapan yang kurang memadai.","to touch upon; to reach":"menyinggung; menjangkau","This report touches upon social issues many people would rather not face.":"Laporan ini menyinggung isu-isu sosial yang enggan dihadapi banyak orang.","to focus on; to have in view":"berfokus pada; menyasar","When formulating policy, one should focus on long-term collective interests.":"Saat merumuskan kebijakan, hendaknya berfokus pada kepentingan kolektif jangka panjang.","to focus on":"berfokus pada","This forum focuses on the challenges posed by climate change.":"Forum ini berfokus pada tantangan yang ditimbulkan oleh perubahan iklim.","to place emphasis on":"menitikberatkan pada","This set of materials places relatively more emphasis on spoken expression.":"Rangkaian materi ini relatif lebih menitikberatkan pada ekspresi lisan.","to figure out; to ponder":"mencerna; merenungkan","He repeatedly pondered the director's intent, striving to play the role well.":"Ia berulang kali merenungkan maksud sutradara, berupaya memerankan tokoh itu dengan baik.","to speculate; to conjecture":"menerka; menduga-duga","Before the truth is clarified, we shouldn't recklessly speculate.":"Sebelum kebenarannya jelas, kita tidak boleh sembarangan berspekulasi.","to elucidate; to expound":"menjelaskan; menguraikan","This lecture deeply elucidated the author's core ideas.":"Kuliah ini menjelaskan secara mendalam gagasan inti penulis.","to reveal; to disclose":"mengungkap; menyingkap","This study reveals the close relationship between sleep and memory.":"Studi ini mengungkap hubungan erat antara tidur dan daya ingat.","to criticize; to censure":"mengkritik; mencela","This inefficient system has long been widely criticized.":"Sistem yang tidak efisien ini sudah lama dikritik secara luas.","to interrogate; to press with questions":"menginterogasi; mendesak dengan pertanyaan","Under the reporters' relentless questioning, the spokesperson looked somewhat flustered.":"Di bawah desakan pertanyaan para wartawan, juru bicara itu tampak agak gugup.","to refute; to rebut":"membantah; menyanggah","He cited abundant data and forcefully refuted the other side's claim.":"Ia mengutip banyak data dan dengan tegas membantah klaim pihak lawan.","to critique; to criticize":"mengkritisi; mengkritik","This scholar is known for daring to critique the ills of the times.":"Sarjana ini dikenal karena berani mengkritik penyakit zaman.","to subvert; to overturn":"menjungkirbalikkan; menggulingkan","This technology completely subverted people's notions of communication.":"Teknologi ini benar-benar menjungkirbalikkan anggapan orang tentang komunikasi.","to eliminate; to dispel":"menghilangkan; menghapus","Only through candid communication did the two sides gradually dispel their misunderstandings.":"Hanya melalui komunikasi yang terbuka, kedua pihak perlahan menghapus kesalahpahaman mereka.","to quell; to calm down":"meredakan; menenangkan","The authorities quickly issued a statement to quell public concerns.":"Pihak berwenang segera mengeluarkan pernyataan untuk meredakan kekhawatiran publik.","to resolve; to defuse":"menyelesaikan; mencairkan","A humorous remark cleverly defused the awkwardness in the room.":"Sebuah lelucon dengan cerdik mencairkan kecanggungan di ruangan itu.","to mediate":"menengahi; memediasi","After the neighborhood chief mediated, the two neighbors finally made peace.":"Setelah ketua RT menengahi, kedua tetangga itu akhirnya berdamai.","to negotiate; to parley":"bernegosiasi; berunding","After much negotiation among the parties, the agreement was finally signed.":"Setelah banyak negosiasi antarpihak, perjanjian itu akhirnya ditandatangani.","to master; to control":"menguasai; mengendalikan","This writer can effortlessly master a variety of literary styles.":"Penulis ini dapat menguasai berbagai gaya sastra dengan mudah.","to dominate; to dictate":"mendominasi; mendikte","Rather than be dominated by emotion, better to learn to master it.":"Daripada dikuasai emosi, lebih baik belajar mengendalikannya.","to dominate; to allocate":"mengatur; mengalokasikan","We should learn to allocate our own time wisely.":"Kita sebaiknya belajar mengalokasikan waktu sendiri dengan bijak.","to gauge; to judge the right measure":"menakar; menimbang kadar yang tepat","You must gauge the right measure in your words so as not to offend.":"Kamu harus menakar kadar kata-katamu dengan tepat agar tidak menyinggung.","to make clear; to declare":"menegaskan; menyatakan","This monument declares humanity's eternal pursuit of peace.":"Monumen ini menyatakan pengejaran abadi umat manusia akan perdamaian.","profound; abstruse":"mendalam; sukar dipahami","This philosophy book is profound; you must read it repeatedly to grasp it.":"Buku filsafat ini mendalam; kamu harus membacanya berulang kali untuk memahaminya.","obscure; cryptic":"kabur; berteka-teki","This poem's language is too obscure for ordinary readers to comprehend.":"Bahasa puisi ini terlalu kabur untuk dipahami pembaca awam.","easy to understand; plain":"mudah dipahami; sederhana","This teacher excels at explaining complex principles with plain examples.":"Guru ini pandai menjelaskan prinsip yang rumit dengan contoh yang sederhana.","comprehensive; thorough":"komprehensif; menyeluruh","This plan is remarkably comprehensive, with almost no loopholes.":"Rencana ini sangat komprehensif, nyaris tanpa celah.","detailed; exhaustive":"terperinci; menyeluruh","The report provides an exhaustive explanation of the entire process.":"Laporan itu memberikan penjelasan terperinci tentang seluruh proses.","unique; original (insight)":"unik; orisinal (wawasan)","His analysis of market trends often shows unique insight.":"Analisisnya tentang tren pasar kerap menunjukkan wawasan yang unik.","pertinent; to the point":"tepat sasaran; mengena","His criticism, though harsh, is very much to the point.":"Kritiknya, meski keras, sangat tepat sasaran.","apt; fitting":"tepat; pas","This metaphor is very apt, making the point clear at once.":"Metafora ini sangat tepat, membuat maksudnya langsung jelas.","delicate; exquisite":"halus; lembut","This film portrays its characters' psychology with great delicacy.":"Film ini menggambarkan psikologi tokohnya dengan sangat halus.","grand; magnificent":"megah; agung","This novel is grand in scope, spanning the fates of three generations.":"Novel ini megah dalam cakupannya, membentang meliputi nasib tiga generasi.","meaningful and enduring":"penuh makna dan berkesan lama","This essay's language is plain, yet its mood is deeply meaningful and enduring.":"Bahasa esai ini sederhana, namun nuansanya penuh makna dan berkesan lama.","vague; hollow; empty":"kosong; hampa","This article's arguments are hollow, lacking concrete examples to support them.":"Argumen artikel ini kosong, tanpa contoh konkret untuk mendukungnya.","vague; sweeping; general":"kabur; umum; tak spesifik","Your answer is too vague—could you be a bit more specific?":"Jawabanmu terlalu kabur—bisakah sedikit lebih spesifik?","biased; partial":"berat sebelah; bias","If reporting is biased, it loses its credibility.":"Jika pemberitaan berat sebelah, ia kehilangan kredibilitasnya.","majestic; boundless in momentum":"megah; berdaya dobrak tak terbatas","This landscape painting has a majestic momentum that stuns the viewer.":"Lukisan pemandangan ini memiliki daya megah yang membuat penontonnya terpukau.","just like; as if":"seolah-olah; bagaikan","This town is now thronged with tourists, having become just like a popular attraction.":"Kota ini kini dipadati wisatawan, seolah telah menjadi objek wisata populer.","might as well; simply":"sekalian saja; lebih baik langsung","Since he couldn't sleep, he simply got up and finished his work.":"Karena tak bisa tidur, ia sekalian saja bangun dan menyelesaikan pekerjaannya.","rather too; a bit too":"agak terlalu; sedikit terlalu","Demanding that of others is rather too harsh.":"Menuntut hal itu dari orang lain agak terlalu keras.","how could it be that...not (rhetorical)":"mana mungkin tidak... (retoris)","How could I not want to help you? It's just that I'm truly unable to.":"Mana mungkin aku tak mau membantumu? Hanya saja aku benar-benar tak sanggup.","nothing but; simply":"tidak lain hanyalah; semata-mata","Parents are this strict simply because they want their children to fare well.":"Orang tua sebegitu keras semata-mata karena ingin anak-anaknya sejahtera.","generally; on the whole":"secara umum; pada dasarnya","What he said is generally true, with only a few minor discrepancies.":"Apa yang ia katakan pada dasarnya benar, hanya ada beberapa perbedaan kecil.","or; or else (formal)":"atau; ataukah (formal)","Whether this was coincidence or a deliberate arrangement remains undecided.":"Apakah ini kebetulan ataukah pengaturan yang disengaja masih belum dapat dipastikan.","to have great foresight":"memiliki pandangan jauh ke depan","With great foresight, this entrepreneur positioned himself in green energy years ago.":"Dengan pandangan jauh ke depan, pengusaha ini telah merambah energi hijau bertahun-tahun lalu.","to plan deeply and think far ahead":"merencanakan secara mendalam dan berpikir jauh ke depan","He acts with deep, far-sighted planning, always anticipating every possibility.":"Ia bertindak dengan perencanaan yang mendalam dan berpandangan jauh, selalu mengantisipasi setiap kemungkinan.","to consider the overall situation":"mempertimbangkan situasi secara keseluruhan","To consider the overall situation, he chose to set aside his personal biases for the time being.":"Demi kepentingan keseluruhan, ia memilih untuk sementara mengesampingkan prasangka pribadinya.","to hit the nail on the head with one remark":"sekali ucap langsung mengena pada inti","He hit the nail on the head in one remark, making everyone present suddenly see clearly.":"Sekali ucap ia langsung mengena pada inti, membuat semua yang hadir tiba-tiba tersadar.","to coincide without prior discussion":"sepakat tanpa berunding lebih dulu","Our ideas coincided without any prior discussion—we're really in sync.":"Gagasan kami bertepatan tanpa berunding sebelumnya—kami benar-benar sehati.","each airs their own view":"masing-masing menyampaikan pendapatnya sendiri","At the meeting everyone aired their own views, and the atmosphere was lively.":"Dalam rapat itu semua orang menyampaikan pendapatnya masing-masing, dan suasananya hidup.","to guide according to the circumstances":"membimbing sesuai keadaan","A good teacher knows how to guide according to circumstances and spark students' interest.":"Guru yang baik tahu cara membimbing sesuai keadaan dan membangkitkan minat siswa.","to suit the remedy to the case":"menyesuaikan obat dengan penyakitnya","To solve the root problem, you must first find the cause and suit the remedy to the case.":"Untuk menyelesaikan masalah hingga ke akar, kamu harus menemukan penyebabnya dulu dan menyesuaikan obat dengan penyakitnya.","to attend to one thing and lose another":"mengurus yang satu, terabaikan yang lain","Short-handed, one inevitably attends to one thing and loses another, doing neither well.":"Kekurangan tenaga, mau tak mau mengurus yang satu dan mengabaikan yang lain, keduanya jadi tak beres.","to cite classics and authorities":"mengutip karya klasik dan rujukan","He likes to cite classics in his writing, and his prose shows considerable erudition.":"Ia suka mengutip karya klasik dalam tulisannya, dan prosanya menunjukkan keluasan pengetahuan yang cukup besar.","to complement each other and shine":"saling melengkapi dan menonjolkan","This essay paired with exquisite illustrations—the two complement each other beautifully.":"Esai ini dipadukan dengan ilustrasi yang indah—keduanya saling melengkapi dengan memukau.","abstract":"abstrak","This concept is too abstract—could you give an example?":"Konsep ini terlalu abstrak—bisakah kamu memberi contoh?","concept":"konsep","This book explains complex economic concepts very clearly.":"Buku ini menjelaskan konsep-konsep ekonomi yang rumit dengan sangat jelas.","theory":"teori","It works in theory, but in practice it is full of difficulties.":"Secara teori berhasil, tetapi dalam praktik penuh dengan kesulitan.","viewpoint":"sudut pandang","Everyone has a different viewpoint, so listen more to what others think.":"Setiap orang punya sudut pandang berbeda, jadi lebih banyaklah mendengarkan pendapat orang lain.","premise; precondition":"premis; prasyarat","The precondition for cooperation is mutual trust between both sides.":"Prasyarat untuk kerja sama adalah kepercayaan timbal balik antara kedua pihak.","hypothesis; assumption":"hipotesis; asumsi","This is just a hypothesis; more data is needed to prove it.":"Ini hanya hipotesis; diperlukan lebih banyak data untuk membuktikannya.","logic":"logika","His argument sounds reasonable, but there are holes in its logic.":"Argumennya terdengar masuk akal, tetapi ada celah dalam logikanya.","context; thread":"konteks; alur","To understand this sentence, you first need to grasp the context of the whole passage.":"Untuk memahami kalimat ini, kamu perlu terlebih dahulu menangkap konteks seluruh paragraf.","Let's analyze the data first, then decide on the next step.":"Mari kita analisis dulu datanya, baru tentukan langkah berikutnya.","to interpret":"menafsirkan; membawakan","This actor interprets the character's loneliness perfectly.":"Aktor ini menafsirkan kesepian tokohnya dengan sempurna.","News reports should be objective, not just your own feelings.":"Pemberitaan harus objektif, bukan sekadar perasaanmu sendiri.","subjective":"subjektif","This is just my subjective opinion, for reference only.":"Ini hanya pendapat subjektif saya, sekadar sebagai referensi.","argumentation; exposition":"argumentasi; pemaparan","The argumentation in this paper is very persuasive.":"Argumentasi dalam makalah ini sangat meyakinkan.","Every judgment needs a basis; you can't rely on feelings alone.":"Setiap penilaian butuh dasar; kamu tak bisa hanya mengandalkan perasaan.","category; scope":"kategori; lingkup","This question is beyond the scope of my expertise.":"Pertanyaan ini di luar lingkup keahlian saya.","to explore; to discuss":"menjajaki; membahas","This panel will explore the ethical issues of artificial intelligence.":"Panel ini akan membahas isu-isu etika kecerdasan buatan.","to expound":"menguraikan; memaparkan","In the first chapter, the author expounds the core ideas of the whole book.":"Pada bab pertama, penulis menguraikan gagasan inti seluruh buku.","to summarize; to induce":"merangkum; menyimpulkan","Please summarize everyone's opinions into three key points.":"Tolong rangkum pendapat semua orang menjadi tiga poin utama.","inference":"kesimpulan; penarikan kesimpulan","This inference lacks supporting evidence and doesn't hold up.":"Kesimpulan ini kurang bukti pendukung dan tidak dapat dipertahankan.","Some scholars have questioned the data sources of this report.":"Sejumlah sarjana mempertanyakan sumber data laporan ini.","After multiple rounds of negotiation, the two sides finally reached a consensus.":"Setelah beberapa putaran negosiasi, kedua pihak akhirnya mencapai konsensus.","to sign a contract":"menandatangani kontrak","We plan to formally sign the contract with them next week.":"Kami berencana menandatangani kontrak secara resmi dengan mereka minggu depan.","clause; terms":"klausul; ketentuan","Before signing, please read every clause of the contract carefully.":"Sebelum menandatangani, harap baca setiap klausul kontrak dengan saksama.","operations":"operasional; kinerja usaha","The company's operations this year are much better than last year.":"Kinerja usaha perusahaan tahun ini jauh lebih baik daripada tahun lalu.","strategy":"strategi","Facing a new market, we must adjust our marketing strategy.":"Menghadapi pasar baru, kita harus menyesuaikan strategi pemasaran.","to evaluate; to assess":"mengevaluasi; menilai","Before making a decision, let's assess the risks first.":"Sebelum mengambil keputusan, mari kita nilai dulu risikonya.","The benefits of this investment won't be visible for several years.":"Manfaat investasi ini baru akan terlihat beberapa tahun kemudian.","to coordinate overall":"mengoordinasikan secara menyeluruh","She's coordinating this event—everyone just needs to cooperate.":"Ia yang mengoordinasikan acara ini—semua orang tinggal bekerja sama saja.","to integrate":"mengintegrasikan; memadukan","We plan to integrate the functions of the two departments.":"Kami berencana mengintegrasikan fungsi kedua departemen.","to execute; to implement":"menjalankan; melaksanakan","No matter how good the plan is, it's useless if poorly executed.":"Sebagus apa pun rencananya, percuma jika pelaksanaannya buruk.","to supervise":"mengawasi","The government's administration needs to be supervised by the people.":"Penyelenggaraan pemerintahan perlu diawasi oleh rakyat.","risk":"risiko","Investment always carries risks; please assess them carefully.":"Investasi selalu mengandung risiko; harap nilai dengan cermat.","to fulfill; to honor":"memenuhi; menunaikan","Since you've signed the contract, you must fulfill the obligations in it.":"Karena kamu sudah menandatangani kontrak, kamu harus memenuhi kewajiban di dalamnya.","to hold business talks":"melakukan pembicaraan bisnis","Next month I'm going to Tokyo to discuss a partnership deal.":"Bulan depan aku akan ke Tokyo untuk membahas kesepakatan kemitraan.","rights and interests":"hak dan kepentingan","Consumers should know how to protect their own rights and interests.":"Konsumen sebaiknya tahu cara melindungi hak dan kepentingannya sendiri.","to transform":"bertransformasi; beralih rupa","If traditional industries don't transform, they can hardly survive.":"Jika industri tradisional tidak bertransformasi, mereka sulit bertahan.","consciousness; awareness":"kesadaran","In recent years, people's environmental awareness has risen considerably.":"Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, kesadaran lingkungan masyarakat meningkat cukup pesat.","values":"nilai-nilai; tata nilai","When two people's values differ too much, getting along is hard.":"Ketika tata nilai dua orang terlalu berbeda, sulit untuk akur.","to identify with; to agree":"menyetujui; sependapat","I really agree with his view—education does need reform.":"Aku sangat setuju dengan pandangannya—pendidikan memang perlu direformasi.","contradiction":"kontradiksi; pertentangan","The contradiction between ideals and reality troubles him deeply.":"Pertentangan antara idealisme dan kenyataan sangat menggelisahkannya.","conflict":"konflik; perselisihan","The two had a conflict over a misunderstanding and only made up later.":"Keduanya berselisih karena salah paham dan baru kemudian berbaikan.","to compromise":"berkompromi; mengalah","Negotiation is about mutual concessions—someone has to compromise first.":"Negosiasi adalah soal saling mengalah—seseorang harus berkompromi lebih dulu.","dignity":"martabat; harga diri","No matter how poor you are, you must not lose your dignity as a person.":"Semiskin apa pun kamu, kamu tak boleh kehilangan martabatmu sebagai manusia.","motive; motivation":"motif; motivasi","The clearer your motivation for learning a language, the easier it is to keep going.":"Semakin jelas motivasimu belajar bahasa, semakin mudah untuk terus bertahan.","potential":"potensi","This young athlete has great potential and is worth developing.":"Atlet muda ini memiliki potensi besar dan layak dikembangkan.","prejudice; bias":"prasangka; bias","We often hold prejudices against others without realizing it.":"Kita sering menyimpan prasangka terhadap orang lain tanpa menyadarinya.","to reflect on":"merefleksikan; berintrospeksi","After the failure, he seriously reflected on his own problems.":"Setelah kegagalan itu, ia serius merefleksikan masalahnya sendiri.","to embrace; to tolerate":"merangkul; menoleransi","A mature society should embrace different voices.":"Masyarakat yang matang seharusnya merangkul suara-suara yang berbeda.","tradition":"tradisi","Gathering around the table for a reunion dinner at Lunar New Year is a Taiwanese tradition.":"Berkumpul di meja makan untuk santap malam reuni saat Tahun Baru Imlek adalah tradisi Taiwan.","to pass down; to inherit":"mewariskan; meneruskan","This craft has been passed down for three generations.":"Kerajinan ini telah diwariskan selama tiga generasi.","aesthetics; sense of beauty":"estetika; cita rasa keindahan","Every era has its own standards of beauty.":"Setiap zaman memiliki standar keindahannya sendiri.","realm; level of attainment":"tingkatan; taraf pencapaian","His tea artistry has reached a masterful realm.":"Seni tehnya telah mencapai taraf keahlian yang tinggi.","self-cultivation; composure":"keluhuran budi; ketenangan diri","Staying calm even when insulted like that—he really has composure.":"Tetap tenang meski dihina seperti itu—ia benar-benar memiliki keluhuran budi.","deep-seated foundation":"fondasi yang mengakar dalam","This old city has a profound cultural foundation.":"Kota tua ini memiliki fondasi budaya yang mengakar dalam.","sentiment; feelings":"nuansa perasaan; sentimen","This old coffee shop is full of nostalgic sentiment.":"Kedai kopi tua ini penuh dengan nuansa nostalgia.","to sublimate":"menyublimkan; mengangkat menjadi lebih tinggi","He sublimated the pain of heartbreak into one moving song after another.":"Ia menyublimkan derita patah hati menjadi satu demi satu lagu yang menyentuh.","twice the result with half the effort":"hasil dua kali lipat dengan usaha separuh","With the right method, language learning takes half the effort for double the results.":"Dengan metode yang tepat, belajar bahasa cukup separuh usaha untuk hasil dua kali lipat.","to be readily solved":"terpecahkan dengan mudah","Once we found the key issue, the other difficulties were easily resolved.":"Begitu kami menemukan masalah kuncinya, kesulitan lainnya pun terpecahkan dengan mudah.","to weigh; consider carefully":"menimbang; mempertimbangkan dengan saksama","I'm still weighing how to translate this passage.":"Aku masih menimbang bagaimana menerjemahkan bagian ini.","to suddenly realize":"tiba-tiba tersadar; mendadak paham","Only after hearing the teacher's explanation did I suddenly get it.":"Baru setelah mendengar penjelasan guru, aku mendadak paham.","a common sight; nothing new":"pemandangan biasa; bukan hal baru","In big cities, working overtime late into the night has long been a common sight.":"Di kota-kota besar, lembur hingga larut malam sudah lama menjadi pemandangan biasa.","meticulous":"cermat; teliti","He is meticulous in his work, not letting even a decimal point slip by.":"Ia cermat dalam bekerja, sampai titik desimal pun tak dibiarkan lolos.","the loss outweighs the gain":"kerugiannya melebihi keuntungannya","I bought cheap goods to save a little money, but they kept breaking—the loss outweighed the gain.":"Aku membeli barang murah demi menghemat sedikit uang, tetapi terus rusak—kerugiannya melebihi keuntungannya.","step by step":"selangkah demi selangkah; bertahap","Language learning should proceed step by step—you can't rush it.":"Belajar bahasa harus dilakukan selangkah demi selangkah—tak bisa terburu-buru.","to go all out":"mengerahkan segenap tenaga","This is our last chance, so we must go all out.":"Ini kesempatan terakhir kita, jadi kita harus mengerahkan segenap tenaga.","In recent years Taipei's old districts have transformed into creative parks.":"Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, kawasan tua Taipei telah berubah menjadi taman kreatif.","rare and commendable":"langka dan patut dipuji","To have such a sense of responsibility at a young age is truly rare and commendable.":"Memiliki rasa tanggung jawab seperti itu di usia muda benar-benar langka dan patut dipuji.","to influence imperceptibly":"memengaruhi secara tak terasa","Parents' words and deeds influence children imperceptibly.":"Ucapan dan perbuatan orang tua memengaruhi anak secara tak terasa.","insignificant; trivial":"sepele; tak berarti","Compared with your effort, what I did is really insignificant.":"Dibandingkan dengan usahamu, apa yang kulakukan benar-benar tak berarti.","to infer other cases from one instance":"menarik kesimpulan lain dari satu contoh","Good students can infer new cases from one example, without the teacher spelling everything out.":"Siswa yang baik bisa menarik kesimpulan baru dari satu contoh, tanpa perlu guru menjelaskan segalanya.","to clarify; to elucidate":"menjelaskan; menegaskan","This editorial clarifies the government's position on energy policy.":"Tajuk rencana ini menegaskan posisi pemerintah mengenai kebijakan energi.","to examine dialectically":"menelaah secara dialektis","The author examines the relationship between tradition and modernity dialectically.":"Penulis menelaah hubungan antara tradisi dan modernitas secara dialektis.","paradox":"paradoks","Pursuing efficiency only to lower quality of life—that is the paradox of modern society.":"Mengejar efisiensi tetapi justru menurunkan kualitas hidup—itulah paradoks masyarakat modern.","corroborating evidence":"bukti penguat","This unearthed document provides strong corroboration for his theory.":"Dokumen yang digali ini memberikan bukti penguat yang kuat bagi teorinya.","textual research":"kajian tekstual; penelitian sumber","The historical drama's research on costumes and etiquette is quite rigorous.":"Kajian tentang kostum dan tata krama dalam drama sejarah ini cukup cermat.","pulse; dynamics":"denyut; dinamika","Journalists must keep their finger on the pulse of society at all times.":"Wartawan harus selalu memegang denyut nadi masyarakat.","crux; sticking point":"titik krusial; simpul persoalan","The crux of the failed negotiation lies in the huge gap between the two sides' price expectations.":"Titik krusial dari gagalnya negosiasi terletak pada besarnya jurang ekspektasi harga kedua pihak.","clue; inkling":"petunjuk; tanda-tanda","Recent data already show signs of an economic recovery.":"Data terkini sudah menunjukkan tanda-tanda pemulihan ekonomi.","prototype; embryonic form":"purwarupa; bentuk awal","This draft already has the makings of a full-fledged policy.":"Draf ini sudah memiliki bentuk awal sebuah kebijakan yang utuh.","outline; contour":"garis besar; kerangka","After the briefing, I gained a preliminary grasp of the project's overall outline.":"Setelah pemaparan itu, saya memperoleh gambaran awal tentang garis besar keseluruhan proyek.","Through third-party mediation, labor and management finally returned to the negotiating table.":"Melalui mediasi pihak ketiga, pekerja dan manajemen akhirnya kembali ke meja perundingan.","to deal with; to maneuver among":"menghadapi; berkelindan di antara","As a PR officer, she has to maneuver among all kinds of media every day.":"Sebagai staf humas, ia harus berkelindan dengan berbagai media setiap hari.","to map out; to plan":"merancang; menyusun rencana","After taking office, the mayor immediately set about mapping out a long-term blueprint for the city.":"Setelah menjabat, wali kota langsung mulai merancang cetak biru jangka panjang untuk kota itu.","to draft; to work out":"menyusun; merumuskan","The relevant agencies are drafting a package of measures to address the declining birthrate.":"Instansi terkait sedang menyusun paket langkah untuk mengatasi penurunan angka kelahiran.","to converge; to pool":"menghimpun; mengumpulkan","This platform pools professional opinions from various fields.":"Platform ini menghimpun pendapat para profesional dari berbagai bidang.","to compile; to collate":"menghimpun; mengompilasi","Please compile the feedback from each group into a single report.":"Tolong himpun masukan dari setiap kelompok menjadi satu laporan.","to temper; to forge":"menempa; menggembleng","Years of frontline experience forged his exceptional judgment.":"Pengalaman bertahun-tahun di garis depan menempa daya penilaiannya yang luar biasa.","to hone; to spur one another on":"mengasah; saling memacu","Team members spur one another on, and their skills keep improving.":"Anggota tim saling memacu, dan keterampilan mereka terus meningkat.","to consolidate":"mengonsolidasikan; memperkukuh","Regular review helps consolidate what you have learned.":"Pengulangan secara teratur membantu memperkukuh apa yang telah kamu pelajari.","to disintegrate; to collapse":"berantakan; runtuh","Internal distrust caused the entire alliance to disintegrate rapidly.":"Ketidakpercayaan internal membuat seluruh aliansi cepat berantakan.","to paralyze; to be paralyzed":"melumpuhkan; menjadi lumpuh","Once the system crashed, operations across the company were almost paralyzed.":"Begitu sistemnya crash, operasional seluruh perusahaan nyaris lumpuh.","to check; to curb":"membendung; menekan","The government has introduced heavy penalties in hopes of curbing drunk driving.":"Pemerintah memberlakukan hukuman berat dengan harapan menekan kasus mengemudi dalam keadaan mabuk.","to eradicate; to put an end to":"memberantas; mengakhiri sampai tuntas","Only with transparent institutions can the room for corruption be eliminated.":"Hanya dengan institusi yang transparan, ruang bagi korupsi dapat diberantas.","The new traffic-signal design has effectively eased rush-hour congestion.":"Desain lampu lalu lintas yang baru berhasil mengurangi kemacetan pada jam sibuk.","resilience":"daya lenting; ketangguhan","Taiwan's SMEs have shown remarkable resilience amid the crisis.":"UKM Taiwan menunjukkan ketangguhan yang luar biasa di tengah krisis.","tension":"ketegangan","The film's narrative is full of tension, leaving viewers breathless.":"Alur film ini penuh ketegangan, membuat penonton menahan napas.","vision; scale; framework":"visi; cakupan pandangan","A leader's vision determines how far the organization can go.":"Visi seorang pemimpin menentukan sejauh mana organisasi bisa melangkah.","horizons; field of vision":"cakrawala; wawasan","Working abroad has broadened my horizons considerably.":"Bekerja di luar negeri telah memperluas cakrawala saya secara signifikan.","bottom line":"batas akhir; garis merah","We can make concessions in negotiations, but our bottom line must not be crossed.":"Kita bisa mengalah dalam negosiasi, tetapi batas akhir kita tak boleh dilanggar.","blind spot":"titik buta","Outsiders can often spot the blind spots in the thinking of those involved.":"Orang luar sering dapat melihat titik buta dalam pikiran pihak yang terlibat.","hidden concern":"kekhawatiran tersembunyi; masalah laten","Brain drain is a long-standing hidden concern for this industry.":"Hengkangnya tenaga ahli merupakan kekhawatiran tersembunyi yang lama membayangi industri ini.","turning point; opportunity":"titik balik; peluang","The pandemic became an opportunity for companies to push digital transformation.":"Pandemi menjadi peluang bagi perusahaan untuk mendorong transformasi digital.","variable; uncertainty":"variabel; ketidakpastian","Exchange-rate fluctuations are the biggest variable in this investment plan.":"Fluktuasi nilai tukar adalah variabel terbesar dalam rencana investasi ini.","symptom; sign":"gejala; tanda","Declining consumer spending is often one of the symptoms of a recession.":"Menurunnya belanja konsumen sering kali menjadi salah satu gejala resesi.","aesthetics":"estetika","The cafe's interior design reflects a unique aesthetic of everyday life.":"Desain interior kafe ini mencerminkan estetika kehidupan sehari-hari yang unik.","philosophical truth":"kebenaran filosofis","The animation seems lighthearted, but it actually contains profound philosophy.":"Animasi itu tampak ringan, tetapi sebenarnya mengandung filosofi yang mendalam.","moral; implied meaning":"pesan moral; makna tersirat","The moral of this fable is a reminder not to lose the big picture over small gains.":"Pesan moral fabel ini mengingatkan agar tidak kehilangan yang besar demi keuntungan kecil.","imagery":"citraan; imaji","The poet uses the imagery of the sea to express a longing for freedom.":"Penyair menggunakan citraan laut untuk mengungkapkan kerinduan akan kebebasan.","moral backbone; strength of character":"keteguhan moral; ketegaran watak","He never bowed to power in his life, showing the backbone of an intellectual.":"Sepanjang hidupnya ia tak pernah tunduk pada kekuasaan, menunjukkan keteguhan seorang intelektual.","magnanimity; bearing":"kebesaran jiwa; kelapangan hati","Remaining humble and teachable in the face of criticism—that is true magnanimity.":"Tetap rendah hati dan mau belajar saat menghadapi kritik—itulah kebesaran jiwa yang sejati.","success comes naturally when conditions are ripe":"keberhasilan datang dengan sendirinya bila kondisinya matang","With a solid foundation, promotion comes naturally in due course.":"Dengan fondasi yang kukuh, promosi datang dengan sendirinya pada waktunya.","to pool collective wisdom":"menghimpun kearifan kolektif","This is a thorny problem—let's pool our ideas and work out a solution together.":"Ini masalah pelik—mari kita himpun ide dan cari solusinya bersama.","to strive for ever greater perfection":"terus mengejar kesempurnaan yang lebih tinggi","The master craftsman strives for perfection in every detail and never cuts corners.":"Sang maestro pengrajin mengejar kesempurnaan dalam setiap detail dan tak pernah asal-asalan.","the burden is heavy and the road is long":"beban berat dan jalan masih panjang","Achieving the net-zero goal is truly a heavy task with a long road ahead.":"Mencapai target nol-bersih benar-benar tugas berat dengan jalan yang masih panjang.","to stay vigilant in times of peace":"tetap waspada di saat aman","When business is going well, a company should stay alert to danger and prepare in advance.":"Ketika bisnis sedang lancar, perusahaan sebaiknya tetap waspada terhadap bahaya dan bersiap lebih dahulu.","to prevent trouble before it happens":"mencegah masalah sebelum terjadi","Regular equipment inspections are precisely about preventing problems before they occur.":"Pemeriksaan peralatan secara berkala justru bertujuan mencegah masalah sebelum terjadi.","to complement each other":"saling melengkapi","Theory and practice complement each other; neither can be dispensed with.":"Teori dan praktik saling melengkapi; keduanya tak boleh diabaikan.","different paths lead to the same destination":"jalan berbeda menuju tujuan yang sama","The two schools took different approaches but arrived at the same conclusion.":"Kedua aliran menempuh pendekatan berbeda tetapi tiba pada kesimpulan yang sama.","achievable overnight; attainable in one step":"tercapai dalam semalam; diraih dalam satu langkah","Language proficiency cannot be achieved overnight; it takes long-term accumulation.":"Kemahiran berbahasa tak bisa dicapai dalam semalam; ia butuh akumulasi jangka panjang.","to be influenced by constant exposure":"terpengaruh oleh paparan yang terus-menerus","Having grown up surrounded by it, she naturally has a deep attachment to the tea ceremony.":"Tumbuh dalam lingkungan itu, ia secara alami memiliki keterikatan mendalam pada upacara minum teh.","to dissect; to analyze in depth":"membedah; menganalisis secara mendalam","This commentary dissects in depth the structural causes of soaring housing prices.":"Ulasan ini membedah secara mendalam penyebab struktural melonjaknya harga rumah.","to sort out; to untangle":"menata; mengurai","Before you start writing, sort out the structure of your paper first.":"Sebelum mulai menulis, tata dulu struktur makalahmu.","to scrutinize; to examine closely":"mencermati; menelaah dengan saksama","The incident prompted society to re-examine the role of the media.":"Peristiwa itu mendorong masyarakat untuk menelaah kembali peran media.","to gain insight into":"memahami secara mendalam; menembus inti","A good product manager can discern needs that users never voice.":"Manajer produk yang baik mampu memahami kebutuhan yang tak pernah diucapkan pengguna.","to weigh; to balance":"menimbang; menyeimbangkan","Policymaking requires carefully weighing efficiency against fairness.":"Perumusan kebijakan menuntut penimbangan yang cermat antara efisiensi dan keadilan.","to brew; to take shape gradually":"mengeram; perlahan terbentuk","The idea for this novel had been brewing in his mind for a full decade.":"Gagasan untuk novel ini telah mengeram di benaknya selama satu dekade penuh.","to contain; to embody":"mengandung; menyimpan","This proverb embodies the practical wisdom of our forebears.":"Peribahasa ini mengandung kearifan praktis nenek moyang kita.","to highlight; to manifest":"menonjolkan; memperlihatkan","The building's design highlights the local cultural character.":"Desain bangunan ini menonjolkan karakter budaya setempat.","to throw into relief; to underscore":"menyoroti; mempertegas","The blackout threw the problem of the aging power grid into sharp relief.":"Pemadaman listrik itu mempertegas masalah jaringan listrik yang menua.","magnanimity; graciousness":"kelapangan hati; kemurahan sikap","Facing dissenting voices, those in power should have the grace to accept criticism.":"Menghadapi suara yang berbeda, mereka yang berkuasa seharusnya memiliki kelapangan hati untuk menerima kritik.","Society & Systems":"Masyarakat & Sistem","National Health Insurance: One Card for Every Hospital":"Asuransi Kesehatan Nasional: Satu Kartu untuk Semua Rumah Sakit","You feel feverish, wander into a neighborhood clinic, and walk out having seen a doctor and picked up medicine for just a few dollars. Live in Taiwan and you realize how remarkable this ordinary experience is. Let's look at the world-famous National Health Insurance up close.":"Anda merasa demam, mampir ke klinik dekat rumah, lalu keluar setelah diperiksa dokter dan menebus obat hanya dengan beberapa dolar. Tinggal di Taiwan membuat Anda sadar betapa luar biasanya pengalaman sederhana ini. Mari kita lihat lebih dekat Asuransi Kesehatan Nasional yang terkenal di dunia.","Taiwan's National Health Insurance (NHI) officially launched in 1995 and is now thirty years old. Its core idea is simple: whether you're an office worker, a student, an elderly person, or a child, as long as you live in Taiwan and have legal residency, you are automatically enrolled. Everyone pays a monthly premium based on income, the money is pooled together, and when someone falls ill, gets injured, or needs surgery, that shared fund covers the medical costs.":"Asuransi Kesehatan Nasional (NHI) Taiwan resmi diluncurkan pada tahun 1995 dan kini berusia tiga puluh tahun. Gagasan intinya sederhana: entah Anda seorang pekerja kantoran, pelajar, orang lanjut usia, atau anak-anak, selama Anda tinggal di Taiwan dan memiliki izin tinggal yang sah, Anda otomatis terdaftar. Setiap orang membayar iuran bulanan berdasarkan penghasilan, uang itu dikumpulkan bersama, dan ketika seseorang sakit, cedera, atau perlu operasi, dana bersama itulah yang menanggung biaya pengobatan.","For foreigners, the thing you feel most is that green \"NHI card.\" It's a small IC card with your photo and identity details. When you see a doctor, you just hand the card to the front desk; the nurse gives it a quick swipe, and all your visit records, allergy history, and current medications appear on the doctor's screen. No need to carry a stack of paper records or repeat your medical history—the whole process is fast and seamless.":"Bagi orang asing, hal yang paling terasa adalah \"kartu NHI\" hijau itu. Kartu itu berupa kartu IC kecil yang memuat foto dan data identitas Anda. Saat berobat, Anda cukup menyerahkan kartu ke resepsionis; perawat menggeseknya sebentar, lalu seluruh riwayat kunjungan, riwayat alergi, dan obat yang sedang Anda konsumsi muncul di layar dokter. Tak perlu membawa setumpuk berkas kertas atau mengulang riwayat penyakit Anda—seluruh prosesnya cepat dan mulus.","What surprises many people is the price. For a single outpatient visit in Taiwan, the \"registration fee\" and \"co-payment\" you pay yourself usually add up to just a hundred-something to three or four hundred NT dollars, and picking up medicine is often only tens of dollars. Whether it's a cold, a dental visit, or refilling chronic-illness medication, the burden is light. Most of the cost has already been paid by NHI, and citizens pay only a small share—which is why many Taiwanese go see a doctor at the first sign of feeling unwell.":"Yang membuat banyak orang terkejut adalah harganya. Untuk satu kali kunjungan rawat jalan di Taiwan, \"biaya pendaftaran\" dan \"biaya urun\" yang Anda bayar sendiri biasanya hanya berjumlah seratusan sampai tiga atau empat ratus dolar NT, dan menebus obat sering kali hanya puluhan dolar. Entah itu flu, periksa gigi, atau mengambil ulang obat penyakit kronis, bebannya ringan. Sebagian besar biaya sudah ditanggung NHI, dan warga hanya membayar sebagian kecil—itulah sebabnya banyak orang Taiwan langsung berobat begitu merasa sedikit tak enak badan.","This system is internationally famous not only for being cheap but also for being convenient and fair. You can decide for yourself which clinic and which doctor to see, without needing to book weeks in advance as in some countries. Large hospitals, small clinics, traditional Chinese medicine, and dentists are almost all part of NHI. Even in remote countryside and outlying islands, the government works to make sure everyone has access to a doctor. The WHO and many countries have come to Taiwan to \"learn the ropes\" and study the system.":"Sistem ini terkenal di dunia bukan hanya karena murah, tetapi juga karena praktis dan adil. Anda bisa menentukan sendiri klinik dan dokter mana yang ingin dikunjungi, tanpa perlu memesan berminggu-minggu sebelumnya seperti di sebagian negara. Rumah sakit besar, klinik kecil, pengobatan tradisional Tionghoa, dan dokter gigi hampir semuanya termasuk dalam NHI. Bahkan di pedesaan terpencil dan pulau-pulau terluar, pemerintah berupaya memastikan semua orang bisa mendapatkan layanan dokter. WHO dan banyak negara telah datang ke Taiwan untuk \"belajar\" dan mempelajari sistem ini.","Of course, such a handy system has its headaches too. Because seeing a doctor is so easy and cheap, some people rush to the hospital for the smallest ailment, causing heavy use of medical resources and putting frequent financial strain on NHI. Medical staff also carry heavy workloads, and debates about \"sweatshop hospitals\" resurface from time to time. So the government keeps adjusting premiums, co-payments, and coverage, striving to balance \"everyone can afford it\" against \"there's enough money to go around.\"":"Tentu saja, sistem sepraktis ini juga punya masalahnya sendiri. Karena berobat begitu mudah dan murah, sebagian orang bergegas ke rumah sakit untuk keluhan sekecil apa pun, sehingga sumber daya medis terpakai berlebihan dan keuangan NHI kerap tertekan. Tenaga medis pun memikul beban kerja yang berat, dan perdebatan soal \"rumah sakit yang memeras tenaga\" sesekali muncul kembali. Maka pemerintah terus menyesuaikan iuran, biaya urun, dan cakupan layanan, berupaya menyeimbangkan antara \"semua orang mampu membayarnya\" dan \"dananya cukup untuk semua\".","For foreigners living in Taiwan, the good news is: as long as you work or study here, or have lived here on a residency permit for a set period, you can usually join NHI and receive almost the same treatment as locals. Many foreigners who have lived in Taiwan find that after going home, what they miss most isn't the food but that NHI card that lets you \"see a doctor anytime without worry.\" That little card actually holds the warmth of a whole society looking after one another.":"Bagi orang asing yang tinggal di Taiwan, kabar baiknya: selama Anda bekerja atau belajar di sini, atau telah tinggal dengan izin tinggal selama jangka waktu tertentu, biasanya Anda bisa bergabung dengan NHI dan menerima layanan yang hampir sama dengan warga lokal. Banyak orang asing yang pernah tinggal di Taiwan mendapati bahwa setelah pulang ke negaranya, yang paling mereka rindukan bukanlah makanannya, melainkan kartu NHI yang membuat Anda bisa \"berobat kapan saja tanpa khawatir\". Kartu kecil itu sesungguhnya menyimpan kehangatan seluruh masyarakat yang saling menjaga satu sama lain.","National Health Insurance (NHI)":"Asuransi Kesehatan Nasional (NHI)","NHI card (IC card)":"kartu NHI (kartu IC)","insurance premium":"iuran/premi asuransi","registration fee":"biaya pendaftaran","co-payment":"biaya urun (co-payment)","outpatient visit":"kunjungan rawat jalan","to pick up medicine":"menebus/mengambil obat","medical record":"rekam medis","chronic illness":"penyakit kronis","residency (legal stay)":"izin tinggal (tinggal secara sah)","benefits/coverage":"manfaat/cakupan","Taiwan's NHI card can even record your organ-donation wishes. It used to be a paper booklet, but was fully switched to IC cards in 2004. During the pandemic, Taiwan linked this system to a 'mask rationing' scheme—show your card and the system tracked where and how many masks you'd bought—which drew global attention. Few places in the world have turned a single card into such deep social infrastructure.":"Kartu NHI Taiwan bahkan bisa mencatat keinginan Anda untuk mendonorkan organ. Dulu berupa buku kertas, tetapi pada tahun 2004 sepenuhnya beralih ke kartu IC. Selama pandemi, Taiwan menghubungkan sistem ini dengan skema 'penjatahan masker'—tunjukkan kartu Anda dan sistem mencatat di mana serta berapa banyak masker yang telah Anda beli—yang menarik perhatian dunia. Hanya sedikit tempat di dunia yang mengubah satu kartu menjadi infrastruktur sosial sedalam ini.","Trash Doesn't Touch the Ground: Chasing the Musical Garbage Truck":"Sampah Tak Menyentuh Tanah: Mengejar Truk Sampah Bermusik","At dusk, when the melody of 'A Maiden's Prayer' drifts in from somewhere, residents pour out of their homes with bags in hand—a scene unique to Taiwan. Why do garbage trucks play music, and why does everyone run to chase them? Let's peek into Taiwan's 'trash doesn't touch the ground' culture.":"Saat senja, ketika melodi 'A Maiden's Prayer' terdengar entah dari mana, warga berhamburan keluar rumah dengan kantong sampah di tangan—pemandangan khas Taiwan. Mengapa truk sampah memutar musik, dan mengapa semua orang berlarian mengejarnya? Mari kita intip budaya 'sampah tak menyentuh tanah' di Taiwan.","On Taiwan's streets and alleys, garbage trucks don't roll by quietly—they play music as they go. The two most common tunes are 'A Maiden's Prayer' and 'Für Elise.' Almost every Taiwanese grows up hearing these two melodies, and the moment the music starts, everyone knows: the garbage truck is here, time to go out and take out the trash.":"Di jalan-jalan dan gang-gang Taiwan, truk sampah tidak melintas dengan diam—mereka memutar musik sambil berjalan. Dua lagu yang paling umum adalah 'A Maiden's Prayer' dan 'Für Elise'. Hampir setiap orang Taiwan tumbuh dengan mendengar kedua melodi ini, dan begitu musiknya mulai, semua orang tahu: truk sampah datang, saatnya keluar membuang sampah.","This system is called 'trash doesn't touch the ground.' It means you can't just pile your garbage in a roadside bin or on the ground—you have to 'wait for the truck and hand your trash directly to the sanitation crew.' The truck passes through each neighborhood at a fixed time on a fixed route, and residents must come out with their trash during that window and toss it into the truck in person. This way, no stinking mounds of garbage—magnets for cockroaches and rats—build up on the streets.":"Sistem ini disebut 'sampah tak menyentuh tanah'. Artinya, Anda tidak boleh sembarangan menumpuk sampah di tong pinggir jalan atau di tanah—Anda harus 'menunggu truk dan menyerahkan sampah langsung kepada petugas kebersihan'. Truk melewati setiap lingkungan pada waktu tetap dengan rute tetap, dan warga harus keluar membawa sampahnya dalam rentang waktu itu lalu melemparnya sendiri ke dalam truk. Dengan begitu, tidak ada gunungan sampah berbau busuk—yang mengundang kecoa dan tikus—menumpuk di jalanan.","Even more important is sorting 'recyclables' and 'food waste.' Following behind the garbage truck there's usually a second 'recycling truck.' You separate recyclable items—plastic bottles, paper, steel and aluminum cans, glass, PET bottles—and hand them to the recycling truck; household leftovers, fruit peels, and vegetable scraps go separately into a 'food-waste bucket,' and this food waste is used to feed pigs or make compost. Only truly non-recyclable 'general trash' goes into the government-mandated special garbage bags and into the truck.":"Yang lebih penting lagi adalah memilah 'barang daur ulang' dan 'sisa makanan'. Di belakang truk sampah biasanya ada 'truk daur ulang' kedua. Anda memisahkan barang yang bisa didaur ulang—botol plastik, kertas, kaleng baja dan aluminium, kaca, botol PET—lalu menyerahkannya ke truk daur ulang; sisa makanan rumah tangga, kulit buah, dan sisa sayur dimasukkan terpisah ke dalam 'ember sisa makanan', dan sisa makanan ini dipakai untuk memberi makan babi atau membuat kompos. Hanya 'sampah umum' yang benar-benar tak bisa didaur ulang yang dimasukkan ke kantong sampah khusus yang diwajibkan pemerintah lalu ke dalam truk.","For Taiwanese, chasing the garbage truck is almost a national sport. Come evening, you'll see people in flip-flops dashing down from their apartments with bags big and small, and others who, to avoid missing it, just stand at the mouth of the alley scrolling on their phones while they wait. If that day you happen to work overtime, go on a date, or oversleep and miss the truck, you have to keep your trash until the next day—or ask a neighbor or family member to take it out for you. That tense feeling of 'racing the garbage truck' is a shared life memory for many Taiwanese.":"Bagi orang Taiwan, mengejar truk sampah nyaris menjadi olahraga nasional. Menjelang malam, Anda akan melihat orang-orang bersandal jepit berlari turun dari apartemen sambil menenteng kantong besar dan kecil, dan ada pula yang, agar tak ketinggalan, cukup berdiri di mulut gang sambil menggulir ponsel sembari menunggu. Kalau hari itu Anda kebetulan lembur, kencan, atau kesiangan hingga ketinggalan truk, Anda harus menyimpan sampah sampai keesokan harinya—atau menitipkannya pada tetangga atau anggota keluarga. Rasa tegang 'berlomba dengan truk sampah' itu adalah kenangan hidup bersama bagi banyak orang Taiwan.","When this system was first rolled out, quite a few people found it a hassle: why couldn't they just dump trash downstairs anytime, like before? But over the decades, Taiwan's streets have become much cleaner, and its recycling rate ranks among the world's best. The alleys once piled with garbage are gone, replaced by music that sounds right on time and residents lining up to wait. Once people got used to it, they actually came to feel that a city like this is cleaner and more orderly.":"Ketika sistem ini pertama kali diberlakukan, cukup banyak orang merasa merepotkan: kenapa tidak boleh membuang sampah di bawah kapan saja seperti dulu? Namun selama beberapa dekade, jalanan Taiwan menjadi jauh lebih bersih, dan tingkat daur ulangnya termasuk yang terbaik di dunia. Gang-gang yang dulu penuh tumpukan sampah kini lenyap, digantikan musik yang berbunyi tepat waktu dan warga yang berbaris menunggu. Setelah terbiasa, orang justru merasa kota seperti ini lebih bersih dan tertib.","If you've just moved to Taiwan, the first bit of daily-life intel you'll want to dig up is usually: 'What time does the garbage truck come to my area?' You can ask your landlord or neighbors, or look up the government's published truck times and routes online. And the day you too start reflexively grabbing your trash bag and rushing out the moment you hear 'A Maiden's Prayer'—congratulations, you've blended into everyday Taiwanese life.":"Kalau Anda baru pindah ke Taiwan, informasi sehari-hari pertama yang biasanya ingin Anda gali adalah: 'Jam berapa truk sampah datang ke daerah saya?' Anda bisa bertanya kepada pemilik kos atau tetangga, atau mencari jadwal dan rute truk yang diumumkan pemerintah secara daring. Dan pada hari ketika Anda pun mulai secara refleks menyambar kantong sampah dan bergegas keluar begitu mendengar 'A Maiden's Prayer'—selamat, Anda sudah membaur ke dalam kehidupan sehari-hari orang Taiwan.","garbage truck":"truk sampah","'trash doesn't touch the ground' (collection system)":"'sampah tak menyentuh tanah' (sistem pengumpulan)","recycling":"daur ulang","food waste":"sisa makanan","sorting/classification":"pemilahan","sanitation crew":"petugas kebersihan","PET/plastic bottle":"botol PET/plastik","designated garbage bag":"kantong sampah resmi","compost":"kompos","alleys and lanes":"gang dan lorong","dusk, early evening":"senja, petang","to blend in, integrate":"membaur, berbaur","The choice of 'A Maiden's Prayer' was reportedly an accident. A widely told story says that in the 1960s–70s, a health official heard his daughter practicing the piece on the piano, thought it was nice, and adopted it as the truck's tune. Note that in Taiwan '垃圾' is commonly pronounced 'lèsè' rather than the dictionary 'lājī'—a fun quirk of local usage. In recent years, more areas offer apps that track the truck's location in real time.":"Pemilihan 'A Maiden's Prayer' konon terjadi secara kebetulan. Kisah yang banyak beredar menyebutkan bahwa pada tahun 1960-an–70-an, seorang pejabat kesehatan mendengar putrinya berlatih lagu itu di piano, merasa lagunya bagus, lalu menjadikannya nada truk sampah. Perlu dicatat, di Taiwan '垃圾' umumnya dilafalkan 'lèsè' alih-alih 'lājī' seperti dalam kamus—keunikan menarik dalam penggunaan lokal. Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, makin banyak wilayah menyediakan aplikasi yang melacak lokasi truk secara real-time.","Taiwan's Democracy and Election Culture":"Demokrasi dan Budaya Pemilu Taiwan","As elections near, streets fill with flags and banners, loud rallies light up the nights, and candidates shake hands at markets from early morning—elections in Taiwan feel like a festival. Let's look at why they get so lively, and what democracy means to the people of Taiwan.":"Menjelang pemilu, jalanan dipenuhi bendera dan spanduk, kampanye akbar yang riuh menyemarakkan malam, dan para kandidat menjabat tangan warga di pasar sejak pagi buta—pemilu di Taiwan terasa seperti sebuah perayaan. Mari kita lihat mengapa suasananya begitu meriah, dan apa arti demokrasi bagi rakyat Taiwan.","Taiwan's democracy today is the product of a history that isn't very long but was hard-won. From the lifting of martial law in the late 1980s to the first direct popular election of a president in 1996, Taiwan moved over a few decades from an authoritarian system to the free elections everyone now takes for granted. Precisely because that road was hard, many Taiwanese especially cherish the ballot in their hands.":"Demokrasi Taiwan hari ini adalah hasil dari sejarah yang tidak terlalu panjang, tetapi diraih dengan susah payah. Dari pencabutan darurat militer pada akhir 1980-an hingga pemilihan presiden langsung oleh rakyat yang pertama pada tahun 1996, dalam beberapa dekade Taiwan bergerak dari sistem otoriter menuju pemilu bebas yang kini dianggap semua orang sebagai hal yang wajar. Justru karena jalan itu berat, banyak orang Taiwan sangat menghargai surat suara di tangan mereka.","Taiwan holds many kinds of elections—president, legislators, city and county mayors, councilors, borough chiefs—so there's an important election almost every year or two. In election season, one of the liveliest sights is the 'rally' (zàoshì wǎnhuì). Supporters gather in plazas or stadiums, wave flags and chant slogans, candidates give speeches on stage, and below there's music and cheering—an atmosphere as fervent as a big concert.":"Taiwan menyelenggarakan banyak jenis pemilu—presiden, anggota legislatif, wali kota dan bupati, anggota dewan, kepala kelurahan—sehingga hampir setiap satu atau dua tahun ada pemilu penting. Pada musim pemilu, salah satu pemandangan paling meriah adalah 'kampanye akbar' (zàoshì wǎnhuì). Para pendukung berkumpul di alun-alun atau stadion, mengibarkan bendera dan meneriakkan yel-yel, kandidat berpidato di panggung, dan di bawah ada musik serta sorak-sorai—suasananya menyala seperti konser besar.","Beyond big rallies, there's a more everyday way of canvassing called 'sweeping the streets' (sǎojiē). Candidates and their teams walk into traditional markets, night markets, and temple squares, shaking hands with people along the way, bowing, handing out flyers, and repeating 'please, please, your support means a lot' hundreds of times. You might be buying groceries when a candidate warmly shakes your hand. This face-to-face contact turns politics from a distant name into a living person standing right in front of you.":"Selain kampanye akbar, ada cara berkampanye yang lebih sehari-hari yang disebut 'menyapu jalan' (sǎojiē). Para kandidat dan timnya masuk ke pasar tradisional, pasar malam, dan pelataran kuil, menjabat tangan orang di sepanjang jalan, membungkuk, membagikan selebaran, dan mengulang 'mohon, mohon, dukungan Anda sangat berarti' ratusan kali. Bisa jadi Anda sedang berbelanja saat seorang kandidat dengan hangat menjabat tangan Anda. Kontak tatap muka ini mengubah politik dari sekadar nama yang jauh menjadi sosok nyata yang berdiri tepat di depan Anda.","On election day, Taiwan's polling stations are usually set up in schools or community centers. Taiwan uses paper marking and hand-counting: voters receive a ballot, stamp a mark next to their chosen candidate, and drop it in the box. When voting closes, counting staff pull out each ballot on the spot, call out the name aloud, and tally with tick marks—the whole process fully public, with anyone free to watch from the side. This 'open the box in the light' transparency is a key reason Taiwanese trust their election results.":"Pada hari pemilu, tempat pemungutan suara di Taiwan biasanya didirikan di sekolah atau balai warga. Taiwan menggunakan penandaan di kertas dan penghitungan manual: pemilih menerima surat suara, membubuhkan tanda di samping kandidat pilihannya, lalu memasukkannya ke kotak. Saat pemungutan ditutup, petugas penghitung mengeluarkan tiap surat suara di tempat, membacakan namanya dengan lantang, dan mencatat dengan garis hitung—seluruh prosesnya sepenuhnya terbuka, siapa pun bebas menyaksikan dari samping. Transparansi 'membuka kotak di bawah terang' inilah salah satu alasan utama orang Taiwan memercayai hasil pemilu mereka.","Taiwan's voter turnout stays consistently high, often exceeding 70% in presidential elections. Many people who work or study away from home make a special trip on election day—by bus or high-speed rail—to 'go home and vote,' because in Taiwan you currently still have to return to your registered household district to cast a ballot. Stations fill with crowds of returnees dragging luggage, a distinctive scene of election season. This feeling of 'no matter how far, I'll go back to cast my vote' shows just how much elections matter to many people.":"Tingkat partisipasi pemilih di Taiwan selalu tinggi, sering melampaui 70% dalam pemilihan presiden. Banyak orang yang bekerja atau belajar jauh dari kampung halaman sengaja menempuh perjalanan pada hari pemilu—dengan bus atau kereta cepat—untuk 'pulang dan memberikan suara', karena di Taiwan saat ini Anda masih harus kembali ke distrik domisili terdaftar untuk mencoblos. Stasiun-stasiun dipadati kerumunan orang yang pulang sambil menyeret koper, pemandangan khas musim pemilu. Perasaan 'sejauh apa pun, saya akan pulang untuk memberikan suara' ini menunjukkan betapa berartinya pemilu bagi banyak orang.","Of course, however lively an election is, it also has a solemn side. Once counting ends and the results are clear, the losing side usually gives a statement and concedes defeat, and society quickly returns to its normal rhythm. For many Taiwanese, being able to peacefully decide through the ballot who leads their society is an important part of their identity. This belief that 'my vote matters' is the most moving thing about Taiwan's democratic culture.":"Tentu saja, semeriah apa pun sebuah pemilu, ada pula sisi khidmatnya. Begitu penghitungan selesai dan hasilnya jelas, pihak yang kalah biasanya menyampaikan pernyataan dan mengakui kekalahan, lalu masyarakat cepat kembali ke ritme normalnya. Bagi banyak orang Taiwan, kemampuan menentukan secara damai lewat surat suara siapa yang memimpin masyarakat mereka adalah bagian penting dari jati diri mereka. Keyakinan bahwa 'suara saya berarti' inilah hal paling mengharukan dalam budaya demokrasi Taiwan.","ballot, vote":"surat suara, memberikan suara","president":"presiden","legislator":"anggota legislatif","campaign rally":"kampanye akbar","street canvassing":"kampanye jalanan","to canvass for votes":"mengumpulkan/meminta dukungan suara","polling station":"tempat pemungutan suara","vote counting":"penghitungan suara","voter turnout":"tingkat partisipasi pemilih","to return to one's hometown":"pulang ke kampung halaman","In Taiwan you still generally must return to your registered household district to vote—absentee or mail-in voting hasn't been introduced. So the day before an election, transport gets crowded with the rush of people heading from cities back to their hometowns. Taiwanese campaigns also make much of each candidate's assigned number, and speeches typically chant number and name together: 'Number X, so-and-so, please, please!' The 'reading out' of each ballot at counting is a scene so familiar it's broadcast live on TV.":"Di Taiwan pada umumnya Anda masih harus kembali ke distrik domisili terdaftar untuk memilih—pemungutan suara jarak jauh atau lewat pos belum diberlakukan. Maka sehari sebelum pemilu, transportasi dipadati arus orang yang bergerak dari kota kembali ke kampung halaman. Kampanye di Taiwan juga sangat menonjolkan nomor urut yang diberikan kepada tiap kandidat, dan pidato biasanya menyerukan nomor dan nama secara bersamaan: 'Nomor X, si Anu, mohon, mohon!' Adegan 'membacakan' tiap surat suara saat penghitungan begitu akrab hingga disiarkan langsung di TV.","Cities & Regions":"Kota & Wilayah","Taipei: The Fast-Paced Capital":"Taipei: Ibu Kota Berirama Cepat","Tap through the gate onto the MRT, and a train arrives every few minutes, carrying you on schedule to the next neighborhood—Taipei is a city of speed. Yet just beyond the towers, green mountains rise up, and duck into an alley and you'll find old teahouses and cafés breathing quietly. Busy, yet somehow calming. Let's look at the many faces of Taiwan's capital.":"Tempelkan kartu di gerbang untuk masuk MRT, dan setiap beberapa menit sebuah kereta datang, membawa Anda tepat waktu ke kawasan berikutnya—Taipei adalah kota kecepatan. Namun tepat di balik gedung-gedung pencakar langit, gunung-gunung hijau menjulang, dan bila Anda menyelinap ke sebuah gang, Anda akan menemukan kedai teh dan kafe tua yang bernapas dengan tenang. Sibuk, tetapi entah bagaimana menenangkan. Mari kita lihat berbagai wajah ibu kota Taiwan.","Taipei is Taiwan's political, economic, and cultural center, and for many people it's their first impression of the island. It sits in the north, ringed by mountains, with a flat basin in the middle and the Tamsui River flowing past the city. The Greater Taipei area is home to several million people; by day, crowds of commuters and students pour into the center from every direction, and by evening they drift back out to the suburbs—an ebb and flow as regular as the tides.":"Taipei adalah pusat politik, ekonomi, dan budaya Taiwan, dan bagi banyak orang inilah kesan pertama mereka tentang pulau ini. Kota ini terletak di utara, dikelilingi pegunungan, dengan cekungan datar di tengah dan Sungai Tamsui mengalir melewati kota. Kawasan Taipei Raya dihuni beberapa juta orang; pada siang hari, kerumunan pekomuter dan pelajar mengalir ke pusat kota dari segala arah, dan menjelang malam mereka menyebar kembali ke pinggiran—pasang surut yang seteratur gelombang laut.","What makes Taipei's speed possible is its public transit, above all the MRT. Taipei's MRT is clean and punctual; eating and drinking are banned in the carriages, and on escalators people automatically stand on the right, leaving the left for those in a hurry. With short intervals and easy transfers—plus a single EasyCard that works on the MRT, buses, and even convenience-store purchases—getting around the city is remarkably smooth. For many Taipei residents, life runs on the MRT timetable.":"Yang memungkinkan kecepatan Taipei adalah transportasi umumnya, terutama MRT. MRT Taipei bersih dan tepat waktu; makan dan minum dilarang di dalam gerbong, dan di eskalator orang otomatis berdiri di sisi kanan, menyisakan sisi kiri untuk mereka yang terburu-buru. Dengan jeda antar-kereta yang singkat dan perpindahan yang mudah—ditambah satu kartu EasyCard yang bisa dipakai di MRT, bus, bahkan untuk berbelanja di minimarket—berkeliling kota terasa sangat lancar. Bagi banyak warga Taipei, hidup berjalan mengikuti jadwal MRT.","When it comes to Taipei landmarks, the most famous is of course Taipei 101. This skyscraper—once the tallest building in the world—is shaped like segments of bamboo growing upward, symbolizing steady rise. At its foot lies Xinyi District, Taipei's most fashionable area, where department stores line up one after another and crowds never stop on weekends. On New Year's Eve, hundreds of thousands pack in here to look up at the fireworks launched from 101 and count down to the new year together. Xinyi is also home to the headquarters of many international and financial firms, with sharply dressed office workers streaming in and out.":"Bicara soal ikon Taipei, yang paling terkenal tentu saja Taipei 101. Pencakar langit ini—yang pernah menjadi gedung tertinggi di dunia—berbentuk seperti ruas-ruas bambu yang tumbuh ke atas, melambangkan kenaikan yang mantap. Di kakinya terletak Distrik Xinyi, kawasan paling modis di Taipei, tempat pusat perbelanjaan berjajar satu demi satu dan keramaian tak pernah reda pada akhir pekan. Pada malam Tahun Baru, ratusan ribu orang berjejal di sini untuk menengadah menyaksikan kembang api yang diluncurkan dari 101 dan bersama-sama menghitung mundur menyambut tahun baru. Xinyi juga menjadi lokasi kantor pusat banyak perusahaan internasional dan keuangan, dengan para pekerja kantoran berbusana rapi yang hilir mudik.","But Taipei isn't only high-rises and fast tempo. Head toward the Shida and Gongguan areas and the mood changes completely. Close to several universities, these streets are full of students, along with one independent bookshop, small café, secondhand record store, and cheap eatery after another. Young people love to curl up in cafés to read, work on laptops, or chat with friends, staying a whole afternoon once they sit down. Taipei's café culture is highly developed—from chains to quirky little places with just a few tables, you can always find a corner to call your own.":"Namun Taipei bukan cuma gedung tinggi dan irama cepat. Menuju kawasan Shida dan Gongguan, suasananya berubah total. Dekat dengan beberapa universitas, jalanan ini penuh mahasiswa, ditambah satu demi satu toko buku independen, kafe kecil, toko piringan hitam bekas, dan warung makan murah. Anak-anak muda gemar meringkuk di kafe untuk membaca, bekerja dengan laptop, atau mengobrol dengan teman, betah seharian penuh begitu duduk. Budaya kafe Taipei sangat berkembang—dari gerai waralaba sampai tempat kecil nyentrik yang cuma punya beberapa meja, Anda selalu bisa menemukan sudut yang terasa milik Anda sendiri.","Another of Taipei's charms is that the city and the mountains are very close. From downtown, take the MRT and switch to a bus and you'll soon reach Yangmingshan—flowers in spring, hot springs in winter. If you fancy a hike, Elephant Mountain (Xiangshan) is just a few stops from Xinyi; twenty or thirty minutes on foot and you're on the ridge, and when you turn around, the whole Taipei basin and 101 lie at your feet. Office workers who've been busy all week often head out at the crack of dawn on weekends, walking into the hills to breathe fresh air and let themselves slow down from the fast pace.":"Pesona lain Taipei adalah kota dan gunungnya yang sangat berdekatan. Dari pusat kota, naik MRT lalu berganti bus, Anda akan segera tiba di Yangmingshan—bunga bermekaran di musim semi, sumber air panas di musim dingin. Jika ingin mendaki, Gunung Gajah (Xiangshan) hanya beberapa stasiun dari Xinyi; berjalan kaki dua puluh atau tiga puluh menit Anda sudah sampai di punggung bukit, dan saat berbalik, seluruh cekungan Taipei dan gedung 101 terhampar di kaki Anda. Para pekerja kantoran yang sibuk sepanjang minggu sering berangkat saat fajar menyingsing pada akhir pekan, berjalan ke perbukitan untuk menghirup udara segar dan membiarkan diri melambat dari ritme yang cepat.","So Taipei really has many faces: the morning tension of catching the MRT, the midday bustle of Xinyi, the aroma of coffee in a Shida alley at dusk, and the leisure of the mountains on weekends. Its pace is fast but not cold, crowded but convenient. First-time visitors may be startled by its rhythm, but live here a while and you'll find that this city always has a way of letting you find your own comfortable balance between fast and slow. That, perhaps, is what makes Taipei most enchanting.":"Jadi Taipei sungguh punya banyak wajah: ketegangan pagi mengejar MRT, keramaian siang di Xinyi, aroma kopi di sebuah gang Shida saat senja, dan santainya pegunungan pada akhir pekan. Iramanya cepat tetapi tidak dingin, padat tetapi praktis. Pengunjung pertama kali mungkin terkejut oleh ritmenya, tetapi tinggallah sebentar di sini dan Anda akan mendapati kota ini selalu punya cara membiarkan Anda menemukan keseimbangan nyaman Anda sendiri antara cepat dan lambat. Itulah, barangkali, yang membuat Taipei paling memikat.","capital city":"ibu kota","MRT / metro (Taiwan term)":"MRT / kereta bawah tanah (istilah Taiwan)","EasyCard (transit IC card)":"EasyCard (kartu IC transportasi)","basin":"cekungan","skyscraper":"pencakar langit","Xinyi District (Taipei's downtown)":"Distrik Xinyi (pusat kota Taipei)","New Year's Eve countdown":"hitung mundur malam Tahun Baru","independent bookshop":"toko buku independen","café":"kafe","mountain ridge":"punggung gunung","pace, tempo":"tempo, irama","Taipei 101 is world-famous for its New Year's fireworks, but it's also known for ultra-fast elevators that whisk you from B1 to the 89th-floor observatory in about 37 seconds. To counter swaying, a giant golden 'tuned mass damper'—a huge suspended ball—hangs near the top and can be viewed as a tourist attraction. Taipei's closeness to mountains is no accident: the city lies in a basin ringed by hills, which is also part of why summers can feel hot and muggy as heat gets trapped.":"Taipei 101 terkenal di dunia karena kembang api Tahun Barunya, tetapi juga dikenal karena lift super cepat yang membawa Anda dari lantai B1 ke dek observasi lantai 89 dalam sekitar 37 detik. Untuk meredam guncangan, sebuah 'peredam massa selaras' emas raksasa—bola tergantung yang sangat besar—digantung di dekat puncak dan bisa dilihat sebagai objek wisata. Kedekatan Taipei dengan pegunungan bukan kebetulan: kota ini terletak di cekungan yang dikelilingi perbukitan, yang juga menjadi salah satu sebab musim panas terasa panas dan pengap karena panas terperangkap.","Tainan: The Slow-Living Old Capital and Its Food":"Tainan: Kota Tua Berkehidupan Santai dan Kulinernya","The day begins, while it's still cool, with a bowl of beef soup, and turn a corner into an alley and you'll run into a four-hundred-year-old temple—Tainan is a city where time flows a little more slowly. Let's explore the easygoing charm and delicious flavors of Taiwan's oldest capital, also known as its 'food capital.'":"Hari dimulai, saat udara masih sejuk, dengan semangkuk sup daging sapi, dan begitu berbelok ke sebuah gang Anda akan berjumpa dengan kuil berusia empat ratus tahun—Tainan adalah kota tempat waktu mengalir sedikit lebih lambat. Mari kita jelajahi pesona santai dan cita rasa lezat dari ibu kota tertua Taiwan, yang juga dijuluki 'ibu kota kuliner'.","Tainan lies in southwestern Taiwan and is the island's oldest city, and it was once Taiwan's capital. More than four hundred years ago, this was among the first places developed by Han settlers and outside powers, leaving behind a wealth of temples, old streets, and historic sites. Walk through Tainan and you'll notice there aren't many tall buildings—instead there are low old houses, red-brick walls, and tree shade. The pace of life here is clearly slower than in Taipei, and people speak in a gentler, warmer tone.":"Tainan terletak di barat daya Taiwan dan merupakan kota tertua di pulau ini, serta pernah menjadi ibu kota Taiwan. Lebih dari empat ratus tahun lalu, tempat ini termasuk yang pertama dikembangkan oleh para pendatang Han dan kekuatan asing, meninggalkan banyak kuil, jalan tua, dan situs bersejarah. Berjalanlah menyusuri Tainan dan Anda akan menyadari tak banyak gedung tinggi—yang ada justru rumah-rumah tua yang rendah, dinding bata merah, dan naungan pepohonan. Irama hidup di sini jelas lebih lambat daripada Taipei, dan orang-orang berbicara dengan nada yang lebih lembut dan hangat.","Tainan is called the 'old capital' mainly because it has especially many historic sites and temples. Chihkan Tower and Anping Fort are historic structures that have survived for four hundred years, and the Confucius Temple is Taiwan's earliest official school—red walls, green tiles, quiet and dignified. Life for Tainan people is tightly bound up with temples; shrines large and small are tucked between residential alleys, hosting lively festivals and deity processions on holidays, and serving as places where residents chat, cool off, and pray on ordinary days.":"Tainan disebut 'kota tua' terutama karena punya sangat banyak situs bersejarah dan kuil. Menara Chihkan dan Benteng Anping adalah bangunan bersejarah yang bertahan selama empat ratus tahun, dan Kuil Konfusius merupakan sekolah resmi paling awal di Taiwan—berdinding merah, beratap genteng hijau, tenang dan berwibawa. Kehidupan orang Tainan terjalin erat dengan kuil; kelenteng besar dan kecil terselip di antara gang-gang permukiman, menggelar festival meriah dan arak-arakan dewa pada hari raya, serta menjadi tempat warga mengobrol, berteduh dari panas, dan berdoa pada hari-hari biasa.","Still, what draws the most people to Tainan on purpose is the food. Tainan is widely acknowledged as Taiwan's 'food capital,' and many local snacks originated right here. Early-morning beef soup is a signature Tainan breakfast: thinly sliced fresh (never frozen) beef is placed in a bowl and scalding broth is poured straight over it, turning the meat a tender pink in an instant; add a bowl of minced-pork rice and you have a perfect start to the day. Danzai noodles use a broth simmered from shrimp heads, topped with a small spoon of minced pork and a single shrimp—modest in size, yet a concentrated essence of Tainan flavor.":"Meski begitu, yang paling banyak menarik orang datang khusus ke Tainan adalah makanannya. Tainan diakui luas sebagai 'ibu kota kuliner' Taiwan, dan banyak jajanan lokal berasal dari sini. Sup daging sapi pagi buta adalah sarapan khas Tainan: daging sapi segar (bukan beku) yang diiris tipis diletakkan di mangkuk lalu kaldu mendidih dituangkan langsung ke atasnya, seketika mengubah dagingnya menjadi merah muda lembut; tambahkan semangkuk nasi cincang babi dan Anda punya awal hari yang sempurna. Mi danzai memakai kaldu yang direbus dari kepala udang, ditaburi sesendok kecil daging babi cincang dan seekor udang—porsinya sederhana, tetapi merupakan sari pati cita rasa Tainan yang pekat.","Tainan's food list is endless. Wa-gui (savory rice pudding) is soft steamed rice-flour cake filled with pork, egg yolk, and mushroom, drizzled with a special sauce—savory, fragrant, and smooth. Shrimp rolls wrap fresh shrimp paste and deep-fry it, crisp outside and tender within, a specialty of the Anping area. There's also 'coffin bread,' eel yi-mian noodles, milkfish congee, and all sorts of douhua (tofu pudding) and mango shaved ice. Almost every old street hides a famous shop or two with a queue. Many places open only half a day and close once they sell out, so if you want to eat, you'll need to get up early.":"Daftar kuliner Tainan tak ada habisnya. Wa-gui (puding beras gurih) adalah kue tepung beras kukus yang lembut berisi daging babi, kuning telur, dan jamur, disiram saus istimewa—gurih, harum, dan lembut. Lumpia udang membungkus pasta udang segar lalu digoreng, renyah di luar dan lembut di dalam, spesialitas kawasan Anping. Ada pula 'roti peti mati', mi yi-mian belut, bubur ikan bandeng, serta aneka douhua (puding tahu) dan es serut mangga. Hampir setiap jalan tua menyembunyikan satu atau dua kedai terkenal yang antre. Banyak tempat hanya buka setengah hari dan tutup begitu dagangan habis, jadi kalau ingin makan, Anda harus bangun pagi-pagi.","Visitors who come to eat in Tainan often notice one thing: the food here tends to be sweet. Even fried noodles, minced pork, and braised dishes carry a hint of sweetness. There are many theories about why Tainan loves sweetness so much: some say it's because Tainan used to produce sugar, which was cheap; others say sweetness signals generosity and sincerity toward guests. Whatever the reason, that faint sweetness has become the most distinctive character of Tainan cuisine—a flavor other cities can't imitate.":"Pengunjung yang datang untuk makan di Tainan sering memperhatikan satu hal: makanan di sini cenderung manis. Bahkan mi goreng, daging babi cincang, dan masakan kecap pun menyimpan sedikit rasa manis. Ada banyak teori mengapa Tainan begitu menyukai rasa manis: sebagian bilang karena dulu Tainan memproduksi gula sehingga gula murah; yang lain bilang rasa manis menandakan kemurahan hati dan ketulusan kepada tamu. Apa pun alasannya, kemanisan samar itu telah menjadi ciri paling khas kuliner Tainan—cita rasa yang tak bisa ditiru kota lain.","Spend a few days in Tainan and you'll gradually grasp the city's philosophy: no need to rush. Have a leisurely bowl of beef soup in the morning, hide from the sun in a café built inside an old house at noon, stroll the temple forecourt and watch the sunset at dusk, and make a round of the night market in the evening. Time seems to slow here, and the distance between people shrinks too. If Taipei represents Taiwan's speed, Tainan represents its warmth—a gentle reminder that eating well and living well are, in themselves, things worth taking seriously.":"Habiskan beberapa hari di Tainan dan Anda akan perlahan memahami filosofi kota ini: tak perlu terburu-buru. Nikmati semangkuk sup daging sapi dengan santai di pagi hari, berlindung dari terik di kafe yang dibangun di dalam rumah tua saat siang, susuri pelataran kuil dan pandangi matahari terbenam kala senja, lalu berkeliling pasar malam di malam hari. Waktu seakan melambat di sini, dan jarak antarmanusia pun menyusut. Jika Taipei mewakili kecepatan Taiwan, Tainan mewakili kehangatannya—pengingat lembut bahwa makan dengan baik dan hidup dengan baik, pada dirinya sendiri, adalah hal yang layak ditekuni dengan sungguh-sungguh.","old / ancient capital":"kota tua / ibu kota kuno","historic site / monument":"situs bersejarah / monumen","temples":"kuil","beef soup (Tainan breakfast specialty)":"sup daging sapi (spesialitas sarapan Tainan)","danzai noodles (shrimp-broth noodles)":"mi danzai (mi berkuah udang)","minced-pork rice":"nasi daging babi cincang","wa-gui (savory steamed rice pudding)":"wa-gui (puding beras kukus gurih)","shrimp roll (deep-fried)":"lumpia udang (goreng)","milkfish":"ikan bandeng","local snacks / street food":"jajanan lokal / makanan kaki lima","tends to be sweet":"cenderung manis","slow living":"hidup santai","Tainan's beef soup is said to taste so good because cattle are raised nearby and 'warm' (never frozen, freshly slaughtered) beef is used the same morning. That's why famous beef-soup shops open at dawn and often sell out before noon. Tainan was long split into 'Tainan City' and 'Tainan County' until 2010, when they merged into a single special municipality. There's even a saying, 'For food, go to Tainan'—locals' devotion to and pride in their cuisine is exceptional.":"Sup daging sapi Tainan konon terasa begitu lezat karena sapinya diternakkan di dekat sana dan daging sapi 'hangat' (bukan beku, baru disembelih) dipakai pada pagi yang sama. Itulah sebabnya kedai sup daging sapi terkenal buka saat fajar dan sering habis sebelum tengah hari. Tainan lama terbagi menjadi 'Kota Tainan' dan 'Kabupaten Tainan' sampai tahun 2010, ketika keduanya digabung menjadi satu kota madya khusus. Bahkan ada pepatah, 'Kalau soal makanan, pergilah ke Tainan'—kecintaan dan kebanggaan warga lokal terhadap kulinernya sungguh luar biasa.","The East Coast and Islands: The 'Back Mountains' and Ocean Escapes":"Pantai Timur dan Kepulauan: 'Gunung Belakang' dan Pelarian ke Laut","Leave the bustle of Taipei and Tainan behind, cross the mountains and head east—there you'll find the blue Pacific and endless green valleys. Hualien and Taitung, and outlying islands like Penghu and Orchid Island. Let's explore the most laid-back, most nature-rich 'other side' of Taiwan.":"Tinggalkan hiruk-pikuk Taipei dan Tainan, seberangi pegunungan dan menujulah ke timur—di sana Anda akan menemukan Samudra Pasifik yang biru dan lembah-lembah hijau tak berujung. Hualien dan Taitung, serta pulau-pulau terluar seperti Penghu dan Pulau Anggrek (Orchid Island). Mari kita jelajahi 'sisi lain' Taiwan yang paling santai dan paling kaya alam.","Eastern Taiwan—the counties of Hualien and Taitung—developed relatively late and has a smaller population, because it's blocked behind the towering Central Mountain Range. People in the west used to call this region the 'back mountains,' with a hint of remoteness and mystery. Precisely because transport was inconvenient and development limited, the east instead preserved Taiwan's cleanest air and most expansive scenery, becoming a kind of pure land in many people's hearts.":"Taiwan bagian timur—Kabupaten Hualien dan Taitung—berkembang relatif terlambat dan berpenduduk lebih sedikit, karena terhalang oleh Pegunungan Tengah yang menjulang. Orang di barat dulu menyebut wilayah ini 'gunung belakang', dengan nuansa keterpencilan dan misteri. Justru karena transportasinya tidak nyaman dan pembangunannya terbatas, timur malah menyimpan udara terbersih dan pemandangan terluas di Taiwan, menjadi semacam tanah suci di hati banyak orang.","The most unforgettable thing about the east is the magnificent scenery where mountains and sea press up against each other. Here two parallel mountain ranges enclose the long East Rift Valley, where rice paddies, indigenous villages, and small towns are scattered across the valley floor, their colors shifting with the seasons. On the other side of the ranges lies the boundless Pacific. Drive the Provincial Highway 11 coastal road and there are sheer cliffs on your left and the deep-blue ocean on your right—a vastness that makes you pull over just to gaze quietly.":"Hal paling tak terlupakan tentang timur adalah pemandangan megah tempat gunung dan laut saling berhimpitan. Di sini dua barisan pegunungan yang sejajar mengapit Lembah Retak Timur (East Rift Valley) yang memanjang, tempat sawah, desa penduduk asli, dan kota-kota kecil tersebar di dasar lembah, warnanya berganti mengikuti musim. Di sisi lain pegunungan terbentang Samudra Pasifik yang tak berbatas. Berkendaralah di jalan pesisir Jalan Provinsi 11, di kiri Anda tebing curam dan di kanan lautan biru pekat—keluasan yang membuat Anda menepi hanya untuk memandanginya diam-diam.","Hualien's most famous sight is the majestic Taroko Gorge. Over millions of years, river water carved deep, narrow gorges out of hard marble; the rock walls tower into the clouds, and roads and trails are cut along the cliffs. Taitung, meanwhile, is more relaxed: on 'Mr. Brown Avenue,' golden waves of rice stretch all the way to the foot of the mountains beneath a high blue sky, and each summer the Hot Air Balloon Festival sends colorful balloons drifting over the Luye Highland—Taitung's most romantic signature scene.":"Pemandangan paling terkenal di Hualien adalah Ngarai Taroko yang megah. Selama jutaan tahun, air sungai mengukir ngarai yang dalam dan sempit dari batu marmer keras; dinding batunya menjulang hingga awan, dan jalan serta jalur setapak dipahat di sepanjang tebing. Sementara itu, Taitung lebih santai: di 'Mr. Brown Avenue', gelombang padi keemasan terhampar hingga ke kaki gunung di bawah langit biru yang tinggi, dan setiap musim panas Festival Balon Udara menerbangkan balon-balon warna-warni yang melayang di atas Dataran Tinggi Luye—pemandangan khas Taitung yang paling romantis.","Beyond the main island's east coast, Taiwan has several enchanting outlying islands, each with its own character. Penghu is made up of many small islands, with white beaches, crystal-clear water, and ancient basalt formations—a summer paradise for swimming and fireworks. Kinmen lies very close to the opposite shore and preserves many wartime tunnels and bunkers, along with traditional Minnan villages and sorghum liquor; its quiet, weighty atmosphere is quite different from the main island.":"Selain pantai timur pulau utama, Taiwan memiliki beberapa pulau terluar yang memikat, masing-masing dengan karakternya sendiri. Penghu terdiri dari banyak pulau kecil, dengan pantai putih, air jernih, dan formasi basal purba—surga musim panas untuk berenang dan menonton kembang api. Kinmen terletak sangat dekat dengan pantai seberang dan menyimpan banyak terowongan serta bunker masa perang, ditambah desa-desa Minnan tradisional dan arak sorgum; suasananya yang tenang dan sarat sejarah sangat berbeda dari pulau utama.","Farther out to sea off Taitung lie two even more pristine islands—Orchid Island (Lanyu) and Green Island (Ludao). Lanyu is the homeland of the Tao people, with traditional semi-underground houses, distinctive plank boats, and an annual flying-fish season—a culture tightly bound to the sea. Green Island is famous for its clear underwater world and is a diver's favorite, home to one of the world's rare 'seabed hot springs.' Getting to these islands isn't easy, but that's exactly why they preserve the purest nature and the slowest pace of life.":"Lebih jauh ke laut lepas dari Taitung terdapat dua pulau yang bahkan lebih perawan—Pulau Anggrek (Lanyu) dan Pulau Hijau (Ludao). Lanyu adalah tanah air suku Tao, dengan rumah semi-bawah-tanah tradisional, perahu papan yang khas, dan musim ikan terbang tahunan—budaya yang terikat erat dengan laut. Pulau Hijau terkenal dengan dunia bawah lautnya yang jernih dan menjadi favorit para penyelam, tempat salah satu 'sumber air panas dasar laut' yang langka di dunia. Mencapai pulau-pulau ini tidak mudah, tetapi justru itulah sebabnya mereka menyimpan alam paling murni dan irama hidup paling lambat.","For many Taiwanese living the fast pace of the big western cities, the east coast and islands are a place to 'escape everyday life.' Take a long holiday, ride the train south along the east coast, or hop a boat or plane to an island for a few days—watch the sea, space out, eat seafood, keep your itinerary loose, and rush nothing. Back in the city, your heart feels recharged. This world of 'back mountains' and open sea is like Taiwan's back garden, a reminder to everyone that this island is far wider and more beautiful than what you see from the cities.":"Bagi banyak orang Taiwan yang menjalani irama cepat kota-kota besar di barat, pantai timur dan kepulauannya adalah tempat untuk 'lari dari kehidupan sehari-hari'. Ambil cuti panjang, naik kereta ke selatan menyusuri pantai timur, atau lompat ke perahu atau pesawat menuju sebuah pulau selama beberapa hari—memandangi laut, melamun, menyantap makanan laut, membiarkan rencana perjalanan longgar, dan tak terburu-buru sama sekali. Kembali ke kota, hati Anda terasa terisi ulang. Dunia 'gunung belakang' dan laut lepas ini bagaikan taman belakang Taiwan, pengingat bagi semua orang bahwa pulau ini jauh lebih luas dan indah daripada yang terlihat dari kota.","'back mountains' (nickname for the east coast)":"'gunung belakang' (julukan untuk pantai timur)","rift valley":"lembah retak","the Pacific Ocean":"Samudra Pasifik","Taroko Gorge":"Ngarai Taroko","gorge, canyon":"ngarai, jurang","outlying island":"pulau terluar","Penghu (islands)":"Penghu (kepulauan)","basalt":"basal","(indigenous) village, tribe":"desa, suku (penduduk asli)","diving":"menyelam","flying fish":"ikan terbang","to escape everyday life":"lari dari kehidupan sehari-hari","The name 'back mountains' is a leftover from when political and economic power sat in the west, casting the east beyond the ranges as the 'other side.' Today, that untouched nature is its greatest draw. The Tao people of Orchid Island treat flying fish as sacred, with detailed traditional rules about when to catch and how to eat them. Penghu's summer fireworks festival is a beloved annual event, drawing crowds for fireworks launched over the sea. If you travel the east, the cliff-hugging Suhua Highway and drives along Highway 11 and Highway 9 through the rice fields are especially spectacular.":"Nama 'gunung belakang' adalah sisa dari masa ketika kekuatan politik dan ekonomi berada di barat, menjadikan timur di seberang pegunungan sebagai 'sisi lain'. Kini, alam yang belum terjamah itu justru menjadi daya tarik terbesarnya. Suku Tao di Pulau Anggrek memperlakukan ikan terbang sebagai hal sakral, dengan aturan tradisional yang rinci tentang kapan menangkap dan bagaimana menyantapnya. Festival kembang api musim panas Penghu adalah acara tahunan yang digemari, menarik kerumunan untuk menyaksikan kembang api yang diluncurkan di atas laut. Jika Anda menjelajahi timur, Jalan Raya Suhua yang menempel di tebing serta perjalanan menyusuri Jalan 11 dan Jalan 9 melewati sawah-sawah sungguh spektakuler.","Nature & Ecology":"Alam & Ekologi","The Formosan Black Bear and Endemic Species: An Island's Exclusive Life":"Beruang Hitam Formosa dan Spesies Endemik: Kehidupan Eksklusif Sebuah Pulau","A bear with a white 'V' on its chest, a wildcat prowling the night forest, a salmon trying to return to the river where it was born—these are creatures found only in Taiwan, or that evolved here into special forms. Let's explore why such a small island holds so much unique life.":"Seekor beruang dengan tanda 'V' putih di dadanya, seekor kucing liar yang mengendap-endap di hutan malam, seekor salmon yang berusaha kembali ke sungai tempatnya lahir—inilah makhluk-makhluk yang hanya ada di Taiwan, atau yang berevolusi di sini menjadi bentuk-bentuk khusus. Mari kita telusuri mengapa pulau sekecil ini menyimpan begitu banyak kehidupan yang unik.","When people think of Taiwan's wildlife, the first that often comes to mind is the Formosan black bear. It is Taiwan's only native bear and the largest land mammal on the island. Its coat is jet black, and its most recognizable feature is the white or pale-yellow 'V' on its chest—many say it looks like a moon worn on its body, which is fitting since it belongs to the family of Asian black bears (moon bears). Because they are so few and so elusive, very few people ever see one in the wild with their own eyes.":"Ketika orang membayangkan satwa liar Taiwan, yang pertama kali sering terlintas adalah beruang hitam Formosa. Ini adalah satu-satunya beruang asli Taiwan dan mamalia darat terbesar di pulau itu. Bulunya hitam legam, dan ciri yang paling mudah dikenali adalah tanda 'V' putih atau kuning pucat di dadanya—banyak yang mengatakan tampak seperti bulan yang dikenakan di tubuhnya, dan itu memang cocok karena ia termasuk keluarga beruang hitam Asia (beruang bulan). Karena jumlahnya sangat sedikit dan sangat sulit ditemui, amat sedikit orang yang pernah melihatnya langsung di alam liar.","The reason Taiwan holds so many plants and animals 'found nowhere else' has much to do with its geological life story. Taiwan is an island on the edge of the Pacific, with mountains over three thousand meters rising through its center. During the ice ages, sea levels were lower, and some animals walked from the mainland to Taiwan across land bridges. When the seas later rose and cut Taiwan off from the outside world, these creatures were 'locked in' on the island, evolving on their own over hundreds of thousands of years until they slowly grew different from their relatives elsewhere. Such species that exist 'only in one place' are called endemic species.":"Alasan Taiwan menyimpan begitu banyak tumbuhan dan hewan yang 'tak ditemukan di tempat lain' sangat terkait dengan kisah pembentukan geologisnya. Taiwan adalah pulau di tepi Samudra Pasifik, dengan gunung-gunung setinggi lebih dari tiga ribu meter menjulang di tengahnya. Selama zaman es, permukaan laut lebih rendah, dan sebagian hewan berjalan dari daratan utama ke Taiwan melalui jembatan darat. Ketika laut kemudian naik dan memutus Taiwan dari dunia luar, makhluk-makhluk ini 'terkurung' di pulau itu, berevolusi sendiri selama ratusan ribu tahun hingga perlahan berbeda dari kerabatnya di tempat lain. Spesies yang hanya ada 'di satu tempat' seperti itu disebut spesies endemik.","Besides the black bear, Taiwan has a cat that everyone loves and worries about—the leopard cat (shíhǔ). It is the only wild feline still living in Taiwan, a bit larger than a house cat, its body covered in cloud-like markings with two white streaks beside each eye. Leopard cats mostly live in the 'low hills,' the zone where human activity meets the forest. Precisely because they live so close to people, they are often hit by cars while crossing roads, or find survival ever harder as their habitat is developed into farmland and houses—making them the most heart-wrenching star of conservation.":"Selain beruang hitam, Taiwan punya seekor kucing yang dicintai sekaligus dikhawatirkan semua orang—kucing kuwuk (shíhǔ). Inilah satu-satunya kucing liar yang masih hidup di Taiwan, sedikit lebih besar dari kucing rumahan, tubuhnya bercorak seperti awan dengan dua garis putih di samping tiap matanya. Kucing kuwuk kebanyakan hidup di 'perbukitan rendah', zona tempat aktivitas manusia bertemu hutan. Justru karena mereka hidup begitu dekat dengan manusia, mereka sering tertabrak mobil saat menyeberang jalan, atau makin sulit bertahan hidup ketika habitatnya diubah menjadi lahan pertanian dan rumah—menjadikan mereka bintang konservasi yang paling memilukan.","If the black bear lives in the high mountains and the leopard cat in the low hills, then one fish hides in the cold streams high in the mountains, and its story is even more legendary—the Formosan landlocked salmon (Oncorhynchus masou formosanus). Salmon normally live in cold oceans and migrate up rivers to spawn, but this Taiwanese salmon was trapped in the mountain streams of central Taiwan and became a 'landlocked' salmon that never goes to sea in its whole life. A living witness of the ice age, it is called the 'national treasure fish.' Because it can survive only in clean, cold water, its numbers once grew extremely perilous, and only through breeding programs has it slowly stabilized.":"Jika beruang hitam hidup di pegunungan tinggi dan kucing kuwuk di perbukitan rendah, maka ada seekor ikan yang bersembunyi di aliran sungai dingin tinggi di pegunungan, dan kisahnya bahkan lebih legendaris—salmon terkurung-daratan Formosa (Oncorhynchus masou formosanus). Salmon biasanya hidup di lautan dingin dan bermigrasi ke hulu sungai untuk bertelur, tetapi salmon Taiwan ini terjebak di aliran sungai pegunungan Taiwan tengah dan menjadi salmon 'terkurung daratan' yang seumur hidup tak pernah ke laut. Sebagai saksi hidup zaman es, ia dijuluki 'ikan pusaka nasional'. Karena hanya bisa bertahan di air bersih dan dingin, jumlahnya pernah amat kritis, dan baru melalui program penangkaran ia perlahan stabil kembali.","These endemic species are precious not only because they are rare, but because they are the 'factory design' of this land of Taiwan—once gone, they can never come back. In recent decades, Taiwanese society has placed ever greater value on conservation: the government designates protected areas and limits forest development, while civic groups pour effort into surveys, rescue, and release back into the wild. Setting up 'animal crossings' beside roads for leopard cats, installing infrared cameras for black bears, and cleaning streams for the landlocked salmon are all done in the hope that these old neighbors can stay with us for good.":"Spesies endemik ini berharga bukan hanya karena langka, melainkan karena mereka adalah 'rancangan asli pabrik' dari tanah Taiwan ini—sekali lenyap, tak akan pernah kembali. Dalam beberapa dekade terakhir, masyarakat Taiwan makin menghargai konservasi: pemerintah menetapkan kawasan lindung dan membatasi pembukaan hutan, sementara kelompok masyarakat mencurahkan tenaga untuk survei, penyelamatan, dan pelepasliaran kembali ke alam. Membangun 'jalur penyeberangan satwa' di tepi jalan untuk kucing kuwuk, memasang kamera inframerah untuk beruang hitam, dan membersihkan aliran sungai untuk salmon terkurung-daratan, semuanya dilakukan dengan harapan agar tetangga-tetangga lama ini bisa selamanya tinggal bersama kita.","For travelers coming to Taiwan, it may be hard to actually meet a black bear or leopard cat in the wild, but you can learn their stories at the Endemic Species Research Institute, at zoos, or at ecological education centers around the island. Next time you walk a mountain road in Taiwan and see a 'watch for animals' sign, or spot the 'black bear' printed on cookies, buses, or lottery tickets, take a moment to think: this island is home to neighbors found nowhere else in the world, and their fate rests in the balance of a single human thought.":"Bagi wisatawan yang datang ke Taiwan, mungkin sulit benar-benar berjumpa dengan beruang hitam atau kucing kuwuk di alam liar, tetapi Anda bisa mempelajari kisah mereka di Institut Penelitian Spesies Endemik, di kebun binatang, atau di pusat-pusat edukasi ekologi di seluruh pulau. Lain kali saat Anda berjalan di jalan pegunungan Taiwan dan melihat rambu 'awas satwa', atau menemukan gambar 'beruang hitam' tercetak di biskuit, bus, atau tiket lotre, luangkan sejenak untuk merenung: pulau ini adalah rumah bagi tetangga-tetangga yang tak ada di tempat lain di dunia, dan nasib mereka bergantung pada keseimbangan satu pikiran manusia saja.","Formosan black bear":"beruang hitam Formosa","endemic species":"spesies endemik","leopard cat":"kucing kuwuk","Formosan landlocked salmon":"salmon terkurung-daratan Formosa","conservation":"konservasi","mammal":"mamalia","habitat":"habitat","migration (of fish)":"migrasi (ikan)","landlocked (type)":"terkurung daratan (jenis)","restoration, captive breeding & release":"pemulihan, penangkaran & pelepasliaran","low hills (near human settlements)":"perbukitan rendah (dekat permukiman)","endangered":"terancam punah","In Taiwan the black bear has become a near-national mascot: a black bear features in 'OhBear,' the tourism bureau's mascot, in many local characters, and in the forestry agency's logo. Researchers estimate that only a few hundred wild Formosan black bears likely remain, and the species is listed as endangered. Leopard cats live mainly in the hill country of the central-west, such as Miaoli, and to reduce roadkill, slow-down signs and animal crossings are being built in many areas. Taiwan is rich not only in endemic mammals but also in endemic birds (like the Swinhoe's and Mikado pheasants), insects, and plants—so much so that the whole island is called a 'laboratory of evolution.'":"Di Taiwan beruang hitam nyaris menjadi maskot nasional: seekor beruang hitam tampil dalam 'OhBear', maskot biro pariwisata, dalam banyak karakter lokal, dan dalam logo badan kehutanan. Para peneliti memperkirakan kemungkinan hanya tersisa beberapa ratus beruang hitam Formosa liar, dan spesies ini terdaftar sebagai terancam punah. Kucing kuwuk hidup terutama di daerah perbukitan tengah-barat, seperti Miaoli, dan untuk mengurangi kematian di jalan, rambu pelan-pelan serta jalur penyeberangan satwa dibangun di banyak wilayah. Taiwan kaya bukan hanya akan mamalia endemik, tetapi juga burung endemik (seperti pegar Swinhoe dan pegar Mikado), serangga, dan tumbuhan—begitu kayanya sampai seluruh pulau ini disebut 'laboratorium evolusi'.","Taiwan's Oceans and Coral Reefs: An Island Embraced by the Sea":"Lautan dan Terumbu Karang Taiwan: Pulau dalam Pelukan Laut","Taiwan is an island surrounded by sea on all sides. Countless creatures carried by the warm Kuroshio Current, coral reefs in every color, clear waters where sea turtles glide—Taiwan is often talked about for its green mountains, but its blue side is astonishingly rich too. Let's dive into the Taiwan that lies beneath the waves.":"Taiwan adalah pulau yang dikelilingi laut di segala sisi. Makhluk-makhluk tak terhitung yang dibawa Arus Hangat Kuroshio, terumbu karang beraneka warna, air jernih tempat penyu meluncur—Taiwan sering dibicarakan karena gunung-gunung hijaunya, tetapi sisi birunya pun kaya luar biasa. Mari kita menyelam ke Taiwan yang berada di bawah ombak.","Taiwan is an island held tightly in the sea's embrace, and the waters around it each have their own character. To the east lies the deep Pacific, where a warm current, the Kuroshio, flows from south to north, carrying vast amounts of plankton and schools of fish. To the west is the shallower Taiwan Strait, with a gentle seabed and rich fisheries. The long, narrow north-south shape, combined with waters where cold and warm currents meet, gives the seas around Taiwan an astonishing variety of marine life—a small island that nonetheless holds a remarkably high share of the world's marine species.":"Taiwan adalah pulau yang didekap erat oleh laut, dan perairan di sekelilingnya masing-masing punya karakter sendiri. Di timur terbentang Samudra Pasifik yang dalam, tempat arus hangat Kuroshio mengalir dari selatan ke utara, membawa plankton dalam jumlah besar dan gerombolan ikan. Di barat ada Selat Taiwan yang lebih dangkal, dengan dasar laut yang landai dan perikanan yang kaya. Bentuknya yang panjang dan sempit dari utara ke selatan, dipadu perairan tempat arus dingin dan hangat bertemu, memberi laut di sekitar Taiwan keanekaragaman hayati laut yang menakjubkan—pulau kecil yang toh menyimpan porsi spesies laut dunia yang luar biasa tinggi.","When people think of Taiwan's sea, the first place many picture is Kenting at the southern tip. It is Taiwan's most famous seaside resort, with fine white sand, deep-blue water, and abundant coral reefs. There's sea breeze in winter and sunshine in summer, and people come all year round to swim, surf, and dive. The Kenting area is designated as a national park, its underwater world a riot of color—for many, it's the place where they first put on a snorkel mask, dipped their face into the sea, and saw living coral and tropical fish.":"Ketika membayangkan laut Taiwan, tempat pertama yang terlintas bagi banyak orang adalah Kenting di ujung selatan. Inilah resor tepi laut paling terkenal di Taiwan, dengan pasir putih halus, air biru pekat, dan terumbu karang yang melimpah. Ada angin laut di musim dingin dan sinar matahari di musim panas, dan orang datang sepanjang tahun untuk berenang, berselancar, dan menyelam. Kawasan Kenting ditetapkan sebagai taman nasional, dunia bawah lautnya penuh warna—bagi banyak orang, di sinilah pertama kali mereka memakai masker snorkel, mencelupkan wajah ke laut, dan melihat karang hidup serta ikan tropis.","To see cleaner, more pristine sea, many people take a boat or plane to two outlying islands off the east coast—Green Island (Lüdao) and Orchid Island (Lanyu). Far from city lights and pollution, the water here is so clear that visibility is extremely high, making it a paradise for Taiwan's divers. Green Island has a famous seabed hot spring and vast stretches of coral, while Orchid Island is the homeland of the Tao (Yami) people, who preserve a traditional culture deeply tied to the ocean. Here, the moment you dive in, you may brush past schools of tropical fish and sea turtles.":"Untuk melihat laut yang lebih bersih dan lebih perawan, banyak orang naik perahu atau pesawat ke dua pulau terluar di lepas pantai timur—Pulau Hijau (Lüdao) dan Pulau Anggrek (Lanyu). Jauh dari lampu kota dan polusi, airnya di sini begitu jernih sehingga jarak pandangnya sangat tinggi, menjadikannya surga bagi para penyelam Taiwan. Pulau Hijau punya sumber air panas dasar laut yang terkenal dan hamparan karang yang luas, sedangkan Pulau Anggrek adalah tanah air suku Tao (Yami), yang menjaga budaya tradisional yang terikat erat dengan laut. Di sini, begitu Anda menyelam, Anda mungkin berserempetan dengan gerombolan ikan tropis dan penyu.","Coral reefs are often called the 'rainforests of the sea.' Coral may look like rock or plant, but it is actually a tiny animal that lives thanks to the photosynthesis of the symbiotic algae inside it, building up bit by bit into a vast reef. This kaleidoscope of reef is home and feeding ground to countless fish, shrimp, shellfish, and sea turtles. You could say that once a healthy coral reef forms, it holds up the whole web of life across the waters; and conversely, once the coral sickens, the entire underwater world dims along with it.":"Terumbu karang sering disebut 'hutan hujan laut'. Karang mungkin terlihat seperti batu atau tumbuhan, tetapi sebenarnya ia hewan mungil yang hidup berkat fotosintesis alga simbiosis di dalamnya, membangun dirinya sedikit demi sedikit menjadi terumbu yang luas. Terumbu warna-warni ini adalah rumah dan tempat mencari makan bagi ikan, udang, kerang, dan penyu yang tak terhitung. Bisa dibilang begitu terumbu karang yang sehat terbentuk, ia menopang seluruh jaring kehidupan di perairan itu; dan sebaliknya, begitu karangnya sakit, seluruh dunia bawah laut pun ikut meredup.","Taiwan's sea has its own 'superstars' too. Every spring and summer, pods of whales and dolphins appear off the coast of Hualien and Taitung, and 'whale watching' has become a popular activity along the east coast. If you're lucky, you can see whole schools of spinner dolphins leap from the water and twist in the air, or even meet a giant sperm whale. And while diving or snorkeling, the most breathtaking encounter is often a sea turtle drifting leisurely past your eyes; the area around Xiaoliuqiu is famous for its many turtles and is called by many the 'hometown of sea turtles.'":"Laut Taiwan pun punya 'bintang-bintang'-nya sendiri. Setiap musim semi dan panas, kawanan paus dan lumba-lumba muncul di lepas pantai Hualien dan Taitung, dan 'menonton paus' menjadi kegiatan populer di sepanjang pantai timur. Jika beruntung, Anda bisa melihat seluruh kawanan lumba-lumba spinner melompat dari air dan berputar di udara, atau bahkan berjumpa dengan paus sperma raksasa. Dan saat menyelam atau snorkeling, perjumpaan paling memukau sering kali adalah seekor penyu yang meluncur santai melintas di depan mata Anda; kawasan sekitar Xiaoliuqiu terkenal karena banyaknya penyu dan oleh banyak orang disebut 'kampung halaman penyu'.","Such a beautiful ocean is, in fact, under no small pressure. Rising water temperatures cause coral to 'bleach' and even die; carelessly discarded plastic trash and abandoned fishing nets entangle sea turtles and fish; and overfishing makes certain species ever scarcer. In recent years Taiwanese have placed growing importance on marine conservation: setting up marine protected areas, promoting beach cleanups, cutting single-use plastics, and regulating whale-watching and diving. More and more people believe that only by treating this sea well will it keep giving back its beauty and its harvests to this island wrapped in ocean.":"Lautan yang seindah itu sebenarnya berada di bawah tekanan yang tak kecil. Naiknya suhu air menyebabkan karang 'memutih' dan bahkan mati; sampah plastik yang dibuang sembarangan dan jaring ikan yang ditinggalkan menjerat penyu dan ikan; serta penangkapan ikan berlebihan membuat sejumlah spesies makin langka. Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir orang Taiwan makin mementingkan konservasi laut: mendirikan kawasan lindung laut, menggalakkan pembersihan pantai, mengurangi plastik sekali pakai, dan mengatur wisata menonton paus dan menyelam. Makin banyak orang percaya bahwa hanya dengan memperlakukan laut ini dengan baik, ia akan terus mengembalikan keindahan dan hasilnya kepada pulau yang dibalut lautan ini.","ocean, sea":"lautan, laut","coral reef":"terumbu karang","the Kuroshio (warm current)":"Kuroshio (arus hangat)","snorkeling":"snorkeling","whale watching":"menonton paus","sea turtle":"penyu","(coral) bleaching":"pemutihan (karang)","beach cleanup":"pembersihan pantai","biodiversity":"keanekaragaman hayati","overfishing":"penangkapan ikan berlebihan","Though small in area, the waters around Taiwan are said to host roughly one-tenth of the world's marine fish species, making it a region of exceptionally high marine biodiversity. In recent years a dedicated government body, the Ocean Affairs Council, was established to manage the protection and use of the sea. At Xiaoliuqiu, green sea turtles are seen near the shore every day and can be swum with while snorkeling, making it very popular—though touching or feeding the turtles is banned by law. The Tao people of Orchid Island are known for their traditional plank-built canoes and flying-fish fishing culture, a way of life with the sea that is still handed down today.":"Meski luasnya kecil, perairan di sekitar Taiwan disebut menampung sekitar sepersepuluh spesies ikan laut dunia, menjadikannya kawasan dengan keanekaragaman hayati laut yang sangat tinggi. Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, sebuah badan pemerintah khusus, Dewan Urusan Kelautan, dibentuk untuk mengelola perlindungan dan pemanfaatan laut. Di Xiaoliuqiu, penyu hijau terlihat di dekat pantai setiap hari dan bisa diajak berenang saat snorkeling, sehingga sangat populer—meski menyentuh atau memberi makan penyu dilarang oleh hukum. Suku Tao di Pulau Anggrek dikenal dengan kano papan tradisional dan budaya penangkapan ikan terbang mereka, cara hidup bersama laut yang masih diwariskan hingga kini.","Taiwan's National Parks: Ecosystems from Seabed to Cloud":"Taman Nasional Taiwan: Ekosistem dari Dasar Laut hingga Awan","From snowy peaks nearly four thousand meters high, to marble gorges carved into cliffs, to volcanoes trailing steam, to tropical coral reefs—Taiwan holds within this small island a nature that feels like a whole world in miniature. Let's tour the national parks that protect these varied landscapes, from mountain to sea.":"Dari puncak-puncak bersalju setinggi hampir empat ribu meter, ngarai marmer yang terpahat di tebing, gunung berapi yang mengepulkan uap, hingga terumbu karang tropis—Taiwan menyimpan di dalam pulau kecil ini alam yang terasa seperti seluruh dunia dalam bentuk mini. Mari kita berkeliling taman-taman nasional yang melindungi bentang alam beragam ini, dari gunung hingga laut.","Though Taiwan is not large in area, it is in fact a 'high-mountain island.' It has more than two hundred peaks over three thousand meters, a density among the highest in the world. Because of this, Taiwan's landscapes can change dramatically over short distances: from coral reefs by the sea, you climb all the way up to mountains cold year-round, passing subtropical, temperate, and frigid forests along the way. To protect these precious and fragile environments, Taiwan has established several national parks one after another, enclosing its most representative mountains, rivers, and seas to leave them for future generations.":"Meski luasnya tidak besar, Taiwan sebenarnya adalah 'pulau pegunungan tinggi'. Ia memiliki lebih dari dua ratus puncak di atas tiga ribu meter, kepadatan yang termasuk tertinggi di dunia. Karena itu, bentang alam Taiwan bisa berubah drastis dalam jarak yang pendek: dari terumbu karang di tepi laut, Anda mendaki terus hingga ke gunung yang dingin sepanjang tahun, melewati hutan subtropis, sedang, dan dingin di sepanjang jalan. Untuk melindungi lingkungan yang berharga dan rapuh ini, Taiwan mendirikan beberapa taman nasional satu demi satu, memagari gunung, sungai, dan lautnya yang paling representatif agar tersisa bagi generasi mendatang.","Speaking of Taiwan's high mountains, one cannot leave out Yushan National Park. Within it, the main peak of Yushan (Jade Mountain) rises to nearly 3,952 meters, the highest point in Taiwan and often called a symbol of the island. Many climbers regard 'climbing Yushan to watch the sunrise' as a must-do in life, setting out for the summit in the dark before dawn just to watch, from the ridgeline, the sun rise out of a sea of clouds. This is also home to high-mountain animals like the Formosan sambar deer, yellow-throated marten, and white-whiskered laughingthrush—every blade of grass and every tree striving to live in the harsh conditions of high altitude.":"Bicara soal pegunungan tinggi Taiwan, tak boleh melewatkan Taman Nasional Yushan. Di dalamnya, puncak utama Yushan (Gunung Giok) menjulang hampir 3.952 meter, titik tertinggi di Taiwan dan sering disebut sebagai lambang pulau ini. Banyak pendaki menganggap 'mendaki Yushan untuk menyaksikan matahari terbit' sebagai hal yang wajib dilakukan seumur hidup, berangkat ke puncak dalam gelap sebelum fajar hanya untuk menyaksikan, dari punggung gunung, matahari terbit dari lautan awan. Ini juga rumah bagi hewan pegunungan tinggi seperti rusa sambar Formosa, musang leher kuning, dan burung poksai janggut putih—setiap helai rumput dan setiap pohon berjuang untuk hidup dalam kondisi keras di ketinggian.","If Yushan symbolizes Taiwan's 'height,' then Taroko National Park symbolizes its 'peril' and 'wonder.' The most famous sight here is a deep gorge that a river carved over several million years through hard marble strata—Taroko Gorge. Walking a trail cut along the cliffs, you look up at rock walls soaring into the clouds and down at an emerald, rushing stream; the shock of being surrounded by the power of nature leaves many first-time visitors speechless. Among the gorge live Formosan macaques and many kinds of birds.":"Jika Yushan melambangkan 'ketinggian' Taiwan, maka Taman Nasional Taroko melambangkan 'kecuraman' dan 'keajaibannya'. Pemandangan paling terkenal di sini adalah ngarai dalam yang diukir sungai selama beberapa juta tahun menembus lapisan marmer keras—Ngarai Taroko. Berjalan di jalur setapak yang dipahat di sepanjang tebing, Anda menengadah ke dinding batu yang menjulang ke awan dan menunduk ke sungai zamrud yang deras; keterkejutan karena dikelilingi kekuatan alam membuat banyak pengunjung pertama kali terpana tanpa kata. Di dalam ngarai hidup monyet Formosa dan aneka jenis burung.","Leaving the high mountains for the outskirts of Taipei, there is Yangmingshan National Park. What makes it most special is that it bears the mark of a volcano. Here you'll find a geothermal valley venting sulfur steam and Xiaoyoukeng with its rising white plumes, a faint smell of sulfur drifting in the air. In spring the hills burst with azaleas and calla lilies; in autumn silver grass ripples like white waves in the wind on the slopes. Being close to the city, Yangmingshan has become the 'backyard' Taipei residents most love on holidays—soak in hot springs, admire flowers, walk the trails, and in a single day you can escape from the city into the mountain woods.":"Beranjak dari pegunungan tinggi ke pinggiran Taipei, ada Taman Nasional Yangmingshan. Yang membuatnya paling istimewa adalah ia menyandang jejak gunung berapi. Di sini Anda akan menemukan lembah panas bumi yang menyemburkan uap belerang dan Xiaoyoukeng dengan kepulan asap putihnya, aroma belerang samar mengambang di udara. Di musim semi, perbukitan meriah oleh azalea dan bunga calla lily; di musim gugur, rumput perak beriak seperti gelombang putih tertiup angin di lerengnya. Karena dekat dengan kota, Yangmingshan menjadi 'halaman belakang' yang paling disukai warga Taipei pada hari libur—berendam di sumber air panas, mengagumi bunga, menyusuri jalur setapak, dan dalam satu hari Anda bisa kabur dari kota ke rimba pegunungan.","And at the island's southernmost tip, Kenting National Park reveals an entirely different side of Taiwan. It was Taiwan's first national park, and its bounds include not only land but also the seas and coral reefs to the south. The climate is warm, like summer all year, with tropical forests and strange uplifted-coral rock formations on land, and colorful coral and tropical fish in the water. Every autumn, tens of thousands of migratory birds pass through Kenting on their way south to warmer wintering grounds, creating a spectacular 'raptor-watching' season that draws crowds of birdwatchers.":"Dan di ujung paling selatan pulau, Taman Nasional Kenting mengungkap sisi Taiwan yang sama sekali berbeda. Inilah taman nasional pertama Taiwan, dan wilayahnya mencakup bukan hanya daratan, tetapi juga laut dan terumbu karang di sebelah selatan. Iklimnya hangat, seperti musim panas sepanjang tahun, dengan hutan tropis dan formasi batu karang terangkat yang aneh di daratan, serta karang warna-warni dan ikan tropis di dalam air. Setiap musim gugur, puluhan ribu burung migran melintasi Kenting dalam perjalanan ke selatan menuju daerah musim dingin yang lebih hangat, menciptakan musim 'menonton burung pemangsa' yang spektakuler yang menarik kerumunan pengamat burung.","From soaring Yushan and rugged Taroko to volcanic Yangmingshan and oceanic Kenting, Taiwan's national parks cover almost every ecosystem 'from the seabed to the clouds.' In recent years, the idea of ecotourism has grown ever more popular: on the trails, don't stray off the path, don't feed wild animals, carry your trash back down the mountain, keep your voice low, and leave nothing but footprints. These seemingly small rules all exist so that the next person to come can see the same beautiful scenery. When you step into Taiwan's mountains and seas, you become not just a visitor, but part of what protects this land.":"Dari Yushan yang menjulang dan Taroko yang terjal hingga Yangmingshan yang vulkanik dan Kenting yang berlaut, taman-taman nasional Taiwan mencakup hampir setiap ekosistem 'dari dasar laut hingga awan'. Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, gagasan ekowisata makin populer: di jalur setapak, jangan menyimpang dari jalan, jangan memberi makan satwa liar, bawa turun sampah Anda dari gunung, pelankan suara, dan jangan tinggalkan apa pun selain jejak kaki. Aturan yang tampak sepele ini semuanya ada agar orang berikutnya yang datang bisa melihat pemandangan indah yang sama. Ketika Anda melangkah ke gunung dan laut Taiwan, Anda menjadi bukan sekadar pengunjung, melainkan bagian dari yang melindungi tanah ini.","national park":"taman nasional","Yushan (Jade Mountain, Taiwan's highest peak)":"Yushan (Gunung Giok, puncak tertinggi Taiwan)","Taroko":"Taroko","volcano":"gunung berapi","trail, walkway":"jalur setapak, jalan setapak","ecotourism":"ekowisata","mountain climbing, hiking":"mendaki gunung, hiking","sea of clouds":"lautan awan","migratory bird":"burung migran","sulfur":"belerang","altitude, elevation":"ketinggian","Taiwan currently has nine national parks. Besides Yushan, Taroko, Yangmingshan, and Kenting mentioned above, there are Shei-Pa (covering the Xueshan Range), Kinmen (protecting the battlefield heritage and nature of Kinmen Island), the South Penghu Marine park (guarding Penghu's basalt coasts), and vast mountain areas containing Taiwan's highest peaks. In many high-mountain areas, an 'entry/park permit' (a hiking registration and permit) is required for environmental protection and safety, and popular routes like Yushan's main peak are so sought-after they're allocated by lottery. Because parts of Taroko's trails can be closed after earthquakes in recent years, it's wise to check the latest opening information before you go.":"Taiwan saat ini memiliki sembilan taman nasional. Selain Yushan, Taroko, Yangmingshan, dan Kenting yang disebut di atas, ada Shei-Pa (mencakup Pegunungan Xueshan), Kinmen (melindungi warisan medan perang dan alam Pulau Kinmen), Taman Laut Penghu Selatan (menjaga pesisir basal Penghu), serta kawasan pegunungan luas yang memuat puncak-puncak tertinggi Taiwan. Di banyak kawasan pegunungan tinggi, diperlukan 'izin masuk/izin taman' (registrasi dan izin pendakian) demi perlindungan lingkungan dan keselamatan, dan rute populer seperti puncak utama Yushan begitu diminati sampai dialokasikan lewat undian. Karena sebagian jalur Taroko bisa ditutup setelah gempa dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, bijak untuk memeriksa informasi pembukaan terbaru sebelum berangkat.","Work & Living":"Kerja & Kehidupan","Taiwan's Workplace Culture: Year-End Feasts, Bonuses, and Life Among Colleagues":"Budaya Kerja Taiwan: Jamuan Akhir Tahun, Bonus, dan Kehidupan di Antara Rekan Kerja","As the year winds down, two words hover in the mind of every Taiwanese office worker: 'weiya' (the year-end feast) and 'nianzhong' (the year-end bonus). There's overtime, but also warm camaraderie; there are demanding bosses, but also dependable senior colleagues. Taiwan's workplace is a very human place that no set of rules alone can capture. Let's step into a day at the office.":"Menjelang akhir tahun, dua kata selalu melayang di benak setiap pekerja kantoran Taiwan: 'weiya' (jamuan akhir tahun) dan 'nianzhong' (bonus akhir tahun). Ada lembur, tetapi juga kehangatan persahabatan; ada atasan yang menuntut, tetapi juga senior yang bisa diandalkan. Tempat kerja di Taiwan adalah tempat yang sangat manusiawi yang tak bisa ditangkap hanya oleh seperangkat aturan. Mari kita masuk ke dalam satu hari di kantor.","In Taiwan, a job is often more than just 'earning a paycheck'—relationships among colleagues can feel almost like a second family. At many companies, lunchtime brings a round of 'Shall we order boxed meals together?', and in the afternoon someone will organize a group order for bubble tea—a cup of pearl milk tea here, a cup of black tea there—chatting a bit along the way. These small daily exchanges add a touch of warmth to the office and help newcomers blend into the team more easily.":"Di Taiwan, sebuah pekerjaan sering kali lebih dari sekadar 'mencari gaji'—hubungan antar-rekan kerja bisa terasa hampir seperti keluarga kedua. Di banyak perusahaan, jam makan siang memunculkan seruan 'Kita pesan nasi kotak bareng, yuk?', dan di sore hari seseorang akan mengoordinasi pesanan boba bersama—satu gelas teh susu mutiara di sini, satu gelas teh hitam di sana—sambil sedikit mengobrol. Interaksi kecil sehari-hari ini menambah kehangatan di kantor dan membantu pendatang baru lebih mudah membaur ke dalam tim.","That said, Taiwan's workplace has its harder side too, namely 'overtime.' In some industries—especially tech and services—overtime is almost routine. There's a system called 'responsibility-based work' (zerenzhi), nominally 'just get the job done, we don't count the hours,' but in practice it often becomes 'the work never ends, so you have no choice but to stay.' As a result, 'What time do you get off work?' can be a sensitive and very real question in Taiwan.":"Meski begitu, tempat kerja Taiwan juga punya sisi yang lebih berat, yaitu 'lembur'. Di sebagian industri—terutama teknologi dan jasa—lembur nyaris menjadi rutinitas. Ada sistem yang disebut 'kerja berbasis tanggung jawab' (zerenzhi), yang secara nama berarti 'yang penting pekerjaan selesai, kami tak menghitung jam', tetapi dalam praktiknya sering menjadi 'pekerjaan tak pernah habis, jadi Anda tak punya pilihan selain tinggal'. Akibatnya, 'Jam berapa kamu pulang kerja?' bisa menjadi pertanyaan yang sensitif dan sangat nyata di Taiwan.","At year's end, two big events fire up the whole workplace: the 'year-end bonus' (nianzhong jiangjin) and the 'weiya' feast. The year-end bonus is usually paid before Lunar New Year; generous companies give several months' salary, stingy ones maybe just a few thousand dollars, and the amount often becomes the yardstick by which employees judge whether a company is 'decent' to them. Whether you get a bonus—and how big—is a favorite topic that everyone loves to quietly compare when friends gather before the New Year.":"Menjelang akhir tahun, ada dua peristiwa besar yang menghidupkan seluruh dunia kerja: 'bonus akhir tahun' (nianzhong jiangjin) dan pesta 'weiya'. Bonus akhir tahun biasanya dibayarkan sebelum Tahun Baru Imlek; perusahaan yang murah hati memberi beberapa bulan gaji, yang pelit mungkin hanya beberapa ribu dolar, dan besarannya sering menjadi tolok ukur bagi karyawan untuk menilai apakah sebuah perusahaan cukup 'baik' kepada mereka. Apakah kamu mendapat bonus—dan seberapa besar—adalah topik favorit yang suka diam-diam dibandingkan setiap kali teman-teman berkumpul menjelang Tahun Baru.","The 'weiya' is a Taiwanese company's once-a-year year-end banquet, rooted in the folk custom of worshiping the Earth God and now evolved into a grand feast where firms reward their staff. Big companies book out hotels, lay on lavish banquet dishes, hire singers to perform, and hold lucky draws—the top prize is sometimes a scooter, an appliance, even tens of thousands in cash. The boss takes the stage to speak and toast, while employees eat and wait in anticipation for their number to be drawn. The thrill of winning a big weiya prize is a shared memory for Taiwan's office workers.":"'Weiya' adalah jamuan akhir tahun yang digelar perusahaan Taiwan setahun sekali, berakar dari tradisi rakyat memuja Dewa Bumi dan kini berkembang menjadi pesta besar tempat perusahaan menghargai karyawannya. Perusahaan besar memesan seluruh hotel, menyuguhkan hidangan jamuan mewah, mengundang penyanyi tampil, dan mengadakan undian—hadiah utamanya kadang berupa skuter, peralatan elektronik, bahkan puluhan ribu uang tunai. Bos naik ke panggung untuk berpidato dan bersulang, sementara karyawan makan sambil menanti dengan penuh harap nomornya ditarik. Sensasi memenangkan hadiah besar di weiya adalah kenangan bersama para pekerja kantoran Taiwan.","Working in Taiwan, you'll also gradually learn how to address the people around you. Those who joined before you and have more experience are usually called 'qianbei' (senior/mentor); the person who trains and teaches you might be your 'supervisor' or 'leader.' To outsiders, everyone habitually calls the head of a small business 'laoban' (boss)—even at a roadside food stall, customers often call out 'Laoban!' Seniors guiding newcomers, old hands looking after rookies: this relationship of mutual care across ranks is an important unspoken rule of Taiwan's workplace.":"Saat bekerja di Taiwan, kamu juga akan perlahan belajar cara menyapa orang-orang di sekitarmu. Mereka yang bergabung lebih dulu dan lebih berpengalaman biasanya dipanggil 'qianbei' (senior/mentor); orang yang melatih dan mengajarimu mungkin 'supervisor' atau 'leader'-mu. Kepada orang luar, semua orang terbiasa memanggil pemilik usaha kecil dengan sebutan 'laoban' (bos)—bahkan di warung pinggir jalan pun pelanggan sering berseru 'Laoban!' Senior membimbing pendatang baru, orang lama menjaga pemula: hubungan saling peduli antarjenjang ini adalah aturan tak tertulis yang penting di dunia kerja Taiwan.","On the whole, Taiwan's workplace culture strikes a balance between 'human warmth' and 'efficiency.' It isn't as fixated on strict hierarchy and elaborate etiquette as some places; colleagues can joke around, eat together, and hit the karaoke after work—yet when work comes, everyone can knuckle down and give it their all. For foreigners, simply being willing to greet others first and learning a few phrases of common Taiwanese speech usually lets you quickly feel your colleagues' goodwill and find your place on this land.":"Secara keseluruhan, budaya kerja Taiwan menyeimbangkan antara 'kehangatan manusiawi' dan 'efisiensi'. Ia tidak sekaku sebagian tempat dalam hal hierarki ketat dan tata krama yang rumit; rekan kerja bisa bercanda, makan bersama, dan pergi karaoke sepulang kerja—namun ketika pekerjaan datang, semua orang bisa serius dan mengerahkan segenap tenaga. Bagi orang asing, cukup dengan mau menyapa lebih dulu dan mempelajari beberapa frasa bahasa Taiwan yang umum, biasanya kamu akan cepat merasakan niat baik rekan-rekan kerja dan menemukan tempatmu di tanah ini.","salary, wages":"gaji, upah","'responsibility-based' work system (often means unpaid overtime)":"sistem kerja 'berbasis tanggung jawab' (sering berarti lembur tanpa bayaran)","year-end bonus":"bonus akhir tahun","weiya, company year-end feast":"weiya, jamuan akhir tahun perusahaan","boss, owner, proprietor":"bos, pemilik, juragan","senior colleague, mentor":"senior, mentor","supervisor, manager":"atasan, manajer","colleague, coworker":"rekan kerja","boxed meal, bento":"nasi kotak, bento","hand-shaken drink (bubble-tea-style beverage)":"minuman kocok tangan (minuman ala bubble tea)","lucky draw, raffle":"undian berhadiah","The 'weiya' has a counterpart called 'touya' (the second day of the second lunar month), the first 'ya' feast of the year, praying for a prosperous business year. There's an old, ominous tradition that at a weiya, whoever the roast chicken's head pointed to was quietly being told 'your contract won't be renewed'—i.e., you're fired (this has largely died out). In Taiwan, the term '22K' also became a buzzword symbolizing the social problem of low starting salaries for young people, so talk of pay is also a mirror of each generation's mood.":"'Weiya' punya padanan bernama 'touya' (hari kedua bulan dua Imlek), jamuan 'ya' pertama dalam setahun, untuk memohon tahun usaha yang makmur. Ada tradisi lama yang berkonotasi buruk: pada weiya, siapa pun yang ditunjuk oleh kepala ayam panggang diam-diam sedang diberi tahu 'kontrakmu tidak akan diperpanjang'—alias kamu dipecat (kini tradisi ini nyaris punah). Di Taiwan, istilah '22K' juga menjadi kata populer yang melambangkan masalah sosial rendahnya gaji awal anak muda, sehingga bicara soal upah juga mencerminkan suasana hati tiap generasi.","Stir-Fry Joints and Nightlife: Taiwan After Hours":"Warung Tumis dan Kehidupan Malam: Taiwan Selepas Kerja","When work ends and the sun goes down, another side of Taiwan comes alive. Plastic stools, sweating bottles of beer, flames leaping from a wok—at a 'rechao' stir-fry joint, you knock back a few with colleagues and friends, then drift on to a second and a third venue. Let's step into the heat and see how Taiwanese unwind after dark.":"Ketika kerja usai dan matahari terbenam, sisi lain Taiwan menjadi hidup. Bangku plastik, botol-botol bir berembun, api yang menyembur dari wajan—di warung tumis 'rechao', kamu menenggak beberapa gelas bersama rekan kerja dan teman, lalu berlanjut ke tempat kedua dan ketiga. Mari masuk ke tengah keramaian dan lihat bagaimana orang Taiwan melepas penat setelah gelap.","If you had to pick the one place that best captures a Taiwanese night, many would vote for the 'rechao' stir-fry joint. A rechao is a Taiwanese quick stir-fry restaurant—affordable and fast. Signs often read 'hundred-dollar stir-fry,' meaning many dishes cost just a hundred NT dollars a plate. There's usually no air-conditioning; red plastic stools and round tables fill the room, handwritten menus paper the walls, the kitchen stir-fries over roaring flames, spatula and wok clang away, and the whole place steams with heat and buzzes with voices.":"Kalau harus memilih satu tempat yang paling menggambarkan malam Taiwan, banyak yang akan memilih warung tumis 'rechao'. Rechao adalah restoran tumis cepat khas Taiwan—murah dan cepat. Papan namanya sering bertuliskan 'tumisan seratus dolar', artinya banyak hidangan hanya seharga seratus dolar NT per piring. Biasanya tanpa AC; bangku plastik merah dan meja bundar memenuhi ruangan, menu tulisan tangan menempel di dinding, dapur menumis di atas api yang berkobar, sudip dan wajan berdenting, dan seluruh tempat mengepul panas serta riuh oleh suara orang.","The soul of rechao, besides the food, is 'Taiwan Beer.' It's the island's most classic brand, chilled ice-cold, and paired with stir-fried clams, popcorn chicken, three-cup chicken, and fried rice for the most authentic combo. Everyone chats while they 'ganbei' (bottoms up), clinking glasses and shouting 'Ho gan la!'—Taiwanese for 'drink it dry.' This unfussy atmosphere of big bites and big gulps is exactly how Taiwanese relax and bond.":"Jiwa dari rechao, selain makanannya, adalah 'Taiwan Beer'. Ini merek paling klasik di pulau tersebut, didinginkan hingga sedingin es, dan dipadukan dengan kerang tumis, ayam popcorn, ayam tiga cawan, dan nasi goreng untuk kombinasi paling autentik. Semua orang mengobrol sambil 'ganbei' (habiskan sampai tandas), mengadu gelas dan berteriak 'Ho gan la!'—bahasa Taiwan untuk 'minum sampai habis'. Suasana santai makan banyak dan minum banyak inilah cara orang Taiwan bersantai dan mempererat hubungan.","Taiwanese drinking has an important culture called 'xu tan'—moving to the next venue (barhopping). When a meal or a round is done, if everyone's still not satisfied, someone will propose 'Come on, let's hit another spot!' So you move from the rechao joint to an izakaya, a bar, even on to KTV to sing. First stop, second stop, third stop—you keep changing venues, drinking later and later. Whether or not you're up for the next round can even signal how deep the friendship runs.":"Budaya minum orang Taiwan punya hal penting bernama 'xu tan'—berpindah ke tempat berikutnya (barhopping). Ketika sebuah santapan atau satu ronde selesai, jika semua orang masih belum puas, seseorang akan mengusulkan 'Ayo, pindah ke tempat lain!' Maka kamu berpindah dari warung rechao ke izakaya, ke bar, bahkan lanjut ke KTV untuk bernyanyi. Tempat pertama, kedua, ketiga—kamu terus berganti tempat, minum makin larut. Mau atau tidaknya kamu lanjut ke ronde berikutnya bahkan bisa menandakan seberapa dalam persahabatan itu.","Beyond rechao, Taiwan's nightlife is genuinely diverse. Those who like a Japanese vibe head to an 'izakaya' for skewers and sake and a quieter mood; young people wanting to relax and chat seek out a bar with a mixologist and order a signature cocktail; those craving something livelier make for a nightclub, dancing into the small hours amid pounding music and lights. Taipei's Xinyi and East districts, and the bar streets of every big city, overflow with crowds come the weekend.":"Selain rechao, kehidupan malam Taiwan benar-benar beragam. Mereka yang menyukai nuansa Jepang pergi ke 'izakaya' untuk sate dan sake serta suasana yang lebih tenang; anak muda yang ingin bersantai dan mengobrol mencari bar dengan mixologist dan memesan koktail khas; yang mendambakan sesuatu yang lebih meriah menuju kelab malam, menari hingga dini hari di tengah musik menghentak dan cahaya lampu. Distrik Xinyi dan distrik Timur Taipei, serta jalan-jalan bar di setiap kota besar, dipenuhi kerumunan saat akhir pekan tiba.","Worth noting is that Taiwan's nightlife is relatively safe. Even after drinking into the small hours, walking the streets and taking the MRT home usually isn't much of a worry. Late-night convenience stores are always lit up—hungry, you can grab a bowl of instant noodles or oden; needing to sober up, there are roadside stalls selling rice porridge with side dishes or braised snacks (luwei). This environment of 'party to your heart's content and still get home safely' is something many foreigners especially love after arriving in Taiwan.":"Yang patut dicatat, kehidupan malam Taiwan tergolong aman. Bahkan setelah minum hingga dini hari, berjalan di jalanan dan naik MRT pulang biasanya bukan hal yang perlu dikhawatirkan. Toko swalayan larut malam selalu menyala—kalau lapar, kamu bisa menyantap semangkuk mi instan atau oden; kalau perlu menyadarkan diri dari mabuk, ada gerobak pinggir jalan yang menjual bubur nasi berlauk atau camilan rebusan kecap (luwei). Lingkungan 'berpesta sepuasnya dan tetap pulang dengan selamat' inilah yang secara khusus disukai banyak orang asing setelah tiba di Taiwan.","For Taiwanese, these few hours after work aren't just about eating and drinking—they're a ritual for releasing stress and keeping relationships alive. By day you chase targets in the office and get watched by your boss; by night a table of rechao and a few Taiwan Beers wash the exhaustion away. When the alarm rings the next morning, you can head back to work refreshed. This rhythm of tension and release is the best portrait of how Taiwanese 'work hard and live hard' alike.":"Bagi orang Taiwan, beberapa jam setelah kerja ini bukan sekadar soal makan dan minum—melainkan ritual untuk melepas stres dan menjaga hubungan tetap hidup. Di siang hari kamu mengejar target di kantor dan diawasi bos; di malam hari semeja rechao dan beberapa botol Taiwan Beer membasuh kelelahan. Saat alarm berbunyi keesokan paginya, kamu bisa kembali bekerja dengan segar. Ritme tegang dan lepas inilah gambaran terbaik tentang bagaimana orang Taiwan sama-sama 'bekerja keras dan hidup total'.","rechao, Taiwanese stir-fry eatery/pub":"rechao, warung tumis/pub khas Taiwan","Taiwan Beer":"Taiwan Beer (bir Taiwan)","cheers; bottoms up":"bersulang; minum sampai habis","to move to the next venue; barhopping":"pindah ke tempat berikutnya; barhopping","izakaya (Japanese-style pub)":"izakaya (pub bergaya Jepang)","bar":"bar","nightclub":"kelab malam","salt-and-pepper fried chicken (popcorn chicken)":"ayam goreng garam merica (ayam popcorn)","luwei, braised snacks in soy sauce":"luwei, camilan rebusan berbumbu kecap","cocktail; mixed drink":"koktail; minuman campur","to sober up":"menyadarkan diri dari mabuk","to release stress":"melepas stres","At rechao joints, the Taiwanese rallying cry 'ho gan la' inevitably appears once people are tipsy. It originally spread from a beer commercial jingle and is now the standard signal for 'drink it dry!' Taiwan also punishes drunk driving (jiujia) very harshly, so after drinking, the norm is to call a 'designated driver' (daijia) or head home by taxi or MRT. That's exactly why everyone can enjoy barhopping worry-free. For non-drinkers, there's also the kind custom of 'joining with tea' instead of alcohol.":"Di kedai rechao, seruan khas Taiwan 'ho gan la' pasti muncul begitu orang-orang mulai mabuk ringan. Awalnya menyebar dari jingle iklan bir dan kini menjadi aba-aba standar untuk 'minum sampai habis!' Taiwan juga menghukum mengemudi dalam keadaan mabuk (jiujia) dengan sangat berat, jadi setelah minum, kebiasaannya adalah memanggil 'sopir pengganti' (daijia) atau pulang naik taksi atau MRT. Justru karena itulah semua orang bisa menikmati barhopping tanpa khawatir. Bagi yang tidak minum alkohol, ada juga kebiasaan baik 'ikut dengan teh' sebagai ganti minuman keras.","The 'Boss' Spirit: From Grease-Stained Hands to Owner, a Taiwanese Dream":"Semangat 'Bos': Dari Tangan Berlumur Oli hingga Menjadi Pemilik, Sebuah Impian Taiwan","Walk through Taiwan and you'll find small shops and workshops packed along every street—the morning-market lunchbox stand, the back-alley machine shop, the night-market stall—most of them small businesses run by families. In Taiwanese, a boss is called 'touke,' and the wish to 'one day have a shop of my own' runs deep in many Taiwanese hearts. Let's look at the entrepreneurial DNA that supports Taiwan's economy from the ground up.":"Berjalanlah menyusuri Taiwan dan kamu akan menemukan toko kecil dan bengkel berjejal di setiap jalan—lapak nasi kotak di pasar pagi, bengkel mesin di gang belakang, gerai di pasar malam—sebagian besar adalah usaha kecil yang dijalankan keluarga. Dalam bahasa Taiwan, bos disebut 'touke', dan keinginan untuk 'suatu hari punya toko sendiri' tertanam dalam di hati banyak orang Taiwan. Mari kita lihat DNA kewirausahaan yang menopang ekonomi Taiwan dari akar rumput.","On the surface, Taiwan's economy has world-famous giants like TSMC, but what truly holds up employment and daily life is a vast number of 'small and medium-sized enterprises' (SMEs). Taiwan has over 1.5 million SMEs—the overwhelming majority of all firms—providing most people's jobs. From the corner breakfast shop and hardware store to small factories filling international orders, these unremarkable little businesses are the real backbone of Taiwan's economy.":"Di permukaan, ekonomi Taiwan punya raksasa terkenal dunia seperti TSMC, tetapi yang benar-benar menopang lapangan kerja dan kehidupan sehari-hari adalah sejumlah besar 'usaha kecil dan menengah' (UKM). Taiwan memiliki lebih dari 1,5 juta UKM—mayoritas mutlak dari seluruh perusahaan—yang menyediakan pekerjaan bagi sebagian besar orang. Dari kedai sarapan di sudut jalan dan toko perkakas hingga pabrik kecil yang menggarap pesanan internasional, usaha-usaha kecil yang tampak biasa ini adalah tulang punggung sejati ekonomi Taiwan.","Taiwan has a vivid saying: 'grease-stained hands become the boss' (heishou bian touke). 'Heishou'—literally 'black hands'—refers to skilled workers who repair cars or do machine work, their hands coated in grease in the factory; 'touke' is Taiwanese for 'boss.' The saying tells the story of an apprentice who starts at the bottom and, relying on solid skills and years of hard graft, finally opens a shop and becomes the boss. Such legends of turning one's life around by hand abound among Taiwan's older generation.":"Taiwan punya pepatah yang gamblang: 'tangan berlumur oli menjadi bos' (heishou bian touke). 'Heishou'—harfiahnya 'tangan hitam'—merujuk pada pekerja terampil yang memperbaiki mobil atau menggarap mesin, tangannya berlumur oli di pabrik; 'touke' adalah bahasa Taiwan untuk 'bos'. Pepatah ini mengisahkan seorang murid magang yang memulai dari bawah dan, dengan mengandalkan keterampilan yang mumpuni serta bertahun-tahun kerja keras, akhirnya membuka toko dan menjadi bos. Legenda mengubah nasib dengan tangan sendiri seperti ini bertaburan di kalangan generasi tua Taiwan.","For many Taiwanese, 'being the boss' is not just about making money—it's a life goal and a bone-deep value. They'd rather be their own touke and toil a bit harder than spend a lifetime working for someone else; this mindset makes Taiwanese especially willing to take the risk of starting a business. Even just taking over a tiny drink shop or a food truck, or renting a stall at the night market, many people want to taste what it's like to 'run your own business.' This unyielding spirit of wanting to make it big is precisely the 'boss spirit' (touke jingshen).":"Bagi banyak orang Taiwan, 'menjadi bos' bukan sekadar soal menghasilkan uang—melainkan tujuan hidup dan nilai yang mendarah daging. Mereka lebih memilih menjadi touke sendiri dan bekerja sedikit lebih keras daripada seumur hidup bekerja untuk orang lain; pola pikir ini membuat orang Taiwan sangat berani mengambil risiko memulai usaha. Bahkan hanya dengan mengambil alih kedai minuman kecil atau gerobak makanan, atau menyewa lapak di pasar malam, banyak orang ingin merasakan bagaimana rasanya 'menjalankan usaha sendiri'. Semangat pantang menyerah yang ingin sukses besar inilah yang disebut 'semangat bos' (touke jingshen).","The night market is the finest stage for this boss spirit. Those who want to start a business but lack much capital often begin by running a stall. Rent is cheaper than opening a shop; a cart, a sign, and one signature snack are enough to get going. Many now-famous chain brands began from a single small night-market stall. Selling fried chicken cutlets, bubble tea, scallion pancakes—step by step they build up customers and a reputation, and finally expand and open branches. Stories like this play out again and again in Taiwan.":"Pasar malam adalah panggung terbaik bagi semangat bos ini. Mereka yang ingin memulai usaha tetapi tidak punya banyak modal sering memulai dengan berjualan di lapak. Sewanya lebih murah daripada membuka toko; sebuah gerobak, papan nama, dan satu camilan andalan sudah cukup untuk memulai. Banyak merek waralaba yang kini terkenal bermula dari satu lapak kecil di pasar malam. Menjual potongan ayam goreng, bubble tea, panekuk daun bawang—selangkah demi selangkah mereka membangun pelanggan dan reputasi, lalu akhirnya berkembang dan membuka cabang. Kisah seperti ini terjadi berulang kali di Taiwan.","Of course, being the boss is never easy. Open a shop and you'll fret over rent, ingredient costs, staffing, the weather, and whether customers show up—and you have to stand on the front line yourself, out early and back late, no days off all year. Many small-shop owners are 'principal and bell-ringer both,' handling everything from purchasing and cooking to the register and the cleaning. When the economy sours, shops closing one after another is also a common sight on Taiwan's streets. Behind the romance of starting a business lies very real hardship.":"Tentu saja, menjadi bos tidak pernah mudah. Buka toko dan kamu akan pusing memikirkan sewa, biaya bahan, tenaga kerja, cuaca, dan apakah pelanggan datang—dan kamu harus berdiri di garis depan sendiri, berangkat pagi pulang malam, tanpa libur sepanjang tahun. Banyak pemilik toko kecil menjadi 'kepala sekolah sekaligus tukang bel', mengurus segalanya dari belanja dan memasak hingga kasir dan bersih-bersih. Ketika ekonomi memburuk, toko-toko yang tutup satu demi satu juga pemandangan umum di jalanan Taiwan. Di balik romantika memulai usaha tersimpan kesulitan yang sangat nyata.","Hardship notwithstanding, this boss spirit—'better be the head of a chicken than the tail of an ox'—remains deeply etched in Taiwan's character. It fills Taiwan's streets with all kinds of small shops and human warmth, and gives this island an inexhaustible vitality and resilience. Walk through Taiwan and behind every stall and every little shop you see may lie a boss's dream of 'carving out a piece of the sky by one's own effort.' That is Taiwan's most moving—and most genuine—side.":"Sekalipun penuh kesulitan, semangat bos ini—'lebih baik jadi kepala ayam daripada ekor sapi'—tetap terpahat dalam di karakter Taiwan. Ia memenuhi jalanan Taiwan dengan segala macam toko kecil dan kehangatan manusiawi, serta memberi pulau ini vitalitas dan ketangguhan yang tak habis-habisnya. Berjalanlah menyusuri Taiwan, dan di balik setiap lapak dan setiap toko kecil yang kamu lihat mungkin tersimpan impian seorang bos untuk 'merintis sepetak langit dengan usaha sendiri'. Itulah sisi Taiwan yang paling mengharukan—dan paling tulus.","(Taiwanese) boss, business owner":"(bahasa Taiwan) bos, pemilik usaha","small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs)":"usaha kecil dan menengah (UKM)","grease-handed mechanic; blue-collar technician":"montir bertangan oli; teknisi kerah biru","to set up a stall / vend":"membuka lapak / berjualan keliling","stall, vendor booth":"lapak, kios pedagang","to open a shop":"membuka toko","fried chicken cutlet (night-market snack)":"potongan ayam goreng (camilan pasar malam)","to make it; rise to success (from Taiwanese)":"berhasil; meraih sukses (dari bahasa Taiwan)","'Touke' is a Taiwanese (Hokkien) word that shows up often in everyday talk. Haggling at a market or stall, a customer calling out 'Touke, make it a bit cheaper!' is a classic exchange. Many Taiwanese SMEs are family-run; during the boom of the 1960s–80s, people spoke of 'the living room as the factory,' when whole families stayed up through the night making goods for export. This grassroots entrepreneurial power is the force that pushed Taiwan into being a land of 'MIT' (Made in Taiwan).":"'Touke' adalah kata bahasa Taiwan (Hokkien) yang sering muncul dalam percakapan sehari-hari. Saat menawar di pasar atau lapak, pelanggan yang berseru 'Touke, kurangi sedikit dong!' adalah dialog klasik. Banyak UKM Taiwan dikelola keluarga; pada masa keemasan 1960-an–80-an, orang bicara tentang 'ruang tamu sebagai pabrik', ketika seisi keluarga begadang semalaman membuat barang untuk ekspor. Kekuatan kewirausahaan akar rumput inilah yang mendorong Taiwan menjadi negeri 'MIT' (Made in Taiwan).","Language & Expressions":"Bahasa & Ungkapan","Taiwanese Proverbs & Sayings: Old Wisdom Hidden in Daily Life":"Peribahasa & Ungkapan Taiwan: Kearifan Lama yang Tersembunyi dalam Keseharian","Chat with people in Taiwan and words like 'chīa kín lòng phòa uánn,' 'guīmáo,' or 'túchuí' suddenly pop up—not in your dictionary, yet everyone uses them naturally. These are proverbs and slang born from Taiwanese life, and learning them instantly makes your speech sound more 'local.' Let's look at some common ones, with their meanings and when to use them.":"Mengobrol dengan orang Taiwan, kata-kata seperti 'chīa kín lòng phòa uánn', 'guīmáo', atau 'túchuí' tiba-tiba muncul—tak ada di kamusmu, namun semua orang memakainya dengan wajar. Ini adalah peribahasa dan bahasa gaul yang lahir dari kehidupan Taiwan, dan mempelajarinya seketika membuat tutur katamu terdengar lebih 'lokal'. Mari kita lihat beberapa yang umum, beserta arti dan kapan menggunakannya.","Let's start with one everyone hears: '呷緊弄破碗' (chīa kín lòng phòa uánn). Originally Taiwanese, it literally means 'eat too fast and you break the bowl,' warning that 'the more you rush, the easier it is to slip up.' Say you're rushing to hand in a report and end up saving the wrong file or losing your data—a coworker will grin and say, 'See? Rush your food and you break the bowl!' It's much like 'haste makes waste,' but coming from a Taiwanese it feels more everyday and vivid.":"Mari mulai dengan yang sering didengar semua orang: '呷緊弄破碗' (chīa kín lòng phòa uánn). Aslinya bahasa Taiwan, harfiahnya berarti 'makan terlalu cepat maka mangkuknya pecah', memperingatkan bahwa 'makin terburu-buru, makin mudah berbuat salah'. Misalnya kamu tergesa-gesa menyerahkan laporan lalu malah menyimpan file yang salah atau kehilangan data—seorang rekan kerja akan nyengir dan berkata, 'Tuh kan? Makan buru-buru, mangkuknya pecah!' Mirip sekali dengan 'terburu nafsu malah gagal', tetapi keluar dari mulut orang Taiwan terasa lebih membumi dan hidup.","Next, '一兼二顧' (yī jiān èr gù). It means 'doing one thing while also taking care of another'—in other words, 'killing two birds with one stone.' Taiwanese love it for describing a smart, economical arrangement. For example: 'I caught a concert while I was in Japan for a business trip—truly two birds with one stone.' Or a mom exercising while binge-watching a drama might say smugly, 'See, two things at once, how great.' It carries a thrifty, time-savvy philosophy of life.":"Berikutnya, '一兼二顧' (yī jiān èr gù). Artinya 'mengerjakan satu hal sekaligus mengurus hal lain'—dengan kata lain, 'sekali dayung dua tiga pulau terlampaui'. Orang Taiwan gemar memakainya untuk menggambarkan pengaturan yang cerdas dan hemat. Misalnya: 'Saya sekalian nonton konser waktu dinas ke Jepang—benar-benar sekali dayung dua pulau'. Atau seorang ibu yang berolahraga sambil maraton drama mungkin berkata bangga, 'Tuh, dua hal sekaligus, hebat kan.' Ia mengandung filosofi hidup yang hemat dan pandai memanfaatkan waktu.","Now two super-handy adjectives: '龜毛' (guīmáo) and '鴨霸' (yābà). '龜毛' describes someone extremely picky, demanding, and fussy over tiny details—someone who asks thirty questions when ordering, or repacks their luggage several times, gets told, 'You're being way too guīmáo.' '鴨霸' describes someone domineering, bullying, and unreasonable, who wants every advantage for themselves. Of a person who cuts in line and acts righteous about it, Taiwanese will frown and say, 'This person is so yābà.'":"Sekarang dua kata sifat yang sangat praktis: '龜毛' (guīmáo) dan '鴨霸' (yābà). '龜毛' menggambarkan orang yang amat rewel, banyak menuntut, dan cerewet soal detail kecil—orang yang bertanya tiga puluh kali saat memesan, atau mengemasi kopernya berulang kali, akan disebut, 'Kamu terlalu guīmáo.' '鴨霸' menggambarkan orang yang suka menindas, memaksakan kehendak, dan tak masuk akal, yang ingin semua keuntungan untuk dirinya. Terhadap orang yang menyerobot antrean tapi merasa benar, orang Taiwan akan mengernyit dan berkata, 'Orang ini yābà sekali.'","Another word Taiwanese use daily: '凸槌' (túchuí). It means 'to slip up, make a mistake, mess up.' Originally a billiards (pool) term for a miscued shot where the cue slips, it became everyday speech. A host misspeaking is 'túchuí'; a machine suddenly breaking down can also be 'túchuí.' For example: 'Today my computer túchuí-ed halfway through my presentation, the screen totally froze—so awkward.' Vivid and easy to remember, it's a Taiwanese favorite for poking fun at slip-ups.":"Kata lain yang dipakai orang Taiwan sehari-hari: '凸槌' (túchuí). Artinya 'terpeleset, membuat kesalahan, mengacau'. Awalnya istilah biliar untuk pukulan meleset ketika stik tergelincir, lalu menjadi bahasa sehari-hari. Pembawa acara yang salah bicara adalah 'túchuí'; mesin yang tiba-tiba rusak juga bisa 'túchuí'. Misalnya: 'Hari ini komputer saya túchuí di tengah presentasi, layarnya benar-benar macet—malu sekali.' Gamblang dan mudah diingat, kata ini favorit orang Taiwan untuk menertawakan kekeliruan.","Finally, a word brimming with Taiwanese warmth: '揪團' (jiūtuán). '揪' means 'to invite, to rally,' so '揪團' is 'to round everyone up to join in or buy together.' A coworker wanting to order bubble tea together will call out in the group chat: 'Anyone want a drink? I'll organize a group order!' It works for carpooling on trips, group-buying fruit, gathering people for ball games—everything. Taiwanese love to jiūtuán because a crowd is lively and often gets a discount too. This eagerness to 'gather the gang' is one of the loveliest sides of Taiwanese society.":"Terakhir, kata yang sarat kehangatan Taiwan: '揪團' (jiūtuán). '揪' berarti 'mengajak, mengumpulkan', jadi '揪團' adalah 'mengumpulkan semua orang untuk ikut atau membeli bersama'. Rekan kerja yang ingin memesan bubble tea bersama akan berseru di grup chat: 'Ada yang mau minum? Aku buka pesanan bareng, ya!' Ini berlaku untuk nebeng mobil saat jalan-jalan, patungan beli buah, mengumpulkan orang untuk main bola—segalanya. Orang Taiwan suka jiūtuán karena ramai-ramai itu seru, dan sering dapat diskon juga. Antusiasme 'mengumpulkan kawan-kawan' ini adalah salah satu sisi termanis masyarakat Taiwan.","haste makes waste (Taiwanese proverb)":"terburu nafsu malah gagal (peribahasa Taiwan)","kill two birds with one stone":"sekali dayung dua tiga pulau terlampaui","nitpicky, fussy, overly particular":"rewel, cerewet, terlalu banyak menuntut","domineering, bullying, unreasonable":"suka menindas, memaksakan kehendak, tak masuk akal","to slip up, mess up":"terpeleset, mengacau","to organize a group (order/activity)":"mengoordinasi grup (pesanan/kegiatan bersama)","more haste, less speed (formal proverb)":"makin tergesa makin lambat (peribahasa formal)","to calculate carefully, be thrifty":"berhitung cermat, hemat","picky, fault-finding":"pemilih, suka mencari-cari kesalahan","to cut in line":"menyerobot antrean","to poke fun at, call out":"menertawakan, menyindir","to gather friends and companions":"mengumpulkan teman dan kawan","A hallmark of Taiwanese proverbs and slang is how many come from the Taiwanese (Hokkien) language. '呷緊弄破碗' and '鴨霸,' for instance, are Taiwanese pronunciations written in Chinese characters, and read differently from standard Mandarin. That's exactly why using them naturally gives a strong 'I actually live in Taiwan' vibe. But note that '龜毛' and '鴨霸' judge someone's character, so saying them to a person's face can sting—it's safest to use them jokingly among close friends.":"Ciri khas peribahasa dan bahasa gaul Taiwan adalah banyak yang berasal dari bahasa Taiwan (Hokkien). '呷緊弄破碗' dan '鴨霸', misalnya, adalah pelafalan bahasa Taiwan yang ditulis dengan aksara Tionghoa, dan dibaca berbeda dari Mandarin baku. Justru itulah memakainya dengan wajar memberi kesan kuat 'saya benar-benar tinggal di Taiwan'. Tetapi perhatikan bahwa '龜毛' dan '鴨霸' menilai karakter seseorang, jadi mengatakannya langsung di depan orang bisa menyakiti—paling aman memakainya untuk bercanda di antara teman dekat.","Taiwanese Mini-Class: The Local Flavor Sprinkled into Mandarin":"Kelas Kecil Bahasa Taiwan: Cita Rasa Lokal yang Ditaburkan ke dalam Mandarin","Even when speaking Mandarin (Guóyǔ), people in Taiwan sprinkle in words from Taiwanese (Hokkien): 'pháinn-sè,' 'a-sá-lih,' 'hó-ka-tsài'... Just one of these tucked into a sentence makes the conversation instantly more Taiwanese and warm. Let's learn some staple Taiwanese phrases used by young and old alike—their meanings, usage, and romanization (Tâi-lô).":"Bahkan saat berbicara Mandarin (Guóyǔ), orang Taiwan menyelipkan kata-kata dari bahasa Taiwan (Hokkien): 'pháinn-sè', 'a-sá-lih', 'hó-ka-tsài'... Cukup satu saja diselipkan ke dalam kalimat, percakapan seketika terasa lebih Taiwan dan hangat. Mari pelajari beberapa ungkapan bahasa Taiwan yang jamak dipakai tua maupun muda—arti, penggunaan, dan romanisasinya (Tâi-lô).","The most classic Taiwanese greeting has to be '呷飽沒？' (Tâi-lô: Tsia̍h pá--buē), literally 'Have you eaten yet?' But it isn't really asking whether you've had a meal—like English 'How are you?', it's a way of greeting and showing care. When an elder sees you, their first line is often 'Have you eaten?' You needn't earnestly report the menu; smiling and replying 'Yes, and you?' is the most fitting response. This phrase distills the Taiwanese culture of 'food as heaven, caring for people through food.'":"Sapaan bahasa Taiwan yang paling klasik tentu '呷飽沒？' (Tâi-lô: Tsia̍h pá--buē), harfiahnya 'Sudah makan?'. Tapi ini bukan benar-benar menanyakan apakah kamu sudah makan—seperti 'How are you?' dalam bahasa Inggris, ini cara menyapa dan menunjukkan perhatian. Ketika orang tua bertemu denganmu, kalimat pertamanya sering 'Sudah makan?'. Kamu tak perlu sungguh-sungguh melaporkan menunya; tersenyum dan menjawab 'Sudah, Anda sendiri?' adalah respons paling pas. Ungkapan ini menyari budaya Taiwan 'makanan adalah segalanya, peduli pada orang lewat makanan'.","Next is '母湯' (mǔtāng), on young people's lips daily. It's actually a homophone play on the Taiwanese '毋通' (Tâi-lô: M̄-thang), meaning 'must not, don't, don't do that.' Because '毋通' sounds like '母湯' ('mother's soup'), the internet started writing it with those two characters—funny and cute. When a friend is about to do something dangerous or silly, you can say, 'Mǔtāng! That's dangerous.' It adds a dose of humor and warmth over a stern 'you can't.'":"Berikutnya '母湯' (mǔtāng), yang tiap hari ada di mulut anak muda. Sebenarnya ini permainan homofon dari kata bahasa Taiwan '毋通' (Tâi-lô: M̄-thang), yang berarti 'tidak boleh, jangan, jangan lakukan itu'. Karena '毋通' terdengar seperti '母湯' ('sup ibu'), warganet mulai menuliskannya dengan dua aksara itu—lucu dan menggemaskan. Ketika teman hendak melakukan sesuatu yang berbahaya atau konyol, kamu bisa berkata, 'Mǔtāng! Itu berbahaya.' Ini menambahkan humor dan kehangatan ketimbang 'tidak boleh' yang kaku.","In election season you'll definitely hear '凍蒜' (dòngsuàn). It's a homophone of the Taiwanese '當選' (Tâi-lô: Tòng-suán, 'get elected'), and written in Chinese it happens to be '凍蒜' ('frozen garlic')—a funny image. At rallies, supporters chant in unison 'Dòngsuàn! Dòngsuàn!' to cheer a candidate on and wish them a smooth win. The word now goes beyond elections: when a friend faces an exam, a match, or an interview, you can shout 'Dòngsuàn!' for them—meaning 'wishing you success, may you triumph.'":"Di musim pemilu kamu pasti mendengar '凍蒜' (dòngsuàn). Ini homofon dari kata bahasa Taiwan '當選' (Tâi-lô: Tòng-suán, 'terpilih'), dan ditulis dalam aksara Tionghoa kebetulan menjadi '凍蒜' ('bawang putih beku')—citra yang lucu. Di kampanye, para pendukung serentak meneriakkan 'Dòngsuàn! Dòngsuàn!' untuk menyemangati kandidat dan mendoakan kemenangan yang mulus. Kini kata ini melampaui pemilu: ketika teman menghadapi ujian, pertandingan, atau wawancara, kamu bisa berteriak 'Dòngsuàn!' untuknya—artinya 'semoga sukses, semoga menang'.","To describe personality, Taiwanese love 'a-sá-lih' (Tâi-lô; actually from Japanese 'assari'). It describes someone decisive, generous, and no-nonsense—if they say yes they mean yes, if they treat you they really treat you, not stingy at all. For example: 'The boss is so a-sá-lih—without a word he added extra dishes for us.' By contrast, '歹勢' (Tâi-lô: Pháinn-sè) means 'sorry, excuse me, embarrassed,' usable when you trouble someone or want to gently decline: 'Sorry, I'll pass this time.' Together, these two words vividly capture the Taiwanese character—loyal in feeling yet courteous.":"Untuk menggambarkan kepribadian, orang Taiwan gemar 'a-sá-lih' (Tâi-lô; sebenarnya dari bahasa Jepang 'assari'). Ini menggambarkan orang yang tegas, murah hati, dan tanpa basa-basi—kalau iya berarti iya, kalau mentraktir ya benar-benar mentraktir, sama sekali tidak pelit. Misalnya: 'Bosnya a-sá-lih sekali—tanpa banyak bicara langsung menambah hidangan untuk kami.' Sebaliknya, '歹勢' (Tâi-lô: Pháinn-sè) berarti 'maaf, permisi, sungkan', bisa dipakai saat kamu merepotkan seseorang atau ingin menolak dengan halus: 'Maaf, kali ini saya lewatkan dulu.' Bersama-sama, kedua kata ini dengan gamblang menangkap karakter orang Taiwan—setia dalam perasaan namun santun.","Two more super-practical Taiwanese words: '甲意' (Kah-ì) and '好家在' (Hó-ka-tsài). '甲意' means 'to like, to fancy.' Seeing something they like, Taiwanese say, 'I really Kah-ì this one!'—sounding more local and heartfelt than plain 'like.' '好家在' means 'thankfully, luckily, good thing,' expressing the relief of a sigh let out. For example: 'Hó-ka-tsài I brought an umbrella, or I'd have been soaked like a drowned rat.' It's a Taiwanese person's most natural reaction to a close call.":"Dua kata bahasa Taiwan lagi yang sangat praktis: '甲意' (Kah-ì) dan '好家在' (Hó-ka-tsài). '甲意' berarti 'suka, naksir'. Melihat sesuatu yang disukai, orang Taiwan berkata, 'Aku Kah-ì banget yang ini!'—terdengar lebih lokal dan tulus daripada sekadar 'suka'. '好家在' berarti 'untunglah, syukurlah, mujur', mengungkapkan lega seperti tarikan napas panjang. Misalnya: 'Hó-ka-tsài aku bawa payung, kalau tidak sudah basah kuyup seperti tikus kecebur.' Inilah reaksi paling alami orang Taiwan saat lolos dari situasi nyaris celaka.","A reminder: most of these Taiwanese words are for relaxed, casual speech and aren't quite right for formal documents or reports. But in everyday chat, texting friends, and watching variety shows, they're everywhere. You don't need to master all of Taiwanese—just understanding these few high-frequency words and using one or two now and then will make Taiwanese friends light up and think, 'You really get Taiwan.' The most charming part of a language often hides in words the textbooks never teach yet people use every single day.":"Sebuah pengingat: sebagian besar kata bahasa Taiwan ini untuk tutur santai dan akrab, dan kurang pas untuk dokumen atau laporan resmi. Tetapi dalam obrolan sehari-hari, berkirim pesan dengan teman, dan menonton acara ragam, semuanya ada di mana-mana. Kamu tak perlu menguasai seluruh bahasa Taiwan—cukup memahami beberapa kata yang sering muncul ini dan sesekali memakai satu-dua, teman-teman Taiwan akan berbinar dan berpikir, 'Kamu benar-benar paham Taiwan.' Bagian paling memikat dari sebuah bahasa sering bersembunyi di kata-kata yang tak pernah diajarkan buku pelajaran namun dipakai orang setiap hari.","Have you eaten? (a greeting)":"Sudah makan? (sebuah sapaan)","don't / you shouldn't (from 毋通)":"jangan / sebaiknya jangan (dari 毋通)","get elected! (a cheer of support)":"semoga terpilih! (sorak dukungan)","decisive and generous (from Japanese 'assari')":"tegas dan murah hati (dari bahasa Jepang 'assari')","sorry / excuse me / embarrassed":"maaf / permisi / sungkan","to like, to fancy":"suka, naksir","thankfully, luckily":"untunglah, syukurlah","Taiwanese (Hokkien) language":"bahasa Taiwan (Hokkien)","homophone / sound-alike":"homofon / kata yang bunyinya mirip","soaked to the skin (drowned rat)":"basah kuyup (seperti tikus kecebur)","without a word, right away":"tanpa banyak bicara, langsung saja","variety show":"acara ragam (variety show)","Taiwanese (Tâi-gí, formally Taiwanese Hokkien) is a language distinct from standard Mandarin, with quite different pronunciation and grammar. There was an era when its use in schools was restricted, but today, with rising interest in local culture and identity, it's been revalued and is widely used on TV, in music, and in dramas. The romanization shown here is 'Tâi-lô,' the official system. Many words like 'a-sá-lih' entered Taiwanese from Japanese during the colonial era—trace the words and you glimpse Taiwan's own history.":"Bahasa Taiwan (Tâi-gí, secara resmi Hokkien Taiwan) adalah bahasa yang berbeda dari Mandarin baku, dengan pelafalan dan tata bahasa yang cukup berbeda. Pernah ada masa ketika penggunaannya di sekolah dibatasi, tetapi kini, seiring meningkatnya minat pada budaya dan identitas lokal, ia dinilai ulang dan banyak dipakai di TV, musik, dan drama. Romanisasi yang ditampilkan di sini adalah 'Tâi-lô', sistem resminya. Banyak kata seperti 'a-sá-lih' masuk ke bahasa Taiwan dari bahasa Jepang pada masa kolonial—telusuri kata-katanya dan kamu akan menyaksikan sekilas sejarah Taiwan sendiri.","Internet Slang & Youth Speak: Keeping Up with Taiwan's Rhythm":"Bahasa Gaul Internet & Bahasa Anak Muda: Mengikuti Irama Taiwan","Chat with young Taiwanese or scroll through social media and you'll meet words that never appear in any textbook: 'yǐdú bù huí,' 'shì zài hāluō,' 'sēn 77'... This youth speak—mixing numbers, net slang, and memes—is a mirror of the mood and humor of the moment. Let's decode the staple phrases flying around today's Taiwan, along with their meaning and vibe.":"Mengobrol dengan anak muda Taiwan atau menggulir media sosial, kamu akan menemui kata-kata yang tak pernah muncul di buku pelajaran mana pun: 'yǐdú bù huí', 'shì zài hāluō', 'sēn 77'... Bahasa anak muda ini—yang mencampur angka, bahasa gaul internet, dan meme—adalah cermin suasana hati dan humor masa kini. Mari kita pecahkan frasa-frasa andalan yang beredar di Taiwan sekarang, berikut arti dan nuansanya.","Let's start with the most heart-wrenching: '已讀不回' (yǐdú bù huí). Today's messaging apps show when a message is 'read,' so when you see the other person has clearly read yours yet keeps not replying, that anxiety and small hurt is called '已讀不回' (read-and-no-reply). It's become a keyword for describing romance, friendship, and work interactions. For example: 'I texted him yesterday and got read-and-no-replied—does he not like me?' Just four characters capture modern social anxiety perfectly.":"Mari mulai dengan yang paling menyayat hati: '已讀不回' (yǐdú bù huí). Aplikasi pesan sekarang menunjukkan kapan sebuah pesan 'dibaca', jadi ketika kamu melihat lawan bicara jelas-jelas sudah membaca pesanmu tetapi terus tidak membalas, kecemasan dan luka kecil itu disebut '已讀不回' (dibaca tapi tak dibalas). Ini menjadi kata kunci untuk menggambarkan interaksi asmara, persahabatan, dan pekerjaan. Misalnya: 'Kemarin aku kirim pesan ke dia dan cuma di-read tanpa dibalas—apa dia tidak suka aku?' Hanya empat aksara, tapi persis menangkap kecemasan sosial modern.","Next, the dramatic '是在哈囉' (shì zài hāluō). When someone says or does something baffling, jaw-dropping, and illogical, you can throw up your hands and say, 'Shì zài hāluō?'—close to 'What on earth are you doing?' or 'What the heck?' It comes from a comic homophone of a song lyric, loaded with speechless, snarky vibes. A great match for it is '傻眼' (shǎyǎn), describing being stunned, speechless, unsure how to react—for example: 'He actually showed up two hours late, I was totally stunned.'":"Berikutnya, si dramatis '是在哈囉' (shì zài hāluō). Ketika seseorang mengatakan atau melakukan sesuatu yang membingungkan, bikin melongo, dan tak logis, kamu bisa mengangkat tangan dan berkata, 'Shì zài hāluō?'—mirip 'Kamu ini sebenarnya sedang apa?' atau 'Apa-apaan ini?' Ia berasal dari homofon lucu sebuah lirik lagu, sarat nuansa tak habis pikir dan sinis. Padanan yang pas untuknya adalah '傻眼' (shǎyǎn), yang menggambarkan tercengang, tak bisa berkata-kata, bingung harus bereaksi bagaimana—misalnya: 'Dia benar-benar datang telat dua jam, aku sampai melongo.'","Also emotion-related is '森77' (sēn 77). It's a homophone game on '生氣氣' ('angry'): '森' sounds like '生,' and '77' reads like 'qìqì,' so together it's a cute way to say 'really mad, all in a huff.' Using numbers and homophones to make 'anger' sound soft and a little coquettish is a very typical move in Taiwanese net language. For example: 'You keep ignoring me, now I'm sēn 77!' They're complaining, yet because they used 'sēn 77' it comes off a bit funny and cute, and half the anger melts away.":"Yang juga berkaitan dengan emosi adalah '森77' (sēn 77). Ini permainan homofon dari '生氣氣' ('marah'): '森' terdengar seperti '生', dan '77' dibaca seperti 'qìqì', sehingga digabung menjadi cara imut mengatakan 'benar-benar kesal, ngambek'. Memakai angka dan homofon untuk membuat 'kemarahan' terdengar lembut dan sedikit manja adalah gaya yang sangat khas dalam bahasa internet Taiwan. Misalnya: 'Kamu terus mengabaikanku, sekarang aku sēn 77!' Mereka mengeluh, tapi karena memakai 'sēn 77' jadi terkesan agak lucu dan menggemaskan, dan separuh amarahnya pun mencair.","For the sharpest read on people, it has to be '塑膠' (sùjiāo) and '綠茶' (lǜchá). 'Treating someone as 塑膠' means 'acting as if they don't exist, deliberately ignoring them'—since plastic is lifeless and dispensable. For example: 'I said hi and he ignored me—am I plastic to him?' '綠茶,' meanwhile, describes someone who seems pure and harmless on the surface but is scheming underneath, skilled at playing weak to win favor—clearly derogatory, so use it carefully, since it judges another person's character.":"Untuk membaca watak orang paling tajam, tentu '塑膠' (sùjiāo) dan '綠茶' (lǜchá). 'Memperlakukan seseorang sebagai 塑膠' berarti 'berlagak seolah mereka tak ada, sengaja mengabaikan mereka'—karena plastik itu tak bernyawa dan bisa dibuang. Misalnya: 'Aku menyapa tapi dia mengabaikanku—apa aku ini plastik baginya?' Sementara '綠茶' menggambarkan orang yang tampak polos dan tak berbahaya di permukaan tetapi penuh muslihat di baliknya, pandai berpura-pura lemah untuk merebut simpati—jelas berkonotasi negatif, jadi pakailah dengan hati-hati karena ia menilai karakter orang lain.","Number homophones are also a Taiwanese youth favorite, the classic being '484.' It reads like '是不是' ('isn't it / is it'), often used in questions. For example, '你484餓了？' means 'Aren't you hungry?' and '他484喜歡你？' means 'Doesn't he like you?' Typing numbers is fast and cheeky, a regular in online chat. This game of swapping similar-sounding numbers for words makes text look breezy and meme-y, and tests how attuned you are to the rhythm of how Taiwanese speak.":"Homofon angka juga favorit anak muda Taiwan, yang paling klasik adalah '484'. Bacanya seperti '是不是' ('bukan / iya kan'), sering dipakai dalam pertanyaan. Misalnya, '你484餓了？' berarti 'Kamu lapar kan?' dan '他484喜歡你？' berarti 'Dia suka kamu kan?' Mengetik angka itu cepat dan jenaka, langganan dalam obrolan daring. Permainan mengganti kata dengan angka yang bunyinya mirip ini membuat teks terlihat santai dan bernuansa meme, sekaligus menguji seberapa peka kamu pada irama cara orang Taiwan berbicara.","Finally, we can't skip '迷因' (míyīn), the phonetic rendering of English 'meme'—the funny images, videos, and jokes that go viral online. A photo with a hilarious caption, a wildly remixed short clip—any of it can be a meme. Taiwan's meme culture is highly developed, often blending current events, Taiwanese, and homophones, with humor that's fast and local. Getting the memes is almost like receiving the younger generation's passport. These slang words change fast—new ones pop up, old ones fade—but it's exactly this rapid renewal that keeps language forever fresh and fun.":"Terakhir, kita tak boleh melewatkan '迷因' (míyīn), transliterasi bunyi dari kata Inggris 'meme'—gambar, video, dan lelucon lucu yang viral di internet. Sebuah foto dengan takarir kocak, klip pendek yang di-remix habis-habisan—semuanya bisa jadi meme. Budaya meme Taiwan sangat berkembang, sering memadukan peristiwa terkini, bahasa Taiwan, dan homofon, dengan humor yang cepat dan lokal. Memahami meme hampir seperti menerima paspor generasi muda. Kata-kata gaul ini berubah cepat—yang baru bermunculan, yang lama memudar—tetapi justru pembaruan yang kilat inilah yang membuat bahasa selamanya segar dan menyenangkan.","read but no reply (left on read)":"dibaca tapi tak dibalas (di-read doang)","what the heck? / what are you on about?":"apa-apaan ini? / kamu ngomong apa sih?","stunned, speechless, dumbfounded":"tercengang, tak bisa berkata-kata, terbengong","all in a huff (cute 'so mad')":"ngambek (versi imut 'kesal banget')","to ignore someone (treat as invisible)":"mengabaikan seseorang (menganggapnya tak terlihat)","a scheming person feigning innocence (derogatory)":"orang licik yang berpura-pura polos (bermakna negatif)","isn't it? (number pun on 是不是)":"iya kan? (pelesetan angka dari 是不是)","meme (phonetic loan)":"meme (pinjaman bunyi)","a gag, joke, punchline":"sebuah lelucon, gurauan, punchline","scheming, ulterior motives":"penuh muslihat, punya niat tersembunyi","pass, passport (access)":"kartu akses, paspor (jalan masuk)","to go out of fashion":"ketinggalan zaman","Taiwanese internet slang largely forms in three patterns: (1) number puns like '484 = 是不是'; (2) homophone swaps like '森77 = 生氣氣' and '母湯 = 毋通'; and (3) phonetic loans like '迷因 = meme.' These emerge from PTT (Taiwan's huge bulletin board), Dcard, and various social media, spreading in a flash. Since slang changes fast, there's no need to memorize it all. Ask a Taiwanese friend 'What does this mean?' and they'll usually be delighted to explain—which itself makes a great conversation starter.":"Bahasa gaul internet Taiwan sebagian besar terbentuk dalam tiga pola: (1) pelesetan angka seperti '484 = 是不是'; (2) penggantian homofon seperti '森77 = 生氣氣' dan '母湯 = 毋通'; dan (3) pinjaman bunyi seperti '迷因 = meme'. Semua ini muncul dari PTT (papan buletin raksasa Taiwan), Dcard, dan berbagai media sosial, lalu menyebar dalam sekejap. Karena bahasa gaul berubah cepat, tak perlu menghafal semuanya. Tanyakan pada teman Taiwan 'Ini artinya apa?' dan biasanya mereka dengan senang hati menjelaskan—yang justru menjadi pembuka obrolan yang bagus.","Practical Living":"Kehidupan Praktis","Seeing a Doctor in Taiwan: A Practical Guide to Clinics, Hospitals, and Your NHI Card":"Berobat di Taiwan: Panduan Praktis Klinik, Rumah Sakit, dan Kartu NHI Anda","A sore throat, a fever, a wrenched back—live in Taiwan long enough and a day will come when you need to see a doctor. But many people worry: 'Where do I go? What do I bring? How much will it cost?' This article walks you through the whole process of seeing a doctor in Taiwan, step by step, so that even a first-timer won't get lost.":"Sakit tenggorokan, demam, salah urat di punggung—tinggal cukup lama di Taiwan dan akan tiba hari saat kamu perlu ke dokter. Tetapi banyak orang cemas: 'Ke mana saya harus pergi? Apa yang harus dibawa? Berapa biayanya?' Artikel ini memandu kamu melewati seluruh proses berobat di Taiwan, langkah demi langkah, agar bahkan pemula pun tak akan tersesat.","The first concept to grasp when seeing a doctor in Taiwan is the difference between a 'clinic' (zhěnsuǒ) and a 'hospital' (yīyuàn). For minor illnesses—colds, diarrhea, an itchy rash and other everyday complaints—you usually just go straight to a clinic near your home; there's no need to trek all the way to a big hospital. Clinics are small, see you quickly, usually take no appointment, and you can walk in, register, wait a bit, and see the doctor. Only when you genuinely need to be hospitalized, have surgery, or have a complex condition requiring detailed tests do you go to a 'hospital,' especially a fully-equipped 'medical center.'":"Konsep pertama yang harus dipahami saat berobat di Taiwan adalah perbedaan antara 'klinik' (zhěnsuǒ) dan 'rumah sakit' (yīyuàn). Untuk penyakit ringan—pilek, diare, ruam gatal, dan keluhan sehari-hari lainnya—biasanya kamu cukup langsung ke klinik dekat rumah; tak perlu jauh-jauh ke rumah sakit besar. Klinik itu kecil, cepat memeriksamu, biasanya tanpa perlu janji temu, dan kamu bisa masuk, mendaftar, menunggu sebentar, lalu bertemu dokter. Hanya ketika kamu benar-benar perlu dirawat inap, menjalani operasi, atau memiliki kondisi rumit yang membutuhkan pemeriksaan mendalam, barulah kamu pergi ke 'rumah sakit', terutama 'pusat medis' yang berperalatan lengkap.","Always remember to bring your 'NHI card' (jiànbǎokǎ). This card is the single most important thing for seeing a doctor in Taiwan; with it, your registration and medicine fees are calculated at insured rates, so one outpatient visit usually costs you only about NT$100 to NT$400 out of pocket. When you arrive at the clinic, the first step is to 'register' (guàhào) at the front desk and hand over your NHI card; the nurse will log you in and give you a number. If it's your first time at that clinic, you may also fill out a basic information form. Once registered, you sit in the waiting area, and a wall sign or screen shows which number is currently being seen.":"Selalu ingat membawa 'kartu NHI' (jiànbǎokǎ). Kartu ini adalah hal yang paling penting untuk berobat di Taiwan; dengannya, biaya pendaftaran dan obatmu dihitung dengan tarif tertanggung, sehingga satu kunjungan rawat jalan biasanya hanya menghabiskan sekitar NT$100 hingga NT$400 dari kantongmu. Setibanya di klinik, langkah pertama adalah 'mendaftar' (guàhào) di meja depan dan menyerahkan kartu NHI; perawat akan mendatamu dan memberimu nomor. Jika ini kunjungan pertamamu di klinik itu, kamu mungkin juga mengisi formulir data dasar. Setelah terdaftar, kamu duduk di ruang tunggu, dan papan atau layar di dinding menunjukkan nomor mana yang sedang diperiksa.","What stumps many people at first is 'which department should I actually see?' Most clinics in Taiwan are divided by specialty, clearly marked on the signboard: for a cold, fever, or cough, look for 'family medicine' (jiāyīkē) or 'ENT' (ěrbíhóukē); for stomachache or diarrhea, 'gastroenterology' (chángwèikē); for skin problems, 'dermatology'; for eye trouble, 'ophthalmology'; and for a toothache, of course, 'dentistry.' If you're truly unsure, the safest bet is to register with 'family medicine' first—family doctors handle a bit of everything, and if needed the doctor will 'refer' (zhuǎnzhěn) you to a more specialized department.":"Yang membuat banyak orang bingung pada awalnya adalah 'sebenarnya saya harus ke poli mana?' Sebagian besar klinik di Taiwan dibagi menurut spesialisasi, tertera jelas di papan nama: untuk pilek, demam, atau batuk, cari 'kedokteran keluarga' (jiāyīkē) atau 'THT' (ěrbíhóukē); untuk sakit perut atau diare, 'gastroenterologi' (chángwèikē); untuk masalah kulit, 'dermatologi'; untuk gangguan mata, 'oftalmologi'; dan untuk sakit gigi, tentu saja, 'kedokteran gigi'. Kalau kamu benar-benar ragu, pilihan teraman adalah mendaftar ke 'kedokteran keluarga' dulu—dokter keluarga menangani sedikit dari segalanya, dan bila perlu dokter akan 'merujuk' (zhuǎnzhěn) kamu ke poli yang lebih spesialis.","After seeing the doctor, the next step is 'picking up medicine' (lǐngyào). At small clinics, care and pharmacy are often combined (yīyào héyī): after the consultation you collect your medicine and pay at the same desk—very convenient. At large hospitals or some clinics, the doctor writes a 'prescription' (chǔfāngjiān), which you take to a 'pharmacy' (yàojú) to fill. Insured medicine in Taiwan is cheap, and the pharmacist will explain how to take each drug, how many times a day, and whether before or after meals. Be sure to listen carefully, or read the printed instructions on the medicine bag—they're usually quite detailed. If you're allergic to any medication, always tell the doctor and pharmacist first.":"Setelah bertemu dokter, langkah berikutnya adalah 'mengambil obat' (lǐngyào). Di klinik kecil, layanan medis dan apotek sering digabung (yīyào héyī): usai konsultasi kamu mengambil obat dan membayar di meja yang sama—sangat praktis. Di rumah sakit besar atau sebagian klinik, dokter menuliskan 'resep' (chǔfāngjiān), yang kamu bawa ke 'apotek' (yàojú) untuk ditebus. Obat tertanggung di Taiwan murah, dan apoteker akan menjelaskan cara meminum tiap obat, berapa kali sehari, serta sebelum atau sesudah makan. Pastikan menyimak dengan saksama, atau baca petunjuk yang tercetak di kantong obat—biasanya cukup rinci. Jika kamu alergi terhadap obat tertentu, selalu beri tahu dokter dan apoteker lebih dulu.","If in the middle of the night you suddenly run a high fever, bleed from an injury, or develop a very serious condition, go to the hospital 'emergency room' (jízhěn). The ER has doctors around the clock, but it's for 'urgent, dangerous' patients: cases are triaged by severity and the most critical are seen first, so going to the ER for a mild cold may mean a long wait and a higher cost than a regular outpatient visit. Also, for long-term 'chronic illness' medications—such as high blood pressure or diabetes—the doctor can issue a 'chronic-illness repeat prescription,' letting you collect three months' worth at once so you don't have to come in every month.":"Jika di tengah malam kamu tiba-tiba demam tinggi, mengalami luka berdarah, atau menderita kondisi yang sangat serius, pergilah ke 'unit gawat darurat' (jízhěn) rumah sakit. UGD punya dokter sepanjang waktu, tetapi diperuntukkan bagi pasien yang 'mendesak dan berbahaya': kasus ditriase menurut tingkat keparahan dan yang paling kritis diperiksa lebih dulu, jadi datang ke UGD hanya untuk pilek ringan bisa berarti menunggu lama dan biaya yang lebih tinggi daripada rawat jalan biasa. Selain itu, untuk obat 'penyakit kronis' jangka panjang—seperti darah tinggi atau diabetes—dokter dapat menerbitkan 'resep ulang penyakit kronis', yang memungkinkanmu mengambil persediaan tiga bulan sekaligus sehingga kamu tak perlu datang setiap bulan.","In short, seeing a doctor in Taiwan is actually simpler than many imagine: bring your NHI card, first judge whether it's a minor or major illness, pick the right department, register, get examined, pick up your medicine—the whole process often wraps up in half an hour to an hour. Foreigners new to Taiwan can start by memorizing where the nearby clinics and pharmacies are, and ask a colleague or neighbor, 'Which clinic around here is good?' Once you're familiar with it, you'll find that this cheap and convenient medical system is one of the most reassuring things about living in Taiwan.":"Singkatnya, berobat di Taiwan sebenarnya lebih sederhana daripada yang dibayangkan banyak orang: bawa kartu NHI, pertama nilai apakah ini penyakit ringan atau berat, pilih poli yang tepat, mendaftar, diperiksa, ambil obat—seluruh prosesnya sering rampung dalam setengah jam hingga satu jam. Orang asing yang baru di Taiwan bisa mulai dengan menghafal lokasi klinik dan apotek terdekat, lalu bertanya pada rekan kerja atau tetangga, 'Klinik mana di sekitar sini yang bagus?' Setelah terbiasa, kamu akan mendapati sistem medis yang murah dan praktis ini adalah salah satu hal paling menenangkan tentang hidup di Taiwan.","to see a doctor":"berobat ke dokter","to register (for a visit)":"mendaftar (untuk berobat)","NHI card":"kartu NHI","medical department/specialty":"poli/spesialisasi medis","family medicine":"kedokteran keluarga","ENT (otolaryngology)":"THT (otolaringologi)","prescription":"resep","referral":"rujukan","Note: In Taiwan, visiting a large hospital without a referral means a higher co-payment, while coming with a referral (zhuǎnzhěn) from a clinic costs less—a design meant to keep minor cases from flooding big hospitals. If you have a mild problem at night or on a holiday, look for a clinic advertising 'night/holiday hours.' You can check most clinics' hours on the NHI Administration website or Google Maps, and a first visit goes smoothly with your passport or residency permit. Keep the printed 'medicine bag' rather than tossing it—you can show it to the doctor at your next visit.":"Catatan: Di Taiwan, berkunjung ke rumah sakit besar tanpa rujukan berarti biaya urun (co-payment) lebih tinggi, sedangkan datang dengan rujukan (zhuǎnzhěn) dari klinik lebih murah—rancangan yang bertujuan mencegah kasus ringan membanjiri rumah sakit besar. Jika kamu punya masalah ringan di malam hari atau hari libur, cari klinik yang memasang 'jam malam/hari libur'. Kamu bisa mengecek jam buka sebagian besar klinik di situs Badan Asuransi Kesehatan atau Google Maps, dan kunjungan pertama berjalan lancar dengan paspor atau izin tinggalmu. Simpan 'kantong obat' bercetak itu alih-alih membuangnya—kamu bisa menunjukkannya kepada dokter pada kunjungan berikutnya.","Working in Taiwan: A Foreigner's Guide to Job Hunting and the Workplace":"Bekerja di Taiwan: Panduan Mencari Kerja dan Dunia Kerja untuk Orang Asing","You'd like to work in Taiwan—and the moment you decide, a pile of questions appears: where to look for jobs, what documents you need, and how salary and social insurance work. This article lays out, in practical terms, the whole journey of a foreigner finding a job and starting work in Taiwan—from job sites and résumés to interviews, work permits, and taxes.":"Kamu ingin bekerja di Taiwan—dan begitu kamu memutuskan, setumpuk pertanyaan muncul: di mana mencari lowongan, dokumen apa yang dibutuhkan, dan bagaimana gaji serta jaminan sosial bekerja. Artikel ini memaparkan secara praktis seluruh perjalanan seorang asing mencari kerja dan mulai bekerja di Taiwan—dari situs lowongan dan resume hingga wawancara, izin kerja, dan pajak.","The mainstream way to find a job in Taiwan is through 'job sites.' The most popular are 104 Job Bank and 1111 Job Bank, plus the newer CakeResume and Yourator aimed at younger people and foreign firms. You register, fill in your 'résumé' (lǚlì), and then search for openings and apply directly. If you speak Chinese, your options multiply; if you rely mainly on English, specifically target 'foreign companies' (wàishāng) or 'startups' (xīnchuàng gōngsī), which more often work in English and are more used to hiring foreigners.":"Cara utama mencari kerja di Taiwan adalah lewat 'situs lowongan'. Yang paling populer adalah 104 Job Bank dan 1111 Job Bank, ditambah CakeResume dan Yourator yang lebih baru dan menyasar anak muda serta perusahaan asing. Kamu mendaftar, mengisi 'resume' (lǚlì), lalu mencari lowongan dan melamar langsung. Jika kamu bisa berbahasa Mandarin, pilihanmu berlipat ganda; jika kamu terutama mengandalkan bahasa Inggris, targetkan secara khusus 'perusahaan asing' (wàishāng) atau 'startup' (xīnchuàng gōngsī), yang lebih sering bekerja dalam bahasa Inggris dan lebih terbiasa merekrut orang asing.","After sending your résumé comes the 'interview.' A Taiwanese interview usually starts by asking about your experience, why you want to join this company, and your salary expectations. Dressing neatly, arriving on time, and showing a sincere attitude—these few things matter. Foreigners are often also asked about 'your visa status' and 'your Chinese level,' so it's best to prepare answers in advance. There may be more than one round: some companies have a first and second interview, or even ask you to do an 'assignment' (zuòyè) or a short test—increasingly common in Taiwan, so no need to be too nervous.":"Setelah mengirim resume, tibalah 'wawancara'. Wawancara di Taiwan biasanya dimulai dengan menanyakan pengalamanmu, mengapa kamu ingin bergabung dengan perusahaan ini, dan ekspektasi gajimu. Berpakaian rapi, datang tepat waktu, dan menunjukkan sikap tulus—beberapa hal ini penting. Orang asing sering juga ditanya tentang 'status visamu' dan 'tingkat kemampuan Mandarinmu', jadi sebaiknya siapkan jawaban terlebih dahulu. Bisa jadi ada lebih dari satu tahap: sebagian perusahaan mengadakan wawancara pertama dan kedua, atau bahkan memintamu mengerjakan 'tugas' (zuòyè) atau tes singkat—makin lazim di Taiwan, jadi tak perlu terlalu gugup.","For a foreigner to work legally in Taiwan, the crucial items are a 'work permit' (gōngzuò xǔkě) and a 'residency permit' (jūliúzhèng). Typically the company first applies for your 'work permit' (commonly called a work card); once you have it, you use it to apply for the 'residency permit,' the ARC. Only with an ARC can you legally reside and work long-term, and also get a phone number, open a bank account, and join the NHI. Most of this paperwork is handled with help from the company's HR (rénzī); your job is to prepare documents like your passport, proof of education, and photos, and to cooperate patiently.":"Agar orang asing bisa bekerja secara sah di Taiwan, dua hal krusialnya adalah 'izin kerja' (gōngzuò xǔkě) dan 'izin tinggal' (jūliúzhèng). Biasanya perusahaan lebih dulu mengajukan 'izin kerja'-mu (umumnya disebut kartu kerja); begitu kamu memilikinya, kamu memakainya untuk mengajukan 'izin tinggal', yakni ARC. Hanya dengan ARC kamu bisa tinggal dan bekerja secara sah dalam jangka panjang, sekaligus mendapatkan nomor telepon, membuka rekening bank, dan mengikuti NHI. Sebagian besar dokumen ini diurus dengan bantuan HRD (rénzī) perusahaan; tugasmu adalah menyiapkan dokumen seperti paspor, bukti pendidikan, dan foto, serta bekerja sama dengan sabar.","Once you start work, the company enrolls you in 'labor insurance' (láobǎo) and 'health insurance' (jiànbǎo)—the basic protections for employees in Taiwan. 'Labor insurance' pays benefits when you're unemployed, injured, giving birth, or retiring; 'health insurance' is the National Health Insurance you use to see doctors. There's also the 'labor pension' (láotuì): the employer must contribute at least 6% of your salary each month into your personal pension account. Part of this money is deducted from your salary and part is borne by the company, all clearly itemized on the monthly pay slip (xīnzīdān) you receive.":"Begitu kamu mulai bekerja, perusahaan mendaftarkanmu ke 'asuransi tenaga kerja' (láobǎo) dan 'asuransi kesehatan' (jiànbǎo)—perlindungan dasar bagi karyawan di Taiwan. 'Asuransi tenaga kerja' membayar tunjangan saat kamu menganggur, cedera, melahirkan, atau pensiun; 'asuransi kesehatan' adalah Jaminan Kesehatan Nasional yang kamu pakai untuk berobat. Ada pula 'dana pensiun tenaga kerja' (láotuì): pemberi kerja wajib menyetor minimal 6% dari gajimu setiap bulan ke rekening pensiun pribadimu. Sebagian dari uang ini dipotong dari gajimu dan sebagian ditanggung perusahaan, semuanya dirinci jelas pada slip gaji bulanan (xīnzīdān) yang kamu terima.","On pay, Taiwan mainly uses a 'monthly salary' system, and what's usually quoted is the 'monthly salary.' Many companies also give a 'year-end bonus,' typically one to two months' pay, more at better firms. Note: when a figure is quoted during recruiting, clarify 'monthly salary times how many months,' because some companies fold the year-end bonus in to make the annual figure look higher. Also, Taiwan's minimum wage (basic wage) is adjusted yearly, and the law sets overtime pay, annual leave (tèxiū), and labor/health insurance—all rights you're entitled to, so it's best to read the employment contract carefully before signing.":"Soal upah, Taiwan terutama memakai sistem 'gaji bulanan', dan yang biasanya disebutkan adalah 'gaji bulanan'. Banyak perusahaan juga memberi 'bonus akhir tahun', umumnya satu sampai dua bulan gaji, lebih banyak di perusahaan yang lebih baik. Perhatikan: ketika sebuah angka disebut saat rekrutmen, perjelas 'gaji bulanan dikali berapa bulan', karena sebagian perusahaan memasukkan bonus akhir tahun agar angka tahunan tampak lebih tinggi. Selain itu, upah minimum (upah dasar) Taiwan disesuaikan setiap tahun, dan undang-undang mengatur upah lembur, cuti tahunan (tèxiū), serta asuransi tenaga kerja/kesehatan—semuanya hak yang berhak kamu terima, jadi sebaiknya baca kontrak kerja dengan cermat sebelum menandatangani.","Finally, there's 'filing taxes' (bàoshuì). If you have income in Taiwan you must pay income tax, and every May is filing season. A foreigner's tax rate depends on how long you've lived in Taiwan: reside 183 days or more within the year and you count as a 'tax resident,' able to file at the same progressive rates as locals and to itemize deductions; live fewer days than that and the rate is higher. Your company usually 'withholds' (yùkòu) part of your tax in advance, and the May filing settles any over- or under-payment. Taiwan's filing system is very convenient—you can complete it online—and if you're lost the first time, ask your company or use the government's online tutorials.":"Terakhir, ada 'melapor pajak' (bàoshuì). Jika kamu berpenghasilan di Taiwan, kamu wajib membayar pajak penghasilan, dan setiap bulan Mei adalah musim pelaporan. Tarif pajak orang asing bergantung pada berapa lama kamu tinggal di Taiwan: bermukim 183 hari atau lebih dalam setahun dan kamu dihitung sebagai 'penduduk pajak', bisa melapor dengan tarif progresif yang sama dengan penduduk lokal serta merinci potongan; tinggal kurang dari itu dan tarifnya lebih tinggi. Perusahaanmu biasanya 'memotong di muka' (yùkòu) sebagian pajakmu, dan pelaporan bulan Mei menyelesaikan kelebihan atau kekurangan bayar. Sistem pelaporan Taiwan sangat praktis—kamu bisa menyelesaikannya secara daring—dan jika bingung pada kali pertama, tanyakan pada perusahaanmu atau gunakan panduan daring pemerintah.","job hunting":"mencari kerja","job bank / recruiting site":"bursa kerja / situs rekrutmen","résumé/CV":"resume/CV","work permit":"izin kerja","residency permit (ARC)":"izin tinggal (ARC)","labor insurance":"asuransi tenaga kerja","labor pension":"dana pensiun tenaga kerja","salary/wages":"gaji/upah","filing taxes":"melapor pajak","income tax":"pajak penghasilan","employment contract":"kontrak kerja","Note: When foreigners take jobs in Taiwan, some roles impose conditions on the employer, such as a minimum monthly salary per foreign hire (professional posts generally above a set amount)—a mechanism to protect local employment. Recently an 'Employment Gold Card' was created for highly skilled talent; qualifying holders get entry, work, residence, and even tax benefits bundled together, with no employer needed. When changing jobs, you may need to update the 'occupation' on your residency permit, so confirm with the new company or the Ministry of Labor before quitting. Keep your pay slips—they serve as proof of insurance and income for mortgages and various applications.":"Catatan: Ketika orang asing mengambil pekerjaan di Taiwan, sebagian posisi menetapkan syarat bagi pemberi kerja, seperti gaji bulanan minimum per pekerja asing (posisi profesional umumnya di atas jumlah tertentu)—mekanisme untuk melindungi lapangan kerja lokal. Baru-baru ini dibuat 'Employment Gold Card' untuk tenaga berkeahlian tinggi; pemegang yang memenuhi syarat memperoleh manfaat masuk, bekerja, tinggal, bahkan pajak sekaligus, tanpa memerlukan pemberi kerja. Saat berganti pekerjaan, kamu mungkin perlu memperbarui 'pekerjaan' pada izin tinggalmu, jadi pastikan dulu ke perusahaan baru atau Kementerian Tenaga Kerja sebelum berhenti. Simpan slip gajimu—ia berfungsi sebagai bukti asuransi dan penghasilan untuk KPR dan berbagai pengajuan.","Renting and Moving: The Complete Process from House-Hunting to Move-In":"Menyewa dan Pindah Rumah: Proses Lengkap dari Mencari Rumah hingga Menempati","To live in Taiwan, the first thing you need is a place to stay. But where do you search for a place, what should you check when viewing, how much is the deposit, and how do you sign the lease? For a first-timer it's all a bit bewildering. This article practically walks you through the whole process of renting and settling in—from finding a place, viewing, and signing, to water, electricity, and internet setup, moving day, and getting your trash routine ready.":"Untuk tinggal di Taiwan, hal pertama yang kamu butuhkan adalah tempat tinggal. Tapi di mana mencari tempat, apa yang harus diperiksa saat melihat unit, berapa uang jaminannya, dan bagaimana menandatangani sewa? Bagi pemula, semuanya agak membingungkan. Artikel ini secara praktis memandu kamu melewati seluruh proses menyewa dan menetap—dari mencari tempat, melihat unit, dan menandatangani, hingga pemasangan air, listrik, dan internet, hari pindahan, serta menyiapkan rutinitas sampahmu.","For finding rentals in Taiwan, the site most people use is '591 (591租屋網),' where nearly all landlords and agents post listings. You can filter by area, rent, and unit type (suite, private room, whole-floor home). A 'suite' (tàofáng) is a single room with its own bathroom, while a 'private room' (yǎfáng) is a separate room but shares the bathroom and kitchen with others, so the rent is cheaper. Besides 591, you can also check rental groups on Facebook, or simply walk around the neighborhood you want to live in—many older apartments post a red paper reading '租' (for rent) by the entrance.":"Untuk mencari sewaan di Taiwan, situs yang paling banyak dipakai adalah '591 (591租屋網)', tempat hampir semua pemilik dan agen memasang iklan. Kamu bisa menyaring berdasarkan area, harga sewa, dan tipe unit (suite, kamar privat, rumah satu lantai penuh). 'Suite' (tàofáng) adalah satu kamar dengan kamar mandi sendiri, sedangkan 'kamar privat' (yǎfáng) adalah kamar terpisah tetapi berbagi kamar mandi dan dapur dengan orang lain, sehingga sewanya lebih murah. Selain 591, kamu juga bisa mengecek grup sewa rumah di Facebook, atau sekadar berjalan-jalan di lingkungan yang kamu inginkan—banyak apartemen lama menempel kertas merah bertuliskan '租' (disewakan) di dekat pintu masuk.","When you find a place you like, always 'view it' (kànfáng)—go see it in person. A few key things to check: is the water pressure enough, are there signs of leaks, is the ventilation and natural light good, is the area too noisy, and are the phone signal and water heater working properly. Also clarify 'does the rent include water, electricity, and internet,' 'how many months' deposit (yājīn) is required,' and 'is cooking or keeping pets allowed.' Taiwanese suites usually come with basic furniture and appliances—bed, fridge, air conditioner, washing machine—but every unit differs, so it's best to confirm each item on the spot.":"Ketika kamu menemukan tempat yang disukai, selalu 'lihat unitnya' (kànfáng)—datang melihat langsung. Beberapa hal penting yang perlu diperiksa: apakah tekanan airnya cukup, adakah tanda kebocoran, apakah sirkulasi udara dan cahaya alaminya baik, apakah areanya terlalu bising, serta apakah sinyal telepon dan pemanas air berfungsi dengan baik. Perjelas juga 'apakah sewa sudah termasuk air, listrik, dan internet', 'berapa bulan uang jaminan (yājīn) yang diminta', dan 'apakah boleh memasak atau memelihara hewan'. Suite di Taiwan biasanya dilengkapi perabot dan peralatan dasar—ranjang, kulkas, AC, mesin cuci—tetapi tiap unit berbeda, jadi sebaiknya pastikan setiap barang di tempat.","Once you decide to rent, you enter the 'signing' (qiānyuē) and 'paying the deposit' stage. A Taiwanese lease is usually for one year, rent is paid monthly, and the deposit (yājīn) is generally 'two months' rent'; when you move out, if the place isn't damaged, the landlord must return the deposit. Before signing, be sure to read the 'lease contract' (zūlìn qìyuē) from start to finish: the term, rent, deposit, how utilities are calculated, whether early termination is allowed, who's responsible for repairs, and so on—all should be put in black and white. The government provides a 'model lease contract'; if the landlord's terms seem odd, you can compare them against the template.":"Begitu kamu memutuskan menyewa, kamu memasuki tahap 'penandatanganan' (qiānyuē) dan 'membayar uang jaminan'. Sewa di Taiwan biasanya untuk satu tahun, sewa dibayar per bulan, dan uang jaminan (yājīn) umumnya 'dua bulan sewa'; ketika kamu pindah, jika tempatnya tidak rusak, pemilik wajib mengembalikan uang jaminan. Sebelum menandatangani, pastikan membaca 'kontrak sewa' (zūlìn qìyuē) dari awal sampai akhir: jangka waktu, sewa, uang jaminan, cara menghitung utilitas, apakah pengakhiran dini diperbolehkan, siapa yang bertanggung jawab atas perbaikan, dan sebagainya—semuanya harus tertulis hitam di atas putih. Pemerintah menyediakan 'kontrak sewa contoh'; jika ketentuan pemilik terasa aneh, kamu bisa membandingkannya dengan templat itu.","Around move-in, the most important practical steps are transferring or setting up 'water, electricity, gas, and internet.' If it's a 'whole-floor home,' you often pay water and electricity directly to Taipower and the water company yourself, so confirm the previous tenant settled their bills and 'transfer' (guòhù) the accounts into your name. Gas comes in two kinds—'bottled gas' and 'natural (piped) gas'; with bottled gas, note the gas shop's phone number and call for a delivery when you're running low. For internet, you can apply yourself with providers like Chunghwa Telecom, and installation usually happens within a few days. It's best to confirm these details with the landlord one by one at signing.":"Menjelang pindahan, langkah praktis terpenting adalah memindahkan atau memasang 'air, listrik, gas, dan internet'. Jika ini 'rumah satu lantai penuh', kamu sering membayar air dan listrik langsung ke Taipower dan perusahaan air sendiri, jadi pastikan penyewa sebelumnya telah melunasi tagihannya dan 'balik nama' (guòhù) akun-akun itu ke namamu. Gas ada dua jenis—'gas tabung' dan 'gas alam (pipa)'; dengan gas tabung, catat nomor telepon toko gas dan telepon untuk pengiriman saat persediaan menipis. Untuk internet, kamu bisa mendaftar sendiri ke penyedia seperti Chunghwa Telecom, dan pemasangan biasanya terjadi dalam beberapa hari. Sebaiknya konfirmasikan detail-detail ini satu per satu dengan pemilik saat penandatanganan.","Next comes 'moving' (bānjiā). If you don't have much, you can just call a taxi or a small moving 'van' (xiǎo huòchē) and make a few trips; if you have a lot or large furniture, hire a 'moving company,' whose quotes you can find online—just clarify upfront whether it's priced 'by the job' or 'by the hour,' and whether they charge for floors and whether there's an elevator. On moving day, wrap fragile items in bubble wrap first and label the outside of each box with its contents to save a lot of effort. Taiwanese also have a custom of 'picking an auspicious date to move,' and many choose a lucky day to move in for peace of mind.":"Berikutnya adalah 'pindahan' (bānjiā). Jika barangmu tidak banyak, kamu bisa memanggil taksi atau 'mobil bak kecil' (xiǎo huòchē) dan bolak-balik beberapa kali; jika barangmu banyak atau ada perabot besar, sewa 'jasa pindahan', yang harganya bisa kamu cari daring—cukup perjelas di awal apakah dihitung 'per pekerjaan' atau 'per jam', apakah ada biaya per lantai, dan apakah ada lift. Pada hari pindahan, bungkus dulu barang mudah pecah dengan bubble wrap dan tuliskan isi di luar tiap kardus agar menghemat banyak tenaga. Orang Taiwan juga punya kebiasaan 'memilih tanggal baik untuk pindah', dan banyak yang memilih hari mujur untuk pindah demi ketenangan hati.","Finally, don't forget to set up your 'trash and recycling.' Most places in Taiwan use 'trash doesn't touch the ground': the garbage truck comes at fixed times, and you must bring your trash out at the right window and hand it to the sanitation crew; general trash must go in the government-mandated 'designated garbage bags,' while recyclables and food waste are separated. So after moving in, be sure to first ask the landlord or neighbors, 'What time does the garbage truck come here, and which corner does it stop at?' Some better-managed complexes or buildings have a 'central trash room' where you can drop it off anytime—much more convenient. Only once you've sorted this out is your new life in Taiwan truly settled.":"Terakhir, jangan lupa mengatur 'sampah dan daur ulang'. Sebagian besar tempat di Taiwan menerapkan 'sampah tak menyentuh tanah': truk sampah datang pada waktu tetap, dan kamu harus membawa sampahmu keluar pada jam yang tepat lalu menyerahkannya kepada petugas kebersihan; sampah umum harus dimasukkan ke 'kantong sampah khusus' yang ditetapkan pemerintah, sedangkan barang daur ulang dan sisa makanan dipisahkan. Jadi setelah pindah, pastikan lebih dulu bertanya pada pemilik atau tetangga, 'Jam berapa truk sampah datang ke sini, dan berhenti di sudut mana?' Sebagian kompleks atau gedung yang dikelola lebih baik memiliki 'ruang sampah terpusat' tempat kamu bisa membuang kapan saja—jauh lebih praktis. Hanya setelah beres soal ini, kehidupan barumu di Taiwan benar-benar mapan.","to rent a place / rental housing":"menyewa tempat / hunian sewa","to view a property":"melihat properti","studio suite (with private bath)":"suite studio (dengan kamar mandi dalam)","private room (shared bath/kitchen)":"kamar privat (kamar mandi/dapur bersama)","lease/rental contract":"kontrak sewa","agent/broker":"agen/perantara","transfer of account/title":"balik nama akun/kepemilikan","to move in":"pindah masuk","Note: In Taiwan rentals, some landlords—citing higher income or land-value taxes—ask you not to put the address in the contract, or are reluctant to let you register residency (household registration) or to issue rent receipts. But a proper contract helps with deposit disputes and company/visa procedures, so it's wise to sign one properly. Rent may be deductible up to a limit on your year-end tax return. Air conditioning is essential in Taiwan's summer, so if electricity is billed separately, always check the per-unit rate. On move-out, 'restoring the original condition' is the rule, so photographing any existing scratches or stains at move-in makes deposit return far less contentious.":"Catatan: Dalam sewa-menyewa di Taiwan, sebagian pemilik—dengan alasan pajak penghasilan atau pajak nilai tanah yang lebih tinggi—memintamu tidak mencantumkan alamat dalam kontrak, atau enggan mengizinkanmu mendaftarkan domisili (registrasi rumah tangga) atau menerbitkan kuitansi sewa. Tetapi kontrak yang benar membantu dalam sengketa uang jaminan serta urusan perusahaan/visa, jadi bijak untuk menandatanganinya dengan benar. Sewa mungkin bisa dikurangkan hingga batas tertentu pada laporan pajak akhir tahunmu. AC sangat penting di musim panas Taiwan, jadi jika listrik ditagih terpisah, selalu cek tarif per unitnya. Saat pindah keluar, 'mengembalikan ke kondisi semula' adalah aturannya, jadi memotret goresan atau noda yang sudah ada saat pindah masuk membuat pengembalian uang jaminan jauh lebih tak berselisih.","Society Today":"Masyarakat Kini","Low Birth Rate and an Aging Society: A Taiwan Growing Old Together":"Angka Kelahiran Rendah dan Masyarakat Menua: Taiwan yang Menua Bersama","Walk down the street and you may spot elderly people doing slow morning exercises in the park more often than you hear a baby cry—that's how many people in Taiwan feel these days. Fewer children, more seniors. Let's look at how this quiet but sweeping change is reshaping the whole society.":"Berjalanlah di jalanan dan kamu mungkin lebih sering melihat orang lanjut usia melakukan senam pagi perlahan di taman daripada mendengar tangis bayi—begitulah yang dirasakan banyak orang di Taiwan belakangan ini. Anak-anak makin sedikit, lansia makin banyak. Mari kita lihat bagaimana perubahan yang senyap namun menyeluruh ini membentuk ulang seluruh masyarakat.","Taiwan is now facing two things at once. The first is a \"low birth rate\": every year, fewer babies are born. The second is an \"aging society\": people aged 65 and over make up an ever-larger share of the total population. These two are really two sides of the same coin. When the average couple has fewer than one child, the number of young people naturally shrinks year by year, while advances in medicine let everyone live longer. And so the age structure of the whole society slowly shifts from \"young\" toward \"old.\"":"Taiwan kini menghadapi dua hal sekaligus. Pertama adalah \"angka kelahiran rendah\": setiap tahun, makin sedikit bayi yang lahir. Kedua adalah \"masyarakat menua\": penduduk berusia 65 tahun ke atas menyusun porsi yang makin besar dari total populasi. Kedua hal ini sebenarnya dua sisi dari mata uang yang sama. Ketika rata-rata pasangan punya kurang dari satu anak, jumlah anak muda secara alami menyusut dari tahun ke tahun, sementara kemajuan kedokteran membuat semua orang hidup lebih lama. Maka struktur usia seluruh masyarakat perlahan bergeser dari \"muda\" menuju \"tua\".","Why are Taiwanese having fewer and fewer children? The reasons are many, and very practical. Housing is too expensive, wages rise slowly, and many young people struggle just to support themselves—let alone raise another child. The cost of childcare and education gives people pause too: nanny fees, tuition, extracurricular classes—item by item, it all adds up to a burden. On top of that, people now marry later, and some choose not to marry at all, so the desire to have children naturally declines. For many couples, \"whether to have a child\" is no longer a given but a decision that requires serious calculation.":"Mengapa orang Taiwan makin sedikit punya anak? Alasannya banyak, dan sangat praktis. Rumah terlalu mahal, upah naik lambat, dan banyak anak muda kesulitan sekadar menghidupi diri sendiri—apalagi membesarkan seorang anak lagi. Biaya pengasuhan dan pendidikan juga membuat orang ragu: upah pengasuh, uang sekolah, les tambahan—satu per satu, semuanya menumpuk menjadi beban. Ditambah lagi, orang kini menikah lebih lambat, dan sebagian memilih tidak menikah sama sekali, sehingga keinginan punya anak secara alami menurun. Bagi banyak pasangan, \"punya anak atau tidak\" bukan lagi hal yang niscaya melainkan keputusan yang butuh perhitungan serius.","As the population ages, the thing most directly affected is caregiving. In the past, within a large extended family, if an elder fell ill, the sons, daughters, and daughters-in-law would simply take turns looking after them. But now families are smaller and young people often work away from home, so who will care for aging parents has become a hard problem for many households. To meet this need, the government has promoted \"long-term care\" services—including home care, daycare centers, meal delivery, rehabilitation, and respite care—hoping to ease the burden on family members.":"Seiring populasi menua, hal yang paling langsung terpengaruh adalah pengasuhan. Dahulu, dalam keluarga besar, jika seorang lansia jatuh sakit, para putra, putri, dan menantu tinggal bergantian merawatnya. Tetapi kini keluarga makin kecil dan anak muda sering bekerja jauh dari rumah, sehingga siapa yang akan merawat orang tua yang menua menjadi masalah pelik bagi banyak rumah tangga. Untuk memenuhi kebutuhan ini, pemerintah menggalakkan layanan \"perawatan jangka panjang\"—termasuk perawatan di rumah, pusat penitipan harian, pengantaran makanan, rehabilitasi, dan perawatan jeda—dengan harapan meringankan beban anggota keluarga.","On the other side, the government is trying every possible way to encourage people to have children. In recent years, cities and counties have rolled out \"birth subsidies\"—a lump sum for the first child, with more added for a second or third—along with monthly \"childcare allowances,\" and have expanded the number of public and affordable childcare places so that dual-income families can hand over their kids with more peace of mind. Still, many young parents say frankly that while these subsidies help, compared with the cost of raising a child for over a decade, they are a drop in the bucket. To truly raise the birth rate, what's needed is a change in the whole environment.":"Di sisi lain, pemerintah berupaya dengan segala cara mendorong orang punya anak. Beberapa tahun terakhir, kota dan kabupaten meluncurkan \"subsidi kelahiran\"—sejumlah uang sekaligus untuk anak pertama, dengan tambahan untuk anak kedua atau ketiga—beserta \"tunjangan pengasuhan\" bulanan, serta memperbanyak tempat penitipan anak publik dan terjangkau agar keluarga berpenghasilan ganda bisa menitipkan anak dengan lebih tenang. Meski begitu, banyak orang tua muda berterus terang bahwa meski subsidi ini membantu, dibandingkan biaya membesarkan anak selama lebih dari satu dekade, itu hanya setetes air di lautan. Untuk benar-benar menaikkan angka kelahiran, yang diperlukan adalah perubahan seluruh lingkungannya.","An aging population is also quietly changing the everyday scenery of Taiwan. Step into a neighborhood and you'll see ever more \"daycare centers\" and \"senior learning\" classrooms, where elders sing, paint, and learn to use smartphones. In markets and on buses, silver-haired figures are increasingly common; many shops and government offices have begun to prioritize \"barrier-free\" design, adding elevators, ramps, and handrails. The care industry also needs a lot of manpower: alongside local care workers, many \"migrant workers\" from Southeast Asia have become a vital force supporting Taiwan's long-term care system.":"Populasi yang menua juga diam-diam mengubah pemandangan sehari-hari Taiwan. Masuklah ke sebuah lingkungan dan kamu akan melihat makin banyak \"pusat penitipan harian\" dan ruang kelas \"pembelajaran lansia\", tempat para lansia bernyanyi, melukis, dan belajar memakai ponsel pintar. Di pasar dan bus, sosok berambut perak makin sering terlihat; banyak toko dan kantor pemerintah mulai mengutamakan desain \"bebas hambatan\", menambahkan lift, ram, dan pegangan tangan. Industri perawatan juga membutuhkan banyak tenaga: di samping pekerja perawatan lokal, banyak \"pekerja migran\" dari Asia Tenggara telah menjadi kekuatan vital yang menopang sistem perawatan jangka panjang Taiwan.","A low birth rate and an aging society are among the most important challenges Taiwan will face over the coming decades. What they move is not just a few numbers, but the labor force, health insurance, pensions, real estate—even the very look of cities and countryside. There is no simple answer to this road, but Taiwanese society is feeling its way forward and adjusting as it goes. Perhaps the point is not only \"how to get people to have more children,\" but \"how to make sure that the old, the young, and children alike can all live with peace of mind on this island.\" That is the homework the whole society must face together.":"Angka kelahiran rendah dan masyarakat menua termasuk tantangan terpenting yang akan dihadapi Taiwan dalam dekade-dekade mendatang. Yang mereka gerakkan bukan sekadar beberapa angka, melainkan angkatan kerja, asuransi kesehatan, dana pensiun, properti—bahkan wajah kota dan desa itu sendiri. Tak ada jawaban sederhana untuk jalan ini, tetapi masyarakat Taiwan meraba jalan maju sambil terus menyesuaikan diri. Mungkin intinya bukan hanya \"bagaimana membuat orang punya lebih banyak anak\", melainkan \"bagaimana memastikan yang tua, yang muda, dan anak-anak sama-sama bisa hidup dengan tenang di pulau ini\". Itulah pekerjaan rumah yang harus dihadapi seluruh masyarakat bersama-sama.","declining/low birth rate":"angka kelahiran menurun/rendah","population aging":"penuaan populasi","birth rate / fertility rate":"angka kelahiran / tingkat kesuburan","childcare (for young children)":"pengasuhan anak (untuk anak kecil)","care worker / caregiver":"pekerja perawatan / pengasuh","adult daycare center":"pusat penitipan harian lansia","seniors, the silver-haired generation":"lansia, generasi berambut perak","childcare allowance":"tunjangan pengasuhan anak","migrant worker":"pekerja migran","barrier-free / accessible":"bebas hambatan / aksesibel","respite care service":"layanan perawatan istirahat (respite care)","Taiwan has already entered an \"aged society,\" with people 65 and older exceeding 14% of the population, and is expected to become a \"super-aged society\" (over 20%) in the near future. Another striking figure is how few babies are born—in recent years annual deaths have outnumbered births, a \"natural population decline.\" Among young Taiwanese, hesitation to marry or have children for financial reasons is sometimes summed up as \"bù gǎn shēng\" (not daring to have kids). A signature policy slogan, \"Ages 0–6, the nation raises them with you,\" has driven the expansion of subsidies.":"Taiwan telah memasuki \"masyarakat menua\", dengan penduduk berusia 65 tahun ke atas melebihi 14% dari populasi, dan diperkirakan akan menjadi \"masyarakat super-tua\" (lebih dari 20%) dalam waktu dekat. Angka mencolok lainnya adalah rendahnya angka kelahiran—dalam beberapa tahun terakhir jumlah kematian tahunan melampaui jumlah kelahiran, sebuah \"penurunan populasi alami\". Di kalangan anak muda Taiwan, keraguan untuk menikah atau memiliki anak karena alasan finansial kadang dirangkum dengan istilah \"bù gǎn shēng\" (tidak berani punya anak). Sebuah slogan kebijakan yang ikonik, \"Usia 0–6, negara membesarkan mereka bersama Anda\", telah mendorong perluasan subsidi.","Taiwan's Religious Diversity: A Street Full of Gods":"Keberagaman Agama Taiwan: Satu Jalan Penuh Dewa","On a single street you may find a Taoist temple wreathed in incense smoke, a quiet Christian church next door, and a Buddhist temple just beyond—in Taiwan this is an utterly ordinary sight. Let's explore Taiwan's religious world, where a great many gods and faiths coexist with remarkable ease.":"Di satu jalan yang sama Anda bisa menemukan kuil Tao yang berselimut asap dupa, gereja Kristen yang tenang di sebelahnya, dan kuil Buddha tak jauh dari situ—di Taiwan ini pemandangan yang benar-benar biasa. Mari kita jelajahi dunia keagamaan Taiwan, tempat begitu banyak dewa dan kepercayaan hidup berdampingan dengan sangat mudah.","Taiwan is an extraordinarily religiously diverse place. Here you'll find Buddhism, Taoism, Protestant Christianity, Catholicism, Islam, and countless forms of \"folk belief.\" What's fascinating is that these faiths don't each keep to themselves—they mingle together in a lively jumble. Ask many Taiwanese \"What religion do you follow?\" and they'll often pause, because they may worship the Buddha, Mazu, and Lord Guan all at once, light a \"bright-light lamp\" at a temple over New Year, and also tag along with friends to sing hymns at church. For them, faith is part of life, not an either-or choice.":"Taiwan adalah tempat dengan keberagaman agama yang luar biasa. Di sini Anda akan menemukan Buddha, Tao, Kristen Protestan, Katolik, Islam, dan tak terhitung bentuk \"kepercayaan rakyat\". Yang menarik, kepercayaan-kepercayaan ini tidak berdiri sendiri-sendiri—semuanya berbaur dalam campuran yang semarak. Tanyakan pada banyak orang Taiwan \"Anda menganut agama apa?\" dan mereka sering tertegun, karena mereka mungkin memuja Buddha, Mazu, dan Dewa Guan sekaligus, menyalakan \"lampu terang\" di kuil saat Tahun Baru, sekaligus ikut teman menyanyikan himne di gereja. Bagi mereka, iman adalah bagian dari hidup, bukan pilihan salah satu.","In Taiwan, the \"temple\" is the most common and most down-to-earth center of faith. Nearly every village and every old street has one, and the main deity enshrined varies: seaside fishing villages mostly worship \"Mazu,\" who protects those who go out to sea; businesspeople often worship \"Lord Guan,\" revering his loyalty and his blessings for wealth; students hoping for success and good exam results go to worship \"Wenchang Dijun,\" the god of scholarship. A temple isn't only a place to pray—it's the community's activity hub, staging glove-puppet shows and open-air banquets during festivals, and serving as a spot where grandpas and grandmas sip tea and chat on ordinary days.":"Di Taiwan, \"kuil\" adalah pusat kepercayaan yang paling umum dan paling membumi. Hampir setiap desa dan setiap jalan tua memilikinya, dan dewa utama yang dipuja berbeda-beda: desa nelayan tepi laut kebanyakan memuja \"Mazu\", yang melindungi mereka yang melaut; para pebisnis sering memuja \"Dewa Guan\", menghormati kesetiaannya dan berkahnya untuk kekayaan; para pelajar yang berharap sukses dan nilai ujian bagus datang memuja \"Wenchang Dijun\", dewa ilmu. Kuil bukan hanya tempat berdoa—ia juga pusat kegiatan masyarakat, menggelar pertunjukan wayang sarung tangan dan jamuan terbuka saat festival, serta menjadi tempat para kakek dan nenek menyeruput teh dan mengobrol di hari-hari biasa.","\"Bàibài\" (worshipping) is a very natural part of daily life for Taiwanese. Opening a new shop calls for it, so does moving into a new home; you pray before exams, and you can go to a temple to ask for safety when you feel unwell. When worshipping, people prepare fruit, cookies, and drinks as offerings, light incense, press their palms together, and voice their heartfelt wishes to the deity—this is called \"bàibài\" or \"jìbài.\" To ask the god's opinion, you cast \"jiǎobēi\": two crescent-shaped wooden blocks dropped on the ground, whose face-up or face-down landing tells you whether the god agrees. For guidance, you can also draw a \"fortune poem\" (qiānshī). These rituals form an intimate dialogue between Taiwanese and their gods.":"\"Bàibài\" (bersembahyang) adalah bagian yang sangat alami dari kehidupan sehari-hari orang Taiwan. Membuka toko baru memerlukannya, begitu pula pindah ke rumah baru; Anda berdoa sebelum ujian, dan bisa pergi ke kuil untuk memohon keselamatan saat merasa kurang sehat. Saat bersembahyang, orang menyiapkan buah, kue, dan minuman sebagai persembahan, menyalakan dupa, mengatupkan kedua telapak tangan, dan menyampaikan harapan tulus mereka kepada dewa—ini disebut \"bàibài\" atau \"jìbài\". Untuk menanyakan pendapat dewa, Anda melempar \"jiǎobēi\": dua balok kayu berbentuk bulan sabit yang dijatuhkan ke tanah, posisi telungkup atau telentangnya memberitahu apakah dewa setuju. Untuk petunjuk, Anda juga bisa mencabut \"syair ramalan\" (qiānshī). Ritual-ritual ini membentuk dialog akrab antara orang Taiwan dan dewa-dewa mereka.","The time of year when you can feel the energy of Taiwanese folk belief most strongly is during the various \"deity processions\" (ràojìng) and temple fairs. A \"procession\" means placing a deity's statue on a palanquin and carrying it along a fixed route to tour the district, warding off evil and praying for blessings on the residents' behalf. The most famous is the springtime \"Mazu procession,\" in which tens of thousands of believers walk on foot behind Mazu for days on end and hundreds of kilometers, while people in the villages along the way prepare free food and drink—a scene both vast and warm. Temple fairs often ring with gongs and drums, and feature brightly colored \"electric flower floats\" blaring music, as lively as a traveling carnival.":"Waktu dalam setahun ketika Anda paling kuat merasakan energi kepercayaan rakyat Taiwan adalah saat berbagai \"arak-arakan dewa\" (ràojìng) dan pesta kuil. \"Arak-arakan\" berarti menempatkan patung dewa di atas tandu dan mengusungnya menyusuri rute tetap untuk berkeliling wilayah, menangkal roh jahat dan memanjatkan berkah bagi warga. Yang paling terkenal adalah \"arak-arakan Mazu\" di musim semi, di mana puluhan ribu umat berjalan kaki di belakang Mazu selama berhari-hari dan ratusan kilometer, sementara warga desa di sepanjang jalan menyiapkan makanan dan minuman gratis—pemandangan yang megah sekaligus hangat. Pesta kuil sering bergema dengan gong dan genderang, serta menampilkan \"kereta bunga elektrik\" warna-warni yang memutar musik keras, semeriah karnaval keliling.","Besides the lively folk beliefs, Buddhism also thrives in Taiwan and has developed a distinctive style of \"Humanistic Buddhism,\" emphasizing putting compassion into practice through social service. Groups like Tzu Chi, Fo Guang Shan, and Dharma Drum Mountain not only expound the scriptures but also run charities, hospitals, and universities, and are among the first to rush in with relief when disaster strikes. Christianity and Catholicism, meanwhile, though not the largest in terms of followers, brought modern medicine and education to Taiwan early on—many long-established hospitals and schools were originally founded by churches.":"Selain kepercayaan rakyat yang semarak, Buddha juga berkembang pesat di Taiwan dan telah mengembangkan gaya khas \"Buddhisme Humanistik\", yang menekankan pengamalan welas asih melalui pelayanan sosial. Kelompok seperti Tzu Chi, Fo Guang Shan, dan Dharma Drum Mountain tidak hanya mengajarkan kitab suci tetapi juga menjalankan lembaga amal, rumah sakit, dan universitas, serta termasuk yang pertama datang memberi bantuan saat bencana melanda. Sementara itu, Kristen dan Katolik, meski bukan yang terbesar dari segi jumlah pengikut, sejak awal membawa kedokteran dan pendidikan modern ke Taiwan—banyak rumah sakit dan sekolah tua yang semula didirikan oleh gereja.","What impresses foreigners most is often the tolerance among Taiwan's religions. Here, faiths rarely quarrel over \"whose is the true god\"; instead, you worship yours and I believe in mine, and we can still respect each other. Within one family, someone may be vegetarian and chant to the Buddha while another attends church services, yet they still gather around the same table at New Year and festivals. This peaceful, coexisting atmosphere springs from the diversity and openness Taiwanese society has long cultivated. Whether you step into a temple thick with incense or sit quietly inside a church, what you feel is really the same thing: people's shared longing for peace, health, and happiness.":"Yang paling mengesankan orang asing sering kali adalah toleransi di antara agama-agama Taiwan. Di sini, kepercayaan jarang berselisih soal \"dewa siapa yang benar\"; sebaliknya, kamu memuja milikmu dan aku percaya milikku, dan kita tetap bisa saling menghormati. Dalam satu keluarga, seseorang mungkin vegetarian dan melafalkan doa kepada Buddha sementara yang lain menghadiri kebaktian gereja, namun mereka tetap berkumpul di meja yang sama saat Tahun Baru dan festival. Suasana hidup berdampingan yang damai ini lahir dari keberagaman dan keterbukaan yang telah lama dipupuk masyarakat Taiwan. Entah Anda melangkah ke kuil yang tebal asap dupa atau duduk tenang di dalam gereja, yang Anda rasakan sebenarnya sama: kerinduan bersama manusia akan kedamaian, kesehatan, dan kebahagiaan.","folk belief / folk religion":"kepercayaan rakyat","temple (Taoist/folk)":"kuil (Tao/rakyat)","to worship / pay respects":"bersembahyang / memberi hormat","Mazu (sea goddess)":"Mazu (dewi laut)","deity, god(s)":"dewa","offering(s)":"persembahan","casting moon blocks (to ask the gods)":"melempar balok bulan (menanyakan pada dewa)","fortune poem / oracle slip":"syair ramalan / kertas ramalan","deity procession (touring the district)":"arak-arakan dewa (berkeliling wilayah)","electric flower float (music/light truck)":"kereta bunga elektrik (truk musik/lampu)","church":"gereja","tolerance, inclusiveness":"toleransi, keterbukaan","Taiwan is said to have over ten thousand officially registered temples and churches nationwide—among the highest densities of \"houses of the gods\" per capita in the world. While the incense tradition runs deep, in recent years, out of concern for health and the environment, more temples have cut back on incense or on burning \"spirit money.\" Casting moon blocks has its own fine etiquette: one up and one down means \"shèng jiǎo\" (the god says yes), both face-down is \"yīn jiǎo\" (no), and both face-up is \"xiào jiǎo\" (the god is \"laughing\"—undecided). Travelers who mind their manners are free to visit, as most temples are open to all.":"Taiwan konon memiliki lebih dari sepuluh ribu kuil dan gereja yang terdaftar resmi di seluruh negeri—termasuk salah satu kepadatan \"rumah para dewa\" per kapita tertinggi di dunia. Meski tradisi dupa mengakar dalam, beberapa tahun terakhir, demi kesehatan dan lingkungan, semakin banyak kuil mengurangi dupa atau pembakaran \"uang arwah\". Melempar balok bulan punya etiketnya sendiri yang halus: satu telentang satu telungkup berarti \"shèng jiǎo\" (dewa berkata ya), keduanya telungkup adalah \"yīn jiǎo\" (tidak), dan keduanya telentang adalah \"xiào jiǎo\" (dewa sedang \"tertawa\"—belum memutuskan). Wisatawan yang menjaga sopan santun bebas berkunjung, karena sebagian besar kuil terbuka untuk semua.","See Taiwan with One Card: A Convenient Public Transport Network":"Jelajahi Taiwan dengan Satu Kartu: Jaringan Transportasi Umum yang Praktis","Zip north–south across the island by high-speed rail, hop between metro and bus in the cities, and cover the last stretch on a shared bike—in Taiwan, even without a car, one card lets you roam the whole island quite freely. Let's look at Taiwan's public transport network, a boon to travelers and residents alike.":"Melesat utara–selatan menyeberangi pulau dengan kereta cepat, berpindah antara MRT dan bus di kota, dan menempuh jarak terakhir dengan sepeda berbagi—di Taiwan, bahkan tanpa mobil, satu kartu memungkinkan Anda menjelajahi seluruh pulau dengan cukup bebas. Mari kita lihat jaringan transportasi umum Taiwan, berkah bagi wisatawan maupun penduduk.","Though Taiwan is an island of no great size, its public transport is remarkably complete. To move quickly between cities, the most convenient option is the \"High Speed Rail\" (HSR). Running along the western corridor, the HSR strings together major cities like Taipei, Taichung, Tainan, and Kaohsiung; from the far north to the far south takes only a little over an hour, making \"a morning meeting in Taipei and lunch in Kaohsiung\" quite ordinary. The trains are new and clean and run frequently—the top choice for many business travelers and tourists.":"Meski Taiwan pulau yang tidak besar, transportasi umumnya sangat lengkap. Untuk berpindah cepat antar kota, pilihan paling praktis adalah \"Kereta Cepat\" (HSR). Membentang di sepanjang koridor barat, HSR merangkai kota-kota besar seperti Taipei, Taichung, Tainan, dan Kaohsiung; dari ujung utara ke ujung selatan hanya butuh sedikit lebih dari satu jam, sehingga \"rapat pagi di Taipei dan makan siang di Kaohsiung\" cukup lumrah. Keretanya baru, bersih, dan sering berangkat—pilihan utama banyak pelaku bisnis dan wisatawan.","If the HSR means \"fast,\" then \"Taiwan Railways\" (TRA) means \"reaching deep.\" The TRA is Taiwan's venerable conventional railway, its lines nearly circling the whole island, reaching the eastern regions of Yilan, Hualien, and Taitung as well as many small towns and rural areas. The TRA runs many train types, from the \"local train\" that stops at every station to the faster \"Tze-Chiang\" and the scenic \"Puyuma\" and \"Taroko\" expresses. Riding the TRA along the east coast, mountains on one side and the Pacific on the other, is for many the most beautiful railway scenery imaginable.":"Jika HSR berarti \"cepat\", maka \"Kereta Api Taiwan\" (TRA) berarti \"menjangkau dalam\". TRA adalah jalur kereta konvensional Taiwan yang bersejarah, jalur-jalurnya nyaris mengelilingi seluruh pulau, mencapai wilayah timur Yilan, Hualien, dan Taitung serta banyak kota kecil dan pedesaan. TRA mengoperasikan banyak jenis kereta, dari \"kereta lokal\" yang berhenti di setiap stasiun hingga \"Tze-Chiang\" yang lebih cepat serta ekspres pemandangan \"Puyuma\" dan \"Taroko\". Menaiki TRA di sepanjang pantai timur, gunung di satu sisi dan Samudra Pasifik di sisi lain, bagi banyak orang adalah pemandangan kereta terindah yang bisa dibayangkan.","In the big cities, the handiest way to get around is the \"MRT\" (metro). The Taipei Metro—with its dense network, frequent service, and punctuality—is a mode of transport many foreigners fall in love with the moment they arrive in Taipei. Kaohsiung, Taoyuan, and Taichung have each gained their own metro systems in turn, making travel in the south and center more convenient. Metro stations don't just take you to your destination; they're often hubs for shopping, eating, and transferring to buses. Note that Taiwan's metro cars have \"priority seats,\" and eating and drinking are expressly forbidden—small rules that keep the riding environment very comfortable.":"Di kota-kota besar, cara paling praktis untuk berkeliling adalah \"MRT\" (kereta bawah tanah). MRT Taipei—dengan jaringannya yang padat, layanan yang sering, dan ketepatan waktunya—adalah moda transportasi yang banyak orang asing jatuh cinta begitu tiba di Taipei. Kaohsiung, Taoyuan, dan Taichung masing-masing kini memiliki sistem MRT sendiri, membuat perjalanan di selatan dan tengah lebih nyaman. Stasiun MRT tak hanya mengantar Anda ke tujuan; keduanya sering menjadi pusat belanja, makan, dan berpindah ke bus. Perlu dicatat, gerbong MRT Taiwan memiliki \"kursi prioritas\", dan makan serta minum dilarang tegas—aturan-aturan kecil yang membuat lingkungan perjalanan sangat nyaman.","Where the metro can't reach, \"city buses\" and \"intercity coaches\" fill the gap. Urban bus routes are densely woven and can get you almost anywhere; for travel between cities, or heading up mountains and down to the coast to reach attractions, you take a \"coach\" (long-distance bus). Coaches are cheap and frequent—a very practical choice on a tight budget. One thing to note: on some Taiwan buses you tap your card both boarding and alighting, while others charge \"on boarding\" or \"on alighting.\" The first time, it's best to read the sign carefully or ask the driver so you're not caught fumbling.":"Di tempat yang tak terjangkau MRT, \"bus kota\" dan \"bus antarkota\" mengisi celahnya. Rute bus dalam kota terjalin rapat dan bisa membawa Anda ke hampir mana saja; untuk perjalanan antar kota, atau naik ke gunung dan turun ke pantai menuju objek wisata, Anda naik \"bus jarak jauh\". Bus jarak jauh murah dan sering—pilihan yang sangat praktis dengan anggaran terbatas. Satu hal yang perlu dicatat: di sebagian bus Taiwan Anda menempelkan kartu saat naik dan turun, sementara yang lain menarik ongkos \"saat naik\" atau \"saat turun\". Pertama kali, sebaiknya baca papan petunjuk dengan teliti atau tanya sopir agar tidak kelabakan.","What ties this whole system together and makes everything incredibly convenient is that little \"EasyCard\" or \"iPASS.\" These two are Taiwan's most widespread electronic fare cards; once loaded with value, they work for the metro, buses, the TRA, and renting public bicycles—and a single \"beep\" also pays for purchases at convenience stores and drinks from vending machines. You never have to dig for change or calculate fares, and there are often transfer discounts. You could say one contactless card is a key that unlocks transport across Taiwan.":"Yang menyatukan seluruh sistem ini dan membuat semuanya sangat praktis adalah kartu kecil \"EasyCard\" atau \"iPASS\". Keduanya adalah kartu tiket elektronik paling luas di Taiwan; setelah diisi saldo, keduanya bisa dipakai untuk MRT, bus, TRA, dan menyewa sepeda umum—dan satu \"bip\" saja juga membayar belanjaan di toko swalayan dan minuman dari mesin penjual otomatis. Anda tak perlu mengais uang receh atau menghitung ongkos, dan sering ada diskon perpindahan. Bisa dibilang satu kartu nirsentuh adalah kunci yang membuka transportasi di seluruh Taiwan.","The last stretch is often handled by \"YouBike.\" This is Taiwan's public bike-share system, its orange frames a common sight on street corners in every major city. Just rent one with an EasyCard or a phone app and ride to the next station to return it; the first short spell is usually free or very cheap—perfect for the last mile \"from the metro station to your destination.\" Combine the HSR, TRA, metro, buses, and coaches with YouBike and one contactless card, and even if you can't drive and don't understand Chinese, you can rely on public transport to explore every corner of the island of Taiwan.":"Jarak terakhir sering ditangani oleh \"YouBike\". Ini adalah sistem sepeda berbagi umum Taiwan, rangka oranyenya pemandangan lazim di sudut jalan setiap kota besar. Cukup sewa satu dengan EasyCard atau aplikasi ponsel lalu kayuh ke stasiun berikutnya untuk mengembalikannya; periode singkat pertama biasanya gratis atau sangat murah—sempurna untuk jarak terakhir \"dari stasiun MRT ke tujuan Anda\". Padukan HSR, TRA, MRT, bus, dan bus jarak jauh dengan YouBike serta satu kartu nirsentuh, maka meski Anda tak bisa menyetir dan tak paham bahasa Mandarin, Anda bisa mengandalkan transportasi umum untuk menjelajahi setiap sudut pulau Taiwan.","High Speed Rail (HSR)":"Kereta Cepat (HSR)","Taiwan Railways (TRA)":"Kereta Api Taiwan (TRA)","metro / MRT":"kereta bawah tanah / MRT","city bus":"bus kota","intercity coach":"bus antarkota","EasyCard":"EasyCard","iPASS (transit card)":"iPASS (kartu transit)","to top up / add value":"mengisi ulang saldo","to transfer (between lines/modes)":"berpindah (antar jalur/moda)","priority seat":"kursi prioritas","service frequency / departures":"frekuensi layanan / keberangkatan","public bike-share (YouBike)":"sepeda berbagi umum (YouBike)","The \"EasyCard\" was originally created for the Taipei Metro and the \"iPASS\" centered on Kaohsiung, but the two are now widely interoperable—either one lets you ride most transport nationwide. The HSR also offers non-reserved seats, so you can hop on the same day. YouBike has evolved from the early \"YouBike 1.0\" to the easier-to-use \"YouBike 2.0.\" One notable thing: on Taiwan's trains and buses there's a strong ethic of yielding priority seats to those who need them, so these seats often stay empty even in crowds. Travelers who buy one transit card will find getting around suddenly much easier.":"\"EasyCard\" semula diciptakan untuk MRT Taipei dan \"iPASS\" berpusat di Kaohsiung, tetapi keduanya kini saling terhubung luas—salah satunya memungkinkan Anda menaiki sebagian besar transportasi di seluruh negeri. HSR juga menyediakan kursi tanpa pesan, jadi Anda bisa langsung naik di hari yang sama. YouBike telah berkembang dari \"YouBike 1.0\" awal menjadi \"YouBike 2.0\" yang lebih mudah dipakai. Satu hal penting: di kereta dan bus Taiwan ada etika kuat untuk merelakan kursi prioritas bagi yang membutuhkan, sehingga kursi ini sering tetap kosong bahkan saat ramai. Wisatawan yang membeli satu kartu transit akan merasa berkeliling tiba-tiba jauh lebih mudah.","Festivals & Belief":"Festival & Kepercayaan","Mid-Autumn BBQ: One Family Grills, the Whole Street Smells Great":"BBQ Pertengahan Musim Gugur: Satu Keluarga Membakar, Seluruh Jalan Wangi","Mid-Autumn is traditionally about moon-gazing, mooncakes, and pomelos. But in Taiwan, on the night of the 15th of the 8th lunar month, the whole city fills with the smell of charcoal and barbecue sauce. Balconies, rooftops, parks—everyone is grilling. Behind this curious scene lies a surprising reason.":"Pertengahan Musim Gugur secara tradisional tentang memandang bulan, kue bulan, dan jeruk bali. Namun di Taiwan, pada malam tanggal 15 bulan 8 kalender lunar, seluruh kota dipenuhi aroma arang dan saus bakaran. Balkon, atap, taman—semua orang sedang membakar. Di balik pemandangan ganjil ini tersimpan alasan yang mengejutkan.","The Mid-Autumn Festival was originally a holiday for admiring the moon and eating mooncakes and pomelos. In Taiwan, though, when Mid-Autumn arrives, the most important activity for every household is actually barbecuing. On the night of the 15th of the 8th lunar month, walk through the alleys of a residential neighborhood and the smell of charcoal and barbecue sauce drifts from every direction. Balconies, rooftops, parks, riverbanks—everywhere you look, people are gathered around a grill. The scene amazes many foreigners spending their first Mid-Autumn in Taiwan.":"Festival Pertengahan Musim Gugur semula adalah hari raya untuk mengagumi bulan serta menyantap kue bulan dan jeruk bali. Namun di Taiwan, ketika Pertengahan Musim Gugur tiba, kegiatan terpenting bagi setiap rumah tangga justru membakar sate. Pada malam tanggal 15 bulan 8 kalender lunar, berjalanlah menyusuri gang-gang permukiman dan aroma arang serta saus bakaran menyebar dari segala arah. Balkon, atap, taman, tepi sungai—ke mana pun Anda memandang, orang berkumpul di sekitar panggangan. Pemandangan ini membuat banyak orang asing yang merayakan Pertengahan Musim Gugur pertama mereka di Taiwan takjub.","Why do Taiwanese barbecue at Mid-Autumn? The custom isn't actually that old. One story goes that around the 1980s, a barbecue-sauce company ran an ad whose slogan—\"one family grills, the whole street smells great\"—stuck deep in people's minds. Add that Mid-Autumn is exactly when families reunite and the weather starts to cool, and barbecuing—hands-on, chatting while you grill—gradually became a nationwide habit. A single advertising line created a festival culture: rare even by world standards.":"Mengapa orang Taiwan membakar sate saat Pertengahan Musim Gugur? Kebiasaan ini sebenarnya tak sekuno itu. Menurut satu cerita, sekitar tahun 1980-an, sebuah perusahaan saus bakaran menayangkan iklan yang slogannya—\"satu keluarga membakar, seluruh jalan wangi\"—tertanam dalam benak orang. Ditambah Pertengahan Musim Gugur tepat saat keluarga berkumpul dan cuaca mulai sejuk, membakar sate—turun tangan sendiri, mengobrol sambil memanggang—perlahan menjadi kebiasaan nasional. Satu baris iklan menciptakan budaya festival: langka bahkan menurut standar dunia.","At a Taiwanese Mid-Autumn barbecue, the point isn't only the eating—it's the togetherness. The spread is usually generous: sausages, chicken wings, corn, clams, sliced bread, and the must-haves, pork jowl and pork belly. Everyone pitches in—someone starts the fire, someone brushes on sauce, someone watches the food—while kids play with sparklers nearby and adults chat over beer. The very process of grilling is part of the reunion.":"Dalam bakaran Pertengahan Musim Gugur ala Taiwan, intinya bukan hanya makan—melainkan kebersamaan. Sajiannya biasanya melimpah: sosis, sayap ayam, jagung, kerang, roti tawar, dan yang wajib ada, pipi babi dan perut babi. Semua ikut membantu—ada yang menyalakan api, ada yang mengoleskan saus, ada yang menjaga makanan—sementara anak-anak bermain kembang api di dekatnya dan orang dewasa mengobrol sambil menikmati bir. Proses membakar itu sendiri adalah bagian dari reuni.","Beyond the grilling, Mid-Autumn keeps its traditional side too. The table usually holds mooncakes and pomelos. Mooncakes come in many kinds, from Cantonese salted-egg-yolk lotus paste to Taiwanese mung-bean pastry, sweet and savory alike. The pomelo is the season's fruit; after eating it, turning the thick rind into a hat to wear on your head is a childhood memory for many Taiwanese. Moon-gazing, pomelos, barbecue—old and new blend together naturally.":"Selain membakar, Pertengahan Musim Gugur tetap mempertahankan sisi tradisionalnya. Meja biasanya berisi kue bulan dan jeruk bali. Kue bulan hadir dalam banyak jenis, dari pasta teratai kuning telur asin ala Kanton hingga kue kacang hijau ala Taiwan, manis maupun gurih. Jeruk bali adalah buah musim ini; setelah memakannya, mengubah kulitnya yang tebal menjadi topi untuk dikenakan di kepala adalah kenangan masa kecil bagi banyak orang Taiwan. Memandang bulan, jeruk bali, bakaran—yang lama dan yang baru berpadu secara alami.","For foreigners living in Taiwan, Mid-Autumn is a festival where you're easily invited and easily make friends. If a coworker or neighbor asks, \"Want to barbecue together for Mid-Autumn?\"—that's practically them treating you as one of their own. Bring a pack of beer or some food, take a seat by the grill, and you'll discover that Taiwanese warmth is hidden right there in the smoke and the aroma.":"Bagi orang asing yang tinggal di Taiwan, Pertengahan Musim Gugur adalah festival di mana Anda mudah diundang dan mudah berteman. Jika seorang rekan kerja atau tetangga bertanya, \"Mau membakar sate bersama untuk Pertengahan Musim Gugur?\"—itu praktis berarti mereka menganggap Anda bagian dari mereka. Bawalah sekaleng bir atau sedikit makanan, duduklah di dekat panggangan, dan Anda akan menemukan bahwa kehangatan orang Taiwan tersembunyi tepat di dalam asap dan aromanya.","barbecue; to grill meat":"membakar sate; memanggang daging","to admire the moon":"mengagumi bulan","mooncake":"kue bulan","pomelo":"jeruk bali","family reunion":"reuni keluarga","sausage":"sosis","charcoal fire":"api arang","\"One family grills, the whole street smells great\" began as a barbecue-sauce ad slogan. The distinctly Taiwanese equation of Mid-Autumn with barbecue is actually a relatively new culture that spread over just a few decades—a fascinating example of commerce fusing with tradition to create a new custom.":"\"Satu keluarga membakar, seluruh jalan wangi\" bermula sebagai slogan iklan saus bakaran. Penyamaan Pertengahan Musim Gugur dengan bakaran yang khas Taiwan ini sebenarnya budaya yang relatif baru, menyebar hanya dalam beberapa dekade—contoh menarik tentang perdagangan yang berpadu dengan tradisi untuk menciptakan kebiasaan baru.","Food":"Makanan","Hot Pot: The Cozy Ritual You Crave the Moment It Turns Cold":"Hot Pot: Ritual Hangat yang Anda Dambakan Begitu Cuaca Mendingin","In Taiwan, the moment it turns cold, hot pot restaurants fill with lines. You gather around a pot in the middle, cook meat and vegetables as you eat, and chat as you go—one meal can last two or three hours. From mala to single-person pots, let's look inside Taiwan's hot pot culture.":"Di Taiwan, begitu cuaca mendingin, restoran hot pot langsung dipenuhi antrean. Anda berkumpul mengelilingi panci di tengah, memasak daging dan sayur sambil makan, dan mengobrol sepanjang jalan—satu kali makan bisa berlangsung dua atau tiga jam. Dari mala hingga panci perorangan, mari kita intip budaya hot pot Taiwan.","In Taiwan, the moment it gets a little cold, hot pot restaurants form long lines. Hot pot is one of Taiwanese people's favorite ways to eat together: a pot of hot broth sits in the middle of the table, and everyone adds sliced meat, vegetables, meatballs, and tofu piece by piece to cook—cooking while eating, eating while chatting, with one meal often stretching two or three hours. The colder it is, the better hot pot tastes, and that steaming scene is the very flavor of a Taiwanese winter.":"Di Taiwan, begitu cuaca sedikit dingin, restoran hot pot langsung mengular antreannya. Hot pot adalah salah satu cara makan bersama favorit orang Taiwan: sepanci kaldu panas berada di tengah meja, dan semua orang memasukkan irisan daging, sayur, bakso, dan tahu satu per satu untuk dimasak—memasak sambil makan, makan sambil mengobrol, dengan satu kali makan sering membentang dua atau tiga jam. Semakin dingin, semakin lezat hot pot terasa, dan pemandangan mengepul itulah cita rasa musim dingin Taiwan.","Taiwan's hot pots come in a dizzying variety. Common ones include the light kombu (kelp) pot, the health-boosting herbal pot, and the love-it-and-fear-it mala pot. The mala pot is usually a \"mandarin-duck pot\"—half spicy mala, half clear broth—so even people who can't take heat can join in. There's also tangy-spicy kimchi pot and rich cheese-milk pot, and every restaurant has its own signature broth.":"Hot pot Taiwan hadir dalam ragam yang memusingkan. Yang umum meliputi panci kombu (rumput laut) yang ringan, panci herbal yang menyehatkan, dan panci mala yang dicintai sekaligus ditakuti. Panci mala biasanya berupa \"panci bebek mandarin\"—separuh mala pedas, separuh kaldu bening—sehingga bahkan orang yang tak tahan pedas pun bisa ikut. Ada juga panci kimchi yang asam-pedas dan panci keju-susu yang gurih, dan setiap restoran punya kaldu andalannya sendiri.","Taiwanese hot pot has another very distinctive culture: the single-person pot. Many restaurants offer individual small hot pots—one little pot in front of each person, with your own portion of broth, meat, and vegetables, so there's no fighting over food and no worrying about hygiene. This solo hot pot is hugely popular in Taiwan; you can enjoy hot pot alone with total ease, which is especially welcoming for foreigners not used to sharing one pot with everyone.":"Hot pot Taiwan punya budaya khas lain yang sangat menonjol: panci perorangan. Banyak restoran menawarkan hot pot kecil individual—satu panci mungil di depan setiap orang, dengan porsi kaldu, daging, dan sayur milik Anda sendiri, sehingga tak ada rebutan makanan dan tak perlu khawatir kebersihan. Hot pot solo ini sangat populer di Taiwan; Anda bisa menikmati hot pot sendirian dengan santai, yang terasa sangat ramah bagi orang asing yang belum terbiasa berbagi satu panci dengan semua orang.","Half the fun of hot pot lies in the add-ins and the dipping sauce. Taiwanese diners often mix their own sauce: soy sauce, shacha sauce, minced garlic, chopped scallion, chili—and among them, shacha sauce is the soul of the most Taiwanese flavor. Many places also offer free all-you-can-eat rice, drinks, and ice cream. At the very end, adding rice or noodles to the leftover broth to make congee or a noodle soup is the perfect finish that only true food lovers know.":"Separuh keseruan hot pot terletak pada bahan tambahan dan saus celupnya. Penikmat Taiwan sering meracik sausnya sendiri: kecap asin, saus shacha, bawang putih cincang, daun bawang, cabai—dan di antaranya, saus shacha adalah jiwa dari cita rasa paling khas Taiwan. Banyak tempat juga menyediakan nasi, minuman, dan es krim sepuasnya secara gratis. Di akhir, menambahkan nasi atau mi ke sisa kaldu untuk dijadikan bubur atau sup mi adalah penutup sempurna yang hanya diketahui para pecinta makanan sejati.","For Taiwanese people, hot pot is more than food—it's the warmth of being together. Whether it's family gathered around the pot for New Year, a friend's birthday, or a coworkers' get-together, hot pot is the safest choice. Because when you circle the same pot of hot broth, everyone's distance naturally shrinks. Next time it turns cold, why not round up a few friends and go share a steaming hot pot together?":"Bagi orang Taiwan, hot pot lebih dari sekadar makanan—ia adalah kehangatan kebersamaan. Entah itu keluarga berkumpul mengelilingi panci saat Tahun Baru, ulang tahun teman, atau acara kumpul rekan kerja, hot pot adalah pilihan paling aman. Sebab ketika mengelilingi panci kaldu panas yang sama, jarak antar semua orang secara alami menyusut. Lain kali saat cuaca mendingin, mengapa tak mengajak beberapa teman untuk berbagi hot pot mengepul bersama?","soup base / broth":"kaldu dasar / kuah","numbing-spicy (mala)":"pedas-kebas (mala)","split (dual-broth) pot":"panci sekat (dua kaldu)","shacha sauce":"saus shacha","dipping sauce":"saus celup","to gather around the pot":"berkumpul mengelilingi panci","Shacha sauce is an essential hot-pot dip in Taiwan, with a distinctive umami from dried shrimp and fish. The single-person pot is a uniquely Taiwanese style that lets you enjoy hot pot even on your own.":"Saus shacha adalah saus celup hot pot yang esensial di Taiwan, dengan umami khas dari udang dan ikan kering. Panci perorangan adalah gaya khas Taiwan yang memungkinkan Anda menikmati hot pot bahkan seorang diri.","Life & Culture":"Kehidupan & Budaya","Typhoon Days: The One News Update All of Taiwan Waits For":"Hari Topan: Satu Kabar Berita yang Ditunggu Seluruh Taiwan","Summer to autumn is Taiwan's typhoon season. When a strong typhoon nears, all of Taiwan fixates on one question: \"Will there be a typhoon day off tomorrow?\" People watch the news and wait for each city and county to announce. Let's look at this uniquely Taiwanese \"waiting for the day off\" culture.":"Musim panas hingga musim gugur adalah musim topan Taiwan. Ketika topan kuat mendekat, seluruh Taiwan terpaku pada satu pertanyaan: \"Apakah besok ada libur karena topan?\" Orang-orang menonton berita dan menunggu setiap kota dan kabupaten mengumumkannya. Mari kita lihat budaya \"menunggu hari libur\" yang khas Taiwan ini.","Every year from summer to autumn is Taiwan's typhoon season. When a strong typhoon approaches, all of Taiwan cares about one thing: \"Will there really be a typhoon day off tomorrow?\" On that day, people stare intently at the news and their phones, waiting for each city and county government to announce whether work and school are canceled tomorrow. That anxious-yet-hopeful feeling of waiting for the day-off announcement is a shared memory for many Taiwanese.":"Setiap tahun dari musim panas hingga musim gugur adalah musim topan Taiwan. Ketika topan kuat mendekat, seluruh Taiwan peduli pada satu hal: \"Apakah besok benar-benar ada libur karena topan?\" Pada hari itu, orang-orang menatap lekat berita dan ponsel mereka, menunggu pemerintah setiap kota dan kabupaten mengumumkan apakah kerja dan sekolah diliburkan besok. Perasaan cemas namun penuh harap menanti pengumuman libur itu adalah kenangan bersama bagi banyak orang Taiwan.","Whether to call a typhoon day off is decided by each city and county government, with criteria tied to wind speed and rainfall. Because conditions differ by locality, amusing scenes sometimes arise: this county gets the day off while the county next door still has to work, and people living on the border feel especially envious—or grumble. The mayors and magistrates who make the call often end up in the news for calling it \"too early\" or for \"not calling it when they should have,\" and the pressure is genuinely considerable.":"Keputusan meliburkan karena topan ditetapkan oleh masing-masing pemerintah kota dan kabupaten, dengan kriteria yang terkait kecepatan angin dan curah hujan. Karena kondisi berbeda tiap daerah, kadang muncul pemandangan lucu: kabupaten ini libur sementara kabupaten sebelah masih harus bekerja, dan orang yang tinggal di perbatasan merasa sangat iri—atau menggerutu. Para wali kota dan bupati yang mengambil keputusan sering masuk berita karena mengumumkannya \"terlalu dini\" atau karena \"tidak meliburkan padahal seharusnya\", dan tekanannya sungguh besar.","Although a typhoon day is a \"day off,\" it isn't for playing. On typhoon days the wind and rain are fierce and going out is dangerous; the government wants everyone to shelter at home. The ideal typhoon day means stocking up on food, instant noodles, and water in advance, shutting doors and windows tight, and staying home to binge shows, sleep, and be with family. The real veterans know: the worst thing to do on a typhoon day is head to the coast to watch the waves, or play in a mountain stream.":"Meski hari topan adalah \"hari libur\", ia bukan untuk bermain. Pada hari topan angin dan hujan ganas dan keluar rumah berbahaya; pemerintah ingin semua orang berlindung di rumah. Hari topan yang ideal berarti menimbun makanan, mi instan, dan air sebelumnya, menutup rapat pintu dan jendela, dan tinggal di rumah untuk maraton tontonan, tidur, dan berkumpul dengan keluarga. Para veteran sejati tahu: hal terbodoh yang bisa dilakukan pada hari topan adalah pergi ke pantai menonton ombak, atau bermain di sungai pegunungan.","For office workers and students, a typhoon day is like a gift dropped from the sky: a day that was supposed to mean work or school suddenly becomes a day to rest at home. Social media instantly fills with typhoon-day posts—some celebrating, others wailing because \"the typhoon veered off and the day off vanished.\" This feeling of the whole nation waiting together for one news update, rejoicing or despairing together, is a collective experience unique to Taiwan.":"Bagi pekerja kantoran dan pelajar, hari topan bagai hadiah yang jatuh dari langit: hari yang seharusnya berarti kerja atau sekolah tiba-tiba menjadi hari beristirahat di rumah. Media sosial seketika dipenuhi unggahan hari topan—ada yang merayakan, ada yang meratap karena \"topannya berbelok dan liburnya lenyap\". Perasaan seluruh bangsa menunggu bersama satu kabar berita, bersuka atau berduka bersama, adalah pengalaman kolektif yang khas Taiwan.","For newcomers to Taiwan, your first typhoon day can be a bit hectic. A few small tips: stock up at the supermarket before the typhoon arrives (shelves are often bought bare); remember to charge your phone; and keep an eye on each city and county government's announcements. As long as you're prepared, a typhoon day is actually a rare chance to rest well and feel Taiwan's \"we're all in this together on one island\" spirit.":"Bagi pendatang baru di Taiwan, hari topan pertama Anda bisa sedikit kalang kabut. Beberapa tips kecil: berbelanja di supermarket sebelum topan tiba (raknya sering diborong habis); jangan lupa mengisi daya ponsel; dan pantau pengumuman masing-masing pemerintah kota dan kabupaten. Asalkan Anda bersiap, hari topan sebenarnya kesempatan langka untuk beristirahat dengan baik dan merasakan semangat \"kita semua senasib di satu pulau\" khas Taiwan.","to have a day off":"mendapat libur","wind speed":"kecepatan angin","rainfall":"curah hujan","to take shelter":"berlindung","to restock; stock up":"menimbun; menyetok","official announcement":"pengumuman resmi","Typhoon days are decided by each city and county, so they vary by area. Before a strong typhoon, stock up on water, food, and a power bank. As a note, every year someone makes the news for going \"rafting\" in a swollen typhoon river—absolutely never copy that.":"Hari libur topan ditetapkan oleh masing-masing kota dan kabupaten, jadi berbeda-beda menurut daerah. Sebelum topan kuat, timbunlah air, makanan, dan power bank. Sebagai catatan, setiap tahun ada saja yang masuk berita karena \"berarung jeram\" di sungai topan yang meluap—jangan sekali-kali menirunya.","Dragon Boat Festival: Zongzi, Dragon Boats, and Standing Eggs":"Festival Perahu Naga: Zongzi, Perahu Naga, dan Menegakkan Telur","The 5th day of the 5th lunar month is the Dragon Boat Festival. People eat zongzi, race dragon boats, and stand eggs upright at noon. Let's look at one of Taiwan's three biggest festivals up close.":"Tanggal 5 bulan 5 kalender lunar adalah Festival Perahu Naga. Orang menyantap zongzi, mengadu perahu naga, dan menegakkan telur pada tengah hari. Mari kita amati dari dekat salah satu dari tiga festival terbesar Taiwan.","The 5th day of the 5th lunar month is the Dragon Boat Festival, one of Taiwan's three biggest holidays. On this day every household eats zongzi—sticky rice wrapped in bamboo leaves, stuffed with pork, shiitake mushrooms, salted egg yolk, peanuts and more, tied with string and steamed or boiled. As the festival nears, many families wrap their own, or receive strings of zongzi from elders and neighbors. That scent of bamboo leaves and glutinous rice is the very taste of the festival.":"Tanggal 5 bulan 5 kalender lunar adalah Festival Perahu Naga, salah satu dari tiga hari raya terbesar Taiwan. Pada hari ini setiap rumah tangga menyantap zongzi—ketan yang dibungkus daun bambu, diisi daging babi, jamur shiitake, kuning telur asin, kacang tanah, dan lainnya, diikat tali lalu dikukus atau direbus. Menjelang festival, banyak keluarga membungkusnya sendiri, atau menerima untaian zongzi dari orang tua dan tetangga. Aroma daun bambu dan ketan itulah cita rasa festival ini.","The festival's main spectacle is dragon boat racing. On rivers and coasts, long dragon boats fill with rowers who paddle in unison to the beat of a drum, while someone at the bow reaches to grab the finish-line flag. Crowds pack the banks cheering, gongs and drums thundering—it's tremendously lively. The custom traces to an ancient legend, said to commemorate the poet Qu Yuan, who threw himself into a river.":"Tontonan utama festival ini adalah balapan perahu naga. Di sungai dan pantai, perahu naga panjang penuh dengan pendayung yang mengayuh serempak mengikuti tabuhan genderang, sementara seseorang di haluan menjulur meraih bendera garis finis. Kerumunan memadati tepian sambil bersorak, gong dan genderang menggelegar—sangat meriah. Tradisi ini berakar pada legenda kuno, konon untuk mengenang penyair Qu Yuan, yang menceburkan diri ke sungai.","Besides zongzi and dragon boats, the festival has a delightful little activity: standing eggs upright. Legend says that at exactly noon on this day, some mysterious force makes eggs easier to balance. So at midday, many kids and adults crouch on the ground, carefully trying to stand an egg on a table or the floor. When it works, everyone cheers happily. It's really just a fun game, yet it's full of festive joy.":"Selain zongzi dan perahu naga, festival ini punya kegiatan kecil yang menyenangkan: menegakkan telur. Legenda mengatakan bahwa tepat tengah hari pada hari ini, ada kekuatan misterius yang membuat telur lebih mudah berdiri seimbang. Maka pada siang hari, banyak anak dan orang dewasa berjongkok di tanah, dengan hati-hati mencoba menegakkan telur di atas meja atau lantai. Ketika berhasil, semua orang bersorak gembira. Sebenarnya hanya permainan seru, tetapi penuh sukacita perayaan.","The festival falls right at the start of summer, as the heat sets in—a time the ancients saw as a \"poison month\" when illness spreads and insects and snakes appear. So the festival is also full of customs to ward off evil and poison: mugwort and calamus hung by the door, children wearing scented sachets, and in some places drinking realgar wine. Behind these customs lies the old wish for the whole family to stay safe and healthy through the hot season.":"Festival ini jatuh tepat di awal musim panas, saat hawa panas mulai—masa yang oleh orang zaman dulu dianggap \"bulan racun\" ketika penyakit menyebar dan serangga serta ular bermunculan. Maka festival ini juga penuh tradisi menangkal roh jahat dan racun: daun baru cina dan jerangau digantung di pintu, anak-anak mengenakan kantong wangi, dan di beberapa tempat orang meminum arak realgar. Di balik tradisi ini tersimpan harapan lama agar seluruh keluarga tetap selamat dan sehat sepanjang musim panas.","For foreigners, the festival is a great chance to get to know Taiwan's traditional culture. You can watch a dragon boat race by the river and feel the whole crowd shouting together, or buy a few zongzi of different styles to compare—southern-style, northern-style, even the sweet alkaline zongzi eaten dipped in sugar. And at noon, don't forget to try standing an egg—you just might be this year's luckiest person.":"Bagi orang asing, festival ini kesempatan bagus untuk mengenal budaya tradisional Taiwan. Anda bisa menonton balapan perahu naga di tepi sungai dan merasakan seluruh kerumunan bersorak bersama, atau membeli beberapa zongzi dengan gaya berbeda untuk dibandingkan—gaya selatan, gaya utara, bahkan zongzi alkali manis yang disantap dengan cocolan gula. Dan pada tengah hari, jangan lupa mencoba menegakkan telur—siapa tahu Anda orang paling beruntung tahun ini.","Dragon Boat Festival":"Festival Perahu Naga","zongzi (sticky rice dumpling)":"zongzi (bakcang, ketan bungkus)","dragon boat":"perahu naga","glutinous rice":"ketan","standing an egg upright":"menegakkan telur","scented sachet":"kantong wangi","to ward off evil":"menangkal roh jahat","Zongzi vary by region: southern-style is boiled with the raw rice for a softer texture, while northern-style is stir-fried first and steamed, giving firmer grains. Standing eggs at noon has no scientific basis, but it's a fun family tradition of the season.":"Zongzi berbeda-beda menurut wilayah: gaya selatan direbus bersama beras mentahnya sehingga teksturnya lebih lembut, sedangkan gaya utara ditumis dulu lalu dikukus, membuat butirannya lebih kenyal. Menegakkan telur pada tengah hari tak berdasar ilmiah, tetapi merupakan tradisi keluarga yang seru di musim ini.","The Traditional Market: Taiwan's Kitchen and Its Warmth":"Pasar Tradisional: Dapur Taiwan dan Kehangatannya","Beyond supermarkets and convenience stores, Taiwan has the lively traditional market. Fresh, cheap, open to haggling, and full of street food—let's look at the human warmth a cold supermarket can't offer.":"Selain supermarket dan toko swalayan, Taiwan punya pasar tradisional yang semarak. Segar, murah, bisa ditawar, dan penuh jajanan kaki lima—mari kita lihat kehangatan manusiawi yang tak bisa ditawarkan supermarket yang dingin.","In Taiwan, beyond supermarkets and convenience stores, there's a place bursting with life: the traditional market. In the early morning it hums with voices—vegetable sellers, fishmongers, butchers one after another, produce piled like little hills, vendors calling out today's prices. The goods are fresh and usually cheaper than at the supermarket, making it where many Taiwanese families shop every day.":"Di Taiwan, selain supermarket dan toko swalayan, ada tempat yang berdenyut penuh kehidupan: pasar tradisional. Pada pagi buta ia berdengung dengan suara—penjual sayur, penjual ikan, penjual daging silih berganti, dagangan bertumpuk seperti bukit-bukit kecil, para pedagang meneriakkan harga hari ini. Barang-barangnya segar dan biasanya lebih murah daripada di supermarket, menjadikannya tempat banyak keluarga Taiwan berbelanja setiap hari.","The best part of wandering the market is the human warmth. At a traditional market you can often haggle or chat a few words with the vendor. The aunties buying vegetables and the fishmonger big brother often all know one another—some even know what your family likes to eat. Sometimes the vendor tosses in an extra bunch of scallions or a bit of ginger, saying, \"This one's on me—go home and cook!\" That warmth between people is something a cold supermarket just can't give.":"Bagian terbaik menyusuri pasar adalah kehangatan manusiawinya. Di pasar tradisional Anda sering bisa menawar atau mengobrol beberapa patah kata dengan pedagang. Para ibu yang membeli sayur dan abang penjual ikan sering saling kenal—beberapa bahkan tahu apa kesukaan makan keluarga Anda. Kadang pedagang menyelipkan seikat daun bawang atau sedikit jahe tambahan sambil berkata, \"Yang ini gratis—pulang dan masaklah!\" Kehangatan antar sesama itu adalah sesuatu yang tak bisa diberikan supermarket yang dingin.","A Taiwanese market isn't only for vegetables. Tucked inside are all kinds of delicious snacks: freshly made scallion pancakes, piping-hot bawan (meatball dumplings), just-fried doughnuts, and every sort of prepared food and braised delicacies. Many people run their morning errands and eat breakfast right there in the market. For a food lover, browsing the market is itself a culinary adventure.":"Pasar Taiwan tak hanya untuk sayur. Terselip di dalamnya beragam jajanan lezat: panekuk daun bawang yang baru dibuat, bawan (pangsit bakso) yang mengepul panas, donat yang baru digoreng, serta segala macam makanan siap saji dan hidangan kecap. Banyak orang menuntaskan urusan pagi mereka sekaligus sarapan langsung di pasar. Bagi pecinta makanan, menyusuri pasar itu sendiri adalah petualangan kuliner.","Beyond the morning market, Taiwan also has evening markets and night markets. The evening market opens at dusk, convenient for people shopping after work, while the night market leans more toward street food and fun. Markets at different times serve people on different schedules, making \"buying groceries\" wonderfully flexible. Whatever you crave, whenever you go, there's always somewhere to browse.":"Selain pasar pagi, Taiwan juga punya pasar sore dan pasar malam. Pasar sore buka saat senja, praktis bagi orang yang berbelanja sepulang kerja, sementara pasar malam lebih condong ke jajanan kaki lima dan hiburan. Pasar pada waktu berbeda melayani orang dengan jadwal berbeda, membuat \"belanja bahan makanan\" jadi sangat fleksibel. Apa pun yang Anda idamkan, kapan pun Anda pergi, selalu ada tempat untuk menyusuri.","For newcomers to Taiwan, the market may feel a little loud and crowded, but it's actually the fastest way to get to know Taiwanese life. Learn a few simple phrases like \"How much is this?\" and \"Give me a better price!\" and you can weave among the stalls like a local. And when a vendor smiles and slips you an extra bunch of scallions, you'll have truly tasted Taiwan's human warmth.":"Bagi pendatang baru di Taiwan, pasar mungkin terasa sedikit berisik dan sesak, tetapi sebenarnya itu cara tercepat mengenal kehidupan Taiwan. Pelajari beberapa frasa sederhana seperti \"Ini berapa harganya?\" dan \"Kasih harga lebih murah dong!\" dan Anda bisa menyelinap di antara lapak seperti warga lokal. Dan ketika seorang pedagang tersenyum dan menyelipkan seikat daun bawang tambahan untuk Anda, Anda benar-benar telah mencicipi kehangatan manusiawi Taiwan.","traditional market":"pasar tradisional","vendor; street stall":"pedagang; lapak","to haggle over the price":"menawar harga","human warmth; kindness":"kehangatan manusiawi; kebaikan","to hawk; call out":"menjajakan; berteriak menawarkan","to shop for groceries":"berbelanja bahan makanan","\"How much is this?\" is the phrase you'll use most at a market. Haggling is normal at traditional markets but not at supermarkets or chains. Market food is mostly cash-only, so having small bills and coins makes things smooth.":"\"Ini berapa harganya?\" adalah frasa yang paling sering Anda gunakan di pasar. Menawar itu lumrah di pasar tradisional tetapi tidak di supermarket atau toko waralaba. Makanan pasar kebanyakan hanya menerima tunai, jadi memiliki uang kecil dan koin membuat semuanya lancar.","When the Ground Shakes: Living on a Trembling Island":"Ketika Tanah Berguncang: Hidup di Pulau yang Bergetar","Taiwan sits on a plate boundary—an island of frequent earthquakes. Sooner or later you'll feel one. Let's look at why Taiwanese stay calm, the preparation behind it, and how to protect yourself when it counts.":"Taiwan berada di batas lempeng—pulau yang sering gempa. Cepat atau lambat Anda akan merasakannya. Mari kita lihat mengapa orang Taiwan tetap tenang, persiapan di baliknya, dan cara melindungi diri saat genting.","Taiwan sits at the boundary of tectonic plates, an island with many earthquakes. Live here and sooner or later you'll feel one—maybe a gentle sway, maybe a big quake that rocks the whole building. For Taiwanese, small quakes are almost part of daily life; many just keep doing what they're doing after a shake, calmly remarking, \"Oh, earthquake.\"":"Taiwan terletak di batas lempeng tektonik, pulau dengan banyak gempa. Tinggallah di sini dan cepat atau lambat Anda akan merasakannya—mungkin ayunan lembut, mungkin gempa besar yang mengguncang seluruh gedung. Bagi orang Taiwan, gempa kecil nyaris bagian dari kehidupan sehari-hari; banyak yang tetap melanjutkan aktivitasnya setelah guncangan, dengan tenang berkomentar, \"Oh, gempa.\"","Taiwanese may look calm, but that calm comes from preparation. Buildings follow strict earthquake-resistance codes, schools run earthquake drills every year, and phones blast a \"national alert\" a few seconds before strong shaking arrives. Those few seconds are short, but they may give you just enough time to get somewhere safe.":"Orang Taiwan mungkin tampak tenang, tetapi ketenangan itu berasal dari persiapan. Bangunan mengikuti kode tahan gempa yang ketat, sekolah mengadakan latihan gempa setiap tahun, dan ponsel memekikkan \"peringatan nasional\" beberapa detik sebelum guncangan kuat tiba. Beberapa detik itu memang singkat, tetapi bisa memberi Anda cukup waktu untuk mencapai tempat aman.","When an earthquake hits, the key mantra is \"Drop, Cover, Hold On.\" Drop to the floor, take cover under a sturdy table, protect your head and neck with your hands, grip a table leg to steady yourself, and wait for the shaking to stop. Don't rush outside, and don't stand near windows or large furniture. Once it's over, calmly check the gas, switch off the power, and if needed evacuate to an open area.":"Ketika gempa terjadi, mantra utamanya adalah \"Merunduk, Berlindung, Berpegangan\". Merunduklah ke lantai, berlindung di bawah meja yang kokoh, lindungi kepala dan leher dengan tangan, cengkeram kaki meja untuk menstabilkan diri, dan tunggu sampai guncangan berhenti. Jangan buru-buru keluar, dan jangan berdiri dekat jendela atau perabot besar. Setelah usai, periksa gas dengan tenang, matikan listrik, dan bila perlu mengungsi ke area terbuka.","Everyday preparation matters too. Many Taiwanese families keep an \"earthquake bag\" with a flashlight, water, dry food, a power bank, everyday medicine, and a little cash. Secure furniture to the wall, and don't put heavy things up high. You won't use this preparation most of the time, but in a real major quake it could be the key to protecting yourself and your family.":"Persiapan sehari-hari juga penting. Banyak keluarga Taiwan menyimpan \"tas gempa\" berisi senter, air, makanan kering, power bank, obat sehari-hari, dan sedikit uang tunai. Kokohkan perabot ke dinding, dan jangan letakkan benda berat di tempat tinggi. Sebagian besar waktu Anda tak akan memakai persiapan ini, tetapi dalam gempa besar yang sungguhan, ia bisa menjadi kunci untuk melindungi diri dan keluarga Anda.","For foreigners, feeling your first earthquake in Taiwan can be very nerve-wracking—and that's completely normal. Start by turning on your phone's earthquake alert, memorize \"Drop, Cover, Hold On,\" and know the shelter points near your home. Earthquakes can't be predicted, but with preparation and a cool head, you can greatly reduce the danger. Living on this trembling island and learning to coexist with earthquakes is part of getting to know Taiwan too.":"Bagi orang asing, merasakan gempa pertama Anda di Taiwan bisa sangat menegangkan—dan itu sepenuhnya wajar. Mulailah dengan mengaktifkan peringatan gempa di ponsel Anda, hafalkan \"Merunduk, Berlindung, Berpegangan\", dan ketahui titik-titik perlindungan dekat rumah Anda. Gempa tak bisa diprediksi, tetapi dengan persiapan dan kepala yang dingin, Anda bisa sangat mengurangi bahaya. Hidup di pulau yang bergetar ini dan belajar berdampingan dengan gempa juga bagian dari mengenal Taiwan.","to shake; sway":"berguncang; bergoyang","earthquake-resistant":"tahan gempa","alert; alarm":"peringatan; alarm","to take cover; shield":"berlindung; melindungi","drill; exercise":"latihan; simulasi","calm; composed":"tenang; kalem","\"Drop, Cover, Hold On\" is the universal basic response during a quake. In Taiwan, the phone's \"national alert\" (early earthquake warning) is on by default. Preparing an earthquake bag and securing your furniture early after you move in brings real peace of mind.":"\"Merunduk, Berlindung, Berpegangan\" adalah respons dasar universal saat gempa. Di Taiwan, \"peringatan nasional\" (peringatan dini gempa) di ponsel aktif secara bawaan. Menyiapkan tas gempa dan mengokohkan perabot Anda sejak awal setelah pindah membawa ketenangan hati yang nyata.","The Lantern Festival: Sky Lanterns, Beehive Fireworks, and a Bowl of Sweet Dumplings":"Festival Lampion: Lampion Langit, Kembang Api Sarang Lebah, dan Semangkuk Onde Manis","On the fifteenth day of the first lunar month, Taiwan glows with lantern light. People write wishes on sky lanterns and let them drift into the night, children walk the lanes with paper lanterns, and families simmer sweet rice-ball dumplings at home. Here is that day, seen through the eyes of someone who lives in Taiwan.":"Pada hari kelima belas bulan pertama kalender lunar, Taiwan bermandikan cahaya lampion. Orang menuliskan harapan pada lampion langit dan melepasnya melayang ke malam, anak-anak menyusuri gang-gang membawa lampion kertas, dan keluarga-keluarga merebus onde manis di rumah. Inilah hari itu, dilihat melalui mata orang yang tinggal di Taiwan.","The Lantern Festival falls on the fifteenth day of the first lunar month, and it is also the last day of the Lunar New Year. Only after this day is the New Year truly over, and everyone settles down and returns to ordinary life. That evening, every household cooks a pot of sweet rice-ball dumplings; sweet as they are, eating them stands for reunion and completeness. The streets are full of light, children run about carrying paper lanterns, and the whole city lights up.":"Festival Lampion jatuh pada hari kelima belas bulan pertama kalender lunar, dan juga hari terakhir Tahun Baru Imlek. Baru setelah hari ini Tahun Baru benar-benar usai, dan semua orang kembali tenang ke kehidupan biasa. Malam itu, setiap rumah tangga memasak sepanci onde manis (tangyuan); semanis onde-onde itu, memakannya melambangkan reuni dan kegenapan. Jalanan penuh cahaya, anak-anak berlarian membawa lampion kertas, dan seluruh kota bermandikan cahaya.","When people think of the Lantern Festival, the first thing many picture is the sky lanterns of Pingxi. After dark, everyone writes their heart's wishes on a sky lantern with a brush—some wish for good health, some for exams to go smoothly, and some to be with the person they love. Once the flame is lit, the lantern slowly swells, and the moment you let go it floats upward, rising higher and higher. Look up, and the whole sky is filled with orange-red points of light—a scene so lovely you hate to blink.":"Ketika orang memikirkan Festival Lampion, hal pertama yang banyak dibayangkan adalah lampion langit Pingxi. Setelah gelap, semua orang menuliskan harapan hati mereka pada lampion langit dengan kuas—ada yang berharap kesehatan, ada yang berharap ujian berjalan lancar, dan ada yang berharap bersama orang yang dicintai. Begitu apinya dinyalakan, lampion perlahan menggembung, dan saat Anda melepasnya ia melayang ke atas, kian tinggi. Tengadahlah, dan seluruh langit dipenuhi titik-titik cahaya merah-jingga—pemandangan yang begitu indah hingga Anda enggan berkedip.","If you love a thrill, you have to go to Yanshui in Tainan to see the beehive fireworks. Tens of thousands of bottle rockets fire off at once, so loud your ears nearly go deaf, and the sparks rush at the crowd like a swarm of bees—which is exactly why they're called beehive fireworks. Anyone who wants a close look must put on a helmet and a thick coat, wrapping up tightly from head to toe, or they really will get burned. It is both dangerous and exhilarating, a wild thing many Taiwanese feel they must experience at least once in their lives.":"Jika Anda menyukai sensasi menegangkan, Anda wajib pergi ke Yanshui di Tainan untuk menyaksikan kembang api sarang lebah. Puluhan ribu roket botol meletus sekaligus, begitu bising hingga telinga nyaris tuli, dan percikannya menyerbu kerumunan bagai kawanan lebah—persis itulah alasan mereka disebut kembang api sarang lebah. Siapa pun yang ingin melihat dari dekat harus mengenakan helm dan mantel tebal, membungkus rapat dari kepala hingga kaki, atau mereka benar-benar akan terbakar. Ini berbahaya sekaligus menggetarkan, hal liar yang banyak orang Taiwan rasa harus dialami setidaknya sekali seumur hidup.","Beyond the local events, there is also the large-scale Taiwan Lantern Festival held every year, in a different city each time. Inside are all sorts of decorative lanterns, and the most eye-catching is the main lantern built around that year's zodiac animal—big and beautiful, and at night it glows, turns, and plays music. Besides looking at the lanterns, many people join the temple procession nearby, walking a stretch behind the deity's parade to feel that mix of lively bustle and devotion. The whole family strolling and gazing at lanterns is the simplest kind of happiness.":"Selain acara-acara lokal, ada juga Festival Lampion Taiwan berskala besar yang digelar setiap tahun, di kota yang berbeda tiap kalinya. Di dalamnya terdapat beragam lampion hias, dan yang paling mencuri perhatian adalah lampion utama yang dibuat berdasarkan hewan zodiak tahun itu—besar dan indah, dan di malam hari ia bercahaya, berputar, serta memainkan musik. Selain menikmati lampion, banyak orang ikut arak-arakan kuil di dekatnya, berjalan sejenak di belakang pawai dewa untuk merasakan perpaduan keramaian dan kekhusyukan. Sekeluarga berjalan-jalan sambil memandangi lampion adalah kebahagiaan yang paling sederhana.","Many foreign friends ask what the difference is between Lantern Festival dumplings and winter-solstice dumplings. In fact, winter-solstice ones are mostly small and unfilled, in red and white; the ones eaten at the Lantern Festival are larger, wrapped around sesame or peanut. Besides eating, the Lantern Festival has a delightful tradition called lantern riddles—riddles are written on lanterns for everyone to guess, and a correct answer earns a little prize. Watching children carry their paper lanterns while grown-ups puzzle over the answers beneath the lights, you feel just how warm this festival really is.":"Banyak teman asing bertanya apa beda onde Festival Lampion dan onde titik balik matahari musim dingin. Sebenarnya, yang untuk titik balik musim dingin kebanyakan kecil dan tanpa isi, berwarna merah dan putih; yang disantap saat Festival Lampion lebih besar, dibungkus isian wijen atau kacang. Selain makan, Festival Lampion punya tradisi menyenangkan bernama tebak-tebakan lampion—teka-teki ditulis pada lampion untuk ditebak semua orang, dan jawaban yang benar mendapat hadiah kecil. Menyaksikan anak-anak membawa lampion kertas mereka sementara orang dewasa memutar otak menebak jawaban di bawah cahaya, Anda merasakan betapa hangatnya festival ini sebenarnya.","the lunar calendar":"kalender lunar","the fifteenth day of the first lunar month":"hari kelima belas bulan pertama kalender lunar","sweet glutinous rice-ball dumplings":"onde manis dari ketan (tangyuan)","family reunion; being together":"reuni keluarga; kebersamaan","sky lantern":"lampion langit","a wish; something one hopes for":"harapan; sesuatu yang didambakan","beehive fireworks":"kembang api sarang lebah","lantern festival (large lantern exhibition)":"festival lampion (pameran lampion besar)","a temple deity procession":"arak-arakan dewa kuil","guessing lantern riddles":"menebak teka-teki lampion","A note: at the Lantern Festival, Taiwanese families cook sweet rice-ball dumplings, and children walk about carrying paper lanterns. Pingxi's sky lanterns, Yanshui's beehive fireworks, and the large-scale Taiwan Lantern Festival are all real places and events. For safety, if you watch the beehive fireworks up close, always protect yourself with a helmet and a thick coat covering your whole body.":"Sebuah catatan: saat Festival Lampion, keluarga Taiwan memasak onde manis, dan anak-anak berjalan-jalan membawa lampion kertas. Lampion langit Pingxi, kembang api sarang lebah Yanshui, dan Festival Lampion Taiwan berskala besar semuanya tempat dan acara nyata. Demi keselamatan, jika Anda menonton kembang api sarang lebah dari dekat, selalu lindungi diri dengan helm dan mantel tebal yang menutupi seluruh tubuh.","Food & Drink":"Makanan & Minuman","Kingdom of Fruit: Taiwan's Year-Round Sweetness":"Kerajaan Buah: Manisnya Taiwan Sepanjang Tahun","Taiwan is so rich in fruit that it's called the \"Kingdom of Fruit.\" Mango, pineapple, sugar apple, wax apple—whenever you visit, there's a sweet fruit in season waiting for you. From the everyday view of someone living in Taiwan, this article introduces the fruits and growing regions of each season, the roadside fruit stands, and even gift boxes and exports.":"Taiwan begitu kaya buah hingga dijuluki \"Kerajaan Buah\". Mangga, nanas, srikaya, jambu air—kapan pun Anda berkunjung, ada buah manis yang sedang musim menanti Anda. Dari sudut pandang sehari-hari orang yang tinggal di Taiwan, artikel ini memperkenalkan buah-buahan dan wilayah penghasil tiap musim, lapak buah pinggir jalan, hingga parsel hadiah dan ekspor.","Taiwan is called the \"Kingdom of Fruit\" because its climate is perfect for growing fruit. Sitting on the border between the subtropical and tropical zones, Taiwan gets plenty of sunshine and rain all year round, so every kind of fruit grows big and sweet. From the lowlands to the high mountains, different elevations produce different fruits. Walk into a market and you'll see the stalls piled high with colorful fruit.":"Taiwan dijuluki \"Kerajaan Buah\" karena iklimnya sempurna untuk menanam buah. Terletak di perbatasan antara zona subtropis dan tropis, Taiwan mendapat banyak sinar matahari dan hujan sepanjang tahun, sehingga setiap jenis buah tumbuh besar dan manis. Dari dataran rendah hingga pegunungan tinggi, ketinggian yang berbeda menghasilkan buah yang berbeda. Masuklah ke pasar dan Anda akan melihat lapak-lapak menumpuk penuh buah warna-warni.","The most eagerly awaited fruit of summer is the mango. Mangoes from Yujing in Tainan are especially famous, and when the season comes, the orchards are covered in golden Irwin mangoes. Taiwanese people love turning mango into mango shaved ice—fresh mango cut into big chunks, topped with condensed milk and a scoop of ice cream, and one bite chases away the heat. The hotter it gets, the better mango ice sells.":"Buah yang paling dinanti di musim panas adalah mangga. Mangga dari Yujing di Tainan sangat terkenal, dan ketika musimnya tiba, kebun-kebun dipenuhi mangga Irwin keemasan. Orang Taiwan gemar mengubah mangga menjadi es serut mangga—mangga segar dipotong bongkahan besar, disiram susu kental manis dan sesendok es krim, dan satu gigitan mengusir hawa panas. Makin panas cuacanya, makin laris es mangga.","Besides summer mangoes, Taiwan has a signature fruit for every season. Spring brings wax apples and lychees, summer brings pineapples and longans, and autumn and winter bring sugar apples and papayas. Guanmiao pineapples, Madou pomelos, and Taitung sugar apples are all famous regional specialties. Bananas and guavas are available almost all year round—cheap and delicious.":"Selain mangga musim panas, Taiwan punya buah andalan untuk setiap musim. Musim semi membawa jambu air dan leci, musim panas membawa nanas dan lengkeng, dan musim gugur serta dingin membawa srikaya dan pepaya. Nanas Guanmiao, jeruk bali Madou, dan srikaya Taitung semuanya spesialisasi daerah yang terkenal. Pisang dan jambu biji tersedia hampir sepanjang tahun—murah dan lezat.","In Taiwan, buying fruit is incredibly convenient. Roadside fruit stands often cut it up on the spot—the vendor will ask if you'd like it \"cut up,\" then pack it in a box so you can eat as you walk. At the night market you can also order a fruit platter with watermelon, guava, and pineapple. This freshly cut fruit is fresh and clean, and it's part of everyday life for many people.":"Di Taiwan, membeli buah sangat praktis. Lapak buah pinggir jalan sering memotongnya di tempat—pedagang akan bertanya apakah Anda mau \"dipotong\", lalu mengemasnya dalam kotak agar bisa Anda makan sambil berjalan. Di pasar malam Anda juga bisa memesan piring buah berisi semangka, jambu biji, dan nanas. Buah yang baru dipotong ini segar dan bersih, dan menjadi bagian kehidupan sehari-hari banyak orang.","Taiwanese fruit isn't just for eating at home—it also makes a great gift. During festivals and holidays, many people buy beautiful fruit gift boxes for their elders or business clients. High-quality mangoes, sugar apples, and pineapples are even exported to Japan, Korea, and other countries, letting people abroad taste Taiwan's sweetness too. For many farmers, exports are a very important source of income.":"Buah Taiwan tak hanya untuk disantap di rumah—ia juga hadiah yang bagus. Saat festival dan hari raya, banyak orang membeli parsel buah yang cantik untuk orang tua atau klien bisnis mereka. Mangga, srikaya, dan nanas berkualitas tinggi bahkan diekspor ke Jepang, Korea, dan negara lain, sehingga orang di luar negeri pun bisa mencicipi manisnya Taiwan. Bagi banyak petani, ekspor adalah sumber pendapatan yang sangat penting.","\"Kingdom of Fruit,\" a nickname for fruit-rich Taiwan":"\"Kerajaan Buah\", julukan untuk Taiwan yang kaya buah","the season when a fruit is in season/harvested":"musim ketika buah sedang panen/musimnya","mango shaved ice":"es serut mangga","wax apple":"jambu air","sugar apple / custard apple":"srikaya","wendan pomelo":"jeruk bali wendan","fruit stand / fruit stall":"lapak buah","cut fresh on the spot":"dipotong segar di tempat","a plate/platter of cut fruit":"sepiring buah potong","to export (overseas)":"mengekspor (ke luar negeri)","In Taiwan, knowing where each fruit is grown and when it's in season makes travel much more fun—Yujing mangoes in summer, Taitung sugar apples in winter, always the tastiest thing for that season and place. At markets and night markets, ask for it \"cut fresh on the spot\" (現切) and you can sample a little of many kinds, so be sure to give it a try.":"Di Taiwan, mengetahui di mana tiap buah ditanam dan kapan musimnya membuat perjalanan jauh lebih seru—mangga Yujing di musim panas, srikaya Taitung di musim dingin, selalu yang paling lezat untuk musim dan tempat itu. Di pasar dan pasar malam, mintalah \"dipotong segar di tempat\" (現切) dan Anda bisa mencicipi sedikit dari banyak jenis, jadi pastikan untuk mencobanya.","Taiwanese Tea: From \"Old Man Tea\" to a Cup of High-Mountain Oolong":"Teh Taiwan: Dari \"Teh Orang Tua\" hingga Secangkir Oolong Gunung Tinggi","In Taiwan, tea is not just a drink — it is a way of life. From high-mountain tea grown on misty peaks, to \"old man tea\" brewed slowly in tiny pots, to the bubble tea sold on every street corner, each cup holds the warmth and daily rhythm of Taiwanese life. Today, let's look at Taiwan's tea culture through the eyes of the people who live there.":"Di Taiwan, teh bukan sekadar minuman — ia adalah cara hidup. Dari teh gunung tinggi yang tumbuh di puncak-puncak berkabut, hingga \"teh orang tua\" yang diseduh perlahan dalam teko-teko mungil, sampai teh boba yang dijual di setiap sudut jalan, setiap cangkir menyimpan kehangatan dan irama harian kehidupan Taiwan. Hari ini, mari kita lihat budaya teh Taiwan melalui mata orang-orang yang tinggal di sana.","Taiwan is a mountainous island. With the towering Central Mountain Range, plenty of cloud and mist, and big temperature swings between day and night, it is perfect for growing tea. The higher the altitude, the more slowly the tea trees grow, and the more fragrant and mellow the leaves become — which is why we speak of \"high-mountain tea.\" Dongding, Alishan, and Lishan are all famous growing regions. The oolong tea from here is light, fragrant, and smooth, a taste many Taiwanese have grown up with.":"Taiwan adalah pulau pegunungan. Dengan Pegunungan Tengah yang menjulang, kabut dan awan yang melimpah, serta perbedaan suhu siang-malam yang besar, ia sempurna untuk menanam teh. Semakin tinggi ketinggiannya, semakin lambat pohon teh tumbuh, dan semakin harum serta lembut daunnya — itulah sebabnya kita menyebut \"teh gunung tinggi\". Dongding, Alishan, dan Lishan semuanya wilayah penghasil yang terkenal. Teh oolong dari sini ringan, harum, dan halus, cita rasa yang menemani banyak orang Taiwan tumbuh besar.","Older folks love to brew \"old man tea,\" using a tiny pot and tiny cups, steeping slowly and sipping slowly. First they warm the pot with hot water, then add the leaves; sometimes they even pour out the first brew, a step called \"rinsing the tea.\" The tea doesn't taste sweet right away, but after a moment a sweetness rises from deep in your throat — this is the \"returning sweetness,\" and the more you drink, the richer it gets. A group gathered around a little table, brewing tea and chatting, can easily sit there for a whole afternoon.":"Orang tua gemar menyeduh \"teh orang tua\", memakai teko mungil dan cangkir-cangkir kecil, menyeduh perlahan dan menyeruput perlahan. Pertama mereka menghangatkan teko dengan air panas, lalu memasukkan daunnya; kadang mereka bahkan membuang seduhan pertama, langkah yang disebut \"membilas teh\". Teh tak langsung terasa manis, tetapi sesaat kemudian rasa manis naik dari dalam tenggorokan — inilah \"manis yang kembali\" (aftertaste), dan makin banyak Anda minum, makin kaya rasanya. Sekelompok orang berkumpul di meja kecil, menyeduh teh dan mengobrol, bisa dengan mudah duduk di sana sepanjang sore.","When people want to buy good tea, many go to a \"tea shop.\" Step inside and the owner will usually invite you to sit down and brew a pot for you to taste. You can smell the leaves and compare teas from different mountains and price ranges. As the owner brews, they'll tell you whether this year's harvest was good. Buying tea is a bit like making a friend — once you like the taste and get along with the owner, you'll keep coming back to the same shop for years.":"Ketika orang ingin membeli teh yang bagus, banyak yang pergi ke \"kedai teh\". Melangkahlah masuk dan pemiliknya biasanya mengajak Anda duduk dan menyeduh sepoci untuk Anda cicipi. Anda bisa mencium aroma daunnya dan membandingkan teh dari gunung dan kisaran harga yang berbeda. Sembari menyeduh, pemiliknya akan memberi tahu apakah panen tahun ini bagus. Membeli teh sedikit seperti berteman — begitu Anda menyukai rasanya dan cocok dengan pemiliknya, Anda akan terus kembali ke kedai yang sama selama bertahun-tahun.","Taiwanese people love the custom of \"offering tea.\" In the countryside, you used to see a barrel of tea by the roadside with the two characters for \"offered tea\" written on it, so passersby could quench their thirst for free. When you visit someone's home, the very first thing the host does is pour you a cup of tea. This plain-looking cup of tea actually holds the warmth and human kindness of the Taiwanese people.":"Orang Taiwan menyukai kebiasaan \"menyuguhkan teh\". Di pedesaan, dulu Anda bisa melihat sebuah tong teh di tepi jalan dengan dua aksara bertuliskan \"teh suguhan\", agar orang yang lewat bisa melepas dahaga secara gratis. Ketika Anda berkunjung ke rumah seseorang, hal pertama yang dilakukan tuan rumah adalah menuangkan secangkir teh untuk Anda. Secangkir teh yang tampak sederhana ini sebenarnya menyimpan kehangatan dan kebaikan hati orang Taiwan.","In recent years, young people don't always sit down to brew tea slowly; they tend to prefer \"hand-shaken drinks.\" Bubble milk tea, green oolong, oolong latte — they grab a cup to go and drink it wherever they wander. Even though hot tea has turned into an iced cold drink, at its heart it is still that same cup of tea. You could say the love of tea has always been part of Taiwanese life; it has simply put on a new look.":"Beberapa tahun terakhir, anak muda tak selalu duduk menyeduh teh perlahan; mereka cenderung menyukai \"minuman kocok tangan\". Teh susu boba, oolong hijau, oolong latte — mereka menyambar segelas untuk dibawa pergi dan meminumnya di mana pun mereka berkeliaran. Meski teh panas telah berubah menjadi minuman dingin bereskrim, pada intinya ia tetap secangkir teh yang sama. Bisa dibilang kecintaan pada teh selalu menjadi bagian kehidupan Taiwan; ia hanya mengenakan wajah baru.","high-mountain tea; tea grown at high altitude, prized for its fragrance":"teh gunung tinggi; teh yang ditanam di ketinggian, dihargai karena aromanya","oolong tea; a semi-oxidized tea, Taiwan's signature tea":"teh oolong; teh semi-oksidasi, teh andalan Taiwan","Dongding; a famous oolong tea growing region":"Dongding; wilayah penghasil teh oolong yang terkenal","to brew / steep tea":"menyeduh teh","\"old man tea\"; tea brewed slowly in tiny pots, enjoyed by elders":"\"teh orang tua\"; teh yang diseduh perlahan dalam teko mungil, digemari orang tua","the sweet aftertaste that rises in the throat after drinking":"manis yang kembali; aftertaste manis yang naik di tenggorokan setelah minum","a tea shop that sells loose tea and offers tastings":"kedai teh yang menjual teh curah dan menawarkan cicipan","the custom of offering tea to others, often for free":"kebiasaan menyuguhkan teh kepada orang lain, sering gratis","human warmth; a caring, friendly atmosphere":"kehangatan manusiawi; suasana yang peduli dan ramah","hand-shaken drinks; take-out drinks like bubble milk tea":"minuman kocok tangan; minuman bawa pulang seperti teh susu boba","If someone in Taiwan offers you tea, it's polite to accept and take at least a sip rather than refusing — receiving their gesture of \"offered tea\" is the best way to return the kindness. In neighborhood tea shops, you're often welcome just to taste, so don't be shy about stepping inside. You'll likely get a taste of Taiwan's warm hospitality along with the tea.":"Jika seseorang di Taiwan menyuguhkan teh untuk Anda, sopan bila menerimanya dan setidaknya menyeruput sedikit daripada menolak — menyambut gestur \"teh suguhan\" mereka adalah cara terbaik membalas kebaikan itu. Di kedai teh sekitar lingkungan, Anda sering dipersilakan sekadar mencicipi, jadi jangan sungkan melangkah masuk. Anda kemungkinan akan mencicipi keramahan hangat Taiwan sekaligus tehnya.","Tomb Sweeping Festival: Grave Visits, Popiah, and Honoring Ancestors":"Festival Ziarah Makam: Berziarah ke Makam, Popiah, dan Menghormati Leluhur","In early April each year, families across Taiwan gather to visit their ancestors' graves for the Tomb Sweeping Festival. This article looks at cleaning and tending the graves, making offerings, the custom of eating popiah, and the value of \"honoring one's origins\" — all from the perspective of everyday life in Taiwan.":"Setiap awal April, keluarga-keluarga di seluruh Taiwan berkumpul untuk berziarah ke makam leluhur pada Festival Ziarah Makam. Artikel ini menyoroti membersihkan dan merawat makam, memberi sesaji, tradisi makan popiah, serta nilai \"menghormati asal-usul\" — semuanya dari sudut pandang kehidupan sehari-hari di Taiwan.","The Tomb Sweeping Festival usually falls on April 4th or 5th and is one of Taiwan's important traditional holidays. On this day, people return to their hometowns to sweep the graves, expressing their remembrance of and respect for their ancestors. Qingming was originally one of the twenty-four solar terms, and over time it merged with the custom of honoring ancestors. As the weather gradually warms, it is also a good season for a trip out to the countryside.":"Festival Ziarah Makam biasanya jatuh pada tanggal 4 atau 5 April dan merupakan salah satu hari raya tradisional penting di Taiwan. Pada hari ini, orang-orang pulang ke kampung halaman untuk membersihkan makam, mengungkapkan kenangan dan penghormatan kepada leluhur. Qingming semula adalah salah satu dari dua puluh empat pembagian musim (jieqi), dan seiring waktu menyatu dengan tradisi menghormati leluhur. Saat cuaca berangsur menghangat, ini juga menjadi musim yang baik untuk berjalan-jalan ke pedesaan.","When Qingming comes around, many people working away from home use the long holiday to return to their hometowns. Early in the morning, the whole family sets off for the cemetery together, carrying fresh flowers, fruit, and joss paper. The elders tidy up the surroundings while telling the children stories about their ancestors. For many families, this is a rare moment of reunion in the course of the year.":"Ketika Qingming tiba, banyak orang yang bekerja jauh dari rumah memanfaatkan libur panjang untuk pulang ke kampung halaman. Pagi-pagi buta, seluruh keluarga berangkat bersama menuju pemakaman, membawa bunga segar, buah-buahan, dan kertas sembahyang. Para orang tua merapikan lingkungan sekitar sambil menceritakan kisah para leluhur kepada anak-anak. Bagi banyak keluarga, inilah momen berkumpul yang langka sepanjang tahun.","On arriving at the grave, people first clear away the weeds around it — this task is called \"peimu\" (tending the grave). Next they place layers of colorful paper money on top of the tomb, called \"guazhi,\" which symbolizes repairing the ancestors' house. Once everything is tidy, the family sets out offerings, lights incense, and pays their respects. Every gesture carries carefulness and reverence.":"Setibanya di makam, orang-orang pertama-tama membersihkan rumput liar di sekitarnya — pekerjaan ini disebut \"培墓\" (peimu, merawat makam). Berikutnya mereka meletakkan lapisan-lapisan uang kertas berwarna-warni di atas makam, disebut \"掛紙\" (guazhi), yang melambangkan memperbaiki rumah para leluhur. Setelah semuanya rapi, keluarga menata sesaji, menyalakan dupa, dan memberi penghormatan. Setiap gerakan mengandung kehati-hatian dan rasa hormat.","Around Qingming, many Taiwanese families eat \"popiah\" (runbing). Popiah is made by wrapping fillings such as cabbage, bean sprouts, shredded egg, and peanut powder in a thin crepe-like skin. The custom arose long ago because such rolls were easy to carry to the graves and required no cooking fire. Gathering together to wrap and eat popiah has become a cherished memory unique to Qingming.":"Menjelang Qingming, banyak keluarga Taiwan makan \"潤餅\" (popiah, runbing). Popiah dibuat dengan membungkus isian seperti kubis, tauge, telur suwir, dan bubuk kacang tanah dalam kulit tipis mirip kulit crepe. Tradisi ini muncul sejak lama karena gulungan seperti itu mudah dibawa ke makam dan tidak memerlukan api untuk memasak. Berkumpul bersama untuk menggulung dan menyantap popiah telah menjadi kenangan berharga yang khas Qingming.","In recent years, more and more families choose to place their ancestors in a \"columbarium niche\" (tawei), making grave visits more convenient and tidy. Some people who live far away even express their feelings through \"online ancestor worship.\" However the form may change, what matters is always the heart of \"honoring one's origins.\" Through Qingming, we remember where we came from and pass that feeling on to the next generation.":"Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, semakin banyak keluarga memilih menempatkan abu leluhur mereka di \"塔位\" (tawei, relung kolumbarium), sehingga ziarah menjadi lebih praktis dan rapi. Sebagian orang yang tinggal jauh bahkan mengungkapkan perasaan mereka melalui \"pemujaan leluhur secara daring\". Bagaimanapun bentuknya berubah, yang selalu penting adalah hati untuk \"menghormati asal-usul\". Melalui Qingming, kita mengingat dari mana kita berasal dan mewariskan perasaan itu kepada generasi berikutnya.","Tomb Sweeping Festival, a traditional day for honoring ancestors.":"Festival Ziarah Makam, hari tradisional untuk menghormati leluhur.","to visit and clean ancestral graves.":"berziarah dan membersihkan makam leluhur.","ancestors.":"leluhur.","a long holiday of consecutive days off.":"libur panjang dengan hari libur berturut-turut.","tending and clearing the area around a grave.":"merawat dan membersihkan area di sekitar makam.","placing paper money on a grave during Qingming.":"meletakkan uang kertas di atas makam saat Qingming.","popiah, a fresh (uncooked) spring roll.":"popiah, lumpia segar (tidak digoreng).","a columbarium niche for storing ashes.":"relung kolumbarium untuk menyimpan abu jenazah.","honoring the departed and remembering distant ancestors sincerely.":"menghormati yang telah tiada dan mengenang leluhur jauh dengan tulus.","cemetery / graveyard.":"pemakaman / kuburan.","\"Shen zhong zhui yuan\" (慎終追遠) means caring for the departed with respect and remembering even one's distant ancestors with a sincere heart. Rather than a day of sorrow, the Tomb Sweeping Festival is a warm occasion for reaffirming family bonds and gratitude.":"\"Shen zhong zhui yuan\" (慎終追遠) berarti mengurus yang telah tiada dengan penuh hormat dan mengenang bahkan leluhur jauh dengan hati yang tulus. Alih-alih hari kesedihan, Festival Ziarah Makam adalah kesempatan hangat untuk menegaskan kembali ikatan keluarga dan rasa syukur.","History & Society":"Sejarah & Masyarakat","Indigenous Peoples: The Island's First Inhabitants":"Masyarakat Adat: Penghuni Pertama Pulau Ini","Long before Han settlers arrived, Taiwan was already home to its Indigenous peoples. Belonging to the Austronesian language family, they carry on their own languages and cultures to this day. This article introduces the history of the island's first inhabitants and their rich, proud heritage.":"Jauh sebelum pendatang Han tiba, Taiwan sudah menjadi rumah bagi masyarakat adatnya. Termasuk dalam rumpun bahasa Austronesia, mereka melestarikan bahasa dan budaya mereka sendiri hingga hari ini. Artikel ini memperkenalkan sejarah penghuni pertama pulau ini dan warisan mereka yang kaya dan membanggakan.","Taiwan's Indigenous peoples are the island's first inhabitants; they had already lived here for thousands of years before Han immigrants arrived. They belong to the Austronesian language family, one of the most widely spread language families in the world, reaching from the Pacific islands all the way to Southeast Asia. Many scholars believe Taiwan is very likely one of the important places where the Austronesian family originated. So getting to know Taiwan's Indigenous peoples also means learning about a very ancient and precious history.":"Masyarakat adat Taiwan adalah penghuni pertama pulau ini; mereka sudah tinggal di sini selama ribuan tahun sebelum para imigran Han datang. Mereka termasuk dalam rumpun bahasa Austronesia, salah satu rumpun bahasa yang paling luas persebarannya di dunia, membentang dari kepulauan Pasifik hingga jauh ke Asia Tenggara. Banyak sarjana meyakini Taiwan sangat mungkin merupakan salah satu tempat penting asal-usul rumpun Austronesia. Jadi, mengenal masyarakat adat Taiwan juga berarti mempelajari sejarah yang sangat kuno dan berharga.","Today the Taiwanese government officially recognizes sixteen Indigenous peoples, each with its own language, culture, and traditions. The most populous is the Amis; others include the Paiwan, Atayal, Bunun, Puyuma, Rukai, Tsou, Saisiyat, and the Tao living on Orchid Island, among others. These peoples live across the mountains, the plains, and the outlying islands, each having developed its own distinctive clothing, music, and way of life. This diversity is one of the most beautiful parts of Taiwanese culture.":"Kini pemerintah Taiwan secara resmi mengakui enam belas suku adat, masing-masing dengan bahasa, budaya, dan tradisinya sendiri. Yang terbanyak jumlahnya adalah suku Amis; lainnya meliputi Paiwan, Atayal, Bunun, Puyuma, Rukai, Tsou, Saisiyat, dan suku Tao yang tinggal di Pulau Orchid, dan lain-lain. Masyarakat ini tinggal di pegunungan, dataran, dan pulau-pulau terluar, masing-masing telah mengembangkan pakaian, musik, dan cara hidup khasnya sendiri. Keragaman ini adalah salah satu bagian terindah dari budaya Taiwan.","Festivals are a very important part of Indigenous culture. The Amis Harvest Festival is one of the best-known ceremonies, where people sing and dance together to give thanks to their ancestors and to nature's blessings. The Bunun are famous around the world for their beautiful \"eight-part polyphonic singing.\" In the tribal villages, elders pass down traditional skills and stories from one generation to the next. These festivals are not only celebrations but also moments that strengthen ethnic identity and bonds.":"Festival merupakan bagian yang sangat penting dalam budaya masyarakat adat. Festival Panen suku Amis adalah salah satu upacara paling terkenal, di mana orang-orang bernyanyi dan menari bersama untuk berterima kasih kepada leluhur dan atas berkah alam. Suku Bunun terkenal di seluruh dunia karena \"nyanyian polifoni delapan suara\" mereka yang indah. Di desa-desa suku, para tetua mewariskan keterampilan tradisional dan cerita dari satu generasi ke generasi berikutnya. Festival-festival ini bukan hanya perayaan, tetapi juga momen yang memperkuat identitas dan ikatan etnis.","In the past, for various reasons, many Indigenous languages were gradually lost, and younger generations became less able to speak their mother tongues. In recent years, more and more people have come to value passing these languages on, and schools now offer courses in Indigenous languages. \"Name rectification\" is another important movement, for example changing names once imposed by outsiders back to the names the people themselves identify with; the Truku and the Seediq were among the peoples recognized officially only later on. Through cultural revitalization, Indigenous peoples are working hard to reclaim their own pride and roots.":"Di masa lalu, karena berbagai alasan, banyak bahasa adat berangsur hilang, dan generasi muda semakin kurang mampu berbicara bahasa ibu mereka. Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, semakin banyak orang menghargai pewarisan bahasa-bahasa ini, dan sekolah-sekolah kini menawarkan mata pelajaran bahasa adat. \"Pelurusan nama\" adalah gerakan penting lainnya, misalnya mengubah nama yang dulu dipaksakan pihak luar kembali ke nama yang diakui masyarakat itu sendiri; suku Truku dan Seediq termasuk di antara suku yang baru diakui secara resmi belakangan. Melalui revitalisasi budaya, masyarakat adat berupaya keras merebut kembali kebanggaan dan akar mereka sendiri.","In modern times, many Indigenous people shine in music and sports. Indigenous singers are known for their moving voices, and quite a few famous Indigenous artists have thrived in the Mandarin-language music scene while also bringing songs in their own languages to the world. On the sports field, too, many outstanding Indigenous athletes have brought glory to Taiwan. Through their talents, they help more people see the culture and strength of the Indigenous peoples.":"Di zaman modern, banyak orang dari masyarakat adat bersinar di bidang musik dan olahraga. Penyanyi dari masyarakat adat dikenal karena suara mereka yang menyentuh, dan cukup banyak seniman adat terkenal yang berjaya di kancah musik berbahasa Mandarin sekaligus membawa lagu-lagu dalam bahasa mereka sendiri ke dunia. Di lapangan olahraga pun, banyak atlet dari masyarakat adat yang luar biasa telah mengharumkan nama Taiwan. Melalui bakat mereka, mereka membantu lebih banyak orang melihat budaya dan kekuatan masyarakat adat.","Indigenous peoples; the earliest inhabitants of Taiwan, belonging to the Austronesian family.":"masyarakat adat; penghuni paling awal Taiwan, termasuk rumpun Austronesia.","the Austronesian language family, spread widely from the Pacific to Southeast Asia.":"rumpun bahasa Austronesia, tersebar luas dari Pasifik hingga Asia Tenggara.","to officially recognize or acknowledge (e.g., by the government).":"mengakui atau mengesahkan secara resmi (misalnya oleh pemerintah).","a tribal village or community of Indigenous people.":"sebuah desa suku atau komunitas masyarakat adat.","a festival or ceremony.":"sebuah festival atau upacara.","the Harvest Festival, held by the Amis and others to give thanks.":"Festival Panen, yang diselenggarakan oleh suku Amis dan lainnya untuk bersyukur.","a people's own language; mother tongue.":"bahasa milik suatu suku; bahasa ibu.","to pass down and inherit (across generations).":"mewariskan dan mewarisi (lintas generasi).","name rectification; restoring a proper, self-identified name.":"pelurusan nama; memulihkan nama yang benar dan diakui sendiri.","cultural revitalization; efforts to revive a fading culture.":"revitalisasi budaya; upaya menghidupkan kembali budaya yang memudar.","A note of respect for Taiwan's Indigenous peoples: sixteen peoples are officially recognized today, each with its own language and culture. In Taiwan the correct and respectful term is \"Indigenous peoples\" (原住民族), not \"ethnic minorities.\" The history and culture of these first inhabitants are an essential part of understanding the island of Taiwan.":"Sebuah catatan hormat untuk masyarakat adat Taiwan: enam belas suku diakui secara resmi saat ini, masing-masing dengan bahasa dan budayanya sendiri. Di Taiwan, istilah yang tepat dan sopan adalah \"masyarakat adat\" (原住民族), bukan \"minoritas etnis\". Sejarah dan budaya para penghuni pertama ini merupakan bagian penting untuk memahami pulau Taiwan.","Hakka Culture: The Unyielding Spirit and the Tung Blossoms of May":"Budaya Hakka: Semangat Pantang Menyerah dan Bunga Tung Bulan Mei","Many ethnic groups live together in Taiwan, and the Hakka are one of its most important. They still carefully preserve their own language, cuisine, and the unyielding spirit known as \"ngang-kiang\" (hard-necked). This article introduces the charm of Taiwan's Hakka culture.":"Banyak kelompok etnis hidup berdampingan di Taiwan, dan suku Hakka adalah salah satu yang terpenting. Mereka masih dengan cermat melestarikan bahasa, kuliner, dan semangat pantang menyerah yang dikenal sebagai \"硬頸\" (ngang-kiang, keras kepala). Artikel ini memperkenalkan pesona budaya Hakka Taiwan.","The Hakka are one of Taiwan's important ethnic groups. Most of their ancestors migrated to Taiwan from the Guangdong and Fujian regions of China, and over several hundred years they gradually put down roots in this land. Today the Hakka live mainly in Taoyuan, Hsinchu, and Miaoli in the north — the area people call \"Tao-Zhu-Miao\" — as well as the \"Liudui\" region around Kaohsiung and Pingtung in the south. In these places you can often hear the warm Hakka language and feel a strong Hakka atmosphere.":"Suku Hakka adalah salah satu kelompok etnis penting di Taiwan. Sebagian besar leluhur mereka bermigrasi ke Taiwan dari wilayah Guangdong dan Fujian di Tiongkok, dan selama beberapa ratus tahun mereka berangsur berakar di tanah ini. Kini suku Hakka terutama tinggal di Taoyuan, Hsinchu, dan Miaoli di utara — kawasan yang orang sebut \"Tao-Zhu-Miao\" — serta wilayah \"Liudui\" di sekitar Kaohsiung dan Pingtung di selatan. Di tempat-tempat ini kamu sering dapat mendengar bahasa Hakka yang hangat dan merasakan suasana Hakka yang kental.","The Hakka language is one of the Hakka people's most precious cultural treasures; it sounds different from Mandarin and from Taiwanese, with its own distinctive intonation. The Hakka often describe their character with the word \"ngang-kiang\" (hard-necked), meaning steadfast and not easily bowed. Life in the past was not easy, but through thrift and hard work they gradually built a better life little by little. This hard-necked, thrifty spirit still deeply shapes the Hakka today.":"Bahasa Hakka adalah salah satu harta budaya paling berharga bagi orang Hakka; bunyinya berbeda dari Mandarin maupun bahasa Taiwan, dengan intonasi khasnya sendiri. Orang Hakka sering menggambarkan watak mereka dengan kata \"硬頸\" (ngang-kiang, keras kepala), yang berarti teguh dan tidak mudah tunduk. Kehidupan di masa lalu tidaklah mudah, tetapi lewat hemat dan kerja keras mereka berangsur membangun kehidupan yang lebih baik sedikit demi sedikit. Semangat keras kepala dan hemat ini masih membentuk orang Hakka secara mendalam hingga kini.","Every April and May is the most beautiful season in the Hakka villages. At this time the tung trees blossom all over the hills, and the white petals drift down like falling snow, so people call it \"May Snow.\" Lively Tung Blossom Festivals are held in many places, and crowds drive up into the mountains to admire the flowers while experiencing Hakka culture. Walking along a path carpeted with tung blossoms and listening to Hakka folk songs is truly romantic. The Tung Blossom Festival has become one of Taiwan's well-known seasonal events.":"Setiap bulan April dan Mei adalah musim terindah di desa-desa Hakka. Pada saat ini pohon tung bermekaran di seluruh perbukitan, dan kelopak putihnya berguguran bagaikan salju turun, sehingga orang menyebutnya \"Salju Bulan Mei\". Festival Bunga Tung yang meriah digelar di banyak tempat, dan orang berbondong-bondong berkendara naik ke gunung untuk menikmati bunga sambil mengalami budaya Hakka. Berjalan menyusuri jalan setapak yang berhampar bunga tung sambil mendengarkan lagu rakyat Hakka sungguh romantis. Festival Bunga Tung telah menjadi salah satu acara musiman terkenal di Taiwan.","Speaking of Hakka culture, one cannot leave out Hakka cuisine. Because the Hakka once lived hard lives, their dishes are made to go well with rice and to keep for a long time, tending toward salty and savory flavors. The most famous is \"Hakka stir-fry,\" made by frying pork, dried tofu, squid, and spring onions together — salty, savory, and perfect with rice. There is also \"lei cha\" (ground tea), in which tea leaves, peanuts, and sesame are ground into a powder and steeped in hot water — fragrant and healthy. \"Ban-tiao\" is a wide noodle made from rice, smooth and tender, a favorite Hakka snack for many people.":"Bicara soal budaya Hakka, kita tidak bisa melewatkan kuliner Hakka. Karena orang Hakka dulu hidup susah, hidangan mereka dibuat agar cocok dengan nasi dan tahan lama, cenderung berasa asin dan gurih. Yang paling terkenal adalah \"tumis Hakka\", dibuat dengan menumis daging babi, tahu kering, cumi, dan daun bawang bersama-sama — asin, gurih, dan pas dengan nasi. Ada juga \"擂茶\" (lei cha, teh tumbuk), di mana daun teh, kacang tanah, dan wijen ditumbuk menjadi bubuk lalu diseduh dengan air panas — harum dan menyehatkan. \"粄條\" (ban-tiao) adalah mi lebar yang terbuat dari beras, halus dan lembut, camilan Hakka favorit bagi banyak orang.","Beyond language and food, the Hakka preserve their traditions in many ways. The brightly colored Hakka floral cloth, often patterned with large peonies and blossoms, looks festive and warm, and is now made into bags and clothes that are very popular. The traditional blue shirt (lam-sam) was a garment Hakka women often wore in the past — plain and durable, symbolizing a thrifty way of life. In terms of faith, the Hakka especially honor the \"Yimin\" (righteous martyrs), commemorating ancestors who sacrificed themselves to protect their homeland. Through these traditions, the Hakka spirit is passed down from generation to generation.":"Selain bahasa dan makanan, orang Hakka melestarikan tradisi mereka dengan berbagai cara. Kain bermotif bunga Hakka yang berwarna cerah, sering bermotif peoni dan bunga besar, tampak meriah dan hangat, dan kini dijadikan tas serta pakaian yang sangat populer. Baju biru tradisional (藍衫, lam-sam) adalah busana yang dulu sering dikenakan perempuan Hakka — sederhana dan tahan lama, melambangkan gaya hidup hemat. Dalam hal kepercayaan, orang Hakka secara khusus menghormati \"Yimin\" (義民, para martir yang benar), memperingati leluhur yang mengorbankan diri untuk melindungi tanah air mereka. Melalui tradisi-tradisi ini, semangat Hakka diwariskan dari generasi ke generasi.","the Hakka people, one of Taiwan's important ethnic groups":"orang Hakka, salah satu kelompok etnis penting di Taiwan","the Hakka language spoken by the Hakka people":"bahasa Hakka yang dituturkan oleh orang Hakka","hard-necked; steadfast and unyielding":"keras kepala; teguh dan pantang menyerah","diligent and thrifty":"rajin dan hemat","the Tung Blossom Festival, held in April–May":"Festival Bunga Tung, digelar pada April–Mei","Hakka stir-fry, a classic Hakka dish":"tumis Hakka, hidangan Hakka klasik","lei cha; ground tea with peanuts and sesame":"擂茶 (lei cha); teh tumbuk dengan kacang tanah dan wijen","ban-tiao; wide rice noodles":"粄條 (ban-tiao); mi beras lebar","the traditional blue shirt worn by Hakka women":"baju biru tradisional yang dikenakan perempuan Hakka","the righteous martyrs honored for defending their homeland":"para martir yang benar, dihormati karena membela tanah air mereka","The Hakka are an essential and cherished ethnic group in Taiwanese society, and their culture enriches Taiwan's diversity. Customs and ways of speaking can vary by region and generation. Visiting Taoyuan, Hsinchu, and Miaoli or the Liudui region in the south — and experiencing Hakka cuisine and the Tung Blossom Festival for yourself — is the best way to feel their warmth and unyielding spirit more deeply.":"Orang Hakka adalah kelompok etnis yang penting dan disayangi dalam masyarakat Taiwan, dan budaya mereka memperkaya keragaman Taiwan. Adat istiadat dan cara bertutur bisa berbeda-beda menurut wilayah dan generasi. Mengunjungi Taoyuan, Hsinchu, dan Miaoli atau wilayah Liudui di selatan — serta mencicipi kuliner Hakka dan menikmati Festival Bunga Tung sendiri — adalah cara terbaik untuk merasakan kehangatan dan semangat pantang menyerah mereka lebih dalam.","The All-Powerful Convenience Store: Taiwan's Everyday Magic":"Minimarket Serba Bisa: Keajaiban Sehari-hari Taiwan","In Taiwan, the convenience store is not just a place to grab a drink. From paying bills to picking up parcels, almost everything in daily life happens here. Let's look at why they're called \"all-powerful.\"":"Di Taiwan, minimarket bukan sekadar tempat membeli minuman. Dari membayar tagihan hingga mengambil paket, hampir segala hal dalam kehidupan sehari-hari terjadi di sini. Mari kita lihat mengapa mereka disebut \"serba bisa\".","In Taiwan, the density of convenience stores is among the highest in the world. Walk through a city and you'll often find two or three stores at a single intersection—sometimes even two 7-Elevens facing each other on the same street. The island has over thirteen thousand outlets, roughly one for every two thousand people, a density that makes the convenience store the most familiar sight in Taiwanese life.":"Di Taiwan, kepadatan minimarket termasuk yang tertinggi di dunia. Berjalanlah menyusuri kota dan kamu akan sering menemukan dua atau tiga gerai di satu persimpangan — kadang bahkan dua 7-Eleven saling berhadapan di jalan yang sama. Pulau ini memiliki lebih dari tiga belas ribu gerai, kira-kira satu untuk setiap dua ribu orang, kepadatan yang membuat minimarket menjadi pemandangan paling akrab dalam kehidupan orang Taiwan.","What surprises foreigners most is that you can \"pay bills\" at a convenience store. Water, electricity, gas, phone, and parking fees—even traffic fines, health insurance premiums, and credit card statements—can be handled right at the counter. The clerk scans a barcode, you hand over the money, and it's done. No special trip to the bank or post office, no waiting in a long line.":"Yang paling membuat orang asing terkejut adalah kamu bisa \"membayar tagihan\" di minimarket. Air, listrik, gas, telepon, dan biaya parkir — bahkan denda lalu lintas, iuran asuransi kesehatan, dan tagihan kartu kredit — dapat diurus langsung di kasir. Pramuniaga memindai barcode, kamu menyerahkan uang, dan selesai. Tak perlu pergi khusus ke bank atau kantor pos, tak perlu antre panjang.","In the age of online shopping, the convenience store is even more indispensable. When you buy something online, you can choose \"store pickup\": the parcel is sent to a store near your home, and after a text notification you go collect it—you can even pay cash on delivery. Conversely, to send something to a friend or return an item to a seller, you bring the parcel to the store, tap through the in-store machine a few times, and it ships out—open twenty-four hours a day.":"Di era belanja daring, minimarket bahkan semakin tak tergantikan. Ketika kamu membeli sesuatu secara online, kamu bisa memilih \"ambil di gerai\": paket dikirim ke gerai dekat rumahmu, dan setelah pemberitahuan lewat SMS kamu pergi mengambilnya — kamu bahkan bisa membayar tunai saat pengambilan. Sebaliknya, untuk mengirim sesuatu ke teman atau mengembalikan barang ke penjual, kamu bawa paket ke gerai, tekan beberapa kali di mesin dalam gerai, dan barang pun terkirim — buka dua puluh empat jam sehari.","Beyond parcels, the store's multi-function kiosk is the real key to being \"all-powerful.\" It prints documents, photocopies, and scans; it sells high-speed rail tickets, concert tickets, and theme-park passes; it even prints out tax-filing forms and collects government fees. Many Taiwanese never set foot in an office all day yet clear every errand, big and small, with a single convenience-store machine.":"Selain paket, mesin kios multifungsi di gerai adalah kunci sesungguhnya dari \"serba bisa\". Ia mencetak dokumen, memfotokopi, dan memindai; menjual tiket kereta cepat, tiket konser, dan tiket taman hiburan; bahkan mencetak formulir pelaporan pajak dan menerima pembayaran biaya pemerintah. Banyak orang Taiwan yang seharian tak pernah menginjak kantor mana pun, namun menuntaskan segala urusan besar dan kecil hanya dengan satu mesin minimarket.","Of course, the basics of food and drink are all there too. Freshly brewed coffee costs just a few tens of dollars a cup, and the morning coffee line rivals any café; oden, tea eggs, bento boxes, and rice balls can be heated anytime, and stores now have seating areas where you can sit, eat, enjoy the air conditioning, and scroll your phone. Some outlets even have ATMs, laundry, and dry-cleaning drop-off—so many functions that you can hardly tell whether it's really a \"store\" at all.":"Tentu saja, kebutuhan dasar makanan dan minuman juga tersedia semua. Kopi seduh segar hanya seharga beberapa puluh dolar per gelas, dan antrean kopi pagi tak kalah dari kafe mana pun; oden, telur teh, kotak bento, dan bola nasi bisa dipanaskan kapan saja, dan gerai kini memiliki area tempat duduk di mana kamu bisa duduk, makan, menikmati pendingin ruangan, dan bermain ponsel. Beberapa gerai bahkan punya ATM, layanan cuci pakaian, dan tempat penitipan cuci kering — begitu banyak fungsi hingga kamu nyaris tak bisa membedakan apakah ini benar-benar sebuah \"toko\".","From a cup of coffee to a parking ticket, the convenience store catches nearly every small need in Taiwanese life. It is not merely a shop but something like the city's public infrastructure—lit up twenty-four hours, always open exactly when you need it. No wonder Taiwanese often say, \"If something comes up, just head to the convenience store first.\"":"Dari secangkir kopi hingga tilang parkir, minimarket menangkap hampir setiap kebutuhan kecil dalam kehidupan orang Taiwan. Ia bukan sekadar toko, melainkan semacam infrastruktur publik kota — menyala dua puluh empat jam, selalu buka tepat saat kamu membutuhkannya. Pantas saja orang Taiwan sering berkata, \"Kalau ada sesuatu, pergi saja dulu ke minimarket.\"","convenience store (short: 超商)":"minimarket (singkatan: 超商)","density":"kepadatan","retail outlet, store branch":"gerai ritel, cabang toko","fine, ticket":"denda, tilang","convenience-store pickup":"pengambilan di minimarket","parcel, package":"paket, bungkusan","cash on delivery":"bayar tunai saat pengiriman","multi-function kiosk":"kios multifungsi","to print":"mencetak","freshly brewed coffee":"kopi seduh segar","to close (for the day)":"tutup (untuk hari itu)","Taiwan's main convenience-store chains are 7-Eleven, FamilyMart (全家), Hi-Life (萊爾富), and OK. The multi-function kiosks have different names per chain—7-Eleven's is \"ibon,\" FamilyMart's is \"FamiPort.\" They're handy for travelers too, for collecting SIM cards or printing tickets, so it's worth learning how they work. Note that whether you can pay by means other than cash varies by kiosk and service, so it's safest to check at the counter.":"Jaringan minimarket utama di Taiwan adalah 7-Eleven, FamilyMart (全家), Hi-Life (萊爾富), dan OK. Kios multifungsi punya nama berbeda di tiap jaringan — milik 7-Eleven bernama \"ibon\", milik FamilyMart bernama \"FamiPort\". Mesin ini juga praktis bagi wisatawan, untuk mengambil kartu SIM atau mencetak tiket, jadi ada baiknya mempelajari cara kerjanya. Perlu dicatat bahwa apakah kamu bisa membayar dengan cara selain tunai berbeda-beda menurut kios dan layanannya, jadi paling aman menanyakannya di kasir.","Hand-Shaken Drink Culture: From Bubble Tea to the World":"Budaya Minuman Kocok Tangan: Dari Bubble Tea ke Dunia","\"Hand-shaken drinks,\" where you can customize even the sweetness and ice level, are a culture deeply rooted in Taiwanese daily life. Let's trace the story from the origins of its icon—bubble tea—to its spread around the world.":"\"Minuman kocok tangan\", di mana kamu bahkan bisa menyesuaikan tingkat kemanisan dan es, adalah budaya yang mengakar dalam kehidupan sehari-hari orang Taiwan. Mari kita telusuri kisahnya dari asal-usul ikonnya — bubble tea — hingga penyebarannya ke seluruh dunia.","\"Hand-shaken drinks\" refers to beverages made to order on the spot, shaken in a cup by hand. In Taiwan you'll find a drink shop on nearly every street, with a cup ranging from a few tens to over a hundred dollars—part of daily life for office workers, students, and homemakers alike. On a hot day, everyone holding a cup of iced drink is one of the most classic scenes on Taiwan's streets.":"\"Minuman kocok tangan\" merujuk pada minuman yang dibuat sesuai pesanan di tempat, dikocok dalam gelas dengan tangan. Di Taiwan kamu akan menemukan kedai minuman di hampir setiap jalan, dengan harga per gelas berkisar dari beberapa puluh hingga lebih dari seratus dolar — bagian dari keseharian pekerja kantoran, pelajar, maupun ibu rumah tangga. Di hari yang panas, semua orang menggenggam segelas minuman dingin adalah salah satu pemandangan paling klasik di jalanan Taiwan.","The source of this craze is the beloved \"bubble tea\" (珍珠奶茶). As the story goes, in the 1980s two teahouses—one in Taichung, one in Tainan—each added cooked tapioca pearls to milk tea, creating this fragrant, chewy drink. Once cooked, the pearls turn glossy and translucent, like beads of pearl, and so the name \"pearl milk tea\" spread, shortened to \"zhēnnǎi.\"":"Sumber demam ini adalah \"bubble tea\" (珍珠奶茶) yang digemari. Menurut kisahnya, pada tahun 1980-an dua kedai teh — satu di Taichung, satu di Tainan — masing-masing menambahkan mutiara tapioka matang ke dalam teh susu, menciptakan minuman yang harum dan kenyal ini. Setelah matang, mutiaranya menjadi mengkilap dan tembus cahaya, bagaikan butiran mutiara, sehingga nama \"teh susu mutiara\" menyebar, disingkat menjadi \"珍奶\" (zhēnnǎi).","The most captivating thing about hand-shaken drinks is customization. When you order, the clerk will always ask about sweetness and ice: sweetness can be full, less sugar, half sugar, slightly sweet, or even none; ice can be regular, less, slight, or none. The weight-conscious order half sugar, no ice; those sensitive to cold order it warm. Everyone can dial in the cup that suits them best, and this freedom is exactly why Taiwanese can't do without hand-shaken drinks.":"Hal paling memikat dari minuman kocok tangan adalah penyesuaian. Ketika kamu memesan, pramuniaga selalu menanyakan kemanisan dan es: kemanisan bisa penuh, kurang gula, setengah gula, sedikit manis, atau bahkan tanpa gula; es bisa biasa, sedikit, sedikit sekali, atau tanpa es. Yang menjaga berat badan memesan setengah gula tanpa es; yang sensitif terhadap dingin memesannya hangat. Setiap orang bisa mengatur gelas yang paling cocok untuknya, dan kebebasan inilah justru alasan orang Taiwan tak bisa lepas dari minuman kocok tangan.","Hand-shaken drinks have long woven themselves into Taiwanese socializing and daily life. Colleagues \"group order\" drinks in the afternoon, filling in each person's preference on a single sheet; friends worn out from shopping buy a cup to sip as they walk; and for treating, apologizing, or celebrating, the single phrase \"my treat—get a drink\" can instantly close the distance. It's not just about quenching thirst; it's a small gesture of goodwill between people.":"Minuman kocok tangan telah lama menyatu dalam pergaulan dan keseharian orang Taiwan. Rekan kerja \"memesan bersama\" minuman di sore hari, mengisi selera masing-masing di satu lembar; teman yang lelah berbelanja membeli segelas untuk diseruput sambil berjalan; dan untuk mentraktir, meminta maaf, atau merayakan, cukup satu kalimat \"aku traktir — ambil minuman\" bisa langsung mendekatkan jarak. Ini bukan sekadar melepas dahaga; ini isyarat kecil niat baik antarmanusia.","This wave that began in Taiwan has now swept across the world. From Japan and Korea to Southeast Asia and on to major cities in the West, drink shops with Chinese-character signs open one after another, and \"bubble tea\" and \"boba\" have become words young people abroad say with ease. Many Taiwanese brands have gone overseas, carrying flavors like tapioca pearls, taro balls, and \"frog-egg\" milk to every corner of the globe.":"Gelombang yang bermula di Taiwan ini kini telah melanda seluruh dunia. Dari Jepang dan Korea hingga Asia Tenggara dan sampai ke kota-kota besar di Barat, kedai minuman dengan papan nama beraksara Tionghoa bermunculan satu demi satu, dan \"bubble tea\" serta \"boba\" telah menjadi kata yang diucapkan anak muda di luar negeri dengan lancar. Banyak merek Taiwan telah melangkah ke luar negeri, membawa cita rasa seperti mutiara tapioka, bola talas, dan susu \"telur katak\" ke setiap penjuru dunia.","A small cup of hand-shaken drink holds not just tea and pearls but also Taiwanese people's care for and passion about life. From street-corner stalls to multinational chains, it has carried the taste of Taiwan to every corner of the world in the most ordinary way. Next time you're in Taiwan, don't forget to step into a drink shop and say your own line out loud: \"half sugar, no ice.\"":"Segelas kecil minuman kocok tangan tak hanya berisi teh dan mutiara, tetapi juga kepedulian dan gairah orang Taiwan terhadap kehidupan. Dari kios sudut jalan hingga jaringan multinasional, ia telah membawa cita rasa Taiwan ke setiap penjuru dunia dengan cara yang paling biasa. Lain kali kamu di Taiwan, jangan lupa mampir ke kedai minuman dan ucapkan sendiri kalimatmu dengan lantang: \"setengah gula, tanpa es.\"","hand-shaken drink":"minuman kocok tangan","bubble/pearl milk tea (short: 珍奶)":"teh susu mutiara/bubble tea (singkatan: 珍奶)","tapioca pearls (larger ones: 珍珠)":"mutiara tapioka (yang lebih besar: 珍珠)","chewiness, bite":"kekenyalan, gigitan","customization":"penyesuaian","sweetness level":"tingkat kemanisan","half sugar":"setengah gula","slightly sweet, low sugar":"sedikit manis, gula rendah","no ice":"tanpa es","slight ice":"es sedikit","to organize a group order":"mengatur pesanan bersama","to quench thirst":"melepas dahaga","Memorizing the ordering \"spell\" makes life easier on the ground. Sweetness goes full → less sugar → half sugar → slightly sweet → none; ice goes regular → less → slight → none, each step lighter. It's common to say it all at once—drink + sweetness + ice—like \"pearl milk tea, half sugar, no ice.\" To add toppings, say things like \"add pearls.\" For hot, say \"熱的\"; for room temperature, \"常溫.\"":"Menghafal \"mantra\" pemesanan membuat hidup lebih mudah saat di lapangan. Kemanisan berurutan penuh → kurang gula → setengah gula → sedikit manis → tanpa gula; es berurutan biasa → sedikit → sedikit sekali → tanpa es, tiap tingkat makin ringan. Umum diucapkan sekaligus — minuman + kemanisan + es — seperti \"teh susu mutiara, setengah gula, tanpa es.\" Untuk menambah topping, ucapkan sesuatu seperti \"tambah mutiara.\" Untuk panas, ucapkan \"熱的\"; untuk suhu ruang, \"常溫.\"","Kingdom of Scooters: Everyday Taiwan on Two Wheels":"Kerajaan Skuter: Keseharian Taiwan di Atas Dua Roda","The moment the light turns green, dozens of scooters surge forward at once. Taiwan is truly a \"kingdom of scooters.\" Let's look at why there are so many, and at the life lived on two wheels.":"Saat lampu berubah hijau, puluhan skuter melaju ke depan sekaligus. Taiwan benar-benar sebuah \"kerajaan skuter\". Mari kita lihat mengapa jumlahnya begitu banyak, dan kehidupan yang dijalani di atas dua roda.","In Taiwan's cities, one of the scenes that leaves the strongest impression on foreign visitors is the sea of scooters packing the space ahead at a red light. The instant it turns green, the swarm surges forward like a tide, engines roaring from every direction. Taiwan has over fourteen million registered scooters—about one for every 1.6 people—so calling it a \"kingdom of scooters\" is no exaggeration at all.":"Di kota-kota Taiwan, salah satu pemandangan yang paling membekas bagi pengunjung asing adalah lautan skuter yang memadati ruang di depan saat lampu merah. Begitu berubah hijau, kawanan itu melaju ke depan bagai gelombang pasang, mesin meraung dari segala arah. Taiwan memiliki lebih dari empat belas juta skuter terdaftar — sekitar satu untuk setiap 1,6 orang — jadi menyebutnya \"kerajaan skuter\" sama sekali tidak berlebihan.","Why so many scooters? The reasons are very practical. Scooters are cheap and fuel-efficient; buying one, plus plates and insurance, is far lower a bar than a car. Parking is easy too—curbsides, arcade walkways, and scooter bays everywhere take them. On top of that, Taiwan's urban streets are dense and its lanes narrow, so cars often get stuck in traffic, while a scooter can weave through nimbly, shortening the commute and sparing you the worry of jams and parking spots.":"Mengapa skuter begitu banyak? Alasannya sangat praktis. Skuter murah dan irit bahan bakar; membelinya, ditambah pelat nomor dan asuransi, ambangnya jauh lebih rendah daripada mobil. Parkir pun mudah — tepi jalan, lorong beratap toko, dan area parkir skuter di mana-mana menampungnya. Ditambah lagi, jalan-jalan kota Taiwan padat dan jalurnya sempit, sehingga mobil sering terjebak macet, sementara skuter bisa menyelinap dengan gesit, mempersingkat perjalanan dan membebaskanmu dari kekhawatiran macet dan tempat parkir.","The most spectacular sight is the rush-hour \"scooter waterfall.\" On Taipei's bridges, or at the big intersections of Hsinchu and Tainan, hundreds of scooters wait out the red light together during commute hours and start off together; seen from above, it looks like a flowing waterfall—utterly striking. The scene has even drawn foreign photographers who come specially to shoot it, becoming a cityscape unique to Taiwan.":"Pemandangan paling spektakuler adalah \"air terjun skuter\" saat jam sibuk. Di jembatan-jembatan Taipei, atau di persimpangan besar Hsinchu dan Tainan, ratusan skuter menunggu lampu merah bersama pada jam berangkat kerja lalu melaju bersama; dilihat dari atas, tampak seperti air terjun yang mengalir — sungguh memukau. Pemandangan ini bahkan menarik fotografer asing yang datang khusus untuk memotretnya, menjadi lanskap kota yang khas Taiwan.","Scooters are not just transport but an extension of Taiwanese life itself. In the morning you take the kids to school and grab breakfast on the way; at noon you deliver bento boxes; after work you swing by the market for groceries. The footboard up front holds your bag, a helmet hangs off it, and the rear seat carries people or cargo alike. Many households have no car but always one or two scooters—the whole family's daily life runs on these two wheels.":"Skuter bukan sekadar alat transportasi, melainkan perpanjangan dari kehidupan orang Taiwan itu sendiri. Di pagi hari kamu mengantar anak ke sekolah dan menyambar sarapan di jalan; di siang hari kamu mengantar kotak bento; sepulang kerja kamu mampir ke pasar untuk belanja. Papan pijakan di depan menaruh tasmu, helm tergantung di situ, dan jok belakang mengangkut orang maupun barang. Banyak rumah tangga tak punya mobil tetapi selalu punya satu atau dua skuter — kehidupan sehari-hari seisi keluarga berjalan di atas dua roda ini.","Of course, too many scooters also bring air pollution and noise. In recent years the government has pushed hard for \"trade in the old, switch to the new,\" encouraging people to swap aging two-stroke scooters for electric ones, with subsidies for making the change. Charging and battery-swap stations keep multiplying on the streets, and quiet, emission-free electric scooters are, bit by bit, changing the sound and air of Taiwan's streets.":"Tentu saja, terlalu banyak skuter juga membawa polusi udara dan kebisingan. Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir pemerintah gencar mendorong \"tukar tambah yang lama, ganti yang baru\", mendorong warga menukar skuter dua-tak yang tua dengan yang listrik, disertai subsidi untuk penggantian tersebut. Stasiun pengisian daya dan penukaran baterai terus bertambah di jalanan, dan skuter listrik yang senyap serta bebas emisi, sedikit demi sedikit, mengubah suara dan udara jalanan Taiwan.","For Taiwanese, scooters carry more than commutes—they carry countless memories of life: the nerves of a first ride, the romance of taking a partner out for a spin, the sight of a parent's back as they drove you to school. These two wheels have run through every avenue and alley, carrying generation after generation's days forward. To truly understand Taiwan, perhaps you can start by understanding this \"sea of scooters.\"":"Bagi orang Taiwan, skuter membawa lebih dari sekadar perjalanan pulang-pergi — ia membawa kenangan hidup yang tak terhitung: gugupnya berkendara untuk pertama kali, romantisnya mengajak pasangan berjalan-jalan, pemandangan punggung orang tua saat mengantarmu ke sekolah. Dua roda ini telah menyusuri setiap jalan besar dan gang, membawa hari-hari generasi demi generasi ke depan. Untuk benar-benar memahami Taiwan, mungkin kamu bisa mulai dengan memahami \"lautan skuter\" ini.","scooter, motorbike (the common Taiwan term)":"skuter, sepeda motor (istilah umum di Taiwan)","red light":"lampu merah","fuel-efficient":"irit bahan bakar","covered arcade walkway":"lorong pejalan kaki beratap toko","scooter parking bay":"area parkir skuter","to weave through, shuttle":"menyelinap, hilir-mudik","\"scooter waterfall\" (rush-hour swarm)":"\"air terjun skuter\" (kawanan saat jam sibuk)","food delivery":"pengantaran makanan","trade-in / scrap-and-replace scheme":"program tukar tambah / rongsok-dan-ganti","electric scooter":"skuter listrik","Riding a scooter in Taiwan requires a license (light or heavy classes) and helmets are mandatory. Travelers can rent, but you'll need an international permit plus the original license, and rules differ by engine size, so check ahead. Many intersections use a \"two-stage turn\" (a hook turn for going left), which can confuse newcomers. Even if you don't ride, watch carefully for turning scooters when crossing the street.":"Mengendarai skuter di Taiwan memerlukan SIM (kelas ringan atau berat) dan helm wajib dipakai. Wisatawan boleh menyewa, tetapi kamu perlu izin internasional ditambah SIM asli, dan aturannya berbeda menurut kapasitas mesin, jadi periksa lebih dulu. Banyak persimpangan menerapkan \"belok dua tahap\" (belok kail untuk ke kiri), yang bisa membingungkan pendatang baru. Bahkan jika kamu tidak berkendara, perhatikan dengan saksama skuter yang berbelok saat menyeberang jalan.","Night-Market Street Food: Taiwan's Late-Night Canteen":"Jajanan Kaki Lima Pasar Malam: Kantin Larut Malam Taiwan","When night falls, Taiwan's streets come alive. The night market is the heart of local food culture and the easiest place for a traveler to taste the real Taiwan.":"Ketika malam tiba, jalanan Taiwan menjadi hidup. Pasar malam adalah jantung budaya kuliner lokal dan tempat termudah bagi seorang wisatawan untuk mencicipi Taiwan yang sesungguhnya.","The moment darkness falls, the night market comes awake. The stall lamps flick on one by one, the oil woks begin to sizzle, and the air fills with the smell of scallion oil, sauces, and charcoal fire. Crowds surge in from every direction—office workers off duty, students out of school, whole families hunting for something to eat. For Taiwanese people, the night market is not just a place to eat; it is a way of life.":"Begitu gelap turun, pasar malam terbangun. Lampu kios menyala satu per satu, wajan minyak mulai mendesis, dan udara dipenuhi aroma minyak daun bawang, saus, dan bara arang. Kerumunan berdatangan dari segala arah — pekerja kantoran yang usai bertugas, pelajar yang pulang sekolah, seisi keluarga yang mencari sesuatu untuk dimakan. Bagi orang Taiwan, pasar malam bukan sekadar tempat makan; ia adalah cara hidup.","If we're talking signature dishes, the oyster omelet (ézǐjiān) ranks near the very top. Fresh oysters go in with leafy greens and egg, all bound with a special potato-starch batter and griddled until crisp outside and tender within, then doused with a big spoonful of sweet-and-savory sauce; one bite and the sea floods your mouth. Next door, stinky tofu is a different kind of dare: pungent to the nose but fragrant on the tongue, its skin fried golden and crunchy, served with Taiwanese pickled cabbage whose sour heat cuts the richness—a true favorite for many.":"Kalau bicara hidangan khas, telur dadar tiram (蚵仔煎, ézǐjiān) berada di peringkat teratas. Tiram segar dimasukkan bersama sayuran hijau dan telur, semuanya diikat dengan adonan tepung kentang khusus dan dipanggang di wajan hingga renyah di luar dan lembut di dalam, lalu disiram sesendok besar saus manis-gurih; sekali gigit, laut membanjiri mulutmu. Di sebelahnya, tahu bau adalah tantangan yang berbeda: menyengat di hidung tetapi harum di lidah, kulitnya digoreng keemasan dan renyah, disajikan dengan asinan kubis Taiwan yang rasa asam-pedasnya memotong kegurihannya — favorit sejati bagi banyak orang.","For a proper feast, salt-and-pepper fried chicken (yánsūjī) can't be skipped. The vendor hands you a basket and lets you pick your own: chicken chunks, chicken skin, fishcake, green beans, cauliflower, pork-blood cake—anything can be fried. Hand it back and the boss dumps it all into the roaring oil, then dusts it with peppered salt and tosses in a fistful of Thai basil fried crisp and fragrant. Eat it hot: it scalds your mouth yet you can't stop. And 'big sausage wraps little sausage' is a purely Taiwanese invention: a glutinous-rice sausage split open as the 'bun,' a fragrant grilled pork sausage tucked inside, plus pickled greens, dried radish, and garlic—one bite and it's the taste of Taiwan through and through.":"Untuk jamuan yang pantas, ayam goreng garam-lada (鹽酥雞, yánsūjī) tak boleh dilewatkan. Penjual menyodorkan keranjang dan membiarkanmu memilih sendiri: potongan ayam, kulit ayam, kue ikan, buncis, kembang kol, kue darah babi — apa saja bisa digoreng. Serahkan kembali dan si bos menuang semuanya ke minyak yang menggelegak, lalu menaburinya dengan garam berlada dan melemparkan segenggam daun kemangi Thai yang digoreng renyah dan harum. Makanlah selagi panas: mulutmu tersengat namun kamu tak bisa berhenti. Dan 'sosis besar membungkus sosis kecil' (大腸包小腸) adalah kreasi murni Taiwan: sosis beras ketan dibelah sebagai 'roti', sosis babi bakar yang harum diselipkan di dalamnya, ditambah asinan sayur, lobak kering, dan bawang putih — sekali gigit dan itulah cita rasa Taiwan seutuhnya.","After all these bold flavors, you naturally want a cup of bubble tea. Taiwan is its birthplace: rich black tea blended with fresh milk, chewy brown-sugar tapioca pearls settled at the bottom, drawn up through a fat straw in one pull—sweet but never cloying. When ordering you can customize it too: choose half-sugar or light-sugar, less ice or no ice, entirely to your own taste. Bubble tea in one hand, fried chicken in the other—this is the most authentic way to eat at a night market.":"Setelah semua cita rasa yang kuat ini, wajar kamu menginginkan segelas bubble tea. Taiwan adalah tempat kelahirannya: teh hitam pekat dicampur susu segar, mutiara tapioka gula merah yang kenyal mengendap di dasar, disedot lewat sedotan besar dalam satu tarikan — manis tapi tak pernah bikin enek. Saat memesan kamu juga bisa menyesuaikannya: pilih setengah gula atau gula sedikit, es sedikit atau tanpa es, sepenuhnya sesuai seleramu sendiri. Bubble tea di satu tangan, ayam goreng di tangan lain — inilah cara paling autentik menikmati santapan di pasar malam.","Ordering is actually easy—just memorize a few phrases. To ask the price, say 'How much is this?'; to commit, say 'I'll take one portion'; if you fear spice, say 'no chili' or 'mild.' The vendor is usually friendly and will even ask, 'For here or to go?' One thing to note: many stalls take cash only, so it's best to keep some small change ready—though in recent years more and more vendors accept mobile payment.":"Memesan sebenarnya mudah — cukup hafalkan beberapa kalimat. Untuk menanyakan harga, ucapkan 'Ini berapa harganya?'; untuk memastikan, ucapkan 'Saya mau satu porsi'; jika takut pedas, ucapkan 'tanpa cabai' atau 'sedikit pedas'. Penjualnya biasanya ramah dan bahkan akan bertanya, 'Makan di sini atau dibawa pulang?' Satu hal yang perlu dicatat: banyak kios hanya menerima tunai, jadi sebaiknya siapkan uang receh — meski dalam beberapa tahun terakhir makin banyak penjual yang menerima pembayaran lewat ponsel.","The reason the night market is the heart of Taiwanese food life is that it fuses 'cheap,' 'delicious,' and 'lively' into one. Here, a couple hundred dollars buys a fully satisfying meal, plus the most genuine human warmth. From Shilin and Raohe to Fengjia and Liuhe, every city has a night market of its own. If you want to truly know Taiwan, don't stop at restaurants—step into a night market, join the flow of the crowd, eat as you walk, and you'll understand.":"Alasan pasar malam menjadi jantung kehidupan kuliner Taiwan adalah karena ia memadukan 'murah', 'lezat', dan 'ramai' menjadi satu. Di sini, beberapa ratus dolar membeli santapan yang sepenuhnya memuaskan, ditambah kehangatan manusiawi yang paling tulus. Dari Shilin dan Raohe hingga Fengjia dan Liuhe, setiap kota punya pasar malamnya sendiri. Jika kamu ingin benar-benar mengenal Taiwan, jangan berhenti di restoran — melangkahlah ke pasar malam, larut dalam arus kerumunan, makan sambil berjalan, dan kamu akan mengerti.","street stall / vendor":"kios kaki lima / penjaja","oyster omelet":"telur dadar tiram","stinky tofu":"tahu bau","salt-and-pepper fried chicken":"ayam goreng garam-lada","grilled sausage in a rice-sausage 'bun'":"sosis bakar dalam 'roti' sosis beras","bubble (pearl) milk tea":"teh susu mutiara (bubble tea)","to customize":"menyesuaikan","to eat in / dine in":"makan di tempat","to take out":"dibawa pulang","human warmth / friendliness":"kehangatan manusiawi / keramahan","The measure word 'fèn' means 'one portion/serving' and 'one order (yí fèn)' is incredibly handy at stalls. It also pays to learn the sweetness scale: full sugar is standard, half sugar is 50%, light sugar is very little, no sugar is none. For ice, the levels go regular, less, light, and none. Next time you're in Taiwan, try ordering 'half sugar, less ice' yourself.":"Kata bantu bilangan '份' (fèn) berarti 'satu porsi/sajian' dan 'satu porsi (一份, yí fèn)' sangat praktis di kios-kios. Ada baiknya juga mempelajari skala kemanisan: gula penuh adalah standar, setengah gula adalah 50%, gula sedikit adalah sangat sedikit, tanpa gula berarti tidak ada. Untuk es, tingkatannya adalah biasa, kurang, sedikit, dan tanpa es. Lain kali di Taiwan, coba pesan sendiri 'setengah gula, es sedikit'.","Taiwan's Breakfast Shops: How the Day Begins":"Kedai Sarapan Taiwan: Bagaimana Hari Dimulai","A Taiwanese day begins at the corner breakfast shop—cheap, fast, and endlessly varied. It's a morning culture all its own.":"Hari orang Taiwan dimulai di kedai sarapan pojok jalan — murah, cepat, dan sangat beragam. Ia adalah budaya pagi yang khas.","In Taiwan, you can find a breakfast shop on almost every street corner. The red signs with white letters read 'Mei-er-Mei,' 'Hong-Ye,' or 'Mai-Wei-Deng'—chains that blanket the island and mark the starting point of many people's day. By six or seven in the morning the griddle is already sizzling, and the deft shop owner flips egg crepes while calling out, 'Number three's ready!'":"Di Taiwan, kamu bisa menemukan kedai sarapan di hampir setiap sudut jalan. Papan merah berhuruf putih bertuliskan 'Mei-er-Mei' (美而美), 'Hong-Ye' (弘爺), atau 'Mai-Wei-Deng' (麥味登) — jaringan yang menyelimuti seluruh pulau dan menandai titik awal hari bagi banyak orang. Pada pukul enam atau tujuh pagi wajan datar sudah mendesis, dan pemilik kedai yang cekatan membalik dadar telur sambil berseru, 'Nomor tiga sudah siap!'","The signature of signatures has to be the egg crepe (dànbǐng). A thin batter skin gets an egg cracked over it, is griddled until lightly browned, then rolled up, cut into segments, and drizzled with the shop's own thick soy sauce. The base is plain, but you can add toppings: cheese, corn, tuna, ham, bacon, even Thai basil. A bite is crisp outside and soft within, the egg and batter aromas intertwining; paired with a cup of warm soy milk, it's simple yet comforting—the most classic Taiwanese breakfast.":"Yang paling khas dari yang khas tentu adalah dadar telur (蛋餅, dànbǐng). Kulit adonan tipis dipecahkan telur di atasnya, dipanggang di wajan datar hingga sedikit kecokelatan, lalu digulung, dipotong-potong, dan disiram kecap kental khas kedai itu. Dasarnya polos, tetapi kamu bisa menambah topping: keju, jagung, tuna, ham, bacon, bahkan daun kemangi Thai. Sekali gigit renyah di luar dan lembut di dalam, aroma telur dan adonan berpadu; dipadukan dengan segelas susu kedelai hangat, sederhana namun menenteramkan — sarapan Taiwan yang paling klasik.","If you want something saltier and more filling, the choices are plenty. Turnip cake (luóbogāo) is griddled golden on both sides, crisp outside and soft within, best with a drizzle of thick soy sauce. The rice roll (fàntuán) wraps glutinous rice around a fried cruller, dried radish, and pork floss, squeezed into a firm cylinder—one keeps you going till noon. Noodle lovers order iron-plate noodles (tiěbǎnmiàn), tossed in black pepper or mushroom sauce with a soft-yolk egg, carried to the table still steaming on the hot plate—a favorite of many students and office workers.":"Jika kamu ingin sesuatu yang lebih asin dan mengenyangkan, pilihannya banyak. Kue lobak (蘿蔔糕, luóbogāo) dipanggang keemasan di kedua sisi, renyah di luar dan lembut di dalam, paling enak disiram kecap kental. Gulung nasi (飯糰, fàntuán) membungkus beras ketan mengelilingi cakwe goreng, lobak kering, dan abon babi, dipadatkan menjadi silinder yang kokoh — satu saja membuatmu bertahan sampai siang. Pencinta mi memesan mi pelat besi (鐵板麵, tiěbǎnmiàn), diaduk dengan saus lada hitam atau saus jamur dengan telur setengah matang, dibawa ke meja masih mengepul di atas pelat panas — favorit banyak pelajar dan pekerja kantoran.","For drinks, soy milk plays the soul role. Hot soy milk is fragrant and smooth—cradling a cup in winter is especially warming—while iced soy milk is refreshing and quenching. Besides soy milk, there's rice milk, black tea, and milk tea. Here's a code phrase you must learn: 'dà bīng nǎi,' short for 'large iced milk tea.' Walk into a breakfast shop and just say 'one egg crepe, one large iced milk tea,' and the owner instantly gets it. That practiced, unspoken rapport is exactly the charm of Taiwan's breakfast shops.":"Untuk minuman, susu kedelai memegang peran jiwa. Susu kedelai panas harum dan lembut — memeluk segelas di musim dingin terasa amat menghangatkan — sedangkan susu kedelai dingin menyegarkan dan melepas dahaga. Selain susu kedelai, ada susu beras, teh hitam, dan teh susu. Ini kalimat sandi yang wajib kamu pelajari: '大冰奶' (dà bīng nǎi), singkatan dari 'teh susu dingin ukuran besar'. Masuklah ke kedai sarapan dan cukup ucapkan 'satu dadar telur, satu teh susu dingin besar', dan pemiliknya langsung mengerti. Keakraban tanpa kata yang sudah terlatih itulah justru pesona kedai sarapan Taiwan.","For many Taiwanese, the breakfast shop is not just a place to fill your stomach but a daily ritual. Students line up at the door before school, office workers rushing to clock in grab a portion to go as they ride past, and retired grandpas and grandmas sit inside eating slowly, chatting a few words with the owner. These little breakfast shops string together the whole neighborhood's mornings and record the daily lives of countless people.":"Bagi banyak orang Taiwan, kedai sarapan bukan sekadar tempat mengisi perut, melainkan ritual harian. Pelajar mengantre di depan pintu sebelum sekolah, pekerja kantoran yang terburu-buru absen menyambar satu porsi untuk dibawa sambil lewat, dan kakek-nenek pensiunan duduk di dalam makan perlahan, mengobrol beberapa patah kata dengan pemiliknya. Kedai-kedai sarapan kecil ini merangkai pagi seluruh lingkungan dan mencatat kehidupan sehari-hari banyak sekali orang.","Taiwan's breakfast culture grew this rich because it's tied to the rhythm of life. Busy city dwellers have no time to cook at home, and breakfast shops are cheap, fast, and full of choices, so they naturally became everyone's kitchen. For fifty or sixty dollars you get made-to-order hot food, mixed and matched to your taste. Next time you land in Taiwan early, don't forget to step into a breakfast shop, order an egg crepe with a large iced milk tea, and begin the day the most Taiwanese way there is.":"Budaya sarapan Taiwan tumbuh sekaya ini karena terikat pada irama kehidupan. Warga kota yang sibuk tak punya waktu memasak di rumah, dan kedai sarapan murah, cepat, serta penuh pilihan, jadi secara alami menjadi dapur semua orang. Dengan lima puluh atau enam puluh dolar kamu mendapat makanan panas yang dibuat sesuai pesanan, dipadupadankan sesuai seleramu. Lain kali kamu tiba pagi-pagi di Taiwan, jangan lupa melangkah ke kedai sarapan, pesan dadar telur dengan teh susu dingin besar, dan mulailah hari dengan cara yang paling Taiwan.","egg crepe / egg pancake roll":"dadar telur / gulung panekuk telur","turnip / radish cake":"kue lobak","rice roll / rice ball":"gulung nasi / bola nasi","soy milk":"susu kedelai","iron-plate noodles":"mi pelat besi","fried dough cruller":"cakwe goreng","thick sweet soy sauce":"kecap manis kental","large iced milk tea (slang)":"teh susu dingin besar (bahasa gaul)","chain store":"toko waralaba / jaringan toko","to add toppings":"menambah topping","ritual":"ritual","Like 'dà bīng nǎi,' Taiwanese drink orders are often abbreviated: 'dà' = large, 'bīng' = iced, 'nǎi' = milk tea. By the same logic you can say 'dà bīng hóng' (large iced black tea) or 'rè dòujiāng' (hot soy milk). Drink sizes are large, medium, and small, and these short orders come across as smooth and local at stalls and breakfast shops.":"Seperti '大冰奶' (dà bīng nǎi), pesanan minuman orang Taiwan sering disingkat: '大' (dà) = besar, '冰' (bīng) = dingin, '奶' (nǎi) = teh susu. Dengan logika yang sama kamu bisa mengucapkan '大冰紅' (dà bīng hóng, teh hitam dingin besar) atau '熱豆漿' (rè dòujiāng, susu kedelai panas). Ukuran minuman ada besar, sedang, dan kecil, dan pesanan singkat ini terdengar lancar dan lokal di kios-kios serta kedai sarapan.","Bento Culture: The Taste of Taiwan in One Box":"Budaya Bento: Cita Rasa Taiwan dalam Satu Kotak","Ask a Taiwanese person about lunch and the first thing that comes to mind is the biàndāng—a box of rice and dishes that sustains the daily life of workers and students alike.":"Tanyakan pada orang Taiwan soal makan siang dan hal pertama yang terlintas adalah biàndāng (便當) — sekotak nasi dan lauk yang menopang kehidupan sehari-hari para pekerja maupun pelajar.","By noon, the areas around Taiwan's office towers and schools grow lively. Long lines form outside bento shops, and the rising steam carries the scent of braising sauce and fried food. The biàndāng is the most common lunch choice for Taiwanese people. Inside a foam or paper box lies a full bed of white rice, topped with one main dish and a few side dishes—generous in portion, gentle on the wallet, and enough to power you through the whole afternoon.":"Menjelang siang, area di sekitar gedung perkantoran dan sekolah di Taiwan menjadi ramai. Antrean panjang terbentuk di depan kedai bento, dan uap yang mengepul membawa aroma saus rebusan dan gorengan. Biàndāng (便當) adalah pilihan makan siang paling umum bagi orang Taiwan. Di dalam kotak busa atau kertas terhampar nasi putih yang penuh, dilengkapi satu lauk utama dan beberapa lauk sampingan — porsinya royal, ramah di kantong, dan cukup untuk menyokongmu sepanjang sore.","When it comes to the bento's main dish, the pork-chop bento and chicken-leg bento are the two great kings. The pork chop is a large cutlet, marinated first, then dredged in flour and deep-fried—crisp outside, tender within, wrapped in soy fragrance. The chicken-leg bento is a whole leg either braised until deeply flavored or fried golden, juicy and substantial—the number one for many. Beyond these there are braised pork chop, braised pork belly, fish cutlet, and more; just choosing the main can leave you hesitating a good long while.":"Soal lauk utama bento, bento iga babi dan bento paha ayam adalah dua raja besar. Iga babi berupa potongan besar, dibumbui dulu, lalu dibalur tepung dan digoreng rendam — renyah di luar, empuk di dalam, terbalut aroma kecap. Bento paha ayam adalah paha utuh yang direbus hingga meresap bumbunya atau digoreng keemasan, berair dan mengenyangkan — nomor satu bagi banyak orang. Selain itu ada iga babi kecap, perut babi kecap, potongan ikan, dan banyak lagi; sekadar memilih lauk utama saja bisa membuatmu ragu cukup lama.","If you want more freedom, head to a zìzhùcān, the self-serve cafeteria. Along the wall stretches a whole row of trays—leafy greens, tofu, braised eggs, scrambled eggs, three-cup chicken, sweet-and-sour fish—dozens of dishes for you to pick. You can serve yourself or ask the auntie to plate it; a common combo is 'three veg, one meat'—three sides plus one main, nutritious and balanced. The auntie's tongs estimate the price as she serves, billing by the dishes at checkout: you pay for what you eat, which is a great deal.":"Jika kamu ingin lebih bebas, pergilah ke zìzhùcān (自助餐), kantin swalayan. Di sepanjang dinding terbentang sebaris penuh nampan — sayuran hijau, tahu, telur kecap, telur orak-arik, ayam tiga cangkir (三杯雞), ikan asam manis — puluhan hidangan untuk kamu pilih. Kamu bisa mengambil sendiri atau meminta si ibu untuk menatanya; kombinasi umum adalah 'tiga sayur, satu daging' — tiga lauk sampingan ditambah satu lauk utama, bergizi dan seimbang. Penjepit si ibu memperkirakan harga saat ia menyajikan, menagih berdasarkan lauknya di kasir: kamu membayar sesuai yang kamu makan, sungguh menguntungkan.","Within Taiwan's bento family there's also a special member—the railway bento. Buying a piping-hot railway bento on the platform or in the carriage while traveling by train is a shared memory for many. The classic pork-chop railway bento presses a braised chop onto white rice, paired with a braised egg, dried tofu, pickled greens, and a piece of leafy vegetable—simple yet hearty. The moment you open the round metal tin or paper box, the braising aroma hits your nose, the scenery flies past the window, and the taste is especially unforgettable.":"Dalam keluarga bento Taiwan juga ada anggota istimewa — bento kereta api. Membeli bento kereta api yang panas mengepul di peron atau di dalam gerbong saat bepergian dengan kereta adalah kenangan bersama bagi banyak orang. Bento kereta iga babi yang klasik menekan sepotong iga kecap di atas nasi putih, dipadu telur kecap, tahu kering, asinan sayur, dan sepotong sayuran hijau — sederhana namun mengenyangkan. Begitu kamu membuka kaleng logam bundar atau kotak kertasnya, aroma rebusan menyergap hidungmu, pemandangan melintas cepat di jendela, dan rasanya sungguh tak terlupakan.","The bento matters so much in Taiwan because it fits busy life perfectly. Office workers get only an hour for lunch; order a bento or run downstairs to buy one, and you can eat right back at your desk. Schools often have catered group-meal bentos delivered, and a whole class eating bentos together at noon is a student-era memory for many. Some companies even have someone place a bulk order for everyone: come noon, a stack of bentos arrives in the office and the aroma instantly fills the whole floor.":"Bento begitu berarti di Taiwan karena ia sangat pas dengan kehidupan yang sibuk. Pekerja kantoran hanya punya satu jam untuk makan siang; pesan bento atau turun sebentar untuk membelinya, dan kamu bisa langsung makan kembali di mejamu. Sekolah sering menyediakan bento katering untuk makan bersama yang diantar, dan sekelas makan bento bersama saat siang adalah kenangan masa sekolah bagi banyak orang. Beberapa perusahaan bahkan menugaskan seseorang untuk memesan dalam jumlah besar bagi semua: menjelang siang, setumpuk bento tiba di kantor dan aromanya seketika memenuhi seluruh lantai.","From the corner bento shop to the railway bento on the train, from office orders to school lunches, the biàndāng threads through Taiwanese working and student life. It doesn't chase grandeur; what it values is substance, convenience, and a warm, full belly. Next time you're in Taiwan, don't rush to find a restaurant—step into a bento shop, point at the glass case, and say 'I'll have a pork-chop bento.' That's the meal closest to everyday Taiwanese life.":"Dari kedai bento pojok jalan hingga bento kereta di atas kereta api, dari pesanan kantor hingga makan siang sekolah, biàndāng (便當) menyusup ke seluruh kehidupan kerja dan pelajar orang Taiwan. Ia tidak mengejar kemewahan; yang ia hargai adalah isi, kepraktisan, dan perut yang hangat dan kenyang. Lain kali kamu di Taiwan, jangan buru-buru mencari restoran — melangkahlah ke kedai bento, tunjuk lemari kaca, dan ucapkan 'Saya mau bento iga babi.' Itulah santapan yang paling dekat dengan kehidupan sehari-hari orang Taiwan.","bento / boxed lunch":"bento / nasi kotak","pork chop / pork rib":"iga babi / kotelet babi","chicken leg / thigh":"paha ayam","self-serve cafeteria":"kantin swalayan","three sides and one meat":"tiga lauk sampingan dan satu daging","railway bento":"bento kereta api","main dish":"lauk utama","side dish":"lauk sampingan","braised (soy) egg":"telur kecap (rebus)","portion / amount":"porsi / takaran","a good deal / worth it":"menguntungkan / sepadan","to order a meal":"memesan makanan","'Biàndāng' is the standard Taiwanese word for a boxed lunch. The 'three veg, one meat' combo used at self-serve cafeterias means picking three sides and one meat dish. To order, 'I'll have one pork-chop bento' with the measure word 'yí ge' (one) works perfectly. At self-serve places the bill is set by the number and type of dishes, so let the staff tally it—they'll do it fast.":"'便當' (biàndāng) adalah kata standar orang Taiwan untuk nasi kotak. Kombinasi 'tiga sayur, satu daging' yang dipakai di kantin swalayan berarti memilih tiga lauk sampingan dan satu lauk daging. Untuk memesan, 'Saya mau satu bento iga babi' dengan kata bantu bilangan '一個' (yí ge, satu) sudah sempurna. Di tempat swalayan tagihan ditentukan oleh jumlah dan jenis lauk, jadi biarkan petugas menghitungnya — mereka melakukannya dengan cepat.","Lunar New Year: The Warmest Reunion of the Year":"Tahun Baru Imlek: Reuni Paling Hangat Sepanjang Tahun","The whole town glows with red lanterns and 'spring couplets,' the smell of slow-cooked dishes drifts from every home, and family members who live apart all head back to their hometowns at once—in Taiwan, 'guònián' is not just a holiday but the most important reunion of the year. From the reunion hotpot on New Year's Eve to red envelopes and temple visits, let's take a peek at the Taiwanese New Year.":"Seluruh kota bersinar dengan lampion merah dan 'bait kuplet musim semi', aroma masakan yang dimasak lama menyebar dari setiap rumah, dan anggota keluarga yang tinggal terpisah semuanya pulang ke kampung halaman sekaligus — di Taiwan, 'guònián' (過年) bukan sekadar hari libur, melainkan reuni terpenting sepanjang tahun. Dari hotpot reuni di Malam Tahun Baru hingga angpau dan ziarah ke kuil, mari kita mengintip Tahun Baru ala Taiwan.","When Taiwanese say 'guònián,' they mean the lunar New Year, which usually falls in late January or early February on the solar calendar—unlike the January 1st New Year most countries celebrate. Guònián isn't just one day but a whole stretch of festivity: from the big pre–New Year's Eve house cleaning and shopping for New Year goods, to the reunion hotpot on New Year's Eve, to the rounds of New Year greetings and outings from the first through the fifth day. All told, the buzz can last nearly half a month. For many who work or study away from home, guònián is simply the time you go home 'no matter what.'":"Ketika orang Taiwan berkata 'guònián' (過年), yang mereka maksud adalah Tahun Baru Imlek, yang biasanya jatuh pada akhir Januari atau awal Februari dalam penanggalan Masehi — berbeda dari Tahun Baru 1 Januari yang dirayakan kebanyakan negara. Guònián bukan sekadar satu hari, melainkan rentang perayaan yang utuh: dari bersih-bersih rumah besar-besaran menjelang Malam Tahun Baru dan berbelanja perlengkapan Tahun Baru, ke hotpot reuni di Malam Tahun Baru, hingga rangkaian ucapan selamat Tahun Baru dan jalan-jalan dari hari pertama sampai kelima. Secara keseluruhan, keramaiannya bisa berlangsung hampir setengah bulan. Bagi banyak orang yang bekerja atau menuntut ilmu jauh dari rumah, guònián adalah saat kamu pulang 'apa pun yang terjadi'.","The most important meal of the New Year is the 'reunion dinner' on New Year's Eve, which Taiwanese often call 'wéilú' (gathering around the pot). The whole family sits around the table, which always holds several auspicious dishes: eating fish means 'surplus year after year,' eating long leafy greens means 'long and lasting,' eating meatballs means 'togetherness and reunion,' and dumplings resemble old gold ingots, symbolizing wealth. No matter how busy people usually are or how far away they live, on this one night everyone tries their best to rush home and finish this meal together.":"Santapan terpenting saat Tahun Baru adalah 'makan malam reuni' di Malam Tahun Baru, yang orang Taiwan sering sebut 'wéilú' (圍爐, berkumpul mengelilingi tungku). Seluruh keluarga duduk mengelilingi meja, yang selalu menyajikan beberapa hidangan pembawa keberuntungan: makan ikan berarti 'berlebih tahun demi tahun' (年年有餘), makan sayuran hijau berbatang panjang berarti 'panjang dan langgeng', makan bakso berarti 'kebersamaan dan reuni', dan pangsit menyerupai batangan emas kuno, melambangkan kekayaan. Sesibuk apa pun orang biasanya atau sejauh apa pun mereka tinggal, pada satu malam ini semua orang berusaha sekuat tenaga bergegas pulang untuk menuntaskan santapan ini bersama-sama.","After the reunion dinner comes the moment children look forward to most—handing out 'red envelopes.' Elders tuck money into small red pouches, the 'hóngbāo,' and give them to the younger generation, wishing them peace, health, and smooth sailing in the new year. Children who receive them say a few auspicious phrases like 'Happy New Year,' 'Wishing you prosperity,' and 'Good health.' Once children grow up and start earning, the roles reverse and they give red envelopes to their parents and grandparents (āgōng, āmà). This switching of roles is a form of filial piety that Taiwanese hold dear.":"Setelah makan malam reuni tibalah momen yang paling dinanti anak-anak — membagikan 'angpau'. Para orang tua menyelipkan uang ke dalam kantong merah kecil, sang 'hóngbāo' (紅包), dan memberikannya kepada generasi muda, mendoakan mereka damai, sehat, dan lancar sepanjang tahun baru. Anak-anak yang menerimanya mengucapkan beberapa kalimat pembawa keberuntungan seperti 'Selamat Tahun Baru', 'Semoga makmur', dan 'Sehat selalu'. Setelah anak-anak dewasa dan mulai berpenghasilan, peran pun terbalik dan mereka memberikan angpau kepada orang tua serta kakek-nenek (阿公 āgōng, 阿嬤 āmà). Pertukaran peran ini adalah wujud bakti yang dijunjung tinggi orang Taiwan.","New Year's Eve has another special custom called 'shǒusuì' (staying up through the night). After the meal and the red envelopes, the family doesn't rush to bed but stays up together chatting, watching special TV programs, and playing cards or board games, trying to keep vigil past midnight. Traditionally, shǒusuì is thought to 'add years' to the elders' lives and symbolizes treasuring the year's final hours—sending off the old year properly and welcoming the new one. At midnight, every household sets off firecrackers and fireworks, using loud sounds to chase away the 'nián' (a legendary beast) and welcome the New Year through the door.":"Malam Tahun Baru punya adat istimewa lain yang disebut 'shǒusuì' (守歲, berjaga sepanjang malam). Setelah santapan dan angpau, keluarga tidak buru-buru tidur, melainkan begadang bersama sambil mengobrol, menonton acara TV spesial, dan bermain kartu atau permainan papan, berusaha berjaga hingga lewat tengah malam. Menurut tradisi, shǒusuì diyakini 'menambah usia' para orang tua dan melambangkan menghargai jam-jam terakhir tahun itu — mengantar tahun lama dengan layak dan menyambut yang baru. Pada tengah malam, setiap rumah menyalakan petasan dan kembang api, memakai bunyi keras untuk mengusir 'nián' (年, seekor binatang buas legendaris) dan menyambut Tahun Baru masuk ke pintu.","Starting on New Year's Day (the first day), it becomes time for 'bàinián' (New Year greetings) and 'zǒuchūn' (spring outings). People put on new clothes, visit the homes of relatives and friends, exchange 'Happy New Year,' and along the way stop by temples to worship and draw a fortune stick, praying for a smooth year—this is 'zǒuchūn.' Taiwanese also value the custom of 'married daughters returning to their parents' home on the second day': on this day a married daughter brings her husband and children back to her own parents' house to celebrate, filling that home with cheer too. During the New Year, shops often have long queues and highways jam up bumper to bumper, because nearly everyone in Taiwan is on the move and reuniting.":"Mulai Hari Tahun Baru (hari pertama), tibalah waktu untuk 'bàinián' (拜年, ucapan selamat Tahun Baru) dan 'zǒuchūn' (走春, jalan-jalan musim semi). Orang-orang mengenakan pakaian baru, mengunjungi rumah kerabat dan teman, saling mengucapkan 'Selamat Tahun Baru', dan sepanjang jalan mampir ke kuil untuk bersembahyang dan menarik batang ramalan, mendoakan tahun yang lancar — inilah 'zǒuchūn'. Orang Taiwan juga menjunjung adat 'anak perempuan yang telah menikah pulang ke rumah orang tuanya pada hari kedua': pada hari ini seorang anak perempuan yang sudah menikah membawa suami dan anak-anaknya kembali ke rumah orang tuanya sendiri untuk merayakan, memenuhi rumah itu dengan keceriaan pula. Selama Tahun Baru, toko-toko sering mengular antreannya dan jalan tol macet beringsut-ingsut, karena hampir semua orang di Taiwan sedang bepergian dan berkumpul kembali.","For a foreigner spending the New Year in Taiwan for the first time, the deepest impression is often not the firecrackers or the red envelopes but the sheer pull of 'going home.' You'll notice that this normally fast-paced, very modern society suddenly slows down during these few days, saving most of its time for family. If you have Taiwanese friends, you may well be invited to share a reunion dinner; that steaming hotpot and a table full of auspicious words will let you truly feel how Taiwanese express their love for family through food and togetherness.":"Bagi orang asing yang merayakan Tahun Baru di Taiwan untuk pertama kalinya, kesan yang paling dalam sering kali bukan petasan atau angpau, melainkan daya tarik yang begitu kuat dari 'pulang ke rumah'. Kamu akan menyadari bahwa masyarakat yang biasanya serba cepat dan sangat modern ini tiba-tiba melambat selama beberapa hari ini, menyisihkan sebagian besar waktunya untuk keluarga. Jika kamu punya teman orang Taiwan, kamu mungkin saja diundang menikmati makan malam reuni; hotpot yang mengepul dan meja yang penuh kata-kata pembawa keberuntungan itu akan membuatmu benar-benar merasakan bagaimana orang Taiwan mengungkapkan cinta kepada keluarga melalui makanan dan kebersamaan.","to celebrate Lunar New Year":"merayakan Tahun Baru Imlek","New Year's Eve":"Malam Tahun Baru","reunion dinner around the pot":"makan malam reuni mengelilingi tungku","New Year's Eve reunion dinner":"makan malam reuni Malam Tahun Baru","red envelope (of money)":"angpau (berisi uang)","staying up on New Year's Eve":"begadang di Malam Tahun Baru","paying New Year visits":"berkunjung mengucapkan selamat Tahun Baru","New Year outings (incl. temple visits)":"jalan-jalan Tahun Baru (termasuk ziarah ke kuil)","auspicious phrases":"ucapan-ucapan yang membawa keberuntungan","wishing you wealth (common New Year greeting)":"semoga banyak rezeki (ucapan Tahun Baru yang umum)","shopping for New Year goods":"berbelanja kebutuhan Tahun Baru","In Taiwan, there's a custom of not sweeping on the first day of the New Year, because sweeping out the good fortune and wealth that has just arrived is considered unlucky. And if you drop and break something, you calmly say 'suìsuì píng'ān' (may every year be peaceful) to undo the bad omen—a pun on 'suì' (to shatter) sounding the same as 'suì' (year). The Lunar New Year holiday is one of Taiwan's longest breaks, and many shops close for several days, so if you're traveling, don't forget to check opening hours.":"Di Taiwan ada kebiasaan tidak menyapu pada hari pertama Tahun Baru, karena menyapu keluar keberuntungan dan rezeki yang baru saja datang dianggap membawa sial. Dan kalau kamu tidak sengaja menjatuhkan lalu memecahkan sesuatu, kamu dengan tenang mengucapkan 'suìsuì píng'ān' (semoga setiap tahun tenteram) untuk menangkal firasat buruk—sebuah permainan kata karena 'suì' (pecah) terdengar sama dengan 'suì' (tahun). Libur Tahun Baru Imlek adalah salah satu libur terpanjang di Taiwan, dan banyak toko tutup selama beberapa hari, jadi kalau kamu bepergian, jangan lupa mengecek jam buka.","Ghost Month & the Zhongyuan Festival: A Little Kindness for the Unseen World":"Bulan Hantu & Festival Zhongyuan: Sedikit Kebaikan untuk Dunia yang Tak Terlihat","When the seventh lunar month arrives, fruit, snacks, and drinks line up in front of shops and homes all over Taiwan, and incense smoke rises into the air. During this month known as 'Ghost Month,' Taiwanese don't so much fear it as graciously host 'guests from the other world.' Let's peek into a world of belief unique to Taiwan, where awe and kindness live side by side.":"Ketika bulan ketujuh penanggalan lunar tiba, buah-buahan, camilan, dan minuman berjajar di depan toko dan rumah di seluruh Taiwan, dan asap dupa mengepul ke udara. Selama bulan yang dikenal sebagai 'Bulan Hantu' ini, orang Taiwan tidak begitu takut, melainkan dengan ramah menjamu 'tamu dari dunia lain'. Mari kita mengintip sebuah dunia kepercayaan yang khas Taiwan, tempat rasa hormat dan kebaikan hidup berdampingan.","In Taiwan's traditional beliefs, the seventh lunar month is called 'Ghost Month.' Legend says that at the start of this month the gates of the underworld open, and the spirits who normally dwell in the other world can return to the human realm to wander and receive people's offerings. Taiwanese don't call them 'ghosts' outright but politely refer to them as 'good brothers,' with a feeling of respect and a wish not to offend. Throughout the month, the social mood becomes more restrained and careful—yet not full of fear, more like 'showing a little more courtesy to unseen guests.'":"Dalam kepercayaan tradisional Taiwan, bulan ketujuh lunar disebut 'Bulan Hantu'. Menurut legenda, pada awal bulan ini gerbang dunia bawah terbuka, dan arwah yang biasanya tinggal di dunia lain dapat kembali ke alam manusia untuk berkeliaran dan menerima persembahan orang-orang. Orang Taiwan tidak menyebut mereka 'hantu' secara terang-terangan, melainkan dengan sopan menyebut mereka 'saudara-saudara baik', dengan perasaan hormat dan harapan agar tidak menyinggung. Sepanjang bulan itu, suasana sosial menjadi lebih menahan diri dan berhati-hati—namun bukan penuh ketakutan, lebih seperti 'menunjukkan sedikit lebih banyak kesopanan kepada tamu yang tak terlihat'.","The most important activity of Ghost Month is 'pǔdù' (the universal deliverance rite). Pǔdù means preparing lavish offerings to host these good brothers who have returned to the human world—letting them eat their fill and be cared for so they won't cause trouble out of neglect. Families, companies, communities, and temples all hold pǔdù: tables are piled with fruit, biscuits, drinks, instant noodles, and snacks, plus a whole chicken and a whole fish, with incense and candles burning in front. After the worship, the offerings aren't wasted but shared among everyone, symbolizing 'sharing' this gesture of care with the good brothers.":"Kegiatan terpenting Bulan Hantu adalah 'pǔdù' (ritual penyelamatan universal). Pǔdù berarti menyiapkan persembahan yang melimpah untuk menjamu para saudara baik yang telah kembali ke dunia manusia—membiarkan mereka makan sampai kenyang dan diperhatikan agar mereka tidak membuat masalah karena diabaikan. Keluarga, perusahaan, komunitas, dan kuil semuanya mengadakan pǔdù: meja-meja penuh dengan buah, biskuit, minuman, mi instan, dan camilan, ditambah seekor ayam utuh dan seekor ikan utuh, dengan dupa dan lilin menyala di depannya. Setelah sembahyang, persembahan itu tidak disia-siakan melainkan dibagikan kepada semua orang, melambangkan 'berbagi' bentuk kepedulian ini dengan para saudara baik.","To help the good brothers find their way, there are thoughtful arrangements too. In some places people 'float water lanterns' on rivers or by the sea, letting small lights drift along the current to light the way home for spirits in the water. In front of temples, tall 'lonely-soul scaffolds' are often built, stacking offerings up high in a truly spectacular sight. These rituals look festive, but behind them hides a very gentle idea: no matter who you are, where you come from, or whether you have descendants to make offerings, in this month everyone deserves to be treated well.":"Untuk membantu para saudara baik menemukan jalan mereka, ada pula pengaturan yang penuh perhatian. Di beberapa tempat orang 'menghanyutkan lampion air' di sungai atau di tepi laut, membiarkan lampu-lampu kecil mengalir mengikuti arus untuk menerangi jalan pulang bagi arwah di dalam air. Di depan kuil sering dibangun 'panggung jiwa kesepian' yang tinggi, menumpuk persembahan tinggi-tinggi dalam pemandangan yang sungguh menakjubkan. Ritual-ritual ini tampak meriah, tetapi di baliknya tersembunyi sebuah gagasan yang sangat lembut: siapa pun kamu, dari mana asalmu, atau apakah kamu punya keturunan yang mempersembahkan sesajen, di bulan ini setiap orang layak diperlakukan dengan baik.","Ghost Month also has quite a few 'taboos'—things your elders will remind you are 'best not to do this month.' Commonly heard ones include: don't go swimming at the beach or river at night, because legend says water spirits look for 'a substitute'; bring in clothes left drying outside at night so the good brothers don't 'borrow and wear' them; and if you hear someone call your name in the dead of night, don't casually turn around and answer. Moreover, this month is generally seen as unsuitable for important matters like moving house, getting married, or having surgery, so many people try to avoid them and wait until the seventh month has passed.":"Bulan Hantu juga memiliki cukup banyak 'pantangan'—hal-hal yang akan diingatkan orang tua bahwa 'sebaiknya jangan dilakukan bulan ini'. Yang umum terdengar antara lain: jangan berenang di pantai atau sungai pada malam hari, karena konon roh air mencari 'pengganti'; masukkan pakaian yang dijemur di luar pada malam hari agar tidak 'dipinjam dan dipakai' para saudara baik; dan jika kamu mendengar seseorang memanggil namamu di tengah malam, jangan sembarangan menoleh dan menjawab. Selain itu, bulan ini umumnya dianggap tidak cocok untuk urusan penting seperti pindah rumah, menikah, atau menjalani operasi, sehingga banyak orang berusaha menghindarinya dan menunggu sampai bulan ketujuh berlalu.","On the fifteenth day of the seventh lunar month comes the climax of the whole Ghost Month—the 'Zhongyuan Festival.' On this day, every household and temples large and small hold their grandest pǔdù, giving thanks to heaven and earth, honoring ancestors, and offering alms to all the good brothers. Zhongyuan actually blends several traditions—folk belief, the Taoist 'Zhongyuan,' and the Buddhist 'Ullambana'—but the core spirit is much alike: honoring and remembering the departed, showing compassion for the dead, and reminding the living to know gratitude and sharing.":"Pada hari kelima belas bulan ketujuh lunar tibalah puncak dari seluruh Bulan Hantu—'Festival Zhongyuan'. Pada hari ini, setiap rumah tangga serta kuil besar dan kecil mengadakan pǔdù termegah mereka, bersyukur kepada langit dan bumi, menghormati leluhur, dan memberi sedekah kepada semua saudara baik. Zhongyuan sebenarnya memadukan beberapa tradisi—kepercayaan rakyat, 'Zhongyuan' Taoisme, dan 'Ullambana' Buddhis—tetapi semangat intinya sangat mirip: menghormati dan mengenang yang telah tiada, menunjukkan belas kasih kepada orang mati, dan mengingatkan yang hidup untuk tahu bersyukur dan berbagi.","For foreigners, Ghost Month may at first feel a bit mysterious, even a little frightening, but once you understand it a bit more, you'll find it's actually full of warmth. Taiwanese don't live in fear; rather, with a mindset of 'worship brings protection,' they keep up a peaceful coexistence with the unseen world. You don't have to fully believe these customs, but if you're willing to pause before an offering table and quietly take it in, you may come to feel this: it is the tenderness and respect a society has kept for life, for death, and for memory.":"Bagi orang asing, Bulan Hantu pada awalnya mungkin terasa agak misterius, bahkan sedikit menakutkan, tetapi begitu kamu memahaminya lebih jauh, kamu akan mendapati bahwa sebenarnya ia penuh kehangatan. Orang Taiwan tidak hidup dalam ketakutan; sebaliknya, dengan pola pikir 'sembahyang mendatangkan perlindungan', mereka menjaga koeksistensi damai dengan dunia yang tak terlihat. Kamu tidak harus sepenuhnya percaya pada adat ini, tetapi jika kamu bersedia berhenti sejenak di depan meja persembahan dan diam-diam meresapinya, kamu mungkin akan merasakan ini: inilah kelembutan dan penghormatan yang dijaga sebuah masyarakat terhadap kehidupan, kematian, dan kenangan.","Ghost Month (the 7th lunar month)":"Bulan Hantu (bulan ke-7 lunar)","Zhongyuan Festival (7/15 lunar)":"Festival Zhongyuan (15/7 lunar)","universal deliverance offering rite":"ritual persembahan penyelamatan universal","'good brothers' (polite term for ghosts)":"'saudara-saudara baik' (istilah sopan untuk hantu)","offerings":"persembahan, sesajen","to worship, make offerings":"bersembahyang, mempersembahkan","taboo":"pantangan, tabu","to burn incense":"membakar dupa","water lantern":"lampion air","ancestors":"leluhur","to bless and protect (from Taiwanese)":"memberkati dan melindungi (dari bahasa Taiwan)","soul, spirit":"jiwa, roh","The term 'good brothers' carries the wisdom of not provoking the spirits. Beyond Ghost Month, Taiwan has a culture of avoiding inauspicious words and choosing indirect, polite phrasing. There are rules for offering fruit too: pineapple is welcome (in Taiwanese it sounds like 'ong-lai,' inviting prosperity), while offering bananas, pears, and plums together is avoided because in Taiwanese it can sound like 'inviting you to come'—another pun-based superstition. Keelung's 'Chicken-Cage Zhongyuan Festival' is one of Taiwan's most famous Ghost Month events, known for the dreamlike sight of floating water lanterns.":"Istilah 'saudara-saudara baik' mengandung kearifan untuk tidak memancing amarah roh. Di luar Bulan Hantu, Taiwan memiliki budaya menghindari kata-kata yang membawa sial dan memilih ungkapan yang tidak langsung dan sopan. Ada pula aturan dalam mempersembahkan buah: nanas disambut baik (dalam bahasa Taiwan bunyinya seperti 'ong-lai', mengundang kemakmuran), sementara mempersembahkan pisang, pir, dan plum bersama-sama dihindari karena dalam bahasa Taiwan bisa terdengar seperti 'mengundangmu datang'—lagi-lagi takhayul berbasis permainan kata. 'Festival Zhongyuan Kandang Ayam' di Keelung adalah salah satu acara Bulan Hantu paling terkenal di Taiwan, dikenal karena pemandangan lampion air mengapung yang bagai mimpi.","The Mazu Pilgrimage: Walking a Hundred Kilometers Alongside a Goddess":"Ziarah Mazu: Berjalan Ratusan Kilometer Bersama Seorang Dewi","Every spring, from a small town in central Taiwan, the palanquin of a goddess sets out on a nine-day journey. It travels over three hundred kilometers on foot, millions gather along the route, and people forget their exhaustion to follow the palanquin—the 'Dajia Mazu Pilgrimage' is now counted among the world's largest religious events. Let's peek into the deep trust Taiwanese hold, deep in their hearts, for Mazu, goddess of the sea.":"Setiap musim semi, dari sebuah kota kecil di Taiwan tengah, tandu seorang dewi berangkat untuk perjalanan sembilan hari. Ia menempuh lebih dari tiga ratus kilometer dengan berjalan kaki, jutaan orang berkumpul di sepanjang rute, dan orang-orang melupakan kelelahan mereka demi mengikuti tandu itu—'Ziarah Mazu Dajia' kini terhitung di antara acara keagamaan terbesar di dunia. Mari kita mengintip kepercayaan mendalam yang disimpan orang Taiwan, jauh di lubuk hati mereka, kepada Mazu, dewi laut.","To understand the 'Mazu pilgrimage,' you first need to know the goddess Mazu. Legend says Mazu's given name was Lin Moniang, a woman who lived by the sea over a thousand years ago—kind-hearted and able to foresee the weather, she often saved fishermen and boats caught in storms. After she passed away, people believed she became a goddess guarding safety at sea and honored her as 'Mazu.' Taiwan is surrounded by ocean, and in earlier times many settlers crossed the sea to reach it, so Mazu naturally became one of the most trusted and most widely worshipped deities.":"Untuk memahami 'ziarah Mazu', pertama-tama kamu perlu mengenal dewi Mazu. Menurut legenda, nama pemberian Mazu adalah Lin Moniang, seorang perempuan yang hidup di tepi laut lebih dari seribu tahun lalu—berhati baik dan mampu meramalkan cuaca, ia sering menyelamatkan nelayan dan perahu yang terjebak badai. Setelah ia wafat, orang-orang percaya ia menjadi dewi penjaga keselamatan di laut dan menghormatinya sebagai 'Mazu'. Taiwan dikelilingi lautan, dan pada masa lampau banyak pendatang menyeberangi laut untuk mencapainya, sehingga Mazu secara alami menjadi salah satu dewa yang paling dipercaya dan paling luas disembah.","A 'ràojìng' (procession, literally 'circuit of the territory') means placing the temple's Mazu statue on a sacred palanquin and carrying her to inspect the places where devotees live along the route—symbolizing Mazu going out in person to bestow blessings on the people along the way. Central Taiwan's 'Dajia Mazu Pilgrimage' is the largest and most famous. Every third lunar month, the Mazu of Zhenlan Temple in Dajia, Taichung sets out on a nine-day, eight-night walking journey of over three hundred kilometers round trip, passing through Taichung, Changhua, Yunlin, and Chiayi before finally returning to Dajia.":"Sebuah 'ràojìng' (arak-arakan, secara harfiah 'mengelilingi wilayah') berarti menempatkan patung Mazu dari kuil di atas tandu suci dan mengaraknya untuk memeriksa tempat-tempat di mana para pemuja tinggal di sepanjang rute—melambangkan Mazu turun langsung untuk melimpahkan berkah kepada orang-orang di sepanjang jalan. 'Ziarah Mazu Dajia' di Taiwan tengah adalah yang terbesar dan paling terkenal. Setiap bulan ketiga lunar, Mazu dari Kuil Zhenlan di Dajia, Taichung berangkat untuk perjalanan kaki sembilan hari delapan malam sejauh lebih dari tiga ratus kilometer pulang pergi, melewati Taichung, Changhua, Yunlin, dan Chiayi sebelum akhirnya kembali ke Dajia.","At the very front of the procession are all kinds of 'zhèntóu' (performance troupes). Zhèntóu are the groups in temple festivals responsible for performing, clearing the way, and guarding the deity—some advancing to drumbeats, some waving flags, and the one everyone knows best, the 'Electro-Techno Third Prince,' which fuses traditional deity-costume figures with electronic music, dancing as it moves forward—very distinctively Taiwanese. There's also the 'herald' who announces the way and the 'head banner' leading in front; the whole procession stretches out grandly. Just watching the zhèntóu pass is enough to feel that surging, boisterous energy.":"Di paling depan arak-arakan ada berbagai macam 'zhèntóu' (rombongan pertunjukan). Zhèntóu adalah kelompok dalam festival kuil yang bertanggung jawab untuk tampil, membuka jalan, dan mengawal dewa—ada yang maju mengikuti tabuhan genderang, ada yang mengibarkan bendera, dan yang paling dikenal semua orang, 'Pangeran Ketiga Elektro-Tekno', yang memadukan figur berkostum dewa tradisional dengan musik elektronik, menari sambil bergerak maju—sangat khas Taiwan. Ada juga 'pewarta' yang mengumumkan jalan dan 'panji utama' yang memimpin di depan; seluruh arak-arakan terbentang megah. Cukup menyaksikan zhèntóu lewat saja sudah cukup untuk merasakan energi yang membuncah dan riuh itu.","The most moving scene in the whole pilgrimage is devotees 'passing under the palanquin.' As Mazu's sacred palanquin comes by, many devotees kneel and prostrate on the ground, letting the heavy palanquin be carried over their bodies, believing this brings Mazu's protection and dispels misfortune. Some pray for a sick family member, some seek success in their careers, safety, or peace of mind. Watching white-haired grandmothers, mothers cradling infants, and sharply suited office workers kneel together on the road, you'll understand this is not just an event but countless people entrusting their deepest wishes to a goddess.":"Pemandangan paling mengharukan dalam seluruh ziarah adalah para pemuja 'melintas di bawah tandu'. Saat tandu suci Mazu lewat, banyak pemuja berlutut dan bersujud di tanah, membiarkan tandu yang berat itu diusung melewati tubuh mereka, percaya bahwa ini mendatangkan perlindungan Mazu dan mengusir kemalangan. Ada yang berdoa untuk anggota keluarga yang sakit, ada yang mencari kesuksesan karier, keselamatan, atau ketenangan hati. Menyaksikan nenek-nenek berambut putih, ibu-ibu yang menggendong bayi, dan pekerja kantoran berjas rapi berlutut bersama di jalan, kamu akan mengerti bahwa ini bukan sekadar acara melainkan tak terhitung banyaknya orang yang menitipkan harapan terdalam mereka kepada seorang dewi.","On the pilgrimage route there's one more thing that astonishes many foreigners—the 'selfless hospitality' along the way. In the towns the palanquin and devotees pass through, households set out meals, fruit, drinks, and snacks, treating all the pilgrims following along for free. Some cook hundreds of bowls of noodles, some offer a place to rest and bathe, and some even massage aching, sore feet. Most ask nothing in return, simply because they believe that 'helping pilgrims who have come from afar is doing good on Mazu's behalf'—and also accumulates blessings for themselves and their families. This human warmth is the most touching sight of the whole pilgrimage.":"Di sepanjang rute ziarah ada satu hal lagi yang membuat banyak orang asing takjub—'keramahan tanpa pamrih' di sepanjang jalan. Di kota-kota yang dilalui tandu dan para pemuja, keluarga-keluarga menyediakan makanan, buah, minuman, dan camilan, menjamu semua peziarah yang ikut secara gratis. Ada yang memasak ratusan mangkuk mi, ada yang menawarkan tempat beristirahat dan mandi, dan bahkan ada yang memijat kaki yang pegal dan nyeri. Kebanyakan tidak meminta imbalan apa pun, semata-mata karena mereka percaya bahwa 'membantu peziarah yang datang dari jauh adalah berbuat baik atas nama Mazu'—dan juga menimbun berkah bagi diri sendiri dan keluarga. Kehangatan kemanusiaan inilah pemandangan paling menyentuh dari seluruh ziarah.","In recent years, the 'Dajia Mazu Pilgrimage' has been covered by many international media, even mentioned in the same breath as the Hajj to Mecca and Vatican events, and is regarded as one of the world's largest religious gatherings. Interestingly, those who walk this road are not only devout old believers but also many young people, foreign backpackers, and even people simply wanting to test themselves. They may not fully grasp every ritual, yet over nine days of walking they come to feel the deepest layer of Taiwanese society: a devotion to faith, kindness toward strangers, and that grounded, moving sense of 'being on the road with your heart anchored to something.'":"Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, 'Ziarah Mazu Dajia' telah diliput banyak media internasional, bahkan disebut sejajar dengan ibadah Haji ke Mekah dan acara-acara Vatikan, dan dianggap sebagai salah satu perkumpulan keagamaan terbesar di dunia. Menariknya, mereka yang menempuh jalan ini bukan hanya penganut lama yang saleh tetapi juga banyak anak muda, backpacker asing, dan bahkan orang-orang yang sekadar ingin menguji diri. Mereka mungkin tidak sepenuhnya memahami setiap ritual, namun selama sembilan hari berjalan mereka mulai merasakan lapisan terdalam masyarakat Taiwan: pengabdian pada keyakinan, kebaikan terhadap orang asing, dan perasaan membumi nan mengharukan tentang 'berada di jalan dengan hati yang tertambat pada sesuatu'.","Mazu (goddess of the sea)":"Mazu (dewi laut)","deity's procession around its territory":"arak-arakan dewa mengelilingi wilayahnya","pilgrimage to offer incense at another temple":"ziarah untuk mempersembahkan dupa di kuil lain","sacred palanquin":"tandu suci","passing under the palanquin for blessing":"melintas di bawah tandu untuk mendapat berkah","temple-festival performance troupe":"rombongan pertunjukan festival kuil","pilgrim, worshipper":"peziarah, pemuja","temple":"kuil","believer, devotee":"penganut, pemuja","to bless and protect":"memberkati dan melindungi","to pray for blessings":"berdoa memohon berkah","devout, pious":"saleh, taat","The start date of the Dajia Mazu Pilgrimage is traditionally decided by asking Mazu herself 'when to set out,' using 'jiao-cup divination'—tossing crescent-shaped wooden blocks and reading their faces for the deity's will. Taiwan also has another famous pilgrimage, the 'Baishatun Mazu,' which has no fixed route: the palanquin's direction is left to Mazu's 'will,' so no one knows where it will head—which is what it's famous for. If you join a pilgrimage, don't forget comfortable shoes and protection against sun and rain. Don't overdo it; plenty of people join partway or walk only a segment.":"Tanggal keberangkatan Ziarah Mazu Dajia secara tradisional ditentukan dengan menanyakan langsung kepada Mazu 'kapan harus berangkat', menggunakan 'ramalan cangkir jiao'—melemparkan balok kayu berbentuk bulan sabit dan membaca sisi-sisinya untuk mengetahui kehendak dewa. Taiwan juga memiliki ziarah terkenal lainnya, 'Mazu Baishatun', yang tidak memiliki rute tetap: arah tandu diserahkan pada 'kehendak' Mazu, sehingga tak seorang pun tahu ke mana ia akan menuju—dan itulah yang membuatnya terkenal. Jika kamu ikut ziarah, jangan lupa sepatu yang nyaman dan pelindung dari panas dan hujan. Jangan memaksakan diri; banyak orang ikut di tengah jalan atau hanya berjalan sebagian saja.","Nature & Travel":"Alam & Wisata","Taiwan's Hot Spring Culture: Soaking on a Volcanic Island":"Budaya Mata Air Panas Taiwan: Berendam di Pulau Vulkanik","On a winter night, chilly and rainy outside, you sink into the water up to your shoulders and feel your whole body slowly unwind—Taiwan's hot springs are richer and deeper than many people expect. Let's explore why this small island bubbles with so many springs, and the local culture of 'pàotāng,' soaking in the hot water.":"Pada suatu malam musim dingin, di luar dingin dan hujan, kamu tenggelam ke dalam air hingga sebahu dan merasakan seluruh tubuhmu perlahan mengendur—mata air panas Taiwan lebih kaya dan lebih mendalam daripada yang dibayangkan banyak orang. Mari kita telusuri mengapa pulau kecil ini menyembur begitu banyak mata air panas, dan budaya lokal 'pàotāng', yaitu berendam di air panas.","Many people don't realize that Taiwan is actually a hot-spring powerhouse. The island sits on the Pacific Ring of Fire, with vigorous magma activity underground; add the squeezing of tectonic plates and shifts in the crust, and groundwater gets heated and surges up to the surface. From north to south, from lowlands to high mountains, Taiwan has more than a hundred hot springs—a density among the highest in the world. You could say Taiwanese are born living atop a 'geothermal treasure trove.'":"Banyak orang tidak menyadari bahwa Taiwan sebenarnya adalah negeri mata air panas yang tangguh. Pulau ini terletak di Cincin Api Pasifik, dengan aktivitas magma yang kuat di bawah tanah; ditambah tekanan lempeng tektonik dan pergeseran kerak bumi, air tanah menjadi panas dan menyembur ke permukaan. Dari utara ke selatan, dari dataran rendah hingga pegunungan tinggi, Taiwan memiliki lebih dari seratus mata air panas—kepadatan yang termasuk tertinggi di dunia. Bisa dibilang orang Taiwan terlahir hidup di atas 'harta karun panas bumi'.","When it comes to Taiwan's most famous hot-spring district, many people first think of Beitou in Taipei. Step out of the metro station and a faint whiff of sulfur hangs in the air, with white steam curling up from the valley—the celebrated 'Thermal Valley.' Beitou's springs are mostly sulfur springs of the 'white sulfur' and 'green sulfur' types, said to be good for the skin and joints. This has been a renowned hot-spring town since the Japanese era, leaving behind many old inns and public bathhouses full of nostalgic charm.":"Bicara soal kawasan mata air panas paling terkenal di Taiwan, banyak orang pertama-tama memikirkan Beitou di Taipei. Keluar dari stasiun metro, aroma belerang samar menggantung di udara, dengan uap putih mengepul dari lembah—'Lembah Termal' yang tersohor. Mata air Beitou kebanyakan adalah mata air belerang jenis 'belerang putih' dan 'belerang hijau', konon baik untuk kulit dan persendian. Tempat ini telah menjadi kota mata air panas ternama sejak era Jepang, meninggalkan banyak penginapan tua dan pemandian umum yang penuh pesona nostalgia.","If you want a more laid-back hot-spring town, Jiaoxi in Yilan is on many people's short list. Jiaoxi's water is a sodium bicarbonate spring—colorless, odorless, and silky to the touch, nicknamed the 'beauty bath.' What's special is that the spring water flows right into the town center: there's a free foot-soaking pool near the station, and hot-spring hotels are just a few steps away. Coming to Jiaoxi in winter to stroll the old street by day, eat hot-spring-grown water spinach, and soak at night is a favorite little getaway for Taiwanese.":"Jika kamu menginginkan kota mata air panas yang lebih santai, Jiaoxi di Yilan ada dalam daftar pilihan banyak orang. Air Jiaoxi adalah mata air natrium bikarbonat—tak berwarna, tak berbau, dan terasa lembut di kulit, dijuluki 'pemandian kecantikan'. Yang istimewa adalah air mata airnya mengalir langsung ke pusat kota: ada kolam rendam kaki gratis dekat stasiun, dan hotel-hotel mata air panas hanya beberapa langkah saja. Datang ke Jiaoxi di musim dingin untuk menyusuri jalan tua di siang hari, menyantap kangkung yang tumbuh dengan air panas, dan berendam di malam hari adalah pelesir kecil favorit orang Taiwan.","When you go soaking, you'll face two options: the 'public pool' and the 'private room bath.' The public pool is a shared bath where many people soak together—usually separated by sex and requiring you to bathe naked; it's cheap and lively, ideal for those who want the traditional experience. A private room bath is a self-contained room where a group of friends or a family can shut the door and soak on their own—very private, and especially popular with couples or families with kids. If you'd rather wear a swimsuit and soak together, there are also outdoor hot-spring pools to choose from.":"Saat pergi berendam, kamu akan dihadapkan pada dua pilihan: 'kolam umum' dan 'kamar rendam pribadi'. Kolam umum adalah pemandian bersama tempat banyak orang berendam bareng—biasanya dipisah berdasarkan jenis kelamin dan mengharuskanmu mandi telanjang; murah dan ramai, ideal bagi yang menginginkan pengalaman tradisional. Kamar rendam pribadi adalah ruangan tertutup tempat sekelompok teman atau satu keluarga bisa menutup pintu dan berendam sendiri—sangat privat, dan terutama digemari pasangan atau keluarga dengan anak. Kalau kamu lebih suka mengenakan baju renang dan berendam bersama, ada juga kolam mata air panas terbuka yang bisa dipilih.","Soaking feels wonderful, but there are a few 'fine points' to mind. Before entering a public pool, you must wash your body clean at the side first; while soaking, don't dip your towel into the water—people usually rest it on their head or the pool's edge. Staying in too long can make you dizzy, so it's best to soak for five to ten minutes, get out to rest, and drink some water. If you have heart problems, have been drinking, or have just eaten a big meal, going straight in is not advised. Remember these basic manners and you can soak with ease and peace of mind.":"Berendam terasa nikmat, tetapi ada beberapa 'hal kecil' yang perlu diperhatikan. Sebelum masuk kolam umum, kamu harus membersihkan tubuh dulu di pinggir; saat berendam, jangan mencelupkan handukmu ke air—orang biasanya meletakkannya di atas kepala atau di tepi kolam. Berendam terlalu lama bisa membuatmu pusing, jadi sebaiknya berendam lima sampai sepuluh menit, keluar untuk beristirahat, dan minum air. Jika kamu punya masalah jantung, baru saja minum alkohol, atau baru saja makan besar, langsung berendam tidak dianjurkan. Ingat tata krama dasar ini dan kamu bisa berendam dengan santai dan tenang.","For Taiwanese, soaking isn't just bathing—it's a distinctly wintry pleasure. When the weather turns cold, the whole family or a few close friends make a date to go to the springs. After soaking until you're warm all over and your cheeks are flushed red, the happiest thing is to sit down to a steaming hot pot, or order a plate of the wild greens, poached chicken, and grilled sausage the spring towns are known for. The colder it is outside, the warmer the water feels—that very contrast is the most soothing flavor of a Taiwanese winter.":"Bagi orang Taiwan, berendam bukan sekadar mandi—ia adalah kenikmatan yang khas musim dingin. Ketika cuaca menjadi dingin, seluruh keluarga atau beberapa teman dekat membuat janji untuk pergi ke mata air panas. Setelah berendam sampai seluruh tubuh hangat dan pipi memerah, hal paling membahagiakan adalah duduk menikmati hot pot yang mengepul, atau memesan sepiring sayuran liar, ayam rebus, dan sosis bakar yang menjadi ciri khas kota-kota mata air panas. Semakin dingin di luar, semakin hangat rasanya air itu—kontras itulah cita rasa paling menenangkan dari musim dingin Taiwan.","to soak in a hot spring":"berendam di mata air panas","geothermal heat":"panas bumi","volcanic belt":"sabuk vulkanik","public bath pool":"kolam pemandian umum","private hot-spring room":"kamar mata air panas pribadi","foot-soaking pool":"kolam rendam kaki","'beauty bath' (skin-friendly spring)":"'pemandian kecantikan' (mata air ramah kulit)","knack, fine points (colloquial)":"kiat, hal-hal kecil penting (bahasa sehari-hari)","dizziness":"pusing","Taiwan even has rare springs that bubble up from the sea. 'Zhaori Hot Spring' on Green Island off Taitung is one of the world's few seabed hot springs, famous for soaking at sunrise while gazing over the Pacific. In Guanziling in the south, there's even a muddy, gray-black 'mud spring'—the variety of water types is astonishing. Many areas took root as hot-spring towns in the Japanese era; in Beitou, the preserved public bathhouse from that time is now the free-to-visit 'Beitou Hot Spring Museum.'":"Taiwan bahkan memiliki mata air langka yang menyembur dari laut. 'Mata Air Panas Zhaori' di Pulau Hijau lepas pantai Taitung adalah salah satu dari sedikit mata air panas dasar laut di dunia, terkenal karena berendam saat matahari terbit sambil memandang Samudra Pasifik. Di Guanziling di selatan, bahkan ada 'mata air lumpur' berwarna abu-abu kehitaman yang kental—ragam jenis airnya sungguh menakjubkan. Banyak kawasan berakar menjadi kota mata air panas pada era Jepang; di Beitou, pemandian umum yang terpelihara dari masa itu kini menjadi 'Museum Mata Air Panas Beitou' yang bebas dikunjungi.","Circling Taiwan by Train: Seeing the Island from the Rails":"Mengelilingi Taiwan dengan Kereta: Melihat Pulau dari Atas Rel","The sea streams past the window, a warm bento box rests on your lap—circling Taiwan by rail, called 'huándǎo,' is a trip many Taiwanese dream of doing at least once in their lives. From the bullet-train-like high-speed line to the leisurely local trains that stop at every station, let's travel the Taiwan you can see from the rails.":"Laut mengalir di balik jendela, kotak bento hangat bersandar di pangkuanmu—mengelilingi Taiwan dengan kereta, disebut 'huándǎo', adalah perjalanan yang diimpikan banyak orang Taiwan untuk dilakukan setidaknya sekali seumur hidup. Dari jalur cepat mirip kereta peluru hingga kereta lokal yang santai berhenti di setiap stasiun, mari kita menjelajahi Taiwan yang bisa kamu lihat dari atas rel.","Taiwan's rail system splits simply into two big categories: 'Taiwan Railway' (Taitie) and 'High Speed Rail' (Gaotie). Taiwan Railway is a loop line encircling the whole island, running from the western plains along the coastline around to the east, stringing towns big and small together like beads. The High Speed Rail is the western bullet line, reaching 300 km/h, taking you from Taipei in the north to Kaohsiung in the south in as little as an hour and a half. One is like a slowly flowing blood vessel; the other, like an expressway running through the body.":"Sistem perkeretaan Taiwan terbagi sederhana menjadi dua kategori besar: 'Kereta Api Taiwan' (Taitie) dan 'Kereta Cepat' (Gaotie). Kereta Api Taiwan adalah jalur melingkar yang mengelilingi seluruh pulau, membentang dari dataran barat menyusuri garis pantai memutar ke timur, merangkai kota besar dan kecil bagai untaian manik. Kereta Cepat adalah jalur peluru sebelah barat, mencapai 300 km/jam, membawamu dari Taipei di utara ke Kaohsiung di selatan hanya dalam waktu sekitar satu setengah jam. Yang satu bagai pembuluh darah yang mengalir perlahan; yang lain bagai jalan tol yang menembus tubuh.","Within Taiwan Railway, trains also come in classes. The fastest and most comfortable is the 'Tze-Chiang' express: few stops, high speed, ideal for long hauls. The 'local train' (qūjiānchē) stops at every station—cheap fares, the train locals ride most for commuting and school, and a great companion for backpackers who want to take it slow and hop off on a whim. There are also tilting trains like the Taroko and Puyuma, which lean slightly through curves, making the mountain-and-sea routes of the east especially fast.":"Di dalam Kereta Api Taiwan, kereta juga terbagi dalam kelas. Yang tercepat dan ternyaman adalah ekspres 'Tze-Chiang': sedikit pemberhentian, berkecepatan tinggi, ideal untuk perjalanan jauh. 'Kereta lokal' (qūjiānchē) berhenti di setiap stasiun—tarif murah, kereta yang paling sering ditumpangi warga lokal untuk pergi kerja dan sekolah, serta teman yang bagus bagi backpacker yang ingin bersantai dan turun sesuka hati. Ada pula kereta miring seperti Taroko dan Puyuma, yang sedikit condong saat menikung, membuat rute gunung-dan-laut di timur terasa sangat cepat.","'Huándǎo'—circling the island—is the romantic byword of Taiwanese rail travel. Buy one ticket, set off from Taipei, and loop around Taiwan clockwise or counterclockwise. The western stretch is crowded and city-dense, one bustling metropolis after another; but once the train turns into the east, the scenery changes completely. Past Yilan and Hualien, one side of the tracks is the unbroken Central Mountain Range and the other the vast Pacific—a sea so brightly blue it streams endlessly past the window, and many first-timers can't resist pulling out their phones to snap away.":"'Huándǎo'—mengelilingi pulau—adalah ungkapan romantis dalam wisata kereta Taiwan. Beli satu tiket, berangkat dari Taipei, dan berputar mengitari Taiwan searah atau berlawanan jarum jam. Bentangan barat padat dan penuh kota, satu metropolis ramai demi metropolis lainnya; tetapi begitu kereta membelok ke timur, pemandangan berubah total. Melewati Yilan dan Hualien, satu sisi rel adalah Pegunungan Tengah yang tak terputus dan sisi lainnya Samudra Pasifik yang luas—laut yang biru cemerlang mengalir tanpa henti di balik jendela, dan banyak orang yang baru pertama kali tak kuasa menahan diri untuk mengeluarkan ponsel dan memotret.","The 'East Rift Valley' and coastline of the east are, for many, the most beautiful stretch of railway in Taiwan. Between Hualien and Taitung, the train sometimes bores into valleys flanked by lush green rice paddies and betel-nut palms; other times it hugs the shore as Pacific waves roll in one after another. This region is sparsely populated and lightly developed, preserving vast tracts of pristine nature. Watching it go by, you come to understand why Taiwanese often say, 'The east is Taiwan's back garden.'":"'Lembah Retakan Timur' dan garis pantai timur, bagi banyak orang, adalah bentangan rel terindah di Taiwan. Antara Hualien dan Taitung, kereta kadang menembus lembah yang diapit sawah hijau subur dan pohon pinang; kali lain ia menyusuri pantai saat ombak Pasifik menggulung silih berganti. Kawasan ini berpenduduk jarang dan sedikit terbangun, menjaga hamparan luas alam yang masih asli. Menyaksikannya berlalu, kamu akan mengerti mengapa orang Taiwan sering berkata, 'Timur adalah taman belakang Taiwan.'","You can't talk about riding the train without mentioning the 'bento.' The Taiwan Railway bento is the soul of Taiwanese rail travel; the most classic is that round metal tin or paper box, lined with white rice and topped with a glossy braised pork rib or chicken leg, alongside a braised egg, pickled greens, and vegetables. The moment the train pulls out, many people can't wait to open their boxes, and the rich aroma of braising sauce fills the whole carriage. Watching the scenery slide past while shoveling down a hot bento—that simple happiness is a shared memory for many Taiwanese.":"Kamu tak bisa bicara soal naik kereta tanpa menyebut 'bento'. Bento Kereta Api Taiwan adalah jiwa dari wisata kereta Taiwan; yang paling klasik adalah kaleng logam bundar atau kotak kertas itu, dialasi nasi putih dan di atasnya iga babi kecap yang mengkilap atau paha ayam, ditemani telur kecap, sayur asin, dan sayuran. Begitu kereta berangkat, banyak orang tak sabar membuka kotak mereka, dan aroma kuat saus kecap memenuhi seluruh gerbong. Menyaksikan pemandangan melintas sambil melahap bento panas—kebahagiaan sederhana itu adalah kenangan bersama banyak orang Taiwan.","The charm of train travel lies precisely in its 'slowness.' You don't have to drive or watch a navigation screen—just settle in by the window and let the sea and mountains unfold slowly before you. You can doze to the regular 'clackety-clack' of the wheels, or trade a few words with the stranger beside you. If you've just arrived in Taiwan, why not pick a stretch of eastern railway and board with a bento in hand? You may find that the best way to know this island isn't rushing through an itinerary, but letting the train carry you along, slowly.":"Pesona wisata kereta terletak justru pada 'kelambatannya'. Kamu tak perlu menyetir atau menatap layar navigasi—cukup duduk nyaman di dekat jendela dan biarkan laut dan gunung terbentang perlahan di depanmu. Kamu bisa terlelap mengikuti bunyi 'klak-klik' roda yang teratur, atau bertukar sepatah dua patah kata dengan orang asing di sebelahmu. Kalau kamu baru saja tiba di Taiwan, mengapa tidak memilih satu bentangan rel timur dan naik dengan bento di tangan? Kamu mungkin akan mendapati bahwa cara terbaik mengenal pulau ini bukanlah bergegas menuntaskan jadwal, melainkan membiarkan kereta membawamu, perlahan.","to circle the island (round-island trip)":"mengelilingi pulau (perjalanan keliling pulau)","Taiwan Railway":"Kereta Api Taiwan (Taitie)","High Speed Rail":"Kereta Cepat (Gaotie)","Tze-Chiang express (fastest local train)":"ekspres Tze-Chiang (kereta lokal tercepat)","local (all-stops) commuter train":"kereta komuter lokal (berhenti di semua stasiun)","pork rib (chop)":"iga babi","rice paddy":"sawah","mountain range":"pegunungan","train carriage":"gerbong kereta","to doze off":"terlelap sejenak","Circling Taiwan by rail ('huándǎo') is also hugely popular by bicycle—many Taiwanese take on a round-island cycle ride at milestones in life (it's even been the subject of films and ads). For rail fans, charming local lines like the Jiji Line in the south and the Alishan mountain railway are highlights. Taiwan Railway bentos can be bought at station kiosks or on board, and at stations like Taipei Main there are sometimes queues for takeaway—the 'railway bento' has become a specialty in its own right.":"Mengelilingi Taiwan dengan kereta ('huándǎo') juga sangat populer dengan sepeda—banyak orang Taiwan menjalani gowes keliling pulau pada momen-momen penting dalam hidup (bahkan menjadi tema film dan iklan). Bagi penggemar kereta, jalur lokal yang memesona seperti Jalur Jiji di selatan dan kereta pegunungan Alishan menjadi sorotan. Bento Kereta Api Taiwan bisa dibeli di kios stasiun atau di dalam kereta, dan di stasiun seperti Taipei Main kadang ada antrean untuk dibawa pulang—'bento kereta api' telah menjadi hidangan khas tersendiri.","Taiwan's High Mountains: A World Above 3,000 Meters on a Small Island":"Pegunungan Tinggi Taiwan: Dunia di Atas 3.000 Meter di Sebuah Pulau Kecil","Say 'Taiwan' and many picture night markets and food, but few imagine peaks over 3,000 meters rising above a sea of clouds. In fact, this small island has many mountains taller than Mount Fuji. Let's explore why an island nation has such towering peaks, and the mountaineering culture unique to Taiwan.":"Sebut 'Taiwan' dan banyak orang membayangkan pasar malam dan makanan, tetapi sedikit yang membayangkan puncak-puncak di atas 3.000 meter menjulang di atas lautan awan. Nyatanya, pulau kecil ini punya banyak gunung yang lebih tinggi daripada Gunung Fuji. Mari kita telusuri mengapa sebuah negara kepulauan memiliki puncak setinggi itu, dan budaya pendakian yang khas Taiwan.","Many people's first impression of Taiwan is an ocean isle, sandy beaches, bustling cities—few know that Taiwan is in fact a 'mountain island.' The whole island has more than 200 peaks above 3,000 meters, extraordinarily rare among the world's islands. Looking down from a plane, you'll notice the center is almost entirely filled by a swath of green mountains: the Central Mountain Range, running north to south and known as Taiwan's 'ridgepole.'":"Kesan pertama banyak orang tentang Taiwan adalah pulau di tengah samudra, pantai berpasir, kota yang ramai—sedikit yang tahu bahwa Taiwan sebenarnya adalah 'pulau gunung'. Seluruh pulau memiliki lebih dari 200 puncak di atas 3.000 meter, sangat langka di antara pulau-pulau di dunia. Melihat ke bawah dari pesawat, kamu akan menyadari bagian tengahnya hampir seluruhnya dipenuhi hamparan gunung hijau: Pegunungan Tengah, membentang dari utara ke selatan dan dikenal sebagai 'tulang punggung' Taiwan.","Why would an island of modest size have so many high mountains? The answer lies underground. Taiwan sits right at the boundary of the Eurasian and Philippine Sea plates; these two vast plates have pushed against each other for ages, shoving what was once seabed strata upward bit by bit, forcing up an entire row of soaring ranges. That force hasn't stopped even now—Taiwan's mountains are actually still quietly 'growing taller' each year, which is also why earthquakes here are frequent.":"Mengapa pulau berukuran sedang bisa memiliki begitu banyak gunung tinggi? Jawabannya ada di bawah tanah. Taiwan terletak tepat di batas antara Lempeng Eurasia dan Lempeng Laut Filipina; kedua lempeng raksasa ini telah saling mendorong sejak lama, mengangkat lapisan yang dulunya dasar laut sedikit demi sedikit ke atas, memaksa naik sederet pegunungan yang menjulang. Gaya itu belum berhenti bahkan sampai sekarang—gunung-gunung Taiwan sebenarnya masih diam-diam 'bertambah tinggi' setiap tahun, yang juga menjadi alasan mengapa gempa bumi di sini sering terjadi.","Taiwan's highest mountain is Yushan (Jade Mountain), at 3,952 meters. It's not only Taiwan's tallest peak but also higher than Japan's Mount Fuji, and a spiritual symbol for many Taiwanese—it's even printed on the NT$1,000 bill. Climbing to Yushan's main summit to watch the sunrise is a lifelong dream for many Taiwanese hikers. You set off in the dark before dawn, and when the sun rises slowly out of the sea of clouds, the emotion of that moment makes even the weariest legs worth it.":"Gunung tertinggi Taiwan adalah Yushan (Gunung Giok), setinggi 3.952 meter. Ia bukan hanya puncak tertinggi Taiwan tetapi juga lebih tinggi daripada Gunung Fuji Jepang, dan menjadi simbol spiritual bagi banyak orang Taiwan—bahkan tercetak di uang kertas NT$1.000. Mendaki ke puncak utama Yushan untuk menyaksikan matahari terbit adalah impian seumur hidup bagi banyak pendaki Taiwan. Kamu berangkat dalam gelap sebelum fajar, dan ketika matahari perlahan terbit dari lautan awan, keharuan saat itu membuat kaki yang paling lelah pun sepadan.","In Taiwan's mountaineering community there's a special term: the 'Baiyue,' or Hundred Peaks. Veteran climbers selected one hundred representative summits from among the mountains over 3,000 meters, each with its own character and difficulty. For many Taiwanese who love climbing, 'completing the Hundred' (climbing all one hundred) is a lofty goal that may take years—even a lifetime—to accumulate. This list has become a unique 'treasure map' within Taiwan's mountaineering culture.":"Dalam komunitas pendaki Taiwan ada istilah khusus: 'Baiyue', atau Seratus Puncak. Para pendaki veteran memilih seratus puncak representatif dari gunung-gunung di atas 3.000 meter, masing-masing dengan karakter dan tingkat kesulitannya sendiri. Bagi banyak orang Taiwan yang gemar mendaki, 'menuntaskan Seratus Puncak' (mendaki seluruh seratus puncak) adalah tujuan luhur yang bisa memakan waktu bertahun-tahun—bahkan seumur hidup—untuk dikumpulkan. Daftar ini telah menjadi 'peta harta karun' yang unik dalam budaya pendakian Taiwan.","The high mountains didn't just nurture a climbing culture—they also gave rise to Taiwan's famous 'high-mountain tea.' On slopes above 1,500 meters, with big day-night temperature swings and clouds and mist wrapping the hills year-round, tea bushes grow slowly, and the leaves they produce are especially tender with a delicate, refined fragrance. The oolong brewed from high-mountain tea areas like Lishan, Alishan, and Shanlinxi is mellow on the palate with a sweet aftertaste rising in the throat, making it a top choice for gifts. You could say Taiwan's high mountains turn 'altitude' directly into the flavor in your cup.":"Pegunungan tinggi tidak hanya menumbuhkan budaya pendakian—mereka juga melahirkan 'teh gunung tinggi' Taiwan yang termasyhur. Di lereng di atas 1.500 meter, dengan perbedaan suhu siang-malam yang besar dan awan serta kabut menyelimuti bukit sepanjang tahun, semak teh tumbuh lambat, dan daun yang dihasilkannya sangat lembut dengan aroma yang halus dan anggun. Oolong yang diseduh dari kawasan teh gunung tinggi seperti Lishan, Alishan, dan Shanlinxi terasa lembut di lidah dengan aftertaste manis yang naik di tenggorokan, menjadikannya pilihan utama untuk hadiah. Bisa dibilang pegunungan tinggi Taiwan mengubah 'ketinggian' langsung menjadi cita rasa dalam cangkirmu.","For Taiwanese, the high mountains long ago became not a distant view but a way of life within reach. Driving up Hehuanshan on a day off to watch the sea of clouds and stargaze, or traversing a ridgeline over several days, has become a shared memory for many families and young people. In recent years the government has gradually opened up the mountains and forests, encouraging everyone to head into them safely. If you get the chance to come to Taiwan, do look up at those peaks hidden behind the clouds—they stand quietly at the island's heart, reminding you that this island is far more three-dimensional, and far vaster, than you imagined.":"Bagi orang Taiwan, pegunungan tinggi sejak lama bukan lagi pemandangan yang jauh melainkan gaya hidup yang terjangkau. Berkendara naik ke Hehuanshan pada hari libur untuk menyaksikan lautan awan dan mengamati bintang, atau menyusuri punggung gunung selama beberapa hari, telah menjadi kenangan bersama banyak keluarga dan anak muda. Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir pemerintah berangsur membuka gunung dan hutan, mendorong semua orang untuk masuk ke dalamnya dengan aman. Jika kamu berkesempatan datang ke Taiwan, tengoklah puncak-puncak yang tersembunyi di balik awan itu—mereka berdiri tenang di jantung pulau, mengingatkanmu bahwa pulau ini jauh lebih berdimensi, dan jauh lebih luas, daripada yang kamu bayangkan.","high mountain":"gunung tinggi","Yushan (Jade Mountain, Taiwan's highest)":"Yushan (Gunung Giok, tertinggi di Taiwan)","the Hundred Peaks (Baiyue)":"Seratus Puncak (Baiyue)","elevation, altitude":"ketinggian, elevasi","tectonic plate":"lempeng tektonik","sunrise":"matahari terbit","high-mountain tea":"teh gunung tinggi","ridgeline":"punggung gunung","sweet aftertaste":"aftertaste manis","Taiwan's Hundred Peaks range from mountains fairly easy even for beginners to tough climbs for the experienced. Popular Hehuanshan has a road reaching near 3,000 meters, making it the 'most accessible 3,000-meter peak in Taiwan,' drawing crowds for sunrises and even snow (which occasionally dusts it in winter). Major high peaks like Yushan require advance application and a lottery for entry—plus mountain-hut reservations—for the sake of ecological protection and safety. In recent years, reckless solo trips and poor preparation leading to accidents have become a concern, and 'climb safely, with respect for the mountains' is a watchword of Taiwan's mountaineering community.":"Seratus Puncak Taiwan berkisar dari gunung yang cukup mudah bahkan bagi pemula hingga pendakian berat bagi yang berpengalaman. Hehuanshan yang populer memiliki jalan yang mencapai hampir 3.000 meter, menjadikannya 'puncak 3.000 meter paling mudah dijangkau di Taiwan', menarik keramaian untuk matahari terbit dan bahkan salju (yang sesekali menyaputnya di musim dingin). Puncak-puncak tinggi utama seperti Yushan mensyaratkan pendaftaran di muka dan undian untuk masuk—ditambah reservasi pondok gunung—demi perlindungan ekologi dan keselamatan. Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, perjalanan solo yang gegabah dan persiapan yang buruk yang berujung kecelakaan menjadi kekhawatiran, dan 'mendaki dengan aman, dengan hormat pada gunung' adalah semboyan komunitas pendaki Taiwan.","Modern Life":"Kehidupan Modern","The Languages of Taiwan: Many Voices in a Single Sentence":"Bahasa-Bahasa Taiwan: Banyak Suara dalam Satu Kalimat","Prick up your ears on a Taiwanese street corner and you'll notice that a single conversation can weave together Mandarin, Taiwanese, and now and then even a word of Japanese or English. What languages are actually spoken in Taiwan? Let's take an everyday look at its rich multilingual landscape.":"Pasang telingamu di sudut jalan Taiwan dan kamu akan menyadari bahwa satu percakapan bisa menganyam bersama bahasa Mandarin, bahasa Taiwan, dan sesekali bahkan sepatah kata bahasa Jepang atau Inggris. Bahasa apa saja yang sebenarnya dituturkan di Taiwan? Mari kita lihat lanskap multibahasa yang kaya itu dari sisi keseharian.","Many people assume Taiwan \"only speaks Chinese,\" but it's actually a quite multilingual society. Official settings and school instruction use \"Guoyu\"—what we commonly call \"Huayu\" (Mandarin). But in markets, in front of temples, and in grandma and grandpa's living rooms, what you hear more often is \"Taiyu,\" that is, Taiwanese Hokkien. Beyond that, there's the \"Hakka\" spoken by the Hakka people, and the \"Indigenous languages\" preserved by the various Indigenous peoples. These languages often coexist right there on the same street in Taiwan.":"Banyak orang mengira Taiwan \"hanya berbahasa Mandarin\", padahal ia sebenarnya masyarakat yang cukup multibahasa. Situasi resmi dan pengajaran di sekolah menggunakan \"Guoyu\"—yang biasa kita sebut \"Huayu\" (Mandarin). Namun di pasar, di depan kuil, dan di ruang tamu kakek-nenek, yang lebih sering kamu dengar adalah \"Taiyu\", yaitu Hokkien Taiwan. Selain itu, ada \"Hakka\" yang dituturkan orang Hakka, dan \"bahasa-bahasa Pribumi\" yang dijaga oleh berbagai suku asli. Bahasa-bahasa ini sering hidup berdampingan tepat di jalan yang sama di Taiwan.","\"Guoyu\" is currently the most widely used language in Taiwan. From news, TV, and official documents to school lessons, nearly everything uses it. Its pronunciation is very close to the Mandarin you learn in textbooks, but Taiwanese people speak it with their own flavor: sentences often end with soft particles like \"o,\" \"la,\" and \"ye,\" which sound friendlier and less sharp-edged. For foreign learners, mastering \"Guoyu\" first means you can communicate wherever you go—the most practical first step.":"\"Guoyu\" saat ini adalah bahasa yang paling luas digunakan di Taiwan. Dari berita, TV, dan dokumen resmi hingga pelajaran sekolah, hampir semuanya memakainya. Pelafalannya sangat mirip dengan Mandarin yang kamu pelajari di buku teks, tetapi orang Taiwan menuturkannya dengan gaya mereka sendiri: kalimat sering diakhiri partikel lembut seperti \"o\", \"la\", dan \"ye\", yang terdengar lebih ramah dan tidak setajam. Bagi pembelajar asing, menguasai \"Guoyu\" lebih dulu berarti kamu bisa berkomunikasi ke mana pun kamu pergi—langkah pertama yang paling praktis.","\"Taiyu,\" meanwhile, is the true \"mother tongue\" of many families. It carries a wealth of everyday emotion—for scolding, joking, or speaking from the heart, Taiwanese often lands with more force. In recent years it has appeared in many pop songs, TV dramas, and ads, and young people are starting to feel that speaking Taiwanese is quite \"cool.\" But because schools taught only Guoyu for a long stretch of the past, many in the younger generation \"can understand it but can't really speak it\"—a linguistic gap that Taiwanese society is now working hard to repair.":"\"Taiyu\", sementara itu, adalah \"bahasa ibu\" yang sesungguhnya bagi banyak keluarga. Ia memuat kekayaan emosi sehari-hari—untuk memarahi, bercanda, atau berbicara dari hati, bahasa Taiwan sering terasa lebih kena. Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir ia muncul di banyak lagu pop, drama TV, dan iklan, dan anak muda mulai merasa bahwa berbahasa Taiwan itu cukup \"keren\". Namun karena sekolah hanya mengajarkan Guoyu selama masa yang panjang di masa lalu, banyak dari generasi muda \"bisa memahaminya tetapi tidak benar-benar bisa menuturkannya\"—sebuah kesenjangan bahasa yang kini sedang giat diperbaiki oleh masyarakat Taiwan.","Besides Taiwanese, Taiwan also has \"Hakka\" and \"Indigenous languages.\" Hakka people live mainly in Taoyuan, Hsinchu, Miaoli, and some southern towns, with their own language, folk songs, and food culture. The Indigenous peoples include more than sixteen groups—Amis, Paiwan, Atayal, Bunun, and others—each with its own language that sounds completely different from Mandarin or Taiwanese. Some of these languages have few speakers and face the danger of disappearing, so the government has designated them all as \"national languages,\" offering courses in schools and working to preserve them through TV and radio.":"Selain bahasa Taiwan, Taiwan juga memiliki \"Hakka\" dan \"bahasa-bahasa Pribumi\". Orang Hakka tinggal terutama di Taoyuan, Hsinchu, Miaoli, dan beberapa kota di selatan, dengan bahasa, lagu rakyat, dan budaya kuliner mereka sendiri. Suku-suku Pribumi mencakup lebih dari enam belas kelompok—Amis, Paiwan, Atayal, Bunun, dan lainnya—masing-masing dengan bahasanya sendiri yang terdengar sama sekali berbeda dari Mandarin atau bahasa Taiwan. Sebagian bahasa ini memiliki sedikit penutur dan menghadapi bahaya kepunahan, sehingga pemerintah menetapkan semuanya sebagai \"bahasa nasional\", menyediakan kursus di sekolah dan berupaya melestarikannya melalui TV dan radio.","The most charming thing about how Taiwanese people speak is the ability to \"switch.\" One and the same person might speak Taiwanese to elders, Guoyu to colleagues, and toss in a few English words with children—mixing three languages in a single sentence is nothing unusual. For example: \"I'll tell you about this case in the afternoon; have you eaten (tsia̍h-pá) yet?\" This natural mixing is called \"code-switching\" in linguistics. It's not a sign of poor command, but the Taiwanese knack for flexibly choosing the most fitting language for the person and the situation.":"Hal paling memikat dari cara orang Taiwan berbicara adalah kemampuan untuk \"beralih\". Satu orang yang sama bisa berbahasa Taiwan kepada orang tua, Guoyu kepada rekan kerja, dan menyelipkan beberapa kata bahasa Inggris dengan anak-anak—mencampur tiga bahasa dalam satu kalimat bukanlah hal aneh. Misalnya: \"Soal kasus ini nanti sore aku ceritakan; sudah makan (tsia̍h-pá) belum?\" Pencampuran alami ini dalam linguistik disebut \"alih kode\" (code-switching). Ini bukan tanda penguasaan yang buruk, melainkan kepiawaian orang Taiwan dalam secara luwes memilih bahasa yang paling pas untuk orang dan situasinya.","For foreigners hoping to fit into Taiwan, there's no need to rush to learn every language from the start. Master Guoyu first, and you can communicate anywhere on the island; stay a while longer and you'll naturally begin to understand the market auntie's Taiwanese and pick up a few phrases like \"to-siā\" (thank you) and \"tsia̍h-pá--bôe\" (have you eaten?). When Taiwanese people hear a foreigner making the effort to speak Taiwanese, they're usually both surprised and delighted. Here language is not just a tool for communication but a bond of identity, memory, and emotion—the more voices you listen to, the better you'll understand this island.":"Bagi orang asing yang berharap membaur di Taiwan, tak perlu terburu-buru mempelajari setiap bahasa sejak awal. Kuasai Guoyu lebih dulu, dan kamu bisa berkomunikasi di mana pun di pulau ini; tinggal lebih lama sedikit dan kamu akan secara alami mulai memahami bahasa Taiwan si ibu penjual di pasar serta menangkap beberapa frasa seperti \"to-siā\" (terima kasih) dan \"tsia̍h-pá--bôe\" (sudah makan?). Ketika orang Taiwan mendengar orang asing berusaha berbahasa Taiwan, mereka biasanya sekaligus terkejut dan senang. Di sini bahasa bukan sekadar alat komunikasi melainkan ikatan identitas, kenangan, dan emosi—semakin banyak suara yang kamu dengarkan, semakin baik kamu memahami pulau ini.","Guoyu; Mandarin (official standard in Taiwan)":"Guoyu; Mandarin (standar resmi di Taiwan)","Huayu; Mandarin Chinese":"Huayu; bahasa Mandarin","Taiwanese (Hokkien)":"bahasa Taiwan (Hokkien)","Southern Min / Hokkien":"Min Selatan / Hokkien","Hakka language":"bahasa Hakka","Indigenous (Austronesian) languages":"bahasa-bahasa Pribumi (Austronesia)","mother tongue":"bahasa ibu","code-switching":"alih kode (code-switching)","to switch (between)":"beralih (di antara)","folk songs, ballads":"lagu rakyat, balada","gap, rupture (generational)":"kesenjangan, keretakan (antargenerasi)","In Taiwan, Taiwanese can be written both in Chinese characters and in romanization (such as 'Pe̍h-ōe-jī' or the Ministry of Education's 'Tâi-lô' system). The 'tsia̍h-pá' (to have eaten) and 'to-siā' (thank you) in the text are Tâi-lô examples. Taiwanese also contains many words borrowed from Japanese during the colonial era—'o-jí-sáng' (uncle), 'to-sáng' (dad), 'thian-puh-lah' (tempura)—still used daily. Conversely, English loanwords have grown in recent years, so Taiwan's languages keep blending and changing at this very moment.":"Di Taiwan, bahasa Taiwan bisa ditulis baik dengan aksara Tionghoa maupun dengan romanisasi (seperti 'Pe̍h-ōe-jī' atau sistem 'Tâi-lô' dari Kementerian Pendidikan). Kata 'tsia̍h-pá' (sudah makan) dan 'to-siā' (terima kasih) dalam teks adalah contoh Tâi-lô. Bahasa Taiwan juga mengandung banyak kata pinjaman dari bahasa Jepang pada era kolonial—'o-jí-sáng' (paman), 'to-sáng' (ayah), 'thian-puh-lah' (tempura)—yang masih dipakai sehari-hari. Sebaliknya, kata pinjaman dari bahasa Inggris bertambah dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, sehingga bahasa-bahasa Taiwan terus berbaur dan berubah tepat pada saat ini.","Cafés and Independent Bookstores: Taiwan's Slow-Life Corners":"Kafe dan Toko Buku Independen: Sudut-Sudut Hidup Santai Taiwan","Walk through a Taiwanese city and you'll stumble on a surprising density of cafés—places where people read all afternoon over a single cup of coffee, or open a laptop to work. And there are even bookstores that stay open all night. Why do Taiwanese people love cafés and bookshops so much? Let's peek into that \"slow-life\" atmosphere.":"Berjalanlah menyusuri kota di Taiwan dan kamu akan menjumpai kepadatan kafe yang mengejutkan—tempat orang membaca sepanjang sore dengan secangkir kopi, atau membuka laptop untuk bekerja. Bahkan ada toko buku yang buka sepanjang malam. Mengapa orang Taiwan begitu menyukai kafe dan toko buku? Mari kita mengintip suasana \"hidup santai\" itu.","The density of cafés in Taiwan is astonishing. From chain brands to tiny independent shops tucked in alleys, you'll spot one every few steps. These cafés aren't just \"places to drink coffee\"—they're more like a second living room within the city. Some people race to finish a report here, some chat with friends the whole afternoon, and some just want to find a quiet corner to zone out. The price of a single coffee actually buys you a stretch of time in which you can slow down.":"Kepadatan kafe di Taiwan sungguh menakjubkan. Dari merek waralaba hingga kedai independen mungil yang terselip di gang, kamu akan menjumpai satu setiap beberapa langkah. Kafe-kafe ini bukan sekadar \"tempat minum kopi\"—mereka lebih seperti ruang tamu kedua di dalam kota. Ada yang bergegas menyelesaikan laporan di sini, ada yang mengobrol dengan teman sepanjang sore, dan ada yang hanya ingin mencari sudut tenang untuk melamun. Harga secangkir kopi sebenarnya membelikanmu sepenggal waktu untuk bisa memperlambat langkah.","When looking for a café in Taiwan, there's a crucial keyword: \"bú xiàn shí\" (no time limit). Some shops write \"no time limit, power outlets, Wi-Fi\" at the door or on the menu, which is sheer heaven for anyone who needs to sit and work or study for a long time. Conversely, some popular spots specify \"two-hour limit\" or \"90-minute dining time,\" especially small shops with few seats and brisk business. Checking the rules before you order is an unwritten courtesy in Taiwan's café culture.":"Saat mencari kafe di Taiwan, ada satu kata kunci penting: \"bú xiàn shí\" (tanpa batas waktu). Beberapa kedai menulis \"tanpa batas waktu, ada stopkontak, Wi-Fi\" di pintu atau di menu, yang merupakan surga bagi siapa saja yang perlu duduk bekerja atau belajar lama. Sebaliknya, beberapa tempat populer menetapkan \"batas dua jam\" atau \"waktu bersantap 90 menit\", terutama kedai kecil dengan sedikit kursi dan ramai pembeli. Memeriksa aturan sebelum memesan adalah kesopanan tak tertulis dalam budaya kafe Taiwan.","Speaking of Taiwan's reading culture, one cannot skip \"Eslite Bookstore\" (Chengpin). Eslite doesn't just sell books; it turned the bookstore into a lifestyle: bright spaces, comfortable sofas, and alongside them stationery, coffee, and exhibitions. It's most famous for once running a bookstore that \"never closed—24 hours,\" giving people who couldn't sleep, who'd just finished a night shift, or who simply wanted to read quietly in the small hours a lit-up place to go. That sense of security—\"there's still a bookstore I can go to late at night\"—has become a warm urban memory in many Taiwanese hearts.":"Bicara soal budaya membaca Taiwan, orang tak bisa melewatkan \"Toko Buku Eslite\" (Chengpin). Eslite tidak sekadar menjual buku; ia mengubah toko buku menjadi gaya hidup: ruang yang terang, sofa yang nyaman, dan di sampingnya alat tulis, kopi, dan pameran. Ia paling terkenal karena pernah menjalankan toko buku yang \"tak pernah tutup—24 jam\", memberi orang yang tak bisa tidur, yang baru selesai kerja malam, atau yang sekadar ingin membaca dengan tenang di dini hari sebuah tempat yang bercahaya untuk didatangi. Rasa aman itu—\"masih ada toko buku yang bisa kudatangi larut malam\"—telah menjadi kenangan kota yang hangat di hati banyak orang Taiwan.","Beyond the big chains, Taiwan has a whole community of lovable, characterful \"independent bookstores.\" They're often hidden in old houses, alleys, or on second floors—small in size but each with its own theme: some specialize in feminism, some focus on travel literature, some care about local land and the environment. The owner is usually the person who knows books best and will personally recommend one that suits you. Walk into an independent bookstore and what you buy isn't just a book, but a taste carefully curated by another person.":"Di luar jaringan besar, Taiwan memiliki seluruh komunitas \"toko buku independen\" yang menawan dan berkarakter. Mereka sering tersembunyi di rumah tua, gang, atau lantai dua—berukuran kecil tetapi masing-masing dengan temanya sendiri: ada yang mengkhususkan diri pada feminisme, ada yang berfokus pada sastra perjalanan, ada yang peduli pada tanah dan lingkungan lokal. Pemiliknya biasanya orang yang paling paham buku dan akan secara pribadi merekomendasikan yang cocok untukmu. Masuk ke toko buku independen dan yang kamu beli bukan sekadar buku, melainkan selera yang dikurasi dengan cermat oleh orang lain.","Why do Taiwanese people love to nest in cafés and bookstores? Part of the reason is that urban homes tend to be small; many people's apartments have no spacious study or living room, so they entrust their \"time to focus, time to relax\" to spaces outside. On the other hand, though Taiwan's pace is busy, society actually values a \"sense of living\"—being able to brew coffee, knowing how to choose a book, being able to sit a whole afternoon at a little shop on a day off is seen as a kind of ability to savor life.":"Mengapa orang Taiwan senang bersarang di kafe dan toko buku? Sebagian alasannya adalah rumah di kota cenderung kecil; apartemen banyak orang tak memiliki ruang belajar atau ruang tamu yang lapang, sehingga mereka menitipkan \"waktu untuk fokus, waktu untuk bersantai\" pada ruang di luar. Di sisi lain, meski laju Taiwan sibuk, masyarakatnya justru menghargai \"rasa kehidupan\"—bisa menyeduh kopi, tahu cara memilih buku, mampu duduk sepanjang sore di kedai kecil pada hari libur dipandang sebagai semacam kemampuan menikmati hidup.","If you've just arrived in Taiwan and want to experience this slow life, it's really not hard at all. Pick an afternoon, walk into a sunlit café, order a pour-over or a latte, bring a book, and just sit down. To go a little deeper, seek out an independent bookstore, chat a bit with the owner, and flip through their carefully chosen books. You'll find that Taiwan's charm lies not only in night markets and street food, but also in these quiet corners you'll find hard to leave.":"Kalau kamu baru saja tiba di Taiwan dan ingin merasakan hidup santai ini, sungguh sama sekali tidak sulit. Pilih satu sore, masuklah ke kafe yang bermandi cahaya matahari, pesan kopi tetes atau latte, bawa sebuah buku, dan duduklah. Untuk lebih mendalam, carilah toko buku independen, mengobrollah sedikit dengan pemiliknya, dan bolak-balik halaman buku yang mereka pilih dengan cermat. Kamu akan mendapati bahwa pesona Taiwan tidak hanya terletak pada pasar malam dan jajanan kaki lima, tetapi juga pada sudut-sudut tenang ini yang akan terasa sulit kamu tinggalkan.","independent bookstore":"toko buku independen","no time limit (on seating)":"tanpa batas waktu (duduk)","time-limited (seating)":"dibatasi waktu (duduk)","power outlet":"stopkontak","pour-over (coffee)":"kopi tetes (pour-over)","latte":"latte","shop owner":"pemilik toko","to recommend":"merekomendasikan","taste, discernment":"selera, kejelian","'Eslite' opened in Taipei in 1989, and its 24-hour Dunnan branch was a cultural landmark across Asia for years (it closed, to much regret, in 2020). A bookstore is also called 'shūjú' in Taiwan, but small, curated shops are distinguished as 'independent bookstores.' Café etiquette for long stays: don't hog seats when it's crowded, and ordering another drink after a while ('a refill / an extra order') leaves a good impression. Two handy words: 'nèiyòng' means dine-in, 'wàidài' means takeout.":"'Eslite' dibuka di Taipei pada 1989, dan cabang Dunnan yang buka 24 jam menjadi ikon budaya di seluruh Asia selama bertahun-tahun (dengan sangat disayangkan tutup pada 2020). Toko buku juga disebut 'shūjú' di Taiwan, tetapi kedai kecil yang dikurasi dibedakan sebagai 'toko buku independen'. Etiket kafe untuk berlama-lama: jangan memonopoli kursi saat ramai, dan memesan minuman lagi setelah beberapa saat ('tambah pesanan') meninggalkan kesan baik. Dua kata praktis: 'nèiyòng' berarti makan di tempat, 'wàidài' berarti dibawa pulang.","Food Delivery and Online Shopping: Tap Your Phone, and It Arrives":"Pesan-Antar Makanan dan Belanja Online: Ketuk Ponselmu, dan Ia Tiba","Rain or shine, day or the dead of night, a few taps on your phone bring hot meals and household goods right to your doorstep—in just a few years, everyday life in Taiwan has completely changed. Let's take a look at the real scene of how food delivery and online shopping have reshaped how people live.":"Hujan atau cerah, siang atau tengah malam buta, beberapa ketukan di ponselmu mendatangkan makanan panas dan barang rumah tangga langsung ke depan pintumu—hanya dalam beberapa tahun, kehidupan sehari-hari di Taiwan berubah total. Mari kita lihat gambaran nyata bagaimana pesan-antar makanan dan belanja online membentuk ulang cara orang hidup.","The most visible change is the \"delivery riders\" zipping all over the streets. Scooter riders in pink or green uniforms with big insulated boxes on their backs have become an everyday sight in Taiwan. Through a delivery app on your phone, without leaving home you can order a nearby bento, hot pot, hand-shaken drinks, and even over-the-counter medicine from a pharmacy or fresh groceries from a supermarket. For people working overtime, parents raising kids, or anyone who doesn't want to go out on a rainy day, delivery is simply a lifesaver.":"Perubahan paling kasat mata adalah para \"kurir pesan-antar\" yang melesat di seluruh jalanan. Pengendara skuter berseragam merah muda atau hijau dengan kotak insulasi besar di punggung telah menjadi pemandangan sehari-hari di Taiwan. Melalui aplikasi pesan-antar di ponselmu, tanpa keluar rumah kamu bisa memesan bento terdekat, hot pot, minuman kocok, bahkan obat bebas dari apotek atau bahan makanan segar dari supermarket. Bagi orang yang lembur, orang tua yang mengasuh anak, atau siapa pun yang tak mau keluar di hari hujan, pesan-antar benar-benar penyelamat.","Ordering delivery is simple: open the app, choose a restaurant, add to cart, confirm your address, pick whether to pay by credit card, e-payment, or \"cash on delivery,\" and hit submit. The app shows in real time \"your food is being prepared,\" \"the rider has picked it up,\" \"five minutes away from you,\" and you can even watch the scooter approach your home on a map. This instant, transparent experience makes even waiting far less anxious.":"Memesan pesan-antar itu sederhana: buka aplikasi, pilih restoran, masukkan ke keranjang, konfirmasi alamatmu, pilih membayar dengan kartu kredit, pembayaran elektronik, atau \"bayar di tempat\", lalu tekan kirim. Aplikasi menampilkan secara langsung \"makananmu sedang disiapkan\", \"kurir telah mengambilnya\", \"lima menit lagi sampai kepadamu\", dan kamu bahkan bisa menyaksikan skuter mendekati rumahmu di peta. Pengalaman yang instan dan transparan ini membuat menunggu pun jauh lebih tidak menegangkan.","Beyond food, Taiwanese people increasingly rely on \"online shopping\" for goods. The most iconic is \"Shopee\" (Xiapi), an app in almost everyone's phone. From clothes, shoes, and electronics to kitchenware, you can buy anything—often cheaper than physical stores, with frequent free-shipping deals and discount coupons. After you place an order, the parcel reaches you via home delivery or a convenience store, and waiting to unbox it has become a small delight for many.":"Selain makanan, orang Taiwan makin bergantung pada \"belanja online\" untuk barang-barang. Yang paling ikonik adalah \"Shopee\" (Xiapi), aplikasi yang ada di ponsel hampir setiap orang. Dari pakaian, sepatu, dan elektronik hingga peralatan dapur, kamu bisa membeli apa saja—sering lebih murah daripada toko fisik, dengan promo gratis ongkir dan kupon diskon yang kerap ada. Setelah kamu memesan, paket sampai kepadamu lewat antar ke rumah atau minimarket, dan menunggu untuk membukanya telah menjadi kesenangan kecil bagi banyak orang.","Taiwanese online shopping has a very special option that foreigners often find novel: \"convenience-store pickup.\" When you buy online, instead of entering your home address, you can pick a nearby convenience store as the \"pickup location.\" When the parcel arrives, your phone gets a notification; you go to that store with your ID or a pickup code, and the clerk brings the parcel out from the back. Because Taiwan's convenience-store density is extremely high, this pickup method is convenient and safe—and you can conveniently pay \"cash on delivery\" too.":"Belanja online di Taiwan memiliki opsi yang sangat khusus yang sering dianggap baru oleh orang asing: \"pengambilan di minimarket\". Saat kamu berbelanja online, alih-alih memasukkan alamat rumahmu, kamu bisa memilih minimarket terdekat sebagai \"lokasi pengambilan\". Ketika paket tiba, ponselmu menerima notifikasi; kamu pergi ke toko itu dengan KTP atau kode pengambilan, dan pramuniaga membawakan paket dari dalam. Karena kepadatan minimarket di Taiwan sangat tinggi, metode pengambilan ini praktis dan aman—dan kamu juga bisa dengan mudah \"membayar di tempat\".","Another very Taiwanese way to shop is \"group buying\" (tuángòu). There's always an enthusiastic \"group mom\" or \"group dad\" in the office who rallies everyone to order fruit, snacks, bentos, or drinks together. Because the volume is large, you often get a cheaper price or free shipping. In neighborhood, school, and company group chats, a line like \"Anyone want to order together?\" can pop up at any time. The very process of rallying a group becomes a small bit of socializing that brings colleagues and neighbors closer.":"Cara berbelanja lain yang sangat khas Taiwan adalah \"beli bersama\" (tuángòu). Selalu ada \"ibu grup\" atau \"bapak grup\" yang antusias di kantor yang mengajak semua orang memesan buah, camilan, bento, atau minuman bersama. Karena jumlahnya besar, kamu sering mendapat harga lebih murah atau gratis ongkir. Di grup chat lingkungan, sekolah, dan perusahaan, kalimat seperti \"Ada yang mau pesan bareng?\" bisa muncul kapan saja. Proses mengajak sekelompok orang itu sendiri menjadi sedikit ajang bersosialisasi yang mendekatkan rekan kerja dan tetangga.","Delivery and online shopping have changed not only how we \"buy things,\" but also quietly changed the distance between people. Some worry that over-reliance on delivery makes everyone go out less and become more of a homebody; others feel these tools give busy modern people precious extra time to spend with family, rest, or do what they love. Either way, for you—just starting life in Taiwan—learning to use these few apps will quickly let you live as conveniently and freely as a local.":"Pesan-antar dan belanja online tidak hanya mengubah cara kita \"membeli barang\", tetapi juga diam-diam mengubah jarak antarmanusia. Sebagian khawatir ketergantungan berlebih pada pesan-antar membuat semua orang lebih jarang keluar dan makin betah di rumah; sebagian lain merasa alat-alat ini memberi manusia modern yang sibuk tambahan waktu berharga untuk bersama keluarga, beristirahat, atau melakukan yang mereka sukai. Bagaimanapun, bagimu—yang baru memulai hidup di Taiwan—belajar menggunakan beberapa aplikasi ini akan cepat membuatmu hidup senyaman dan sebebas warga lokal.","delivery rider":"kurir pesan-antar","online shopping":"belanja online","Shopee (major e-commerce platform)":"Shopee (platform e-commerce besar)","cash on delivery (COD)":"bayar di tempat (COD)","group buying":"beli bersama","to place an order":"memesan","shopping cart":"keranjang belanja","hand-shaken drinks (bubble tea etc.)":"minuman kocok (bubble tea dll.)","Taiwan's food delivery was long split between two giants—'foodpanda' (pink) and 'Uber Eats' (with industry reshuffling underway in recent years). Besides 'cash on delivery,' e-payments like 'LINE Pay' and 'JKOPay' are widespread. 'Convenience-store pickup with payment' means collecting at a store and paying on the spot—reassuring for those who'd rather not use a credit card. Incidentally, 'zháipèi' (home delivery) comes from Japanese and works in Taiwan too—a handy word to know.":"Pesan-antar makanan di Taiwan lama terbagi antara dua raksasa—'foodpanda' (merah muda) dan 'Uber Eats' (dengan penataan ulang industri yang berlangsung dalam beberapa tahun terakhir). Selain 'bayar di tempat', pembayaran elektronik seperti 'LINE Pay' dan 'JKOPay' tersebar luas. 'Pengambilan di minimarket dengan pembayaran' berarti mengambil di toko dan membayar di tempat—menenangkan bagi mereka yang enggan menggunakan kartu kredit. Omong-omong, 'zháipèi' (antar ke rumah) berasal dari bahasa Jepang dan juga berlaku di Taiwan—kata yang berguna untuk diketahui.","History & People":"Sejarah & Manusia","Taiwan's Layered History: An Island Woven from Many Cultures":"Sejarah Berlapis Taiwan: Pulau yang Ditenun dari Banyak Budaya","Walk around Taiwan and you'll notice Indigenous languages, Hokkien and Hakka, buildings from the Japanese era, and postwar streetscapes all overlapping. This island's history wasn't made by a single people or a single age. People who crossed the sea each left a layer of their own culture—and that layering is exactly what makes Taiwan what it is today.":"Berkelilinglah di Taiwan dan kamu akan menyadari bahasa-bahasa Pribumi, Hokkien dan Hakka, bangunan dari era Jepang, dan lanskap jalanan pascaperang semuanya bertumpuk. Sejarah pulau ini tidak dibuat oleh satu bangsa atau satu zaman saja. Orang-orang yang menyeberangi laut masing-masing meninggalkan satu lapisan budaya mereka sendiri—dan pelapisan itulah yang justru menjadikan Taiwan seperti sekarang.","To understand Taiwan's history, it's best to begin with the Indigenous peoples. Thousands of years before anyone else arrived on this island, Austronesian-speaking Indigenous peoples were already living here. Today the state officially recognizes sixteen groups—such as the Amis, Atayal, Paiwan, Bunun, and Tao—each with its own language, ceremonies, and traditions. Their cultures form the oldest and most fundamental layer of Taiwan.":"Untuk memahami sejarah Taiwan, sebaiknya mulai dari suku-suku Pribumi. Ribuan tahun sebelum siapa pun tiba di pulau ini, suku-suku Pribumi penutur bahasa Austronesia telah tinggal di sini. Kini negara secara resmi mengakui enam belas kelompok—seperti Amis, Atayal, Paiwan, Bunun, dan Tao—masing-masing dengan bahasa, upacara, dan tradisinya sendiri. Budaya mereka membentuk lapisan tertua dan paling mendasar dari Taiwan.","By the seventeenth century, Taiwan began to appear on world maps. The Dutch and the Spanish arrived, in the south and north respectively, setting up outposts and trading—a period known as the Dutch–Spanish era. The Dutch built a fort around present-day Tainan, introduced sugarcane and rice cultivation, and recruited many Han migrants from across the strait to open up farmland. Though this foreign rule didn't last very long, it formally ushered Taiwan into the great age of maritime trade.":"Menjelang abad ketujuh belas, Taiwan mulai muncul di peta dunia. Orang Belanda dan Spanyol tiba, masing-masing di selatan dan utara, membangun pos dan berdagang—suatu masa yang dikenal sebagai era Belanda–Spanyol. Orang Belanda membangun benteng di sekitar Tainan masa kini, memperkenalkan budidaya tebu dan padi, serta merekrut banyak pendatang Han dari seberang selat untuk membuka lahan pertanian. Meski kekuasaan asing ini tidak berlangsung lama, ia secara resmi mengantar Taiwan masuk ke zaman besar perdagangan maritim.","Next came the Zheng (Ming loyalist) and Qing periods. In the mid-seventeenth century, Zheng Chenggong led troops that drove out the Dutch and established a regime in Taiwan, bringing more Han migrants, Confucian education, and farming techniques. Taiwan was then incorporated into the Qing empire for over two hundred years. During this time, migrants from Fujian and Guangdong crossed the sea in wave after wave, bringing Hokkien and Hakka along with beliefs such as Mazu and Lord Guan. Many of Taiwan's old temples, old place names, and food customs gradually took shape in this era.":"Berikutnya datang periode Zheng (loyalis Ming) dan Qing. Pada pertengahan abad ketujuh belas, Zheng Chenggong memimpin pasukan yang mengusir orang Belanda dan mendirikan pemerintahan di Taiwan, membawa lebih banyak pendatang Han, pendidikan Konfusius, dan teknik bertani. Taiwan kemudian dimasukkan ke dalam kekaisaran Qing selama lebih dari dua ratus tahun. Selama masa ini, pendatang dari Fujian dan Guangdong menyeberangi laut gelombang demi gelombang, membawa Hokkien dan Hakka beserta kepercayaan seperti Mazu dan Dewa Guan. Banyak kuil tua, nama tempat lama, dan kebiasaan kuliner Taiwan berangsur terbentuk di era ini.","In 1895, Taiwan entered the Japanese colonial period, which lasted fifty years and left a deep and lasting mark. During this time, modern infrastructure—railways, roads, harbors, running water, electricity, schools, and hospitals—was built up piece by piece; the street plans of many cities, old train stations, and government buildings also date from then. The Japanese-style wooden dormitories and red-brick Western-style houses you see in Taiwan today, along with the few Japanese phrases many elders still speak, are all traces left by this chapter of history.":"Pada 1895, Taiwan memasuki periode kolonial Jepang, yang berlangsung lima puluh tahun dan meninggalkan jejak yang dalam dan bertahan lama. Selama masa ini, infrastruktur modern—rel kereta, jalan, pelabuhan, air ledeng, listrik, sekolah, dan rumah sakit—dibangun sepotong demi sepotong; tata jalan banyak kota, stasiun kereta tua, dan gedung pemerintahan juga berasal dari masa itu. Asrama kayu bergaya Jepang dan rumah bergaya Barat berbata merah yang kamu lihat di Taiwan sekarang, beserta beberapa frasa bahasa Jepang yang masih dituturkan banyak orang tua, semuanya adalah jejak yang ditinggalkan babak sejarah ini.","After 1945, Taiwan entered a new postwar phase. A large wave of migrants from many places flowed in again, bringing different accents, tastes, and cultures, and making Taiwanese society even more diverse. Over several decades of development, Taiwan moved step by step from an agricultural society toward industry and technology, gradually opened up in the 1980s and 1990s, and eventually arrived at the democratic society everyone knows today. This process of democratization is an important shared memory in the hearts of many Taiwanese.":"Setelah 1945, Taiwan memasuki fase pascaperang yang baru. Gelombang besar pendatang dari banyak tempat kembali mengalir masuk, membawa aksen, cita rasa, dan budaya yang berbeda, dan menjadikan masyarakat Taiwan makin beragam. Selama beberapa dekade pembangunan, Taiwan bergerak selangkah demi selangkah dari masyarakat agraris menuju industri dan teknologi, berangsur terbuka pada 1980-an dan 1990-an, dan akhirnya sampai pada masyarakat demokratis yang dikenal semua orang sekarang. Proses demokratisasi ini adalah kenangan bersama yang penting di hati banyak orang Taiwan.","Stack these layers of history together and you'll find that what truly makes Taiwan enchanting is its diversity. Indigenous ceremonies, Hokkien and Hakka temple fairs, old houses from the Japanese era, and hometown flavors brought from all over after the war all coexist on this island. Walk down a street and behind a single temple, an old house, or a small dish there often hides a story spanning several eras. Once you understand this, your way of seeing Taiwan becomes gentler and more three-dimensional.":"Tumpuk lapisan-lapisan sejarah ini bersama dan kamu akan mendapati bahwa yang sungguh membuat Taiwan memikat adalah keberagamannya. Upacara Pribumi, pesta kuil Hokkien dan Hakka, rumah-rumah tua dari era Jepang, dan cita rasa kampung halaman yang dibawa dari berbagai penjuru setelah perang semuanya hidup berdampingan di pulau ini. Menyusuri sebuah jalan, dan di balik sebuah kuil, sebuah rumah tua, atau sepiring hidangan kecil sering tersembunyi kisah yang membentang beberapa zaman. Begitu kamu memahami ini, cara pandangmu terhadap Taiwan menjadi lebih lembut dan lebih berdimensi.","Indigenous peoples":"suku-suku Pribumi","Austronesian language family":"rumpun bahasa Austronesia","the Dutch–Spanish period":"periode Belanda–Spanyol","immigrant, migration":"pendatang, migrasi","to reclaim/cultivate land":"membuka/menggarap lahan","Hokkien (Southern Min)":"Hokkien (Min Selatan)","Japanese colonial period":"periode kolonial Jepang","infrastructure":"infrastruktur","democratization":"demokratisasi","diverse, pluralistic":"beragam, majemuk","Because interpretations of Taiwan's history can shift depending on one's standpoint, this article keeps to a neutral view: that of many cultures layered upon one another. Notably, many buildings from the Japanese colonial era still stand in Taiwan, and more and more of them have been restored and turned into cafés, bookstores, and heritage museums. Efforts to preserve Indigenous languages and cultures have also grown in recent years, with school programs and public broadcasts that let people learn each group's language. The 'layers' of history are still very much alive.":"Karena penafsiran sejarah Taiwan dapat bergeser tergantung sudut pandang seseorang, artikel ini berpegang pada pandangan netral: yaitu pandangan tentang banyak budaya yang berlapis satu sama lain. Yang patut dicatat, banyak bangunan dari era kolonial Jepang masih berdiri di Taiwan, dan makin banyak di antaranya telah dipugar dan diubah menjadi kafe, toko buku, dan museum warisan. Upaya melestarikan bahasa dan budaya Pribumi juga tumbuh dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, dengan program sekolah dan siaran publik yang memungkinkan orang mempelajari bahasa setiap kelompok. 'Lapisan-lapisan' sejarah masih sangat hidup.","Old Streets and Heritage: How the Past Lives on Today":"Jalan Tua dan Warisan: Bagaimana Masa Lalu Hidup di Masa Kini","Duck under a red-brick arcade and stroll a lane lined with wooden signboards, and time seems to slow just a little. Taiwan's old streets and heritage sites aren't mere tourist spots. The memory of old trades, daily life, and faith still lives on in the shopfronts and the scent of tea. Let's wander through a few of the most iconic places together.":"Menunduklah di bawah arkade berbata merah dan menyusurilah lorong yang dipenuhi papan nama kayu, dan waktu seakan sedikit melambat. Jalan-jalan tua dan situs warisan Taiwan bukan sekadar tempat wisata. Kenangan akan perdagangan lama, kehidupan sehari-hari, dan keimanan masih hidup di etalase toko dan aroma teh. Mari kita menjelajahi beberapa tempat paling ikonik bersama-sama.","When it comes to old streets in Taipei, the first one many people think of is Dadaocheng. This has been an important commercial hub since the nineteenth century, thriving on trade in tea, dry goods, and fabric thanks to the wharves along the Tamsui River. Step into Dihua Street and the rows of old buildings on both sides include Hokkien-style red-brick shopfronts and Western-style houses decorated with Baroque flourishes. Today, alongside long-established herbal-medicine and dry-goods shops, many creative boutiques and cafés have moved in—old and new interlacing with a special charm.":"Bicara soal jalan-jalan tua di Taipei, yang pertama terpikir oleh banyak orang adalah Dadaocheng. Tempat ini telah menjadi pusat perdagangan penting sejak abad kesembilan belas, berkembang pesat dari perdagangan teh, bahan kering, dan kain berkat dermaga-dermaga di sepanjang Sungai Tamsui. Melangkahlah ke Jalan Dihua dan deretan bangunan tua di kedua sisi mencakup etalase berbata merah bergaya Hokkien dan rumah bergaya Barat berhias ornamen Barok. Kini, di samping toko obat herbal dan bahan kering yang sudah lama berdiri, banyak butik kreatif dan kafe yang masuk—yang lama dan yang baru berjalin dengan pesona tersendiri.","If you want to see more intact Qing-dynasty street houses, head to Lukang in central Taiwan. Lukang was once one of Taiwan's greatest ports, with merchant ships coming and going and temples thick with incense, leaving behind many old temples, historic homes, and narrow lanes. Its most famous spot is 'Breast-Touching Lane'—an alley so narrow two people must turn sideways to pass—along with the finely carved Longshan Temple and Tianhou Temple. Walking through Lukang, you can vividly feel the former prosperity of an old city and how carefully it has been preserved.":"Kalau kamu ingin melihat rumah-rumah jalan era Dinasti Qing yang lebih utuh, pergilah ke Lukang di Taiwan tengah. Lukang dahulu adalah salah satu pelabuhan terbesar Taiwan, dengan kapal-kapal dagang yang hilir mudik dan kuil-kuil yang pekat dengan asap dupa, meninggalkan banyak kuil tua, rumah bersejarah, dan lorong sempit. Tempat paling terkenalnya adalah 'Lorong Sentuh Dada'—gang yang begitu sempit sehingga dua orang harus memiringkan badan untuk berpapasan—beserta Kuil Longshan dan Kuil Tianhou yang berukiran halus. Berjalan menyusuri Lukang, kamu bisa merasakan dengan jelas kemakmuran masa lalu sebuah kota tua dan betapa cermatnya ia dilestarikan.","Jiufen, in the mountains of the north, has a completely different feel. Originally a gold-mining mountain town, Jiufen fell quiet for a time as mining declined, then came alive again thanks to film and tourism. Climb the stone steps and on both sides are old houses stacked layer upon layer against the hillside, with red lanterns strung all the way to the top. At dusk, sea mist drifts up from below and the lights glow warmly through the fog—that atmosphere where mountain meets sea has made Jiufen one of the most unforgettable Taiwanese scenes in many people's hearts.":"Jiufen, di pegunungan utara, memiliki nuansa yang sama sekali berbeda. Awalnya kota pegunungan penambangan emas, Jiufen sempat sunyi selama beberapa waktu saat pertambangan meredup, lalu hidup kembali berkat film dan pariwisata. Naiki tangga batu dan di kedua sisinya ada rumah-rumah tua yang bertumpuk berlapis-lapis di lereng bukit, dengan lampion merah terjulur hingga ke puncak. Saat senja, kabut laut membubung dari bawah dan lampu-lampu bersinar hangat menembus kabut—suasana tempat gunung bertemu laut itulah yang menjadikan Jiufen salah satu pemandangan Taiwan paling tak terlupakan di hati banyak orang.","Beyond whole clusters of old streets, individual heritage sites and old buildings are scattered across Taiwan too. Many train stations, government offices, schools, and dormitories left from the Japanese era are of brick-and-wood construction, with clean, elegant lines. Red-brick official buildings and wooden Japanese-style houses, after restoration, are often reborn as museums, libraries, or arts spaces. These old buildings weren't torn down but repurposed, so that history doesn't just stay in textbooks—you can actually walk in, sit down, and feel it slowly.":"Di luar seluruh gugusan jalan tua, situs warisan dan bangunan tua yang berdiri sendiri juga tersebar di seantero Taiwan. Banyak stasiun kereta, kantor pemerintah, sekolah, dan asrama yang tersisa dari era Jepang berkonstruksi bata-dan-kayu, dengan garis yang bersih dan elegan. Gedung resmi berbata merah dan rumah kayu bergaya Jepang, setelah dipugar, sering terlahir kembali sebagai museum, perpustakaan, atau ruang seni. Bangunan-bangunan tua ini tidak dirobohkan melainkan dialihfungsikan, sehingga sejarah tidak sekadar tinggal di buku teks—kamu benar-benar bisa masuk, duduk, dan merasakannya perlahan.","Why are Taiwanese willing to put in the effort to preserve these old things? Because for many people, old streets and heritage sites aren't just bricks and tiles but a kind of 'root.' Grandparents did business here, prayed here, grew up here—these spaces hold the memories of generation after generation. In recent years, the idea of 'heritage preservation' has drawn ever more attention, with residents, government, and young entrepreneurs working together to make old buildings meet the needs of modern life without losing their original character.":"Mengapa orang Taiwan rela bersusah payah melestarikan benda-benda lama ini? Karena bagi banyak orang, jalan tua dan situs warisan bukan sekadar bata dan genting melainkan semacam 'akar'. Kakek-nenek berdagang di sini, bersembahyang di sini, tumbuh besar di sini—ruang-ruang ini menyimpan kenangan generasi demi generasi. Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, gagasan 'pelestarian warisan' makin banyak menarik perhatian, dengan warga, pemerintah, dan pengusaha muda bahu-membahu agar bangunan tua memenuhi kebutuhan hidup modern tanpa kehilangan karakter aslinya.","Next time you come to Taiwan, why not pick an old street and walk it slowly? Buy a pack of old-fashioned pastries, sip tea brewed by a long-established tea shop, and look up at the carvings above the doorways and the weathered signboards. You'll realize these places move us not because they are 'old,' but because they are 'still alive'—shops still open, people still live here, and the stories go on. The past, in just this way, lives quietly on in today's Taiwan.":"Lain kali kamu datang ke Taiwan, mengapa tidak memilih satu jalan tua dan menyusurinya perlahan? Beli sebungkus kue kuno, seruput teh yang diseduh kedai teh yang sudah lama berdiri, dan tengadahlah menatap ukiran di atas ambang pintu dan papan nama yang lapuk dimakan cuaca. Kamu akan menyadari tempat-tempat ini menyentuh kita bukan karena mereka 'tua', melainkan karena mereka 'masih hidup'—toko masih buka, orang masih tinggal di sini, dan kisah-kisahnya terus berlanjut. Masa lalu, justru dengan cara inilah, hidup dengan tenang di Taiwan masa kini.","old street":"jalan tua","historic site, heritage site":"situs bersejarah, situs warisan","wharf, dock":"dermaga, pelabuhan","red brick":"bata merah","Western-style building":"bangunan bergaya Barat","cultural-creative (industry)":"(industri) kreatif budaya","mining industry":"industri pertambangan","lantern":"lampion","to restore, renovate":"memugar, merenovasi","cultural heritage/property":"warisan/cagar budaya","old-fashioned/nostalgic flavor":"nuansa kuno/nostalgia","shop sign, signboard":"papan nama toko","Before Lunar New Year, Dihua Street in Dadaocheng turns into a bustling 'New Year goods street,' packed with people buying nuts, dried fruit, and dry goods for the holiday. Jiufen, meanwhile, is popular with overseas visitors for evoking the world of a famous Japanese animated film, though the filmmakers have said it wasn't a direct model. Either way, the scene of red lanterns, stone steps, and mountains meeting the sea is unforgettable once you've seen it. If you visit an old street, weekday mornings or evenings are better than the crowded weekends.":"Menjelang Tahun Baru Imlek, Jalan Dihua di Dadaocheng berubah menjadi 'jalan belanja Tahun Baru' yang ramai, dipadati orang-orang yang membeli kacang-kacangan, buah kering, dan bahan makanan kering untuk perayaan. Sementara itu, Jiufen digemari wisatawan asing karena mengingatkan pada dunia sebuah film animasi Jepang terkenal, meski para pembuat filmnya menyatakan tempat itu bukan model langsungnya. Bagaimanapun, pemandangan lampion merah, tangga batu, dan gunung yang bertemu laut sulit dilupakan begitu Anda melihatnya. Jika ingin mengunjungi jalan tua, pagi atau malam di hari kerja lebih baik daripada akhir pekan yang padat.","The Pride of Taiwan: Taiwanese Who Shine on the World Stage":"Kebanggaan Taiwan: Orang Taiwan yang Bersinar di Panggung Dunia","An island not very large, with a population that isn't huge. And yet Taiwan has produced people and companies who stand at the very top of the world—in film, sports, cuisine, and even semiconductors. Taiwanese affectionately and proudly call such people 'the pride of Taiwan.' Today, let's meet a few of them and look at a few of these fields.":"Sebuah pulau yang tidak terlalu besar, dengan penduduk yang tidak banyak pula. Namun Taiwan telah melahirkan orang-orang dan perusahaan yang berdiri di puncak dunia—dalam film, olahraga, kuliner, bahkan semikonduktor. Orang Taiwan dengan penuh sayang dan bangga menyebut mereka 'kebanggaan Taiwan.' Hari ini, mari kita jumpai beberapa di antaranya dan menengok beberapa bidang tersebut.","When it comes to 'the pride of Taiwan,' the first name many people think of is the film director Ang Lee. Born in Taiwan, he later studied film in the United States and went from obscurity to international acclaim. His films span a very wide range of subjects, from stories of Chinese families to Western literary classics, and he has won the Academy Award for Best Director twice. Ang Lee often says it took him many years to slowly find his own way of telling stories, and that patience and persistence have encouraged many young people who want to pursue a creative path.":"Berbicara tentang 'kebanggaan Taiwan,' nama pertama yang terlintas di benak banyak orang adalah sutradara film Ang Lee. Lahir di Taiwan, ia kemudian belajar film di Amerika Serikat dan beranjak dari tak dikenal menjadi diakui secara internasional. Film-filmnya mencakup tema yang sangat luas, dari kisah keluarga Tionghoa hingga karya sastra klasik Barat, dan ia telah dua kali memenangkan Academy Award untuk Sutradara Terbaik. Ang Lee sering berkata bahwa ia butuh bertahun-tahun untuk perlahan menemukan cara berceritanya sendiri, dan kesabaran serta kegigihan itu telah memberi semangat banyak anak muda yang ingin menekuni jalur kreatif.","If Ang Lee stands for culture and art, then the baker Wu Pao-chun walked another moving path. Growing up poor, he became an apprentice at a bakery as a young man and, by relentlessly studying Taiwan's local ingredients, created bread bursting with homegrown flavor. He later won a world-class baking competition, lifting bread with 'the taste of Taiwan' onto the international stage. His story tells everyone: you don't necessarily need a lot of schooling—if you take one thing to its extreme, you can stand at the top of the world all the same.":"Jika Ang Lee mewakili budaya dan seni, maka pembuat roti Wu Pao-chun menempuh jalan mengharukan yang lain. Tumbuh dalam kemiskinan, sejak muda ia magang di sebuah toko roti, dan dengan tekun mempelajari bahan-bahan lokal Taiwan, ia menciptakan roti yang sarat cita rasa negeri sendiri. Ia kemudian memenangkan kompetisi roti kelas dunia, mengangkat roti dengan 'rasa Taiwan' ke panggung internasional. Kisahnya menyampaikan kepada semua orang: Anda tidak harus berpendidikan tinggi—asalkan menekuni satu hal hingga puncaknya, Anda tetap bisa berdiri di puncak dunia.","On the sports field, Taiwan has names to be proud of too. Badminton player Tai Tzu-ying is one of the most brilliant. Not especially tall, she relies on a delicate touch and clever shot placement to produce stroke after jaw-dropping stroke, and she held the world number-one (queen of the court) ranking for a long stretch. Every time she plays in an international tournament, many Taiwanese sit in front of the TV cheering her on. She showed the world that a young athlete from Taiwan can go toe-to-toe with the top players of every nation at the highest level of competition.":"Di arena olahraga, Taiwan juga punya nama-nama yang membanggakan. Pebulu tangkis Tai Tzu-ying adalah salah satu yang paling cemerlang. Meski tidak terlalu tinggi, ia mengandalkan sentuhan halus dan penempatan bola yang cerdik untuk menghasilkan pukulan demi pukulan yang memukau, dan lama menduduki peringkat nomor satu dunia (ratu lapangan). Setiap kali ia bertanding di turnamen internasional, banyak orang Taiwan duduk di depan TV menyemangatinya. Ia menunjukkan kepada dunia bahwa atlet muda dari Taiwan bisa bersaing sengit dengan para pemain top dari setiap negara di level kompetisi tertinggi.","Beyond individuals, Taiwan has an industry the whole world must take seriously: semiconductors. Taiwan leads the world in chip-manufacturing technology, and the most iconic name is TSMC. The phone or computer in your hand—even cars and all kinds of home appliances—very likely contain chips made in Taiwan. These invisible little chips are the heart of modern technology, and they have placed Taiwan at an extremely crucial position in the global supply chain. Some describe it as the 'sacred mountain that guards the nation.'":"Selain individu, Taiwan memiliki industri yang harus diperhitungkan seluruh dunia: semikonduktor. Taiwan memimpin dunia dalam teknologi pembuatan chip, dan nama yang paling ikonik adalah TSMC. Ponsel atau komputer di tangan Anda—bahkan mobil dan berbagai peralatan rumah tangga—sangat mungkin mengandung chip buatan Taiwan. Chip-chip kecil yang tak terlihat ini adalah jantung teknologi modern, dan telah menempatkan Taiwan pada posisi yang sangat penting dalam rantai pasok global. Sebagian orang menyebutnya 'gunung suci penjaga negara.'","Why can a place that isn't very big produce so many 'prides of Taiwan'? One reason may be that spirit of 'refusing to lose' and 'willing to grind' that runs through the Taiwanese. With limited resources and a market that isn't large, many people have no choice but to set their sights on the whole world and strike out with harder work and greater flexibility. Whether making films, baking bread, playing ball, or making chips, behind it there is usually a long story of quiet effort—of falling down and getting back up again.":"Mengapa tempat yang tidak terlalu besar bisa melahirkan begitu banyak 'kebanggaan Taiwan'? Salah satu alasannya mungkin semangat 'pantang kalah' dan 'mau bekerja keras' yang mengalir dalam diri orang Taiwan. Dengan sumber daya terbatas dan pasar yang tidak besar, banyak orang mau tak mau harus mengarahkan pandangan ke seluruh dunia dan berjuang dengan kerja lebih keras serta keluwesan lebih besar. Entah membuat film, memanggang roti, bermain bola, atau membuat chip, di baliknya biasanya ada kisah panjang tentang usaha diam-diam—tentang jatuh dan bangkit kembali.","The phrase 'the pride of Taiwan' actually doesn't belong only to those standing in the spotlight. The students, chefs, engineers, and athletes quietly striving all over the world, and every Taiwanese who lives earnestly at their own post, are in a sense part of this light too. What it represents is a spirit that, even on a small island, is willing to lift its head, work to shine, and let the world see who it is. That spirit may be the most moving strength Taiwan has.":"Frasa 'kebanggaan Taiwan' sebenarnya bukan milik mereka yang berdiri di bawah sorotan lampu saja. Para pelajar, koki, insinyur, dan atlet yang diam-diam berjuang di seluruh dunia, serta setiap orang Taiwan yang hidup dengan sungguh-sungguh di posnya masing-masing, dalam arti tertentu juga bagian dari cahaya ini. Yang diwakilinya adalah semangat yang, meski di pulau kecil, tetap mau mengangkat kepala, berjuang untuk bersinar, dan membiarkan dunia melihat siapa dirinya. Semangat itulah mungkin kekuatan Taiwan yang paling mengharukan.","'the pride of Taiwan'":"'kebanggaan Taiwan'","(film) director":"sutradara (film)","to be internationally renowned":"terkenal di kancah internasional","baker":"pembuat roti","apprentice":"magang, murid","badminton":"bulu tangkis","athlete, player":"atlet, pemain","semiconductor":"semikonduktor","unwilling to admit defeat":"pantang kalah","to work/strive hard (common Taiwan term)":"berjuang/bekerja keras (istilah umum di Taiwan)","'The pride of Taiwan' is a phrase used very often in Taiwanese media and everyday conversation, brought out to honor people who win international awards, athletes who shine at world championships, or companies recognized abroad. TSMC is one of the world's largest contract chipmakers, and its every move draws attention in economic news worldwide. Baseball is also popular in Taiwan, and players who have starred in the U.S. Major Leagues have long been called 'the pride of Taiwan' too. Who counts as the 'light' changes with the times, but the story of 'from a small island to the world' has always encouraged the people of Taiwan.":"'Kebanggaan Taiwan' adalah frasa yang sangat sering dipakai di media dan percakapan sehari-hari orang Taiwan, dikeluarkan untuk menghormati mereka yang meraih penghargaan internasional, atlet yang bersinar di kejuaraan dunia, atau perusahaan yang diakui di luar negeri. TSMC adalah salah satu pembuat chip kontrak terbesar di dunia, dan setiap langkahnya menarik perhatian dalam berita ekonomi di seluruh dunia. Bisbol juga populer di Taiwan, dan para pemain yang pernah bersinar di Major League Amerika Serikat sejak lama juga disebut 'kebanggaan Taiwan.' Siapa yang dianggap 'cahaya' berubah seiring zaman, tetapi kisah 'dari pulau kecil menuju dunia' selalu menyemangati rakyat Taiwan.","Education & Society":"Pendidikan & Masyarakat","Cram-School Culture: The Other Classroom After School":"Budaya Bimbingan Belajar: Kelas Lain Setelah Sekolah","When school lets out in the evening, many kids and teens don't head straight home—they go to a 'cram school.' For Taiwanese students, that's just an ordinary part of daily life. From neon-lit tutoring buildings to the famous 'Nanyang Street' by the station, let's look inside the vast after-school ecosystem that props up Taiwan's exam-driven society.":"Ketika sekolah usai di malam hari, banyak anak dan remaja tidak langsung pulang—mereka pergi ke 'tempat bimbingan belajar.' Bagi pelajar Taiwan, itu hanyalah bagian biasa dari keseharian. Dari gedung les bertabur lampu neon hingga 'Jalan Nanyang' yang terkenal di dekat stasiun, mari kita menengok ke dalam ekosistem belajar tambahan yang luas yang menopang masyarakat Taiwan yang berorientasi ujian.","In Taiwan, the 'cram school' (bǔxíbān) is a place almost every student encounters while growing up. 'Cramming' means paying to attend extra reinforcement classes outside the regular school curriculum, going over subjects like math, English, and science one more time. Walk through a city district, look up at the signboard-covered buildings, and you'll notice that whole towers—from the ground floor to the top—are packed with all kinds of cram schools, their bright lights glowing late into the night.":"Di Taiwan, 'tempat bimbingan belajar' (bǔxíbān) adalah tempat yang hampir setiap pelajar temui saat tumbuh dewasa. 'Belajar tambahan' berarti membayar untuk mengikuti kelas penguatan ekstra di luar kurikulum sekolah reguler, mengulang sekali lagi mata pelajaran seperti matematika, bahasa Inggris, dan sains. Berjalanlah melewati sebuah kawasan kota, tengadahlah ke gedung-gedung yang penuh papan nama, dan Anda akan menyadari seluruh menara—dari lantai dasar hingga puncak—dipenuhi berbagai tempat bimbingan belajar, dengan lampu terang menyala hingga larut malam.","There are more types of cram schools than foreigners tend to imagine. For younger children, if parents are still at work and can't look after them after school, they're sent to an 'ānqīnbān' (after-school care class), where teachers watch over their homework and review, and also mind them until the parents get off work in the evening. Middle- and high-schoolers mostly cram for 'advancement'—preparing for key exams like the huìkǎo, xuécè, and subject tests. Beyond academic subjects, there are classes devoted to English, essay writing, coding, and talents—so many options it makes your head spin.":"Jenis tempat bimbingan belajar lebih banyak daripada yang dibayangkan orang asing. Untuk anak-anak yang lebih kecil, jika orang tua masih bekerja dan tidak bisa mengurus mereka sepulang sekolah, mereka dititipkan ke 'ānqīnbān' (kelas penitipan seusai sekolah), tempat guru mengawasi PR dan pengulangan pelajaran, sekaligus menjaga mereka hingga orang tua pulang kerja di malam hari. Pelajar SMP dan SMA umumnya belajar tambahan untuk 'melanjutkan sekolah'—mempersiapkan ujian penting seperti huìkǎo, xuécè, dan ujian mata pelajaran. Selain mata pelajaran akademik, ada kelas khusus bahasa Inggris, menulis esai, koding, dan bakat—begitu banyak pilihan hingga membuat pusing.","Why is the cram-school habit so strong in Taiwan? The biggest reason behind it is 'academic pressure.' For a long time, society has widely believed that 'only by getting into a good school do you have good prospects,' and the score on a single exam can decide which high school or university you enter. Parents fear their child losing at the starting line, so even when tuition isn't cheap, they grit their teeth and let their kids cram a bit more. Children shuttle back and forth between school and cram school, getting home only at nine or ten at night—a shared memory of youth for many Taiwanese students.":"Mengapa kebiasaan bimbingan belajar begitu kuat di Taiwan? Alasan terbesar di baliknya adalah 'tekanan akademik.' Sejak lama, masyarakat luas percaya bahwa 'hanya dengan masuk sekolah bagus barulah masa depan cerah,' dan nilai satu ujian bisa menentukan SMA atau universitas mana yang Anda masuki. Orang tua takut anaknya kalah di garis start, sehingga meski biayanya tidak murah, mereka menahan diri dan membiarkan anak belajar tambahan sedikit lagi. Anak-anak hilir-mudik antara sekolah dan tempat les, baru sampai rumah pukul sembilan atau sepuluh malam—kenangan masa muda bersama bagi banyak pelajar Taiwan.","Speaking of cramming, you can't skip 'Nanyang Street' near Taipei Main Station. This short street has gathered a huge concentration of cram schools since long ago—especially 'retake classes' that prepare repeat candidates for the university exam—so everyone calls it 'Cram-School Street.' The street is full of students carrying backpacks and lecture handouts, lined with cheap buffet eateries and lunchbox shops where students wolf down a meal and rush off to class. For many Taiwanese, Nanyang Street is practically a byword for 'grinding for exams.'":"Berbicara tentang belajar tambahan, Anda tak bisa melewatkan 'Jalan Nanyang' dekat Stasiun Utama Taipei. Jalan pendek ini sejak lama menghimpun konsentrasi tempat bimbingan belajar yang sangat padat—terutama 'kelas ulangan' yang mempersiapkan peserta ujian ulang untuk ujian masuk universitas—sehingga semua orang menyebutnya 'Jalan Bimbingan Belajar.' Jalan itu penuh pelajar yang menggendong ransel dan membawa lembar materi kuliah, diapit warung buffet murah dan toko nasi kotak tempat pelajar melahap makanan lalu buru-buru pergi ke kelas. Bagi banyak orang Taiwan, Jalan Nanyang praktis menjadi kiasan untuk 'menggenjot diri demi ujian.'","Of course, in recent years society as a whole has begun to reflect on cram-school culture. Some feel that stuffing children full of classes from a young age—leaving them sleep-deprived with no time to play—is simply too hard on them; others question whether endless cramming really makes you better at studying. With falling birthrates, education reforms, and the push for 'multiple-pathway admissions,' advancement no longer hinges on a single exam, and the shape of cramming is slowly shifting. Overall, though, cramming remains extremely common in Taiwan and is unlikely to disappear anytime soon.":"Tentu saja, dalam beberapa tahun terakhir masyarakat secara keseluruhan mulai merefleksikan budaya bimbingan belajar. Sebagian merasa menjejali anak dengan kelas sejak kecil—membuat mereka kurang tidur tanpa waktu bermain—terlalu berat bagi mereka; sebagian lain mempertanyakan apakah belajar tambahan tanpa henti benar-benar membuat lebih pintar. Dengan menurunnya angka kelahiran, reformasi pendidikan, dan dorongan 'jalur masuk beragam,' kelanjutan sekolah tak lagi bergantung pada satu ujian, dan bentuk belajar tambahan perlahan bergeser. Namun secara keseluruhan, belajar tambahan tetap sangat lazim di Taiwan dan kecil kemungkinannya lenyap dalam waktu dekat.","cram school":"tempat bimbingan belajar","after-school care class":"kelas penitipan seusai sekolah","advancement to higher schooling":"melanjutkan ke jenjang sekolah lebih tinggi","academic/advancement pressure":"tekanan akademik/melanjutkan sekolah","to take supplementary lessons; cram":"mengikuti les tambahan; menggenjot belajar","retake/repeater class":"kelas ulangan (untuk peserta ujian ulang)","the General Scholastic Ability Test (a university entrance exam)":"Ujian Kemampuan Skolastik Umum (ujian masuk universitas)","the junior-high comprehensive assessment":"asesmen komprehensif SMP","lecture handout / study material":"lembar materi kuliah / bahan belajar","Nanyang Street (Taipei's famous cram-school street)":"Jalan Nanyang (jalan bimbingan belajar terkenal di Taipei)","starting line":"garis start","multiple-pathway admissions":"penerimaan jalur beragam","The word 'bǔxí' is used in the adult world too. Many working adults attend cram schools to prepare for qualifying exams (civil-service or language tests), and in Taiwan, prep schools for the 'civil-service exam' are a whole big industry. The phenomenon of the 'star teacher' (míngshī) is also distinctive: popular instructors have their faces plastered large on signboards and bus ads, treated almost like celebrities. Asking a Taiwanese student 'Do you go to cram school?' is as natural an ice-breaker as asking about someone's club activities elsewhere.":"Kata 'bǔxí' juga dipakai di dunia orang dewasa. Banyak pekerja mengikuti bimbingan belajar untuk mempersiapkan ujian kualifikasi (ujian pegawai negeri atau ujian bahasa), dan di Taiwan, lembaga persiapan 'ujian pegawai negeri' adalah industri besar tersendiri. Fenomena 'guru bintang' (míngshī) juga khas: instruktur populer wajahnya terpampang besar di papan nama dan iklan bus, diperlakukan hampir seperti selebritas. Menanyai pelajar Taiwan 'Apakah kamu ikut les?' sama wajarnya dengan menanyakan kegiatan klub seseorang di tempat lain sebagai pembuka obrolan.","Military Service: A Shared Rite of Passage for Taiwanese Men":"Wajib Militer: Ritus Peralihan Bersama bagi Pria Taiwan","Talk with male friends in Taiwan long enough and one topic is sure to come up: 'serving in the military' (dāng bīng). Shaved-head boot-camp photos, scary stories about drill instructors, the sweet relief of discharge day… For Taiwanese men, military service is a major life event and a shared memory passed across generations.":"Mengobrol cukup lama dengan teman pria di Taiwan, pasti ada satu topik yang muncul: 'ikut wajib militer' (dāng bīng). Foto kepala plontos saat latihan dasar, cerita seram tentang instruktur, dan lega manisnya hari pembebasan… Bagi pria Taiwan, wajib militer adalah peristiwa besar dalam hidup dan kenangan bersama yang diwariskan lintas generasi.","In Taiwan, any adult man who meets the criteria has the duty to serve in the military—this is called 'compulsory service' (yìwùyì). When you reach a certain age and receive your draft notice, you must set aside your current job or studies and go to the armed forces for training and a period of group living. Taiwanese simply call this 'dāng bīng' (serving as a soldier). For many Taiwanese men, service is a threshold in becoming a man from a boy, and a life experience almost no one can dodge.":"Di Taiwan, setiap pria dewasa yang memenuhi syarat berkewajiban ikut wajib militer—ini disebut 'wajib militer' (yìwùyì). Ketika mencapai usia tertentu dan menerima surat panggilan, Anda harus mengesampingkan pekerjaan atau studi saat ini lalu masuk angkatan bersenjata untuk pelatihan dan hidup berkelompok selama satu periode. Orang Taiwan cukup menyebutnya 'dāng bīng' (menjadi tentara). Bagi banyak pria Taiwan, ini adalah ambang dalam menjadi pria dari seorang bocah, dan pengalaman hidup yang hampir tak seorang pun bisa mengelak.","The first stop of service is 'xīnxùn'—the new-recruit training center. The very first thing when you arrive is often 'shaving the head': you're clipped to a smooth buzz cut, resetting everyone's original hairstyle to zero. Next come putting on the uniform, learning attention and at-ease, folding a quilt into a crisp tofu-block square, and rising early each day for drills. This stretch is the hardest, but precisely because everyone endures it together, it's easy to build a 'band-of-brothers' bond with the buddies in your cohort (tóngtī).":"Perhentian pertama wajib militer adalah 'xīnxùn'—pusat pelatihan rekrut baru. Hal pertama begitu tiba biasanya 'cukur kepala': Anda dipangkas menjadi cepak licin, mengembalikan gaya rambut asli semua orang ke titik nol. Berikutnya mengenakan seragam, belajar sikap siap dan istirahat di tempat, melipat selimut menjadi kotak rapi seperti balok tahu, serta bangun pagi setiap hari untuk berlatih. Fase ini paling berat, tetapi justru karena semua menanggungnya bersama, mudah terjalin ikatan 'saudara seperjuangan' dengan rekan seangkatan (tóngtī).","Life in the military is quite unlike the outside world. Time is sliced fine: when to wake, eat, drill, and sleep are all regulated. Phones are usually collected and kept together, usable only at set times, which many find hard to get used to at first. When soldiers head home on leave, a young man in fatigues (jūnbiànfú) with a buzz cut stands out at the bus terminal or train station—one glance tells you 'that's an ābīnggē (soldier), currently serving.'":"Kehidupan di militer cukup berbeda dari dunia luar. Waktu dibagi sangat rinci: kapan bangun, makan, berlatih, dan tidur semuanya diatur. Ponsel biasanya dikumpulkan dan disimpan bersama, hanya boleh dipakai pada jam-jam tertentu, yang awalnya sulit dibiasakan banyak orang. Ketika prajurit pulang cuti, seorang pemuda berseragam lapangan (jūnbiànfú) dengan rambut cepak mencolok di terminal bus atau stasiun kereta—sekali lihat langsung tahu 'itu ābīnggē (prajurit), sedang bertugas.'","For everyone serving, the most anticipated day is 'discharge' (tuìwǔ). Discharge means the term is complete—you formally take off the uniform and return to a free life. Those near discharge are jokingly called 'old birds' (lǎoniǎo); they count down day by day, some crossing off the remaining days one box at a time on a calendar. On the actual day, many toss out their army-issue things and let out a shout—that feeling of regaining freedom is a rush only those who've served truly understand.":"Bagi setiap orang yang bertugas, hari yang paling dinantikan adalah 'pembebasan' (tuìwǔ). Pembebasan berarti masa tugas selesai—Anda resmi melepas seragam dan kembali ke kehidupan bebas. Mereka yang mendekati pembebasan diledek 'burung tua' (lǎoniǎo); mereka menghitung mundur hari demi hari, sebagian mencoret sisa hari satu kotak demi satu kotak di kalender. Pada hari itu, banyak yang membuang barang tentaranya dan berteriak lepas—rasa kembali merdeka itu kenikmatan yang hanya benar-benar dipahami mereka yang pernah bertugas.","Because nearly every man has served, 'army stories' are one of the easiest topics to bond over among Taiwanese men. Sit down to eat and drink together and it quickly turns into: 'Where did you serve?' 'What assignment did you draw?' 'Did you run into any outrageous senior or officer?' Some tell it with beaming pride, as if recounting heroic deeds; others half-joke that the biggest thing they gained from service was learning to 'endure' and to 'wait.' These shared memories become a kind of unspoken understanding across generations.":"Karena hampir setiap pria pernah bertugas, 'cerita tentara' adalah salah satu topik yang paling mudah mengakrabkan sesama pria Taiwan. Duduk makan dan minum bersama, obrolan cepat berubah menjadi: 'Kamu bertugas di mana?' 'Kamu dapat penempatan apa?' 'Pernah ketemu senior atau perwira yang keterlaluan?' Sebagian menceritakannya dengan bangga, seolah mengisahkan kepahlawanan; yang lain setengah bercanda bahwa hal terbesar yang mereka peroleh dari wajib militer adalah belajar 'bertahan' dan 'menunggu.' Kenangan bersama ini menjadi semacam saling pengertian lintas generasi.","to serve in the military":"menjalani wajib militer","military service":"dinas militer","compulsory/conscript service":"wajib militer (dinas wajib)","basic training / boot camp":"latihan dasar / pelatihan rekrut","to shave one's head":"mencukur kepala","to be discharged from service":"dibebastugaskan dari dinas","soldier (affectionate term)":"prajurit (sebutan akrab)","draft/conscription notice":"surat panggilan wajib militer","fellow recruit of the same cohort":"rekan rekrut seangkatan","military uniform":"seragam militer","to go out for drills":"keluar untuk latihan baris","to serve (a term of duty)":"menjalani (masa tugas)","Taiwan's conscription system has changed a great deal over time. The once two-to-three-year term was shortened in stages—at one point centered on just four months of 'military training'—but in recent years it was extended back to one year. Assignments are often decided by lottery (chōu qiān), so which branch (army, navy, air force) and which unit you end up in is down to luck—hence 'what lot did you draw?' is a staple of army chat. Note that service applies to men; women serve voluntarily. Depending on the physical exam, some do 'alternative service' (tìdàiyì), fulfilling their duty through civil or social work instead.":"Sistem wajib militer Taiwan telah banyak berubah seiring waktu. Masa tugas yang dulu dua hingga tiga tahun dipersingkat secara bertahap—pernah berpusat pada 'pelatihan militer' empat bulan saja—tetapi belakangan diperpanjang kembali menjadi satu tahun. Penempatan sering ditentukan lewat undian (chōu qiān), sehingga di matra mana (darat, laut, udara) dan unit mana Anda berakhir bergantung pada keberuntungan—maka 'kamu dapat undian apa?' menjadi bumbu wajib obrolan tentara. Perhatikan bahwa wajib militer berlaku bagi pria; wanita bertugas secara sukarela. Tergantung pemeriksaan fisik, sebagian menjalani 'dinas alternatif' (tìdàiyì), memenuhi kewajiban melalui pekerjaan sipil atau sosial.","Taiwan Weddings: Etiquette from Engagement to the Banquet":"Pernikahan Taiwan: Etiket dari Pertunangan hingga Resepsi","Get invited to a Taiwanese wedding banquet (xǐyàn) and your first puzzle may be: 'How much should I put in the red envelope?' Avoid the number four, give an even amount—such fine points of 'etiquette' (lǐshù) appear at every turn. From engagement and betrothal gifts to the bride-fetching ritual, the round-table banquet, and the toasts, let's peek into the customs surrounding a Taiwanese wedding.":"Diundang ke resepsi pernikahan Taiwan (xǐyàn), teka-teki pertama Anda mungkin: 'Berapa yang harus kumasukkan ke amplop merah?' Hindari angka empat, beri jumlah genap—detail-detail halus 'etiket' (lǐshù) semacam ini muncul di setiap sudut. Dari pertunangan dan seserahan hingga ritual menjemput pengantin, resepsi meja bundar, dan acara bersulang, mari kita mengintip adat seputar pernikahan Taiwan.","A traditional Taiwanese wedding usually splits into two stages: first the 'engagement' (dìnghūn), then the 'wedding' (jiéhūn). The engagement is when the two families formally confirm the match; the groom's side prepares betrothal gifts and 'wedding cakes' (xǐbǐng), which the bride's side distributes to relatives and friends—effectively announcing, 'our daughter is getting married.' Those who receive the cakes take the hint and later prepare a red envelope to offer their congratulations. Though many young people today streamline the rituals, the engagement and the giving of wedding cakes are traditions many families still keep.":"Pernikahan tradisional Taiwan biasanya terbagi dua tahap: mula-mula 'pertunangan' (dìnghūn), lalu 'pernikahan' (jiéhūn). Pertunangan adalah saat kedua keluarga resmi menegaskan jodoh; pihak mempelai pria menyiapkan seserahan dan 'kue pernikahan' (xǐbǐng), yang dibagikan pihak mempelai wanita kepada kerabat dan teman—seolah mengumumkan, 'putri kami akan menikah.' Mereka yang menerima kue menangkap isyaratnya dan kelak menyiapkan amplop merah untuk memberi selamat. Meski kini banyak anak muda menyederhanakan ritualnya, pertunangan dan pemberian kue pernikahan tetap tradisi yang masih dijaga banyak keluarga.","On the wedding day, one of the most vivid rituals is 'fetching the bride' (yíngqǔ). The groom leads a band of buddies ('brothers') in a motorcade of cars decked with ribbons and flowers, sweeping grandly to the bride's home to bring her back. At the door of the bride's house, the groom often has to clear the 'gate-crashing games' (chuǎngguān) set up by the bridesmaids—making him and his brothers offer all sorts of vows, even do slightly embarrassing stunts, before they'll open the door and let him see the bride. The whole thing is tense and hilarious at once—one of the most joyful segments of many weddings.":"Pada hari pernikahan, salah satu ritual paling semarak adalah 'menjemput pengantin' (yíngqǔ). Mempelai pria memimpin rombongan sahabat ('para saudara') dalam iring-iringan mobil berhias pita dan bunga, melaju megah ke rumah mempelai wanita untuk membawanya pulang. Di depan pintu rumah mempelai wanita, mempelai pria kerap harus melewati 'permainan penghadang pintu' (chuǎngguān) yang disiapkan para pengiring pengantin—memaksanya dan para saudaranya mengucapkan berbagai janji, bahkan melakukan aksi yang sedikit memalukan, sebelum pintu dibuka dan ia boleh menemui mempelai wanita. Keseluruhannya menegangkan sekaligus lucu—salah satu bagian paling menggembirakan dari banyak pernikahan.","If you're invited to a wedding, your most important task is preparing the 'red envelope' (hóngbāo). There are a few unspoken rules of etiquette here: the amount must be 'even,' because good things should come in pairs—common figures are 2,200, 3,600, or 6,600; and you must absolutely avoid 'four,' since 'four' (sì) sounds close to 'death' (sǐ) and is very unlucky. How much you give also depends on your relationship with the couple and on how upscale the banquet venue is.":"Jika diundang ke pernikahan, tugas terpenting Anda adalah menyiapkan 'amplop merah' (hóngbāo). Ada beberapa aturan etiket tak tertulis di sini: jumlahnya harus 'genap,' karena hal baik sebaiknya berpasangan—angka yang lazim adalah 2.200, 3.600, atau 6.600; dan Anda benar-benar harus menghindari 'empat,' sebab 'empat' (sì) terdengar mirip 'mati' (sǐ) dan sangat sial. Berapa yang Anda beri juga bergantung pada hubungan Anda dengan pasangan pengantin dan seberapa mewah tempat resepsinya.","Taiwanese wedding banquets come in many forms. Some hold them in a hotel ballroom, everyone seated table by table in dignified style; many others choose 'bàn zhuō'—an open-air feast set up right in a temple forecourt, an empty lot, or the arcade (qílóu) in front of one's home, with tents pitched, round tables laid out, and a specialist 'master chef' (zǒngpùshī) brought in to cook on site. The 'bàn zhuō' spread is lavish and lively—lobster, 'Buddha Jumps Over the Wall' soup, and big prawns brought out dish after dish—with relatives and neighbors filling dozens of tables, brimming with warm human feeling. It's the wedding scene lodged in many Taiwanese memories.":"Resepsi pernikahan Taiwan hadir dalam banyak bentuk. Sebagian menggelarnya di ballroom hotel, semua duduk meja demi meja secara anggun; banyak yang lain memilih 'bàn zhuō'—jamuan terbuka yang didirikan langsung di halaman kuil, lahan kosong, atau teras beratap (qílóu) di depan rumah, dengan tenda dipasang, meja bundar ditata, dan seorang 'juru masak utama' (zǒngpùshī) profesional didatangkan untuk memasak di tempat. Hidangan 'bàn zhuō' mewah dan meriah—lobster, sup 'Buddha Melompati Tembok,' dan udang besar disajikan hidangan demi hidangan—dengan kerabat dan tetangga memenuhi puluhan meja, sarat kehangatan. Itulah pemandangan pernikahan yang tertanam dalam kenangan banyak orang Taiwan.","Midway through the banquet, the bride and groom change into formal attire and begin 'toasting' (jìngjiǔ) table by table. Cups in hand, they offer a drink and thanks to the guests at each table, while guests return blessings such as 'grow old together' and 'may you soon have a child.' At some events there's also 'teasing the newlyweds' (nào dòngfáng), where relatives and friends crack jokes and set playful challenges for the couple to heat up the mood further. As the feast winds down, the couple and both sets of parents stand at the door to see each guest off, shaking hands and giving thanks, and hand out small return gifts or 'wedding candy' so everyone can carry the joy home.":"Di tengah resepsi, kedua mempelai berganti busana resmi dan mulai 'bersulang' (jìngjiǔ) dari meja ke meja. Dengan gelas di tangan, mereka menawarkan minuman dan ucapan terima kasih kepada tamu di setiap meja, sementara tamu membalas dengan doa seperti 'menua bersama' dan 'segera dikaruniai anak.' Di sebagian acara ada pula 'menggoda pengantin baru' (nào dòngfáng), tempat kerabat dan teman melontarkan lelucon serta tantangan jenaka untuk pasangan demi makin menghangatkan suasana. Saat jamuan usai, pasangan dan kedua orang tua berdiri di pintu mengantar setiap tamu, berjabat tangan dan berterima kasih, lalu membagikan bingkisan kecil balasan atau 'permen pernikahan' agar semua membawa pulang kebahagiaan.","to get engaged; engagement":"bertunangan; pertunangan","to marry; wedding":"menikah; pernikahan","to fetch the bride (ritual)":"menjemput pengantin (ritual)","wedding cakes/pastries (given to relatives and friends)":"kue pernikahan (diberikan kepada kerabat dan teman)","red envelope (cash gift)":"amplop merah (hadiah uang)","etiquette; proper courtesy":"etiket; tata krama yang pantas","wedding banquet":"resepsi pernikahan","wedding feast":"jamuan pernikahan","outdoor banquet (traditional catered feast)":"jamuan terbuka (pesta katering tradisional)","head banquet chef (from Taiwanese)":"juru masak utama jamuan (dari bahasa Taiwan)","to offer a toast":"mengajak bersulang","teasing the newlyweds (wedding-night games)":"menggoda pengantin baru (permainan malam pengantin)","The amount for a red envelope has a 'going rate' that varies by recipient and region. A common rule of thumb: if you attend the banquet, courtesy is to give at least enough to 'cover your seat.' When the invitation arrives—jokingly called a 'red bomb' (hóngsè zhàdàn), because it blows up your budget!—everyone checks the going rate and prepares an even sum. Note that the 'even is good' rule applies to happy occasions like weddings; a funeral condolence gift ('white envelope,' báibāo) follows entirely different rules. Wedding cakes are often given by the box, and sets that let you pick between Chinese-style and Western cookie-style are popular.":"Jumlah untuk amplop merah punya 'tarif berlaku' yang berbeda menurut penerima dan daerah. Aturan praktis yang umum: jika Anda menghadiri resepsi, sopannya beri setidaknya cukup untuk 'menutup kursi Anda.' Ketika undangan tiba—diledek 'bom merah' (hóngsè zhàdàn), karena meledakkan anggaran Anda!—semua orang mengecek tarif berlaku dan menyiapkan jumlah genap. Perhatikan bahwa aturan 'genap itu baik' berlaku untuk acara bahagia seperti pernikahan; sumbangan bela sungkawa pemakaman ('amplop putih,' báibāo) mengikuti aturan yang sama sekali berbeda. Kue pernikahan sering diberikan per kotak, dan set yang memungkinkan memilih antara kue gaya Tionghoa dan kue kering gaya Barat digemari.","Entertainment & Sports":"Hiburan & Olahraga","Baseball: Taiwan's National Sport":"Bisbol: Olahraga Nasional Taiwan","On a summer night, the stands come alive as drums and chants from the cheer squads merge into one, and total strangers high-five in the excitement—in Taiwan, baseball is more than a sport; it's a collective memory passed down across generations. Let's explore why baseball is called the 'national sport' and where that passion comes from.":"Pada malam musim panas, tribun menjadi hidup ketika tabuhan dan sorakan kelompok pendukung menyatu, dan orang-orang yang sama sekali asing bertepuk tangan penuh semangat—di Taiwan, bisbol lebih dari sekadar olahraga; ia kenangan kolektif yang diwariskan lintas generasi. Mari kita telusuri mengapa bisbol disebut 'olahraga nasional' dan dari mana gairah itu berasal.","In Taiwan, if you ask someone 'Which sport best represents Taiwan?' the answer is almost always baseball. People even call it outright the 'national ball.' This attachment has a long history: baseball arrived in Taiwan as early as the Japanese colonial era, and what truly sent the whole island into a frenzy was youth baseball in the 1960s and '70s. Back then, Taiwan's Little League teams repeatedly won world championships, and late-night games drew countless families to their radios and TVs, staying up all night to cheer together.":"Di Taiwan, jika Anda bertanya kepada seseorang 'Olahraga apa yang paling mewakili Taiwan?' jawabannya hampir selalu bisbol. Orang bahkan menyebutnya terus terang 'bola nasional.' Keterikatan ini punya sejarah panjang: bisbol tiba di Taiwan sejak era kolonial Jepang, dan yang benar-benar membuat seluruh pulau demam adalah bisbol remaja pada tahun 1960-an dan 1970-an. Kala itu, tim Little League Taiwan berulang kali memenangkan kejuaraan dunia, dan pertandingan larut malam menarik banyak keluarga ke radio dan TV, begadang semalaman untuk bersorak bersama.","In 1990, Taiwan founded its own professional baseball league, the Chinese Professional Baseball League (CPBL). Ever since, from March to October each year, ballparks across Taiwan fill with fans. Today there are several teams—the Uni-President Lions, CTBC Brothers, Rakuten Monkeys, Wei Chuan Dragons, and more—each with die-hard supporters. For many Taiwanese, going to a game isn't just about who wins; it's a way to spend a day off: buy a ticket, bring family and friends into the stadium, and watch the game while munching on salt-and-pepper fried chicken.":"Pada 1990, Taiwan mendirikan liga bisbol profesionalnya sendiri, Chinese Professional Baseball League (CPBL). Sejak itu, setiap tahun dari Maret hingga Oktober, stadion di seluruh Taiwan dipenuhi penggemar. Kini ada beberapa tim—Uni-President Lions, CTBC Brothers, Rakuten Monkeys, Wei Chuan Dragons, dan lainnya—masing-masing dengan pendukung fanatik. Bagi banyak orang Taiwan, menonton pertandingan bukan sekadar soal siapa yang menang; itu cara menghabiskan hari libur: beli tiket, ajak keluarga dan teman ke stadion, dan menonton sambil mengunyah ayam goreng lada garam.","What truly opens foreigners' eyes is the unique 'cheering culture' of Taiwanese ballparks. Each team has its own 'cheer squad,' led by a 'cheer leader' who stands at the front of the stands with a microphone, plus 'cheerleaders' who dance to rev up the crowd. Every time a player comes up to bat, the whole stadium sings a 'cheer song' written just for him, while fans clap to the beat and wave inflatable thunder sticks. This never-a-dull-moment style of watching—singing from start to finish—leaves a deep impression on fans from Japan, Korea, and the West alike.":"Yang benar-benar membuka mata orang asing adalah 'budaya sorak' unik di stadion bisbol Taiwan. Setiap tim punya 'kelompok pendukung' sendiri, dipimpin seorang 'pemandu sorak' yang berdiri di depan tribun dengan mikrofon, ditambah 'penari sorak' yang menari membakar semangat penonton. Setiap kali seorang pemain maju memukul, seluruh stadion menyanyikan 'lagu sorak' yang ditulis khusus untuknya, sementara penggemar bertepuk mengikuti irama dan mengibaskan tongkat guntur tiup. Gaya menonton tanpa jeda ini—bernyanyi dari awal sampai akhir—meninggalkan kesan mendalam bagi penggemar dari Jepang, Korea, maupun Barat.","Beyond watching games at home, Taiwanese also follow their 'overseas players'—Taiwanese athletes playing pro baseball abroad. The greatest source of pride is players who make it to America's Major League Baseball (MLB). In earlier years there were Chen Chin-feng and Wang Chien-ming; during the years Wang started as a pitcher for the New York Yankees, TVs across Taiwan were packed with fans at dawn. Later, players like Chen Wei-yin and Kuo Hong-chih shone overseas too. Whenever a Taiwanese player takes the field in a foreign land, the whole island seems to hold its breath and cheer right along with him.":"Selain menonton pertandingan di dalam negeri, orang Taiwan juga mengikuti 'pemain di luar negeri'—atlet Taiwan yang bermain bisbol profesional di mancanegara. Kebanggaan terbesar adalah pemain yang berhasil menembus Major League Baseball Amerika (MLB). Di masa awal ada Chen Chin-feng dan Wang Chien-ming; selama tahun-tahun Wang menjadi pitcher andalan New York Yankees, TV di seluruh Taiwan dipadati penggemar saat fajar. Belakangan, pemain seperti Chen Wei-yin dan Kuo Hong-chih juga bersinar di luar negeri. Setiap kali pemain Taiwan turun ke lapangan di negeri asing, seluruh pulau seakan menahan napas dan bersorak bersamanya.","What baseball means to Taiwan long ago surpassed the sport itself. In international competitions like the World Baseball Classic (WBC) or Asian tournaments, the moment Team Taiwan takes the field, the whole society's mood shifts. Office workers sneak a look at the livestream on their phones, and TVs in restaurants and convenience stores all switch to the same channel; a single clutch hit or home run can make an entire street erupt in cheers at once. For Taiwanese, cheering for the national team is also a way of binding people together and affirming that 'we're in this as one.'":"Makna bisbol bagi Taiwan sejak lama telah melampaui olahraga itu sendiri. Dalam kompetisi internasional seperti World Baseball Classic (WBC) atau turnamen Asia, begitu Tim Taiwan turun ke lapangan, suasana hati seluruh masyarakat berubah. Pekerja kantoran diam-diam mengintip siaran langsung di ponsel, dan TV di restoran serta minimarket semua beralih ke saluran yang sama; satu pukulan penentu atau home run bisa membuat seluruh jalan meledak bersorak serentak. Bagi orang Taiwan, mendukung tim nasional juga cara mengikat orang-orang menjadi satu dan menegaskan bahwa 'kita satu.'","If you're in Taiwan, I highly recommend setting aside a day to catch a CPBL game in person. You don't need to know the rules well—just feeling the energy of a packed crowd singing, jumping, and going wild for a single home run is more than worth it. Grab an order of salt-and-pepper chicken and a beer or bubble tea, and shout 'Base hit! Base hit! Home run!' along with the people around you. You'll discover that one of the fastest ways to understand a place is to step into the ballpark its people love most.":"Jika Anda berada di Taiwan, saya sangat menyarankan menyisihkan satu hari untuk menonton langsung pertandingan CPBL. Anda tak perlu paham betul aturannya—cukup merasakan energi kerumunan yang padat menyanyi, melompat, dan menggila demi satu home run saja sudah lebih dari sepadan. Pesan seporsi ayam lada garam dan segelas bir atau teh boba, lalu berteriaklah 'Base hit! Base hit! Home run!' bersama orang-orang di sekitar Anda. Anda akan menemukan bahwa salah satu cara tercepat memahami suatu tempat adalah melangkah masuk ke stadion yang paling dicintai penduduknya.","baseball":"bisbol","national sport (lit. 'national ball')":"olahraga nasional (harfiah: 'bola nasional')","CPBL (Taiwan pro baseball league)":"CPBL (liga bisbol profesional Taiwan)","youth/Little League baseball":"bisbol remaja/Little League","cheer squad":"kelompok pendukung","cheerleaders":"penari sorak (cheerleader)","to cheer someone on; 'go!'":"menyemangati seseorang; 'ayo!'","home run":"home run","base hit":"base hit (pukulan aman)","pitcher":"pelempar (pitcher)","player based overseas":"pemain yang bermain di luar negeri","the Major Leagues (MLB)":"Major League (MLB)","At a Taiwanese ballpark, watch for the commanding presence of the 'cheer leader' who conducts the crowd, and the personal 'cheer songs' written for each player. There are similarities to Japanese pro baseball, but Taiwan leans more toward a show, with on-stage cheer teams dancing throughout the game. '加油 (jiāyóu),' meaning 'go/keep it up,' isn't just for baseball—it's an all-purpose word of encouragement you can offer a friend before an exam or a tired coworker. It's very handy to know in daily life.":"Di stadion bisbol Taiwan, perhatikan kehadiran berwibawa sang 'pemandu sorak' yang mengomando kerumunan, dan 'lagu sorak' personal yang ditulis untuk tiap pemain. Ada kemiripan dengan bisbol profesional Jepang, tetapi Taiwan lebih condong ke pertunjukan, dengan tim sorak menari di panggung sepanjang pertandingan. '加油 (jiāyóu),' yang berarti 'ayo/semangat terus,' bukan hanya untuk bisbol—itu kata penyemangat serbaguna yang bisa Anda ucapkan kepada teman sebelum ujian atau rekan kerja yang lelah. Sangat berguna diketahui dalam kehidupan sehari-hari.","KTV Culture: Singing Until Dawn":"Budaya KTV: Bernyanyi hingga Fajar","A soundproof private room, a thick book of songs, and a steady stream of food and drinks—KTV in Taiwan is far more than a place to sing karaoke. Birthday parties, comforting the heartbroken, long-awaited reunions—everyone gathers here to sing. Let's step into this distinctive social ritual, where friends sing the night away until dawn.":"Ruang privat kedap suara, buku daftar lagu yang tebal, dan makanan serta minuman yang mengalir tiada henti—KTV di Taiwan jauh lebih dari sekadar tempat berkaraoke. Pesta ulang tahun, menghibur yang patah hati, reuni yang lama dinanti—semua orang berkumpul di sini untuk bernyanyi. Mari kita masuki ritual sosial khas ini, tempat teman-teman bernyanyi semalaman hingga fajar.","In Taiwan, KTV is a keyword that has surely shown up in nearly everyone's life. It's basically karaoke plus a TV screen, but Taiwan's KTV is a bit different from what many people picture. It's not a bar stage where one person sings in front of everyone; instead there are rows of 'private rooms'—self-contained spaces with a door, sofas, and a big screen. Once you and your friends close the door, the space is entirely yours: sing however you like, and it doesn't matter how badly you sing.":"Di Taiwan, KTV adalah kata kunci yang pasti pernah muncul dalam hidup hampir semua orang. Pada dasarnya itu karaoke plus layar TV, tetapi KTV Taiwan sedikit berbeda dari yang dibayangkan banyak orang. Ini bukan panggung bar tempat satu orang bernyanyi di depan semua orang; melainkan deretan 'ruang privat'—ruang tertutup berpintu, bersofa, dan berlayar besar. Begitu Anda dan teman-teman menutup pintu, ruang itu sepenuhnya milik Anda: bernyanyilah sesuka hati, dan tak masalah sejelek apa pun suara Anda.","Taiwan's most famous KTV chains are Cashbox and Holiday KTV. Step inside and the décor is often grand and bright; the front desk assigns you a room, and a staff member leads you down a long corridor lined with rooms leaking song after song. Inside your room there's a touchscreen or tablet for picking songs—just type a title or artist and you can queue up the songs you want, one by one, into the play list. Mandarin songs, English songs, Japanese songs, Korean songs, even old Taiwanese-language classics—you can find almost anything.":"Jaringan KTV paling terkenal di Taiwan adalah Cashbox dan Holiday KTV. Begitu masuk, dekorasinya sering megah dan terang; resepsionis menugaskan ruangan untuk Anda, dan seorang staf memandu Anda menyusuri koridor panjang yang diapit ruang-ruang yang membocorkan lagu demi lagu. Di dalam ruangan ada layar sentuh atau tablet untuk memilih lagu—cukup ketik judul atau nama penyanyi, dan Anda bisa mengantrekan lagu-lagu yang diinginkan satu per satu ke daftar putar. Lagu Mandarin, lagu Inggris, lagu Jepang, lagu Korea, bahkan lagu klasik berbahasa Taiwan lawas—hampir semuanya bisa ditemukan.","KTV is so popular in Taiwan because it isn't just about singing—it's a way of gathering. Want to celebrate a birthday? Invite everyone to KTV. A friend is back from abroad? KTV. Coworkers unwinding after work, a club event, even a couple's date—KTV is a likely pick. Inside the room, someone hogs the mic, someone handles the song queue, someone busily films and photographs everyone, and someone sprawls on the sofa eating and chatting. Whether you sing well doesn't really matter; what matters is that everyone is 'together.'":"KTV begitu populer di Taiwan karena bukan sekadar bernyanyi—melainkan cara berkumpul. Ingin merayakan ulang tahun? Ajak semua ke KTV. Teman baru pulang dari luar negeri? KTV. Rekan kerja bersantai seusai kerja, acara klub, bahkan kencan pasangan—KTV kemungkinan besar jadi pilihan. Di dalam ruangan, ada yang memonopoli mikrofon, ada yang mengurus antrean lagu, ada yang sibuk merekam dan memotret semua orang, dan ada yang berbaring di sofa sambil makan dan mengobrol. Pandai bernyanyi atau tidak sebenarnya tak begitu penting; yang penting semua orang 'bersama-sama.'","Taiwan's KTV has another thing that surprises foreigners: the food. Beyond drinks, there's a full menu—fried snacks, hot pot, pasta, fruit platters, desserts, you name it. For many, going to KTV is really 'singing plus dining,' and once they settle in, they stay for hours. Some even joke that the part people take most seriously at KTV is ordering food. Singing, eating, and chatting together, a group often finds the hours slipping by in a flash.":"KTV Taiwan punya satu hal lagi yang mengejutkan orang asing: makanannya. Selain minuman, ada menu lengkap—camilan gorengan, hot pot, pasta, piring buah, pencuci mulut, apa saja ada. Bagi banyak orang, pergi ke KTV sebenarnya 'menyanyi sekaligus makan,' dan begitu duduk nyaman, mereka betah berjam-jam. Sebagian bahkan berseloroh bahwa bagian yang paling serius digarap orang di KTV adalah memesan makanan. Menyanyi, makan, dan mengobrol bersama, satu rombongan sering merasa waktu berlalu secepat kilat.","If one round isn't enough, Taiwanese often 'move on to the next spot' (xùtān)—after one activity ends, they switch venues and keep the fun going. Dinner followed by KTV is a classic route. And if the singing gets too fun, they might sing straight through midnight or even until dawn—that's called an 'all-night sing' (yèchàng). All-night sessions are usually cheaper; a group sings from 11 p.m. until the next morning, and when they step out of KTV, it's already light. Everyone's eyes are bloodshot and their voices hoarse, yet they're grinning ear to ear.":"Jika satu putaran belum cukup, orang Taiwan sering 'lanjut ke tempat berikutnya' (xùtān)—setelah satu kegiatan usai, mereka pindah tempat dan meneruskan keseruan. Makan malam lalu KTV adalah rute klasik. Dan kalau nyanyinya keterlaluan serunya, mereka bisa bernyanyi menembus tengah malam bahkan sampai fajar—itu disebut 'nyanyi semalaman' (yèchàng). Sesi semalaman biasanya lebih murah; satu rombongan bernyanyi dari pukul 11 malam sampai pagi berikutnya, dan saat keluar dari KTV, hari sudah terang. Mata semua orang merah dan suara serak, tapi cengiran tak lepas dari wajah.","For foreigners, KTV is a great chance to blend quickly into a Taiwanese friend group. You don't need to sing well—pick a song you know, bravely grab the mic, and everyone will clap and cheer you on with all their might. You'll also find that singing together shrinks the distance of language and culture remarkably fast. Next time a Taiwanese friend asks, 'Want to go sing?' don't shyly refuse right away—it may well be their invitation to treat you as one of their own.":"Bagi orang asing, KTV adalah kesempatan bagus untuk cepat membaur ke dalam kelompok teman Taiwan. Anda tak perlu pandai bernyanyi—pilih lagu yang Anda tahu, beranikan diri meraih mikrofon, dan semua orang akan bertepuk serta menyemangati Anda sekuat tenaga. Anda juga akan mendapati bahwa bernyanyi bersama memangkas jarak bahasa dan budaya dengan sangat cepat. Lain kali saat teman Taiwan bertanya, 'Mau ikut nyanyi?' jangan buru-buru menolak dengan malu—bisa jadi itu undangan mereka untuk menganggap Anda bagian dari keluarga.","private room (at a KTV, etc.)":"ruang privat (di KTV, dll.)","to queue up / request a song":"mengantrekan / memesan lagu","microphone":"mikrofon","to move on to the next venue":"lanjut ke tempat berikutnya","to sing all night":"bernyanyi semalaman","gathering, get-together":"kumpul-kumpul, pertemuan","waiter, service staff":"pelayan, staf layanan","hoarse (voice)":"serak (suara)","to relax, unwind":"bersantai, melepas penat","one of us, insider":"orang kita sendiri, bagian dari kelompok","to enjoy to the fullest":"menikmati sepuas-puasnya","KTV prices in Taiwan vary a lot by time slot. Weekday afternoons are surprisingly cheap, while Friday and Saturday nights or the eve of a holiday tend to be pricey. Students often hunt for the 'happy-singing time slot' package deals (all-you-can-sing plus a drink bar or buffet). As etiquette, cutting off someone else's song midway without asking is frowned upon, so be careful. Incidentally, small solo karaoke booths have been growing in recent years, and some people enjoy 'KTV for one.'":"Harga KTV di Taiwan sangat berbeda menurut slot waktu. Siang di hari kerja mengejutkan murahnya, sementara malam Jumat dan Sabtu atau malam menjelang hari libur cenderung mahal. Pelajar sering memburu paket 'slot waktu nyanyi hemat' (nyanyi sepuasnya plus bar minuman atau buffet). Sebagai etiket, memotong lagu orang lain di tengah tanpa izin dianggap tidak sopan, jadi berhati-hatilah. Omong-omong, bilik karaoke kecil untuk solo belakangan makin bertambah, dan sebagian orang menikmati 'KTV sendirian.'","Taiwanese Dramas & Pop Culture: From Idol Dramas to the Golden Melody Awards":"Drama Taiwan & Budaya Populer: Dari Drama Idola hingga Golden Melody Awards","Bittersweet idol dramas, buzz-worthy shows that cut into society's pain, Mandarin pop drifting through the streets, and internet slang that spreads overnight on social media—Taiwan's pop culture reaches remarkably far from such a small island. Let's trace how Taiwan's 'soft power' travels out into the world.":"Drama idola yang manis-getir, tayangan viral yang menyentuh luka masyarakat, musik pop Mandarin yang mengalun di jalanan, dan bahasa gaul internet yang menyebar dalam semalam di media sosial—budaya populer Taiwan menjangkau amat jauh dari pulau sekecil itu. Mari kita telusuri bagaimana 'kekuatan lembut' Taiwan merambah ke dunia.","For many Asian viewers, their first impression of Taiwan actually comes from 'idol dramas.' In the early 2000s, 'Meteor Garden,' adapted from a Japanese manga, became a smash hit across Asia and pushed Taiwan's idol dramas to their peak. Dramas of that era typically starred a dashing boy and a hardworking girl; the stories were sweet, brimming with youth, paired with catchy theme songs that glued countless viewers to their TVs—and launched wave after wave of idol stars.":"Bagi banyak penonton Asia, kesan pertama mereka tentang Taiwan sebenarnya datang dari 'drama idola.' Pada awal 2000-an, 'Meteor Garden,' yang diadaptasi dari manga Jepang, menjadi hit besar di seluruh Asia dan mendorong drama idola Taiwan ke puncaknya. Drama era itu umumnya dibintangi seorang pemuda tampan dan gadis pekerja keras; ceritanya manis, penuh nuansa remaja, dipadu lagu tema yang catchy hingga membuat penonton tak lepas dari layar TV—dan melahirkan gelombang demi gelombang bintang idola.","But Taiwanese drama didn't stay with sweet idol romances. Over the past decade or so, its shows have grown bolder and increasingly willing to confront real social issues. Series like 'The World Between Us,' which examines the death penalty and the media, works about school bullying and academic pressure, plus all kinds of suspense, crime, family, and LGBT-themed shows, have been hotly discussed on streaming platforms. This new generation of Taiwanese drama no longer just talks about romance; it earnestly asks: what is really happening in the society we live in?":"Namun drama Taiwan tak berhenti pada kisah cinta idola yang manis. Selama sekitar satu dekade terakhir, tayangannya makin berani dan kian mau menghadapi isu sosial nyata. Serial seperti 'The World Between Us,' yang mengupas hukuman mati dan media, karya tentang perundungan sekolah dan tekanan akademik, ditambah beragam tayangan bergenre misteri, kriminal, keluarga, dan LGBT, ramai diperbincangkan di platform streaming. Generasi baru drama Taiwan ini tak lagi sekadar bicara soal asmara; ia dengan sungguh-sungguh bertanya: apa yang sebenarnya terjadi di masyarakat tempat kita hidup?","In music, Taiwan has long been a key base for 'Mandarin pop.' Many singers and works that swept the Mandarin-speaking world got their start in Taiwan. The most anticipated music event each year is the Golden Melody Awards, dubbed the crowning honors of the Mandarin music scene. It's rather like the major prize of Mandarin music, and the moment the winners are announced, it's usually what everyone is talking about the next day. From pop, rock, and hip-hop to works in Indigenous languages, Taiwanese, and Hakka, all can be seen on this stage.":"Dalam musik, Taiwan sejak lama menjadi basis penting 'pop Mandarin.' Banyak penyanyi dan karya yang menggemparkan dunia berbahasa Mandarin memulai kariernya di Taiwan. Ajang musik yang paling dinanti setiap tahun adalah Golden Melody Awards, yang dijuluki penghormatan tertinggi dunia musik Mandarin. Ia mirip penghargaan puncak musik Mandarin, dan begitu pemenangnya diumumkan, biasanya itulah yang diperbincangkan semua orang keesokan harinya. Dari pop, rock, dan hip-hop hingga karya dalam bahasa pribumi, bahasa Taiwan, dan bahasa Hakka, semua bisa tampil di panggung ini.","Beyond drama and music, Taiwan's pop culture also thrives online. The social platforms young people love, memes (funny images captioned with text), and all sorts of 'internet slang' are part of Taiwanese culture too. Take '五味雜陳' (a jumble of mixed feelings) to describe a complicated mood, or the common online phrases '已讀不回' (seeing a message but not replying) and '+1' (meaning 'me too / I agree')—such expressions keep spawning new trends over time and spread among friends in a flash.":"Selain drama dan musik, budaya populer Taiwan juga berkembang pesat secara daring. Platform sosial yang digemari anak muda, meme (gambar lucu berteks), dan berbagai 'bahasa gaul internet' juga bagian dari budaya Taiwan. Ambil contoh '五味雜陳' (campur aduk lima rasa, menggambarkan perasaan yang rumit), atau frasa daring yang lazim '已讀不回' (membaca pesan tapi tak membalas) dan '+1' (berarti 'aku juga / aku setuju')—ungkapan semacam ini terus melahirkan tren baru dari waktu ke waktu dan menyebar di antara teman dalam sekejap.","These seemingly light forms of entertainment actually accumulate into Taiwan's 'soft power.' A well-made Taiwanese drama might spark foreign viewers' interest in Taiwan's cities, street food, and way of life; a moving song might make someone want to learn Chinese; a viral meme might help more people discover Taiwanese people's humorous, straightforward, and somewhat warm-hearted character. The power of culture often works this way—not through preaching, but through one small surprise after another of 'oh, so this is what Taiwan is like.'":"Bentuk-bentuk hiburan yang tampak ringan ini sebenarnya terakumulasi menjadi 'kekuatan lembut' Taiwan. Sebuah drama Taiwan yang bagus bisa memantik minat penonton asing pada kota, jajanan, dan gaya hidup Taiwan; sebuah lagu yang mengharukan bisa membuat seseorang ingin belajar bahasa Mandarin; sebuah meme viral bisa membantu lebih banyak orang mengenal watak orang Taiwan yang humoris, blak-blakan, dan agak hangat. Kekuatan budaya sering bekerja seperti ini—bukan lewat khotbah, melainkan lewat satu demi satu kejutan kecil 'oh, ternyata begini Taiwan itu.'","If you're learning Chinese, Taiwan's pop culture is actually excellent study material. Follow a Taiwanese drama and you'll pick up natural colloquial speech and tone; listen to Mandarin pop and you'll remember practical sentences and ways to express emotion; understand the memes and slang your friends send you and you'll truly laugh at the same punchlines. Culture and language were never two separate things—once you start enjoying Taiwan's entertainment, your Chinese will, without your realizing it, come to sound more like 'the Chinese Taiwanese people actually speak.'":"Jika Anda sedang belajar bahasa Mandarin, budaya populer Taiwan sebenarnya bahan belajar yang sangat baik. Ikuti sebuah drama Taiwan dan Anda akan menyerap tutur kata dan intonasi kolokial yang alami; dengarkan pop Mandarin dan Anda akan mengingat kalimat praktis serta cara mengungkapkan emosi; pahami meme dan bahasa gaul yang dikirim teman-teman dan Anda akan benar-benar tertawa pada lelucon yang sama. Budaya dan bahasa tak pernah menjadi dua hal terpisah—begitu Anda mulai menikmati hiburan Taiwan, bahasa Mandarin Anda, tanpa Anda sadari, akan terdengar makin mirip 'bahasa Mandarin yang benar-benar dituturkan orang Taiwan.'","idol drama":"drama idola","Taiwanese drama":"drama Taiwan","Golden Melody Awards":"Golden Melody Awards","pop music":"musik pop","Mandarin/Chinese (Sinophone)":"bahasa Mandarin/Tionghoa (Sinofon)","meme":"meme","buzzword, slang":"kata populer, bahasa gaul","read but no reply (leave on 'read')":"sudah dibaca tapi tak dibalas (dibiarkan 'read')","soft power":"kekuatan lembut (soft power)","theme song":"lagu tema","issue, topic (of debate)":"isu, topik (perdebatan)","streaming":"streaming","It helps to note the term '華語 (Huáyǔ).' In Taiwan, standard Chinese may be called '中文,' '國語,' or '華語' depending on context. The Golden Melody Awards are for music, but Taiwan also has the Golden Horse Awards for film and the Golden Bell Awards for television—together the three are called the 'Three Golds.' Internet slang changes fast, so learning it while checking with Taiwanese friends—'Is this still used?'—will help you avoid the mistake of using outdated phrases.":"Ada baiknya mencatat istilah '華語 (Huáyǔ).' Di Taiwan, bahasa Mandarin baku bisa disebut '中文,' '國語,' atau '華語' tergantung konteks. Golden Melody Awards untuk musik, tetapi Taiwan juga punya Golden Horse Awards untuk film dan Golden Bell Awards untuk televisi—ketiganya bersama-sama disebut 'Tiga Emas.' Bahasa gaul internet berubah cepat, jadi mempelajarinya sambil mengecek dengan teman Taiwan—'Ini masih dipakai tidak?'—akan membantu Anda menghindari kesalahan memakai ungkapan yang sudah usang.","A is B":"A adalah B","A + 是 + B":"A + 是 + B","\"是\" links two nouns: A is B. Negative: 不是.":"\"是\" menghubungkan dua kata benda: A adalah B. Bentuk negatif: 不是.","He is not a student.":"Dia bukan seorang pelajar.","Is it ~?":"Apakah ~?","sentence + 嗎？":"kalimat + 嗎？","Add 嗎 to the end of a statement to make a yes/no question. Word order stays the same.":"Tambahkan 嗎 di akhir kalimat pernyataan untuk membuat pertanyaan ya/tidak. Urutan kata tetap sama.","Are you Taiwanese?":"Apakah kamu orang Taiwan?","Is this tasty?":"Apakah ini enak?","negation":"negasi (penyangkalan)","不 + verb/adjective":"不 + kata kerja/kata sifat","Put 不 before a verb/adjective to negate it. 不 becomes bú before a 4th tone. Exception: 有 → 沒有.":"Letakkan 不 sebelum kata kerja/kata sifat untuk menyangkalnya. 不 dibaca bú sebelum nada keempat. Pengecualian: 有 → 沒有.","I don't drink alcohol.":"Saya tidak minum alkohol.","It's not hot today.":"Hari ini tidak panas.","~'s / of":"milik ~ / dari ~","noun A + 的 + noun B":"kata benda A + 的 + kata benda B","的 marks possession, like English 's. Often dropped for close relationships (我媽媽 = my mom).":"的 menandai kepemilikan, seperti 's dalam bahasa Inggris. Sering dihilangkan untuk hubungan dekat (我媽媽 = ibu saya).","This is my phone.":"Ini ponsel saya.","Taiwanese fruit is delicious.":"Buah Taiwan lezat.","adjectival predicate sentence":"kalimat berpredikat kata sifat","subject + 很 + adjective":"subjek + 很 + kata sifat","Adjectives don't need 是. Plain statements usually take 很 before the adjective; here 很 doesn't really mean \"very\".":"Kata sifat tidak memerlukan 是. Kalimat pernyataan biasa umumnya memakai 很 sebelum kata sifat; di sini 很 tidak benar-benar berarti \"sangat\".","Bubble tea is tasty.":"Teh boba enak.","He is busy.":"Dia sibuk.","there is / to have":"ada / memiliki","subject + 有/沒有 + noun":"subjek + 有/沒有 + kata benda","有 covers both possession and existence. Its negative is always 沒有, never 不有.":"有 mencakup kepemilikan sekaligus keberadaan. Bentuk negatifnya selalu 沒有, tidak pernah 不有.","I have two tickets.":"Saya punya dua tiket.","There's no convenience store nearby.":"Tidak ada minimarket di dekat sini.","to be at / at (a place)":"berada di / di (suatu tempat)","A + 在 + place / 在 + place + verb":"A + 在 + tempat / 在 + tempat + kata kerja","在 marks location: A 在 place (A is at place), or 在 place + verb (do something at place).":"在 menandai lokasi: A 在 tempat (A berada di tempat), atau 在 tempat + kata kerja (melakukan sesuatu di tempat).","Where is the station?":"Di mana stasiunnya?","I eat lunch at the office.":"Saya makan siang di kantor.","measure words: 個, 杯, 張…":"kata bantu bilangan: 個, 杯, 張…","number + measure word + noun":"angka + kata bantu bilangan + kata benda","Nouns need a measure word after the number: 一杯茶 (a cup of tea). When unsure, use 個. \"Two\" becomes 兩 before measure words.":"Kata benda memerlukan kata bantu bilangan setelah angka: 一杯茶 (secangkir teh). Jika ragu, gunakan 個. \"Dua\" menjadi 兩 sebelum kata bantu bilangan.","One coffee and two baozi.":"Satu kopi dan dua baozi.","I want to buy three tickets.":"Saya mau membeli tiga tiket.","what, who, where":"apa, siapa, di mana","Put the question word where the answer would go":"Letakkan kata tanya di posisi tempat jawabannya berada","Question words stay in the position of the answer. Don't move them and don't add 嗎.":"Kata tanya tetap berada di posisi jawaban. Jangan pindahkan dan jangan tambahkan 嗎.","What's your name?":"Siapa nama kamu?","And ~? / What about ~?":"Kalau ~? / Bagaimana dengan ~?","noun + 呢？":"kata benda + 呢？","呢 bounces the question back: 你呢? = \"And you?\"":"呢 melemparkan pertanyaan balik: 你呢? = \"Kalau kamu?\"","I'll have tea. And you?":"Saya mau teh. Kalau kamu?","Where's my phone?":"Di mana ponsel saya?","A-not-A question":"Pertanyaan bentuk A-tidak-A","verb/adjective + 不 + verb/adjective":"kata kerja/kata sifat + 不 + kata kerja/kata sifat","Repeat verb + 不 + verb: 要不要? = \"Do you want it or not?\" Very common in Taiwan.":"Ulangi kata kerja + 不 + kata kerja: 要不要? = \"Mau atau tidak?\" Sangat umum di Taiwan.","Do you want to add pearls?":"Mau tambah boba tidak?","Is this OK?":"Ini boleh tidak?","to want / be going to":"mau / akan","要 + noun/verb":"要 + kata benda/kata kerja","要 + noun = \"I'll take...\"; 要 + verb = \"going to\". To decline, say 不用 (no need), not 不要.":"要 + kata benda = \"Saya ambil...\"; 要 + kata kerja = \"akan\". Untuk menolak, katakan 不用 (tidak perlu), bukan 不要.","I'll take a large iced milk tea.":"Saya mau satu teh susu dingin ukuran besar.","I'm going to Taichung tomorrow.":"Besok saya akan pergi ke Taichung.","would like to":"ingin","想 + verb":"想 + kata kerja","想 + verb = \"would like to\". Softer and less definite than 要.":"想 + kata kerja = \"ingin\". Lebih halus dan kurang pasti dibanding 要.","I'd like to learn Taiwanese (Hokkien).":"Saya ingin belajar bahasa Taiwan (Hokkien).","What would you like to eat?":"Kamu ingin makan apa?","can (learned skill)":"bisa (keterampilan yang dipelajari)","會 + verb":"會 + kata kerja","會 = can (learned skill): languages, cooking, driving. Also marks future likelihood.":"會 = bisa (keterampilan yang dipelajari): bahasa, memasak, menyetir. Juga menandai kemungkinan di masa depan.","I speak Japanese and a little Chinese.":"Saya bisa bahasa Jepang dan sedikit bahasa Mandarin.","Will it rain tomorrow?":"Apakah besok akan hujan?","may / be allowed to":"boleh / diizinkan","可以 + verb":"可以 + kata kerja","可以 = may / be allowed to. 可以〜嗎? politely asks for permission.":"可以 = boleh / diizinkan. 可以〜嗎? menanyakan izin dengan sopan.","May I try it on?":"Boleh saya coba pakai?","You may take photos here.":"Kamu boleh mengambil foto di sini.","completion / change of state":"penyelesaian / perubahan keadaan","verb + 了 / sentence-final + 了":"kata kerja + 了 / akhir kalimat + 了","了 after a verb = completed action; at sentence end = change of state. It is NOT a past tense.":"了 setelah kata kerja = tindakan yang selesai; di akhir kalimat = perubahan keadaan. Ini BUKAN bentuk lampau.","I bought three boxes of pineapple cakes.":"Saya membeli tiga kotak kue nanas.","I'm full now.":"Saya sudah kenyang.","have done before":"pernah melakukan","verb + 過":"kata kerja + 過","Verb + 過 = have done before (experience). Negative: 沒 + verb + 過.":"Kata kerja + 過 = pernah melakukan (pengalaman). Bentuk negatif: 沒 + kata kerja + 過.","Have you been to Jiufen?":"Apakah kamu pernah ke Jiufen?","I've never eaten stinky tofu.":"Saya belum pernah makan tahu busuk.","with / and":"dengan / dan","A + 跟/和 + B":"A + 跟/和 + B","跟 / 和 = \"with; and\". In Taiwan 和 is read hàn (not hé). 跟 is more common in speech.":"跟 / 和 = \"dengan; dan\". Di Taiwan 和 dibaca hàn (bukan hé). 跟 lebih umum dalam percakapan.","I stroll the night market with friends.":"Saya jalan-jalan di pasar malam bersama teman.","I'd like pearls and nata de coco.":"Saya mau boba dan nata de coco.","please (do)":"silakan / tolong","請 + verb":"請 + kata kerja","請 + verb = polite request. 請給我〜 = \"Please give me...\".":"請 + kata kerja = permintaan sopan. 請給我〜 = \"Tolong berikan saya...\".","Please give me the menu.":"Tolong berikan saya menunya.","Please say it again.":"Tolong ucapkan sekali lagi.","in the middle of doing":"sedang melakukan","subject + 在 + verb":"subjek + 在 + kata kerja","在 before a verb marks an action in progress (= -ing). 正在 emphasizes \"right now\".":"在 sebelum kata kerja menandai tindakan yang sedang berlangsung (= -ing). 正在 menekankan \"sekarang juga\".","I'm studying Chinese.":"Saya sedang belajar bahasa Mandarin.","He's in a meeting right now.":"Dia sedang rapat sekarang.","A is more ~ than B":"A lebih ~ daripada B","A + 比 + B + adjective":"A + 比 + B + kata sifat","比 marks comparison: A is more ~ than B. Don't use 很; add 多了/一點 after the adjective for degree.":"比 menandai perbandingan: A lebih ~ daripada B. Jangan pakai 很; tambahkan 多了/一點 setelah kata sifat untuk menyatakan tingkatnya.","The HSR is much faster than the train.":"HSR jauh lebih cepat daripada kereta biasa.","Today is a bit hotter than yesterday.":"Hari ini sedikit lebih panas daripada kemarin.","complement of manner":"komplemen cara","verb + 得 + adjective":"kata kerja + 得 + kata sifat","Verb + 得 + adjective describes how an action is done: 說得很好 = speaks well.":"Kata kerja + 得 + kata sifat menggambarkan bagaimana suatu tindakan dilakukan: 說得很好 = berbicara dengan baik.","You speak Chinese very well!":"Kamu berbicara bahasa Mandarin dengan sangat baik!","He goes to sleep very late every day.":"Dia tidur sangat larut setiap hari.","because ~, so …":"karena ~, maka …","因為 + cause, 所以 + result":"因為 + sebab, 所以 + akibat","Links cause and effect. Unlike English, Chinese often uses BOTH 因為 and 所以 in one sentence.":"Menghubungkan sebab dan akibat. Berbeda dengan bahasa Inggris, bahasa Mandarin sering memakai KEDUA 因為 dan 所以 dalam satu kalimat.","Because it's raining, we're not going hiking.":"Karena hujan, kami tidak jadi mendaki gunung.","Because of the typhoon, today is a day off.":"Karena topan, hari ini libur.","although ~, …":"meskipun ~, …","雖然 + A, 但是 + B":"雖然 + A, 但是 + B","\"Although A, B.\" Use both halves together. 但是 can be replaced by the more colloquial 可是.":"\"Meskipun A, B.\" Gunakan kedua bagian bersama-sama. 但是 bisa diganti dengan 可是 yang lebih santai.","The rent is expensive, but transport is convenient.":"Sewanya mahal, tapi transportasinya nyaman.","Tiring, but really fun.":"Melelahkan, tapi sangat menyenangkan.","while doing ~, …":"sambil melakukan ~, …","一邊 + V1, 一邊 + V2":"一邊 + V1, 一邊 + V2","Doing two actions at the same time: \"while doing A, do B.\" Colloquially shortened to 邊…邊….":"Melakukan dua tindakan sekaligus: \"sambil melakukan A, lakukan B.\" Dalam percakapan disingkat menjadi 邊…邊….","He likes watching videos while eating.":"Dia suka menonton video sambil makan.","We chatted while strolling the night market.":"Kami mengobrol sambil jalan-jalan di pasar malam.","more and more ~":"semakin ~","越來越 + adjective":"越來越 + kata sifat","越來越 + adjective = \"more and more ~\". Related: 越 A 越 B = \"the more A, the more B\".":"越來越 + kata sifat = \"semakin ~\". Terkait: 越 A 越 B = \"semakin A, semakin B\".","It's getting hotter and hotter.":"Cuaca semakin panas.","Your Chinese keeps getting better!":"Bahasa Mandarin kamu semakin bagus!","already ~ / only then ~":"sudah ~ / baru ~","time + 就 + V (early) / time + 才 + V (late)":"waktu + 就 + V (lebih awal) / waktu + 才 + V (terlambat)","就 = earlier/sooner than expected; 才 = later than expected. They color the speaker's feeling about timing.":"就 = lebih awal dari yang diharapkan; 才 = lebih lambat dari yang diharapkan. Keduanya menyiratkan perasaan pembicara tentang waktunya.","He was already up at six.":"Dia sudah bangun jam enam.","I didn't get to sleep until midnight.":"Saya baru bisa tidur tengah malam.","finish doing":"selesai melakukan","verb + 完 (+ 了)":"kata kerja + 完 (+ 了)","Verb + 完 = finish doing. Potential: 吃得完 (can finish) / 吃不完 (can't finish).":"Kata kerja + 完 = selesai melakukan. Bentuk potensial: 吃得完 (bisa menghabiskan) / 吃不完 (tidak bisa menghabiskan).","Have you finished your homework?":"Apakah kamu sudah selesai mengerjakan PR?","So much food—we can't finish it all!":"Makanannya banyak sekali—kita tidak akan bisa menghabiskannya!","to / for (someone)":"kepada / untuk (seseorang)","V + 給 + person / 給 + person + V":"V + 給 + orang / 給 + orang + V","給 introduces the receiver: 打電話給你 = call you; 給我看看 = show me.":"給 memperkenalkan penerima: 打電話給你 = menelepon kamu; 給我看看 = tunjukkan pada saya.","I'll call you tonight.":"Nanti malam saya akan menelepon kamu.","This is the pineapple cake I bought for you.":"Ini kue nanas yang saya belikan untuk kamu.","to be interested in ~":"tertarik pada ~","對 + noun + 有興趣":"對 + kata benda + 有興趣","對 X 有興趣 = interested in X. Negative: 沒興趣.":"對 X 有興趣 = tertarik pada X. Bentuk negatif: 沒興趣.","I'm very interested in Taiwanese history.":"Saya sangat tertarik pada sejarah Taiwan.","He has zero interest in cooking.":"Dia sama sekali tidak tertarik memasak.","it was ~ that… (emphasis)":"adalah ~ yang… (penekanan)","是 + emphasized part + V + 的":"是 + bagian yang ditekankan + V + 的","是…的 highlights when/where/how a past event happened: 我是坐高鐵來的 = It was by HSR that I came.":"是…的 menyoroti kapan/di mana/bagaimana suatu peristiwa lampau terjadi: 我是坐高鐵來的 = Saya datang dengan HSR.","When did you come to Taiwan?":"Kapan kamu datang ke Taiwan?","I made this cake myself.":"Kue ini saya buat sendiri.","about to ~":"akan segera ~","快(要) + V/adjective + 了":"快(要) + V/kata sifat + 了","快…了 = about to: 快到了 = almost there; 快下雨了 = it's about to rain.":"快…了 = akan segera: 快到了 = hampir sampai; 快下雨了 = sebentar lagi hujan.","We're almost at the station—get ready to get off.":"Kita hampir sampai stasiun—bersiaplah untuk turun.","Lunar New Year is coming—everyone's shopping for it.":"Tahun Baru Imlek akan tiba—semua orang berbelanja untuk perayaan.","a bit ~ (negative nuance)":"agak ~ (nuansa negatif)","有一點 + adjective":"有一點 + kata sifat","有一點 + adj = \"a bit (too) ~\" (negative nuance). Different from adj + 一點 = \"a little more ~\".":"有一點 + kata sifat = \"agak (terlalu) ~\" (nuansa negatif). Berbeda dengan kata sifat + 一點 = \"sedikit lebih ~\".","This piece of clothing is a bit pricey.":"Baju ini agak mahal.","I'm a bit tired today and want to head home early.":"Hari ini saya agak lelah dan ingin pulang lebih awal.","again":"lagi","再 + V (future) / 又 + V + 了 (past)":"再 + V (masa depan) / 又 + V + 了 (masa lampau)","Both mean \"again\": 再 for future repetition, 又 for past repetition (又遲到了 = late again).":"Keduanya berarti \"lagi\": 再 untuk pengulangan di masa depan, 又 untuk pengulangan di masa lampau (又遲到了 = telat lagi).","Come visit Taiwan again!":"Datanglah berkunjung ke Taiwan lagi!","He was late again today.":"Hari ini dia telat lagi.","don't ~":"jangan ~","別 + verb":"別 + kata kerja","別 + verb = don't (do something); colloquial form of 不要. 別擔心 = don't worry.":"別 + kata kerja = jangan (melakukan sesuatu); bentuk santai dari 不要. 別擔心 = jangan khawatir.","Don't worry—everything will be fine.":"Jangan khawatir—semuanya akan baik-baik saja.","Don't forget your umbrella—it's about to rain.":"Jangan lupa payungmu—sebentar lagi hujan.","every ~ (always) …":"setiap ~ (selalu) …","每 + time/noun + 都 + V":"每 + waktu/kata benda + 都 + V","每 (every) is almost always paired with 都: 每天都運動. Dropping 都 sounds unnatural.":"每 (setiap) hampir selalu dipasangkan dengan 都: 每天都運動. Menghilangkan 都 terdengar tidak alami.","I go hiking every single weekend.":"Setiap akhir pekan saya pergi mendaki.","Every drink shop has its own signature item.":"Setiap kedai minuman punya menu andalannya sendiri.","the 把 disposal construction":"konstruksi disposal 把","subject + 把 + object + verb + complement":"subjek + 把 + objek + kata kerja + komplemen","把 moves the object before the verb to stress what was done to it. The verb must carry a complement (完/掉/好…) or 了.":"把 memindahkan objek ke depan kata kerja untuk menekankan apa yang dilakukan padanya. Kata kerjanya harus disertai komplemen (完/掉/好…) atau 了.","Please turn off the AC.":"Tolong matikan ACnya.","I finished writing the report.":"Saya sudah selesai menulis laporannya.","the passive 被 construction":"konstruksi pasif 被","A + 被 (+ B) + verb + complement":"A + 被 (+ B) + kata kerja + komplemen","被 marks the passive. Often for unpleasant events, but neutral use is common now. The verb needs a complement.":"被 menandai bentuk pasif. Sering untuk kejadian yang tidak menyenangkan, tapi kini pemakaian netral juga umum. Kata kerjanya perlu komplemen.","My umbrella was taken by someone.":"Payung saya diambil orang.","He was sent to Tainan on business by his company.":"Dia ditugaskan perusahaannya untuk dinas ke Tainan.","even…":"bahkan…","連 + extreme example + 都/也 + verb":"連 + contoh ekstrem + 都/也 + kata kerja","連 X 都 = \"even X\". Cites an extreme example; must pair with 都 or 也.":"連 X 都 = \"bahkan X\". Menyebutkan contoh ekstrem; harus dipasangkan dengan 都 atau 也.","He's so busy he doesn't even have time to eat.":"Dia sangat sibuk sampai tidak punya waktu untuk makan.","Even Taiwanese people often write this character wrong.":"Bahkan orang Taiwan pun sering salah menulis karakter ini.","not only… but also…":"tidak hanya… tetapi juga…","不但 A, 而且 B":"不但 A, 而且 B","不但 A 而且 B = \"not only A but also B\". 而且 is often followed by 還/也.":"不但 A 而且 B = \"tidak hanya A tetapi juga B\". 而且 sering diikuti oleh 還/也.","This place is not only cheap but also delicious.":"Tempat ini tidak hanya murah tetapi juga enak.","He speaks not only Mandarin but also fluent Taiwanese.":"Dia tidak hanya bisa berbahasa Mandarin tetapi juga bahasa Taiwan dengan lancar.","yet, however (contrast)":"namun, tetapi (kontras)","subject + 卻 + verb":"subjek + 卻 + kata kerja","卻 = \"yet/however\", an adverb placed after the subject, never sentence-initial. Often combined with 但是.":"卻 = \"namun/tetapi\", kata keterangan yang diletakkan setelah subjek, tidak pernah di awal kalimat. Sering digabung dengan 但是.","I waited two hours, yet he didn't show up.":"Saya menunggu dua jam, tetapi dia tidak muncul.","This phone is expensive, yet it sells well.":"Ponsel ini mahal, namun tetap laris.","since it is the case that…":"karena memang…","既然 A, 就 B":"既然 A, 就 B","既然 = \"since (it's already the case)\", leading to a conclusion or suggestion with 就.":"既然 = \"karena (memang sudah begitu)\", mengarah ke kesimpulan atau saran dengan 就.","Since you're in Taiwan, you must check out a night market.":"Karena kamu sudah di Taiwan, kamu harus mampir ke pasar malam.","Since you're not feeling well, go home early and rest.":"Karena kamu tidak enak badan, pulanglah lebih awal dan istirahat.","as long as…":"asalkan…","只要 A, 就 B":"只要 A, 就 B","只要 A 就 B = \"as long as A, then B\" (sufficient condition). Contrast 只有…才… (necessary condition).":"只要 A 就 B = \"asalkan A, maka B\" (syarat cukup). Bandingkan dengan 只有…才… (syarat perlu).","As long as you practice daily, your Chinese will improve.":"Asalkan kamu berlatih setiap hari, bahasa Mandarinmu akan meningkat.","With just an EasyCard, the MRT and buses are all easy.":"Cukup dengan EasyCard, naik MRT dan bus jadi mudah.","besides / except for":"selain / kecuali","除了 A 以外, 還/也/都 …":"除了 A 以外, 還/也/都 …","除了 A 以外 + 還/也 = \"besides A, also…\"; + 都 = \"except for A, all…\". Two opposite readings!":"除了 A 以外 + 還/也 = \"selain A, juga…\"; + 都 = \"kecuali A, semuanya…\". Dua makna yang berlawanan!","Besides bubble tea, I'd also like winter melon tea.":"Selain teh boba, saya juga mau teh labu putih.","Everyone has arrived except Kobayashi.":"Semua orang sudah datang kecuali Kobayashi.","to make / let someone do":"membuat / membiarkan seseorang melakukan","A + 讓/使 + B + verb":"A + 讓/使 + B + kata kerja","讓/使 = to make/let someone do something. 讓 is colloquial (also \"let me…\"), 使 is written style.":"讓/使 = membuat/membiarkan seseorang melakukan sesuatu. 讓 bersifat percakapan (juga \"biar saya…\"), 使 bersifat tulisan.","This news made everyone happy.":"Berita ini membuat semua orang senang.","Let me think it over before I reply.":"Biar saya pikirkan dulu sebelum menjawab.","when you try V-ing / start V-ing":"ketika mencoba V / mulai V","verb + 起來":"kata kerja + 起來","V起來: ① \"when you V it…\" (看起來 = looks…), ② start V-ing, ③ gather/put away.":"V起來: ① \"ketika kamu V…\" (看起來 = terlihat…), ② mulai V, ③ mengumpulkan/membereskan.","This dish looks spicy but tastes fine.":"Masakan ini terlihat pedas tapi rasanya biasa saja.","Hearing the joke, everyone burst out laughing.":"Mendengar leluconnya, semua orang tertawa terbahak-bahak.","keep on V-ing":"terus melakukan V","verb + 下去":"kata kerja + 下去","V下去 = keep on V-ing (continuing something already begun): 說下去 = go on speaking.":"V下去 = terus melakukan V (melanjutkan sesuatu yang sudah dimulai): 說下去 = terus berbicara.","Don't stop—keep talking.":"Jangan berhenti, teruslah bicara.","With rent this high, I can barely keep living here.":"Dengan sewa setinggi ini, aku hampir tidak bisa terus tinggal di sini.","don't tell me… (rhetorical)":"masa iya… (retoris)","難道 + sentence + 嗎?":"難道 + kalimat + 嗎?","難道 forms a rhetorical question: \"don't tell me…?\" Usually ends with 嗎.":"難道 membentuk pertanyaan retoris: \"masa iya…?\" Biasanya diakhiri dengan 嗎.","Don't tell me you forgot our promise?":"Masa iya kamu lupa janji kita?","Such an easy question—surely he can do it?":"Soal semudah ini, masa iya dia tidak bisa mengerjakannya?","on earth / after all":"sebenarnya / pada akhirnya","到底 + question":"到底 + pertanyaan","到底 intensifies questions: \"on earth / after all\". Not used together with 嗎.":"到底 memperkuat pertanyaan: \"sebenarnya / pada akhirnya\". Tidak dipakai bersama 嗎.","Are you going or not, after all?":"Sebenarnya kamu jadi pergi atau tidak?","What on earth happened here?":"Sebenarnya apa yang terjadi di sini?","A, 甚至 B":"A, 甚至 B","甚至 = \"even; so much so that\", introducing an extreme case. Often 甚至連…都….":"甚至 = \"bahkan; sampai-sampai\", memperkenalkan kasus ekstrem. Sering 甚至連…都….","He works late every day—he doesn't even rest on weekends.":"Setiap hari dia bekerja sampai larut, bahkan akhir pekan pun tidak istirahat.","This movie is so popular even my mom knows it.":"Film ini sangat populer sampai-sampai ibuku pun tahu.","for… / as far as… is concerned":"bagi… / dari sudut pandang…","對 + person + 來說":"對 + orang + 來說","對 X 來說 = \"for X / from X's standpoint\". A very handy opener for opinions.":"對 X 來說 = \"bagi X / dari sudut pandang X\". Pembuka yang sangat praktis untuk menyampaikan pendapat.","For me, pronunciation is the hardest part.":"Bagiku, pelafalan adalah bagian yang paling sulit.","For Taiwanese people, typhoon days off are quite normal.":"Bagi orang Taiwan, libur karena topan adalah hal yang cukup biasa.","as soon as…":"begitu…","一 + verb 1, 就 + verb 2":"一 + kata kerja 1, 就 + kata kerja 2","一 A 就 B = \"as soon as A, B\". Works for both habits and single events.":"一 A 就 B = \"begitu A, langsung B\". Berlaku baik untuk kebiasaan maupun kejadian tunggal.","I pick up my kid right after work.":"Begitu selesai kerja, aku langsung menjemput anakku.","As soon as summer comes, he craves mango shaved ice.":"Begitu musim panas tiba, dia langsung ingin es serut mangga.","the reason … is because …":"alasan … adalah karena …","A 之所以 X, 是因為 Y":"A 之所以 X, 是因為 Y","A formal pattern that states the result first and then explains the reason: 'The reason A does X is because Y.' It puts emphasis on the cause.":"Pola formal yang menyatakan hasil terlebih dahulu lalu menjelaskan alasannya: 'Alasan A melakukan X adalah karena Y.' Pola ini menekankan penyebabnya.","He succeeded because he never gave up.":"Dia berhasil karena tidak pernah menyerah.","The reason this shop is so popular is that its service is exceptionally good.":"Alasan toko ini begitu populer adalah karena pelayanannya luar biasa bagus.","even if…":"meskipun…","即使 X, 也 Y":"即使 X, 也 Y","A concessive pattern meaning 'even if X, still Y.' It supposes an extreme or hypothetical situation and stresses that the conclusion remains unchanged.":"Pola konsesif yang berarti 'meskipun X, tetap Y.' Pola ini mengandaikan situasi ekstrem atau hipotetis dan menekankan bahwa kesimpulannya tidak berubah.","Even if it rains heavily, the event will still take place as scheduled.":"Meskipun hujan deras, acara tetap akan berlangsung sesuai jadwal.","Even if you fail, don't give up easily.":"Meskipun gagal, jangan mudah menyerah.","although / despite the fact that":"walaupun / terlepas dari kenyataan bahwa","儘管 X, (還是/仍然) Y":"儘管 X, (還是/仍然) Y","A concessive connector meaning 'although / despite the fact that X.' Unlike 即使 (hypothetical), 儘管 introduces a real, existing fact, often paired with 還是/仍然 in the second clause.":"Kata penghubung konsesif yang berarti 'walaupun / terlepas dari kenyataan bahwa X.' Berbeda dengan 即使 (hipotetis), 儘管 memperkenalkan fakta nyata yang ada, sering dipasangkan dengan 還是/仍然 di klausa kedua.","Despite being very busy with work, he still makes time to exercise every day.":"Walaupun sangat sibuk dengan pekerjaan, dia tetap menyempatkan diri berolahraga setiap hari.","Although the prices are not cheap, this restaurant is still full every day.":"Walaupun harganya tidak murah, restoran ini tetap penuh setiap hari.","all / any that…":"semua / apa pun yang…","凡是 X, 都 Y":"凡是 X, 都 Y","A formal pattern meaning 'all / any that fall under X.' It is almost always echoed by 都 and stresses that there are no exceptions. Common in rules and announcements.":"Pola formal yang berarti 'semua / apa pun yang termasuk X.' Hampir selalu diikuti oleh 都 dan menekankan bahwa tidak ada pengecualian. Umum dalam peraturan dan pengumuman.","Everyone who takes part in the event can receive a small gift.":"Semua orang yang ikut acara ini bisa mendapat hadiah kecil.","Anything he has decided rarely changes.":"Apa pun yang sudah dia putuskan jarang berubah.","as well as / and also":"serta / dan juga","A, B 以及 C / X, 並且 Y":"A, B 以及 C / X, 並且 Y","Two formal coordinators: 以及 links nouns ('and, as well as', placed before the last item), while 並且 links clauses ('and also, moreover'). They are the written counterparts of 和 and 而且.":"Dua kata penghubung koordinatif formal: 以及 menghubungkan kata benda ('dan, serta', diletakkan sebelum item terakhir), sedangkan 並且 menghubungkan klausa ('dan juga, lagi pula'). Keduanya adalah versi tulis dari 和 dan 而且.","The meeting discussed issues of budget, manpower, and scheduling.":"Rapat itu membahas masalah anggaran, tenaga kerja, serta jadwal.","The company adjusted its leave system and also raised employees' salaries.":"Perusahaan menyesuaikan sistem cutinya dan juga menaikkan gaji karyawan.","while / whereas (contrast)":"sedangkan / sementara (kontras)","A X, 而 B Y":"A X, 而 B Y","A written connector marking contrast between two clauses: 'while / whereas.' The two clauses often share a parallel structure that highlights the difference.":"Kata penghubung tulis yang menandai kontras antara dua klausa: 'sedangkan / sementara.' Kedua klausa sering memiliki struktur paralel yang menonjolkan perbedaannya.","The older brother likes outdoor sports, while the younger brother prefers reading at home.":"Sang kakak suka olahraga luar ruangan, sedangkan sang adik lebih suka membaca di rumah.","It rained all day in the north, whereas the south enjoyed clear skies.":"Di utara hujan sepanjang hari, sementara di selatan langitnya cerah.","owing to / due to (cause)":"karena / disebabkan oleh (penyebab)","由於 X, (因此/所以) Y":"由於 X, (因此/所以) Y","A formal causal connector: 'owing to / due to X.' More formal than 因為 and very common in news and notices, often paired with 因此/所以 in the main clause.":"Kata penghubung sebab yang formal: 'karena / disebabkan oleh X.' Lebih formal daripada 因為 dan sangat umum dalam berita serta pengumuman, sering dipasangkan dengan 因此/所以 di klausa utama.","Due to the approaching typhoon, work and classes are canceled citywide tomorrow.":"Karena topan yang mendekat, besok kerja dan sekolah diliburkan di seluruh kota.","Owing to constantly rising costs, the company decided to adjust its product prices.":"Karena biaya yang terus naik, perusahaan memutuskan untuk menyesuaikan harga produknya.","therefore / consequently":"oleh karena itu / akibatnya","X, 因此/因而 Y":"X, 因此/因而 Y","Formal result connectors: 'therefore / consequently.' More formal than 所以, suitable for reports and news; 因而 is even more literary and marks a natural consequence.":"Kata penghubung hasil yang formal: 'oleh karena itu / akibatnya.' Lebih formal daripada 所以, cocok untuk laporan dan berita; 因而 bahkan lebih bersifat sastra dan menandai konsekuensi yang wajar.","He was always well prepared; therefore he performed well in the interview.":"Dia selalu mempersiapkan diri dengan baik, oleh karena itu dia tampil bagus dalam wawancara.","This product's quality is consistent, and consequently it enjoys deep trust from consumers.":"Kualitas produk ini konsisten, akibatnya ia mendapat kepercayaan yang mendalam dari konsumen.","through / by means of":"melalui / dengan cara","藉由/透過 X, Y":"藉由/透過 X, Y","Means/method markers: 'through / by means of X.' 藉由 is more literary, while 透過 is very common in Taiwan even in speech. The clause that follows states what is achieved through that means.":"Penanda sarana/cara: 'melalui / dengan cara X.' 藉由 lebih bersifat sastra, sedangkan 透過 sangat umum di Taiwan bahkan dalam percakapan. Klausa yang mengikuti menyatakan apa yang dicapai melalui cara itu.","Through this collaboration, the two companies built a good relationship.":"Melalui kerja sama ini, kedua perusahaan membangun hubungan yang baik.","Through the internet, we can communicate with people all over the world.":"Melalui internet, kita bisa berkomunikasi dengan orang-orang di seluruh dunia.","along with / as … changes":"seiring dengan / ketika … berubah","隨著 X, Y":"隨著 X, Y","Means 'along with / as X changes, Y changes too.' 隨著 is typically followed by a noun phrase of change (development, increase), a staple of news writing, often echoed by 越來越 or 逐漸.":"Berarti 'seiring dengan / ketika X berubah, Y pun ikut berubah.' 隨著 biasanya diikuti frasa benda yang menyatakan perubahan (perkembangan, peningkatan), lazim dalam penulisan berita, sering diikuti 越來越 atau 逐漸.","As technology develops, our lives are becoming more and more convenient.":"Seiring berkembangnya teknologi, hidup kita menjadi semakin nyaman.","As he gets older, he pays more and more attention to his health.":"Seiring bertambahnya usia, dia semakin memperhatikan kesehatannya.","aimed at / targeting":"ditujukan untuk / menyasar","針對 X + verb":"針對 X + kata kerja","A preposition meaning 'aimed at / targeting X.' Used when taking measures or making statements directed at a specific issue or group; very common in business and news contexts.":"Preposisi yang berarti 'ditujukan untuk / menyasar X.' Digunakan saat mengambil langkah atau membuat pernyataan yang ditujukan pada isu atau kelompok tertentu; sangat umum dalam konteks bisnis dan berita.","The government launched a new housing policy targeting young people.":"Pemerintah meluncurkan kebijakan perumahan baru yang menyasar kaum muda.","We will adjust the plan according to the client's needs.":"Kami akan menyesuaikan rencana sesuai dengan kebutuhan klien.","and then go further to…":"lalu melangkah lebih jauh untuk…","X, 進而 Y":"X, 進而 Y","A written connector meaning 'and then go further to Y.' It marks progression: the first action becomes the basis for advancing to a further, deeper step.":"Kata penghubung tulis yang berarti 'lalu melangkah lebih jauh untuk Y.' Menandai kemajuan: tindakan pertama menjadi dasar untuk maju ke langkah yang lebih jauh dan lebih dalam.","He started from the bottom and went on to become a senior executive of the company.":"Dia memulai dari bawah lalu berkembang menjadi eksekutif senior perusahaan.","Only by first understanding the cause of a problem can we then go on to find a solution.":"Hanya dengan lebih dulu memahami penyebab masalah, kita baru bisa melangkah untuk menemukan solusinya.","on the contrary / instead":"sebaliknya / justru","(不但沒/不 X), 反而 Y":"(不但沒/不 X), 反而 Y","Means 'on the contrary / instead,' marking an outcome opposite to expectation. Often used in the pattern 不但沒 X，反而 Y ('not only did X not happen, on the contrary Y'). It carries a sense of surprise.":"Berarti 'sebaliknya / justru,' menandai hasil yang berlawanan dengan harapan. Sering dipakai dalam pola 不但沒 X，反而 Y ('bukan hanya X tidak terjadi, sebaliknya justru Y'). Mengandung nuansa keterkejutan.","After taking the medicine, his illness not only didn't improve but actually got worse.":"Setelah minum obat, penyakitnya bukannya membaik malah justru bertambah parah.","I apologized to him, but he got even angrier instead.":"Aku sudah minta maaf padanya, tapi dia justru semakin marah.","let alone / not to mention":"apalagi / jangankan","連 X 都…, (更)何況 Y":"連 X 都…, (更)何況 Y","A rhetorical pattern: 'even X is so, let alone Y.' Typically used as 連 X 都…，何況 Y, implying that Y goes without saying. 更何況 is a common variant.":"Pola retoris: 'bahkan X saja begitu, apalagi Y.' Biasanya dipakai sebagai 連 X 都…，何況 Y, mengisyaratkan bahwa Y sudah pasti demikian. 更何況 adalah variasi yang umum.","Even experts can't solve this problem, let alone us.":"Bahkan para ahli pun tidak bisa memecahkan masalah ini, apalagi kita.","Even adults can't move this box, let alone a child.":"Bahkan orang dewasa saja tidak bisa mengangkat kotak ini, apalagi seorang anak kecil.","rather too / a bit too…":"agak terlalu / sedikit terlalu…","X 未免太 Y 了":"X 未免太 Y 了","Expresses mild criticism: 'rather too / a bit too much.' The set pattern is 未免太…了, which sounds softer than a direct complaint. Do not confuse it with 難免 ('inevitably').":"Mengungkapkan kritik ringan: 'agak terlalu / sedikit berlebihan.' Pola bakunya adalah 未免太…了, yang terdengar lebih halus daripada keluhan langsung. Jangan disamakan dengan 難免 ('tak terhindarkan').","Three hundred dollars for a cup of coffee is really a bit too expensive.":"Tiga ratus dolar untuk secangkir kopi rasanya agak terlalu mahal.","Talking about him like that is rather going too far.":"Membicarakan dia seperti itu rasanya agak keterlaluan.","once … happens":"begitu … terjadi","一旦 X, 就 Y":"一旦 X, 就 Y","A conditional meaning 'once X happens, then Y (follows).' Often carries a warning tone about serious consequences, and is typically echoed by 就 in the main clause.":"Pola kondisional yang berarti 'begitu X terjadi, maka Y (menyusul).' Sering bernada peringatan tentang konsekuensi serius, dan biasanya diikuti 就 di klausa utama.","Once you have signed the contract, you can't cancel it at will.":"Begitu kamu menandatangani kontrak, kamu tidak bisa membatalkannya seenaknya.","Once the data is deleted, it cannot be recovered.":"Begitu data dihapus, ia tidak bisa dipulihkan lagi.","if (literary)":"jika (sastra)","倘若 + condition, (就/則) + result":"倘若 + syarat, (就/則) + hasil","Literary \"if\" (= 如果). Common in writing and formal speech; often paired with 就 or 則.":"\"Jika\" dalam ragam sastra (= 如果). Umum dalam tulisan dan ucapan formal; sering dipasangkan dengan 就 atau 則.","If the plan fails, we'll have to start over.":"Jika rencana ini gagal, kita harus memulai dari awal lagi.","Without everyone's support, we wouldn't have today's results.":"Tanpa dukungan semua orang, kita tidak akan meraih hasil seperti hari ini.","even if (literary)":"sekalipun (sastra)","縱使 + A, 也 + B":"縱使 + A, 也 + B","A more formal 即使: \"even if\". The second clause takes 也.":"Bentuk yang lebih formal dari 即使: \"sekalipun\". Klausa kedua memakai 也.","Even if difficulties abound, we will not give up.":"Sekalipun kesulitan menumpuk, kita tidak akan menyerah.","Even with only a sliver of hope, it's worth a try.":"Sekalipun hanya ada secercah harapan, itu layak dicoba.","for now; tentatively":"untuk sementara; buat sekarang","姑且 + V":"姑且 + V","姑且 = \"for the time being; tentatively\". 姑且不論 = \"setting aside… for now\".":"姑且 = \"untuk sementara waktu; buat sekarang\". 姑且不論 = \"mengesampingkan… dulu\".","Price aside, this design is truly excellent.":"Mengesampingkan harga, desain ini benar-benar luar biasa.","With no better option, let's handle it this way for now.":"Karena tidak ada pilihan yang lebih baik, untuk sementara kita tangani dengan cara ini saja.","might as well; why not try":"tak ada salahnya; kenapa tidak coba","不妨 + V":"不妨 + V","不妨 = \"might as well; why not try\". A gentle, no-pressure suggestion.":"不妨 = \"tak ada salahnya; kenapa tidak coba\". Saran yang lembut dan tanpa tekanan.","If you get the chance, why not visit Taitung?":"Kalau ada kesempatan, kenapa tidak coba berkunjung ke Taitung?","Rather than worrying, you might as well ask him directly.":"Daripada khawatir, tak ada salahnya kamu bertanya langsung padanya.","admittedly ..., but":"memang …, tetapi","A 固然 ~, 但/卻 ~":"A 固然 ~, 但/卻 ~","固然 concedes a point before countering: \"admittedly…, but…\". More argumentative than 雖然.":"固然 mengakui suatu poin sebelum membantahnya: \"memang…, tetapi…\". Lebih bernada argumentatif daripada 雖然.","Salary matters, of course, but a sense of accomplishment matters more.":"Gaji memang penting, tetapi rasa pencapaian lebih penting lagi.","This plan does save money, but the risks aren't small either.":"Rencana ini memang menghemat uang, tetapi risikonya juga tidak kecil.","in view of; given":"mengingat; berdasarkan","鑑於 + situation, + decision/suggestion":"鑑於 + situasi, + keputusan/saran","鑑於 = \"in view of; given\". Formal register for citing grounds before a decision.":"鑑於 = \"mengingat; berdasarkan\". Ragam formal untuk menyebutkan dasar sebelum mengambil keputusan.","In view of the approaching typhoon, work and classes are canceled tomorrow.":"Mengingat topan yang mendekat, besok kerja dan sekolah diliburkan.","Given user feedback, we adjusted the interface design.":"Mengingat masukan dari pengguna, kami menyesuaikan desain antarmukanya.","so as to avoid; lest":"agar terhindar dari; supaya tidak","..., 以免 + undesired result":"..., 以免 + hasil yang tidak diinginkan","以免 = \"so as to avoid; lest\". Placed in the second clause to state what the action prevents.":"以免 = \"agar terhindar dari; supaya tidak\". Diletakkan di klausa kedua untuk menyatakan apa yang dicegah oleh tindakan itu.","Check the weather before heading out, so you don't get caught in the rain.":"Periksa cuaca sebelum berangkat, supaya kamu tidak kehujanan.","Please back up important data to avoid losing it.":"Harap cadangkan data penting agar tidak hilang.","to the point that":"sampai-sampai","cause/degree, 以至於 + result":"penyebab/tingkat, 以至於 + hasil","以至於 = \"to the point that; so much so that\", introducing the resulting extent.":"以至於 = \"sampai-sampai; hingga\", memperkenalkan sejauh mana akibatnya.","He was so focused that he didn't hear anyone calling him.":"Dia begitu fokus sampai-sampai tidak mendengar ada yang memanggilnya.","The game was so popular that the servers crashed for a while.":"Gim ini begitu populer sampai-sampai servernya sempat crash.","and even; up to (literary)":"bahkan; hingga (sastra)","A, B 乃至 C":"A, B 乃至 C","乃至 = \"and even; up to\", extending a list to a broader scope. Formal.":"乃至 = \"bahkan; hingga\", memperluas suatu daftar ke cakupan yang lebih luas. Formal.","This technology affected industry, education, and even society as a whole.":"Teknologi ini memengaruhi industri, pendidikan, bahkan masyarakat secara keseluruhan.","His works are famous in Taiwan and indeed across Asia.":"Karya-karyanya terkenal di Taiwan, bahkan di seluruh Asia.","nothing but; merely":"tak lain hanyalah; semata-mata","A 無非(是) + B":"A 無非(是) + B","無非 = \"nothing but; simply\". Reduces something to its essence, often dismissively.":"無非 = \"tak lain hanyalah; semata-mata\". Menyederhanakan sesuatu ke intinya, sering dengan nada meremehkan.","All that talk of his is simply because he wants your help.":"Semua ucapannya itu tak lain hanyalah karena dia ingin bantuanmu.","However good the ad sounds, it's just trying to get your money.":"Sebagus apa pun iklannya terdengar, itu semata-mata ingin menguras uangmu.","nothing more than; confined to":"tak lebih dari; terbatas pada","A 不外乎 B, C, D":"A 不外乎 B, C, D","不外乎 = \"boils down to nothing more than…\", enumerating the limited possibilities.":"不外乎 = \"pada intinya tak lebih dari…\", menyebutkan kemungkinan-kemungkinan yang terbatas.","Taiwanese small talk boils down to food, weather, and housing prices.":"Obrolan ringan orang Taiwan tak lebih dari soal makanan, cuaca, dan harga rumah.","The causes of failure are nothing more than poor preparation or bad luck.":"Penyebab kegagalan tak lebih dari persiapan yang buruk atau nasib sial.","would rather ... than ...":"lebih baik … daripada …","寧可 A, 也不 B":"寧可 A, 也不 B","寧可 A 也不 B = \"would rather A than B\", choosing the lesser evil with resolve.":"寧可 A 也不 B = \"lebih baik A daripada B\", memilih yang lebih ringan mudaratnya dengan tegas.","I'd rather spend more than live too far away.":"Aku lebih baik mengeluarkan uang lebih daripada tinggal terlalu jauh.","He'd rather work overtime himself than dump work on others.":"Dia lebih baik lembur sendiri daripada melimpahkan pekerjaan kepada orang lain.","rather than ..., better to ...":"daripada …, lebih baik …","與其 A, 不如 B":"與其 A, 不如 B","與其 A 不如 B = \"rather than A, better to B\", recommending the latter.":"與其 A 不如 B = \"daripada A, lebih baik B\", menganjurkan pilihan yang kedua.","Rather than scrolling your phone at home, better to go out and exercise.":"Daripada main ponsel di rumah, lebih baik keluar dan berolahraga.","Rather than complaining about circumstances, change yourself first.":"Daripada mengeluhkan keadaan, lebih baik ubah dirimu terlebih dahulu.","absolutely must":"mutlak harus","非 + V + 不可":"非 + V + 不可","非 V 不可 = double negative for \"absolutely must\". Conveys strong determination or inevitability.":"非 V 不可 = negasi ganda yang berarti \"mutlak harus\". Menyampaikan tekad yang kuat atau keniscayaan.","This famous queue-worthy place—this time I absolutely must try it!":"Tempat terkenal yang layak diantre ini, kali ini aku mutlak harus mencobanya!","Things have reached the point where it simply must be resolved.":"Keadaan sudah sampai pada titik di mana ini mutlak harus diselesaikan.","inevitably will":"pasti akan","勢必 + V":"勢必 + V","勢必 = \"inevitably will\", an objective prediction from the momentum of events.":"勢必 = \"pasti akan\", prediksi objektif berdasarkan momentum dari jalannya peristiwa.","With raw materials rising, prices are bound to follow.":"Dengan naiknya harga bahan baku, harga pasti akan ikut naik.","The falling birthrate will inevitably affect the future workforce.":"Menurunnya angka kelahiran pasti akan memengaruhi tenaga kerja di masa depan.","unavoidable; bound to happen":"tak terhindarkan; pasti terjadi","免不了 + V/noun":"免不了 + V/kata benda","免不了 = \"can't avoid; bound to happen\", with a forgiving, that's-life tone.":"免不了 = \"tak bisa dihindari; pasti terjadi\", dengan nada memaklumi, seperti 'begitulah hidup'.","In a new environment, some discomfort is inevitable at first.":"Di lingkungan baru, sedikit rasa tidak nyaman di awal memang tak terhindarkan.","Living together as a family, small frictions are bound to happen.":"Hidup bersama sebagai keluarga, gesekan-gesekan kecil pasti terjadi.","Greetings & Introductions":"Sapaan & Perkenalan","Hello!":"Halo!","Good morning!":"Selamat pagi!","In Taiwan just \"早!\" also works.":"Di Taiwan cukup \"早!\" saja juga bisa.","My name is Yamada. I'm Japanese.":"Nama saya Yamada. Saya orang Jepang.","I'm learning Chinese. Please be patient with me.":"Saya sedang belajar bahasa Mandarin. Mohon bersabar dengan saya.","Have you eaten? (a common Taiwanese greeting)":"Sudah makan? (sapaan umum di Taiwan)","It's small talk, like \"How are you?\" — not literally about food.":"Ini basa-basi, seperti \"Apa kabar?\" — bukan benar-benar soal makanan.","Drink Stands & Night Markets":"Kedai Minuman & Pasar Malam","One bubble milk tea, please.":"Tolong satu teh susu boba.","Half sugar, less ice.":"Setengah gula, sedikit es.","Sugar: 正常→半→微→無; Ice: 正常→少→微→去. The two axes of every Taiwan drink order!":"Gula: 正常→半→微→無; Es: 正常→少→微→去. Dua sumbu dari setiap pesanan minuman di Taiwan!","Calling the vendor 老闆 (boss) is friendly and very local.":"Memanggil penjual dengan 老闆 (bos) terdengar akrab dan sangat lokal.","Can I eat in?":"Boleh makan di tempat?","內用 = eat in, 外帶 = take out. You'll be asked every time.":"內用 = makan di tempat, 外帶 = bawa pulang. Kamu akan ditanya setiap kali.","Take out, please.":"Bawa pulang, ya.","No cilantro, please.":"Tanpa daun ketumbar, ya.","Is it a bit spicy?":"Apakah ini agak pedas?","At a Restaurant":"Di Restoran","How many? — Two.":"Berapa orang? — Dua orang.","The menu, please.":"Tolong menunya.","I'd like to order.":"Saya mau pesan.","What's your signature dish?":"Apa menu andalan di sini?","Check, please!":"Minta bon, ya!","Night markets and small shops are often cash only.":"Pasar malam dan toko kecil sering kali hanya menerima uang tunai.","Hotels & Lodging":"Hotel & Penginapan","I have a reservation. Here's my passport.":"Saya sudah reservasi. Ini paspor saya.","What time is checkout?":"Jam berapa waktu check-out?","Can I leave my luggage here?":"Boleh menitipkan koper di sini?","Is breakfast included?":"Apakah sudah termasuk sarapan?","The AC seems to be broken.":"Sepertinya ACnya rusak.","What's the WiFi password?":"Apa password WiFinya?","Getting Around":"Berkeliling","I want to go to Taipei Main Station.":"Saya mau ke Stasiun Utama Taipei (Taipei Main Station).","How do I get to the MRT station?":"Bagaimana cara ke stasiun MRT?","Please tell me when we arrive.":"Tolong beri tahu saya kalau sudah sampai.","I'd like to top up 100 NTD (EasyCard).":"Saya mau isi ulang 100 NTD (EasyCard).","You can top up an EasyCard at any convenience store.":"Kamu bisa mengisi ulang EasyCard di minimarket mana saja.","Does this train go to Tamsui?":"Apakah kereta ini menuju Tamsui?","Shopping":"Belanja","I'm just looking.":"Saya cuma lihat-lihat.","Do you have other colors?":"Ada warna lain?","Can you give me a discount?":"Bisa dikasih diskon?","I'll take this one.":"Saya ambil yang ini.","Need a bag? — No thanks.":"Perlu kantong? — Tidak, terima kasih.","Plastic bags cost extra in Taiwan. 不用 is the soft way to decline.":"Di Taiwan kantong plastik dikenai biaya tambahan. 不用 adalah cara halus untuk menolak.","Renting & Landlords":"Menyewa & Pemilik Kos","Is this room still available for rent?":"Apakah kamar ini masih tersedia untuk disewa?","Does the rent include utilities?":"Apakah sewanya sudah termasuk listrik dan air?","Electricity is usually billed separately (電費另計). Watch out for summer AC bills!":"Listrik biasanya ditagih terpisah (電費另計). Hati-hati dengan tagihan AC di musim panas!","Is the deposit two months' rent?":"Apakah depositnya sebesar dua bulan sewa?","I'd like to schedule a viewing.":"Saya mau menjadwalkan untuk melihat kamar.","The water heater is broken—can you send someone to fix it?":"Pemanas airnya rusak—bisa kirim orang untuk memperbaikinya?","What time does the garbage truck come?":"Jam berapa truk sampah datang?","In Taiwan you bring your trash to the truck (the one playing Für Elise).":"Di Taiwan kamu membawa sampahmu sendiri ke truk (yang memutar lagu Für Elise).","Clinics & Pharmacies":"Klinik & Apotek","I'd like to register—first visit.":"Saya mau mendaftar—kunjungan pertama.","I have an NHI card.":"Saya punya kartu NHI (asuransi kesehatan).","Foreign residents can join Taiwan's NHI. Visits often cost just a few hundred NTD.":"Penduduk asing bisa ikut NHI Taiwan. Sekali berobat sering hanya beberapa ratus NTD.","I've had a fever since yesterday.":"Saya demam sejak kemarin.","I'm allergic to seafood.":"Saya alergi makanan laut.","Do I take this medicine after meals?":"Apakah obat ini diminum setelah makan?","Is there a pharmacy nearby?":"Apakah ada apotek di dekat sini?","Banking, Phones & Paperwork":"Bank, Ponsel & Dokumen","I'd like to open an account.":"Saya mau membuka rekening.","Bring your ARC, passport, and a personal seal — Taiwan still loves seals!":"Bawalah ARC, paspor, dan stempel pribadi — Taiwan masih suka pakai stempel!","I'd like to sign up for a mobile plan.":"Saya mau mendaftar paket seluler.","This is my ARC (residence permit).":"Ini ARC (izin tinggal) saya.","Which forms do I need to fill out?":"Formulir apa saja yang perlu saya isi?","Can you order delivery for me?":"Bisa pesankan makanan antar untuk saya?","foodpanda and Uber Eats dominate. 外送 = delivery.":"foodpanda dan Uber Eats mendominasi. 外送 = pesan antar.","At Work":"Di Tempat Kerja","Excuse me, I'd like to take a day off.":"Permisi, saya ingin mengambil cuti sehari.","Where are we on this project?":"Sudah sampai mana progres proyek ini?","I have a meeting this afternoon—I'll get back to you later.":"Sore ini saya ada rapat—nanti saya kabari lagi.","Thanks for your hard work!":"Terima kasih atas kerja kerasnya!","Works almost exactly like Japanese otsukaresama.":"Fungsinya hampir persis seperti \"otsukaresama\" dalam bahasa Jepang.","Sorry to trouble you—thanks!":"Maaf merepotkan—terima kasih ya!","I'm heading out—see you tomorrow!":"Saya pulang dulu—sampai jumpa besok!","Trouble & Emergencies":"Masalah & Keadaan Darurat","Excuse me, may I ask something?":"Permisi, boleh saya bertanya?","不好意思 is Taiwan's all-purpose softener — you'll hear it 10 times a day.":"不好意思 adalah kata pelembut serba guna khas Taiwan — kamu akan mendengarnya sepuluh kali sehari.","I don't understand.":"Saya tidak mengerti.","Please speak slowly.":"Tolong bicara pelan-pelan.","Can we use English?":"Boleh kita pakai bahasa Inggris?","My wallet is gone!":"Dompet saya hilang!","Please call the police.":"Tolong panggilkan polisi.","Emergency numbers: police 110, fire/ambulance 119 — same as Japan.":"Nomor darurat: polisi 110, pemadam/ambulans 119 — sama seperti di Jepang.","I'm lost—where am I?":"Saya tersesat—saya ada di mana ini?","No problem!":"Tidak masalah!","Convenience Stores":"Minimarket","I'd like to pay a bill here.":"Saya mau membayar tagihan di sini.","Taiwan convenience stores pay almost anything — utilities, parking, fines, even credit-card bills.":"Minimarket di Taiwan bisa membayar hampir apa saja — tagihan listrik/air, parkir, denda, bahkan tagihan kartu kredit.","I'm here to pick up a package—here's my phone number.":"Saya mau mengambil paket—ini nomor telepon saya.","Online orders often ship to a store — show a barcode or phone number to collect.":"Pesanan online sering dikirim ke toko — tunjukkan barcode atau nomor telepon untuk mengambilnya.","Could you heat this up for me?":"Bisa tolong hangatkan ini untuk saya?","One medium latte, hot, please.":"Tolong satu latte ukuran sedang, panas.","CITY CAFE (7-11) and Let's Café (FamilyMart) are the daily commuter coffee.":"CITY CAFE (7-11) dan Let's Café (FamilyMart) adalah kopi harian para pekerja komuter.","Can I make copies here?":"Boleh fotokopi di sini?","Kiosks like ibon (7-11) handle copies, printing, tickets and paperwork.":"Kios seperti ibon (7-11) melayani fotokopi, cetak, tiket, dan urusan dokumen.","No bag, thanks.":"Tidak pakai kantong, terima kasih.","Plastic bags cost extra; bringing your own is normal.":"Kantong plastik dikenai biaya; membawa kantong sendiri sudah biasa.","Weather, Typhoons & Earthquakes":"Cuaca, Topan & Gempa Bumi","Will it rain today? Don't forget an umbrella.":"Apakah hari ini akan hujan? Jangan lupa bawa payung.","I hear a typhoon is coming.":"Katanya topan akan datang.","When a typhoon nears, each city may declare work/school off. Check the news or the city's official page the night before.":"Saat topan mendekat, tiap kota bisa mengumumkan libur kerja/sekolah. Cek berita atau halaman resmi kota pada malam sebelumnya.","Is tomorrow a typhoon day off?":"Apakah besok libur karena topan?","Was that an earthquake just now?":"Tadi itu gempa, ya?","Earthquakes are common; phones blast a loud national alert before strong shaking.":"Gempa sering terjadi; ponsel akan membunyikan peringatan nasional yang keras sebelum guncangan kuat.","So hot today—everywhere indoors has the AC on.":"Panas sekali hari ini—di dalam ruangan semuanya menyalakan AC.","It's pouring outside—let's wait a bit before we go.":"Di luar hujan deras—kita tunggu sebentar sebelum pergi.","Temples & Festivals":"Kuil & Perayaan","Let's go pray at the temple.":"Ayo kita berdoa di kuil.","拜拜 means to worship — holding incense and praying for safety, part of everyday Taiwanese life.":"拜拜 berarti bersembahyang — memegang dupa dan berdoa memohon keselamatan, bagian dari keseharian orang Taiwan.","A small token—here's a red envelope for you.":"Sekadar tanda—ini ada angpau untukmu.","Red envelopes: avoid amounts with 4 (sounds like 'death'); pick even, lucky numbers.":"Angpau: hindari jumlah yang mengandung angka 4 (bunyinya mirip 'mati'); pilih angka genap yang membawa keberuntungan.","Want to barbecue together for Mid-Autumn Festival?":"Mau barbekyu bareng saat Festival Pertengahan Musim Gugur?","Taiwan's Mid-Autumn is uniquely spent grilling with family, eating mooncakes and pomelo.":"Pertengahan Musim Gugur di Taiwan unik karena dirayakan dengan memanggang bersama keluarga, makan kue bulan dan jeruk bali.","Happy New Year—may you prosper!":"Selamat Tahun Baru—semoga makmur dan sejahtera!","The classic Lunar New Year greeting; kids reply 紅包拿來 ('hand over the red envelope!').":"Ucapan khas Tahun Baru Imlek; anak-anak menjawab 紅包拿來 ('serahkan angpaunya!').","I'm going back to my hometown in the south for New Year.":"Saya akan pulang ke kampung halaman di selatan untuk merayakan Tahun Baru.","Breakfast at the Convenience Store":"Sarapan di Minimarket","At 7 a.m., Xiaoming walks into a convenience store.":"Pukul 7 pagi, Xiaoming masuk ke sebuah minimarket.","He wants to buy a rice ball and a cup of coffee.":"Dia mau membeli sebuah nasi kepal dan secangkir kopi.","\"Can you heat up this rice ball for me?\"":"\"Bisa tolong hangatkan nasi kepal ini untuk saya?\"","The clerk says: \"Sure, do you want a bag?\"":"Kasir berkata: \"Tentu, mau pakai kantong?\"","\"No thanks. I'll pay with my EasyCard.\"":"\"Tidak, terima kasih. Saya bayar pakai EasyCard.\"","With a \"beep,\" breakfast is bought, and Xiaoming hurries off to work.":"Dengan bunyi \"bip\", sarapan pun terbeli, dan Xiaoming buru-buru berangkat kerja.","rice ball":"nasi kepal","to heat up":"menghangatkan","clerk":"kasir / pelayan toko","How did Xiaoming pay?":"Bagaimana Xiaoming membayar?","With an EasyCard":"Dengan EasyCard","With cash":"Dengan uang tunai","With a credit card":"Dengan kartu kredit","\"我用悠遊卡付\" = pay with EasyCard. In Taiwan you can pay at convenience stores with your transit card.":"\"我用悠遊卡付\" = bayar pakai EasyCard. Di Taiwan kamu bisa membayar di minimarket dengan kartu transportasimu.","Dinner at the Night Market":"Makan Malam di Pasar Malam","In the evening, Aiko goes strolling through the night market with a friend.":"Pada malam hari, Aiko berjalan-jalan di pasar malam bersama seorang teman.","The night market is crowded and lively.":"Pasar malamnya ramai dan meriah.","\"Boss, how much is this fried chicken cutlet?\"":"\"Bos, berapa harga fillet ayam goreng ini?\"","\"Seventy dollars each. Want it spicy?\"":"\"Tujuh puluh dolar per potong. Mau yang pedas?\"","\"Just a little spicy, thanks.\"":"\"Sedikit pedas saja, terima kasih.\"","They also buy bubble tea and eat as they walk.":"Mereka juga membeli teh boba dan makan sambil berjalan.","lively, bustling":"ramai, meriah","fried chicken cutlet":"fillet ayam goreng","portion (measure word)":"porsi (kata bantu bilangan)","to add spice":"menambahkan pedas","to do A while doing B":"melakukan A sambil melakukan B","How did Aiko want her chicken cutlet?":"Aiko mau fillet ayamnya seperti apa?","A little spicy":"Sedikit pedas","Very spicy":"Sangat pedas","Not spicy":"Tidak pedas","\"要一點點辣\" = just a little spicy. \"一點點\" means \"just a tiny bit.\"":"\"要一點點辣\" = sedikit pedas saja. \"一點點\" berarti \"cuma sedikit sekali.\"","Asking for Directions on the MRT":"Menanyakan Arah di MRT","Jianhong wants to go to Taipei 101, but he doesn't know the way.":"Jianhong mau ke Taipei 101, tapi dia tidak tahu jalannya.","He asks the station staff: \"Excuse me, which line do I take to 101?\"":"Dia bertanya kepada petugas stasiun: \"Permisi, untuk ke 101 saya naik jalur yang mana?\"","\"Take the Red Line and get off at Taipei 101/World Trade Center station.\"":"\"Naik Jalur Merah dan turun di stasiun Taipei 101/World Trade Center.\"","\"Do I need to transfer?\" \"No, it's direct.\"":"\"Apakah saya perlu ganti kereta?\" \"Tidak, langsung sampai.\"","\"Great, thank you!\" Jianhong taps his card and enters the station.":"\"Bagus, terima kasih!\" Jianhong menempelkan kartunya lalu masuk ke stasiun.","station staff":"petugas stasiun","line (e.g. Red Line)":"jalur (misalnya Jalur Merah)","to get off":"turun (dari kendaraan)","to transfer (trains)":"berganti kereta / transit","direct (no transfer)":"langsung (tanpa transit)","to tap/swipe a card":"menempelkan/menggesek kartu","Does Jianhong need to transfer?":"Apakah Jianhong perlu berganti kereta?","No, it's direct":"Tidak, langsung sampai","Yes, once":"Ya, satu kali","Yes, twice":"Ya, dua kali","\"不用，直達\" = no need to transfer, it's direct.":"\"不用，直達\" = tidak perlu transit, langsung sampai.","Viewing an Apartment to Rent":"Melihat Apartemen untuk Disewa","Misaki wants to rent a studio near her office, so she searches for a place online.":"Misaki mau menyewa apartemen studio dekat kantornya, jadi dia mencari tempat secara online.","She finds a nice place and calls the landlord to arrange a viewing.":"Dia menemukan tempat yang bagus dan menelepon pemilik untuk mengatur jadwal melihat.","\"How much is the monthly rent? Are water and electricity included?\"":"\"Berapa sewa per bulannya? Apakah air dan listrik sudah termasuk?\"","The landlord says: \"12,000 a month. Water's included, but electricity is charged separately.\"":"Pemilik berkata: \"12.000 per bulan. Air sudah termasuk, tapi listrik ditagih terpisah.\"","Misaki takes a look and feels the room is clean and gets good light.":"Misaki melihat-lihat dan merasa kamarnya bersih serta pencahayaannya bagus.","Because it's close to the MRT station, only a five-minute walk, she decides to rent it.":"Karena dekat dengan stasiun MRT, hanya lima menit jalan kaki, dia memutuskan untuk menyewanya.","The landlord says: \"Then you'll first pay one month's deposit, plus the first month's rent.\"":"Pemilik berkata: \"Kalau begitu, kamu bayar dulu deposit satu bulan, ditambah sewa bulan pertama.\"","studio apartment (en-suite)":"apartemen studio (kamar mandi dalam)","water and electricity (utilities)":"air dan listrik (utilitas)","natural lighting":"pencahayaan alami","charged separately":"ditagih terpisah","How is the electricity bill handled for this room?":"Bagaimana tagihan listrik untuk kamar ini diperlakukan?","Charged separately from the rent":"Ditagih terpisah dari sewa","Included in the rent":"Sudah termasuk dalam sewa","Free":"Gratis","\"電費要另外算\" = electricity is charged separately. Water is included, but electricity is not.":"\"電費要另外算\" = listrik ditagih terpisah. Air sudah termasuk, tetapi listrik tidak.","Ordering and Paying at a Restaurant":"Memesan dan Membayar di Restoran","At noon, Kenichi goes to a small restaurant for lunch with a coworker.":"Saat siang, Kenichi pergi ke sebuah rumah makan kecil untuk makan siang bersama rekan kerja.","The server brings the menu and asks: \"What would you like to order?\"":"Pelayan membawa menu dan bertanya: \"Mau pesan apa?\"","\"I'll have a pork chop rice, and then a bowl of soup.\"":"\"Saya pesan nasi iga babi, lalu satu mangkuk sup.\"","\"Would you like a drink? Today the black tea is buy one get one free.\"":"\"Mau minum sesuatu? Hari ini teh hitam beli satu gratis satu, lho.\"","\"Sure, then give me two black teas, thanks.\"":"\"Boleh, kalau begitu beri saya dua teh hitam, terima kasih.\"","After eating, Kenichi goes to the counter to pay.":"Setelah makan, Kenichi pergi ke kasir untuk membayar.","\"That's 210 in total. Can I pay by card?\" \"Yes, you can also pay by phone.\"":"\"Totalnya 210. Boleh bayar pakai kartu?\" \"Boleh, Anda juga bisa bayar lewat ponsel.\"","waiter/server":"pelayan","pork chop rice (a Taiwan classic)":"nasi iga babi (hidangan khas Taiwan)","buy one get one free":"beli satu gratis satu","to pay the bill":"membayar tagihan","counter/cashier":"kasir","in total":"totalnya","Why did Kenichi get two black teas?":"Mengapa Kenichi mengambil dua teh hitam?","Because it was buy one get one free":"Karena sedang beli satu gratis satu","Because he was very thirsty":"Karena dia sangat haus","Because he bought one for his coworker":"Karena dia membelikan satu untuk rekan kerjanya","\"紅茶買一送一\" = the black tea was buy one get one free, so he got two.":"\"紅茶買一送一\" = teh hitam sedang beli satu gratis satu, jadi dia mendapat dua.","Picking Up a Package at the Convenience Store":"Mengambil Paket di Minimarket","Yumi bought a pair of shoes online, and the seller shipped them to a convenience store.":"Yumi membeli sepasang sepatu secara online, dan penjual mengirimkannya ke minimarket.","She gets a text saying the package has arrived and she can go pick it up.":"Dia menerima pesan singkat yang memberitahu paketnya sudah tiba dan bisa diambil.","She walks into the store and tells the clerk: \"Hi, I'd like to pick up a package.\"":"Dia masuk ke toko dan berkata kepada kasir: \"Halo, saya mau mengambil paket.\"","\"Please give me your pickup number and the last three digits of your phone.\"":"\"Tolong berikan nomor pengambilan dan tiga digit terakhir nomor telepon Anda.\"","The clerk searches a bit, then takes out a box and hands it to her.":"Kasir mencari sebentar, lalu mengeluarkan sebuah kotak dan menyerahkannya kepadanya.","Because she chose cash on delivery, she has to pay 680 first.":"Karena dia memilih bayar di tempat, dia harus membayar 680 dulu.","After paying, the clerk says: \"Here's your receipt, please keep it safe, thanks.\"":"Setelah membayar, kasir berkata: \"Ini struk Anda, tolong simpan baik-baik, terima kasih.\"","package/parcel":"paket","text message (SMS)":"pesan singkat (SMS)","convenience store (short form)":"minimarket (bentuk singkat)","to pick up goods":"mengambil barang","number":"nomor","receipt (uniform invoice)":"struk (faktur seragam)","Why did Yumi have to pay money?":"Mengapa Yumi harus membayar?","Because it was cash on delivery":"Karena itu bayar di tempat","Because there's a pickup fee":"Karena ada biaya pengambilan","Because she hadn't paid shipping":"Karena dia belum membayar ongkos kirim","\"她是貨到付款\" = it was cash on delivery, so she pays when picking up.":"\"她是貨到付款\" = ini bayar di tempat, jadi dia membayar saat mengambil barang.","Describing Symptoms at the Doctor":"Menjelaskan Gejala di Dokter","Yating has been feeling unwell for the past few days, so after work she goes to a clinic to see a doctor.":"Beberapa hari ini Yating merasa tidak enak badan, jadi sepulang kerja dia pergi ke klinik untuk berobat.","She first registers at the counter and hands her National Health Insurance card to the nurse.":"Dia pertama-tama mendaftar di loket dan menyerahkan kartu Asuransi Kesehatan Nasional kepada perawat.","When it's her turn, the doctor asks: \"Where do you feel unwell?\"":"Ketika giliran dia, dokter bertanya: \"Di mana Anda merasa tidak enak?\"","\"Since yesterday I've had a constant sore throat, and a slight fever too.\"":"\"Sejak kemarin tenggorokan saya sakit terus, dan sedikit demam juga.\"","\"Although it's not serious, you'd best rest more and drink plenty of water.\"":"\"Meskipun tidak parah, sebaiknya Anda banyak istirahat dan banyak minum air.\"","The doctor prescribes three days of medicine and reminds her to come back if she doesn't improve.":"Dokter meresepkan obat untuk tiga hari dan mengingatkannya untuk kembali jika tidak membaik.","After picking up her medicine, Yating feels that having health insurance really makes things much easier.":"Setelah mengambil obatnya, Yating merasa memiliki asuransi kesehatan sungguh membuat segalanya jauh lebih mudah.","to feel unwell":"merasa tidak enak badan","to register (at a hospital)":"mendaftar (di rumah sakit)","National Health Insurance card":"kartu Asuransi Kesehatan Nasional","sore throat":"sakit tenggorokan","serious, severe":"parah, serius","to return for a follow-up visit":"kembali untuk kontrol","What did the doctor advise Yating to do?":"Apa yang dokter sarankan kepada Yating?","Rest more and drink plenty of water":"Banyak istirahat dan banyak minum air","Be hospitalized right away":"Segera dirawat inap","Exercise more":"Lebih banyak berolahraga","\"最好多休息、多喝水\" = it's best to rest more and drink plenty of water.":"\"最好多休息、多喝水\" = sebaiknya banyak istirahat dan banyak minum air.","A Job Interview":"Sebuah Wawancara Kerja","Zhihao is applying for a sales job at a trading company, and today is his interview.":"Zhihao melamar posisi penjualan di sebuah perusahaan perdagangan, dan hari ini adalah wawancaranya.","He arrives fifteen minutes early, wearing a neat suit and looking full of energy.":"Dia datang lima belas menit lebih awal, mengenakan setelan rapi dan tampak penuh semangat.","The interviewer asks: \"Please introduce yourself briefly and tell us your strengths.\"":"Pewawancara bertanya: \"Silakan perkenalkan diri Anda secara singkat dan sebutkan kelebihan Anda.\"","\"Not only do I handle pressure well, but I'm also very willing to learn new things.\"":"\"Saya tidak hanya tahan terhadap tekanan, tetapi juga sangat mau belajar hal-hal baru.\"","\"If I have the chance to join your company, I will definitely give it my all.\"":"\"Jika saya berkesempatan bergabung dengan perusahaan Anda, saya pasti akan berusaha sekuat tenaga.\"","The interviewer nods, then asks his views on salary and overtime.":"Pewawancara mengangguk, lalu menanyakan pandangannya tentang gaji dan lembur.","After the interview, the company says they will notify him of the result within a week.":"Setelah wawancara, perusahaan mengatakan akan memberitahukan hasilnya dalam waktu satu minggu.","Zhihao feels he did fairly well, and his heart is full of anticipation.":"Zhihao merasa dirinya cukup baik, dan hatinya penuh harapan.","to apply for (a job)":"melamar (pekerjaan)","self-introduction":"perkenalan diri","strength, merit":"kelebihan, keunggulan","ability to handle pressure":"kemampuan menahan tekanan","to give one's all":"berusaha sekuat tenaga","What did Zhihao give as his strengths?":"Apa yang Zhihao sebutkan sebagai kelebihannya?","Handles pressure well and is willing to learn":"Tahan terhadap tekanan dan mau belajar","Very good at English":"Sangat mahir bahasa Inggris","Has ten years of experience":"Memiliki pengalaman sepuluh tahun","\"不但抗壓性強，而且很願意學習\" = both handles pressure well and is willing to learn.":"\"不但抗壓性強，而且很願意學習\" = tahan terhadap tekanan sekaligus mau belajar.","Preparing for a Typhoon Day":"Bersiap Menghadapi Hari Topan","The weather bureau says a strong typhoon is approaching Taiwan and may make landfall this weekend.":"Badan meteorologi mengatakan sebuah topan kuat sedang mendekati Taiwan dan mungkin mendarat akhir pekan ini.","Meihui rushes to the supermarket before the typhoon and buys instant noodles, bread, and drinking water.":"Meihui bergegas ke supermarket sebelum topan datang dan membeli mi instan, roti, dan air minum.","She also moves the flowerpots from the balcony indoors so the strong wind won't blow them over.":"Dia juga memindahkan pot bunga dari balkon ke dalam agar tidak diterbangkan angin kencang.","That night, the city government announces work and classes are canceled tomorrow, and everyone feels relieved.":"Malam itu, pemerintah kota mengumumkan besok libur kerja dan libur sekolah, dan semua orang merasa lega.","On the day of the typhoon, the wind and rain outside are fierce, and there's almost no one on the streets.":"Pada hari topan, angin dan hujan di luar sangat kencang, dan hampir tidak ada orang di jalanan.","Although she can't go out, Meihui watches movies and cooks noodles at home, spending the day leisurely.":"Meskipun tidak bisa keluar, Meihui menonton film dan memasak mi di rumah, menghabiskan hari dengan santai.","The neighborhood head also reminds everyone in the group chat to report immediately if there's flooding.":"Kepala lingkungan juga mengingatkan semua orang di grup chat untuk segera melapor jika terjadi banjir.","Fortunately there was no serious damage this time, and the typhoon left the next day.":"Untungnya kali ini tidak ada kerusakan serius, dan topan pergi keesokan harinya.","weather bureau":"badan meteorologi","to make landfall":"mendarat (topan)","so as to avoid":"agar terhindar dari","work and classes canceled (typhoon closure)":"libur kerja dan sekolah (peliburan karena topan)","to breathe a sigh of relief":"menghela napas lega","neighborhood head (li chief)":"kepala lingkungan (kepala li)","to flood":"banjir, tergenang","disaster situation, damage":"kondisi bencana, kerusakan","What did the city government announce about the typhoon?":"Apa yang diumumkan pemerintah kota tentang topan?","Work and classes canceled the next day":"Keesokan harinya libur kerja dan sekolah","The MRT would stop all day":"MRT akan berhenti sepanjang hari","Everyone must evacuate":"Semua orang harus mengungsi","\"市政府宣布明天停班停課\" = the city government announced work and classes were canceled the next day.":"\"市政府宣布明天停班停課\" = pemerintah kota mengumumkan keesokan harinya libur kerja dan sekolah.","Opening a Bank Account and Getting a Phone Plan with an ARC":"Membuka Rekening Bank dan Mendapatkan Paket Ponsel dengan ARC","Since he'll start receiving his salary next month, Kenta had no choice but to first go open a bank account.":"Karena bulan depan mulai menerima gaji, Kenta terpaksa harus membuka rekening bank terlebih dahulu.","The staff member said: \"Unless you bring your ARC and a secondary ID, we cannot process the account opening for you.\"":"Petugas berkata: \"Kecuali Anda membawa ARC dan identitas kedua, kami tidak dapat memproses pembukaan rekening untuk Anda.\"","Luckily Kenta had looked it up beforehand and brought his passport along as well.":"Untungnya Kenta sudah mencari tahu sebelumnya dan turut membawa paspornya.","After filling out the application form, he also set up passwords for online banking and his ATM card.":"Setelah mengisi formulir permohonan, dia juga membuat kata sandi untuk perbankan online dan kartu ATM-nya.","With the account done, he next went to a telecom store to apply for a mobile number.":"Setelah rekeningnya selesai, dia lalu pergi ke gerai telekomunikasi untuk mendaftar nomor ponsel.","The clerk explained that although foreigners can get a phone number, they usually need to provide an ARC and proof of a local bank account.":"Petugas menjelaskan bahwa meskipun orang asing bisa mendapatkan nomor telepon, mereka biasanya perlu menyediakan ARC dan bukti rekening bank lokal.","\"Good thing I just opened my account,\" Kenta said with relief, handing the documents to the clerk.":"\"Untung saya baru saja membuka rekening,\" kata Kenta dengan lega, sambil menyerahkan dokumen kepada petugas.","Half an hour later, the number was activated, and he could finally contact his company with a Taiwanese number.":"Setengah jam kemudian, nomornya aktif, dan akhirnya dia bisa menghubungi perusahaannya dengan nomor Taiwan.","ARC (Alien Resident Certificate)":"ARC (Kartu Izin Tinggal Orang Asing)","to open a bank account":"membuka rekening bank","the person in charge, handling staff":"petugas yang menangani","secondary ID document":"dokumen identitas kedua","ATM/debit card":"kartu ATM/debit","mobile phone number (plan)":"nomor ponsel (paket)","to apply for and process":"mengajukan dan memproses","although, even though":"meskipun, walaupun","unless…, otherwise…":"kecuali…, jika tidak…","to have no choice but to":"terpaksa, tidak ada pilihan selain","What did Kenta need in order to open a bank account?":"Apa yang Kenta butuhkan untuk membuka rekening bank?","An ARC and a secondary ID (such as a passport)":"Sebuah ARC dan identitas kedua (seperti paspor)","Only an ARC":"Hanya ARC","Only a phone plan contract":"Hanya kontrak paket ponsel","\"除非您帶著居留證和第二證件，否則…無法辦理開戶\" = both an ARC and a secondary ID are required. Kenta brought his passport to meet this.":"\"除非您帶著居留證和第二證件，否則…無法辦理開戶\" = diperlukan baik ARC maupun identitas kedua. Kenta membawa paspor untuk memenuhi syarat ini.","Resolving a Rental Deposit Dispute":"Menyelesaikan Sengketa Uang Jaminan Sewa","The lease on the studio Meiling rented had ended, but the landlord was reluctant to return the two months' deposit.":"Kontrak sewa studio yang disewa Meiling telah berakhir, tetapi pemilik enggan mengembalikan uang jaminan dua bulan.","The landlord claimed the walls were stained and damaged, and therefore wanted to deduct a repair fee.":"Pemilik mengklaim dindingnya kotor dan rusak, sehingga ingin memotong biaya perbaikan.","Meiling disagreed, saying: \"These marks were there before I moved in; I even took photos as evidence when I received the place.\"":"Meiling tidak setuju, katanya: \"Bekas-bekas ini sudah ada sebelum saya pindah masuk; saya bahkan memotret sebagai bukti saat menerima tempat ini.\"","Since the two sides each told a different story, she decided to take out the lease contract they had signed to clarify responsibility.":"Karena kedua pihak masing-masing punya cerita berbeda, dia memutuskan mengeluarkan kontrak sewa yang telah ditandatangani untuk memperjelas tanggung jawab.","The contract clearly stated that natural wear and tear does not count as damage, and the tenant bears no liability for compensation.":"Kontrak dengan jelas menyatakan bahwa keausan alami tidak dianggap kerusakan, dan penyewa tidak menanggung kewajiban ganti rugi.","In a calm but firm tone, Meiling stated: \"Unless you can prove the damage was caused by me, the deposit should be returned in full.\"":"Dengan nada tenang namun tegas, Meiling menyatakan: \"Kecuali Anda dapat membuktikan kerusakan itu disebabkan oleh saya, uang jaminan harus dikembalikan sepenuhnya.\"","After looking at the photos and the contract, the landlord, though somewhat unwilling, finally agreed to return the entire deposit.":"Setelah melihat foto dan kontrak, pemilik, meskipun agak enggan, akhirnya setuju mengembalikan seluruh uang jaminan.","This experience made Meiling realize how important it is to keep written evidence to protect one's own rights.":"Pengalaman ini membuat Meiling menyadari betapa pentingnya menyimpan bukti tertulis untuk melindungi hak-haknya sendiri.","deposit (security deposit)":"uang jaminan (deposit)","to return, refund":"mengembalikan, membayar balik","to claim, assert":"mengklaim, menegaskan","repair, renovation":"perbaikan, renovasi","to keep as evidence":"menyimpan sebagai bukti","each side tells a different story":"masing-masing pihak punya cerita berbeda","compensation, to compensate":"ganti rugi, mengganti rugi","What was the key factor that let Meiling get her full deposit back?":"Apa faktor kunci yang membuat Meiling mendapatkan kembali seluruh uang jaminannya?","Photos taken before moving in and the contract clauses — written evidence":"Foto yang diambil sebelum pindah masuk dan klausul kontrak — bukti tertulis","Because she loudly protested to the landlord":"Karena dia memprotes pemilik dengan keras","Because she agreed to pay the repair fee herself":"Karena dia setuju membayar biaya perbaikan sendiri","Meiling showed photos from the handover and the contract clause stating wear and tear is not compensable. Written evidence was decisive.":"Meiling menunjukkan foto saat serah terima dan klausul kontrak yang menyatakan keausan tidak dapat diganti rugi. Bukti tertulis menjadi penentu.","Taiwan on the Tip of the Tongue":"Taiwan di Ujung Lidah","For many people, the fastest way to get to know a city is not to flip through a travel guide, but to step into its markets and street corners.":"Bagi banyak orang, cara tercepat mengenal sebuah kota bukanlah membolak-balik panduan wisata, melainkan melangkah ke pasar dan sudut-sudut jalannya.","Taiwan's food culture is precisely what has accumulated, bit by bit, within these little cracks of everyday life.":"Budaya kuliner Taiwan justru adalah sesuatu yang terkumpul sedikit demi sedikit di dalam celah-celah kecil kehidupan sehari-hari.","The night market is perhaps its most vivid microcosm: oil sizzles in the wok, and the aromas of oyster omelet, fried chicken cutlet, and stinky tofu weave together.":"Pasar malam mungkin adalah miniatur paling hidup darinya: minyak mendesis di wajan, dan aroma telur dadar tiram, ayam goreng tepung, serta tahu busuk berpadu menjadi satu.","These snacks seem ordinary, yet behind them often lies a family's decades of craftsmanship and perseverance.":"Camilan-camilan ini tampak biasa saja, namun di baliknya sering tersimpan keahlian dan ketekunan sebuah keluarga selama puluhan tahun.","Beyond street snacks, the boxed meal is an indispensable part of Taiwanese life.":"Selain camilan jalanan, nasi kotak adalah bagian tak terpisahkan dari kehidupan orang Taiwan.","From the pork-chop lunchboxes on train platforms to the self-service eateries outside office buildings, every dish has its own particular care.":"Dari nasi kotak iga babi di peron kereta hingga rumah makan prasmanan di luar gedung perkantoran, setiap hidangan memiliki perhatiannya sendiri.","And the hand-shaken drinks that have swept the globe in recent years have carried the taste of Taiwan to every corner of the world.":"Dan minuman kocok tangan yang melanda seluruh dunia dalam beberapa tahun terakhir telah membawa cita rasa Taiwan ke setiap sudut dunia.","From bubble tea to all kinds of tea drinks, both sweetness and ice can be freely adjusted to personal taste.":"Dari teh boba hingga berbagai minuman teh, baik tingkat kemanisan maupun es bisa disesuaikan bebas menurut selera pribadi.","What makes Taiwanese food so moving lies not only in the flavors themselves, but even more in the passion for life and human warmth behind them.":"Yang membuat kuliner Taiwan begitu menyentuh bukan hanya terletak pada cita rasanya sendiri, tetapi lebih-lebih pada semangat hidup dan kehangatan manusia di baliknya.","as for, to (in 對…而言)":"bagi, terhadap (dalam 對…而言)","microcosm, epitome":"miniatur, cerminan","to intertwine, to weave together":"berpadu, menjalin bersama","to carry, to bear (weight/meaning)":"mengusung, memikul (beban/makna)","perseverance, insistence":"ketekunan, keteguhan","to be particular about, meticulous care":"cermat, perhatian yang teliti","to sweep (a place), to be all the rage":"melanda (suatu tempat), sedang naik daun","the reason why… is because…":"alasan mengapa… adalah karena…","human warmth, the personal touch":"kehangatan manusia, sentuhan pribadi","According to the passage, what is the deepest reason Taiwanese food is so moving?":"Menurut bacaan, apa alasan terdalam mengapa kuliner Taiwan begitu menyentuh?","Not just the flavor itself, but the passion for life and human warmth behind it":"Bukan hanya cita rasanya sendiri, tetapi semangat hidup dan kehangatan manusia di baliknya","Because it is famous and popular worldwide":"Karena terkenal dan populer di seluruh dunia","Because it is cheap and the portions are large":"Karena murah dan porsinya besar","Because you can freely choose sweetness and ice":"Karena Anda bisa bebas memilih kemanisan dan es","The final line, \"not only in the flavors themselves, but even more in the passion for life and human warmth,\" points to warmth as the deepest reason.":"Kalimat terakhir, \"bukan hanya pada cita rasanya sendiri, tetapi lebih-lebih pada semangat hidup dan kehangatan manusia,\" menunjuk kehangatan sebagai alasan terdalam.","The Gift Called Human Warmth":"Hadiah Bernama Kehangatan Manusia","If you had to describe Taiwan in a single word, many locals and travelers alike would, without prior agreement, mention \"human warmth.\"":"Jika Anda harus menggambarkan Taiwan dengan satu kata, banyak penduduk lokal maupun wisatawan akan, tanpa janji sebelumnya, menyebut \"kehangatan manusia.\"","This warmth is not some earth-shattering act, but rather something hidden in the most ordinary of details.":"Kehangatan ini bukanlah tindakan luar biasa yang menggemparkan, melainkan sesuatu yang tersembunyi dalam detail yang paling biasa.","Perhaps it is the umbrella a stranger quietly holds up for you on a rainy day.":"Mungkin itu adalah payung yang diam-diam dipayungkan orang asing untuk Anda di hari hujan.","Perhaps it is the person who, when you ask for directions, simply sets aside what they were doing and walks you straight to your destination.":"Mungkin itu adalah orang yang, ketika Anda menanyakan arah, langsung meninggalkan apa yang sedang dikerjakannya dan mengantar Anda tepat ke tujuan.","The older generation often says that away from home you rely on friends, and a single warm greeting can outweigh a thousand words.":"Generasi tua sering berkata bahwa saat jauh dari rumah kita bergantung pada teman, dan satu sapaan hangat bisa lebih berharga daripada seribu kata.","Whenever New Year or a festival comes around, this warmth grows all the more palpable.":"Setiap kali Tahun Baru atau perayaan tiba, kehangatan ini menjadi semakin terasa.","Neighbors share the New Year dishes they made at home and ask after one another's well-being, as if they were one family.":"Para tetangga berbagi hidangan Tahun Baru yang mereka masak di rumah dan saling menanyakan kabar, seakan-akan mereka satu keluarga.","It is precisely because of such bonds that the distance between people is gradually drawn closer.":"Justru karena ikatan seperti inilah jarak antar manusia perlahan-lahan menjadi semakin dekat.","For many who have left their hometowns far behind, it is precisely this warmth that makes Taiwan a second home.":"Bagi banyak orang yang telah meninggalkan kampung halamannya jauh di belakang, justru kehangatan inilah yang menjadikan Taiwan rumah kedua.","to coincide without prior agreement":"kebetulan sama tanpa janji sebelumnya","earth-shattering, momentous":"menggemparkan, luar biasa besar","unfamiliar, strange":"asing, tak dikenal","straightforwardly, might as well":"langsung saja, sekalian saja","to surpass, to be better than":"melampaui, lebih baik daripada","thick, strong (of atmosphere/feeling)":"kental, pekat (suasana/perasaan)","to show tender care, to ask after someone":"menunjukkan perhatian lembut, menanyakan kabar","bond, tie":"ikatan, jalinan","to leave one's hometown behind":"meninggalkan kampung halaman","warmth, a warm feeling":"kehangatan, perasaan hangat","According to the passage, how does Taiwan's \"human warmth\" reveal itself?":"Menurut bacaan, bagaimana \"kehangatan manusia\" Taiwan menampakkan dirinya?","It hides within the most ordinary details of daily life":"Ia tersembunyi dalam detail paling biasa dari kehidupan sehari-hari","It appears in grand, earth-shattering deeds":"Ia muncul dalam perbuatan besar yang menggemparkan","It is shown through money and expensive gifts":"Ia ditunjukkan melalui uang dan hadiah mahal","It exists only during New Year and festivals":"Ia hanya ada saat Tahun Baru dan perayaan","The text says it is \"not some earth-shattering act, but hidden in the most ordinary details\" — like the umbrella or directions. Festivals only intensify it.":"Teks mengatakan ia \"bukan tindakan menggemparkan, melainkan tersembunyi dalam detail paling biasa\" — seperti payung atau menunjukkan arah. Perayaan hanya memperkuatnya.","imminent; pressing":"mendesak; sudah di depan mata","The problem of pollution is now imminent and cannot be delayed any longer.":"Masalah polusi kini sudah mendesak dan tidak bisa ditunda lagi.","intricate and complex":"rumit dan berbelit-belit","The interpersonal relationships in this case are intricate and hard to untangle.":"Hubungan antarpribadi dalam kasus ini rumit dan sulit diurai.","to handle with ease":"menangani dengan mudah","After years of practice, he now handles this job with ease.":"Setelah bertahun-tahun berlatih, kini ia menangani pekerjaan ini dengan mudah.","time-consuming and wasteful":"membuang waktu dan boros","This approach is time-consuming and wasteful, with very low efficiency.":"Pendekatan ini membuang waktu dan boros, dengan efisiensi yang sangat rendah.","to attract public attention":"menarik perhatian publik","This presidential election is the focus of everyone's attention.":"Pemilihan presiden kali ini menjadi pusat perhatian semua orang.","to prepare before it's too late":"bersiap sebelum terlambat","Wise people prepare in advance before trouble arises.":"Orang bijak bersiap terlebih dahulu sebelum masalah timbul.","apt and appropriate":"tepat dan sesuai","His assessment was apt and fitting, neither exaggerated nor belittling.":"Penilaiannya tepat dan sesuai, tidak dilebih-lebihkan maupun diremehkan.","of a unique style":"bergaya unik dan khas","This restaurant's decor has a unique style that leaves a deep impression.":"Dekorasi restoran ini bergaya unik yang memberikan kesan mendalam.","beyond doubt":"tak diragukan lagi","His professional ability is beyond doubt and highly recognized.":"Kemampuan profesionalnya tak diragukan lagi dan sangat diakui.","paradoxical; bizarre":"paradoksal; ganjil","The way this matter unfolded is deeply paradoxical and puzzling.":"Cara peristiwa ini terjadi sangat paradoksal dan membingungkan.","barrier; fence":"penghalang; pagar pembatas","The internet has broken down the barriers between nations.":"Internet telah meruntuhkan penghalang antarnegara.","conventional pattern; rut":"pola konvensional; kebiasaan lama","This film breaks away from the conventional mold of romance movies.":"Film ini keluar dari pola konvensional film-film roman.","bottleneck":"hambatan; titik macet","The technical bottleneck brought the project to a temporary standstill.":"Hambatan teknis membuat proyek terhenti untuk sementara.","milestone":"tonggak sejarah","This invention is an important milestone in the history of technology.":"Penemuan ini merupakan tonggak sejarah penting dalam sejarah teknologi.","watershed; turning point":"titik balik; garis pemisah","This battle was the watershed of the entire war.":"Pertempuran ini menjadi titik balik dari seluruh perang.","epitome; microcosm":"gambaran mini; miniatur","This small town is a microcosm of Taiwanese society.":"Kota kecil ini adalah miniatur dari masyarakat Taiwan.","to condense; to unite":"menyatukan; merekatkan","This event brought together the cohesion of the community's residents.":"Acara ini menyatukan kekompakan warga komunitas.","to discard; to abandon":"membuang; meninggalkan","We should abandon outdated prejudices.":"Kita seharusnya membuang prasangka yang sudah usang.","to converge; to gather":"menghimpun; mengumpulkan","This city brings together talent from all over the world.":"Kota ini menghimpun talenta dari seluruh penjuru dunia.","to make up for; to compensate":"menebus; mengganti","No amount of money can make up for this regret.":"Tidak ada uang sebanyak apa pun yang bisa menebus penyesalan ini.","scarce; deficient":"langka; kekurangan","This region has long suffered from a scarcity of resources, limiting its development.":"Wilayah ini sejak lama mengalami kelangkaan sumber daya sehingga membatasi perkembangannya.","scarce":"langka","Clean water resources are extremely scarce in that area.":"Sumber air bersih di daerah itu sangat langka.","wise; sagacious":"bijaksana; arif","This elder's words are full of wisdom.":"Ucapan orang tua ini penuh dengan kebijaksanaan.","keen; sharp":"tajam; jeli","A journalist must possess keen powers of observation.":"Seorang jurnalis harus memiliki daya pengamatan yang tajam.","myth; misconception":"mitos; kesalahpahaman","Many people hold a misconception about dieting, thinking they'll lose weight if they don't eat.":"Banyak orang memiliki kesalahpahaman tentang diet, mengira tidak makan akan membuat berat badan turun.","implication; connotation":"makna tersirat; konotasi","The meaning of this poem is profound and worth savoring repeatedly.":"Makna puisi ini mendalam dan layak direnungkan berulang kali.","appearance; surface":"tampilan luar; permukaan","Don't just look at the surface; understand the truth of the matter deeply.":"Jangan hanya melihat permukaannya; pahami kebenaran persoalan secara mendalam.","metaphor":"metafora; kiasan","The author uses the sea as a metaphor for the unpredictability of life.":"Penulis menggunakan lautan sebagai metafora ketidakpastian hidup.","original intention":"niat awal","No matter how busy, he never forgot his original intention for starting the business.":"Sesibuk apa pun, ia tidak pernah melupakan niat awalnya saat memulai usaha.","inertia; force of habit":"inersia; kekuatan kebiasaan","People often find it hard to change old habits because of inertia.":"Orang sering sulit mengubah kebiasaan lama karena inersia.","confidence; inner strength":"kepercayaan diri; ketenangan batin","With ample preparation, you feel more confident when presenting on stage.":"Dengan persiapan yang matang, Anda akan lebih percaya diri saat presentasi di atas panggung.","taste; style; class":"selera; kelas","This restaurant's decor has great taste, making guests feel at home.":"Dekorasi restoran ini bercita rasa tinggi, membuat tamu merasa nyaman seperti di rumah.","prosperity; boom":"kemakmuran; masa jaya","As tourists returned, the small town saw prosperity once again.":"Ketika wisatawan kembali, kota kecil itu kembali mengalami kemakmuran.","malady; drawback":"kelemahan; cacat sistem","The drawbacks of this system have long been criticized.":"Kelemahan sistem ini telah lama dikritik.","oversight; omission":"kelalaian; kekhilafan","This report has some oversights; please check it carefully once more.":"Laporan ini memiliki beberapa kelalaian; mohon periksa kembali dengan teliti.","integrity; good faith":"integritas; itikad baik","The most important thing in business is integrity; you can't deceive customers.":"Hal terpenting dalam bisnis adalah integritas; Anda tidak boleh menipu pelanggan.","conscience":"hati nurani","Facing the temptation of profit, he always held fast to his conscience.":"Menghadapi godaan keuntungan, ia selalu berpegang teguh pada hati nuraninya.","grudge; ill feeling":"dendam; ganjalan hati","After the two spoke openly, the grudge in their hearts gradually dissolved.":"Setelah keduanya berbicara secara terbuka, ganjalan di hati mereka perlahan mencair.","broad-mindedness; magnanimity":"kelapangan hati; kemurahan hati","A successful leader must possess a broad-minded spirit.":"Seorang pemimpin yang sukses harus memiliki jiwa yang berlapang dada.","sentiment; moral character":"sentimen; budi pekerti","Music and art can cultivate a person's sentiments.":"Musik dan seni dapat memupuk budi pekerti seseorang.","demeanor; model bearing":"sikap; kewibawaan teladan","He treats others with modesty and courtesy, showing the demeanor of a master.":"Ia memperlakukan orang lain dengan rendah hati dan santun, memperlihatkan kewibawaan seorang maestro.","boldness; spirit":"keberanian; semangat","This painting has bold strokes, full of majestic spirit.":"Lukisan ini memiliki goresan yang berani, penuh dengan semangat yang megah.","horizon; outlook":"cakrawala; wawasan","Traveling abroad more can broaden one's horizons.":"Lebih sering bepergian ke luar negeri dapat memperluas wawasan seseorang.","attainments; expertise":"penguasaan; kepiawaian","His attainments in calligraphy earn considerable admiration from peers.":"Kepiawaiannya dalam kaligrafi mendapat kekaguman besar dari rekan-rekannya.","to set about; to start":"memulai; mengerjakan","Before setting about it, we must first draw up a plan.":"Sebelum memulainya, kita harus menyusun rencana terlebih dahulu.","He always likes to guess others' thoughts, living quite wearily.":"Ia selalu suka menerka pikiran orang lain, hidupnya jadi cukup melelahkan.","to grope; to explore":"meraba-raba; menjajaki","When first starting a business, you must grope your way slowly on your own.":"Saat baru memulai usaha, Anda harus meraba-raba jalan sendiri secara perlahan.","to be compatible":"kompatibel; cocok","This system is compatible with various different devices.":"Sistem ini kompatibel dengan berbagai perangkat yang berbeda.","to take into account":"mempertimbangkan; memperhitungkan","When making decisions, one must take all parties' interests into account.":"Saat mengambil keputusan, seseorang harus mempertimbangkan kepentingan semua pihak.","to touch; to stir":"menyentuh; menggugah","The plot of this film deeply touched my heart.":"Alur film ini menyentuh hatiku dalam-dalam.","to shake; to rock":"mengguncang; menggemparkan","This news shook the entire society.":"Berita ini mengguncang seluruh masyarakat.","to contend; to rival":"bersaing; menandingi","This small company can hardly contend with multinational corporations.":"Perusahaan kecil ini sulit menandingi korporasi multinasional.","to see clearly; to discern":"melihat dengan jelas; menyingkap","Veteran journalists can often see through to the truth behind events.":"Jurnalis berpengalaman sering dapat menyingkap kebenaran di balik peristiwa.","to accord; to match":"sepadan; sejalan","The two's ideals matched perfectly, so they decided to collaborate.":"Cita-cita keduanya sangat sejalan, sehingga mereka memutuskan untuk bekerja sama.","to flaunt; to advertise as":"menonjolkan; mengklaim sebagai","This shop advertises itself as using purely natural ingredients.":"Toko ini mengklaim dirinya menggunakan bahan-bahan alami murni.","to propose; to advocate":"mengusulkan; menganjurkan","He was the first to advocate energy saving and carbon reduction, drawing many supporters.":"Ia adalah orang pertama yang menganjurkan penghematan energi dan pengurangan karbon, menarik banyak pendukung.","to run in; to adjust to each other":"menyesuaikan diri satu sama lain","A new team needs some time to adjust to one another.":"Tim yang baru membutuhkan waktu untuk saling menyesuaikan diri.","to curb; to check":"menahan; membendung","The government took measures to curb the spread of the epidemic.":"Pemerintah mengambil langkah-langkah untuk membendung penyebaran wabah.","to restrain; to suppress":"menahan; menekan","He tried hard to restrain his emotions and hold back his tears.":"Ia berusaha keras menahan emosinya dan membendung air mata.","to channel; to direct (flow)":"mengalihkan; mengatur arus","Police direct traffic at the intersection to prevent congestion.":"Polisi mengatur arus lalu lintas di persimpangan untuk mencegah kemacetan.","to have both; to combine":"memadukan; memiliki keduanya","This talent has both virtue and ability, highly valued by the company.":"Talenta ini memiliki keutamaan dan kemampuan sekaligus, sangat dihargai perusahaan.","to contain; to hold in store":"menyimpan; mengandung","This mountainous area holds abundant natural resources.":"Kawasan pegunungan ini menyimpan sumber daya alam yang melimpah.","to run through; to penetrate":"menjalari; merangkai keseluruhan","This main thread runs through the entire novel's plot.":"Alur utama ini menjalari seluruh jalan cerita novel tersebut.","to expand; to develop":"memperluas; mengembangkan","The company plans to expand overseas markets to increase revenue.":"Perusahaan berencana memperluas pasar luar negeri untuk meningkatkan pendapatan.","He tactfully declined the other party's invitation.":"Ia dengan halus menolak undangan pihak lain.","meticulous; dense":"cermat; teliti","Her thinking is very meticulous, considering every aspect.":"Pemikirannya sangat cermat, mempertimbangkan setiap aspek.","refined; polished":"terasah; halus terpoles","This article's wording is polished, without any sloppiness.":"Kata-kata dalam artikel ini terpoles halus, tanpa kecerobohan sedikit pun.","vivid; lifelike":"hidup; seperti nyata","This portrait is painted very vividly, true to life.":"Potret ini dilukis dengan sangat hidup, seperti nyata.","His words were very cryptic, leaving people baffled.":"Perkataannya sangat berteka-teki, membuat orang kebingungan.","blatant; explicit":"terang-terangan; blak-blakan","His way of expressing dissatisfaction was too blatant, making people awkward.":"Caranya mengungkapkan ketidakpuasan terlalu terang-terangan, membuat orang canggung.","sharp; pointed":"tajam; menohok","The reporter's questions were very sharp, hard for the official to parry.":"Pertanyaan wartawan itu sangat tajam, sulit ditangkis oleh pejabat tersebut.","harsh; demanding":"keras; menuntut tinggi","This company's demands on employees are extremely harsh.":"Tuntutan perusahaan ini terhadap karyawan sangatlah keras.","tedious; complicated":"berbelit; menyita","The application procedures are very tedious, consuming much time.":"Prosedur pendaftarannya sangat berbelit-belit dan menyita banyak waktu.","lengthy; verbose":"bertele-tele; panjang lebar","This meeting was lengthy and inefficient; everyone was impatient.":"Rapat ini bertele-tele dan tidak efisien; semua orang jadi tidak sabar.","abstruse; hard to understand":"sukar dipahami; berat","This philosophy book's content is abstruse and hard to read.":"Isi buku filsafat ini sukar dipahami dan berat untuk dibaca.","humorous; witty":"jenaka; humoris","He speaks in a witty, humorous way, always making everyone laugh.":"Ia berbicara dengan cara yang jenaka dan humoris, selalu membuat semua orang tertawa.","smooth; slick (socially)":"luwes; pandai bergaul","He is smooth in dealing with people, never easily offending anyone.":"Ia luwes dalam bergaul, tidak mudah menyinggung siapa pun.","calm; unhurried":"tenang; tak tergesa-gesa","Facing the sudden situation, he remained calm and unhurried.":"Menghadapi situasi mendadak itu, ia tetap tenang dan tak tergesa-gesa.","assured; certain":"yakin; penuh kepastian","He looked assured, full of confidence in the match's outcome.":"Ia tampak yakin, penuh percaya diri akan hasil pertandingan.","the general trend of the times":"arus besar zaman","Digitalization is the general trend; enterprises must respond early.":"Digitalisasi adalah arus besar zaman; perusahaan harus segera menyikapinya.","opinions vary widely":"pendapat sangat beragam","Regarding the truth of this incident, outside opinions vary widely.":"Mengenai kebenaran peristiwa ini, pendapat dari luar sangat beragam.","at a loss what to do":"kebingungan tak tahu harus berbuat apa","The two managers' orders contradict each other, leaving staff at a loss.":"Perintah kedua manajer saling bertentangan, membuat staf kebingungan tak tahu harus berbuat apa.","indecisive; hesitant":"ragu-ragu; bimbang","He is indecisive about whether to resign, unable to decide for a long time.":"Ia bimbang apakah harus mengundurkan diri, lama tak bisa memutuskan.","top priority; pressing matter":"prioritas utama; hal mendesak","The top priority is to stabilize public sentiment first, then discuss reforms.":"Prioritas utama adalah menstabilkan sentimen publik terlebih dahulu, baru membahas reformasi.","obvious; self-evident":"jelas; sudah terang","His intention is obvious, needing no further explanation at all.":"Niatnya sudah jelas, sama sekali tidak perlu penjelasan lebih lanjut.","attend to every aspect":"menyeluruh dari segala sisi","This proposal is thorough in every aspect, leaving no fault to find.":"Usulan ini menyeluruh dari segala sisi, tak ada celah untuk dikritik.","to toe the line; abide by rules":"menaati aturan; taat asas","He always follows the rules, never doing anything illegal.":"Ia selalu menaati aturan, tidak pernah melakukan hal yang melanggar hukum.","far behind; unable to catch up":"jauh tertinggal; tak terkejar","His level of expertise leaves peers far behind.":"Tingkat keahliannya membuat rekan-rekan sejawat jauh tertinggal.","a matter of differing opinions":"soal yang tergantung sudut pandang","Whether this film is good is, in fact, a matter of differing opinions.":"Bagus tidaknya film ini, sebenarnya tergantung sudut pandang masing-masing.","but; however (literary)":"tetapi; namun (sastra)","…, 惟 + (contrast / proviso)":"…, 惟 + (kontras / syarat tambahan)","A very formal literary 'but' (= 但是). Used in official documents, editorials, and formal writing, never in speech.":"Kata 'tetapi' yang sangat formal dalam bahasa sastra (= 但是). Digunakan dalam dokumen resmi, tajuk rencana, dan tulisan formal, tidak pernah dalam percakapan.","The plan is largely feasible, but the budget still needs assessment.":"Rencana ini pada dasarnya layak, tetapi anggarannya masih perlu dinilai.","This case is approved in principle, but the details still require further negotiation.":"Kasus ini pada prinsipnya disetujui, tetapi rinciannya masih memerlukan perundingan lebih lanjut.","even if… (still)":"sekalipun… (tetap)","縱使 + (situation), (subj) 亦 + (verb)":"縱使 + (situasi), (subjek) 亦 + (kata kerja)","The literary version of 即使…也 ('even if… still'). A formal concessive; 亦 is the written form of 也.":"Versi sastra dari 即使…也 ('sekalipun… tetap'). Konjungsi konsesif formal; 亦 adalah bentuk tulis dari 也.","Even if the road ahead is hard, we should still press bravely forward.":"Sekalipun jalan di depan sulit, kita tetap harus maju dengan berani.","Even placed in adversity, he never gave up his ideals.":"Sekalipun berada dalam kesulitan, ia tidak pernah menyerah pada cita-citanya.","even A can't…, 遑論 + B (harder thing)":"bahkan A pun tidak bisa…, 遑論 + B (hal yang lebih sulit)","A literary 'let alone.' Since even the smaller thing fails, the bigger one is obviously impossible; strengthens a negative.":"Ungkapan 'apalagi' dalam bahasa sastra. Karena hal yang lebih kecil saja gagal, hal yang lebih besar jelas mustahil; memperkuat kalimat negatif.","He can't even manage everyday conversation, let alone a formal speech.":"Percakapan sehari-hari saja ia tidak mampu, apalagi pidato formal.","He can barely cover basic expenses, much less buy a house.":"Untuk menutupi kebutuhan dasar saja ia sudah kesulitan, apalagi membeli rumah.","and even; extending to":"hingga bahkan; meluas sampai","A, B, 乃至(於) C (widening scope)":"A, B, 乃至(於) C (memperluas cakupan)","A literary connector placed at the end of a list to show scope extending 'even to' a further, often striking, item.":"Konektor sastra yang diletakkan di akhir daftar untuk menunjukkan cakupan yang meluas 'hingga bahkan' ke item yang lebih jauh dan sering kali mengejutkan.","This policy affects every county and city in Taiwan, extending even to remote villages.":"Kebijakan ini memengaruhi setiap kabupaten dan kota di Taiwan, hingga bahkan desa-desa terpencil.","From academia and industry to even the general public, all pay close attention to this issue.":"Dari kalangan akademisi dan industri hingga bahkan masyarakat umum, semua menaruh perhatian besar pada isu ini.","therefore; hence (literary)":"oleh karena itu; maka (sastra)","(cause), 是以 + (conclusion)":"(sebab), 是以 + (kesimpulan)","An archaic, elevated literary 'therefore' (= 所以 / 因此). Introduces a conclusion in editorials and official prose.":"Kata 'oleh karena itu' yang kuno dan tinggi dalam bahasa sastra (= 所以 / 因此). Memperkenalkan kesimpulan dalam tajuk rencana dan prosa resmi.","Resources are limited; therefore they must be allocated with care.":"Sumber daya terbatas; oleh karena itu harus dialokasikan dengan cermat.","Public sentiment is like flowing water; hence governance must not be undertaken carelessly.":"Sentimen publik bagai air yang mengalir; maka pemerintahan tidak boleh dijalankan secara sembrono.","thereby; consequently":"dengan demikian; sehingga","(action/cause), 從而 + (resulting effect)":"(tindakan/sebab), 從而 + (akibat yang dihasilkan)","A literary connector linking an action to the result it directly produces ('thereby'). The two clauses usually share a subject.":"Konektor sastra yang menghubungkan suatu tindakan dengan hasil yang langsung ditimbulkannya ('dengan demikian'). Kedua klausa biasanya berbagi subjek yang sama.","The government eased regulations, thereby driving industrial growth.":"Pemerintah melonggarkan regulasi, dengan demikian mendorong pertumbuhan industri.","He practiced diligently, thereby greatly improving his speaking ability.":"Ia berlatih dengan tekun, dengan demikian sangat meningkatkan kemampuan berbicaranya.","so that; resulting in (usually bad)":"sehingga; mengakibatkan (biasanya buruk)","(cause), 以致(於) + (undesirable result)":"(sebab), 以致(於) + (akibat yang tidak diinginkan)","A literary connector introducing an unwanted result caused by the preceding reason. Normally not used for good outcomes.":"Konektor sastra yang memperkenalkan akibat yang tidak diinginkan yang disebabkan oleh alasan sebelumnya. Biasanya tidak digunakan untuk hasil yang baik.","He made no preparation beforehand, so that he underperformed in the interview.":"Ia tidak melakukan persiapan sebelumnya, sehingga tampil buruk dalam wawancara.","Days of heavy rain resulted in road collapses in many places.":"Hujan lebat berhari-hari mengakibatkan jalan longsor di banyak tempat.","the reason that… is because…":"alasan mengapa… adalah karena…","(subj) 之所以 + (result), 是因為 + (cause)":"(subjek) 之所以 + (hasil), 是因為 + (sebab)","A literary cause-effect frame stating the result first, then emphasizing the reason. Used to foreground the cause.":"Kerangka sebab-akibat sastra yang menyatakan hasil terlebih dahulu, lalu menekankan alasannya. Digunakan untuk menonjolkan penyebabnya.","The reason he succeeded is that he persevered without slackening throughout.":"Alasan mengapa ia berhasil adalah karena ia bertekun tanpa kendur dari awal hingga akhir.","The reason this film is moving is that it authentically portrays human nature.":"Alasan mengapa film ini mengharukan adalah karena ia menggambarkan sifat manusia secara autentik.","in view of; given that":"mengingat; berhubung","有鑑於 + (situation), (subj) + (measure)":"有鑑於 + (situasi), (subjek) + (langkah)","A literary opener meaning 'considering (a situation)', giving grounds for a decision or measure. Common in official and news writing.":"Pembuka sastra yang berarti 'mengingat (suatu situasi)', memberikan dasar bagi suatu keputusan atau langkah. Umum dalam tulisan resmi dan berita.","In view of frequent fraud cases, the police stepped up public awareness efforts.":"Mengingat kasus penipuan yang sering terjadi, polisi meningkatkan upaya penyuluhan kepada masyarakat.","Given the increasingly severe low birth rate, the government rolled out several subsidies.":"Mengingat angka kelahiran rendah yang semakin parah, pemerintah meluncurkan sejumlah subsidi.","only by/if… can…":"hanya dengan/jika… baru…","唯有 + (condition), (subj) 才 + (result)":"唯有 + (syarat), (subjek) 才 + (hasil)","An elevated literary form of 只有…才, stressing that the condition is the sole and necessary one.":"Bentuk sastra yang tinggi dari 只有…才, menekankan bahwa syarat tersebut adalah satu-satunya dan yang diperlukan.","Only by working down to earth can one accumulate genuine ability.":"Hanya dengan bekerja secara membumi seseorang baru dapat mengumpulkan kemampuan yang sejati.","Only if the whole nation unites can the country have any prospects to speak of.":"Hanya jika seluruh bangsa bersatu, negara baru punya prospek yang layak dibicarakan.","rather than…, better to…":"daripada…, lebih baik…","與其 + A, 不如 + B (choose B)":"與其 + A, 不如 + B (pilih B)","A comparative frame preferring B over A ('rather than A, better B'). Slightly formal even in speech.":"Kerangka perbandingan yang lebih memilih B daripada A ('daripada A, lebih baik B'). Sedikit formal bahkan dalam percakapan.","Rather than talk idly about ideals, it's better to get down to earth and act.":"Daripada mengobrol kosong soal cita-cita, lebih baik membumi dan bertindak.","Rather than complain about circumstances, it's better to find a way to change yourself.":"Daripada mengeluhkan keadaan, lebih baik mencari cara untuk mengubah diri sendiri.","would rather… than…":"lebih baik… daripada…","寧可 + A (accept), 也不 + B (refuse)":"寧可 + A (menerima), 也不 + B (menolak)","Expresses firm resolve: willingly accept the unpleasant A rather than do the even worse B.":"Menyatakan tekad yang teguh: rela menerima A yang tak menyenangkan daripada melakukan B yang lebih buruk lagi.","I would rather have it a bit harder than go against my conscience.":"Saya lebih baik hidup sedikit lebih susah daripada melawan hati nurani saya.","He would rather go hungry than accept a handout.":"Ia lebih baik kelaparan daripada menerima sedekah.","tantamount to; no different from":"sama saja dengan; tak berbeda dari","A 無異於 + B (A equals B)":"A 無異於 + B (A sama dengan B)","A literary phrase declaring one act or state effectively 'the same as' another, usually a graver one. Common in criticism or warnings.":"Ungkapan sastra yang menyatakan bahwa suatu tindakan atau keadaan pada dasarnya 'sama dengan' yang lain, biasanya yang lebih serius. Umum dalam kritik atau peringatan.","Ignoring this warning is tantamount to sitting and waiting to perish.":"Mengabaikan peringatan ini sama saja dengan duduk menunggu kehancuran.","This move is no different from leaving the problem to the next generation.":"Langkah ini tak berbeda dari menyerahkan masalah kepada generasi berikutnya.","未免 + 太/過於 + (adj) (+了)":"未免 + 太/過於 + (kata sifat) (+了)","A modal adverb gently judging something as excessive ('a bit too…'). Used in writing and formal speech to soften criticism.":"Adverbia modalitas yang secara halus menilai sesuatu sebagai berlebihan ('agak terlalu…'). Digunakan dalam tulisan dan tuturan formal untuk melunakkan kritik.","Putting it that way is rather too arbitrary.":"Mengatakannya seperti itu agak terlalu sewenang-wenang.","Demanding so much all at once is rather too much to ask of anyone.":"Menuntut sebanyak itu sekaligus agak terlalu berlebihan bagi siapa pun.","The Passing On of Traditional Crafts":"Pewarisan Kerajinan Tradisional","Taiwan's traditional crafts carry the wisdom of its forebears and the memory of the land.":"Kerajinan tradisional Taiwan mengemban kebijaksanaan para leluhur dan kenangan tanah ini.","From wood carving and indigo dyeing to Koji pottery, every piece embodies decades of a craftsman's skill.":"Dari ukiran kayu dan pewarnaan indigo hingga tembikar Koji, setiap karya menjelmakan keahlian seorang perajin selama puluhan tahun.","Yet amid the tide of industrialization and mass production, these skills face the plight of having no successors.":"Namun di tengah gelombang industrialisasi dan produksi massal, keterampilan ini menghadapi kesulitan karena tiada penerus.","The younger generation often regards handicraft as an outdated trade lacking economic benefit.":"Generasi muda sering menganggap kerajinan tangan sebagai pekerjaan usang yang kurang menguntungkan secara ekonomi.","A break in transmission means not only the loss of technique, but also the erosion of cultural identity.":"Terputusnya pewarisan tidak hanya berarti hilangnya teknik, tetapi juga terkikisnya identitas budaya.","Fortunately, in recent years more and more cultural-creative workers have devoted themselves to this field.":"Untungnya, dalam beberapa tahun terakhir semakin banyak pekerja kreatif budaya yang mengabdikan diri di bidang ini.","They attempt to combine ancient techniques with contemporary aesthetics.":"Mereka berupaya memadukan teknik kuno dengan estetika kontemporer.","Only by bringing crafts into daily life can we give them the vitality to endure.":"Hanya dengan membawa kerajinan ke dalam kehidupan sehari-hari, kita baru dapat memberinya daya hidup untuk bertahan.","Preserving tradition is not shelving it away, but letting it be reborn continually within the times.":"Melestarikan tradisi bukanlah menyimpannya di rak, melainkan membiarkannya terus terlahir kembali di dalam zaman.","Only thus can the deft hands and craftsmanship of our forebears shine for later generations.":"Hanya dengan begitu, tangan terampil dan keahlian para leluhur kita dapat bersinar bagi generasi mendatang.","to carry, to bear":"mengemban, memikul","Koji pottery":"tembikar Koji","craftsman":"perajin","mass production":"produksi massal","to have no successors":"tiada penerus","rupture, break":"keretakan, keterputusan","cultural identity":"identitas budaya","to shelve, to set aside":"menyimpan di rak, mengesampingkan","to endow, to give":"memberi, menganugerahkan","craftsmanship, ingenuity":"keahlian, kepiawaian","Taiwan in the Face of Climate Change":"Taiwan Menghadapi Perubahan Iklim","As an island lying at the junction of the tropics and subtropics, Taiwan is especially sensitive to climate change.":"Sebagai pulau yang terletak di batas antara daerah tropis dan subtropis, Taiwan sangat peka terhadap perubahan iklim.","In recent years, disasters triggered by extreme weather have recurred at an alarming frequency.":"Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, bencana yang dipicu cuaca ekstrem terus berulang dengan frekuensi yang mengkhawatirkan.","Summer downpours readily cause landslides in the mountains, while winter droughts leave reservoirs dry.":"Hujan deras di musim panas mudah menyebabkan tanah longsor di pegunungan, sementara kekeringan musim dingin membuat waduk mengering.","Rising sea levels directly threaten the survival of low-lying areas along the western coast.":"Naiknya permukaan laut secara langsung mengancam kelangsungan hidup wilayah dataran rendah di sepanjang pesisir barat.","Agriculture bears the brunt, as both the harvest season and quality of crops are greatly affected by temperature fluctuations.":"Pertanian yang paling terkena dampak, karena baik musim panen maupun kualitas hasil tani sangat dipengaruhi oleh fluktuasi suhu.","In the face of this global crisis, no country can stand aloof.":"Menghadapi krisis global ini, tidak ada negara yang bisa berdiam diri.","In recent years Taiwan has actively promoted transition policies for renewable energy and net-zero emissions.":"Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, Taiwan aktif mendorong kebijakan transisi menuju energi terbarukan dan emisi nol bersih.","Yet the process of energy transition will inevitably entail readjusting industrial structure and the cost of living.":"Namun proses transisi energi mau tak mau akan menuntut penyesuaian ulang struktur industri dan biaya hidup.","Only when government, business, and the people work together can we safeguard this homeland for future generations.":"Hanya ketika pemerintah, dunia usaha, dan rakyat bekerja sama, kita baru dapat menjaga tanah air ini bagi generasi mendatang.","The climate challenge is imminent, and we no longer have room to hesitate or delay.":"Tantangan iklim sudah di depan mata, dan kita tak lagi punya ruang untuk ragu atau menunda.","junction, boundary":"batas, perbatasan","extreme weather":"cuaca ekstrem","at every turn, readily":"mudah sekali, sering kali","to run dry":"mengering","low-lying":"dataran rendah","to bear the brunt":"menanggung dampak terberat","to stay aloof":"berdiam diri, menjauh","net-zero emissions":"emisi nol bersih","to affect, to set in motion":"memengaruhi, menggerakkan","imminent":"sudah di depan mata","Volunteers and Civil Society":"Relawan dan Masyarakat Sipil","A mature civil society is often reflected in the people's zeal to take part in public affairs of their own accord.":"Masyarakat sipil yang matang sering tercermin dari semangat rakyat untuk turut serta dalam urusan publik atas kehendak sendiri.","In Taiwan, volunteer service has long become an indispensable part of many people's lives.":"Di Taiwan, layanan sukarela telah lama menjadi bagian yang tak terpisahkan dari kehidupan banyak orang.","Whether rescuing at disaster sites or accompanying children in remote villages, one sees the figures of volunteers.":"Baik saat menyelamatkan di lokasi bencana maupun menemani anak-anak di desa terpencil, kita dapat melihat sosok para relawan.","This bottom-up force fills the corners that neither government nor market can reach.":"Kekuatan dari bawah ke atas ini mengisi sudut-sudut yang tak terjangkau oleh pemerintah maupun pasar.","The value of a volunteer lies not in the amount of reward, but in that selfless dedication.":"Nilai seorang relawan tidak terletak pada besarnya imbalan, melainkan pada pengabdian tanpa pamrih itu.","Through connection with others, volunteers not only give but also come to know themselves anew in the process.":"Melalui hubungan dengan orang lain, relawan tidak hanya memberi tetapi juga mengenal kembali diri mereka dalam prosesnya.","Yet sustaining the spirit of volunteering relies on a sound system and long-term planning.":"Namun mempertahankan semangat kerelawanan bergantung pada sistem yang mapan dan perencanaan jangka panjang.","If it rests only on momentary passion, the energy of service will ultimately be hard to sustain.":"Jika hanya bertumpu pada semangat sesaat, energi pelayanan pada akhirnya akan sulit dipertahankan.","Only by allowing goodwill to endure can the foundation of civil society grow ever firmer.":"Hanya dengan membiarkan niat baik bertahan lama, fondasi masyarakat sipil baru dapat semakin kokoh.","Every small act of giving will ultimately converge into a vast force that drives society forward.":"Setiap tindakan memberi yang kecil pada akhirnya akan menyatu menjadi kekuatan besar yang menggerakkan masyarakat maju.","civil society":"masyarakat sipil","spontaneous":"spontan, atas kehendak sendiri","zeal, enthusiasm":"semangat, antusiasme","or":"atau","to make up for":"menutupi, melengkapi","amount (much or little)":"jumlah (banyak atau sedikit)","dedication, devotion":"pengabdian, dedikasi","to sustain, to maintain":"mempertahankan, memelihara","foundation":"fondasi, landasan","the verb 'to be'":"kata kerja 'to be'","A + shì + B":"A + shì + B","'是' links two nouns to show A=B. Don't use it before adjectives (wrong: 我是漂亮; correct: 我很漂亮). Negate with '不是'.":"'是' menghubungkan dua kata benda untuk menunjukkan A=B. Jangan gunakan sebelum kata sifat (salah: 我是漂亮; benar: 我很漂亮). Negasikan dengan '不是'.","I am a student.":"Saya adalah seorang pelajar.","He is a teacher.":"Dia adalah seorang guru.","possessive marker 'of'":"penanda kepemilikan 'punya/-nya'","Noun/Pronoun + de + Noun":"Noun/Pronoun + de + Noun","'的' marks possession: owner + 的 + thing = 'owner's thing'. It's normally required after pronouns/nouns, though it can drop with kinship terms (see [[g1-003]]).":"'的' menandai kepemilikan: pemilik + 的 + benda = 'benda milik pemilik'. Biasanya wajib digunakan setelah kata ganti/kata benda, tetapi bisa dihilangkan untuk istilah kekerabatan (lihat [[g1-003]]).","These are Dad's shoes.":"Ini adalah sepatu Ayah.","These are Mom's glasses.":"Ini adalah kacamata Ibu.","'de' can be dropped for close relationships":"'de' dapat dihilangkan untuk hubungan yang dekat","Pronoun + kinship term/affiliation (no 'de')":"Kata ganti + istilah kekerabatan/afiliasi (tanpa 'de')","With kinship terms or affiliations (school, company) right after a pronoun, 'de' can drop, e.g. 我媽媽 = 'my mom'. Ordinary objects like shoes or books still need 'de' (see [[g1-002]]).":"Dengan istilah kekerabatan atau afiliasi (sekolah, perusahaan) tepat setelah kata ganti, 'de' bisa dihilangkan, misalnya 我媽媽 = 'ibu saya'. Benda biasa seperti sepatu atau buku tetap memerlukan 'de' (lihat [[g1-002]]).","My mom is a teacher.":"Ibu saya adalah seorang guru.","My dad is a doctor.":"Ayah saya adalah seorang dokter.","negation adverb placed before verbs/adjectives":"kata keterangan negasi yang diletakkan sebelum kata kerja/kata sifat","bù + verb/adjective":"bù + verb/adjective","'不' negates verbs/adjectives in the present or as a general fact. Before 4th-tone 是 it changes tone to 'bú'. For past events, use '沒' instead of '不'.":"'不' menegasikan kata kerja/kata sifat pada masa kini atau sebagai fakta umum. Di depan 是 (nada 4) nadanya berubah menjadi 'bú'. Untuk peristiwa di masa lalu, gunakan '沒', bukan '不'.","I'm not (a student).":"Saya bukan (seorang pelajar).","He is not a teacher.":"Dia bukan seorang guru.","demonstratives 'this/that' and question word 'which'":"kata tunjuk 'ini/itu' dan kata tanya 'yang mana'","Zhè/Nà + shì + Noun; Nǐ shì nǎ + Noun":"Zhè/Nà + shì + Noun; Nǐ shì nǎ + Noun","'這' points to something near the speaker, '那' to something far, and '哪' asks 'which'. '哪' is not used alone — it needs a measure word or noun (wrong: 哪是你的?; correct: 哪一個是你的?).":"'這' menunjuk pada sesuatu yang dekat dengan pembicara, '那' pada sesuatu yang jauh, dan '哪' digunakan untuk bertanya 'yang mana'. '哪' tidak digunakan sendirian — perlu kata penggolong atau kata benda (salah: 哪是你的?; benar: 哪一個是你的?).","What country are you from?":"Anda berasal dari negara mana?","what (interrogative pronoun)":"apa (kata ganti tanya)","Verb + shénme":"Verb + shénme","\"Shénme\" stays in the same position as the noun it asks about — Chinese does not move it to the front like English \"what.\" Word order matches a statement, e.g. \"你愛吃什麼？\"":"\"Shénme\" tetap berada di posisi yang sama dengan kata benda yang ditanyakannya — bahasa Mandarin tidak memindahkannya ke depan kalimat seperti \"what\" dalam bahasa Inggris. Urutan katanya sama seperti kalimat pernyataan, misalnya \"你愛吃什麼？\"","What do you like to eat?":"Kamu suka makan apa?","What would you like to drink?":"Kamu ingin minum apa?","yes/no question particle":"partikel tanya ya/tidak","Statement + ma?":"Pernyataan + ma?","Adding \"ma\" to the end of a statement turns it into a yes/no question — no inversion needed. Don't combine \"ma\" with question words like \"shénme\" or \"wèishénme,\" which already form a question.":"Menambahkan \"ma\" di akhir kalimat pernyataan mengubahnya menjadi pertanyaan ya/tidak — tanpa perlu pembalikan kata. Jangan gabungkan \"ma\" dengan kata tanya seperti \"shénme\" atau \"wèishénme,\" yang sudah membentuk pertanyaan dengan sendirinya.","Do you like drinking coffee?":"Apakah kamu suka minum kopi?","Are you a teacher?":"Apakah kamu seorang guru?","to be located at":"berada di","Subject + zài + place":"Subjek + zài + tempat","Here \"zài\" is a verb meaning \"to be located at,\" placed right after the subject. Don't confuse it with the progressive marker \"zài + verb,\" which is a different grammar point.":"Di sini \"zài\" adalah kata kerja yang berarti \"berada di,\" diletakkan tepat setelah subjek. Jangan bingung dengan penanda progresif \"zài + kata kerja,\" yang merupakan poin tata bahasa yang berbeda.","He is at school.":"Dia sedang di sekolah.","Mom is at home.":"Ibu sedang di rumah.","address order: large unit to small unit":"urutan alamat: dari unit besar ke unit kecil","Country/City + Road/Street + Number":"Negara/Kota + Jalan + Nomor","A Chinese address is written from the largest unit to the smallest (country → city → street → number) — the reverse of the English order, which starts with the smallest.":"Alamat dalam bahasa Mandarin ditulis dari unit terbesar ke terkecil (negara → kota → jalan → nomor) — kebalikan dari urutan bahasa Inggris, yang dimulai dari unit terkecil.","No. 123 Zhongshan North Road, Taichung, Taiwan":"No. 123 Jalan Zhongshan Utara, Taichung, Taiwan","No. 7, Section 5, Xinyi Road, Taipei City":"No. 7, Segmen 5, Jalan Xinyi, Kota Taipei","date order: year, then month, then day":"urutan tanggal: tahun, lalu bulan, lalu hari","Year + Month + Day":"Tahun + Bulan + Hari","Chinese dates go year → month → day, opposite of English month/day/year. The year is read digit by digit (e.g. \"一九九五\" = yī jiǔ jiǔ wǔ), not as one whole number.":"Tanggal dalam bahasa Mandarin mengikuti urutan tahun → bulan → hari, kebalikan dari bahasa Inggris yang berupa bulan/hari/tahun. Tahun dibaca digit demi digit (misalnya \"一九九五\" = yī jiǔ jiǔ wǔ), bukan sebagai satu angka utuh.","His birthday is June 13, 1995.":"Ulang tahunnya adalah 13 Juni 1995.","Today is September 24, 2026.":"Hari ini adalah 24 September 2026.","Number reading rules":"Aturan membaca angka","Insert 零 (líng) when a zero falls between digit places (108 = 一百零八); the last place can be dropped when context is clear (一百一 = 110)":"Sisipkan 零 (líng) ketika ada angka nol di antara digit (108 = 一百零八); digit terakhir bisa dihilangkan jika konteksnya sudah jelas (一百一 = 110)","Insert 零 whenever a zero falls between number places (108 = 一百零八). The last place can be dropped when context makes it clear (一百一 = 110). Don't confuse this with simple counting (一, 二, 三…).":"Sisipkan 零 setiap kali ada angka nol di antara digit angka (108 = 一百零八). Digit terakhir bisa dihilangkan jika konteksnya sudah jelas (一百一 = 110). Jangan bingung dengan cara menghitung angka biasa (一, 二, 三…).","This book has 108 pages in total.":"Buku ini memiliki total 108 halaman.","This jacket costs 110 dollars.":"Jaket ini seharga 110 dolar.","Number + measure word":"Angka + kata penggolong","Number + Measure word + Noun":"Angka + Kata penggolong + Kata benda","Chinese requires a measure word between the number and the noun (一本書, 一個人). Learners often default to 個 for everything, but each noun category has its own proper measure word.":"Bahasa Mandarin memerlukan kata penggolong di antara angka dan kata benda (一本書, 一個人). Pembelajar sering menggunakan 個 untuk semuanya secara default, padahal setiap kategori kata benda memiliki kata penggolong yang tepat sendiri.","one book, one person":"satu buku, satu orang","I'd like a cup of coffee.":"Saya ingin secangkir kopi.","Question word 'who'":"Kata tanya 'siapa'","誰 (who) stays exactly in the position of the person being asked about — as subject (誰 + verb…) or as object (…+ verb + 誰)":"誰 (siapa) tetap berada tepat di posisi orang yang ditanyakan — sebagai subjek (誰 + kata kerja…) atau sebagai objek (…+ kata kerja + 誰)","Unlike English 'who', 誰 is not fronted — it stays exactly where the answer would go. A common mistake is moving it to the front of the sentence.":"Berbeda dengan 'who' dalam bahasa Inggris, 誰 tidak diletakkan di awal kalimat — kata ini tetap berada di posisi yang sama seperti jawabannya nanti. Kesalahan umum adalah memindahkannya ke awal kalimat.","Who do you like?":"Anda suka siapa?","Who is your teacher?":"Siapa guru Anda?","Question word 'where'":"Kata tanya 'di mana'","Place + 在 + 哪裡/哪兒 (Where is Place?)":"Tempat + 在 + 哪裡/哪兒 (Di mana Tempat itu?)","In Taiwan 哪裡 is far more common than 哪兒 (a northern Mainland form). Keep 在 before the question word — don't drop it and say just 'X 哪裡?'":"Di Taiwan, 哪裡 jauh lebih umum digunakan daripada 哪兒 (bentuk dari Tiongkok bagian utara). Pertahankan 在 sebelum kata tanya — jangan menghilangkannya dan hanya mengatakan 'X 哪裡?'","Where is the post office?":"Di mana kantor pos?","Where is your house?":"Di mana rumah Anda?","Verb/Adj + 不 + same Verb/Adj (forms a yes/no question)":"Kata kerja/Kata sifat + 不 + Kata kerja/Kata sifat yang sama (membentuk pertanyaan ya/tidak)","A-not-A already forms a question, so never add 嗎 at the end (wrong: 你喜歡不喜歡喝咖啡嗎？). Two-syllable verbs like 喜歡 can be shortened to 喜不喜歡.":"Struktur A-tidak-A sudah membentuk pertanyaan dengan sendirinya, jadi jangan pernah menambahkan 嗎 di akhir kalimat (salah: 你喜歡不喜歡喝咖啡嗎？). Kata kerja dua suku kata seperti 喜歡 dapat disingkat menjadi 喜不喜歡.","Do you like to drink coffee?":"Apakah Anda suka minum kopi?","Modifying a noun with a stative verb + 的":"Memodifikasi kata benda dengan kata kerja statif + 的","Vs (+ 很) + 的 + N":"Vs (+ 很) + 的 + N","Vs (stative verbs) modify a noun with 的 in between, as in 'hěn hǎokàn de diànyǐng'. A common mistake is dropping 的 before the noun ('hěn hǎokàn diànyǐng'), which is ungrammatical.":"Vs (kata kerja statif) memodifikasi kata benda dengan 的 di antaranya, seperti pada 'hěn hǎokàn de diànyǐng'. Kesalahan umum adalah menghilangkan 的 sebelum kata benda ('hěn hǎokàn diànyǐng'), yang secara gramatikal salah.","This is a very good movie.":"Ini adalah film yang sangat bagus.","He is a very smart student.":"Dia adalah siswa yang sangat pintar.","Marks that an action has been completed":"Menandai bahwa suatu tindakan telah selesai","S + V + 了 + (Quantity) + O":"S + V + 了 + (Kuantitas) + O","了1 attaches right after the verb to mark that the action is completed, often with a past time word like 昨天. Note the negative form uses 沒(有) + V, not 不V了.":"了1 melekat tepat setelah kata kerja untuk menandai bahwa tindakan tersebut telah selesai, sering disertai kata waktu lampau seperti 昨天. Perhatikan bahwa bentuk negatifnya menggunakan 沒(有) + V, bukan 不V了.","I bought a lot of books yesterday.":"Kemarin saya membeli banyak buku.","He ate three bowls of rice last night.":"Tadi malam dia makan tiga mangkuk nasi.","Connects two nouns, meaning 'and'":"Menghubungkan dua kata benda, berarti 'dan'","N1 + 和 + N2":"N1 + 和 + N2","和1 is a conjunction that links two nouns or noun phrases, meaning 'and'. It cannot connect two verb phrases or clauses — use words like 然後 for that instead.":"和1 adalah kata sambung yang menghubungkan dua kata benda atau frasa nomina, berarti 'dan'. Kata ini tidak dapat menghubungkan dua frasa verba atau klausa — gunakan kata seperti 然後 untuk itu.","The snacks at this restaurant are great — both adults and children like them.":"Camilan di restoran ini enak sekali — baik orang dewasa maupun anak-anak menyukainya.","I'm going to watch a movie with my older sister.":"Saya akan menonton film bersama kakak perempuan saya.","Negates existence or possession: 'there is no...'":"Menegasikan keberadaan atau kepemilikan: 'tidak ada...'","(S) + 沒(有) + O":"(S) + 沒(有) + O","The negation of 有 is always 沒(有), never 不有 — 有 can be dropped, leaving just 沒. It covers both existence ('there is no park') and possession ('I have no money').":"Bentuk negasi dari 有 selalu 沒(有), tidak pernah 不有 — 有 dapat dihilangkan, hanya menyisakan 沒. Ini mencakup baik keberadaan ('tidak ada taman') maupun kepemilikan ('saya tidak punya uang').","There is no park near the library.":"Tidak ada taman di dekat perpustakaan.","There's no money in my wallet.":"Tidak ada uang di dompet saya.","Expresses a future possibility or prediction":"Menyatakan kemungkinan atau prediksi di masa depan","S + 會 + VP":"S + 會 + VP","會1 expresses a prediction or possibility about the future, often paired with time words like 明天/今年 or 可能. Don't confuse it with the other 會 that means a learned ability (e.g. 我會游泳).":"會1 menyatakan prediksi atau kemungkinan tentang masa depan, sering dipasangkan dengan kata waktu seperti 明天/今年 atau 可能. Jangan disamakan dengan 會 lainnya yang berarti kemampuan yang telah dipelajari (misalnya, 我會游泳).","Will you go abroad this year?":"Apakah kamu akan pergi ke luar negeri tahun ini?","It might rain tomorrow.":"Besok mungkin akan hujan.","Continuing action or state":"Tindakan atau keadaan yang sedang berlangsung","V + 著 (+ Object)":"V + 著 (+ Objek)","\"V著\" expresses a state or action that continues/persists, unlike \"了\" (completion) or \"在\" (an action in progress). \"戴著帽子\" describes the ongoing state of wearing a hat. Don't mistake 著 for a past-tense marker.":"\"V著\" menyatakan keadaan atau tindakan yang berlanjut/berlangsung terus, berbeda dengan \"了\" (penyelesaian) atau \"在\" (tindakan yang sedang berlangsung). \"戴著帽子\" menggambarkan keadaan sedang memakai topi. Jangan salah mengira 著 sebagai penanda bentuk lampau.","He is wearing a hat.":"Dia sedang memakai topi.","She is wearing red clothes.":"Dia sedang mengenakan baju merah.","Ordinal numbers (the ~th)":"Angka urutan (ke-~)","第 + Number + (Measure word/Noun)":"第 + Angka + (Kata penggolong/Kata benda)","Add \"第\" before a number to show sequence/order, unlike cardinal numbers used for counting quantity (一個, 兩次). \"第一\" = \"first,\" \"第二\" = \"second.\" Don't drop \"第\" when expressing order.":"Tambahkan \"第\" sebelum angka untuk menunjukkan urutan, berbeda dengan bilangan kardinal yang digunakan untuk menghitung jumlah (一個, 兩次). \"第一\" = \"pertama,\" \"第二\" = \"kedua.\" Jangan menghilangkan \"第\" saat menyatakan urutan.","This is my first time coming to Taiwan.":"Ini pertama kalinya saya datang ke Taiwan.","This is my second time taking the MRT.":"Ini kedua kalinya saya naik MRT.","If... (conditional)":"Jika... (kalimat kondisional)","如果 + condition, (就) + result":"如果 + kondisi, (就) + hasil","\"如果\" introduces a hypothetical condition, and the result clause often pairs with \"就.\" It is similar to \"要是\" but slightly more formal/written. A common mistake is dropping \"如果\" and keeping only \"就.\"":"\"如果\" memperkenalkan kondisi hipotetis, dan klausa hasil sering dipasangkan dengan \"就.\" Ini mirip dengan \"要是\" tetapi sedikit lebih formal/tertulis. Kesalahan umum adalah menghilangkan \"如果\" dan hanya menyisakan \"就.\"","If it rains, I won't go out.":"Jika hujan, saya tidak akan keluar.","If you're free, let's go watch a movie together.":"Kalau kamu senggang, ayo kita nonton film bersama.","Permission (may/can)":"Izin (boleh/dapat)","(不) + 可以 + V":"(不) + 可以 + V","\"可以\" is an auxiliary verb expressing permission; \"不可以\" expresses prohibition. Don't confuse it with \"會\" (learned ability) or \"能\" (capability/condition) — \"可以\" mainly conveys permission or what is allowed.":"\"可以\" adalah kata kerja bantu yang menyatakan izin; \"不可以\" menyatakan larangan. Jangan bingung dengan \"會\" (kemampuan yang dipelajari) atau \"能\" (kemampuan/kondisi) — \"可以\" terutama menyampaikan izin atau apa yang diperbolehkan.","You may not eat during class.":"Kamu tidak boleh makan selama pelajaran.","Can I take photos here?":"Bolehkah saya memotret di sini?","Must/need to (necessity)":"Harus/perlu (keharusan)","Subject + 要 + V":"Subjek + 要 + V","This \"要\" expresses necessity or obligation (\"must/need to\"), distinct from \"要1\" meaning \"want to.\" Context determines the reading — it's common in advice or reminders, e.g. \"要記得\" (must remember to).":"\"要\" di sini menyatakan keharusan atau kewajiban (\"harus/perlu\"), berbeda dengan \"要1\" yang berarti \"ingin.\" Konteks menentukan maknanya — sering muncul dalam nasihat atau pengingat, misalnya \"要記得\" (harus ingat).","You must remember to call Teacher Wang.":"Kamu harus ingat menelepon Guru Wang.","You need to be careful crossing the street.":"Kamu perlu berhati-hati saat menyeberang jalan.","be going to / plan to (intention)":"akan / berencana (niat)","Subject + yào + VP (+ ma)?":"Subjek + yào + Frasa Verba (+ ma)?","Yào + verb expresses intention or an invitation to do something. Unlike yào1 (need) or yào2 (want + noun), yào3 is followed by a verb phrase, and 'yào bu yào' is a common way to invite someone.":"Yào + kata kerja mengungkapkan niat atau ajakan untuk melakukan sesuatu. Berbeda dengan yào1 (butuh) atau yào2 (ingin + kata benda), yào3 diikuti oleh frasa verba, dan 'yào bu yào' adalah cara umum untuk mengajak seseorang.","Are you going to eat together today?":"Apakah kamu berencana makan bersama hari ini?","Are you going to go to the night market with me tomorrow?":"Apakah besok kamu berencana pergi ke pasar malam bersamaku?","duration complement (how long an action lasts)":"pelengkap durasi (berapa lama suatu tindakan berlangsung)","Verb (+ Object) + duration + (le)":"Kata kerja (+ Objek) + durasi + (le)","Place a duration of time after the verb to show how long an action lasts. A point in time goes before the verb, but a duration goes after it — a common mix-up. When there's an object, the verb is often repeated or the object is dropped.":"Letakkan durasi waktu setelah kata kerja untuk menunjukkan berapa lama suatu tindakan berlangsung. Titik waktu diletakkan sebelum kata kerja, sedangkan durasi diletakkan setelahnya — ini sering tertukar. Jika ada objek, kata kerja biasanya diulang atau objeknya dihilangkan.","He has already been in Taiwan for one month.":"Dia sudah berada di Taiwan selama satu bulan.","I have lived in Taipei for three years.":"Saya sudah tinggal di Taipei selama tiga tahun.","but / however (contrast)":"tetapi / namun (kontras)","A, dànshì + B":"A, dànshì + B","Dànshì links two clauses in contrast; the first clause doesn't need 雖然 for dànshì to work on its own. It's close in meaning to kěshì, but dànshì sounds slightly more formal/written.":"Dànshì menghubungkan dua klausa yang berlawanan; klausa pertama tidak perlu menggunakan 雖然 agar dànshì bisa berdiri sendiri. Maknanya dekat dengan kěshì, tetapi dànshì terdengar sedikit lebih formal/tertulis.","This box is big, but the things inside are light.":"Kotak ini besar, tetapi isinya ringan.","I really want to go, but I don't have time.":"Saya sangat ingin pergi, tetapi saya tidak punya waktu.","can (capacity/condition)":"bisa (kapasitas/kondisi)","Subject + néng + VP":"Subjek + néng + Frasa Verba","Néng expresses being able to do something because of conditions or capacity. It's easy to confuse with huì (a learned skill) or kěyǐ (permission), but néng1 focuses on physical/objective conditions.":"Néng mengungkapkan kemampuan melakukan sesuatu karena kondisi atau kapasitas. Kata ini mudah tertukar dengan huì (keterampilan yang dipelajari) atau kěyǐ (izin), tetapi néng1 berfokus pada kondisi fisik/objektif.","His car can seat seven people.":"Mobilnya bisa memuat tujuh orang.","This elevator can hold ten people.":"Lift ini bisa menampung sepuluh orang.","have done ... before (experience)":"pernah melakukan ... (pengalaman)","V + guò (+ Object)":"Kata kerja + guò (+ Objek)","Guò marks past experience ('have done X before') and attaches right after the verb. Unlike le (completion), guò focuses on whether the experience ever happened; negate with méi(yǒu) + V + guò.":"Guò menandakan pengalaman di masa lalu ('pernah melakukan X') dan diletakkan tepat setelah kata kerja. Berbeda dengan le (penyelesaian), guò berfokus pada apakah pengalaman itu pernah terjadi; bentuk negatifnya adalah méi(yǒu) + Kata kerja + guò.","I have watched this movie before.":"Saya pernah menonton film ini.","I have eaten stinky tofu before.":"Saya pernah makan tahu busuk.","as soon as / then":"begitu / lalu","A + jiù + B":"A + jiù + B","\"就\" links two events, showing B happens right after A with no delay — like \"as soon as.\" Contrast with \"才,\" which implies lateness or difficulty.":"\"就\" menghubungkan dua peristiwa, menunjukkan B terjadi tepat setelah A tanpa jeda — seperti \"begitu\". Berbeda dengan \"才\", yang menyiratkan keterlambatan atau kesulitan.","Call me as soon as you get home.":"Begitu sampai rumah, langsung telepon saya.","Go take a shower as soon as you finish eating.":"Begitu selesai makan, langsung mandi.","the ~ one (noun omitted)":"yang ~ (kata benda dihilangkan)","Adj + de":"Kata sifat + de","When the noun after \"的\" is clear from context, it can be dropped — \"藍的\" stands in for \"藍色的外套.\" Only works when the referent was already mentioned.":"Ketika kata benda setelah \"的\" sudah jelas dari konteks, kata itu bisa dihilangkan — \"藍的\" mewakili \"藍色的外套.\" Hanya berlaku jika rujukannya sudah disebutkan sebelumnya.","I like the blue one.":"Saya suka yang biru.","This one is too expensive, I want the cheap one.":"Yang ini terlalu mahal, saya mau yang murah.","huì + bù + huì + V?":"huì + bù + huì + V?","\"會\" here expresses a learned/acquired skill (like driving or playing an instrument). Don't confuse it with \"能\" (situational ability) or \"可以\" (permission).":"\"會\" di sini menyatakan keterampilan yang dipelajari/diperoleh (seperti mengemudi atau bermain alat musik). Jangan disamakan dengan \"能\" (kemampuan situasional) atau \"可以\" (izin).","Can you drive a car?":"Kamu bisa mengemudi mobil?","My older sister can play the piano, but I can't.":"Kakak perempuan saya bisa main piano, tapi saya tidak bisa.","can (situational ability)":"bisa (kemampuan situasional)","bù néng + V":"bù néng + V","\"能\" expresses ability/possibility due to physical condition or circumstances (e.g., being sick). Unlike \"會\" (learned skill), it often implies a temporary restriction.":"\"能\" menyatakan kemampuan/kemungkinan karena kondisi fisik atau keadaan (misalnya sedang sakit). Berbeda dengan \"會\" (keterampilan yang dipelajari), kata ini sering menyiratkan keterbatasan sementara.","He has a cold, so he can't exercise today.":"Dia sedang pilek, jadi hari ini tidak bisa berolahraga.","I hurt my foot, so I can't walk.":"Kaki saya terluka, jadi saya tidak bisa berjalan.","about to (do)":"akan segera (melakukan)","yào + V + le":"yào + V + le","\"要...了\" indicates an imminent action (\"about to happen\"), different from the volitional \"要\" meaning \"want to.\" The \"了\" is essential here.":"\"要...了\" menunjukkan tindakan yang akan segera terjadi (\"hampir terjadi\"), berbeda dengan \"要\" bermakna kehendak yaitu \"ingin.\" \"了\" di sini sangat penting.","I'm about to go out, so if you have something to say, say it quickly.":"Saya akan segera keluar, jadi kalau ada yang mau dikatakan, cepat katakan.","The movie is about to start, let's go in quickly.":"Filmnya akan segera mulai, ayo cepat masuk.","be done to (passive)":"dikenai tindakan (pasif)","Object/Patient + 被 (+ Agent) + Verb":"Objek/Penerima tindakan + 被 (+ Pelaku) + Kata kerja","The 被 passive puts the affected object/person as subject: Subject + 被 (+ agent) + Verb, often with a resultative ending (了, 破, etc.). Don't confuse it with the 把 construction, which keeps the original subject and moves the object before the verb instead.":"Pasif dengan \"被\" menjadikan objek/orang yang terkena dampak sebagai subjek: Subjek + 被 (+ pelaku) + Kata kerja, sering disertai penanda hasil (了, 破, dll.). Jangan disamakan dengan struktur \"把\", yang mempertahankan subjek asli dan memindahkan objek ke depan kata kerja.","The box was opened.":"Kotaknya sudah dibuka.","The window was broken.":"Jendelanya sudah pecah.","verb + result (stative verb complement)":"kata kerja + hasil (pelengkap kata kerja statif)","V + Vs (+ 了/嗎)":"V + Vs (+ 了/嗎)","Attach a stative verb (飽, 完, 懂, 好, etc.) right after the main verb to show the result the action achieved, not just that the action happened. Negate with 沒 + V + Vs, never with 不, since it describes a completed result.":"Tempelkan kata kerja statif (飽, 完, 懂, 好, dll.) tepat setelah kata kerja utama untuk menunjukkan hasil yang dicapai tindakan tersebut, bukan sekadar bahwa tindakan itu terjadi. Negasikan dengan 沒 + V + Vs, jangan pernah dengan 不, karena ini menggambarkan hasil yang sudah selesai.","Are you full? (Have you had enough to eat?)":"Kamu sudah kenyang? (Sudah makan cukup?)","I finished my homework.":"Saya sudah menyelesaikan pekerjaan rumah saya.","to/with (target of an action)":"kepada/dengan (sasaran suatu tindakan)","A + 跟 + B + 說/借/商量…":"A + 跟 + B + 說/借/商量…","Here 跟 introduces the person a communicative or transactional action is directed at: 跟 + person + 說/借/商量. This differs from the accompaniment sense of 跟 (跟...一起), which marks a companion rather than a target.":"Di sini, 跟 memperkenalkan orang yang menjadi sasaran suatu tindakan komunikatif atau transaksional: 跟 + orang + 說/借/商量. Ini berbeda dengan makna kebersamaan dari 跟 (跟...一起), yang menandai teman yang menyertai, bukan sasaran tindakan.","He told me a very interesting story.":"Dia menceritakan kepada saya sebuah cerita yang sangat menarik.","Mom borrowed NT$200 from me.":"Ibu meminjam NT$200 dari saya.","want to":"ingin","S + 想 + Verb (Phrase)":"S + 想 + Verb (Phrase)","想 is a modal verb meaning 'want to / would like to,' used as 想 + verb (phrase). It sounds softer and less decisive than 要. Negate with 不想, not 沒想.":"想 adalah kata kerja modal yang berarti 'ingin', digunakan dalam pola 想 + kata kerja (frasa). Kesannya lebih lembut dan kurang tegas dibandingkan 要. Bentuk negatifnya adalah 不想, bukan 沒想.","My little sister wants to eat ice cream.":"Adik perempuan saya ingin makan es krim.","I want to drink bubble milk tea.":"Saya ingin minum teh susu boba.","with (someone)":"dengan (seseorang)","A + 和 + B + Verb":"A + 和 + B + Verb","Here 和 works like 跟 (accompaniment 'with'): A + 和 + B + verb, naming the person one does something together with. Don't confuse it with the conjunction 和 that simply links two nouns ('A and B').":"Di sini, 和 berfungsi seperti 跟 (makna kebersamaan 'dengan'): A + 和 + B + kata kerja, menyebutkan orang yang diajak melakukan sesuatu bersama. Jangan bingungkan dengan kata sambung 和 yang hanya menghubungkan dua kata benda ('A dan B').","My little sister loves chatting with Dad.":"Adik perempuan saya suka sekali mengobrol dengan Ayah.","My little brother often plays basketball with friends.":"Adik laki-laki saya sering bermain basket dengan teman-teman.","from (a place of origin)":"dari (tempat asal)","Subject + 從 + place + verb":"Subject + 從 + place + verb","\"從\" marks the starting point (place or time) of an action and must be followed by a place/time word. Don't confuse it with \"到\", which marks the destination.":"\"從\" menandai titik awal (tempat atau waktu) suatu tindakan dan harus diikuti oleh kata yang menyatakan tempat/waktu. Jangan bingungkan dengan \"到\", yang menandai titik tujuan.","I come from France.":"Saya berasal dari Prancis.","She comes from the United States, and I come from Japan.":"Dia berasal dari Amerika Serikat, dan saya berasal dari Jepang.","using (a tool or means)":"menggunakan (alat atau sarana)","Subject + 用 + tool + verb":"Subject + 用 + tool + verb","\"用\" introduces the tool or means used to do an action; the \"用 + noun\" phrase goes before the main verb. Don't confuse it with \"跟\" (with, marking a person).":"\"用\" memperkenalkan alat atau sarana yang digunakan untuk melakukan suatu tindakan; frasa \"用 + kata benda\" diletakkan sebelum kata kerja utama. Jangan bingungkan dengan \"跟\" (dengan, menandai seseorang).","He can eat with chopsticks.":"Dia bisa makan menggunakan sumpit.","I call my mom using my cellphone.":"Saya menelepon ibu saya menggunakan ponsel.","progressive aspect: to be doing something":"aspek progresif: sedang melakukan sesuatu","Subject + (zhèng)zài + verb":"Subject + (zhèng)zài + verb","\"(正)在 + verb\" expresses an action happening right now, and \"呢\" can be added at the end. To negate it, use \"沒(有)\", not \"不\".":"\"(正)在 + kata kerja\" menyatakan suatu tindakan yang sedang berlangsung saat ini, dan \"呢\" dapat ditambahkan di akhir kalimat. Untuk menegasikannya, gunakan \"沒(有)\", bukan \"不\".","The students are playing soccer.":"Para siswa sedang bermain sepak bola.","Dad is washing the car.":"Ayah sedang mencuci mobil.","question particle: \"what about...?\"":"partikel tanya: \"bagaimana dengan...?\"","Noun/pronoun + 呢?":"Kata benda/kata ganti + 呢?","\"呢\" forms an elliptical question meaning \"what about...?\" that refers back to something already said. Unlike \"嗎\" (yes/no questions), it can't stand alone without prior context.":"\"呢\" membentuk pertanyaan elipsis yang berarti \"bagaimana dengan...?\", merujuk kembali pada sesuatu yang sudah disebutkan sebelumnya. Berbeda dengan \"嗎\" (pertanyaan ya/tidak), kata ini tidak bisa berdiri sendiri tanpa konteks sebelumnya.","He's German, what about you?":"Dia orang Jerman, bagaimana dengan kamu?","I want to drink milk tea, what about you?":"Saya mau minum teh susu, bagaimana dengan kamu?","although..., but... (concessive)":"meskipun..., tetapi... (konsesif)","(Suīrán) + A, kěshì + B":"(Suīrán) + A, kěshì + B","\"雖然\" can be omitted, but \"可是\" cannot; the first clause concedes a fact and the second contrasts it. The concessive clause always comes first, fixed word order.":"\"雖然\" boleh dihilangkan, tetapi \"可是\" tidak boleh; klausa pertama mengakui suatu fakta dan klausa kedua mengontraskannya. Klausa konsesif selalu berada di depan, urutan katanya tetap.","Although he isn't very rich, he is very happy.":"Meskipun dia tidak terlalu kaya, dia sangat bahagia.","Although it's raining, we're still going hiking.":"Meskipun sedang hujan, kami tetap pergi mendaki.","pluralizes nouns/pronouns referring to people":"membentuk jamak untuk kata benda/kata ganti yang merujuk pada orang","N (person) + 們":"N (orang) + 們","\"們\" attaches to nouns/pronouns referring to people to mark plural. Not used with objects/animals (×蘋果們), nor together with a specific number (×三個人們).":"\"們\" ditambahkan pada kata benda/kata ganti yang merujuk pada orang untuk menandai bentuk jamak. Tidak digunakan pada benda/hewan (×蘋果們), maupun bersama dengan angka tertentu (×三個人們).","The children are all playing outside.":"Anak-anak semuanya sedang bermain di luar.","The students are all doing homework in the classroom.":"Para siswa semuanya sedang mengerjakan pekerjaan rumah di kelas.","to begin doing an action":"mulai melakukan suatu tindakan","(Time/Subject) + 開始 (start) + V":"(Waktu/Subjek) + 開始 (mulai) + V","\"開始\" is followed by a verb (phrase) to mean \"start to...\". Time expressions go before 開始. 開始 can also stand alone as a verb (e.g. 電影開始了 \"the movie has started\").":"\"開始\" diikuti oleh kata kerja (frasa) yang berarti \"mulai...\". Keterangan waktu diletakkan sebelum 開始. 開始 juga dapat berdiri sendiri sebagai kata kerja (misalnya 電影開始了 \"filmnya sudah mulai\").","We start class at ten o'clock.":"Kami mulai kelas pukul sepuluh.","I start work at seven in the morning.":"Saya mulai bekerja pukul tujuh pagi.","asking how/by what means":"menanyakan cara/dengan cara apa","(Subject) + 怎麼 (how) + V":"(Subjek) + 怎麼 (bagaimana) + V","\"怎麼\" precedes a verb to ask about method/means (\"how\"). Easy to confuse with \"為什麼\" (why, asking for a reason). Also distinct from \"怎麼樣\" (how is it, asking about condition/manner).":"\"怎麼\" diletakkan sebelum kata kerja untuk menanyakan metode/cara (\"bagaimana\"). Mudah tertukar dengan \"為什麼\" (mengapa, menanyakan alasan). Juga berbeda dari \"怎麼樣\" (bagaimana keadaannya, menanyakan kondisi/cara).","How do I get from here to the station?":"Bagaimana cara saya pergi dari sini ke stasiun?","How do you write this character?":"Bagaimana cara menulis karakter ini?","expressing ability/possibility (\"can\")":"mengungkapkan kemampuan/kemungkinan (\"bisa\")","Subject + 可以 (can) + V":"Subjek + 可以 (bisa) + V","Here \"可以\" doesn't mean permission (\"may\") but ability or whether circumstances allow it (\"can\"). Note that in this sense the negative usually uses \"不能\" rather than \"不可以\".":"Di sini \"可以\" tidak berarti izin (\"boleh\") melainkan kemampuan atau apakah keadaan memungkinkan (\"bisa\"). Perlu diperhatikan bahwa dalam makna ini, bentuk negatifnya biasanya menggunakan \"不能\", bukan \"不可以\".","Can you read and understand a Chinese menu?":"Bisakah kamu membaca dan memahami menu berbahasa Mandarin?","She can ride a bike to school by herself.":"Dia bisa naik sepeda ke sekolah sendirian.","asking for a reason (\"why\")":"menanyakan alasan (\"mengapa\")","(Subject) + 為什麼 (why) + VP?":"(Subjek) + 為什麼 (mengapa) + VP?","\"為什麼\" is a question word asking for a reason (\"why\") and can appear before or after the subject. Don't confuse it with \"怎麼\" (asking how/method) — 為什麼 = why, 怎麼 = how.":"\"為什麼\" adalah kata tanya untuk menanyakan alasan (\"mengapa\") dan bisa muncul sebelum atau sesudah subjek. Jangan disamakan dengan \"怎麼\" (menanyakan cara/metode) — 為什麼 = mengapa, 怎麼 = bagaimana.","Why can't you eat your food?":"Mengapa kamu tidak bisa makan makananmu?","Why didn't you answer the phone?":"Mengapa kamu tidak menjawab telepon?","to give (double object)":"memberi (objek ganda)","A + 給 + Recipient + Thing":"A + 給 + Penerima + Benda","\"給\" takes two objects: 給 + recipient + thing given. English speakers sometimes put the thing before the person; Mandarin fixes the order as 給+person+thing.":"\"給\" mengambil dua objek: 給 + penerima + benda yang diberikan. Penutur bahasa Inggris terkadang meletakkan benda sebelum orangnya; bahasa Mandarin menetapkan urutannya sebagai 給+orang+benda.","He gave me a book.":"Dia memberi saya sebuah buku.","I gave him a cup of coffee.":"Saya memberinya secangkir kopi.","see/hear successfully (resultative)":"melihat/mendengar dengan berhasil (komplemen hasil)","V (看/聽/遇...) + 見":"V (看/聽/遇...) + 見","\"見\" attaches to perception verbs (看/聽/遇) as a resultative complement marking that perception actually succeeded. \"看\" alone only describes the action of looking, while \"看見\" confirms something was actually seen.":"\"見\" melekat pada kata kerja persepsi (看/聽/遇) sebagai komplemen hasil yang menandakan bahwa persepsi itu benar-benar berhasil. \"看\" saja hanya menggambarkan tindakan melihat, sedangkan \"看見\" memastikan bahwa sesuatu benar-benar terlihat.","I saw Li Minghua's bicycle downstairs.":"Saya melihat sepeda Li Minghua di lantai bawah.","I heard his voice at the MRT station.":"Saya mendengar suaranya di stasiun MRT.","change of state":"perubahan keadaan","VP + 了 (change of state)":"VP + 了 (perubahan keadaan)","Sentence-final \"了\" (了2) signals a new state that differs from before, not completion of an action. It's easy to confuse with the verb-suffix \"了1\" (completion), but 了2 sits at the end and marks a change of state.":"\"了\" di akhir kalimat (了2) menandakan keadaan baru yang berbeda dari sebelumnya, bukan penyelesaian suatu tindakan. Ini mudah tertukar dengan akhiran kata kerja \"了1\" (penyelesaian), tetapi 了2 berada di akhir kalimat dan menandai perubahan keadaan.","The weather has changed.":"Cuacanya sudah berubah.","My younger brother has grown taller.":"Adik laki-laki saya sudah tambah tinggi.","please don't (negative command)":"tolong jangan (kalimat perintah negatif)","(請) + 不要 + VP":"(請) + 不要 + VP","\"不要\" forms a negative command (\"don't...\"); adding \"請\" in front softens it into a polite request or notice. \"不要\" and \"別\" are near-synonyms, but \"別\" feels more direct/colloquial while \"請不要\" is polite enough for written notices.":"\"不要\" membentuk perintah negatif (\"jangan...\"); menambahkan \"請\" di depannya membuatnya lebih halus menjadi permintaan atau pemberitahuan yang sopan. \"不要\" dan \"別\" hampir bersinonim, tetapi \"別\" terasa lebih langsung/kolokial sedangkan \"請不要\" cukup sopan untuk digunakan pada pemberitahuan tertulis.","Please don't talk!":"Tolong jangan bicara!","Please don't eat in the library.":"Tolong jangan makan di perpustakaan.","approximately (-odd)":"kira-kira (lebih dari...)","Round number (十/二十...) + 幾 + Measure + N":"Bilangan bulat (十/二十...) + 幾 + Kata bantu bilangan + N","Here \"幾\" attaches after a round number (十幾, 二十幾) to mean \"-odd\"/\"more than X\", an approximate quantity — not the interrogative \"幾\" (\"how many?\"). Learners sometimes mistake it for a question.":"Di sini \"幾\" melekat setelah bilangan bulat (十幾, 二十幾) untuk menyatakan makna \"lebih dari...\"/\"lebih dari X\", suatu jumlah perkiraan — bukan \"幾\" yang bersifat tanya (\"berapa?\"). Pelajar terkadang salah mengiranya sebagai pertanyaan.","There are more than ten restaurants on this street.":"Di jalan ini ada lebih dari sepuluh restoran.","There are more than thirty books in his room.":"Ada lebih dari tiga puluh buku di kamarnya.","please":"tolong, silakan","Qǐng + (person) + Verb":"Qǐng + (orang) + Kata kerja","\"請\" softens a request or command and is placed before the verb or the addressee. Common mistake: confusing it with \"請問,\" which is used specifically to ask a question politely, not to request an action.":"\"請\" melembutkan sebuah permintaan atau perintah dan diletakkan sebelum kata kerja atau sebelum orang yang dituju. Kesalahan umum: mengira sama dengan \"請問\", yang secara khusus digunakan untuk bertanya dengan sopan, bukan untuk meminta suatu tindakan.","Please come over here.":"Silakan ke sini.","Please be a bit quieter.":"Tolong sedikit lebih tenang.","do X in a ... way":"melakukan X dengan cara ...","(V+O+) V + 得 + Complement":"(V+O+) V + 得 + Pelengkap","\"V得+complement\" describes how an action is done or its result; when there's an object, the verb repeats (V+O+V得+complement). Common mistake: confusing this 得 (de) with 的 (de) or 地 (de), which sound alike but have different grammatical roles.":"\"V得+pelengkap\" menjelaskan bagaimana suatu tindakan dilakukan atau hasilnya; jika ada objek, kata kerjanya diulang (V+O+V得+pelengkap). Kesalahan umum: mengacaukan 得 (de) ini dengan 的 (de) atau 地 (de), yang bunyinya sama tetapi memiliki peran tata bahasa berbeda.","Wang Meimei's Chinese characters are written very beautifully.":"Karakter Tionghoa tulisan Wang Meimei sangat indah.","He speaks Chinese very fluently.":"Dia berbicara bahasa Mandarin dengan sangat lancar.","to help / do something for someone":"membantu / melakukan sesuatu untuk seseorang","Bāng + Person + Verb":"Bāng + Orang + Kata kerja","\"幫\" means to do something for/help someone, in the pattern 幫+person+verb. Common mistake: placing 幫 after the verb (following English \"help me do X\" order) instead of before the person.":"\"幫\" berarti melakukan sesuatu untuk/membantu seseorang, dengan pola 幫+orang+kata kerja. Kesalahan umum: meletakkan 幫 setelah kata kerja (mengikuti urutan bahasa Inggris \"help me do X\") alih-alih sebelum orangnya.","Could you go to the post office and mail a letter for me?":"Bisakah kamu pergi ke kantor pos dan mengirimkan surat untukku?","Could you grab that book for me?":"Bisakah kamu ambilkan buku itu untukku?","before / in the past":"sebelumnya / di masa lalu","yǐqián / V + yǐqián":"yǐqián / V + yǐqián","\"以前\" means \"before/in the past.\" It can stand alone as a time word, or follow a clause as \"before doing X\" (V+以前). Common mistake: mixing it up with its opposite, 以後 (\"after\").":"\"以前\" berarti \"sebelumnya/di masa lalu\". Kata ini bisa berdiri sendiri sebagai kata keterangan waktu, atau mengikuti sebuah klausa dengan arti \"sebelum melakukan X\" (V+以前). Kesalahan umum: tertukar dengan lawan katanya, 以後 (\"setelah\").","I used to work at a hospital.":"Dulu saya bekerja di rumah sakit.","I didn't use to like coffee, but now I like it a lot.":"Dulu saya tidak suka kopi, tapi sekarang saya sangat menyukainya.","out (directional complement)":"keluar (pelengkap arah)","V + 出 + (place/object)":"V + 出 + (tempat/objek)","\"V出 + place\" shows movement from inside to outside a location, without needing \"從\" before the place. Common mistake: adding \"從\" redundantly, or confusing plain \"出\" with \"出來,\" which adds a viewpoint toward the speaker.":"\"V出 + tempat\" menunjukkan pergerakan dari dalam ke luar suatu tempat, tanpa perlu \"從\" sebelum tempat tersebut. Kesalahan umum: menambahkan \"從\" secara berlebihan, atau mengacaukan \"出\" biasa dengan \"出來\", yang menambahkan sudut pandang ke arah pembicara.","As soon as Wang Meimei walked out of the restaurant, she saw her roommate.":"Begitu Wang Meimei keluar dari restoran, dia melihat teman sekamarnya.","He walked out of the classroom to go buy a drink.":"Dia keluar dari ruang kelas untuk membeli minuman.","do more/less of something":"melakukan sesuatu lebih banyak/lebih sedikit","duō/shǎo + Verb (+ yìdiǎn/quantity)":"duō/shǎo + Kata kerja (+ yìdiǎn/jumlah)","\"Duō/shǎo\" go before the verb to mean \"do more/less of it.\" A common mistake is placing them after the verb (×吃多); \"yìdiǎn\" usually follows the verb instead.":"\"Duō/shǎo\" diletakkan sebelum kata kerja untuk berarti \"melakukannya lebih banyak/lebih sedikit\". Kesalahan umum adalah meletakkannya setelah kata kerja (×吃多); sebagai gantinya \"yìdiǎn\" biasanya mengikuti kata kerja.","You can eat a bit more fruit.":"Kamu bisa makan sedikit lebih banyak buah.","You should eat less sweets.":"Kamu sebaiknya makan lebih sedikit makanan manis.","also / too":"juga","A + yě + Verb/Adjective":"A + yě + Kata kerja/Kata sifat","\"Yě\" (\"also/too\") goes right before the verb, not at the end of the sentence like English \"too\" (avoid ×...日文也). Don't confuse it with \"dōu\" (\"all/both\").":"\"Yě\" (\"juga\") diletakkan tepat sebelum kata kerja, bukan di akhir kalimat seperti \"too\" dalam bahasa Inggris (hindari ×...日文也). Jangan bingung dengan \"dōu\" (\"semua/kedua-duanya\").","He can speak Chinese, and he can also speak Japanese.":"Dia bisa berbicara bahasa Mandarin, dan dia juga bisa berbicara bahasa Jepang.","I like drinking coffee, and I also like drinking tea.":"Saya suka minum kopi, dan saya juga suka minum teh.","at the time of / during":"pada saat / selama","zài + time/occasion + de shíhòu":"zài + waktu/kesempatan + de shíhòu","\"Zài + time/occasion + de shíhòu\" means \"at the time of / when.\" Don't confuse it with \"zài\" for location (zài jiā) or ongoing action (zài chīfàn). A common mistake is dropping \"de shíhòu.\"":"\"Zài + waktu/kesempatan + de shíhòu\" berarti \"pada saat / ketika.\" Jangan bingung dengan \"zài\" untuk lokasi (zài jiā) atau tindakan yang sedang berlangsung (zài chīfàn). Kesalahan umum adalah menghilangkan \"de shíhòu.\"","He goes to the United States at Christmas.":"Dia pergi ke Amerika Serikat saat Natal.","He goes on a trip to Japan during his vacation.":"Dia pergi berlibur ke Jepang selama masa liburannya.","after":"setelah","Action/time + yǐhòu, …":"Tindakan/waktu + yǐhòu, …","\"Yǐhòu\" follows a verb phrase or time word to mean \"after that.\" Unlike \"hòulái\" (afterwards), which can stand alone, \"yǐhòu\" needs a preceding action or time as its anchor. Remember its opposite, \"yǐqián\" (before).":"\"Yǐhòu\" mengikuti frasa kata kerja atau kata waktu dan berarti \"setelah itu.\" Berbeda dengan \"hòulái\" (kemudian), yang bisa berdiri sendiri, \"yǐhòu\" membutuhkan tindakan atau waktu sebelumnya sebagai acuan. Ingat lawan katanya, \"yǐqián\" (sebelum).","After finishing breakfast, he went to school.":"Setelah selesai sarapan, dia pergi ke sekolah.","After class, I'm going to go buy a drink at the convenience store.":"Setelah kelas selesai, saya akan pergi membeli minuman di toko serba ada.","how / what... like":"bagaimana / seperti apa","Subject + (state/situation) + zěnmeyàng?":"Subjek + (keadaan/situasi) + zěnmeyàng?","\"Zěnmeyàng\" goes at the end of a sentence to ask for an opinion or description of a state. Don't confuse it with \"zěnme\" (how, asking about method), which goes before the verb (e.g., zěnme qù?).":"\"Zěnmeyàng\" diletakkan di akhir kalimat untuk menanyakan pendapat atau meminta deskripsi suatu keadaan. Jangan bingung dengan \"zěnme\" (bagaimana, menanyakan cara), yang diletakkan sebelum kata kerja (misalnya, zěnme qù?).","What do you think of this restaurant?":"Menurutmu restoran ini bagaimana?","Asking \"how many/how much\" with 幾 or 多少":"Menanyakan \"berapa\" dengan 幾 atau 多少","Jǐ + measure word / Duōshao + (measure word) + noun":"Jǐ + kata penggolong / Duōshao + (kata penggolong) + kata benda","\"Jǐ\" expects a small number (usually under 10) and needs a measure word after it; \"duōshao\" works for any quantity and the measure word is optional. Use \"duōshao qián\" for prices.":"\"Jǐ\" digunakan saat mengharapkan angka kecil (biasanya di bawah 10) dan memerlukan kata penggolong setelahnya; \"duōshao\" bisa digunakan untuk jumlah berapa pun dan kata penggolongnya opsional. Gunakan \"duōshao qián\" untuk menanyakan harga.","How many hours does it take to go from Taipei to Taichung by train?":"Berapa jam waktu yang dibutuhkan untuk pergi dari Taipei ke Taichung dengan kereta?","How much is this coffee?":"Kopi ini berapa harganya?","\"What should [I/we] do?\" — expressing a problem":"\"[Saya/kita] harus bagaimana?\" — mengungkapkan suatu masalah","(Subject) + problem statement, zěnme bàn?":"(Subjek) + pernyataan masalah, zěnme bàn?","\"Zěnme bàn\" is a fixed expression used alone when facing a problem, meaning \"what should I do?\" Unlike \"zěnme\" + verb (asking how to do something), it expresses worry or a request for help, not a method.":"\"Zěnme bàn\" adalah ungkapan tetap yang digunakan sendiri saat menghadapi suatu masalah, berarti \"apa yang harus saya lakukan?\" Berbeda dengan \"zěnme\" + kata kerja (menanyakan cara melakukan sesuatu), ungkapan ini menyatakan kekhawatiran atau permintaan bantuan, bukan cara.","I forgot to bring money today, what should I do?":"Hari ini saya lupa membawa uang, bagaimana ini?","My keys are missing, what should I do?":"Kunci saya hilang, bagaimana ini?","Preposition meaning \"with\" (accompaniment)":"Preposisi yang berarti \"bersama\" (menyertai)","A + gēn + B + (yìqǐ) + verb":"A + gēn + B + (yìqǐ) + verba","Here \"gēn\" is a preposition meaning \"with,\" often paired with \"yìqǐ\" (together). Don't confuse it with the conjunction \"gēn\" that simply links two nouns (A and B).":"Di sini \"gēn\" adalah preposisi yang berarti \"bersama\", sering dipasangkan dengan \"yìqǐ\" (bersama-sama). Jangan bingung dengan konjungsi \"gēn\" yang hanya menghubungkan dua kata benda (A dan B).","I go to the library with my older sister to borrow books.":"Saya pergi ke perpustakaan bersama kakak perempuan saya untuk meminjam buku.","I go to watch a movie with my classmate.":"Saya pergi menonton film bersama teman sekelas saya.","Polite phrase before a question, \"excuse me, may I ask...\"":"Ungkapan sopan sebelum pertanyaan, berarti \"permisi, boleh saya bertanya...\"","Qǐngwèn + question":"Qǐngwèn + pertanyaan","\"Qǐngwèn\" is a polite opener placed at the start of a question, typically used with strangers or in formal situations; it's rarely used in casual chats with friends.":"\"Qǐngwèn\" adalah pembuka sopan yang diletakkan di awal pertanyaan, biasanya digunakan dengan orang asing atau dalam situasi formal; jarang digunakan dalam obrolan santai dengan teman.","Excuse me, what is your name?":"Permisi, siapa nama Anda?","Tag question at the end of a sentence asking for agreement, \"...okay?\"":"Pertanyaan penegas di akhir kalimat untuk meminta persetujuan, berarti \"...oke?\"","Suggestion/request + hǎo ma?":"Saran/permintaan + hǎo ma?","\"Hǎo ma\" is added after a suggestion or request to ask for agreement, like an English tag question. Unlike a plain yes/no question with \"ma,\" it must follow a concrete proposal or request.":"\"Hǎo ma\" ditambahkan setelah saran atau permintaan untuk meminta persetujuan, seperti pertanyaan penegas dalam bahasa Inggris. Berbeda dengan pertanyaan ya/tidak biasa dengan \"ma\", ini harus mengikuti usulan atau permintaan yang konkret.","Please say it one more time, okay?":"Tolong katakan sekali lagi, oke?","Let's discuss it again tomorrow, okay?":"Besok kita bicarakan lagi, oke?","\"What's wrong with...?\" (asking what happened)":"\"...kenapa?\" (menanyakan apa yang terjadi)","person + zěnme le?":"orang + zěnme le?","\"Zěnme le\" asks what's wrong when something seems off, unlike \"zěnme yàng,\" which just asks for an opinion or how something turned out. Don't mix the two up.":"\"Zěnme le\" digunakan untuk menanyakan ada apa ketika sesuatu tampak tidak beres, berbeda dengan \"zěnme yàng\" yang hanya menanyakan pendapat atau bagaimana hasil sesuatu. Jangan sampai tertukar keduanya.","Li Minghua didn't come to work today. What happened to him?":"Li Minghua tidak masuk kerja hari ini. Ada apa dengannya?","You don't look so well. What's wrong?":"Kamu terlihat kurang sehat. Kenapa?","verb + dào/zài indicating the resulting location of an action":"verba + dào/zài yang menunjukkan lokasi hasil dari suatu tindakan","V + dào + place (+ qù/lái) / V + zài + place":"V + dào + tempat (+ qù/lái) / V + zài + tempat","\"V + dào + place\" shows movement reaching a destination (often followed by qù/lái), while \"V + zài + place\" shows the resulting static location of an action. A common mistake is swapping the two — using zài for movement or dào for a fixed location.":"\"V + dào + tempat\" menunjukkan pergerakan mencapai suatu tujuan (sering diikuti oleh qù/lái), sedangkan \"V + zài + tempat\" menunjukkan lokasi statis hasil dari suatu tindakan. Kesalahan umum adalah menukar keduanya — menggunakan zài untuk pergerakan atau dào untuk lokasi tetap.","Auntie walks over to the supermarket across the street to buy groceries.":"Bibi berjalan ke supermarket di seberang jalan untuk membeli belanjaan.","My friend has always lived in Kaohsiung.":"Teman saya selalu tinggal di Kaohsiung.","\"from... to...\" (time range)":"\"dari... sampai...\" (rentang waktu)","cóng + time A + dào + time B":"cóng + waktu A + dào + waktu B","This marks a time span from start to end. It shares the same pattern as \"cóng...dào...2,\" but that one is for distance/place, not time. A common mistake is dropping \"cóng\" and using only \"dào.\"":"Pola ini menandai rentang waktu dari awal hingga akhir. Pola ini sama dengan \"cóng...dào...2\", tetapi yang itu digunakan untuk jarak/tempat, bukan waktu. Kesalahan umum adalah menghilangkan \"cóng\" dan hanya menggunakan \"dào\".","This company's working hours are from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.":"Jam kerja perusahaan ini adalah dari pukul 8 pagi sampai pukul 5 sore.","The library is open from Monday to Friday.":"Perpustakaan buka dari hari Senin sampai Jumat.","\"from... to...\" (place/distance range)":"\"dari... sampai...\" (rentang jarak/tempat)","cóng + place A + dào + place B":"cóng + tempat A + dào + tempat B","This marks a route from a starting place to a destination. It has the same structure as \"cóng...dào...1\" but is used for place/distance, often paired with a clause stating how long it takes.":"Pola ini menunjukkan rute dari tempat awal ke tempat tujuan. Strukturnya sama dengan \"cóng...dào...1\", tetapi digunakan untuk tempat/jarak, dan sering disertai klausa yang menyatakan berapa lama waktu yang dibutuhkan.","It takes three and a half hours to drive from Taipei to Nantou.":"Naik mobil dari Taipei ke Nantou memakan waktu tiga setengah jam.","It's about twenty minutes by bike from my house to school.":"Dari rumah saya ke sekolah naik sepeda memakan waktu sekitar dua puluh menit.","\"all/both\" (adverb summarizing the whole subject)":"\"semua/keduanya\" (kata keterangan yang merangkum seluruh subjek)","plural subject + dōu + verb/adjective":"subjek jamak + dōu + kata kerja/kata sifat","\"Dōu\" always sits after the subject and before the verb, showing that something applies to every member of a plural subject. It can't be used with a single person/item, and learners often mistakenly place it before the subject.":"\"Dōu\" selalu diletakkan setelah subjek dan sebelum kata kerja, menunjukkan bahwa sesuatu berlaku untuk setiap anggota dari subjek jamak. Kata ini tidak bisa digunakan untuk satu orang/benda saja, dan pembelajar sering keliru meletakkannya sebelum subjek.","We all like jogging.":"Kami semua suka jogging.","They are all Taiwanese.":"Mereka semua orang Taiwan.","expresses direction with lái/qù":"menyatakan arah dengan lái/qù","V + lái/qù":"V + lái/qù","\"Lái\" marks movement toward the speaker and \"qù\" marks movement away, attached right after the verb. Don't confuse this with compound directional complements like \"進來/出去\".":"\"Lái\" menandai gerakan menuju pembicara dan \"qù\" menandai gerakan menjauh, diletakkan tepat setelah kata kerja. Jangan bingungkan ini dengan pelengkap arah majemuk seperti \"進來/出去\".","I brought your things here.":"Saya membawa barang-barang Anda ke sini.","He went ahead to buy something.":"Dia pergi duluan untuk membeli sesuatu.","expresses cause and result":"menyatakan sebab dan akibat","Yīnwèi + reason, suǒyǐ + result":"Yīnwèi + alasan, suǒyǐ + akibat","\"Yīnwèi\" introduces the reason and \"suǒyǐ\" the result; in speech only one of the two is often used, but written Chinese typically keeps both.":"\"Yīnwèi\" memperkenalkan alasan dan \"suǒyǐ\" memperkenalkan akibat; dalam percakapan sering hanya salah satu yang digunakan, tetapi dalam bahasa Mandarin tulis biasanya keduanya dipertahankan.","Because they don't have money, they can't travel abroad.":"Karena mereka tidak punya uang, mereka tidak bisa bepergian ke luar negeri.","Because there's a test tomorrow, I'm going to study at home tonight.":"Karena besok ada ujian, malam ini saya akan belajar di rumah.","lists different portions of a whole":"menyebutkan bagian-bagian berbeda dari suatu keseluruhan","(whole), yǒude..., yǒude...":"(keseluruhan), yǒude..., yǒude...","Used to divide a whole into groups and describe each one's trait; often appears without the following noun (\"yǒude rén\" shortened to \"yǒude\"), and can list more than two groups.":"Digunakan untuk membagi suatu keseluruhan menjadi beberapa kelompok dan menjelaskan ciri masing-masing; sering muncul tanpa kata benda yang mengikutinya (\"yǒude rén\" disingkat menjadi \"yǒude\"), dan bisa menyebutkan lebih dari dua kelompok.","Some of the classmates can speak English, and some can speak French.":"Sebagian teman sekelas bisa berbahasa Inggris, dan sebagian lagi bisa berbahasa Prancis.","Some of these fruits are sweet, and some are sour.":"Sebagian buah-buahan ini manis, dan sebagian lagi asam.","indicates the destination before continuing with an action":"menunjukkan tempat tujuan sebelum melanjutkan dengan suatu tindakan","dào + place + qù/lái + VP":"dào + tempat + qù/lái + VP","\"Dào\" marks the destination, \"qù/lái\" adds direction, then the action (VP) follows. Unlike \"qù + place + VP\" (e.g. qù xuéxiào shàngkè), this pattern requires \"dào\" before the place.":"\"Dào\" menandai tempat tujuan, \"qù/lái\" menambahkan arah, lalu diikuti tindakan (VP). Berbeda dengan \"qù + tempat + VP\" (misalnya qù xuéxiào shàngkè), pola ini mengharuskan \"dào\" diletakkan sebelum tempat.","Where are you going to travel to?":"Anda mau bepergian ke mana?","I'm going to Taipei tomorrow for a meeting.":"Besok saya akan pergi ke Taipei untuk rapat.","expresses an excessive degree":"menyatakan tingkat yang berlebihan","tài + adjective + le":"tài + kata sifat + le","Expresses that a degree is excessive, often with a negative nuance. Unlike neutral \"hěn + adj\", \"tài + adj + le\" usually implies the speaker disapproves.":"Menyatakan bahwa suatu tingkatan berlebihan, sering dengan nuansa negatif. Berbeda dengan \"hěn + adj\" yang netral, \"tài + adj + le\" biasanya menyiratkan bahwa pembicara tidak setuju.","This hotel is too expensive, I don't want to stay here.":"Hotel ini terlalu mahal, saya tidak mau menginap di sini.","This piece of clothing is too small, I can't fit into it.":"Baju ini terlalu kecil, saya tidak bisa memakainya.","or (in questions offering a choice)":"atau (dalam pertanyaan yang menawarkan pilihan)","A + háishì + B":"A + háishì + B","'還是' offers a choice inside a question ('A or B?'); unlike '或者', which links options in statements, '還是' is used only in questions.":"'還是' menawarkan pilihan dalam sebuah pertanyaan ('A atau B?'); berbeda dengan '或者' yang menghubungkan pilihan dalam kalimat pernyataan, '還是' hanya digunakan dalam pertanyaan.","Does Dad want to eat rice or noodles tonight?":"Malam ini Ayah mau makan nasi atau mi?","Do you want to drink coffee or tea?":"Kamu mau minum kopi atau teh?","both... and... (two simultaneous qualities)":"baik... maupun... (dua sifat yang terjadi bersamaan)","yòu + Adj/V1 + yòu + Adj/V2":"yòu + Kata sifat/Kata kerja 1 + yòu + Kata sifat/Kata kerja 2","Used to state two qualities or actions of the same subject at once; '又' always appears in a pair (never alone) and sits directly before each adjective or verb.":"Digunakan untuk menyatakan dua sifat atau tindakan dari subjek yang sama secara bersamaan; '又' selalu muncul berpasangan (tidak pernah sendiri) dan diletakkan tepat sebelum setiap kata sifat atau kata kerja.","This restaurant is both cheap and famous.":"Restoran ini murah sekaligus terkenal.","This bubble tea is both sweet and delicious.":"Teh susu mutiara ini manis sekaligus enak.","a little / somewhat (usually negative nuance)":"agak / sedikit (biasanya dengan nuansa negatif)","yǒu (yì)diǎn + Adjective":"yǒu (yì)diǎn + Kata sifat","'有點' goes before an adjective to soften an undesirable state; unlike the degree adverb '很', it is typically followed by a negative-leaning adjective, not a positive one.":"'有點' diletakkan sebelum kata sifat untuk memperhalus keadaan yang tidak diinginkan; berbeda dengan kata keterangan tingkat '很', kata ini biasanya diikuti oleh kata sifat yang bernuansa negatif, bukan positif.","I'm a little tired.":"Saya agak lelah.","This piece of clothing is a bit expensive.":"Baju ini agak mahal.","(at) place + 的 + noun — the one located at ...":"(di) tempat + 的 + kata benda — yang berada di ...","(zài) + Place Word + de + Noun":"(zài) + Kata Tempat + de + Kata Benda","A place word plus '的' modifies a following noun to mean 'the N that is at/in [place]'; '在' can be dropped, but the order (place + 的 + N) stays fixed.":"Kata tempat ditambah '的' memodifikasi kata benda yang mengikutinya, bermakna 'N yang berada di [tempat]'; '在' boleh dihilangkan, tetapi urutan (tempat + 的 + N) tetap tidak berubah.","The computer on the desk is my younger brother's.":"Komputer yang ada di meja itu milik adik laki-laki saya.","The cake in the fridge was made by Mom.":"Kue yang ada di kulkas itu dibuat oleh Ibu.","from/since (a starting point in time)":"dari/sejak (titik awal waktu)","cóng + Time Point + kāishǐ":"cóng + Titik Waktu + kāishǐ","'從' marks a starting point in time, often paired with '開始' ('starting from...'); don't confuse this with 從1, which marks a starting point in space (從 + place).":"'從' menandai titik awal waktu, sering dipasangkan dengan '開始' ('mulai dari...'); jangan bingungkan ini dengan 從1, yang menandai titik awal tempat (從 + tempat).","Starting in the morning, there are already a lot of people lining up at the post office.":"Sejak pagi, sudah banyak orang mengantre di kantor pos.","Starting next month, I'm going to exercise every day.":"Mulai bulan depan, saya akan berolahraga setiap hari.","upward/rising movement (get up, stand up)":"gerakan ke atas/naik (bangun, berdiri)","V + 起來 (e.g. 站起來, 坐起來)":"V + 起來 (mis. 站起來, 坐起來)","Here \"起來\" marks a movement from a lower position to a higher one, completing the verb's direction (e.g. standing up). Don't confuse it with the other \"V起來\" meaning \"it seems/looks\" (看起來).":"Di sini \"起來\" menandai gerakan dari posisi lebih rendah ke posisi lebih tinggi, melengkapi arah kata kerja (misalnya berdiri). Jangan bingung dengan \"V起來\" lain yang berarti \"tampaknya/kelihatannya\" (看起來).","He stood up and walked out of the room.":"Dia berdiri dan berjalan keluar ruangan.","The puppy jumps up as soon as it hears footsteps.":"Anak anjing itu langsung melompat begitu mendengar suara langkah kaki.","\"a bit more ~\" (a mild request for more of a quality)":"\"lebih ~ sedikit\" (permintaan halus agar suatu sifat lebih ditingkatkan sedikit)","Stative verb (adjective) + 一點":"Kata kerja statif (kata sifat) + 一點","Adding \"一點\" after an adjective softly asks for a bit more of that quality (often advice or a mild command). This differs from the comparative \"比…一點\", which needs an explicit point of comparison.":"Menambahkan \"一點\" setelah kata sifat adalah cara halus untuk meminta sedikit lebih banyak sifat tersebut (biasanya berupa saran atau perintah ringan). Ini berbeda dengan perbandingan \"比…一點\", yang memerlukan titik perbandingan yang jelas.","Be a bit more careful when moving house.":"Lebih berhati-hatilah sedikit saat pindah rumah.","Speak a little more quietly — my sister is sleeping.":"Bicaralah sedikit lebih pelan — adik perempuan saya sedang tidur.","\"a bit more than [number]\" (number + 多 + measure word)":"\"lebih dari [angka] sedikit\" (angka + 多 + kata penggolong)","Number + 多 + measure word (一個多小時, 兩萬多塊)":"Angka + 多 + kata penggolong (一個多小時, 兩萬多塊)","\"多\" sits between the number and the measure word to mean \"a bit more than that number\" (e.g. 一個多小時 = a bit over an hour). Keep the order Number + 多 + measure word — don't say \"多一個小時\".":"\"多\" berada di antara angka dan kata penggolong, berarti \"lebih dari angka itu sedikit\" (misalnya 一個多小時 = sedikit lebih dari satu jam). Pertahankan urutan Angka + 多 + kata penggolong — jangan katakan \"多一個小時\".","They chatted for over an hour.":"Mereka mengobrol selama lebih dari satu jam.","This laptop cost me over twenty thousand NT dollars.":"Laptop ini menghabiskan biaya saya lebih dari dua puluh ribu dolar NT.","\"until/up to ~\" (an action continues to a point in time or place)":"\"sampai ~\" (suatu tindakan berlangsung hingga suatu titik waktu atau tempat)","V (+ object + V) + 到 + time/place":"V (+ objek + V) + 到 + waktu/tempat","\"到\" as a complement marks the endpoint (time or place) that an action continues to. With an object, the verb repeats: V+O+V到 (上課上到...). This differs from the resultative \"到\" meaning \"successfully\" (as in 看到 = manage to see).":"\"到\" sebagai pelengkap menandai titik akhir (waktu atau tempat) yang menjadi batas berlangsungnya suatu tindakan. Jika ada objek, kata kerja diulang: V+O+V到 (上課上到...). Ini berbeda dengan \"到\" resultatif yang berarti \"berhasil\" (seperti pada 看到 = berhasil melihat).","Wang Meimei had class until 5 p.m. today.":"Hari ini Wang Meimei ada kelas sampai jam 5 sore.","I did homework until 11 p.m. last night.":"Tadi malam saya mengerjakan PR sampai jam 11 malam.","\"again\" (repetition of something that already happened)":"\"lagi\" (pengulangan sesuatu yang sudah terjadi)","又 + V (used for a realized/past repetition)":"又 + V (digunakan untuk pengulangan yang sudah terjadi/di masa lalu)","\"又\" is used for a repetition that has already happened (a past event or a realized pattern). For a repetition expected in the future, use \"再\" instead (明天再來 is correct, ×明天又來 is not).":"\"又\" digunakan untuk pengulangan yang sudah terjadi (peristiwa masa lalu atau pola yang sudah terwujud). Untuk pengulangan yang diperkirakan terjadi di masa depan, gunakan \"再\" (明天再來 benar, ×明天又來 salah).","He forgot to do his homework again.":"Dia lupa mengerjakan PR lagi.","It's raining, and the bus is late again.":"Sedang hujan, dan bus terlambat lagi.","also (did); in addition (a past, already-realized action)":"juga (telah melakukan); selain itu (tindakan masa lalu yang sudah terjadi)","V-le ..., yòu V-le ...":"V-le ..., yòu V-le ...","\"Yòu\" marks a repeated or additional action that has already happened. Don't confuse it with \"zài,\" which is used for actions not yet realized (future repetition).":"\"Yòu\" menandai tindakan berulang atau tambahan yang sudah terjadi. Jangan bingung dengan \"zài\", yang digunakan untuk tindakan yang belum terwujud (pengulangan di masa depan).","He went to Taichung, and then went to Kaohsiung too.":"Dia pergi ke Taichung, lalu pergi ke Kaohsiung juga.","He ate a hamburger, and then ate an order of fries too.":"Dia makan hamburger, lalu makan sepiring kentang goreng juga.","come/go (direction of motion relative to the speaker)":"datang/pergi (arah gerakan relatif terhadap penutur)","V + guòlái (toward the speaker) / V + guòqù (away from the speaker)":"V + guòlái (ke arah penutur) / V + guòqù (menjauhi penutur)","\"Guòlái\" indicates movement toward the speaker's position; \"guòqù\" indicates movement away from it. Direction is always judged from the speaker's viewpoint, a common source of errors for learners.":"\"Guòlái\" menunjukkan gerakan menuju posisi penutur; \"guòqù\" menunjukkan gerakan menjauh darinya. Arah selalu ditentukan dari sudut pandang penutur, yang sering menjadi sumber kesalahan bagi pembelajar.","The child ran over to me, laughing.":"Anak itu berlari ke arahku sambil tertawa.","The MRT arrived, so everyone hurried over to catch it.":"MRT sudah tiba, jadi semua orang bergegas menuju ke sana untuk mengejarnya.","come/go down (directional complement for downward movement)":"turun (pelengkap arah untuk gerakan ke bawah)","V + xiàlái (down, toward the speaker) / V + xiàqù (down, away from the speaker)":"V + xiàlái (turun, ke arah penutur) / V + xiàqù (turun, menjauhi penutur)","\"Xiàlái/xiàqù\" are directional complements for downward movement. \"Xiàlái\" often implies coming to rest or moving toward the speaker (as in \"zuò xiàlái,\" sit down), while \"xiàqù\" implies moving away and downward.":"\"Xiàlái/xiàqù\" adalah pelengkap arah untuk gerakan ke bawah. \"Xiàlái\" sering menyiratkan berhenti atau bergerak ke arah penutur (seperti pada \"zuò xiàlái\", duduk), sedangkan \"xiàqù\" menyiratkan bergerak menjauh dan ke bawah.","Once everyone arrives, you can find a place to sit down and rest.":"Setelah semua orang tiba, kamu bisa mencari tempat untuk duduk dan beristirahat.","He slowly walked down the stairs.":"Dia perlahan-lahan berjalan turun tangga.","A is more ... than B":"A lebih ... daripada B","A + bǐ + B + adjective":"A + bǐ + B + kata sifat","\"Bǐ\" directly compares two things. Its negation is usually expressed with \"méiyǒu\" (e.g., 弟弟沒有哥哥高) rather than \"bù bǐ,\" and \"hěn\" is not placed before the adjective in this pattern.":"\"Bǐ\" membandingkan dua hal secara langsung. Bentuk negatifnya biasanya diungkapkan dengan \"méiyǒu\" (misalnya, 弟弟沒有哥哥高), bukan \"bù bǐ\", dan \"hěn\" tidak diletakkan sebelum kata sifat dalam pola ini.","The younger brother is taller than the older brother.":"Adik laki-laki lebih tinggi daripada kakak laki-laki.","This piece of clothing is more expensive than that one.":"Baju ini lebih mahal daripada yang itu.","A is the same as / as ... as B":"A sama dengan / se... dengan B","A + gēn + B + yíyàng (+ adjective)":"A + gēn + B + yíyàng (+ kata sifat)","\"Gēn ... yíyàng\" expresses equality between two things. Adding an adjective after \"yíyàng\" specifies in what way they're equal (omitting it implies they are identical overall). Unlike the \"bǐ\" comparative, it shows sameness, not superiority.":"\"Gēn ... yíyàng\" menyatakan kesetaraan antara dua hal. Menambahkan kata sifat setelah \"yíyàng\" menentukan dalam hal apa keduanya setara (jika dihilangkan, berarti keduanya identik secara keseluruhan). Berbeda dengan perbandingan \"bǐ\", pola ini menunjukkan kesamaan, bukan keunggulan.","This book is as expensive as that one.":"Buku ini semahal buku itu.","My height is the same as my older sister's.":"Tinggi badanku sama dengan kakak perempuanku.","as soon as...then...":"begitu... langsung...","Yī + Action A + jiù + Action B":"Yī + Tindakan A + jiù + Tindakan B","Marks two actions happening in immediate succession with almost no gap; note 一 is read \"yí\" before a 4th-tone syllable (as in xiàkè, since 下 is tone 4).":"Menandai dua tindakan yang terjadi berurutan hampir tanpa jeda; perlu diperhatikan bahwa 一 dibaca \"yí\" sebelum suku kata bernada 4 (seperti pada xiàkè, karena 下 bernada 4).","They go home as soon as class ends.":"Begitu kelas selesai, mereka langsung pulang.","I wash my hands as soon as I get home.":"Begitu sampai di rumah, saya langsung mencuci tangan.","emphasizes when/where/how a past event happened":"menekankan kapan/di mana/bagaimana suatu peristiwa di masa lalu terjadi","(Shì) + emphasized element + Verb + de":"(Shì) + unsur yang ditekankan + Kata kerja + de","Highlights details (time/place/means) of an event both speakers already know happened; unlike 了, which simply reports that an event occurred, 是...的 spotlights the circumstances.":"Menyoroti detail (waktu/tempat/cara) suatu peristiwa yang sudah diketahui terjadi oleh kedua penutur; berbeda dengan 了 yang hanya melaporkan bahwa suatu peristiwa terjadi, 是...的 menyoroti keadaan di sekitarnya.","I came from the United States.":"Saya datang dari Amerika Serikat.","He came by plane.":"Dia datang naik pesawat.","easy to.../hard to...":"mudah.../sulit...","Hǎo/Nán + Verb":"Hǎo/Nán + Kata kerja","好/難 before a verb expresses how easy or hard it is to perform that action (好吃 = easy to eat = delicious); the subject is the semantic object of the verb, not the one performing it.":"好/難 di depan kata kerja menyatakan mudah atau sulitnya melakukan tindakan tersebut (好吃 = mudah dimakan = enak); subjeknya adalah objek semantik dari kata kerja, bukan pelaku tindakan.","This computer is very easy to use.":"Komputer ini sangat mudah digunakan.","after doing...then...":"setelah melakukan...lalu...","Verb A + le + (Object) + jiù + Verb B":"Kata kerja A + le + (Objek) + jiù + Kata kerja B","Similar to 一...就... ([[g2-096]]), but here 了 marks that Action A is completed before Action B follows, so a time gap is allowed; 一...就... instead stresses near-simultaneity.":"Mirip dengan 一...就... ([[g2-096]]), tetapi di sini 了 menandai bahwa Tindakan A selesai sebelum Tindakan B terjadi, sehingga boleh ada jarak waktu; sedangkan 一...就... justru menekankan hampir bersamaan.","I go to class right after I eat breakfast.":"Saya langsung pergi ke kelas setelah sarapan.","He goes out to play right after he finishes his homework.":"Dia langsung keluar bermain setelah menyelesaikan pekerjaan rumahnya.","from...towards...":"dari...menuju...","Cóng + starting point + wǎng + direction/place + Verb":"Cóng + titik awal + wǎng + arah/tempat + Kata kerja","從 marks the starting point and 往 marks the direction or destination of movement; very common when giving directions, with 往 followed by a direction word (left/right) or a place name.":"從 menandai titik awal, sedangkan 往 menandai arah atau tujuan pergerakan; struktur ini sangat umum digunakan saat memberi petunjuk arah, dengan 往 diikuti kata arah (kiri/kanan) atau nama tempat.","Walk from the school towards the library and you'll get there.":"Berjalanlah dari sekolah menuju perpustakaan, nanti sampai di sana.","Turn right from here and it's the MRT station.":"Dari sini belok kanan, itu stasiun MRT.","expresses the distance or time between A and B":"menyatakan jarak atau waktu antara A dan B","A + lí + B + (distance/time)":"A + lí + B + (jarak/waktu)","Lí marks the distance or time gap between two points; unlike cóng (\"from,\" motion) or dào (\"to,\" destination), lí never takes a verb directly after it — it's followed straight by a distance or time expression.":"Lí menandai jarak atau selisih waktu antara dua titik; berbeda dengan cóng (\"dari\", pergerakan) atau dào (\"ke\", tujuan), lí tidak pernah diikuti langsung oleh kata kerja — melainkan langsung diikuti oleh ungkapan jarak atau waktu.","It only takes ten minutes to walk from my house to school.":"Dari rumah saya ke sekolah hanya perlu sepuluh menit jalan kaki.","The post office isn't far from my house — it's five minutes by bike.":"Kantor pos tidak jauh dari rumah saya — naik sepeda hanya lima menit.","a verb phrase modifies a noun with 的":"frasa kata kerja menerangkan kata benda dengan 的","VP + de + N":"Frasa kata kerja + de + Kata benda","A verb phrase placed before 的 works like a relative clause modifying the noun that follows; there's no relative pronoun as in English, so you must infer from context whether N is the logical subject or object of the VP.":"Frasa kata kerja yang diletakkan sebelum 的 berfungsi seperti klausa relatif yang menerangkan kata benda yang mengikutinya; tidak ada kata ganti relatif seperti dalam bahasa Inggris, jadi Anda harus menyimpulkan dari konteks apakah N adalah subjek atau objek logis dari frasa kata kerja tersebut.","I know an English teacher who can speak German.":"Saya kenal seorang guru bahasa Inggris yang bisa bicara bahasa Jerman.","I have a roommate who's really good at cooking.":"Saya punya teman sekamar yang sangat pandai memasak.","duō + adjective asks about a degree or measurement":"duō + kata sifat digunakan untuk menanyakan tingkat atau ukuran","duō + stative verb (gāo/dà/yuǎn...)?":"duō + kata kerja statif (gāo/dà/yuǎn...)?","Duō means \"how\" and attaches directly to scalar stative verbs like gāo/dà/yuǎn to ask for a measurement or degree; unlike jǐ + measure word (which asks for a small countable number), duō needs no measure word and just goes straight before the adjective.":"Duō berarti \"seberapa\" dan langsung melekat pada kata kerja statif berskala seperti gāo/dà/yuǎn untuk menanyakan ukuran atau tingkat; berbeda dengan jǐ + kata penggolong (yang menanyakan jumlah kecil yang bisa dihitung), duō tidak memerlukan kata penggolong dan langsung diletakkan sebelum kata sifat.","How tall is your older brother?":"Seberapa tinggi kakak laki-lakimu?","How old is your younger sister this year?":"Berapa umur adik perempuanmu tahun ini?","V + in/out/up/back + (object) + come/go shows the direction of movement":"V + masuk/keluar/naik/kembali + (objek) + datang/pergi menunjukkan arah pergerakan","V + jìn/chū/shàng/huí + (object) + lái/qù":"V + jìn/chū/shàng/huí + (Objek) + lái/qù","Jìn/chū/shàng/huí show the path of motion (in/out/up/back), while lái/qù show whether it's toward or away from the speaker; when a non-place object is added, it goes between the two parts (V + direction + object + lái/qù), which is the key difference from a simple two-part directional complement.":"Jìn/chū/shàng/huí menunjukkan arah gerakan (masuk/keluar/naik/kembali), sedangkan lái/qù menunjukkan apakah arah tersebut menuju atau menjauhi pembicara; ketika ditambahkan objek yang bukan tempat, objek itu diletakkan di antara kedua bagian (V + arah + objek + lái/qù), inilah perbedaan utama dari pelengkap arah dua bagian yang sederhana.","The elevator was taking too long, so I walked up from the second floor.":"Liftnya lama sekali, jadi saya berjalan naik dari lantai dua.","He ran back to the dorm.":"Dia berlari kembali ke asrama.","the pronoun is dropped when the same subject continues into the next clause":"kata ganti dihilangkan ketika subjek yang sama berlanjut ke klausa berikutnya","S + V1..., (Ø) + V2...":"S + V1..., (Ø) + V2...","When the subject is already clear from context, Mandarin naturally drops the pronoun (tā, etc.) in the following clause instead of repeating it — similar to Japanese subject omission, but unlike English, which requires restating \"he/she\" in every clause.":"Ketika subjek sudah jelas dari konteks, bahasa Mandarin secara alami menghilangkan kata ganti (tā, dst.) pada klausa berikutnya alih-alih mengulanginya — mirip dengan penghilangan subjek dalam bahasa Jepang, tetapi berbeda dengan bahasa Inggris, yang mengharuskan penyebutan ulang \"he/she\" di setiap klausa.","After looking at the menu, he decided to order a sandwich.":"Setelah melihat menu, dia memutuskan untuk memesan sandwich.","After class, she went to the library to read.":"Setelah kelas selesai, dia pergi ke perpustakaan untuk membaca.","Expressing an approximate number":"Menyatakan angka perkiraan","Round ten + 幾 (+ classifier)":"Bilangan puluhan bulat + 幾 (+ kata penggolong)","'幾' attached after a round ten (十幾, 二十幾) expresses an approximate number like '-some'. A question such as 幾個? simply asks 'how many', while an answer like 十幾個 is the typical approximate-number form.":"'幾' yang ditambahkan setelah bilangan puluhan bulat (十幾, 二十幾) menyatakan angka perkiraan seperti '-an' (misalnya \"dua puluhan\"). Pertanyaan seperti 幾個? hanya menanyakan 'berapa banyak', sedangkan jawaban seperti 十幾個 adalah bentuk angka perkiraan yang umum.","How many dumplings did you eat?":"Kamu makan berapa banyak pangsit?","He's in his twenties, roughly.":"Umurnya sekitar dua puluhan.","Placing the topic at the front of the sentence":"Meletakkan topik di awal kalimat","Topic, + Comment":"Topik, + Komentar","In spoken Mandarin (especially Taiwan Mandarin), a noun that is not the grammatical subject can still be fronted as the 'topic', set off by a pause/comma, with the rest of the sentence commenting on it — 筆 isn't the subject of 幾塊錢一枝 but can still lead the sentence as its topic.":"Dalam bahasa Mandarin lisan (khususnya Mandarin Taiwan), sebuah kata benda yang bukan subjek gramatikal tetap bisa diletakkan di depan sebagai 'topik', dipisahkan oleh jeda/koma, dengan sisa kalimat mengomentarinya — 筆 bukan subjek dari 幾塊錢一枝 tetapi tetap bisa memimpin kalimat sebagai topiknya.","As for pens, how much is one?":"Kalau pulpen, satu berapa harganya?","As for watermelons, how much is one?":"Kalau semangka, satu berapa harganya?","Already did (completion, not mere experience)":"Sudah melakukan (penyelesaian, bukan sekadar pengalaman)","yǐjīng + V + guò + (le)":"yǐjīng + V + guò + (le)","'已經 V 過 了' emphasizes that a specific action is finished (e.g. this morning), unlike experiential 'V過' which describes past experience without a fixed time. It overlaps closely with plain 了.":"'已經 V 過 了' menekankan bahwa suatu tindakan tertentu telah selesai (misalnya, tadi pagi), berbeda dengan 'V過' yang bersifat pengalaman, yang menggambarkan pengalaman masa lalu tanpa waktu yang pasti. Ini memiliki kemiripan erat dengan 了 biasa.","I already watched the TV news this morning.":"Tadi pagi saya sudah menonton berita di TV.","He already did his homework yesterday.":"Kemarin dia sudah mengerjakan PR-nya.","V1 while V2-ing (manner/simultaneous action)":"V1 sambil V2 (cara/tindakan bersamaan)","V1 + zhe + (Object) + V2":"V1 + zhe + (Objek) + V2","'V1-zhe V2' means doing V2 while V1-ing (manner/simultaneous action), always followed by a second verb — unlike standalone 'V著' which shows a persisting state (e.g. 門開著, the door is open).":"'V1-zhe V2' berarti melakukan V2 sambil melakukan V1 (cara/tindakan bersamaan), selalu diikuti oleh kata kerja kedua — berbeda dengan 'V著' yang berdiri sendiri, yang menunjukkan keadaan yang sedang berlangsung (misalnya, 門開著, pintu sedang terbuka).","They are watching TV while eating cookies.":"Mereka sedang menonton TV sambil makan biskuit.","Mom talked to me while smiling.":"Ibu berbicara dengan saya sambil tersenyum.","V到 = succeeded in V-ing (result complement of achievement)":"V到 = berhasil melakukan V (pelengkap hasil pencapaian)","Verb + dào + (Object)":"Kata kerja + dào + (Objek)","'V到' is a result complement showing the action succeeded in reaching its goal (找到 = managed to find, 買到 = managed to buy). Don't confuse it with 到 meaning 'arrive at a place' or with perception verbs like 看到/聽到.":"'V到' adalah pelengkap hasil yang menunjukkan bahwa suatu tindakan berhasil mencapai tujuannya (找到 = berhasil menemukan, 買到 = berhasil membeli). Jangan disamakan dengan 到 yang berarti 'tiba di suatu tempat' atau dengan kata kerja persepsi seperti 看到/聽到.","He found that supermarket.":"Dia menemukan supermarket itu.","I finally managed to buy that book.":"Akhirnya saya berhasil membeli buku itu.","not until / only then":"baru setelah itu / barulah","A, then only (after that) B":"A, baru (setelah itu) B","Marks that B only happens after A, later than expected. Don't confuse with 才4 (small quantity) or 就 (earlier than expected).":"Menandakan bahwa B baru terjadi setelah A, lebih lambat dari yang diharapkan. Jangan disamakan dengan 才4 (jumlah sedikit) atau 就 (lebih cepat dari yang diharapkan).","He only agreed with the doctor's opinion after reading the report.":"Dia baru setuju dengan pendapat dokter setelah membaca laporan itu.","I waited a long time before the bus finally came.":"Saya menunggu lama sekali sebelum bus akhirnya datang.","only (emphasizing a small amount)":"hanya (menekankan jumlah yang sedikit)","cái + number/quantity":"cái + angka/jumlah","Emphasizes that a number or degree is smaller/less than expected. Distinct from 才1, which marks a delayed sequence of events.":"Menekankan bahwa suatu angka atau tingkat lebih kecil/sedikit dari yang diharapkan. Berbeda dengan 才1, yang menandakan urutan kejadian yang tertunda.","The last time I saw you, you were only eleven years old.":"Terakhir kali saya bertemu kamu, kamu baru berusia sebelas tahun.","It's only eight o'clock now, so we still have time.":"Sekarang baru jam delapan, jadi kita masih punya waktu.","to make/cause someone to do or feel something":"membuat/menyebabkan seseorang melakukan atau merasakan sesuatu","A + ràng + B + VP (A causes B to VP)":"A + ràng + B + VP (A menyebabkan B melakukan VP)","讓1 shows that A causes B to do/feel something as a result — a causal relation, unlike 讓2 (permission) or 叫1 (a direct verbal order).":"讓1 menunjukkan bahwa A menyebabkan B melakukan/merasakan sesuatu sebagai akibatnya — hubungan sebab-akibat, berbeda dengan 讓2 (izin) atau 叫1 (perintah lisan langsung).","Drinking a cup of warm milk before bed can help me sleep better.":"Minum secangkir susu hangat sebelum tidur dapat membantu saya tidur lebih nyenyak.","This movie made me very moved.":"Film ini membuat saya sangat terharu.","to let/allow (asking or granting permission)":"membiarkan/mengizinkan (meminta atau memberikan izin)","(Can/May) + ràng + wǒ + VP":"(Bisakah/Bolehkah) + ràng + wǒ + VP","讓2 is used to ask for or grant permission. Unlike causative 讓1, pairing it with 能不能/可以 makes a polite request; using 讓 alone can sound like a command.":"讓2 digunakan untuk meminta atau memberikan izin. Berbeda dengan 讓1 yang bersifat kausatif, memadukannya dengan 能不能/可以 menjadikannya permintaan yang sopan; menggunakan 讓 saja bisa terdengar seperti perintah.","Could you let me sit here and rest for a bit?":"Bisakah kamu membiarkan saya duduk di sini dan istirahat sebentar?","Please let me take a look at your passport.":"Tolong biarkan saya melihat paspor Anda.","to tell/order someone to do something":"menyuruh/memerintahkan seseorang melakukan sesuatu","A + jiào + B + VP (A tells B to VP)":"A + jiào + B + VP (A menyuruh B melakukan VP)","A causative verb meaning someone verbally instructs another person. Structurally similar to 讓1, but 叫 carries a stronger nuance of a direct spoken order, while 讓 covers broader indirect causes.":"Kata kerja kausatif yang berarti seseorang memberi perintah secara lisan kepada orang lain. Secara struktur mirip dengan 讓1, tetapi 叫 memiliki nuansa yang lebih kuat sebagai perintah lisan langsung, sedangkan 讓 mencakup sebab-sebab tidak langsung yang lebih luas.","My boss told me to go to the meeting with him this afternoon.":"Bos saya menyuruh saya pergi rapat bersamanya sore ini.","Mom told me to come home and eat dinner.":"Ibu menyuruh saya pulang untuk makan malam.","to tell/have someone do something (causative)":"menyuruh/membuat seseorang melakukan sesuatu (kausatif)","A + 叫 + B + Verb Phrase":"A + 叫 + B + Frasa Verba","\"叫\" expresses causation: \"A 叫 B + verb\" means A tells/has B do something, with a nuance of ordering or requesting. It is more direct than \"請\" and slightly more forceful than \"讓.\"":"\"叫\" menyatakan sebab-akibat (kausatif): \"A 叫 B + kata kerja\" berarti A menyuruh/meminta B melakukan sesuatu, dengan nuansa perintah atau permintaan. Ini lebih langsung daripada \"請\" dan sedikit lebih tegas daripada \"讓.\"","I told someone to go buy lunch boxes and bring them back.":"Saya menyuruh seseorang pergi membeli kotak makan siang lalu membawanya kembali.","Mom told me to take out the trash.":"Ibu menyuruh saya membuang sampah.","softens a wh-question at the end of the sentence":"melembutkan pertanyaan kata tanya di akhir kalimat","Question word + ... + 呢?":"Kata tanya + ... + 呢?","\"呢\" placed at the end of a wh-question (什麼, 誰, 哪裡, 怎麼, etc.) softens the tone and shows the speaker is genuinely wondering. This differs from the \"呢\" used in short elliptical questions like \"你呢?\"":"\"呢\" yang diletakkan di akhir pertanyaan kata tanya (什麼, 誰, 哪裡, 怎麼, dsb.) melembutkan nada bicara dan menunjukkan penutur benar-benar bertanya-tanya. Ini berbeda dari \"呢\" yang digunakan dalam pertanyaan elips singkat seperti \"你呢?\"","When can you start working?":"Kapan kamu bisa mulai bekerja?","Who on earth did this?":"Sebenarnya siapa yang melakukan ini?","placing \"沒有\" at the end of a sentence to ask whether something has happened":"meletakkan \"沒有\" di akhir kalimat untuk menanyakan apakah sesuatu sudah terjadi","V(過) + O + 沒有?":"V(過) + O + 沒有?","\"V(過) + O + 沒有?\" asks whether an action has happened or been experienced, with \"沒有\" at the end functioning like \"嗎.\" It is close in meaning to \"了沒\" and common in speech.":"\"V(過) + O + 沒有?\" digunakan untuk menanyakan apakah suatu tindakan sudah terjadi atau pernah dialami, dengan \"沒有\" di akhir kalimat berfungsi seperti \"嗎.\" Ini mirip maknanya dengan \"了沒\" dan umum digunakan dalam bahasa lisan.","Have you all visited the campus?":"Apakah kalian semua sudah mengunjungi kampus?","Have you eaten stinky tofu before?":"Apakah kamu pernah makan tahu busuk?","must / have to (strong obligation)":"harus / wajib (kewajiban kuat)","Subject + 必須 + Verb Phrase":"Subjek + 必須 + Frasa kata kerja","\"必須\" expresses a strong, often objective obligation, stronger than \"應該\" (should), leaving no room for choice. Its negation is \"不必\" (not necessary), never \"不必須.\"":"\"必須\" menyatakan kewajiban yang kuat, sering bersifat objektif, lebih kuat daripada \"應該\" (seharusnya), tanpa memberi ruang untuk pilihan. Bentuk negatifnya adalah \"不必\" (tidak perlu), bukan \"不必須.\"","This meeting is very important, so you must attend on time.":"Rapat ini sangat penting, jadi kamu harus hadir tepat waktu.","There's a test tomorrow, so you must review carefully tonight.":"Besok ada ujian, jadi malam ini kamu harus belajar dengan cermat.","to/until — marking the endpoint of a range":"sampai/hingga — menandai titik akhir suatu rentang","(從) A + 到 + B":"(從) A + 到 + B","\"到\" here marks the endpoint of a range from a starting point (often with 從/由), used for time, place, or sequence, as in \"從A到B.\" Distinguish this from the verb \"到\" meaning \"to arrive.\"":"\"到\" di sini menandai titik akhir suatu rentang dari titik awal (sering dengan 從/由), digunakan untuk waktu, tempat, atau urutan, seperti dalam \"從A到B.\" Bedakan ini dari kata kerja \"到\" yang berarti \"tiba.\"","Students from third grade to sixth grade all have to stay after school to practice dancing.":"Siswa dari kelas tiga sampai kelas enam semua harus tinggal di sekolah setelah jam pelajaran untuk berlatih menari.","This shop is open from Monday to Friday.":"Toko ini buka dari hari Senin sampai Jumat.","if... then...":"jika... maka...","yàoshi A, jiù B":"yàoshi A, jiù B","\"要是\" introduces a casual, spoken conditional and pairs with \"就\" to state the result or instruction. It's more colloquial than \"如果\"; learners often forget to add \"就\" in the second clause.":"\"要是\" mengawali kalimat kondisional yang santai dan lisan, serta berpasangan dengan \"就\" untuk menyatakan hasil atau instruksi. Ini lebih informal daripada \"如果\"; pelajar sering lupa menambahkan \"就\" pada klausa kedua.","If you have a fever, stay home and rest today.":"Jika kamu demam, hari ini tinggallah di rumah untuk beristirahat.","If you're not feeling well, go home early and rest.":"Jika kamu merasa tidak enak badan, pulanglah lebih awal dan beristirahat.","if... (in that case)":"jika... (dalam hal itu)","A dehuà, jiù B":"A dehuà, jiù B","\"的話\" is placed after a clause to mark a spoken hypothesis; it can combine with \"要是/如果\" or stand alone to form a conditional sentence.":"\"的話\" diletakkan setelah sebuah klausa untuk menandai sebuah andaian dalam bahasa lisan; kata ini bisa digabungkan dengan \"要是/如果\" atau berdiri sendiri untuk membentuk kalimat kondisional.","If it rains, I won't go.":"Kalau hujan, saya tidak akan pergi.","If it snows tomorrow, we won't go out.":"Kalau besok turun salju, kami tidak akan keluar.","A is not as... as B":"A tidak se... dengan B","A méiyǒu B (zhème/nàme) + adjective":"A méiyǒu B (zhème/nàme) + kata sifat","This compares A and B, showing A falls short of B's degree — a negative comparison, the reverse direction of \"A比B...\".":"Struktur ini membandingkan A dan B, menunjukkan bahwa A tidak mencapai tingkat B — sebuah perbandingan negatif, kebalikan dari arah \"A比B...\".","The situation isn't as serious as you think.":"Situasinya tidak seserius yang kamu pikirkan.","This exam wasn't as hard as the last one.":"Ujian ini tidak sesulit ujian yang lalu.","not only... but also...":"tidak hanya... tetapi juga...","búdàn A, érqiě B":"búdàn A, érqiě B","Used when both clauses share the same subject, showing B intensifies or adds to A. \"而且\" leans slightly more formal/written than \"還/也\".":"Digunakan ketika kedua klausa memiliki subjek yang sama, menunjukkan bahwa B memperkuat atau menambahkan pada A. \"而且\" sedikit lebih formal/tertulis dibandingkan \"還/也\".","This story is not only easy to understand, but also very interesting.":"Cerita ini tidak hanya mudah dipahami, tetapi juga sangat menarik.","This restaurant is not only cheap, but also very delicious.":"Restoran ini tidak hanya murah, tetapi juga sangat enak.","búdàn A, hái/yě B":"búdàn A, hái/yě B","A similar additive structure to \"不但……而且……\", but using \"還/也\" sounds more casual and is more common in everyday spoken Mandarin than \"而且\".":"Struktur penambahan yang mirip dengan \"不但……而且……\", tetapi penggunaan \"還/也\" terdengar lebih santai dan lebih umum dalam bahasa Mandarin lisan sehari-hari dibandingkan \"而且\".","At the convenience store, you can not only buy things but also send packages.":"Di minimarket, kamu tidak hanya bisa membeli barang tetapi juga bisa mengirim paket.","This phone is not only cheap but also very easy to use.":"Ponsel ini tidak hanya murah tetapi juga sangat mudah digunakan.","moreover, and also":"selain itu, dan juga","A, érqiě B (adds further, often stronger, information)":"A, érqiě B (menambahkan informasi lebih lanjut, sering kali lebih kuat)","Use 而且 to add further, often intensifying, information to what was just said. Don't confuse it with the contrastive 但是; 而且 can stand alone or pair with 不但.":"Gunakan 而且 untuk menambahkan informasi lebih lanjut, yang sering kali memperkuat apa yang baru saja dikatakan. Jangan disamakan dengan 但是 yang bersifat kontras; 而且 bisa berdiri sendiri atau berpasangan dengan 不但.","Summer in Taiwan is very hot, and moreover very humid.":"Musim panas di Taiwan sangat panas, dan selain itu juga sangat lembap.","The food at this restaurant is delicious, and moreover it's not expensive.":"Makanan di restoran ini enak, dan selain itu juga tidak mahal.","really/truly + adjective (emphasis)":"benar-benar/sungguh + kata sifat (penekanan)","zhēn + Vs (stative verb/adjective)":"zhēn + Vs (kata kerja statif/kata sifat)","真 expresses the speaker's genuine feeling or exclamation, stronger in tone than 很. Don't confuse it with 真的, which confirms that something is actually true.":"真 mengungkapkan perasaan tulus atau seruan penutur, dengan nada yang lebih kuat daripada 很. Jangan disamakan dengan 真的, yang menegaskan bahwa sesuatu memang benar.","That house is really great, and it's right near the school too.":"Rumah itu benar-benar bagus, dan juga letaknya persis dekat sekolah.","This bubble tea is really delicious.":"Teh susu mutiara ini benar-benar enak.","the more... the more...":"semakin... semakin...","yuè + A + yuè + B (A and B share the same subject)":"yuè + A + yuè + B (A dan B memiliki subjek yang sama)","越A越B shows that as A intensifies, B intensifies too, both from the same subject. Don't confuse it with 越來越, which describes one thing changing over time, not two linked actions.":"越A越B menunjukkan bahwa seiring A meningkat, B juga ikut meningkat, keduanya berasal dari subjek yang sama. Jangan disamakan dengan 越來越, yang menggambarkan satu hal yang berubah seiring waktu, bukan dua tindakan yang saling terkait.","The typhoon came, and the rain got heavier and heavier as it fell.":"Topan datang, dan hujan turun semakin lebat.","The more he talked, the angrier he got.":"Semakin banyak dia bicara, semakin marah dia.","more and more / increasingly":"semakin lama semakin / semakin","yuè lái yuè + Vs (adjective/stative verb)":"yuè lái yuè + Vs (kata sifat/verba statif)","越來越 marks a one-directional change over time, usually followed by an adjective and often ending with 了. Don't confuse it with 越A越B, which links two different actions or qualities.":"越來越 menandai perubahan satu arah seiring waktu, biasanya diikuti oleh kata sifat dan sering diakhiri dengan 了. Jangan disamakan dengan 越A越B, yang menghubungkan dua tindakan atau sifat yang berbeda.","His Chinese has been getting better and better.":"Bahasa Mandarinnya semakin lama semakin baik.","The weather has been getting colder and colder.":"Cuacanya semakin lama semakin dingin.","originally, at first":"awalnya, pada mulanya","běnlái + A, hòulái/kěshì + B (contrast between the original state A and the later state B)":"běnlái + A, hòulái/kěshì + B (kontras antara keadaan awal A dan keadaan berikutnya B)","本來 states the original situation or plan before a change, usually paired with 後來 or 可是 to show the contrast. It needs a following clause with the changed result — it can't stand alone.":"本來 menyatakan situasi atau rencana awal sebelum terjadi perubahan, biasanya dipasangkan dengan 後來 atau 可是 untuk menunjukkan kontras. Diperlukan klausa berikutnya yang menyatakan hasil yang berubah — tidak bisa berdiri sendiri.","We didn't know each other at first, but after chatting a bit we quickly became close.":"Awalnya kami tidak saling kenal, tetapi setelah mengobrol sebentar kami cepat menjadi akrab.","I originally planned to go out today, but it started raining.":"Awalnya saya berencana keluar hari ini, tetapi hujan mulai turun.","then / after that (sequence)":"kemudian / setelah itu (urutan)","A, ránhòu B":"A, ránhòu B","Ránhòu links actions in sequence and can start a new clause on its own, unlike hòulái, which only narrates past events, not future plans. Learners often overuse ránhòu as filler in speech; in writing, avoid chaining too many ránhòu in a row.":"Ránhòu menghubungkan tindakan secara berurutan dan dapat memulai klausa baru dengan sendirinya, berbeda dengan hòulái, yang hanya menceritakan peristiwa masa lalu, bukan rencana masa depan. Pembelajar sering terlalu banyak menggunakan ránhòu sebagai kata pengisi saat berbicara; dalam tulisan, hindari merangkai terlalu banyak ránhòu secara berturut-turut.","I like to eat the vegetables first, then the meat, and only then the rice.":"Saya suka makan sayur dulu, lalu daging, baru kemudian nasi.","I do my homework first, and then watch TV.":"Saya mengerjakan PR dulu, lalu menonton TV.","doing two things at the same time":"melakukan dua hal secara bersamaan","A + yìbiān + Verb1 + yìbiān + Verb2":"A + yìbiān + Verba1 + yìbiān + Verba2","Yìbiān...yìbiān... needs one single subject doing two actions simultaneously, and yìbiān must be repeated before each verb. Avoid pairing actions that can't physically happen at once.":"Yìbiān...yìbiān... memerlukan satu subjek tunggal yang melakukan dua tindakan secara bersamaan, dan yìbiān harus diulang sebelum setiap verba. Hindari memasangkan tindakan yang secara fisik tidak mungkin dilakukan bersamaan.","He is eating while looking at his phone.":"Dia makan sambil melihat ponselnya.","She does her homework while listening to music.":"Dia mengerjakan PR sambil mendengarkan musik.","first...then... (sequence of actions)":"pertama...kemudian... (urutan tindakan)","Xiān + Verb1 + zài + Verb2":"Xiān + Verba1 + zài + Verba2","Xiān...zài... marks the fixed order of two actions by the same subject. Note zài here means 'then', not 'again' (its more common meaning). It stresses sequence more strongly than ránhòu, which just links clauses loosely.":"Xiān...zài... menandai urutan tetap dari dua tindakan yang dilakukan oleh subjek yang sama. Perhatikan bahwa zài di sini berarti 'kemudian', bukan 'lagi' (arti yang lebih umum). Ini menekankan urutan lebih kuat daripada ránhòu, yang hanya menghubungkan klausa secara longgar.","Everyone finds a seat first, then orders food.":"Semua orang mencari tempat duduk dulu, baru memesan makanan.","I wash my hands first and then eat.":"Saya mencuci tangan dulu baru makan.","about to happen soon":"akan segera terjadi","(Time word) + jiù yào + Verb/Adj + le":"(Kata waktu) + jiù yào + Verba/Adjektiva + le","Jiù yào...le marks something about to happen soon and often pairs with a specific time word like xià ge xīngqī. A key contrast with kuàiyào...le (the next point) is that kuàiyào generally cannot follow a specific future time word like míngtiān.":"Jiù yào...le menandai sesuatu yang akan segera terjadi dan sering dipasangkan dengan kata waktu tertentu seperti xià ge xīngqī. Perbedaan penting dengan kuàiyào...le (poin berikutnya) adalah bahwa kuàiyào umumnya tidak bisa mengikuti kata waktu masa depan tertentu seperti míngtiān.","School is about to start next week.":"Sekolah akan segera dimulai minggu depan.","The train is about to arrive at the station.":"Kereta akan segera tiba di stasiun.","(Subject) + kuàiyào + Verb/Adj + le":"(Subjek) + kuàiyào + Kata kerja/Kata sifat + le","Kuàiyào...le is close in meaning to jiù yào...le, but unlike jiù yào it cannot directly follow a specific future time word such as míngtiān or xià xīngqī. A common mistake is saying míngtiān kuàiyào...le — use jiù yào there instead.":"Kuàiyào...le memiliki arti yang mirip dengan jiù yào...le, tetapi berbeda dengan jiù yào, kuàiyào tidak bisa langsung mengikuti kata waktu masa depan yang spesifik seperti míngtiān atau xià xīngqī. Kesalahan umum adalah mengatakan míngtiān kuàiyào...le — gunakan jiù yào untuk kasus tersebut.","Summer vacation is about to end.":"Liburan musim panas akan segera berakhir.","My younger sister is about to cry.":"Adik perempuan saya hampir menangis.","V + 一下 (do something briefly)":"V + 一下 (melakukan sesuatu sebentar)","V + 一下":"V + 一下","\"V一下\" softens a verb into a brief, casual action or polite request (\"just take a look\"). Don't confuse it with \"V一次\", which counts occurrences. It works like verb reduplication (看看) but is far more common in speech.":"\"V一下\" melunakkan kata kerja menjadi tindakan singkat dan santai atau permintaan yang sopan (\"coba lihat sebentar\"). Jangan disamakan dengan \"V一次\", yang menghitung jumlah kejadian. Pola ini bekerja seperti pengulangan kata kerja (看看), tetapi jauh lebih umum digunakan dalam percakapan.","I'll take you to the nearby library to have a look around.":"Saya akan mengajak Anda melihat-lihat perpustakaan di dekat sini.","Wait for me a moment, I'll be right back.":"Tunggu saya sebentar, saya akan segera kembali.","(When) ...的時候 (during the time when)":"(Saat) ...的時候 (pada waktu ketika)","(When) A 的時候, B":"(Saat) A 的時候, B","\"(When)...的時候\" marks the time frame during which something is happening; \"當\" is optional and more literary. Don't confuse it with \"如果\" (if) — 的時候 states an actual time, while 如果 states a hypothetical condition.":"\"(Saat)...的時候\" menandai kerangka waktu terjadinya suatu peristiwa; \"當\" bersifat opsional dan lebih formal/sastra. Jangan disamakan dengan \"如果\" (jika) — 的時候 menyatakan waktu yang nyata, sedangkan 如果 menyatakan kondisi hipotesis.","When he's angry, it's best not to joke around with him.":"Saat dia sedang marah, sebaiknya jangan bercanda dengannya.","When it rains, I like to read books at home.":"Saat hujan turun, saya suka membaca buku di rumah.","V + 上 (upward, onto, closing)":"V + 上 (ke atas, menempel, menutup)","V + 上":"V + 上","The verb + \"上\" directional complement shows upward movement, or attaching/closing something onto a surface (關上, 穿上). Distinguish it from \"起\", which emphasizes lifting something up from below.":"Pelengkap arah kata kerja + \"上\" menunjukkan gerakan ke atas, atau memasang/menutup sesuatu pada suatu permukaan (關上, 穿上). Bedakan dengan \"起\", yang menekankan mengangkat sesuatu dari bawah.","He just went back upstairs again; I don't know what he went to get.":"Dia baru saja naik ke atas lagi; saya tidak tahu dia pergi mengambil apa.","Please close the window.":"Tolong tutup jendelanya.","V + 下 (downward, settling into place)":"V + 下 (ke bawah, menetap pada posisinya)","V + 下":"V + 下","The verb + \"下\" directional complement shows downward movement or settling into a position (坐下, 躺下). It also extends to the abstract sense of \"recording\" something, as in 寫下. Don't confuse the direction with \"上\", its opposite.":"Pelengkap arah kata kerja + \"下\" menunjukkan gerakan ke bawah atau menetap pada suatu posisi (坐下, 躺下). Pola ini juga meluas ke makna abstrak \"mencatat\" sesuatu, seperti pada 寫下. Jangan disamakan arahnya dengan \"上\", yang merupakan kebalikannya.","They chose the seat closest to the door and sat down.":"Mereka memilih kursi yang paling dekat dengan pintu lalu duduk.","It's too hot, let's sit down and rest for a bit first.":"Cuacanya terlalu panas, ayo duduk dan istirahat sebentar dulu.","V + 起 (lift up)":"V + 起 (mengangkat)","V + 起":"V + 起","The verb + \"起\" directional complement shows lifting something up from a lower position (拿起, 撿起, 舉起). Keep it distinct from \"起來\", a more complex, later-level pattern that adds a sense of an action starting or a change occurring.":"Pelengkap arah kata kerja + \"起\" menunjukkan tindakan mengangkat sesuatu dari posisi yang lebih rendah (拿起, 撿起, 舉起). Bedakan dengan \"起來\", pola yang lebih kompleks dan tingkat lanjut, yang menambahkan makna dimulainya suatu tindakan atau terjadinya suatu perubahan.","He picked up a pen and wrote down the phone number and address.":"Dia mengambil pena dan menuliskan nomor telepon serta alamatnya.","He picked up a pen from the ground.":"Dia mengambil sebuah pena dari tanah.","V + 滿 (fill up)":"V + 滿 (mengisi penuh)","S + V + 滿 (+了) + O":"S + V + 滿 (+了) + O","\"V+滿\" is a result complement meaning the action fills something up completely. Common mistake: putting 了 before 滿 (should be V+滿+了). It marks the result of an action, not just \"a lot of.\"":"\"V+滿\" adalah pelengkap hasil yang berarti tindakan tersebut membuat sesuatu menjadi penuh sepenuhnya. Kesalahan umum: meletakkan 了 sebelum 滿 (seharusnya V+滿+了). Ini menandai hasil dari suatu tindakan, bukan sekadar berarti \"banyak\".","The bus was packed full of standing passengers.":"Bus itu penuh sesak dengan penumpang yang berdiri.","The classroom was filled with seated students.":"Ruang kelas dipenuhi siswa yang duduk.","also...also... (both)":"juga...juga... (keduanya)","A + (也) + V1, 也 + V2":"A + (也) + V1, 也 + V2","Links two verb phrases with 也...也... to show both things are true or possible. Different from 又...又...: 也...也... often pairs options/abilities, while 又...又... pairs simultaneous states or qualities.":"Menghubungkan dua frasa kata kerja dengan 也...也... untuk menunjukkan bahwa kedua hal tersebut benar atau memungkinkan. Berbeda dari 又...又...: 也...也... biasanya memasangkan pilihan/kemampuan, sedangkan 又...又... memasangkan keadaan atau sifat yang terjadi secara bersamaan.","Strawberries can be made into juice, and also into cake.":"Stroberi bisa dibuat menjadi jus, dan juga bisa dibuat menjadi kue.","He can speak both Chinese and English.":"Dia bisa berbicara bahasa Mandarin maupun bahasa Inggris.","sometimes...sometimes...":"kadang...kadang...","有時候 + V1, 有時候 + V2":"有時候 + V1, 有時候 + V2","Describes alternating situations for the same subject — \"sometimes X, sometimes Y\" occurring irregularly over time. Don't confuse it with 一邊...一邊..., which means doing two things at the same time.":"Menggambarkan situasi yang berganti-ganti untuk subjek yang sama — \"kadang X, kadang Y\" yang terjadi secara tidak teratur seiring waktu. Jangan disamakan dengan 一邊...一邊..., yang berarti melakukan dua hal secara bersamaan.","The department store's promotions are sometimes discounts, sometimes free gifts.":"Promosi department store itu kadang berupa diskon, kadang berupa hadiah gratis.","Sometimes I ride my bike to work, and sometimes I take the MRT.":"Kadang saya naik sepeda ke tempat kerja, kadang saya naik MRT.","to/toward (someone)":"kepada/terhadap (seseorang)","A + 對 + B + V":"A + 對 + B + V","A preposition marking the target of an action or emotion (\"toward/at someone\"). Easily confused with 跟 (a partner doing something together); 對 marks a one-directional action toward the target.":"Preposisi yang menandai target suatu tindakan atau emosi (\"terhadap/kepada seseorang\"). Mudah tertukar dengan 跟 (mitra yang melakukan sesuatu bersama-sama); 對 menandai tindakan satu arah menuju target.","After Miss Li heard the news, she smiled happily at me.":"Setelah Nona Li mendengar berita itu, dia tersenyum gembira kepada saya.","The teacher said some encouraging words to the students.":"Guru mengatakan beberapa kata-kata penyemangat kepada para siswa.","interested in...":"tertarik pada...","A + 對 + N + 有興趣":"A + 對 + N + 有興趣","Fixed pattern \"對 + object + 有興趣\" means \"interested in ___.\" Different from 喜歡 (liking/enjoying); 有興趣 expresses curiosity or interest. Common mistake: using 興趣 as a verb (×他興趣畫畫).":"Pola tetap \"對 + objek + 有興趣\" berarti \"tertarik pada ___.\" Berbeda dari 喜歡 (menyukai/menikmati); 有興趣 mengungkapkan rasa ingin tahu atau ketertarikan. Kesalahan umum: menggunakan 興趣 sebagai kata kerja (×他興趣畫畫).","He is very interested in drawing and wants to be a painter in the future.":"Dia sangat tertarik pada menggambar dan ingin menjadi pelukis di masa depan.","My younger sister is very interested in music and practices the piano every day.":"Adik perempuan saya sangat tertarik pada musik dan berlatih piano setiap hari.","on behalf of / instead of":"atas nama / menggantikan","A + 替 + B + VP (A does the action for/instead of B)":"A + 替 + B + VP (A melakukan tindakan untuk/menggantikan B)","'替' is a coverb marking who benefits from or is substituted for in an action, similar to 'for/on behalf of'. Don't confuse it with '給', which marks the recipient of an action rather than substitution.":"'替' adalah kata kerja bantu (coverb) yang menandai siapa yang diuntungkan atau digantikan dalam suatu tindakan, mirip dengan 'untuk/atas nama'. Jangan disamakan dengan '給', yang menandai penerima suatu tindakan, bukan penggantian.","Could you wrap up the gift for me?":"Bisakah kamu membungkuskan hadiah ini untuk saya?","Mom is sick, so I'll go grocery shopping for her.":"Ibu sedang sakit, jadi saya akan pergi belanja bahan makanan untuknya.","in order to / for the purpose of":"agar / untuk tujuan","為了 + goal, Subject + VP (states the purpose before the action)":"為了 + tujuan, Subjek + FV (menyatakan tujuan sebelum tindakan)","'為了' introduces a purpose or goal before the action that achieves it, and can appear either before or after the subject. Unlike '因為' (which gives a reason/cause), '為了' points to an intended, not-yet-realized goal.":"'為了' memperkenalkan tujuan atau sasaran sebelum tindakan yang mencapainya, dan dapat muncul sebelum atau sesudah subjek. Berbeda dengan '因為' (yang menyatakan alasan/sebab), '為了' menunjuk pada tujuan yang dimaksudkan namun belum terwujud.","He came to Taiwan (in order) to learn Chinese.":"Dia datang ke Taiwan untuk belajar bahasa Mandarin.","I study every night for the exam.":"Saya belajar setiap malam demi ujian.","verb reduplication (do a bit of / try doing) — ABAB pattern for two-syllable verbs":"reduplikasi kata kerja (melakukan sedikit / mencoba melakukan) — pola ABAB untuk kata kerja dua suku kata","VP (2-syllable) + same VP again → ABAB (e.g. 討論討論)":"FV (2 suku kata) + FV yang sama diulang → ABAB (misalnya 討論討論)","Reduplicating a two-syllable verb (ABAB, e.g. 討論討論) softens the action, suggesting 'give it a try' or 'do it a bit'. Unlike one-syllable AA reduplication (看看), the whole two-syllable verb repeats as a single unit.":"Mereduplikasi kata kerja dua suku kata (ABAB, misalnya 討論討論) melunakkan tindakan, menyiratkan 'coba lakukan' atau 'lakukan sedikit'. Berbeda dengan reduplikasi AA untuk kata kerja satu suku kata (看看), seluruh kata kerja dua suku kata diulang sebagai satu kesatuan.","Where to go during winter break — let's discuss it together.":"Mau ke mana saat libur musim dingin — ayo kita diskusikan bersama.","When you have time, could you tell me a bit about this place?":"Kalau ada waktu, bisakah kamu ceritakan sedikit tentang tempat ini?","reduplicated stative verb as predicate (AA的/AABB的) — intensifies description":"kata kerja statif yang direduplikasi sebagai predikat (AA的/AABB的) — memperkuat deskripsi","Subject (+ noun) + reduplicated stative verb (AA的/AABB的)":"Subjek (+ kata benda) + kata kerja statif yang direduplikasi (AA的/AABB的)","A one-syllable stative verb reduplicates as AA的 (大大的) and a two-syllable one as AABB的 (乾乾淨淨的), forming a vivid descriptive predicate. Don't confuse this with verb reduplication like 討論討論, which signals 'trying a bit', not intensified description.":"Kata kerja statif satu suku kata direduplikasi menjadi AA的 (大大的) dan yang dua suku kata menjadi AABB的 (乾乾淨淨的), membentuk predikat deskriptif yang hidup. Jangan disamakan dengan reduplikasi kata kerja seperti 討論討論, yang menandakan 'mencoba sedikit', bukan deskripsi yang diperkuat.","My roommate has big eyes and long hair.":"Teman sekamar saya bermata besar dan berambut panjang.","He cleaned the room until it was spotless.":"Dia membersihkan kamar sampai bersih sekali.","reduplicated stative verb as an attributive modifier (AA的 + noun)":"kata kerja statif yang direduplikasi sebagai pewatas atributif (AA的 + kata benda)","reduplicated stative verb (AA的) + noun (e.g. 短短的時間)":"kata kerja statif yang direduplikasi (AA的) + kata benda (misalnya 短短的時間)","AA的 (e.g. 短短的) modifies a following noun as an attributive, emphasizing the quality vividly. It has the same AA的 form used as a predicate (see the related point on stative-verb reduplication as predicate), but here it sits before a noun as a modifier instead.":"AA的 (misalnya 短短的) mewatasi kata benda yang mengikutinya sebagai atributif, menekankan sifat secara hidup. Bentuknya sama dengan AA的 yang digunakan sebagai predikat (lihat poin terkait tentang reduplikasi kata kerja statif sebagai predikat), tetapi di sini ia berada sebelum kata benda sebagai pewatas.","This shop's cakes are famous — they always sell out within a short time.":"Kue dari toko ini terkenal — selalu terjual habis dalam waktu singkat.","There's a tall tree in the park, and lots of kids like playing underneath it.":"Di taman ada pohon yang tinggi, dan banyak anak-anak suka bermain di bawahnya.","repeating a state verb (AABB) as an adverb":"mereduplikasi kata kerja statif (AABB) sebagai kata keterangan","AABB (reduplicated state verb) + 地 + Verb":"AABB (kata kerja statif yang direduplikasi) + 地 + Kata kerja","Reduplicate a disyllabic state verb into AABB and add 地 to describe how an action is done; monosyllabic ones instead double as AA (e.g. 慢慢). Don't confuse with plain repetition used only for emphasis.":"Reduplikasikan kata kerja statif dua suku kata menjadi AABB dan tambahkan 地 untuk menjelaskan cara suatu tindakan dilakukan; sedangkan yang satu suku kata direduplikasi menjadi AA (misalnya 慢慢). Jangan disamakan dengan pengulangan biasa yang hanya digunakan untuk penekanan.","He's sitting quietly.":"Dia sedang duduk dengan tenang.","The children are playing happily.":"Anak-anak sedang bermain dengan gembira.","try doing V once":"coba lakukan V sekali","V + V + 看":"V + V + 看","Reduplicating a verb and adding 看 means \"try V-ing and see (what happens)\" — a light suggestion. It's not used for past events (avoid ×吃吃看了) or in negative sentences.":"Mereduplikasi kata kerja lalu menambahkan 看 berarti 'coba V dan lihat (apa yang terjadi)' — sebuah saran ringan. Struktur ini tidak digunakan untuk peristiwa masa lalu (hindari ×吃吃看了) atau dalam kalimat negatif.","This bread is delicious, try eating it.":"Roti ini enak, coba dimakan.","Try on this piece of clothing.":"Coba pakaian ini.","not yet":"belum","還沒(有) + Verb (Phrase)":"還沒(有) + Kata Kerja (Frasa Kerja)","Marks an action that hasn't happened yet; 有 is optional (還沒吃 = 還沒有吃). Unlike 不 (plain negation), 還沒 implies the action is still expected to happen later.":"Menandai suatu tindakan yang belum terjadi; 有 bersifat opsional (還沒吃 = 還沒有吃). Berbeda dengan 不 (negasi biasa), 還沒 menyiratkan bahwa tindakan tersebut masih diharapkan akan terjadi di kemudian hari.","I haven't given you the money for the train ticket I just bought yet.":"Saya belum memberimu uang untuk tiket kereta yang baru saja saya beli.","He hasn't eaten breakfast yet.":"Dia belum makan sarapan.","not very / not too":"tidak terlalu / tidak begitu","不太/不很 + Adj (Verb)":"不太/不很 + Kata Sifat (Kata Kerja)","A softened way to say something isn't very (adj/verb); 不太 is common in speech while 不很 is more formal and less frequent. Don't confuse it with 很不 (a strong negative).":"Cara yang lebih halus untuk mengatakan sesuatu tidak begitu (kata sifat/kata kerja); 不太 umum digunakan dalam percakapan, sedangkan 不很 lebih formal dan jarang digunakan. Jangan bingung dengan 很不 (negasi yang kuat).","The place where you live isn't very easy to find, so it took me a while to find it.":"Tempat tinggalmu tidak terlalu mudah ditemukan, jadi butuh waktu bagi saya untuk menemukannya.","This movie isn't very good.":"Film ini tidak terlalu bagus.","don't need to / no need to":"tidak perlu","不用/不必 + Verb (Phrase)":"不用/不必 + Kata Kerja (Frasa Kerja)","Expresses that something isn't necessary; 不用 is common in speech, 不必 sounds slightly more formal/polite. Don't confuse with 不能 (cannot/not allowed) — 不用來 (\"no need to come\") ≠ 不能來 (\"can't come\").":"Menyatakan bahwa sesuatu tidak diperlukan; 不用 umum digunakan dalam percakapan, 不必 terdengar sedikit lebih formal/sopan. Jangan bingung dengan 不能 (tidak bisa/tidak diperbolehkan) — 不用來 (\"tidak perlu datang\") ≠ 不能來 (\"tidak bisa datang\").","He rented a place outside, so he doesn't need to live at school this semester anymore.":"Dia menyewa tempat tinggal di luar, jadi semester ini dia tidak perlu tinggal di sekolah lagi.","You don't need to worry about this.":"Kamu tidak perlu khawatir tentang hal ini.","Is it that...? (softened guessing question)":"Apakah...? (pertanyaan dugaan yang diperhalus)","Shì bu shì + VP":"Shì bu shì + Frasa Verba","\"Shì bu shì\" turns a statement into a soft guessing question and can be inserted right before the verb phrase—unlike \"是嗎,\" which only tags the whole sentence.":"\"Shì bu shì\" mengubah sebuah pernyataan menjadi pertanyaan dugaan yang halus dan dapat disisipkan tepat sebelum frasa verba—berbeda dengan \"是嗎,\" yang hanya dapat ditambahkan di akhir seluruh kalimat.","You don't look so well—are you sick?":"Kamu terlihat kurang sehat—apakah kamu sakit?","Did you forget to bring your umbrella?":"Apakah kamu lupa membawa payung?","How about...? (seeking agreement)":"Bagaimana kalau...? (mencari persetujuan)","VP + hǎo bu hǎo":"Frasa Verba + hǎo bu hǎo","\"Hǎo bu hǎo\" follows a suggestion to seek the listener's agreement, sounding more casual and spoken than the similar \"好嗎.\"":"\"Hǎo bu hǎo\" mengikuti sebuah saran untuk mencari persetujuan pendengar, terdengar lebih santai dan lisan dibandingkan dengan \"好嗎\" yang serupa.","Let's pick a location and open a shop to do business, how about that?":"Kita pilih satu lokasi lalu buka toko untuk berbisnis, bagaimana?","Shall we go watch a movie together tomorrow?":"Bagaimana kalau besok kita nonton film bersama?","quite a lot of... (emphasizing quantity)":"cukup banyak... (menekankan jumlah)","hǎo + jǐ/duō/xiē + measure word":"hǎo + jǐ/duō/xiē + kata penggolong","\"Hǎo\" before \"jǐ/duō/xiē\" + measure word emphasizes that the quantity is larger than expected, unlike the neutral \"jǐ/duō/xiē\" alone.":"\"Hǎo\" sebelum \"jǐ/duō/xiē\" + kata penggolong menekankan bahwa jumlahnya lebih banyak dari yang diharapkan, berbeda dengan \"jǐ/duō/xiē\" netral saja.","He loves eating dumplings—he eats several plates every time.":"Dia sangat suka makan pangsit—setiap kali makan beberapa piring.","I waited for the bus for several hours.":"Saya menunggu bus selama beberapa jam.","adverbial marker showing manner":"penanda adverbia yang menunjukkan cara","Adj/manner word + de + Verb":"Kata sifat/kata cara + de + Kata kerja","\"Dì\" (read as neutral \"de\") links a manner word to the following verb. Learners often confuse it with \"的\" (attributive) or \"得\" (complement), all pronounced \"de.\"":"\"Dì\" (dibaca netral sebagai \"de\") menghubungkan kata cara dengan kata kerja yang mengikutinya. Pembelajar sering mengacaukannya dengan \"的\" (atributif) atau \"得\" (pelengkap), yang semuanya diucapkan \"de\".","He walks slowly.":"Dia berjalan pelan-pelan.","She smiled happily.":"Dia tersenyum dengan gembira.","I wonder whether... / not sure if...":"Entah apakah... / tidak yakin apakah...","Bù zhīdào + (yes/no question) + clause":"Bù zhīdào + (pertanyaan ya/tidak) + klausa","\"Bù zhīdào\" at the start of a sentence introduces an embedded yes/no question (是不是/能不能/會不會...), meaning \"I wonder whether...\"; the subject \"我\" is usually dropped.":"\"Bù zhīdào\" di awal kalimat memperkenalkan pertanyaan ya/tidak yang disisipkan (是不是/能不能/會不會...), yang berarti \"entah apakah...\"; subjek \"我\" biasanya dihilangkan.","I wonder if I'll be able to get up at six tomorrow morning.":"Entah apakah saya bisa bangun jam enam besok pagi.","I wonder whether he'll come to class today.":"Entah apakah dia akan datang ke kelas hari ini.","then, in that case":"kalau begitu, dalam hal itu","If..., then...":"Jika..., maka...","\"那麼\" introduces a conclusion or suggestion based on a stated condition, similar to \"then/in that case.\" In casual speech it's often shortened to \"那.\" Common after \"如果/要是\" clauses.":"\"那麼\" memperkenalkan kesimpulan atau saran berdasarkan kondisi yang telah disebutkan, mirip dengan \"kalau begitu/dalam hal itu.\" Dalam percakapan santai sering disingkat menjadi \"那.\" Umum muncul setelah klausa \"如果/要是\".","If you don't agree, then what do you suggest we should do?":"Kalau kamu tidak setuju, lalu menurutmu kita sebaiknya bagaimana?","If you don't want to go watch a movie, then let's go shopping.":"Kalau kamu tidak mau nonton film, kalau begitu kita pergi belanja saja.","then, in that case (casual)":"kalau begitu, dalam hal itu (santai)","(situation), then subject + (就)...":"(situasi), lalu subjek + (就)...","\"那\" picks up on what was just said or the current situation and introduces a spoken conclusion, more casual than \"那麼.\" Often paired with \"就.\"":"\"那\" mengambil dari apa yang baru saja dikatakan atau situasi saat ini dan memperkenalkan kesimpulan lisan, lebih santai daripada \"那麼.\" Sering dipasangkan dengan \"就.\"","Thanks, then I won't stand on ceremony.":"Terima kasih, kalau begitu saya tidak sungkan lagi.","You're already full, then I'll just eat the rest.":"Kamu sudah kenyang, kalau begitu saya habiskan sisanya saja.","don't (prohibition / friendly reminder)":"jangan (larangan / pengingat yang ramah)","(please) + don't + VP":"(tolong) + jangan + Frasa kerja","\"別\" is a colloquial contraction of \"不要,\" used for prohibitions or friendly reminders. Adding \"請\" makes it more polite; it's softer and more common in daily speech than \"不要.\"":"\"別\" adalah bentuk singkat sehari-hari dari \"不要,\" digunakan untuk larangan atau pengingat yang ramah. Menambahkan \"請\" membuatnya lebih sopan; kata ini lebih halus dan lebih umum digunakan dalam percakapan sehari-hari dibandingkan \"不要.\"","After you get off the plane, don't forget to make a phone call.":"Setelah turun dari pesawat, jangan lupa menelepon.","Don't worry, everything will be fine.":"Jangan khawatir, semuanya akan baik-baik saja.","please + VP (polite command)":"tolong + Frasa kerja (perintah sopan)","(please) + verb (phrase)":"(tolong) + kata kerja (frasa)","A verb phrase alone forms a command; adding \"請\" makes it polite, appropriate for elders or customers. Bare verb commands also appear in instructions and signs.":"Frasa kerja saja sudah membentuk perintah; menambahkan \"請\" membuatnya sopan, cocok untuk orang yang lebih tua atau pelanggan. Perintah dengan kata kerja polos juga muncul dalam petunjuk dan papan tanda.","Please drive carefully!":"Tolong berkendara dengan hati-hati!","Please be a little quieter, the baby is sleeping right now.":"Tolong pelankan sedikit suaranya, bayinya sedang tidur.","let's just... instead (suggestion after weighing options)":"lebih baik... saja (saran setelah mempertimbangkan pilihan)","..., let's just + VP + (吧)":"..., lebih baik + VP + (吧)","Used to suggest a choice after weighing options, meaning \"let's just... instead.\" \"還是\" conveys \"after all,\" while \"吧\" softens it into a suggestion, implying more deliberation than a plain \"吧\" suggestion.":"Digunakan untuk menyarankan suatu pilihan setelah mempertimbangkan berbagai opsi, berarti \"lebih baik... saja\". \"還是\" menyampaikan makna \"bagaimanapun juga/setelah dipikir-pikir\", sedangkan \"吧\" melunakkan kalimat menjadi sebuah saran, menyiratkan pertimbangan yang lebih matang dibandingkan saran dengan \"吧\" biasa.","There are too many people in line right now, let's just wait a bit and come back later!":"Sekarang antreannya terlalu banyak orang, lebih baik tunggu sebentar lalu kembali lagi nanti!","It's raining outside, let's just go hiking again tomorrow instead.":"Di luar sedang hujan, lebih baik pergi mendaki lagi besok saja.","should / ought to (obligation, advice)":"seharusnya / sebaiknya (kewajiban, saran)","S + 應該 + VP":"S + 應該 + VP","\"應該\" expresses what the speaker believes ought to be done — obligation or advice. Don't confuse it with \"可以\" (permission) or \"會\" (future likelihood). It's followed directly by a verb phrase.":"\"應該\" mengungkapkan apa yang menurut pembicara seharusnya dilakukan — kewajiban atau saran. Jangan disamakan dengan \"可以\" (izin) atau \"會\" (kemungkinan di masa depan). Kata ini langsung diikuti oleh frasa verba.","You should wipe off your sweat after exercising.":"Setelah berolahraga, kamu sebaiknya menyeka keringat.","It's cold, so you should put on another jacket.":"Cuacanya dingin, jadi kamu sebaiknya memakai jaket lagi.","should (norm-based expectation)":"seharusnya (ekspektasi berdasarkan norma/aturan)","This use of \"應該\" shares the same core meaning (\"should/ought to\") but tends to appear when the obligation comes from a rule or common expectation rather than personal advice — e.g. deadlines, procedures.":"Penggunaan \"應該\" ini memiliki makna inti yang sama (\"seharusnya/harus\") tetapi cenderung muncul ketika kewajiban berasal dari suatu aturan atau ekspektasi umum, bukan saran pribadi — misalnya tenggat waktu, prosedur.","Homework should be handed in to the teacher on time.":"Pekerjaan rumah seharusnya diserahkan kepada guru tepat waktu.","You should arrive five minutes early for the meeting.":"Kamu sebaiknya tiba lima menit lebih awal untuk rapat.","can (bring about a result)":"dapat (menghasilkan suatu akibat)","A + 可以 + 讓/使 + B + result":"A + 可以 + 讓/使 + B + hasil","Here \"可以\" doesn't mean permission — it expresses that something can bring about a beneficial result, often paired with 讓/使 + outcome. Distinguish it from 可以1 (permission) and 可以2 (ability).":"\"可以\" di sini bukan berarti izin — kata ini mengungkapkan bahwa sesuatu dapat menghasilkan suatu akibat yang bermanfaat, sering dipasangkan dengan 讓/使 + hasil. Bedakan dengan 可以1 (izin) dan 可以2 (kemampuan).","Swimming can make your body healthier.":"Berenang dapat membuat tubuhmu lebih sehat.","Drinking plenty of water can improve your skin.":"Minum banyak air dapat memperbaiki kulitmu.","start to (do)":"mulai (melakukan sesuatu)","V + 起來 (begin to V)":"V + 起來 (mulai V)","Here \"V起來\" marks the start of an action (\"begin to V\"), unlike the directional \"V起來\" (e.g. 站起來 \"stand up\"). It's common with verbs of emotion or sound, like laughing, crying, or singing.":"\"V起來\" di sini menandai awal suatu tindakan (\"mulai V\"), berbeda dengan \"V起來\" yang bermakna arah (misalnya 站起來 \"berdiri\"). Penggunaan ini umum pada kata kerja yang berkaitan dengan emosi atau suara, seperti tertawa, menangis, atau bernyanyi.","As soon as he heard the news, he burst out laughing happily.":"Begitu mendengar kabar itu, dia langsung tertawa terbahak-bahak dengan gembira.","The baby started crying as soon as she saw her mother.":"Bayi itu langsung mulai menangis begitu melihat ibunya.","put away / gather up":"menyimpan / merapikan","V + 起來 (put away/gather)":"V + 起來 (menyimpan/merapikan)","Here \"V起來\" indicates the result of gathering, closing up, or putting something away — as in 收起來, 摺起來, 包起來. It differs from the directional sense (standing up) and the inchoative sense (starting to laugh), so keep them distinct.":"\"V起來\" di sini menunjukkan hasil dari tindakan mengumpulkan, melipat, atau menyimpan sesuatu — seperti pada 收起來, 摺起來, 包起來. Ini berbeda dengan makna arah (berdiri) dan makna permulaan (mulai tertawa), jadi perlu dibedakan dengan jelas.","Summer has arrived, so the winter clothes can be put away.":"Musim panas telah tiba, jadi baju musim dingin bisa disimpan.","When you're done using it, remember to put the tools away.":"Setelah selesai menggunakannya, ingat untuk merapikan alat-alatnya.","V + 下去 (continue V-ing)":"V + 下去 (terus melakukan V)","\"V下去\" marks continuing an action already in progress; \"不能再V下去了\" means \"can't keep V-ing anymore.\" Don't confuse this aspectual use with the directional \"go down\" sense of 下去.":"\"V下去\" menandai kelanjutan suatu tindakan yang sedang berlangsung; \"不能再V下去了\" berarti \"tidak bisa terus V lagi.\" Jangan sampai bingung antara penggunaan aspek ini dengan makna arah \"turun ke bawah\" dari 下去.","Time's up, I can't keep talking anymore.":"Waktu habis, saya tidak bisa terus bicara lagi.","This game is too boring; I don't want to keep watching it anymore.":"Permainan ini terlalu membosankan; saya tidak mau terus menontonnya lagi.","only then (necessary condition)":"baru (syarat yang diperlukan)","(要/只有) A, 才 + B":"(要/只有) A, 才 + B","Here \"才\" marks a necessary condition — \"only if/by doing A can B happen,\" often paired with \"要…才…\" or \"只有…才…\". Don't confuse it with the \"才\" that comments on something being surprisingly early or small in amount.":"Di sini \"才\" menandai syarat yang diperlukan — \"hanya jika/dengan melakukan A maka B bisa terjadi,\" sering dipasangkan dengan \"要…才…\" atau \"只有…才…\". Jangan bingung dengan \"才\" yang mengomentari sesuatu yang ternyata terlalu cepat atau sedikit jumlahnya.","Only with a lot of practice can you learn a language well.":"Hanya dengan banyak berlatih kamu baru bisa menguasai suatu bahasa dengan baik.","You have to make a reservation first before you can go in and visit.":"Kamu harus melakukan reservasi terlebih dahulu baru bisa masuk dan berkunjung.","just did X (then immediately)":"baru saja melakukan X (lalu segera)","A + 才 + V1, 就 + V2":"A + 才 + V1, 就 + V2","Here \"才\" shows something just happened, and paired with \"就\" it presents two events occurring in quick succession. Don't confuse this with \"才2,\" which marks a necessary condition (\"only if...then\").":"Di sini \"才\" menunjukkan sesuatu baru saja terjadi, dan ketika dipasangkan dengan \"就\" ia menggambarkan dua peristiwa yang terjadi berurutan dengan cepat. Jangan bingung dengan \"才2,\" yang menandai syarat yang diperlukan (\"hanya jika...maka\").","He had just gone out when it started to rain.":"Dia baru saja keluar ketika hujan mulai turun.","I had just arrived at the office when I got a call from a client.":"Saya baru saja tiba di kantor ketika menerima telepon dari klien.","even just X already... (emphasis)":"baru X saja sudah... (penekanan)","光/只 + A, 就 + B":"光/只 + A, 就 + B","\"光…就…\" emphasizes that even a limited part alone already reaches a surprising degree (\"just X alone already...\"). It pairs with a limiting word like 光/只, unlike the \"就\" that simply marks sequence (\"then, right away\").":"\"光…就…\" menekankan bahwa bahkan hanya bagian yang terbatas saja sudah mencapai tingkat yang mengejutkan (\"baru X saja sudah...\"). Ini dipasangkan dengan kata pembatas seperti 光/只, berbeda dengan \"就\" yang hanya menandai urutan (\"lalu, langsung\").","There are a lot of banks on this street—just this intersection alone has four.":"Ada banyak sekali bank di jalan ini—baru di persimpangan ini saja sudah ada empat.","The stuff at this shop is expensive—just one cup of coffee alone costs two hundred dollars.":"Barang-barang di toko ini mahal—baru satu cangkir kopi saja sudah dua ratus dolar.","even more than... (comparison)":"bahkan lebih... daripada... (perbandingan)","A + 比 + B + 還 + adjective":"A + 比 + B + 還 + kata sifat","In the comparative pattern \"A比B還+adjective,\" \"還\" adds emphasis meaning \"even more,\" often implying the result is surprising. It functions much like \"更\" but is more common in spoken Taiwanese Mandarin.":"Dalam pola perbandingan \"A比B還+kata sifat,\" \"還\" menambahkan penekanan yang berarti \"bahkan lebih,\" sering menyiratkan hasilnya mengejutkan. Fungsinya mirip dengan \"更\" tetapi lebih umum digunakan dalam bahasa Mandarin lisan Taiwan.","At this restaurant, the water is even more expensive than the drinks.":"Di restoran ini, air putih bahkan lebih mahal daripada minumannya.","The younger sister's Chinese is even better than the older sister's.":"Bahasa Mandarin adik perempuan bahkan lebih baik daripada kakak perempuannya.","willing to (do)":"bersedia (melakukan)","Subject + 願意 + Verb (+ Object)":"Subjek + 願意 + Verba (+ Objek)","願意 expresses consent or willingness to do something, often in response to a request or offer — different from 想/要 which express simple desire. Negate with 不願意.":"願意 mengungkapkan persetujuan atau kesediaan untuk melakukan sesuatu, sering sebagai tanggapan atas suatu permintaan atau tawaran — berbeda dengan 想/要 yang menyatakan keinginan sederhana. Bentuk negatifnya adalah 不願意.","If there is a suitable job, would you be willing to accept it?":"Jika ada pekerjaan yang cocok, apakah kamu bersedia menerimanya?","She is willing to help us move.":"Dia bersedia membantu kami pindahan.","as long as... then...":"asalkan... maka...","只要 + condition, 就 + result":"只要 + syarat, 就 + hasil","只要...就... states a sufficient condition — this alone is enough. Learners often confuse it with 只有...才..., which states a necessary/exclusive condition.":"只要...就... menyatakan syarat yang cukup — cukup dengan syarat ini saja. Pembelajar sering keliru dengan 只有...才..., yang menyatakan syarat yang perlu/eksklusif.","As long as he has free time, he will go to attend this party.":"Selama dia punya waktu luang, dia akan datang menghadiri pesta ini.","As long as you work hard, you will succeed.":"Selama kamu bekerja keras, kamu akan berhasil.","only if...then... (exclusive condition)":"hanya jika...baru... (syarat eksklusif)","只有 + the only condition, 才 + result":"只有 + satu-satunya syarat, 才 + hasil","只有...才... marks a necessary/exclusive condition (no other way works), stricter than the sufficient-condition 只要...就.... A common mistake is using 只要 when 只有 is meant.":"只有...才... menandai syarat yang perlu/eksklusif (tidak ada cara lain yang berhasil), lebih ketat daripada syarat cukup 只要...就.... Kesalahan umum adalah menggunakan 只要 padahal yang dimaksud adalah 只有.","Only in an environment where you study Chinese can you learn it well.":"Hanya di lingkungan tempat kamu belajar bahasa Mandarin, kamu baru bisa mempelajarinya dengan baik.","Only by practicing a lot can you make progress.":"Hanya dengan banyak berlatih, kamu baru bisa membuat kemajuan.","have no choice but to":"tidak punya pilihan lain selain","Subject + 只好 + Verb Phrase":"Subjek + 只好 + Frasa Verba","只好 expresses a reluctant, forced choice given the circumstances — 'have no choice but to.' Unlike 只要...就.../只有...才... (which state conditions), 只好 marks the resulting action, not a condition.":"只好 mengungkapkan pilihan yang enggan dan terpaksa akibat keadaan — 'tidak punya pilihan lain selain.' Berbeda dengan 只要...就.../只有...才... (yang menyatakan syarat), 只好 menandai tindakan yang dihasilkan, bukan syarat.","It started raining heavily outside, so we had no choice but to stay in the hotel.":"Di luar mulai turun hujan lebat, jadi kami tidak punya pilihan lain selain tinggal di hotel.","My phone died, so I had no choice but to use a public phone.":"Ponsel saya mati, jadi saya tidak punya pilihan lain selain menggunakan telepon umum.","no matter... always...":"tidak peduli... selalu...","不管 + question word/alternative, 都 + result":"不管 + kata tanya/bentuk alternatif, 都 + hasil","不管 is followed by a question word (什麼/誰/怎麼) or an alternative form (A不A) to show the result stays the same regardless of the variable. The following 都 is required and should not be dropped.":"不管 diikuti oleh kata tanya (什麼/誰/怎麼) atau bentuk alternatif (A不A) untuk menunjukkan bahwa hasilnya tetap sama apa pun variabelnya. 都 yang mengikutinya wajib ada dan tidak boleh dihilangkan.","If you have any problem, no matter what time it is, you can call me.":"Jika kamu punya masalah apa pun, tidak peduli jam berapa pun, kamu bisa menelepon saya.","No matter whether the weather is good or not, we will set off.":"Tidak peduli cuacanya baik atau tidak, kami akan tetap berangkat.","more and more, [unit] by [unit]":"semakin lama semakin, [satuan] demi [satuan]","yī + M + bǐ + yī + M + adjective":"yī + M + bǐ + yī + M + kata sifat","Repeats a measure word (day, year, etc.) to show a gradual, ongoing change, followed by an adjective. Similar to 越來越, but emphasizes comparison unit-by-unit. Common mistake: writing the measure word only once instead of twice.":"Mengulang kata penggolong (hari, tahun, dsb.) untuk menunjukkan perubahan yang bertahap dan berkelanjutan, diikuti oleh kata sifat. Mirip dengan 越來越, tetapi menekankan perbandingan satuan demi satuan. Kesalahan umum: menulis kata penggolong hanya sekali, bukan dua kali.","Autumn has arrived, and the weather is getting colder day by day.":"Musim gugur telah tiba, cuaca semakin hari semakin dingin.","His Chinese is getting better day by day.":"Bahasa Mandarinnya semakin hari semakin baik.","much more ~ (than)":"jauh lebih ~ (daripada)","A + bǐ + B + stative verb + de duō":"A + bǐ + B + verba statif + de duō","Used after a 比 comparison to emphasize a large difference; 得多 attaches right after the stative verb and is interchangeable with 很多 in this position. Common mistake: placing 得多 somewhere else in the sentence instead of right after the adjective.":"Digunakan setelah perbandingan dengan 比 untuk menekankan perbedaan yang besar; 得多 melekat tepat setelah verba statif dan dapat dipertukarkan dengan 很多 pada posisi ini. Kesalahan umum: menempatkan 得多 di tempat lain dalam kalimat, bukan tepat setelah kata sifat.","His older brother is much older than him.":"Kakak laki-lakinya jauh lebih tua darinya.","This piece of clothing is much more expensive than that one.":"Baju ini jauh lebih mahal daripada yang itu.","A, especially (is) B":"A, terutama (adalah) B","Highlights a standout example within something already mentioned; 是 is optional but sounds more natural before a noun phrase. Similar to 特別, but 尤其 specifically singles out part of a group or situation already stated.":"Menyoroti contoh yang menonjol dari sesuatu yang sudah disebutkan; 是 bersifat opsional tetapi terdengar lebih alami sebelum frasa nomina. Mirip dengan 特別, tetapi 尤其 secara khusus menunjuk bagian tertentu dari kelompok atau situasi yang sudah disebutkan.","Department stores are often crowded, especially on weekends and holidays.":"Department store sering kali ramai, terutama pada akhir pekan dan hari libur.","I like fruit, especially mangoes.":"Saya suka buah-buahan, terutama mangga.","can/cannot manage to finish V":"bisa/tidak bisa menyelesaikan V","V + de/bù + liǎo":"V + de/bù + liǎo","A potential complement asking whether something can be finished or handled, due to quantity or ability limits. Here 了 is pronounced 'liǎo', not the aspect particle 'le' — a common mistake is misreading it as 'le'. It normally pairs with a quantifiable object.":"Pelengkap potensial yang menanyakan apakah sesuatu bisa diselesaikan atau ditangani, karena keterbatasan jumlah atau kemampuan. Di sini 了 dibaca 'liǎo', bukan partikel aspek 'le' — kesalahan umum adalah membacanya sebagai 'le'. Biasanya berpasangan dengan objek yang dapat dihitung jumlahnya.","Can you carry this many things?":"Bisakah kamu membawa barang sebanyak ini?","I can't handle this matter by myself.":"Saya tidak bisa menangani urusan ini sendirian.","can/cannot V (achieve the result)":"bisa/tidak bisa V (mencapai hasil)","V + de/bù + result complement":"V + de/bù + pelengkap hasil","Inserts 得 (possible) or 不 (impossible) between a verb and its result complement to show whether that result can be achieved. Unlike g3-184's V得/不了 (about finishing a quantity), this pairs with specific result complements like 懂/完/見. It cannot be used with a bare adjective.":"Menyisipkan 得 (mungkin) atau 不 (tidak mungkin) di antara kata kerja dan pelengkap hasilnya untuk menunjukkan apakah hasil tersebut bisa dicapai atau tidak. Berbeda dengan g3-184 (V得/不了, tentang menyelesaikan suatu jumlah), pola ini berpasangan dengan pelengkap hasil tertentu seperti 懂/完/見. Tidak bisa digunakan dengan kata sifat murni.","He can read and understand Chinese menus.":"Dia bisa membaca dan memahami menu berbahasa Mandarin.","I can't understand Taiwanese when I hear it.":"Saya tidak mengerti bahasa Taiwan (Hokkien) ketika mendengarnya.","whether something fits (into a space)":"apakah sesuatu muat (di dalam suatu ruang)","Noun + Verb + 得/不 + 下 (+ Object)":"Noun + Verb + 得/不 + 下 (+ Object)","\"V 得/不下\" expresses whether a space or container has enough room for something, focusing on physical capacity rather than general ability (which uses 得了/不了).":"\"V 得/不下\" menyatakan apakah sebuah ruang atau wadah memiliki cukup tempat untuk sesuatu, berfokus pada kapasitas fisik, bukan kemampuan secara umum (yang menggunakan 得了/不了).","Can a sofa fit in this room?":"Apakah sofa ini muat di ruangan ini?","This fridge is too small; it can't fit all this food.":"Kulkas ini terlalu kecil, tidak muat untuk semua makanan ini.","question word + 都/也 = \"any-/every-\"":"kata tanya + 都/也 = \"apa pun/setiap\"","Question word + (都/也) + Verb/Adjective":"Question word + (都/也) + Verb/Adjective","A question word (誰/什麼/哪裡…) followed by 都/也 loses its question meaning and instead means \"any-/every-\" — different from an actual question, a common confusion for beginners.":"Kata tanya (誰/什麼/哪裡…) yang diikuti 都/也 kehilangan makna pertanyaannya dan berarti \"apa pun/setiap\" — berbeda dari pertanyaan sungguhan, ini adalah kebingungan umum bagi pemula.","There are lots of seats here, so you can sit anywhere you like.":"Di sini banyak tempat duduk, jadi kamu bisa duduk di mana saja sesukamu.","He's easygoing, so you can chat with him anytime.":"Dia orangnya santai, jadi kamu bisa mengobrol dengannya kapan saja.","almost, roughly":"hampir, kira-kira","Subject + 差不多 + (都) + Predicate":"Subject + 差不多 + (都) + Predicate","差不多 means \"almost/roughly\" for degree, quantity, or time, often paired with 都 to stress \"nearly all.\" Unlike the guess-word 大概, 差不多 implies the value is genuinely close to the actual one.":"差不多 berarti \"hampir/kira-kira\" untuk menyatakan derajat, jumlah, atau waktu, sering dipasangkan dengan 都 untuk menekankan \"hampir semua\". Berbeda dengan kata perkiraan 大概, 差不多 menyiratkan bahwa nilainya benar-benar mendekati nilai sebenarnya.","We can start the party now — the guests have pretty much all arrived.":"Sekarang kita bisa mulai pestanya — tamu-tamu hampir semuanya sudah datang.","It's about five o'clock now, we should head home.":"Sekarang sudah sekitar jam lima, kita sebaiknya pulang.","extremely (adjective)~":"sangat/luar biasa (kata sifat)~","Stative Verb + 極了/得不得了/得很":"Stative Verb + 極了/得不得了/得很","極了/得不得了/得很 all attach after a stative verb (adjective) to mean \"extremely,\" but differ in tone: 極了 is the most natural colloquial choice, 得不得了 exaggerates for emphasis/surprise, and 得很 is more neutral/written. None of the three can follow an ordinary action verb — only stative verbs.":"極了/得不得了/得很 semuanya melekat setelah kata kerja statif (kata sifat) untuk menyatakan \"sangat/ekstrem\", tetapi berbeda nuansanya: 極了 adalah pilihan lisan paling alami, 得不得了 melebih-lebihkan untuk penekanan/keterkejutan, dan 得很 lebih netral/bergaya tulisan. Ketiganya tidak bisa mengikuti kata kerja tindakan biasa — hanya kata kerja statif.","He finally got concert tickets, and he was over the moon.":"Dia akhirnya mendapatkan tiket konser, dan dia sangat senang sekali.","This restaurant's beef noodles are incredibly delicious — we go eat there often.":"Mi sapi di restoran ini enak sekali — kami sering makan di sana.","unbearably/to death (extreme)":"tak tertahankan/mati rasanya (ekstrem)","Stative Verb + 死了":"Kata Kerja Statif + 死了","\"Vs死了\" follows a stative verb to mean \"unbearably/to death,\" an even more exaggerated, colloquial version of 極了 — typically used to complain about negative or intense feelings (busy, tired, hot). 死了 here is purely figurative, not literal death.":"\"Vs死了\" mengikuti kata kerja statif untuk menyatakan \"tak tertahankan/mati rasanya\", versi lisan yang lebih berlebihan daripada 極了 — biasanya digunakan untuk mengeluh tentang perasaan negatif atau intens (sibuk, lelah, panas). 死了 di sini murni bermakna kiasan, bukan kematian secara harfiah.","School work is killing me with how busy it is, and after class I still have to go to my part-time job.":"Tugas sekolah membuatku sibuk setengah mati, dan setelah kelas aku masih harus pergi kerja paruh waktu.","It's boiling hot today — I keep sweating like crazy.":"Hari ini panas sekali — aku terus berkeringat tak berhenti.","Expresses an extreme degree ('extremely ~')":"Menyatakan tingkat ekstrem (\"sangat ~\")","Stative Verb + 壞了":"Kata Kerja Statif + 壞了","'壞了' literally means 'broken,' but after a stative verb it's a colloquial intensifier meaning 'extremely.' Common fixed pairs include 餓壞了, 嚇壞了, 累壞了 — don't translate literally.":"\"壞了\" secara harfiah berarti \"rusak\", tetapi setelah kata kerja statif ia menjadi penguat makna dalam bahasa lisan yang berarti \"sangat\". Pasangan tetap yang umum termasuk 餓壞了, 嚇壞了, 累壞了 — jangan diterjemahkan secara harfiah.","He was busy all day and didn't eat anything, so he's starving.":"Dia sibuk seharian dan belum makan apa pun, jadi dia lapar sekali.","My little sister got lost, and mom was worried sick.":"Adik perempuanku tersesat, dan ibu jadi sangat khawatir sekali.","Expresses a slight excess in degree ('a little too ~')":"Menyatakan sedikit kelebihan tingkat (\"agak terlalu ~\")","Stative Verb + 了一點":"Kata Kerja Statif + 了一點","'Vs了一點' shows the degree slightly exceeds a standard, often implying a comparison or change. Unlike '有點Vs' (placed before the verb, no comparison implied), '了一點' goes after and suggests 'a bit more than expected/before.'":"\"Vs了一點\" menunjukkan tingkatnya sedikit melebihi suatu standar, sering mengandung makna perbandingan atau perubahan. Berbeda dengan \"有點Vs\" (diletakkan sebelum kata kerja, tanpa makna perbandingan), \"了一點\" diletakkan setelahnya dan menyiratkan \"sedikit lebih dari yang diharapkan/sebelumnya\".","Although there are a few more people in line, this restaurant's beef noodle soup is very famous.":"Meskipun antreannya sedikit lebih ramai, mi sapi restoran ini sangat terkenal.","This piece of clothing is a bit expensive, but the quality is very good.":"Baju ini agak sedikit mahal, tapi kualitasnya sangat bagus.","Expresses doing an action briefly/lightly, using the 把-construction with a reduplicated verb":"Menyatakan tindakan yang dilakukan secara singkat/ringan, menggunakan struktur 把 dengan kata kerja reduplikasi","把 + Object + V(一)V":"把 + Objek + V(一)V","Reduplicating the verb (V一V) after 把+Object softens the action, implying it's done briefly or casually. Just '把衣服洗' alone sounds incomplete/unnatural — the reduplication is what makes it colloquial and natural.":"Reduplikasi kata kerja (V一V) setelah 把+Objek melunakkan tindakan tersebut, menyiratkan bahwa itu dilakukan sebentar atau secara santai. Hanya mengatakan \"把衣服洗\" saja terdengar tidak lengkap/tidak alami — reduplikasi inilah yang membuatnya terdengar lisan dan alami.","The weather's nice today, remember to wash your clothes a little before you go out.":"Cuacanya bagus hari ini, ingat cuci baju sebentar sebelum keluar rumah ya.","Comb your hair a bit first, we're about to head out.":"Sisir dulu rambutmu sebentar, kita akan segera berangkat.","Expresses moving something to a destination via an action (把-construction + 到 + place + 來/去)":"Menyatakan pemindahan sesuatu ke suatu tujuan melalui suatu tindakan (struktur 把 + 到 + tempat + 來/去)","把 + Object + V到 + Place (+來/去)":"把 + Objek + V到 + Tempat (+來/去)","'把O V到地方' shows that as a result of the action, the object ends up at a specific place. Add 來 if movement is toward the speaker, 去 if away; it can be omitted when the speaker isn't at the destination.":"\"把O V到地方\" menunjukkan bahwa sebagai hasil dari tindakan tersebut, objek berakhir di suatu tempat tertentu. Tambahkan 來 jika gerakannya menuju pembicara, 去 jika menjauh; bisa dihilangkan jika pembicara tidak berada di tempat tujuan.","Please drive the car to the parking lot.":"Tolong kendarai mobilnya ke tempat parkir.","He moved the luggage into the room.":"Dia memindahkan bagasi ke dalam kamar.","Expresses that the object is disposed of/completely dealt with as a result of the action (把-construction + Verb + 了)":"Menyatakan bahwa objek dibuang/ditangani secara tuntas sebagai hasil dari tindakan tersebut (struktur 把 + Kata Kerja + 了)","把 + Object + Verb + 了":"把 + Objek + Kata Kerja + 了","'把O V了' expresses that the object is disposed of, gone, or completely finished with — common verbs include 賣了, 丟了, 吃了. Unlike '把O V到...', the focus isn't on where it went but that it's now gone/done.":"'把O V了' menyatakan bahwa objek dibuang, hilang, atau sudah selesai sepenuhnya — kata kerja yang umum digunakan antara lain 賣了, 丟了, 吃了. Berbeda dengan '把O V到...', fokusnya bukan ke mana perginya, melainkan bahwa objek itu kini sudah tidak ada/selesai.","This piece of clothing doesn't fit anymore, so I plan to sell it.":"Baju ini sudah tidak muat lagi, jadi saya berencana menjualnya.","The milk in the fridge went bad, so mom poured it out.":"Susu di dalam kulkas sudah basi, jadi ibu membuangnya.","Bǎ + object + verb + result complement (emphasizes the completed result)":"Bǎ + objek + kata kerja + pelengkap hasil (menekankan hasil yang telah selesai)","Bǎ + O + V + Result Complement (+ le)":"Bǎ + O + V + Pelengkap Hasil (+ 了)","A bǎ-sentence stating the result of an action on the object. The verb must be followed by a result complement like 好 or 完; leaving it out makes the sentence feel unfinished.":"Kalimat bǎ yang menyatakan hasil suatu tindakan terhadap objek. Kata kerja harus diikuti oleh pelengkap hasil seperti 好 atau 完; jika dihilangkan, kalimat akan terasa belum selesai.","He has washed the vegetables clean.":"Dia sudah mencuci sayur sampai bersih.","I washed the bowls clean.":"Saya sudah mencuci mangkuk sampai bersih.","Bǎ + object + verb + zài + place (the object ends up at that location)":"Bǎ + objek + kata kerja + zài + tempat (objek akhirnya berada di tempat tersebut)","Bǎ + O + V + zài + Place":"Bǎ + O + V + zài + Tempat","Shows where an object ends up after the action. 在 must be followed by a place word; don't move the 在+place phrase in front of 把.":"Menunjukkan di mana objek berakhir setelah tindakan dilakukan. 在 harus diikuti oleh kata tempat; jangan memindahkan frasa 在+tempat ke depan 把.","I put the book on the table.":"Saya meletakkan buku itu di atas meja.","I put the key in the drawer.":"Saya menaruh kunci itu di dalam laci.","Bǎ + N1 (thing) + V + gěi + N2 (person) — hand/send the thing to someone":"Bǎ + N1 (benda) + V + gěi + N2 (orang) — menyerahkan/mengirimkan benda itu kepada seseorang","Bǎ + N1 + V + gěi + N2":"Bǎ + N1 + V + gěi + N2","Emphasizes handing or sending a thing to someone using bǎ. The verb is limited to transfer verbs like 寄, 送, 還, and 給 is always followed by the recipient.":"Menekankan tindakan menyerahkan atau mengirimkan sesuatu kepada seseorang dengan menggunakan bǎ. Kata kerja terbatas pada kata kerja transfer seperti 寄, 送, 還, dan 給 selalu diikuti oleh penerima.","After you get home, please send the mail to me.":"Setelah kamu sampai di rumah, tolong kirimkan surat itu kepada saya.","I gave the birthday present to my older sister.":"Saya memberikan hadiah ulang tahun itu kepada kakak perempuan saya.","Bèi + (agent) + V + de + result/degree — a passive expressing the resulting state or degree":"Bèi + (pelaku) + V + de + hasil/tingkat — kalimat pasif yang menyatakan keadaan atau tingkat akibat","Bèi + (N) + V + de + Result/Degree Complement":"Bèi + (N) + V + de + Pelengkap Hasil/Tingkat","Adds a degree complement to a passive sentence to show how strongly the action affected the subject. The agent (N) is optional; after 得 comes an adjective or a potential-form result.":"Menambahkan pelengkap tingkat pada kalimat pasif untuk menunjukkan seberapa kuat tindakan itu memengaruhi subjek. Pelaku (N) bersifat opsional; setelah 得 muncul kata sifat atau hasil dalam bentuk potensial.","The neighbor's noise was too loud, and my younger sister couldn't sleep because of it.":"Suara berisik dari tetangga terlalu keras, sehingga adik perempuan saya tidak bisa tidur karenanya.","He did poorly on the exam, and his father scolded him so much that he felt very upset.":"Dia mendapat nilai buruk dalam ujian, dan dimarahi ayahnya sampai merasa sangat kesal.","actually / in fact (introduces a truth that differs from what was assumed)":"sebenarnya / sesungguhnya (memperkenalkan kebenaran yang berbeda dari yang diasumsikan sebelumnya)","(previous statement), qíshí + the actual fact":"(pernyataan sebelumnya), qíshí + fakta sebenarnya","An adverb that corrects a prior assumption or statement by revealing the real situation. It can appear at the start of a sentence or after the subject; more colloquial than 事實上.":"Kata keterangan yang mengoreksi asumsi atau pernyataan sebelumnya dengan mengungkapkan situasi yang sebenarnya. Kata ini bisa muncul di awal kalimat atau setelah subjek; lebih bersifat percakapan dibandingkan 事實上.","Exercising twice a week is actually not that hard.":"Berolahraga dua kali seminggu sebenarnya tidak sesulit itu.","This question looks hard, but it's actually simple.":"Soal ini terlihat sulit, tetapi sebenarnya sederhana.","everything is fine except for one thing":"semuanya baik-baik saja kecuali satu hal","Subject + 什麼都 + VP1, 就是 + VP2 (the one exception, often negative)":"Subjek + 什麼都 + VP1, 就是 + VP2 (satu pengecualian, biasanya bernada negatif)","什麼都 states a broad 'anything goes,' then 就是 marks the single exception. Beginners often mistake this 就是 for the copula 'to be' rather than the adverb meaning 'just/only.'":"什麼都 menyatakan makna umum 'apa saja boleh,' lalu 就是 menandai satu pengecualian. Pemula sering salah mengira 就是 di sini sebagai kopula 'adalah,' padahal sebenarnya adverbia yang berarti 'hanya/cuma'.","He eats anything, except he's just too scared to eat stinky tofu.":"Dia makan apa saja, hanya saja dia terlalu takut untuk makan tahu busuk.","I'll eat any kind of fruit, except I just don't like durian.":"Saya makan buah apa saja, hanya saja saya tidak suka durian.","action completed and ready/well done":"tindakan telah selesai dan sudah siap/beres","V + 好 (+ le)":"V + 好 (+ le)","好 as a resultative complement marks that an action is finished AND its result is now ready/satisfactory. Unlike 完, which only marks the action ending, 好 adds a sense of 'all set.' A common error is swapping 好 and 完 freely, e.g. saying 準備完 instead of 準備好.":"好 sebagai pelengkap hasil menandai bahwa suatu tindakan telah selesai DAN hasilnya kini sudah siap/memuaskan. Berbeda dengan 完, yang hanya menandai berakhirnya tindakan, 好 menambahkan nuansa 'sudah beres.' Kesalahan umum adalah menukar 好 dan 完 secara sembarangan, misalnya mengatakan 準備完 alih-alih 準備好.","A typhoon is coming soon, so Mom already bought all the food and water in advance.":"Topan akan segera datang, jadi Ibu sudah membeli semua makanan dan air terlebih dahulu.","Dinner is ready, we can eat now.":"Makan malam sudah siap, kita bisa makan sekarang.","action is finished/used up":"tindakan telah selesai/habis","V + 完 (+ object / le)":"V + 完 (+ object / le)","完 simply marks that an action ran its full course and is over, without 好's nuance of 'ready/well done.' Pay attention to word order V完+object (e.g. 買完菜), not placing the object before the verb.":"完 hanya menandai bahwa suatu tindakan telah berlangsung sepenuhnya dan berakhir, tanpa nuansa 'siap/beres' seperti 好. Perhatikan urutan kata V完+objek (misalnya 買完菜), jangan menempatkan objek sebelum kata kerja.","He just finished buying groceries at the market.":"Dia baru saja selesai membeli bahan makanan di pasar.","I've already finished my homework.":"Saya sudah selesai mengerjakan PR.","two actions in a row, no conjunction needed":"dua tindakan berurutan, tidak perlu kata sambung","VP1 + VP2 (in the order the actions occur)":"VP1 + VP2 (sesuai urutan terjadinya tindakan)","A serial verb construction places two verb phrases sharing one subject back-to-back, in the order the actions happen, with no conjunction between them; the second VP often shows the purpose of the first. Inserting 然後 or 和 between them is a common mistake.":"Konstruksi verba berangkai menempatkan dua frasa verba yang berbagi satu subjek secara berurutan, sesuai urutan terjadinya tindakan, tanpa kata sambung di antaranya; frasa verba kedua sering menunjukkan tujuan dari frasa pertama. Menyisipkan 然後 atau 和 di antara keduanya adalah kesalahan yang umum terjadi.","I'm going home to eat dinner now.":"Saya pulang untuk makan malam sekarang.","He goes to the library to read books.":"Dia pergi ke perpustakaan untuk membaca buku.","had only just done A when B already happened":"baru saja melakukan A ketika B sudah terjadi","才 + VP1, (Subject) + 就 + VP2":"才 + VP1, (Subjek) + 就 + VP2","才 stresses that very little time had passed, and 就 shows the next event followed right away, usually with a sense of surprise at how soon it happened. This differs from 一...就..., which states immediate succession without implying the interval felt surprisingly short.":"才 menekankan bahwa waktu yang berlalu sangat singkat, sedangkan 就 menunjukkan bahwa kejadian berikutnya langsung menyusul, biasanya dengan nuansa keheranan atas betapa cepatnya hal itu terjadi. Ini berbeda dari struktur 一...就..., yang hanya menyatakan kejadian yang langsung berurutan tanpa menyiratkan bahwa jedanya terasa mengejutkan singkat.","I had only been talking with him for a little while when he already left early because he had something to do.":"Saya baru berbicara dengannya sebentar, tetapi dia sudah pulang lebih awal karena ada urusan.","My little sister had only been asleep for a little while when she already woke up.":"Adik perempuan saya baru tidur sebentar tetapi sudah terbangun lagi.","hasn't (done) for (a period of time)":"belum (melakukan) selama (suatu jangka waktu)","Duration + méi + V (+ le)":"Duration + méi + V (+ le)","\"Duration + méi + verb (+ le)\" expresses that an action has not occurred for a stretch of time, continuing up to now. Unlike a normal negative sentence, the time duration comes before the verb, not after.":"\"Durasi + méi + kata kerja (+ le)\" menyatakan bahwa suatu tindakan tidak terjadi selama suatu jangka waktu, berlanjut hingga sekarang. Berbeda dengan kalimat negatif biasa, durasi waktu diletakkan sebelum kata kerja, bukan sesudahnya.","He hasn't slept for two days, so let him sleep a bit more.":"Dia sudah dua hari tidak tidur, jadi biarkan dia tidur lebih lama sedikit.","I haven't showered for three days, I really want to take a hot shower.":"Saya sudah tiga hari belum mandi, saya benar-benar ingin mandi air panas.","starting from / from ... on":"mulai dari / sejak ... dan seterusnya","Cóng + time point + qǐ":"Cóng + time point + qǐ","\"Cóng + time point + qǐ\" marks a starting point, similar to \"cóng...kāishǐ\" but qǐ sounds slightly more formal or written.":"\"Cóng + titik waktu + qǐ\" menandai suatu titik awal, mirip dengan \"cóng...kāishǐ\" tetapi qǐ terdengar sedikit lebih formal atau bergaya tulisan.","From now on, you should eat more vegetables and less meat.":"Mulai sekarang, kamu sebaiknya makan lebih banyak sayur dan lebih sedikit daging.","Starting next month, I'm going to start exercising.":"Mulai bulan depan, saya akan mulai berolahraga.","can/cannot afford to V":"mampu/tidak mampu (secara finansial) untuk V","V + de/bu + qǐ":"V + de/bu + qǐ","\"Verb + de/bu + qǐ\" is a potential complement meaning one can or cannot afford something, usually about money. Unlike néng/huì, which express general ability, qǐ specifically implies financial capacity.":"\"Kata kerja + de/bu + qǐ\" adalah pelengkap potensial yang menyatakan mampu atau tidak mampu melakukan sesuatu, biasanya terkait uang. Berbeda dengan néng/huì yang menyatakan kemampuan secara umum, qǐ secara khusus menyiratkan kemampuan finansial.","This watch is on sale now, so even an average student can afford it.":"Jam tangan ini sedang diskon sekarang, jadi bahkan siswa biasa pun mampu membelinya.","This restaurant is too expensive, I can't afford to eat here.":"Restoran ini terlalu mahal, saya tidak mampu makan di sini.","can/cannot tell (by observation)":"bisa/tidak bisa mengenali (melalui pengamatan)","V + (de/bu) + chūlái":"V + (de/bu) + chūlái","\"Verb + de/bu + chūlái\" expresses being able (or unable) to tell, recognize, or perceive something through observation. Here chūlái is abstract, meaning a judgment or result \"emerges,\" not literal movement outward.":"\"Kata kerja + de/bu + chūlái\" menyatakan mampu (atau tidak mampu) mengenali, membedakan, atau menangkap sesuatu melalui pengamatan. Di sini chūlái bersifat abstrak, berarti suatu penilaian atau hasil \"muncul\", bukan gerakan keluar secara harfiah.","Judging from the way he talks, you can't tell that he's nervous.":"Dilihat dari cara bicaranya, kamu tidak bisa mengenali bahwa dia sedang gugup.","She's changed so much that I almost couldn't recognize who she was.":"Dia berubah begitu banyak sehingga saya hampir tidak bisa mengenali siapa dia.","to firmly fix/hold/remember through V":"menetapkan/memegang/mengingat dengan kuat melalui V","V + zhù":"V + zhù","\"Verb + zhù\" is a resultative complement showing the object becomes firmly fixed or held in place as a result of the action. \"Jìzhù\" means to firmly commit something to memory — unlike \"jìde\" (to remember, a state), it emphasizes completing the act of memorizing.":"\"Kata kerja + zhù\" adalah pelengkap hasil yang menunjukkan objek menjadi tetap atau tertahan di tempatnya sebagai akibat dari tindakan tersebut. \"Jìzhù\" berarti mengingat sesuatu dengan kuat dan mantap — berbeda dengan \"jìde\" (mengingat, suatu keadaan), kata ini menekankan selesainya tindakan menghafal.","My older sister learned it just once and remembered all the steps.":"Kakak perempuan saya belajar sekali saja dan sudah mengingat semua langkahnya.","He grabbed my hand and wouldn't let me go.":"Dia menggenggam erat tangan saya dan tidak mau melepaskannya.","the action reaches its goal/result":"tindakan mencapai tujuan/hasilnya","V + 著 (zháo)":"V + 著 (zháo)","\"著\" (zháo) shows an action reached its result, e.g. 睡著 \"fell asleep.\" Don't confuse it with durative 著 (zhe) — same character, different meaning.":"\"著\" (zháo) menunjukkan bahwa suatu tindakan telah mencapai hasilnya, misalnya 睡著 \"tertidur\". Jangan bingung dengan 著 (zhe) yang bermakna durasi/berlangsung — karakter yang sama, tetapi maknanya berbeda.","He fell asleep quickly right after finishing his milk.":"Dia langsung tertidur segera setelah menghabiskan susunya.","He looked for a long time and finally found his passport.":"Dia mencari lama sekali dan akhirnya menemukan paspornya.","whether one has the physical strength to move something":"apakah seseorang memiliki tenaga fisik untuk memindahkan sesuatu","V + de/bu + dòng":"V + de/bu + dòng","\"V得/不動\" is a potential complement showing whether you're physically strong enough to move something. Don't confuse it with the broader \"V得/不了 (liǎo)\" (able/unable to do something) or the modal \"能.\"":"\"V得/不動\" adalah pelengkap potensial yang menunjukkan apakah kamu cukup kuat secara fisik untuk memindahkan sesuatu. Jangan bingung dengan \"V得/不了 (liǎo)\" yang lebih umum (mampu/tidak mampu melakukan sesuatu) atau kata modal \"能\".","Can you carry these bookshelves?":"Bisakah kamu mengangkat rak buku ini?","This table is too heavy — I can't move it by myself.":"Meja ini terlalu berat — saya tidak bisa memindahkannya sendirian.","having become used to / accustomed to doing something":"sudah terbiasa / menjadi biasa melakukan sesuatu","V + guàn (+ le)":"V + guàn (+ le)","\"V慣\" is a result complement showing repeated experience has made something a habit (e.g. 住慣 = used to living somewhere). It differs from the noun/verb \"習慣,\" so the two aren't interchangeable.":"\"V慣\" adalah pelengkap hasil yang menunjukkan bahwa pengalaman berulang telah membuat sesuatu menjadi kebiasaan (misalnya 住慣 = terbiasa tinggal di suatu tempat). Ini berbeda dari kata benda/kata kerja \"習慣,\" sehingga keduanya tidak dapat saling menggantikan.","He's already gotten used to city life, so he often feels out of place when he goes to the countryside.":"Dia sudah terbiasa dengan kehidupan kota, jadi dia sering merasa canggung ketika pergi ke pedesaan.","I've gotten used to living in Taipei, so suddenly moving to the countryside feels a bit hard to adjust to.":"Saya sudah terbiasa tinggal di Taipei, jadi jika tiba-tiba pindah ke pedesaan akan agak sulit menyesuaikan diri.","something disappearing, being disposed of, or used up":"sesuatu yang menghilang, dibuang, atau habis digunakan","V + diào (+ le)":"V + diào (+ le)","\"V掉\" is a result complement showing something disappears or gets disposed of because of the action (e.g. 賣掉 = sold off, 丟掉 = thrown away). Unlike plain \"V完\" (finished), it always carries the sense of something being removed or gone.":"\"V掉\" adalah pelengkap hasil yang menunjukkan sesuatu menghilang atau dibuang akibat tindakan tersebut (misalnya 賣掉 = terjual habis, 丟掉 = dibuang). Berbeda dengan \"V完\" (selesai) yang sederhana, kata ini selalu membawa makna bahwa sesuatu telah disingkirkan atau hilang.","Business was great today — we sold out four pairs of shoes in no time.":"Bisnis hari ini sangat bagus — kami berhasil menjual habis empat pasang sepatu dalam sekejap.","The fruit in the fridge went bad, so I threw it all away.":"Buah di kulkas sudah busuk, jadi saya membuang semuanya.","an action continuing on and on without stopping":"suatu tindakan yang terus berlangsung tanpa henti","V + ge + bùtíng/méiwán":"V + ge + bùtíng/méiwán","\"V個不停/沒完\" is a colloquial pattern showing an action goes on and on without stopping, often with a complaining tone. Here \"個\" isn't the measure word for counting — it's a structural particle emphasizing manner, so don't confuse the two uses.":"\"V個不停/沒完\" adalah pola bahasa sehari-hari yang menunjukkan suatu tindakan berlangsung terus-menerus tanpa henti, sering dengan nada mengeluh. Di sini \"個\" bukan kata penggolong untuk menghitung — melainkan partikel struktural yang menekankan cara, jadi jangan sampai keliru dengan penggunaan yang lain.","He loves dancing — whenever he hears music, he dances non-stop.":"Dia sangat suka menari — setiap kali mendengar musik, dia menari tanpa henti.","Whenever he starts talking about basketball, he goes on and on until everyone's sick of hearing it.":"Setiap kali dia mulai membicarakan bola basket, dia terus bicara tanpa henti sampai semua orang bosan mendengarnya.","do something to one's heart's content":"melakukan sesuatu sepuas hati","V + 個 + 夠":"V + 個 + 夠","'V個夠' attaches directly after a verb to add a colloquial nuance of doing something 'to one's heart's content' or 'until fully satisfied.' '個' is unstressed (neutral tone) and no object follows.":"'V個夠' ditempelkan langsung setelah kata kerja untuk menambahkan nuansa bahasa sehari-hari yang berarti melakukan sesuatu 'sepuas hati' atau 'sampai benar-benar puas.' '個' diucapkan tanpa tekanan (nada netral) dan tidak diikuti oleh objek.","This concert has thirty songs in total, so you can listen to your heart's content in one go.":"Konser ini memiliki total tiga puluh lagu, jadi kamu bisa mendengarkan sepuasnya sekaligus.","This all-you-can-eat restaurant is very cheap, so you can eat to your heart's content.":"Restoran all-you-can-eat ini sangat murah, jadi kamu bisa makan sepuasnya.","Place + V: something exists/is located somewhere":"Tempat + V: sesuatu ada/berada di suatu tempat","Place Word + V + 著 + (quantity) + Noun":"Kata Tempat + V + 著 + (jumlah) + Kata Benda","This 'Place + V(+著)' pattern states that something exists at a location (existential sentence). The subject is the place, and the noun that follows is typically new information, often with a quantifier.":"Pola 'Tempat + V(+著)' ini menyatakan bahwa sesuatu berada di suatu lokasi (kalimat eksistensial). Subjeknya adalah tempat, dan kata benda yang mengikutinya biasanya merupakan informasi baru, sering disertai kata penggolong.","There is a lot of fresh fruit placed on the dining table.":"Di atas meja makan diletakkan banyak buah segar.","There is a painting hanging on the wall.":"Di dinding tergantung sebuah lukisan.","'會...的': a confident prediction that something will happen":"'會...的': prediksi yang penuh keyakinan bahwa sesuatu akan terjadi","(是) + 會 + V/Adj + 的":"(是) + 會 + V/Adj + 的","Adding sentence-final '的' after '會 + V' turns a simple possibility into a confident assertion that something will definitely happen — stronger in certainty than '會V' alone.":"Menambahkan '的' di akhir kalimat setelah '會 + V' mengubah kemungkinan biasa menjadi pernyataan yang penuh keyakinan bahwa sesuatu pasti akan terjadi — lebih kuat kepastiannya dibandingkan hanya '會V' saja.","As people grow up, their way of thinking will change.":"Seiring bertambahnya usia seseorang, cara berpikirnya akan berubah.","As long as you practice hard, your Chinese will improve.":"Selama kamu berlatih dengan giat, bahasa Mandarinmu akan meningkat.","'(連)...都/也+不/沒...': emphasizes an extreme case ('not even...')":"'(連)...都/也+不/沒...': menekankan kasus ekstrem ('bahkan tidak...')","(連) + N/Clause + 都/也 + 不/沒 + V":"(連) + N/Klausa + 都/也 + 不/沒 + V","'連' can be omitted, but '都/也' cannot — they form the required emphatic pairing. This structure cites an extreme example to strongly deny something ('not even...'). The quantity-word pattern '一...都/也不/沒' works the same way.":"'連' dapat dihilangkan, tetapi '都/也' tidak bisa — keduanya membentuk pasangan penekanan yang wajib ada. Struktur ini mengutip contoh ekstrem untuk menyangkal sesuatu dengan tegas ('bahkan tidak...'). Pola kata bilangan '一...都/也不/沒' bekerja dengan cara yang sama.","I didn't even know that a gym had opened right next to my house.":"Saya bahkan tidak tahu bahwa ada pusat kebugaran yang baru buka tepat di sebelah rumah saya.","He left without saying a single word.":"Dia pergi tanpa mengucapkan sepatah kata pun.","'not A, then B': it must be one or the other of two possibilities":"'bukan A, maka B': harus salah satu dari dua kemungkinan","不是 + A, 就是 + B":"不是 + A, 就是 + B","Expresses that one of two options, A or B, is always the case — similar to '或者...或者...' but more assertive, emphasizing that it's strictly one or the other.":"Menyatakan bahwa salah satu dari dua pilihan, A atau B, selalu berlaku — mirip dengan '或者...或者...' tetapi lebih tegas, menekankan bahwa itu pasti salah satu dari keduanya.","On weekends, he either plays basketball or goes jogging.":"Pada akhir pekan, dia bermain basket atau jogging.","This drink is either too sweet or too sour.":"Minuman ini terlalu manis atau terlalu asam.","doing an action briefly or casually":"melakukan suatu tindakan sebentar atau secara santai","V + 了 + V (verb reduplication for a brief, completed action)":"V + 了 + V (reduplikasi kata kerja untuk tindakan singkat yang telah selesai)","Reduplicating a verb softens the action to \"do it a little.\" Use \"V了V\" for something already done; use plain \"VV\" or \"V一V\" for general or future actions.":"Reduplikasi kata kerja melunakkan tindakan menjadi \"melakukannya sedikit.\" Gunakan \"V了V\" untuk sesuatu yang sudah dilakukan; gunakan \"VV\" atau \"V一V\" biasa untuk hal yang bersifat umum atau akan datang.","Ms. Wang smiled happily for a moment.":"Nona Wang tersenyum bahagia sejenak.","He thought about it for a moment and decided not to go.":"Dia berpikir sejenak lalu memutuskan untuk tidak pergi.","expresses \"one by one\" / \"step by step\"":"menyatakan \"satu per satu\" / \"langkah demi langkah\"","yī + measure word + yī + measure word":"yī + kata penggolong + yī + kata penggolong","Repeating \"yī + measure word\" twice shows an action happening gradually, one unit at a time; the same measure word must be used both times.":"Mengulangi \"yī + kata penggolong\" dua kali menunjukkan suatu tindakan yang terjadi secara bertahap, satu unit pada satu waktu; kata penggolong yang sama harus digunakan kedua kalinya.","They climbed up step by step.":"Mereka mendaki setapak demi setapak.","We got on the bus one by one.":"Kami naik bus satu per satu.","expresses a change to \"no longer doing something\"":"menyatakan perubahan menjadi \"tidak lagi melakukan sesuatu\"","bú zài + verb (phrase) + le":"bú zài + kata kerja (frasa) + le","This shows a change from a past habit or state to no longer being true now. The final \"了\" is required — dropping it makes the change unclear.":"Ini menunjukkan perubahan dari kebiasaan atau keadaan di masa lalu menjadi tidak lagi berlaku sekarang. \"了\" di akhir kalimat wajib ada — menghilangkannya membuat perubahan tersebut tidak jelas.","After finding a job, he no longer worries about money.":"Setelah mendapatkan pekerjaan, dia tidak lagi khawatir tentang uang.","After I moved, I no longer take the bus to work.":"Setelah saya pindah rumah, saya tidak lagi naik bus untuk pergi kerja.","expresses strong negation, \"not at all\"":"menyatakan penyangkalan yang kuat, \"sama sekali tidak\"","yìdiǎn + (noun) + yě/dōu + bù/méi + verb/adj":"yìdiǎn + (kata benda) + yě/dōu + bù/méi + kata kerja/kata sifat","\"一點都/也不\" strongly negates an adjective or state, while \"一點也沒 + verb\" strongly negates a completed action. \"都\" is common in speech; \"也\" often precedes a negated verb.":"\"一點都/也不\" menyangkal dengan kuat suatu kata sifat atau keadaan, sedangkan \"一點也沒 + kata kerja\" menyangkal dengan kuat suatu tindakan yang telah selesai. \"都\" umum digunakan dalam bahasa lisan; \"也\" sering mendahului kata kerja yang dinegasikan.","When I was young, I wasn't tired at all even after staying up all night.":"Saat masih kecil, saya sama sekali tidak lelah meskipun begadang semalaman.","I haven't eaten anything at all today.":"Hari ini saya sama sekali belum makan apa pun.","expresses \"never (up to now)\" or \"never, as a firm rule\"":"menyatakan \"belum pernah (sampai sekarang)\" atau \"tidak pernah, sebagai aturan tetap\"","cónglái + bù/méi + verb (guo)":"cónglái + bù/méi + kata kerja (guo)","\"從來沒 + verb過\" means the experience has never happened at all, while \"從來不 + verb\" means it's a firm habit never to do something. Unlike degree negations like \"一點也不\", this negates frequency or experience, not degree.":"\"從來沒 + kata kerja過\" berarti pengalaman itu belum pernah terjadi sama sekali, sedangkan \"從來不 + kata kerja\" berarti kebiasaan tetap untuk tidak pernah melakukan sesuatu. Berbeda dengan negasi tingkat seperti \"一點也不\", ini menegasikan frekuensi atau pengalaman, bukan tingkat.","Li Minghua has never taken a flight before.":"Li Minghua belum pernah naik pesawat sebelumnya.","I never drink coffee.":"Saya tidak pernah minum kopi.","Negative question confirming a situation":"Pertanyaan negatif untuk mengonfirmasi suatu situasi","(situation), Subject + 不/沒 + VP + 嗎?":"(situasi), Subjek + 不/沒 + VP + 嗎?","Used to confirm a guess about someone's state (\"Aren't you...?\"). Use 沒 for past actions, 不 for states/habits. Unlike a plain yes/no question with 嗎, the speaker already has a hunch based on what they observe.":"Digunakan untuk mengonfirmasi dugaan tentang keadaan seseorang (\"Bukankah kamu...?\"). Gunakan 沒 untuk tindakan di masa lalu, 不 untuk keadaan/kebiasaan. Berbeda dengan pertanyaan ya/tidak biasa dengan 嗎, penutur sudah memiliki dugaan berdasarkan apa yang mereka amati.","Why did you come home so early today—aren't you feeling well?":"Kenapa hari ini kamu pulang begitu awal—bukankah kamu merasa tidak enak badan?","You look so pale—didn't you sleep well?":"Wajahmu terlihat pucat sekali—bukankah kamu tidak tidur nyenyak?","Rhetorical question emphasizing \"Isn't it...?\"":"Pertanyaan retoris yang menekankan \"Bukankah...?\"","Subject + 不是/沒 + VP + 嗎?":"Subjek + 不是/沒 + VP + 嗎?","The speaker is confident of the answer and uses this to press agreement or confirmation—stronger in tone than plain 不/沒+嗎, implying \"obviously, right?\" Use 不是 for facts/qualities already true, 沒 to confirm something hasn't happened.":"Penutur yakin dengan jawabannya dan menggunakan ini untuk mendesak persetujuan atau konfirmasi—nada lebih kuat daripada 不/沒+嗎 biasa, menyiratkan \"jelas begitu, kan?\". Gunakan 不是 untuk fakta/sifat yang sudah benar, 沒 untuk mengonfirmasi sesuatu yang belum terjadi.","If joining the activity means meeting more people, isn't that a good thing?":"Jika mengikuti kegiatan ini berarti bertemu lebih banyak orang, bukankah itu hal yang baik?","Didn't you already say you were full? Why are you still eating?":"Bukankah kamu sudah bilang kenyang? Kenapa masih makan?","Repeating a question word to mean \"whatever/wherever/whoever...\"":"Mengulang kata tanya untuk menyatakan makna \"apa pun/di mana pun/siapa pun...\"","Subject + 想/要 + QW + 就 + VP + QW":"Subjek + 想/要 + QW + 就 + VP + QW","The same question word (什麼, 哪裡, 誰, etc.) appears twice to mean \"it's entirely up to you / anything goes.\" A common mistake is changing or dropping the second question word—both must match exactly.":"Kata tanya yang sama (什麼, 哪裡, 誰, dsb.) muncul dua kali untuk menyatakan makna \"sepenuhnya terserah kamu / apa pun boleh\". Kesalahan umum adalah mengubah atau menghilangkan kata tanya kedua—keduanya harus sama persis.","This essay has no set topic, so you can write about whatever you want.":"Esai ini tidak memiliki topik yang ditentukan, jadi kamu bisa menulis tentang apa pun yang kamu inginkan.","You can go wherever you want—I'm fine with anywhere.":"Kamu boleh pergi ke mana pun yang kamu mau—di mana saja saya tidak masalah.","\"Among them/it\"—picking out part of a whole already mentioned":"\"Di antaranya\"—memilih sebagian dari keseluruhan yang telah disebutkan sebelumnya","(sentence naming a whole), 其中 + description of part of it":"(kalimat yang menyebutkan suatu keseluruhan), 其中 + deskripsi sebagian darinya","Refers back to a group or set just mentioned to single out part of it (\"among them...\"). The whole must be stated first (a number, a list, a category)—it can't open a sentence on its own.":"Merujuk kembali ke kelompok atau kumpulan yang baru disebutkan untuk memilih sebagiannya (\"di antaranya...\"). Keseluruhannya harus disebutkan terlebih dahulu (angka, daftar, kategori)—tidak bisa membuka kalimat sendirian.","Of the two brothers, one is suited to business and the other to teaching.":"Dari kedua bersaudara itu, satu cocok untuk bisnis dan yang lain cocok untuk mengajar.","This shop sells many kinds of snacks; among them, the most famous is braised pork rice.":"Toko ini menjual berbagai macam camilan; di antaranya, yang paling terkenal adalah nasi babi kecap.","\"Etc.\"—added after listing examples to show the list isn't complete":"\"Dan lain-lain\"—ditambahkan setelah menyebutkan contoh untuk menunjukkan bahwa daftarnya belum lengkap","像是/如 + A, B, C + 等(等)":"像是/如 + A, B, C + 等(等)","Placed after two or more listed examples to show there are more of the same kind. At the end of a sentence either 等 or 等等 works, but mid-sentence (before more text follows) only the single 等 sounds natural.":"Diletakkan setelah dua atau lebih contoh yang disebutkan untuk menunjukkan masih ada hal lain yang sejenis. Di akhir kalimat, baik 等 maupun 等等 bisa digunakan, tetapi di tengah kalimat (jika masih ada teks berikutnya) hanya 等 tunggal yang terdengar alami.","He loves sweets, like chocolate, cake, ice cream, and so on.":"Dia suka makanan manis, seperti cokelat, kue, es krim, dan sebagainya.","The school teaches many languages, such as English, Japanese, and Korean.":"Sekolah ini mengajarkan banyak bahasa, seperti bahasa Inggris, Jepang, dan Korea.","expressing a range with 以上/以下/以內/以外 (\"or more/less,\" \"within/beyond\")":"menyatakan suatu rentang dengan 以上/以下/以內/以外 (\"atau lebih/atau kurang\", \"dalam batas/di luar batas\")","Number (+ measure word) + 以上/以下/以內/以外":"Angka (+ kata penggolong) + 以上/以下/以內/以外","Attaches after a quantity to mark a boundary: 以上/以下 include the stated number, while 以內/以外 mark inside/outside a range. Common mistake: dropping the number before it.":"Melekat setelah suatu jumlah untuk menandai batas: 以上/以下 mencakup angka yang disebutkan, sedangkan 以內/以外 menandai bagian dalam/luar suatu rentang. Kesalahan umum: menghilangkan angka sebelum kata ini.","He spends more than two hours commuting every day.":"Dia menghabiskan lebih dari dua jam untuk pergi bekerja setiap hari.","There's a convenience store within five minutes of here.":"Ada minimarket dalam jarak lima menit dari sini.","expressing an exception with \"除了A以外，都B\" (all except A)":"menyatakan pengecualian dengan \"除了A以外，都B\" (semua kecuali A)","除了 + A (以外), + 都 + B":"除了 + A (以外), + 都 + B","Marks A as the sole exception, with 都 referring to everything else. Don't confuse this with the addition pattern \"除了A以外，還B,\" which adds something rather than excluding it.":"Menandai A sebagai satu-satunya pengecualian, sedangkan 都 merujuk pada semua hal lainnya. Jangan bingungkan dengan pola penambahan \"除了A以外，還B\", yang menambahkan sesuatu, bukan mengecualikannya.","Except for beef, I can eat all other kinds of meat.":"Kecuali daging sapi, saya bisa makan semua jenis daging lainnya.","Except for Sundays, I have to go to work every day.":"Kecuali hari Minggu, saya harus pergi bekerja setiap hari.","expressing addition with \"除了A以外，還/也B\" (besides A, also B)":"menyatakan penambahan dengan \"除了A以外，還/也B\" (selain A, juga B)","除了 + A + 以外, + 還/也 + B":"除了 + A + 以外, + 還/也 + B","Expresses addition: besides A, there is also B. Similar in form to the exclusion pattern \"除了A以外，都B\" — use 還/也 for \"in addition,\" 都 for \"all except.\"":"Menyatakan penambahan: selain A, ada juga B. Bentuknya mirip dengan pola pengecualian \"除了A以外，都B\" — gunakan 還/也 untuk \"selain itu\", dan 都 untuk \"semua kecuali\".","Besides a cup, this event also gives out a towel.":"Selain gelas, acara ini juga membagikan handuk.","Besides a bed, this room also has a desk.":"Selain tempat tidur, kamar ini juga memiliki meja.","expressing an approximate amount with 左右":"menyatakan jumlah perkiraan dengan 左右","Number + (measure word) + 左右":"Angka + (kata bantu bilangan) + 左右","Shows an approximate quantity (time, money, age, etc.). Avoid pairing it with 大約/大概 in the same phrase — 左右 alone already means \"approximately.\"":"Menunjukkan jumlah perkiraan (waktu, uang, usia, dll.). Hindari memakainya bersama 大約/大概 dalam satu frasa — 左右 saja sudah berarti \"kira-kira\".","It takes him about an hour to commute to work by public transportation every day.":"Setiap hari ia membutuhkan waktu sekitar satu jam untuk pergi bekerja dengan transportasi umum.","This jacket costs around NT$2,000.":"Jaket ini harganya sekitar NT$2.000.","expressing percentages with 百分之 + number":"menyatakan persentase dengan 百分之 + angka","百分之 + number":"百分之 + angka","\"百分之 + number\" expresses a percentage (百分之五 = 5%). Say 百分之 before the number, and don't read the \"%\" symbol literally.":"\"百分之 + angka\" menyatakan persentase (百分之五 = 5%). Ucapkan 百分之 sebelum angkanya, dan jangan membaca simbol \"%\" secara harfiah.","Only five percent of the people here have never been abroad.":"Hanya lima persen orang di sini yang belum pernah ke luar negeri.","Eighty percent of the students in this class can speak English.":"Delapan puluh persen siswa di kelas ini bisa berbicara bahasa Inggris.","expressing multiples":"menyatakan kelipatan","A + 是 + B + 的 + N + 倍 (+ Adj)":"A + 是 + B + 的 + N + 倍 (+ Adj)","Use \"A是B的N倍\" to say A is N times B. Always say 兩倍, never 二倍. 倍 only works for multiples larger than the base—use 一半 for \"half,\" not a fraction of 倍.":"Gunakan \"A是B的N倍\" untuk mengatakan A adalah N kali B. Selalu ucapkan 兩倍, jangan pernah 二倍. 倍 hanya berlaku untuk kelipatan yang lebih besar dari angka dasar — gunakan 一半 untuk \"setengah\", bukan pecahan dari 倍.","My sister's luggage is twice as heavy as mine.":"Koper kakak perempuan saya beratnya dua kali lipat koper saya.","This car costs three times as much as that car.":"Mobil ini harganya tiga kali lipat mobil itu.","expressing fractions":"menyatakan pecahan","N + 分之 + M":"N + 分之 + M","Say fractions as \"denominator + 分之 + numerator\" (三分之一 = 1/3)—reversed from English \"one third.\" Don't flip numerator and denominator.":"Ucapkan pecahan sebagai \"penyebut + 分之 + pembilang\" (三分之一 = 1/3) — kebalikan dari bahasa Inggris \"one third\". Jangan membalik pembilang dan penyebut.","He probably only rode about a third of this bike path.":"Dia mungkin hanya mengendarai sekitar sepertiga dari jalur sepeda ini.","I only ate a quarter of this cake.":"Saya hanya makan seperempat dari kue ini.","reading arithmetic operations":"cara membaca operasi hitung","A + 加/減/乘以/除以 + B + 等於 + C":"A + 加/減/乘以/除以 + B + 等於 + C","Use 加/減/乘以/除以 for +,−,×,÷ and place 等於 before the answer. A common mistake is dropping the 以 in 乘以/除以.":"Gunakan 加/減/乘以/除以 untuk +, −, ×, ÷ dan letakkan 等於 sebelum jawabannya. Kesalahan umum adalah menghilangkan 以 pada 乘以/除以.","Three plus two equals five, did you know that?":"Tiga tambah dua sama dengan lima, kamu tahu itu?","Eight divided by four equals two.":"Delapan dibagi empat sama dengan dua.","reading decimal points":"cara membaca titik desimal","Integer + 點 + decimal digits (read one by one)":"Bilangan bulat + 點 + digit desimal (dibaca satu per satu)","Read decimals as \"integer part + 點 + each digit separately\" (3.25 → 三點二五). Don't read the decimal part as a whole number like 二十五.":"Bacalah desimal sebagai \"bagian bulat + 點 + setiap digit secara terpisah\" (3.25 → 三點二五). Jangan membaca bagian desimal sebagai bilangan utuh seperti 二十五.","This fish weighs 3.25 kilograms.":"Ikan ini beratnya 3,25 kilogram.","My height is 1.65 meters.":"Tinggi badan saya 1,65 meter.","focusing on what the VP is":"menekankan pada apa isi VP","S + VP + 的 + 是 + O":"S + VP + 的 + 是 + O","\"VP+的+是+X\" highlights X as the focused answer to \"what [VP] is.\" Don't confuse it with plain \"VP+的\" (no 是) used alone as a nominalized noun phrase.":"\"VP+的+是+X\" menonjolkan X sebagai jawaban yang difokuskan untuk \"apa yang [VP]\". Jangan disamakan dengan \"VP+的\" biasa (tanpa 是) yang dipakai sendiri sebagai frasa nomina.","What this book discusses is the history of the Americas.":"Yang dibahas buku ini adalah sejarah benua Amerika.","What he likes is that shop's beef noodles.":"Yang dia sukai adalah mi sapi toko itu.","stop doing X":"berhenti melakukan X","Bié (zài) + VP + le":"Bié (zài) + VP + le","\"Bié zài...le\" means \"stop doing X\" — used to tell someone to stop an ongoing or repeated action. The final \"le\" marks a change of state. Unlike plain \"不要\", it implies the action was already happening.":"\"Bié zài...le\" berarti \"berhenti melakukan X\" — digunakan untuk menyuruh seseorang menghentikan tindakan yang sedang berlangsung atau berulang. \"le\" di akhir menandai perubahan keadaan. Berbeda dengan \"不要\" biasa, ini menyiratkan bahwa tindakan tersebut sudah terjadi sebelumnya.","Stop talking now, the match is about to start!":"Berhentilah bicara sekarang, pertandingannya akan segera dimulai!","Stop playing with your phone, hurry up and do your homework!":"Berhenti main ponsel, cepat kerjakan PR-mu!","may / be allowed to (formal written \"可以\")":"boleh / diizinkan (bentuk tulisan formal dari \"可以\")","(bù) kě + VP":"(bù) kě + VP","\"可\" is the formal written equivalent of \"可以\" (\"may/can\"), common in rules, notices, and official texts. In everyday speech, use \"可以\" instead — mixing them up sounds unnatural.":"\"可\" adalah bentuk tulisan formal yang setara dengan \"可以\" (\"boleh/dapat\"), umum digunakan dalam peraturan, pengumuman, dan teks resmi. Dalam percakapan sehari-hari, gunakan \"可以\" sebagai gantinya — mencampuradukkan keduanya akan terdengar tidak wajar.","The general public may not use this school's swimming pool for free.":"Masyarakat umum tidak diperbolehkan menggunakan kolam renang sekolah ini secara gratis.","Loud talking is not permitted inside the library.":"Berbicara keras tidak diperbolehkan di dalam perpustakaan.","can / be able to (formal written ability)":"dapat / mampu (kemampuan dalam bentuk tulisan formal)","kě + VP (expressing ability)":"kě + VP (menyatakan kemampuan)","\"可2\" expresses ability in formal writing, similar to \"能/可以\". It often appears in \"不但可...還能...\" patterns listing abilities. Unlike \"可1\" (permission), here it means capability, not being allowed.":"\"可2\" mengungkapkan kemampuan dalam tulisan formal, mirip dengan \"能/可以\". Ini sering muncul dalam pola \"不但可...還能...\" saat menyebutkan berbagai kemampuan. Berbeda dengan \"可1\" (izin), di sini artinya kapabilitas, bukan diperbolehkan.","He can not only understand what the teacher covers in class but also point out the key ideas.":"Dia tidak hanya bisa memahami apa yang diajarkan guru di kelas, tetapi juga bisa menunjukkan poin-poin utamanya.","This software can not only translate articles but also fix grammar mistakes.":"Perangkat lunak ini tidak hanya bisa menerjemahkan artikel, tetapi juga bisa memperbaiki kesalahan tata bahasa.","can (lead to) — an action/fact making a result possible":"dapat (menghasilkan) — suatu tindakan/fakta yang memungkinkan terjadinya suatu hasil","(action/fact) + kě + VP (result)":"(tindakan/fakta) + kě + VP (hasil)","\"可3\" is used when the subject is an action or fact (not a person), meaning \"doing this can lead to...\". Unlike \"可2\" (personal ability), the subject here is an event, and \"可\" shows its potential effect.":"\"可3\" digunakan ketika subjeknya adalah suatu tindakan atau fakta (bukan orang), yang berarti \"melakukan hal ini dapat menyebabkan...\". Berbeda dengan \"可2\" (kemampuan pribadi), subjek di sini adalah suatu peristiwa, dan \"可\" menunjukkan efek potensialnya.","Doing recycling properly can improve the environment.":"Melakukan daur ulang dengan benar dapat memperbaiki lingkungan.","Drinking more water can help prevent colds.":"Minum lebih banyak air dapat membantu mencegah pilek.","should / ought to":"sebaiknya / seharusnya","(bù) gāi + VP":"(bù) gāi + VP","\"該\" means \"should/ought to\", expressing obligation or what's proper — a shortened, more colloquial form close to \"應該\". Don't confuse it with \"會\" (will/likely), which expresses prediction, not obligation.":"\"該\" berarti \"seharusnya/sebaiknya\", mengungkapkan kewajiban atau hal yang pantas — bentuk yang lebih singkat dan sehari-hari, dekat dengan \"應該\". Jangan disamakan dengan \"會\" (akan/kemungkinan), yang mengungkapkan prediksi, bukan kewajiban.","We shouldn't normally eat overly salty food.":"Biasanya kita sebaiknya tidak makan makanan yang terlalu asin.","If you're not feeling well, you should go see a doctor.":"Jika kamu merasa tidak enak badan, kamu sebaiknya pergi ke dokter.","should / it's time to":"sebaiknya / sudah waktunya","Subject + 該 + Verb (+ 了)":"Subjek + 該 + Verba (+ 了)","\"該\" is a colloquial, shortened form of \"應該,\" expressing that circumstances now call for an action. It often pairs with sentence-final \"了\" to signal \"the time has come.\" Learners sometimes drop the \"了\" and lose that nuance, or confuse it with \"會\" (will happen) rather than \"should.\"":"\"該\" adalah bentuk sehari-hari yang lebih singkat dari \"應該\", yang mengungkapkan bahwa keadaan sekarang menuntut suatu tindakan. Kata ini sering berpasangan dengan \"了\" di akhir kalimat untuk menandakan \"saatnya telah tiba\". Pembelajar terkadang menghilangkan \"了\" sehingga kehilangan nuansa itu, atau menyamakannya dengan \"會\" (akan terjadi) alih-alih \"seharusnya\".","It's getting late, I should head home now.":"Hari sudah semakin larut, aku sebaiknya pulang sekarang.","It's already 12 o'clock, we should eat now.":"Sekarang sudah jam 12, kita sebaiknya makan sekarang.","to produce/come up with (resultative complement 出)":"menghasilkan/memikirkan (komplemen hasil 出)","Verb + 出 + (Object)":"Verba + 出 + (Objek)","Here \"出\" is a resultative complement meaning \"to bring something into existence,\" used with verbs like 想出 (think up), 提出 (propose), 找出 (find out) for abstract, mental results — not physical movement outward. Learners often confuse it with the literal \"exit\" sense of 出 in verbs like 走出去.":"Di sini \"出\" adalah komplemen hasil yang berarti \"membuat sesuatu muncul/tercipta\", digunakan dengan kata kerja seperti 想出 (memikirkan), 提出 (mengusulkan), 找出 (menemukan) untuk hasil yang abstrak dan bersifat pemikiran — bukan gerakan fisik ke luar. Pembelajar sering menyamakannya dengan makna harfiah \"keluar\" dari 出 dalam kata kerja seperti 走出去.","At key moments, he can always come up with useful ideas or solutions.":"Pada saat-saat penting, dia selalu bisa memikirkan ide atau solusi yang berguna.","After discussing it, we finally came up with a solution.":"Setelah mendiskusikannya, kami akhirnya menemukan sebuah solusi.","on top of that / also (unexpectedly)":"selain itu / bahkan (secara tak terduga)","..., (time/situation) + 還 + Verb":"..., (waktu/situasi) + 還 + Verba","This \"還\" adds an extra, often burdensome or unexpected item on top of a situation already mentioned. Since \"還\" can also mean \"still\" (continuation), tell them apart by context — here a first fact is already stated, and 還 introduces something additional.":"\"還\" ini menambahkan sesuatu, yang seringkali memberatkan atau tak terduga, di atas situasi yang sudah disebutkan sebelumnya. Karena \"還\" juga bisa berarti \"masih\" (kelanjutan), bedakan keduanya lewat konteks — di sini sebuah fakta pertama sudah dinyatakan, dan 還 memperkenalkan sesuatu yang tambahan.","He works during the day, and in the evening he also tutors, so he has no time at all to reply to messages.":"Dia bekerja di siang hari, dan di malam hari dia juga mengajar les, jadi dia sama sekali tidak punya waktu untuk membalas pesan.","She's already very busy, and on top of that she has to go work a part-time job on weekends.":"Dia sudah sangat sibuk, dan selain itu dia masih harus bekerja paruh waktu di akhir pekan.","seems / looks (like)":"sepertinya / terlihat (seperti)","Subject + 看起來/聽起來 + Adjective":"Subjek + 看起來/聽起來 + Kata sifat","Here \"V起來\" (as in 看起來, 聽起來) forms a fixed expression meaning \"it appears/sounds like...\", expressing a judgment based on perception. It differs from the literal \"stand up\" sense of V起來 and the inchoative \"start doing\" sense (e.g., 哭起來, \"burst into tears\") — don't mix the uses up.":"Di sini \"V起來\" (seperti pada 看起來, 聽起來) membentuk ungkapan tetap yang berarti \"tampaknya/kedengarannya...\", mengungkapkan penilaian berdasarkan persepsi. Ini berbeda dari makna harfiah \"berdiri\" pada V起來 dan makna inkoatif \"mulai melakukan\" (misalnya 哭起來, \"menangis tersedu-sedu\") — jangan mencampuradukkan penggunaannya.","You look very tired today.":"Hari ini kamu terlihat sangat lelah.","This dish smells great, I want to eat it soon.":"Masakan ini baunya harum sekali, aku ingin segera memakannya.","cannot help but / have no choice but to":"tidak bisa tidak / terpaksa harus","Subject + 不能不/不得不/不可不 + Verb":"Subjek + 不能不/不得不/不可不 + Kata kerja","All three are double negatives meaning \"cannot not do X\" → \"must / have no choice but to.\" \"不得不\" is the most common and colloquial, framing the action as forced by outside circumstances. \"不可不\" is more literary, often used in advice or warnings. \"不能不\" sits in between. They aren't always freely interchangeable, so it helps to learn each with its typical example sentence.":"Ketiganya adalah bentuk negasi ganda yang berarti \"tidak bisa tidak melakukan X\" → \"harus / terpaksa.\" \"不得不\" paling umum dan sehari-hari, menggambarkan tindakan yang dipaksa oleh keadaan luar. \"不可不\" lebih bersifat sastra, sering dipakai dalam nasihat atau peringatan. \"不能不\" berada di antara keduanya. Ketiganya tidak selalu bisa saling menggantikan secara bebas, jadi sebaiknya pelajari masing-masing beserta kalimat contoh khasnya.","After sweating all day, I have no choice but to wash my clothes.":"Setelah berkeringat seharian, aku terpaksa mencuci pakaian.","Because he was too busy with work, he had no choice but to cancel his travel plans.":"Karena terlalu sibuk dengan pekerjaan, dia terpaksa membatalkan rencana bepergiannya.","compared to...":"dibandingkan dengan...","Gēn/hé + A + bǐqǐlái, B...":"Gēn/hé + A + bǐqǐlái, B...","Introduces an explicit point of comparison before stating how B differs. 跟 and 和 are interchangeable here. Unlike the simple '比' comparison, this pattern emphasizes contrasting whole situations, not just one quality.":"Memperkenalkan titik perbandingan yang eksplisit sebelum menyatakan perbedaan B. 跟 dan 和 dapat saling dipertukarkan di sini. Berbeda dari perbandingan sederhana dengan '比', pola ini menekankan perbandingan seluruh situasi, bukan hanya satu sifat.","Compared to studying in one's own country, studying abroad is a bigger challenge.":"Dibandingkan dengan belajar di negeri sendiri, belajar di luar negeri adalah tantangan yang lebih besar.","Compared to taking the bus, taking the MRT is much more convenient.":"Dibandingkan dengan naik bus, naik MRT jauh lebih praktis.","A is like B, ...":"A seperti B, ...","A + xiàng + B + yíyàng + (adj./verb)":"A + xiàng + B + yíyàng + (kata sifat/kata kerja)","States that A shares the same quality or state as B, typically followed by an adjective or verb phrase. Negation commonly appears as 不像 or 不再像, as in the official example.":"Menyatakan bahwa A memiliki sifat atau keadaan yang sama dengan B, biasanya diikuti oleh kata sifat atau frasa kata kerja. Bentuk negasinya biasanya muncul sebagai 不像 atau 不再像, seperti pada contoh resmi.","After graduation, we no longer meet often like we used to.":"Setelah lulus, kami tidak lagi sering bertemu seperti dulu.","His personality is as stubborn as his father's.":"Kepribadiannya sama keras kepalanya dengan ayahnya.","A is not as good as B":"A tidak sebaik B","A + bùrú + B":"A + bùrú + B","Compares A to B and states that A falls short of B. 不如 functions as a verb meaning 'not as good as' and can be followed directly by an adjective (不如 B + adj.) to specify in what way.":"Membandingkan A dengan B dan menyatakan bahwa A tidak sebaik B. 不如 berfungsi sebagai kata kerja yang berarti \"tidak sebaik\" dan dapat langsung diikuti oleh kata sifat (不如 B + kata sifat) untuk menjelaskan dalam hal apa.","In recent years, development near the train station hasn't kept pace with the new district.":"Belakangan ini, perkembangan di dekat stasiun kereta tidak secepat kawasan baru.","This shop's coffee isn't as good as the one downstairs.":"Kopi di toko ini tidak seenak yang di lantai bawah.","How...!":"Betapa...!","duō + adjective + a":"duō + kata sifat + a","An exclamatory pattern expressing how high a degree is. 多 originates as an interrogative ('how much') but here builds an exclamation; the sentence-final 啊 is nearly obligatory in speech.":"Pola seru yang menyatakan tingginya suatu tingkatan. 多 pada dasarnya adalah kata tanya (\"berapa banyak\") tetapi di sini membentuk kalimat seru; 啊 di akhir kalimat hampir wajib digunakan dalam percakapan lisan.","His new hairstyle is so good-looking!":"Gaya rambut barunya bagus sekali!","This room is so clean!":"Kamar ini bersih sekali!","almost / nearly did...":"hampir / nyaris...","chà yìdiǎn (jiù) + verb phrase":"chà yìdiǎn (jiù) + frasa kata kerja","Expresses that something nearly happened but ultimately did not, often carrying the speaker's relief or regret. 就 is optional and adds emphasis.":"Menyatakan bahwa sesuatu hampir terjadi tetapi akhirnya tidak terjadi, sering membawa perasaan lega atau menyesal dari penutur. 就 bersifat opsional dan berfungsi untuk penekanan.","He almost was late.":"Dia hampir terlambat.","I almost forgot to bring my keys.":"Saya hampir lupa membawa kunci.","related to ~":"berhubungan dengan ~","gēn + A + (méi) yǒuguān":"gēn + A + (méi) yǒuguān","\"跟...有關\" states that two things are related, using 跟 as \"with,\" not \"about.\" Unlike 因為, it shows a loose association, not a direct cause.":"\"跟...有關\" menyatakan bahwa dua hal saling berhubungan, menggunakan 跟 dengan arti \"dengan,\" bukan \"tentang.\" Berbeda dengan 因為, ini menunjukkan hubungan yang longgar, bukan sebab langsung.","Modern people's illnesses are often related to stress.":"Penyakit orang modern sering berhubungan dengan stres.","His skin problems might be related to stress.":"Masalah kulitnya mungkin berhubungan dengan stres.","bring ~ to ~":"membawa ~ bagi ~","A + gěi + B + dàilái + C":"A + gěi + B + dàilái + C","\"給...帶來...\" means \"bring [abstract result] to [someone]\" — 帶來 is for effects or consequences, not physical objects, and 給 marking the recipient cannot be omitted.":"\"給...帶來...\" berarti \"membawa [hasil abstrak] bagi [seseorang]\" — 帶來 digunakan untuk efek atau akibat, bukan benda fisik, dan 給 yang menandai penerima tidak boleh dihilangkan.","Continuing to work can bring us a stable income.":"Terus bekerja dapat membawa kita penghasilan yang stabil.","Exercise can bring the body a lot of benefits.":"Berolahraga dapat membawa banyak manfaat bagi tubuh.","if not A, then not B":"jika tidak A, maka tidak B","bù + A, (jiù) bù + B":"bù + A, (jiù) bù + B","\"不...不...\" states \"if you don't do A, then B won't happen\" — a colloquial way of omitting 如果 from 如果不...就不..., common in spoken Mandarin.":"\"不...不...\" menyatakan \"jika tidak melakukan A, maka B tidak akan terjadi\" — ini adalah cara informal yang menghilangkan 如果 dari struktur 如果不...就不..., yang umum dalam bahasa Mandarin lisan.","If you don't come, the event can't start.":"Jika kamu tidak datang, acara tidak bisa dimulai.","If we don't work hard, we won't succeed.":"Jika kita tidak bekerja keras, kita tidak akan berhasil.","it depends on ~":"tergantung pada ~","(yào/děi) kàn + (question-word clause)":"(yào/děi) kàn + (question-word clause)","\"看/要看/得看\" + a clause with a question word means \"it depends on ~.\" 要看 is neutral, while 得看 emphasizes an unavoidable, necessary condition.":"\"看/要看/得看\" + klausa dengan kata tanya berarti \"tergantung pada ~.\" 要看 bersifat netral, sedangkan 得看 menekankan kondisi yang tidak dapat dihindari dan diperlukan.","When you encounter a problem, it depends on what attitude each person takes to face it — the way of handling it will be different.":"Ketika menghadapi masalah, tergantung pada sikap masing-masing orang dalam menghadapinya — cara penanganannya akan berbeda.","Who wins this match depends on the athletes' performance on that day.":"Siapa yang memenangkan pertandingan ini tergantung pada performa para atlet pada hari itu.","no matter (whether) ~":"tidak peduli (apakah) ~","bùlùn/wúlùn + question word / A huò B":"bùlùn/wúlùn + question word / A huò B","\"不論/無論\" pairs with 都/也 later in the sentence to mean \"regardless of the condition, the result is the same.\" 無論 sounds slightly more formal/written than 不論, which fits both speech and writing.":"\"不論/無論\" berpasangan dengan 都/也 di bagian kalimat berikutnya untuk menyatakan \"apa pun kondisinya, hasilnya tetap sama.\" 無論 terdengar sedikit lebih formal/tertulis dibandingkan 不論, yang cocok untuk bahasa lisan maupun tulisan.","In recent years, whether it's businesses or individuals, internet usage has become more and more common.":"Dalam beberapa tahun terakhir, baik perusahaan maupun individu, penggunaan internet menjadi semakin umum.","Whether it rains or shines, we have to set out.":"Baik hujan maupun cerah, kita harus tetap berangkat.","it's just that... (mild contrast)":"hanya saja... (kontras ringan)","A, only B (mild qualification)":"A, hanya saja B (kualifikasi ringan)","\"只是\" softly adds a minor exception or drawback without overturning the main point, unlike the stronger \"但是/可是\" which can signal a full contrast.":"\"只是\" menambahkan pengecualian atau kekurangan kecil secara halus tanpa membalikkan poin utama, berbeda dengan \"但是/可是\" yang lebih kuat dan dapat menandakan kontras penuh.","He's very healthy, it's just that his eyes aren't very good.":"Dia sangat sehat, hanya saja matanya kurang bagus.","The food at this restaurant is delicious, it's just that the price is a bit high.":"Makanan di restoran ini enak, hanya saja harganya agak mahal.","yet/unexpectedly (contrary to expectation)":"namun/tak disangka (bertentangan dengan harapan)","A, (but) B 卻 + unexpected result":"A, (tetapi) B 卻 + hasil yang tak terduga","\"卻\" is an adverb placed before the verb/adjective to stress an outcome contrary to expectation; it can appear with or without \"但是\" and still shows contrast on its own.":"\"卻\" adalah kata keterangan yang diletakkan sebelum kata kerja/kata sifat untuk menekankan hasil yang bertentangan dengan harapan; kata ini dapat muncul dengan atau tanpa \"但是\" dan tetap menunjukkan kontras dengan sendirinya.","It's very sunny outside, but the temperature is surprisingly low.":"Di luar sangat cerah, tetapi suhunya justru rendah.","He studies very hard, but his grades haven't improved at all.":"Dia belajar sangat rajin, tetapi nilainya sama sekali tidak membaik.","otherwise / or else":"kalau tidak / jika tidak","A, (or) otherwise B":"A, (atau) kalau tidak B","\"不然\" (or \"要不然\") introduces the undesirable result if the preceding condition isn't followed — a casual, spoken alternative to a more formal \"如果不…的話\".":"\"不然\" (atau \"要不然\") memperkenalkan hasil yang tidak diinginkan jika kondisi sebelumnya tidak dipenuhi — alternatif lisan yang santai untuk bentuk yang lebih formal \"如果不…的話\".","Dad told us to hurry up, otherwise the boat is going to leave.":"Ayah menyuruh kami cepat-cepat, kalau tidak kapalnya akan berangkat.","You'd better hurry and do your homework, or you'll get scolded by the teacher tomorrow.":"Kamu sebaiknya cepat mengerjakan PR, kalau tidak besok akan dimarahi guru.","indeed/really (emphatic 是 before adjective)":"memang/benar-benar (是 penegas sebelum kata sifat)","(Topic) + 是 + Adjective (for emphasis)":"(Topik) + 是 + Kata sifat (untuk penekanan)","This \"是\" isn't the equational \"A是B\"; placed before an adjective it emphasizes agreement/confirmation with something just said, close to \"真的\" but more often used to affirm a prior remark.":"\"是\" di sini bukan \"是\" penyetaraan dalam pola \"A是B\"; ketika diletakkan sebelum kata sifat, kata ini menekankan persetujuan/konfirmasi terhadap sesuatu yang baru saja dikatakan, mirip dengan \"真的\" tetapi lebih sering digunakan untuk menegaskan pernyataan sebelumnya.","(The cost of publishing a travel magazine) is indeed high.":"(Biaya menerbitkan majalah wisata) memang tinggi.","That movie really is very good, you should go watch it.":"Film itu benar-benar bagus, kamu harus menontonnya.","who would have known... (rhetorical, expresses the unexpected)":"siapa sangka... (pertanyaan retoris, mengungkapkan hal yang tak terduga)","A, 哪裡知道(哪裡想到) + unexpected B":"A, 哪裡知道(哪裡想到) + B yang tak terduga","Here \"哪裡\" isn't asking about location — paired with \"知道/想到\" it forms a rhetorical question meaning \"how could one have known,\" stressing an unexpected fact; don't confuse it with the literal \"where\" question.":"Di sini \"哪裡\" bukan menanyakan lokasi — jika dipadukan dengan \"知道/想到\", kata ini membentuk pertanyaan retoris yang berarti \"bagaimana mungkin seseorang bisa tahu\", menekankan suatu fakta yang tak terduga; jangan disamakan dengan pertanyaan harfiah \"di mana\".","He originally planned to go rent a movie, but who would have known that store had actually closed three days earlier!":"Awalnya dia berencana pergi menyewa film, tetapi siapa sangka toko itu ternyata sudah tutup sejak tiga hari sebelumnya!","I thought the exam would be easy, but who knew the questions would be this hard!":"Kukira ujiannya akan mudah, tetapi siapa sangka soalnya sesulit ini!","as soon as said, done / changes suddenly":"begitu dikatakan langsung terjadi / berubah secara tiba-tiba","shuō + V + jiù + V":"shuō + V + jiù + V","\"Shuō X jiù X\" means doing X right after saying it, or something changing abruptly with no warning — it stresses suddenness or unpredictability, unlike the neutral \"馬上\".":"\"Shuō X jiù X\" berarti melakukan X segera setelah mengatakannya, atau sesuatu berubah secara mendadak tanpa peringatan — ungkapan ini menekankan kemendadakan atau ketidakpastian, berbeda dengan \"馬上\" yang bersifat netral.","The weather in the mountains isn't very stable — it often changes just like that.":"Cuacanya di gunung tidak terlalu stabil — sering berubah begitu saja.","He just up and left — he went out without even packing his bags.":"Dia langsung pergi begitu saja — keluar tanpa bahkan mengemasi barangnya.","通過 + means/event, + result":"通過 + sarana/peristiwa, + hasil","\"通過 + means\" indicates achieving a result via a certain method or channel; it's fairly formal/written. Unlike \"經過\" (which stresses the passing of time/process), \"通過\" stresses the means used.":"\"通過 + sarana\" menunjukkan pencapaian suatu hasil melalui metode atau saluran tertentu; penggunaannya cukup formal/bersifat tulisan. Berbeda dengan \"經過\" (yang menekankan berlalunya waktu/proses), \"通過\" menekankan sarana yang digunakan.","Through this conversation, the teacher came to understand the students' thoughts even better.":"Melalui percakapan ini, guru menjadi lebih memahami pikiran para siswa.","Through this competition, we learned a lot about teamwork.":"Melalui kompetisi ini, kami belajar banyak tentang kerja sama tim.","after (a period of time / process)":"setelah (suatu periode waktu / proses)","經過 + time/process (之後), + result":"經過 + waktu/proses (之後), + hasil","\"經過 + time/process\" stresses the duration or stage something has gone through, often followed by \"之後\". Unlike \"通過\", it focuses on the passage of time/process itself, not the means to a result.":"\"經過 + waktu/proses\" menekankan durasi atau tahap yang telah dilalui sesuatu, sering diikuti oleh \"之後\". Berbeda dengan \"通過\", ungkapan ini berfokus pada berlalunya waktu/proses itu sendiri, bukan pada cara untuk mencapai suatu hasil.","After some time had passed, he was already able to adapt to graduate school life.":"Setelah beberapa waktu berlalu, dia sudah bisa beradaptasi dengan kehidupan pascasarjana.","After several months of practice, her Chinese improved a lot.":"Setelah beberapa bulan berlatih, bahasa Mandarinnya sangat meningkat.","use X as/to do Y":"menggunakan X untuk melakukan Y","ná + N + lái + V":"ná + N + lái + V","\"拿 + noun + 來 + verb\" means using something as a means or material for the following action. Here \"拿\" isn't the literal act of holding something, but the abstract sense of \"using/taking X as.\"":"\"拿 + kata benda + 來 + kata kerja\" berarti menggunakan sesuatu sebagai sarana atau bahan untuk tindakan berikutnya. Di sini \"拿\" bukan tindakan memegang secara harfiah, melainkan bermakna abstrak \"menggunakan/mengambil X sebagai...\".","During class, the teacher often uses their own experience as examples.":"Selama pelajaran, guru sering menggunakan pengalaman pribadinya sebagai contoh.","He often uses movie lines to make jokes.":"Dia sering menggunakan dialog film untuk membuat lelucon.","according to":"sesuai dengan, menurut","按照 + standard/instruction, + action":"按照 + standar/instruksi, + tindakan","\"按照 + rule/instruction\" means acting in accordance with a standard, and sounds fairly formal. It's close to \"根據\", but \"按照\" stresses following something exactly, while \"根據\" stresses basing a judgment on facts.":"\"按照 + aturan/instruksi\" berarti bertindak sesuai dengan suatu standar, dan terdengar cukup formal. Ungkapan ini mirip dengan \"根據\", tetapi \"按照\" menekankan kepatuhan yang tepat terhadap sesuatu, sedangkan \"根據\" menekankan dasar penilaian atas fakta.","They planned a three-day, two-night trip according to the guidebook's recommendations.":"Mereka merencanakan perjalanan tiga hari dua malam sesuai dengan rekomendasi buku panduan.","Please complete the homework according to the teacher's instructions.":"Harap selesaikan pekerjaan rumah sesuai dengan instruksi guru.","following/according to (a method)":"mengikuti/sesuai dengan (suatu cara)","A + 照（著）+ B + V":"A + 照（著）+ B + V","Means \"following/according to\" a method or model. \"照\" shows imitation of a way of doing something; \"著\" is optional. Close to \"按照\" but more colloquial.":"Berarti \"mengikuti/sesuai dengan\" suatu cara atau model. \"照\" menunjukkan peniruan terhadap suatu cara melakukan sesuatu; \"著\" bersifat opsional. Mirip dengan \"按照\" tetapi lebih bersifat lisan/sehari-hari.","I make dumplings the way my mom does.":"Saya membuat pangsit dengan cara ibu saya.","You can cook according to the recipe.":"Kamu bisa memasak sesuai dengan resep.","taking advantage of / while":"memanfaatkan / selagi","趁（著）+ time/opportunity + V":"趁（著）+ waktu/kesempatan + V","Means \"taking advantage of / while (a time or condition still holds)\". Expresses acting before an opportunity or state changes. \"著\" is optional.":"Berarti \"memanfaatkan / selagi (suatu waktu atau kondisi masih berlangsung)\". Mengungkapkan tindakan yang dilakukan sebelum kesempatan atau keadaan itu berubah. \"著\" bersifat opsional.","Taking advantage of the New Year holiday, Dad visited a lot of relatives.":"Memanfaatkan libur Tahun Baru, Ayah mengunjungi banyak sanak saudara.","Taking advantage of the holiday, we went to Tainan to have fun.":"Memanfaatkan hari libur, kami pergi ke Tainan untuk bersenang-senang.","distance from (time/space)":"jarak dari (waktu/ruang)","A + 離 + B + 還/只/有 + distance":"A + 離 + B + 還/只/有 + jarak","A preposition marking distance between two points in time or space: \"離 + reference point + 還/只/有 + distance\". Don't confuse with \"從\", which marks a starting point, not a distance.":"Kata depan yang menandai jarak antara dua titik dalam waktu atau ruang: \"離 + titik acuan + 還/只/有 + jarak\". Jangan disamakan dengan \"從\", yang menandai titik awal, bukan jarak.","There are only two days left until Chinese New Year, and train tickets are almost all sold out.":"Hanya tersisa dua hari lagi menuju Tahun Baru Imlek, dan tiket kereta hampir habis terjual.","It's not far from the MRT station — five minutes on foot and you're there.":"Tempatnya tidak jauh dari stasiun MRT — jalan kaki lima menit juga sampai.","while V-ing, unexpectedly...":"sedang V, tak disangka...","V著V著 + jiù + ... + le":"V著V著 + jiù + ... + le","Means \"while doing V, V, (unexpectedly) ... happened\". Repeating the same verb shows the action was continuing, and \"就...了\" marks a sudden, often unnoticed change that followed.":"Berarti \"sedang V, V, (tanpa disadari) ... terjadi\". Pengulangan kata kerja yang sama menunjukkan tindakan itu sedang berlangsung, dan \"就...了\" menandai perubahan yang tiba-tiba, sering kali tidak disadari, yang terjadi setelahnya.","My younger brother often reads in bed, and before he knows it, he falls asleep.":"Adik laki-lakiku sering membaca di tempat tidur, dan tanpa disadari, dia pun tertidur.","He kept scrolling on his phone, and before he knew it, he'd forgotten the time.":"Dia terus menggulir ponselnya, dan tanpa disadari, dia lupa waktu.","already long ago":"sudah sejak lama","早就 + V(過) + 了":"早就 + V(過) + 了","Means \"already long ago\" — stronger emphasis than \"早\" alone, often implying the speaker feels it happened earlier than expected or that it's obvious.":"Berarti \"sudah sejak lama\" — penekanannya lebih kuat daripada hanya \"早\", sering kali menyiratkan bahwa pembicara merasa hal itu terjadi lebih awal dari yang diharapkan atau bahwa itu sudah jelas.","Let's talk about something else — he already heard this story a long time ago.":"Bicarakan hal lain saja — cerita ini sudah lama dia dengar.","Don't worry, I finished my homework a long time ago.":"Jangan khawatir, aku sudah lama menyelesaikan PR-ku.","within":"dalam","Time/Quantity + 以內/之內":"Time/Quantity + 以內/之內","Both mark \"within\" a range or deadline, placed after a quantity/time expression. \"以內\" often implies an upper limit (at most), while \"之內\" is more general; with time words they're often interchangeable.":"Keduanya menandai arti \"dalam\" suatu rentang atau batas waktu, diletakkan setelah ungkapan jumlah/waktu. \"以內\" sering menyiratkan batas atas (paling banyak), sedangkan \"之內\" lebih umum; dengan kata-kata waktu, keduanya sering dapat saling menggantikan.","The website's number of users increased tenfold within a single day.":"Jumlah pengguna situs web itu meningkat sepuluh kali lipat hanya dalam satu hari.","He promised to finish writing the report within three days.":"Dia berjanji akan menyelesaikan penulisan laporan dalam waktu tiga hari.","now...now...":"kadang...kadang...","一會兒 + A, 一會兒 + B":"一會兒 + A, 一會兒 + B","\"一會兒A, 一會兒B\" shows a state or action alternating rapidly between two things. It reads slightly more neutral/written than the more colloquial \"一下A一下B\".":"\"一會兒A, 一會兒B\" menggambarkan suatu keadaan atau tindakan yang berganti-ganti dengan cepat antara dua hal. Ungkapan ini terdengar sedikit lebih netral/tertulis dibandingkan dengan \"一下A一下B\" yang lebih bersifat percakapan.","He played four or five roles all by himself — one moment a bus driver, the next moment a boss.":"Dia sendirian memerankan empat lima peran — kadang jadi sopir bus, kadang jadi bos.","My little sister cries one moment and laughs the next — no one can figure out what she's thinking.":"Adik perempuanku kadang menangis kadang tertawa — tidak ada yang bisa menebak apa yang dia pikirkan.","now...now... (colloquial)":"kadang...kadang... (bahasa percakapan)","一下 + A, 一下 + B":"一下 + A, 一下 + B","\"一下A, 一下B\" is a colloquial way to describe a state or action changing back and forth rapidly. It's nearly synonymous with \"一會兒A, 一會兒B\" but sounds more casual and spoken.":"\"一下A, 一下B\" adalah cara percakapan untuk menggambarkan suatu keadaan atau tindakan yang berubah-ubah dengan cepat. Ungkapan ini hampir bersinonim dengan \"一會兒A, 一會兒B\" tetapi terdengar lebih santai dan lisan.","Spring weather is cold one moment and hot the next, so it's very easy to catch a cold.":"Cuaca musim semi kadang dingin kadang panas, jadi sangat mudah masuk angin.","This kid cries one moment and laughs the next — his mom is totally confused.":"Anak ini kadang menangis kadang tertawa — ibunya benar-benar bingung.","both...and...":"baik...maupun...","既 + A, 又 + B":"既 + A, 又 + B","\"既A又B\" shows two qualities or actions both being true at once; it's a slightly more written-style expression, and A/B are usually parallel in length and part of speech.":"\"既A又B\" menunjukkan dua sifat atau tindakan yang sama-sama benar pada saat yang sama; ini adalah ungkapan yang sedikit lebih formal/tertulis, dan A/B biasanya sejajar dalam panjang dan jenis katanya.","The fruit this shop sells is both fresh and delicious.":"Buah yang dijual toko ini segar sekaligus enak.","This job is both easy and pays fairly well, so everyone wants to do it.":"Pekerjaan ini mudah sekaligus gajinya cukup tinggi, jadi semua orang ingin melakukannya.","as soon as [action] starts":"begitu [tindakan] dimulai","一 + V + 起, S + then...":"一 + V + 起, S + lalu...","\"一V起\" means \"as soon as [action] starts\", followed by the resulting change or reaction. It's similar to \"一V就\", but \"起\" adds a sense of the topic/action \"coming up\" or being brought up.":"\"一V起\" berarti \"begitu [tindakan] dimulai\", diikuti oleh perubahan atau reaksi yang terjadi. Ini mirip dengan \"一V就\", tetapi \"起\" menambahkan nuansa topik/tindakan yang \"muncul\" atau \"diangkat\".","As soon as the topic turns to favorite foods, everyone becomes very interested.":"Begitu topik beralih ke makanan favorit, semua orang langsung sangat tertarik.","As soon as Grandma recalls something from her childhood, she laughs.":"Begitu Nenek teringat sesuatu dari masa kecilnya, dia langsung tertawa.","starting a new action/role (often surprising)":"memulai tindakan/peran baru (sering mengejutkan)","V + 起 + N + 來 (+ 了)":"V + 起 + N + 來 (+ 了)","\"V起N來\" marks the start of an action or state, often implying an unexpected change. The object N is inserted between 起 and 來. Don't confuse it with plain \"V起來\" (e.g. 想起來), which has no object slot.":"\"V起N來\" menandai dimulainya suatu tindakan atau keadaan, sering kali menyiratkan perubahan yang tak terduga. Objek N disisipkan di antara 起 dan 來. Jangan bingungkan dengan \"V起來\" biasa (misalnya 想起來), yang tidak memiliki slot objek.","He hated going to school the most, but now, surprisingly, he has actually become a teacher.":"Dia dulu paling benci pergi ke sekolah, tetapi sekarang, mengejutkan sekali, dia justru menjadi guru.","After graduating, she couldn't find her ideal job, so she started her own business.":"Setelah lulus, dia tidak menemukan pekerjaan idamannya, jadi dia mulai membuka usaha sendiri.","completely used up / all gone (none left)":"habis terpakai sepenuhnya / habis sama sekali (tidak tersisa)","V + 光 (+ 了)":"V + 光 (+ 了)","\"V光\" is a resultative complement meaning the object is completely used up, none left. Unlike \"V完\" which just marks completion, \"V光\" emphasizes nothing remains at all.":"\"V光\" adalah pelengkap hasil yang berarti objeknya telah habis terpakai sepenuhnya, tidak tersisa. Berbeda dengan \"V完\" yang hanya menandai selesainya suatu tindakan, \"V光\" menekankan bahwa sama sekali tidak ada yang tersisa.","All the bread at home has been eaten up (none left).":"Semua roti di rumah sudah habis dimakan (tidak tersisa sama sekali).","My younger brother ate up a whole bag of cookies all by himself.":"Adik laki-lakiku menghabiskan sebungkus penuh kue kering sendirian.","because of ... (reason/cause)":"karena ... (alasan/sebab)","因為 + Reason + 的關係, (Result)":"因為 + Reason + 的關係, (Result)","A softer, more indirect way to state a cause than plain \"因為\", often used to avoid pinning blame directly. Commonly paired with \"所以\" in the result clause.":"Ini adalah cara yang lebih halus dan tidak langsung untuk menyatakan sebab dibandingkan \"因為\" biasa, sering digunakan untuk menghindari menyalahkan secara langsung. Biasanya dipasangkan dengan \"所以\" pada klausa hasil.","Because of work, my older brother often turns off his phone, so it's hard to reach him.":"Karena pekerjaan, kakak laki-lakiku sering mematikan ponselnya, jadi sulit dihubungi.","Because of the weather, today's event has been changed to be held indoors.":"Karena cuaca, acara hari ini diubah menjadi diadakan di dalam ruangan.","additionally, separately (addition)":"selain itu, secara terpisah (tambahan)","..., 另外 (+ 還) + additional information":"..., 另外 (+ 還) + additional information","Used to add a separate, additional piece of information apart from what was just said. Unlike \"而且\", which piles on emphasis to the same point, \"另外\" introduces a distinct extra item.":"Digunakan untuk menambahkan informasi terpisah yang berbeda dari yang baru saja disebutkan. Berbeda dengan \"而且\" yang menambah penekanan pada poin yang sama, \"另外\" memperkenalkan hal tambahan yang berbeda.","This restaurant has a great atmosphere; additionally, it also offers a free play area for children.":"Restoran ini memiliki suasana yang bagus; selain itu, juga menyediakan area bermain gratis untuk anak-anak.","The coffee at this shop is delicious; additionally, the desserts are also very popular.":"Kopi di kedai ini enak; selain itu, kue-kue penutupnya juga sangat digemari.","on top of that, in addition (cumulative reason)":"selain itu, ditambah lagi (alasan kumulatif)","..., 再加上 + additional cause/condition, (result)":"..., 再加上 + additional cause/condition, (result)","Piles an extra cause or condition onto an existing one to strengthen the result, emphasizing cumulative causation. Unlike \"另外\", which adds parallel information, \"再加上\" stresses that the reasons stack up to produce the outcome.":"Menambahkan sebab atau kondisi tambahan pada sebab yang sudah ada untuk memperkuat hasil, menekankan akumulasi penyebab. Berbeda dengan \"另外\" yang menambahkan informasi paralel, \"再加上\" menekankan bahwa alasan-alasan tersebut menumpuk hingga menghasilkan suatu akibat.","My older brother's job is stable now, and on top of that he has money saved from before, so life is going pretty well.":"Pekerjaan kakak laki-laki saya sekarang sudah stabil, dan selain itu dia juga punya uang tabungan dari sebelumnya, jadi hidupnya berjalan cukup baik.","This shop has a great location, and on top of that the owner is very friendly, so business is always good.":"Toko ini punya lokasi yang bagus, dan selain itu pemiliknya juga sangat ramah, jadi bisnisnya selalu berjalan baik.","not only...but also...":"tidak hanya... tetapi juga...","A + 不只 + B1, 而且/還/也 + B2":"A + 不只 + B1, 而且/還/也 + B2","\"不只\" pairs with 而且/還/也 to add an extra point beyond the first, like \"not only...but also.\" A common mistake is dropping the second half, leaving 不只 alone, which sounds incomplete.":"\"不只\" berpasangan dengan 而且/還/也 untuk menambahkan satu poin lagi selain poin pertama, seperti \"tidak hanya... tetapi juga...\". Kesalahan umum adalah menghilangkan bagian kedua, sehingga 不只 berdiri sendiri, yang terdengar tidak lengkap.","This cup's design is not only good-looking, but also very convenient.":"Desain gelas ini tidak hanya bagus, tetapi juga sangat praktis.","besides/except for...":"selain.../kecuali...","除了 + A + 之外, (也/還/都/不) + B":"除了 + A + 之外, (也/還/都/不) + B","\"除了...之外\" means \"in addition to\" when followed by 也/還, but here it pairs with 不 to mean \"except for/only,\" as in \"besides water, she drinks nothing else.\" Learners often mistranslate it as always additive.":"\"除了...之外\" berarti \"selain itu juga\" ketika diikuti oleh 也/還, tetapi di sini ia berpasangan dengan 不 untuk berarti \"kecuali/hanya\", seperti dalam \"selain air, dia tidak minum apa pun yang lain\". Pembelajar sering salah menerjemahkannya sebagai selalu bermakna penambahan.","Besides drinking water, my older sister usually doesn't drink any other beverages.":"Selain minum air putih, kakak perempuan saya biasanya tidak minum minuman lain.","Besides Chinese, I can also speak a little Japanese.":"Selain bahasa Mandarin, saya juga bisa berbicara sedikit bahasa Jepang.","like...and so on":"seperti... dan sebagainya","像 + example1, example2, example3 + 什麼的":"像 + example1, example2, example3 + 什麼的","\"像...什麼的\" lists a few examples casually and closes with \"and so on,\" similar to spoken \"like...and stuff.\" It's more colloquial than 等等 and is rarely used in formal writing.":"\"像...什麼的\" mencantumkan beberapa contoh secara santai dan diakhiri dengan makna \"dan sebagainya\", mirip dengan ungkapan lisan \"seperti... dan lain-lain\". Ungkapan ini lebih kolokial dibandingkan 等等 dan jarang digunakan dalam tulisan formal.","Taiwan has some foods — like stinky tofu, pig-intestine noodles, and pig's-blood cake — that I had never eaten before.":"Taiwan memiliki beberapa makanan — seperti tahu bau, mi usus babi, dan kue darah babi — yang belum pernah saya makan sebelumnya.","The things this shop sells, like bubble milk tea and fried chicken and so on, are all very popular.":"Barang-barang yang dijual toko ini, seperti teh susu boba dan ayam goreng dan sebagainya, semuanya sangat populer.","just/only, nothing more":"hanya/sekadar, tidak lebih","(只/只不過) + verb phrase/是〜 + 而已":"(只/只不過) + verb phrase/是〜 + 而已","The sentence-final particle 而已 downplays scope, meaning \"just/merely,\" and is usually paired with 只 or 只不過 for emphasis. Using 而已 alone without 只 is possible but sounds less natural.":"Partikel akhir kalimat 而已 memperkecil cakupan, berarti \"hanya/sekadar\", dan biasanya dipasangkan dengan 只 atau 只不過 untuk penekanan. Menggunakan 而已 sendirian tanpa 只 masih mungkin, tetapi terdengar kurang alami.","The content of the first class was merely teaching some basic movements.":"Isi kelas pertama hanya mengajarkan beberapa gerakan dasar saja.","I'm not angry, just a bit tired, that's all.":"Saya tidak marah, hanya sedikit lelah saja.","within/outside/east/west... of a reference point":"di dalam/di luar/timur/barat... dari suatu titik acuan","reference point + 以 + 內/外/左/右/東/西/南/北":"reference point + 以 + 內/外/左/右/東/西/南/北","\"以\" attaches after a reference point to mark range or direction; \"以內\" usually includes the boundary itself, though context matters. \"以左/以右\" appear more in maps or formal writing than in everyday speech.":"\"以\" ditambahkan setelah suatu titik acuan untuk menandai jangkauan atau arah; \"以內\" biasanya mencakup batas itu sendiri, meskipun tergantung konteks. \"以左/以右\" lebih sering muncul di peta atau tulisan formal daripada dalam percakapan sehari-hari.","You can't eat inside the yellow line at the MRT station.":"Anda tidak boleh makan di dalam garis kuning di stasiun MRT.","The area outside this line is no longer within our school's boundary.":"Area di luar garis ini sudah bukan lagi bagian dari batas sekolah kami.","introducing a topic":"memperkenalkan suatu topik","說到/談到/講到 + topic, ...":"說到/談到/講到 + topic, ...","Use 說到/談到/講到 at the start of a sentence to open a new topic, like \"speaking of X.\" It only shifts topic, unlike 對……來說 (stance) or 拿……來說 (example) taught nearby.":"Gunakan 說到/談到/講到 di awal kalimat untuk membuka topik baru, seperti \"berbicara tentang X\". Fungsinya hanya untuk mengalihkan topik, berbeda dengan 對……來說 (menyatakan sudut pandang) atau 拿……來說 (memberi contoh) yang diajarkan di dekatnya.","Speaking of IT equipment, all the computers in this library are the latest models.":"Berbicara tentang peralatan IT, semua komputer di perpustakaan ini adalah model terbaru.","Speaking of travel, the place I most want to go is Japan.":"Kalau bicara soal traveling, tempat yang paling ingin saya kunjungi adalah Jepang.","taking X as an example":"dengan mengambil X sebagai contoh","拿 + X + 來說, ...":"拿 + X + 來說, ...","拿……來說 introduces a concrete example, meaning \"taking X for example.\" Never drop 來說 after X. Unlike 對……來說, which states a viewpoint, this pattern is for illustrating with a case.":"拿……來說 digunakan untuk memberikan contoh konkret, yang berarti \"dengan mengambil X sebagai contoh.\" Jangan pernah menghilangkan 來說 setelah X. Berbeda dengan 對……來說, yang menyatakan sudut pandang, pola ini digunakan untuk menjelaskan dengan sebuah contoh kasus.","Taking Taiwan as an example, the elderly population keeps growing while the birth rate keeps falling.":"Dengan mengambil Taiwan sebagai contoh, populasi lansia terus bertambah sementara angka kelahiran terus menurun.","Take the MRT for example — it's really crowded during rush hour.":"Ambil MRT sebagai contoh — pada jam sibuk benar-benar sangat padat.","from X's perspective":"dari sudut pandang X","對 + X + 來說, ...":"對 + X + 來說, ...","對……來說 means \"from X's point of view,\" used to state how something appears or matters to X. Don't confuse it with 拿……來說 (giving an example); never omit 來說 after X.":"對……來說 berarti \"dari sudut pandang X,\" digunakan untuk menyatakan bagaimana sesuatu tampak atau berarti bagi X. Jangan bingungkan dengan 拿……來說 (memberikan contoh); jangan pernah menghilangkan 來說 setelah X.","For a young child, playing is the most important thing in his life.":"Bagi seorang anak kecil, bermain adalah hal yang paling penting dalam hidupnya.","For foreigners, writing traditional characters is much harder than recognizing them.":"Bagi orang asing, menulis aksara tradisional jauh lebih sulit daripada mengenalinya.","softened negation (\"not really/very\")":"negasi yang diperhalus (\"tidak benar-benar/tidak begitu\")","不是 + 很/太 + adjective":"不是 + 很/太 + adjective","Here 不是 + 很/太 + adjective softens a negative statement, like \"not really/not very,\" gentler than plain 不. Don't mistake this for 不是 used as \"is not\" in an identity sentence.":"Di sini 不是 + 很/太 + kata sifat memperhalus sebuah pernyataan negatif, seperti \"tidak benar-benar/tidak begitu,\" lebih halus dibanding 不 saja. Jangan salah mengira ini dengan 不是 yang digunakan sebagai \"bukan\" dalam kalimat identitas.","The meaning of this sentence isn't very clear — could you explain it?":"Arti kalimat ini tidak begitu jelas — bisakah Anda menjelaskannya?","The things at this shop aren't very expensive, so you can buy with confidence.":"Barang-barang di toko ini tidak begitu mahal, jadi Anda bisa membeli dengan tenang.","less than (a quantity)":"kurang dari (suatu jumlah)","不到 + quantity":"不到 + quantity","不到 goes before a number or amount to mean \"less than / not even X,\" stating an objective shortfall. Distinguish it from 不夠 (\"not enough\"), which expresses subjective insufficiency, not a precise quantity.":"不到 diletakkan sebelum angka atau jumlah untuk berarti \"kurang dari / tidak sampai X,\" menyatakan kekurangan secara objektif. Bedakan dengan 不夠 (\"tidak cukup\"), yang mengungkapkan kekurangan secara subjektif, bukan jumlah yang pasti.","Children under 90 centimeters tall can enter for free.":"Anak-anak dengan tinggi kurang dari 90 sentimeter dapat masuk gratis.","This movie ended in less than two hours.":"Film ini berakhir dalam waktu kurang dari dua jam.","asking what happened / what's going on":"menanyakan apa yang terjadi / ada apa","shì + zěnme (yī) huí shì (+ ma)":"shì + zěnme (yī) huí shì (+ ma)","\"怎麼(一)回事\" is a colloquial way to ask what happened or why something occurred; adding \"一\" softens the tone slightly without changing meaning. Don't confuse it with \"什麼事\" (what matter), which just asks about a topic, not a cause.":"\"怎麼(一)回事\" adalah cara informal untuk menanyakan apa yang terjadi atau mengapa sesuatu terjadi; penambahan \"一\" sedikit memperhalus nada bicara tanpa mengubah artinya. Jangan bingungkan dengan \"什麼事\" (ada hal apa), yang hanya menanyakan suatu topik, bukan penyebabnya.","I heard your older sister had a fight with her roommate — do you know what happened?":"Saya dengar kakak perempuanmu bertengkar dengan teman sekamarnya — kamu tahu apa yang terjadi?","My phone suddenly wouldn't turn on this morning — what on earth is going on?":"Tadi pagi ponsel saya tiba-tiba tidak bisa menyala — sebenarnya ada apa ini?","doubling a measure word to mean \"every single one\"":"menggandakan kata bantu bilangan untuk berarti \"setiap satu tanpa kecuali\"","MW + MW (+ dōu) + VP":"MW + MW (+ dōu) + VP","Reduplicating a measure word (AA form) means \"every single one without exception,\" and is usually followed by \"都\". Not all measure words can be doubled this way — it's common with words like 個個, 張張, 件件, 朵朵, but not with every measure word.":"Menggandakan kata bantu bilangan (bentuk AA) berarti \"setiap satu tanpa terkecuali,\" dan biasanya diikuti oleh \"都\". Tidak semua kata bantu bilangan bisa digandakan dengan cara ini — hal ini umum digunakan pada kata seperti 個個, 張張, 件件, 朵朵, tetapi tidak berlaku untuk semua kata bantu bilangan.","This year's roses have all bloomed beautifully, every single one.":"Mawar tahun ini mekar indah, setiap satu tanpa kecuali.","The athletes in this competition are all amazing, each and every one.":"Para atlet dalam kompetisi ini semuanya luar biasa, tanpa kecuali.","\"because of X, (a bad result happens)\"":"\"karena X, (terjadi hasil buruk)\"","(cause) + hài + (person) + (negative result)":"(sebab) + hài + (orang) + (hasil negatif)","\"害\" is a verb meaning \"to cause (someone) a bad result,\" carrying a sense of blame or annoyance. Unlike the neutral \"因為\" (because), \"害\" implies the speaker feels inconvenienced or wronged by the cause.":"\"害\" adalah kata kerja yang berarti \"menyebabkan (seseorang) mengalami hasil yang buruk\", mengandung nuansa menyalahkan atau kekesalan. Berbeda dengan \"因為\" (karena) yang netral, \"害\" menyiratkan bahwa pembicara merasa dirugikan atau diperlakukan tidak adil oleh sebab tersebut.","He forgot to bring his phone, so I couldn't find him all day because of it.":"Dia lupa membawa ponselnya, jadi karena itu saya tidak bisa menemukannya sepanjang hari.","The rain ruined our picnic — it got canceled because of it.":"Hujan merusak acara piknik kami — karena itu acaranya dibatalkan.","use \"把\" to change an object into a new state or result":"menggunakan \"把\" untuk mengubah suatu objek menjadi keadaan atau hasil baru","bǎ + Object + V + chéng + result":"bǎ + Objek + V + chéng + hasil","\"把...V成...\" shows that an object was transformed into a different thing or state through an action, and must be used with \"把\". Don't confuse it with \"變成\", which describes the subject itself changing, not something being changed by an action on an object.":"\"把...V成...\" menunjukkan bahwa suatu objek diubah menjadi sesuatu atau keadaan lain melalui suatu tindakan, dan harus digunakan bersama \"把\". Jangan disamakan dengan \"變成\", yang menggambarkan subjek itu sendiri yang berubah, bukan sesuatu yang diubah oleh suatu tindakan terhadap objek.","Please translate the English into Chinese.":"Silakan terjemahkan bahasa Inggris ke dalam bahasa Mandarin.","Mom decorated the living room to look like Christmas.":"Ibu mendekorasi ruang tamu agar terlihat seperti Natal.","use \"把\" to treat/regard something as X":"menggunakan \"把\" untuk memperlakukan/menganggap sesuatu sebagai X","bǎ + Object + dàngzuò + N":"bǎ + Objek + dàngzuò + N","\"把...當作/當做...\" means to regard or treat an object as something (a role, purpose, or category), without physically changing it. This differs from \"把...V成...\", where the object actually changes into a new state or form.":"\"把...當作/當做...\" berarti menganggap atau memperlakukan suatu objek sebagai sesuatu (suatu peran, tujuan, atau kategori), tanpa mengubahnya secara fisik. Ini berbeda dengan \"把...V成...\", di mana objek benar-benar berubah menjadi keadaan atau bentuk baru.","Grandpa regards traveling as the most important activity after retirement.":"Kakek menganggap bepergian sebagai kegiatan paling penting setelah pensiun.","Many people regard exercise as a way to relieve stress.":"Banyak orang menganggap olahraga sebagai cara untuk melepaskan stres.","be regarded/treated as (passive)":"dianggap/diperlakukan sebagai (pasif)","N1 + 被 + N2 + 當作/看作 + N3":"N1 + 被 + N2 + 當作/看作 + N3","\"Bei + agent + V作/做 + N\" means \"is regarded/treated as N by agent.\" Only pairs with a small set of verbs like 當作/看作. Unlike a plain 被 passive, it specifies the resulting identity.":"\"Bei + pelaku + V作/做 + N\" berarti \"dianggap/diperlakukan sebagai N oleh pelaku.\" Hanya berpasangan dengan sejumlah kecil kata kerja seperti 當作/看作. Berbeda dengan kalimat pasif 被 biasa, struktur ini menentukan identitas hasilnya.","He was mistaken for a thief by his neighbor.":"Dia disangka sebagai pencuri oleh tetangganya.","That old jacket is worn by him as pajamas.":"Jaket lama itu dipakainya sebagai baju tidur.","be turned into (passive result)":"diubah menjadi (hasil pasif)","N1 + 被 + N2 + V + 成 + result":"N1 + 被 + N2 + V + 成 + hasil","\"Bei + agent + V成 + result\" shows the action changed something into a resulting state or form. Unlike V作/做 (identity/treatment), V成 marks a change of shape or condition.":"\"Bei + pelaku + V成 + hasil\" menunjukkan bahwa tindakan tersebut mengubah sesuatu menjadi suatu keadaan atau bentuk hasil. Berbeda dengan V作/做 (identitas/perlakuan), V成 menandai perubahan bentuk atau kondisi.","He was beaten by someone and seriously injured.":"Dia dipukul oleh seseorang dan terluka parah.","The cake was cut by him into eight pieces.":"Kue itu dipotongnya menjadi delapan bagian.","be affected by N":"dipengaruhi oleh N","N(subject) + 受 + N(cause) + V (影響/歡迎, etc.)":"N(subjek) + 受 + N(sebab) + V (影響/歡迎, dsb.)","\"(Subject) 受 + N + V (like 影響)\" means \"affected by N, ...happens.\" Unlike 被, 受 works for both good and bad influence and commonly pairs with fixed phrases like 受影響/受歡迎.":"\"(Subjek) 受 + N + V (seperti 影響)\" berarti \"dipengaruhi oleh N, ...terjadi.\" Berbeda dengan 被, 受 dapat digunakan untuk pengaruh baik maupun buruk dan biasanya berpasangan dengan frasa tetap seperti 受影響/受歡迎.","This year, bananas were affected by production volume, so the price dropped very low.":"Tahun ini, pisang terpengaruh oleh volume produksi, sehingga harganya turun sangat rendah.","This exam was affected by the weather, so many people were late.":"Ujian ini terkena dampak cuaca, sehingga banyak orang datang terlambat.","generally speaking":"secara umum","一般來說, + clause":"一般來說, + klausa","Placed at the start of a sentence to state a general tendency, setting aside exceptions. It softens an assertion and is often followed by a contrasting exception.":"Diletakkan di awal kalimat untuk menyatakan kecenderungan umum, tanpa memperhitungkan pengecualian. Ungkapan ini melunakkan suatu pernyataan dan sering diikuti oleh pengecualian yang kontras.","Generally speaking, the more income one has, the higher one's spending tends to be.":"Secara umum, semakin tinggi pendapatan seseorang, semakin tinggi pula pengeluarannya.","Generally speaking, winter in Taipei is colder than in the south.":"Secara umum, musim dingin di Taipei lebih dingin daripada di selatan.","tell me, don't you think...?":"coba bilang, bukankah...?","你說, + clause (often a question)":"你說, + klausa (sering berupa pertanyaan)","Used at the start of a spoken sentence to invite the listener's opinion while expressing one's own doubt or surprise. \"你說\" here isn't literal \"you say\" but more like \"tell me / what do you think.\"":"Digunakan di awal kalimat lisan untuk mengajak lawan bicara memberikan pendapat, sekaligus mengungkapkan keraguan atau keheranan pembicara. \"你說\" di sini bukan berarti harfiah \"kamu bilang\", melainkan lebih seperti \"coba bilang / menurutmu bagaimana\".","Tell me, it's so late already—do you think he'll still come back to eat?":"Coba bilang, sudah selarut ini, menurutmu dia masih akan pulang untuk makan tidak?","Tell me, with weather like this, do we still need to go out?":"Coba bilang, dengan cuaca seperti ini, apa kita masih perlu keluar?","it looks like / it seems that":"sepertinya / tampaknya","看樣子 + inference":"看樣子 + inferensi","Expresses an inference based on what the speaker observes; similar to 好像, but 看樣子 emphasizes a judgment drawn from visible clues. Avoid using it for facts already confirmed.":"Mengungkapkan sebuah dugaan berdasarkan apa yang diamati pembicara; mirip dengan 好像, tetapi 看樣子 menekankan penilaian yang diambil dari petunjuk yang terlihat. Hindari penggunaannya untuk fakta yang sudah dipastikan.","My older brother is in great shape; it looks like he has a habit of exercising regularly.":"Kakak laki-laki saya bertubuh sangat bugar, sepertinya dia punya kebiasaan berolahraga secara teratur.","The sky is dark; it looks like it's about to rain.":"Langit gelap, sepertinya sebentar lagi akan hujan.","who would have known / unexpectedly":"siapa sangka / tak disangka","誰知道 + unexpected result":"誰知道 + hasil tak terduga","Expresses surprise or dissatisfaction at an unexpected outcome; literally a rhetorical \"who knew,\" not a real question — don't mistake it for an interrogative sentence.":"Mengungkapkan keterkejutan atau ketidakpuasan atas hasil yang tak terduga; secara harfiah merupakan pertanyaan retoris \"siapa yang tahu\", bukan pertanyaan sungguhan — jangan disalahartikan sebagai kalimat tanya.","It had only rained for an hour, but who would have guessed the house would flood.":"Baru hujan satu jam saja, tapi siapa sangka rumahnya sampai kebanjiran.","He's usually very careful, but who would have thought he'd still get into a car accident this time.":"Dia biasanya sangat hati-hati, tapi siapa sangka kali ini dia tetap mengalami kecelakaan mobil.","so, that's why (casual)":"jadi, makanya (santai)","所以啦 + conclusion":"所以啦 + kesimpulan","A colloquial form of 所以 with the particle 啦 added, showing the speaker's realization or mild emphasis; not used in written registers. Carries more feeling than plain 所以.":"Merupakan bentuk lisan dari 所以 dengan tambahan partikel 啦, menunjukkan kesadaran atau penekanan ringan dari pembicara; tidak digunakan dalam ragam tulisan. Mengandung lebih banyak perasaan dibandingkan 所以 biasa.","So yeah, next time we should go line up earlier.":"Makanya lain kali kita harus antre lebih awal.","Everyone says that shop is delicious, so let's go try it today.":"Semua orang bilang toko itu enak, makanya hari ini kita coba ke sana, yuk.","really / truly can be said to (emphatic)":"benar-benar / sungguh dapat dikatakan (penekanan)","可 + 算是/說是 + evaluation":"可 + 算是/說是 + penilaian","Here 可 functions as an adverb before verbs like 算是/說是 to emphasize the speaker's strong conviction; distinct from the 可 in 可以 (permission) — don't confuse the two uses.":"Di sini 可 berfungsi sebagai kata keterangan sebelum kata kerja seperti 算是/說是 untuk menekankan keyakinan kuat pembicara; berbeda dengan 可 dalam 可以 (izin) — jangan sampai kedua penggunaan ini tertukar.","This beef noodle restaurant can really be said to be the most famous one in Taipei.":"Restoran mi sapi ini benar-benar bisa dikatakan sebagai yang paling terkenal di Taipei.","This movie can really be called the most moving film of the year.":"Film ini benar-benar bisa disebut sebagai film paling mengharukan tahun ini.","and / with (formal, written)":"dan / dengan (formal, bahasa tulis)","A + 與 + B":"A + 與 + B","A formal written equivalent of 和/跟, common in formal writing and documents; in everyday speech 和/跟 sounds more natural.":"Merupakan padanan formal dalam bahasa tulis untuk 和/跟, umum digunakan dalam tulisan dan dokumen resmi; dalam percakapan sehari-hari, 和/跟 terdengar lebih alami.","Sun Moon Lake and Alishan are both famous tourist spots in Taiwan.":"Danau Sun Moon Lake dan Gunung Alishan sama-sama merupakan tempat wisata terkenal di Taiwan.","Both teachers and students should follow the school's rules.":"Baik guru maupun murid harus mematuhi peraturan sekolah.","(verb) + yǔ + person + (verb)":"(kata kerja) + yǔ + orang + (kata kerja)","Yǔ is a formal, written-style preposition meaning 'with,' similar to the more colloquial gēn. It appears as 'yǔ + person + verb.' In everyday speech, gēn sounds more natural than yǔ.":"Yǔ adalah kata depan formal bergaya bahasa tulis yang berarti 'dengan', mirip dengan gēn yang lebih umum digunakan dalam bahasa sehari-hari. Yǔ muncul dalam pola 'yǔ + orang + kata kerja'. Dalam percakapan sehari-hari, gēn terdengar lebih alami daripada yǔ.","This writer loves to share life's touching moments with readers.":"Penulis ini suka berbagi momen-momen mengharukan dalam hidup dengan para pembaca.","He likes to share travel photos with friends.":"Dia suka berbagi foto perjalanan dengan teman-teman.","from (a starting point)":"dari (suatu titik awal)","yóu + starting point + verb + dào + endpoint":"yóu + titik awal + kata kerja + dào + titik akhir","Yóu is a formal preposition marking the starting point of a change or range, often used as 'yóu + starting point + verb + dào + endpoint.' Don't confuse it with the other use of yóu that marks who is responsible for an action (e.g., zhè jiàn shì yóu wǒ fùzé).":"Yóu adalah kata depan formal yang menandai titik awal suatu perubahan atau rentang, sering digunakan dalam pola 'yóu + titik awal + kata kerja + dào + titik akhir'. Jangan disamakan dengan penggunaan yóu lainnya yang menandai siapa yang bertanggung jawab atas suatu tindakan (misalnya, zhè jiàn shì yóu wǒ fùzé).","Late at night, the temperature on the mountain drops from ten degrees to below zero.":"Pada malam hari, suhu di gunung turun dari sepuluh derajat hingga di bawah nol derajat.","His weight decreased from sixty kilograms to fifty-five kilograms.":"Berat badannya turun dari enam puluh kilogram menjadi lima puluh lima kilogram.","somewhat, a little":"agak, sedikit","duōshǎo + verb (+ le)":"duōshǎo + kata kerja (+ le)","Here duōshǎo is not the question word 'how much/many' but an adverb meaning 'to some extent, a little.' Placed before a verb, it shows something happened to a certain degree. Don't confuse it with the interrogative duōshǎo qián (how much money).":"Di sini duōshǎo bukan kata tanya 'berapa banyak', melainkan kata keterangan yang berarti 'sampai taraf tertentu, sedikit'. Ditempatkan sebelum kata kerja, kata ini menunjukkan bahwa sesuatu terjadi sampai tingkat tertentu. Jangan disamakan dengan kata tanya duōshǎo qián (berapa uangnya).","He's saved up a bit of money, so you don't need to worry.":"Dia sudah menabung sedikit uang, jadi kamu tidak perlu khawatir.","I know a little about this matter, so you can ask me.":"Saya tahu sedikit tentang hal ini, jadi kamu bisa bertanya kepada saya.","already (emphatic)":"sudah (penegasan)","dōu + verb (+ guò) + ... + le":"dōu + kata kerja (+ guò) + ... + le","This dōu doesn't mean 'all' but emphasizes that something has already happened, used as 'dōu + verb (+ guò) + ... + le' to express frustration or exasperation. Don't confuse it with the dōu meaning 'all/everyone' (e.g., dàjiā dōu lái le).":"Dōu di sini bukan berarti 'semua', melainkan menegaskan bahwa sesuatu sudah terjadi, digunakan dalam pola 'dōu + kata kerja (+ guò) + ... + le' untuk mengungkapkan rasa kesal atau jengkel. Jangan disamakan dengan dōu yang berarti 'semua/semua orang' (misalnya, dàjiā dōu lái le).","I've already reminded him several times, but he still forgets to return the books.":"Saya sudah mengingatkannya beberapa kali, tapi dia masih lupa mengembalikan buku.","I've already told you many times, why are you still late?":"Saya sudah bilang berkali-kali, kenapa kamu masih terlambat?","away, off (resultative complement)":"hilang, lenyap (pelengkap hasil)","V + qù":"V + qù","Here qù is not the main verb 'to go' but a resultative complement after a verb, showing that something is removed or disappears as a result — as in chúqù, mǒqù, shīqù. Note that this qù does not take a following location.":"Di sini qù bukan kata kerja utama 'pergi', melainkan pelengkap hasil setelah kata kerja, yang menunjukkan bahwa sesuatu dihilangkan atau lenyap sebagai akibatnya — seperti pada chúqù, mǒqù, shīqù. Perlu diperhatikan bahwa qù ini tidak diikuti oleh keterangan tempat.","He removed the name from the list.":"Dia menghapus nama itu dari daftar.","The teacher wiped the words off the blackboard.":"Guru itu menghapus tulisan dari papan tulis.","to change/correct (something) back to the right state":"mengubah/memperbaiki (sesuatu) kembali ke keadaan yang benar","Subject + bǎ + O + V + guòlái":"Subjek + bǎ + O + V + guòlái","Here \"過來\" is a resultative complement meaning a shift from a bad/wrong state to a correct one, often paired with 把. Don't confuse it with the literal directional \"come over.\"":"\"過來\" di sini adalah pelengkap hasil yang menyatakan perubahan dari keadaan buruk/salah menjadi benar, sering dipasangkan dengan 把. Jangan disamakan dengan makna arah harfiahnya, yaitu \"datang ke sini\".","Parents use educational methods to correct their child's bad behavior.":"Orang tua menggunakan metode pendidikan untuk memperbaiki perilaku buruk anak mereka.","He finally corrected the pronunciation he had been saying wrong.":"Akhirnya dia memperbaiki pengucapan yang selama ini salah dia ucapkan.","fairly / passably ~ (a moderate, acceptable degree)":"cukup / lumayan ~ (tingkat sedang, dapat diterima)","Subject + hái + suàn + adjective":"Subjek + hái + suàn + kata sifat","\"還算\" is a set phrase expressing a modest, qualified positive assessment. Don't confuse this 還 with 還是 (still) or 還有 (also/there's still), which use different senses.":"\"還算\" adalah frasa tetap yang menyatakan penilaian positif yang sederhana dan bersyarat. Jangan disamakan 還 di sini dengan 還是 (masih) atau 還有 (juga/masih ada), yang memiliki makna berbeda.","The price of this sofa set is fairly cheap.":"Harga set sofa ini cukup murah.","This shop's service is fairly good.":"Layanan toko ini cukup baik.","\"才不~\" expresses strong, defiant denial or disagreement":"\"才不~\" menyatakan penyangkalan atau ketidaksetujuan yang kuat dan menantang","Subject + cái + bù + VP + (ne)":"Subjek + cái + bù + Frasa verba + (ne)","Unlike the 才 marking fact/reason/condition (才1–4), this 才 signals the speaker's strong pushback, often paired with 呢 for emphasis. Don't confuse it with the \"not until ~\" sense of 才.":"Berbeda dengan 才 yang menandai fakta/alasan/syarat (才1–4), 才 di sini menunjukkan penolakan keras dari pembicara, sering dipasangkan dengan 呢 untuk penekanan. Jangan disamakan dengan makna \"baru ~\" pada 才.","A skirt this short — no way he'd dare wear it!":"Rok sependek ini — mana mungkin dia berani memakainya!","I definitely don't believe what he says!":"Aku sama sekali tidak percaya apa yang dia katakan!","\"A is as (this/that) ~ as B\" — A reaches the same degree as B":"\"A se~ (seperti ini/itu) dengan B\" — A mencapai tingkat yang sama dengan B","A + yǒu + B + zhème/nàme + adjective":"A + yǒu + B + zhème/nàme + kata sifat","This pattern uses 有 to say two things reach the same degree; 這麼 refers to something near, 那麼 to something more distant. Unlike 比 (which shows superiority), this shows equal degree, not \"more than.\"":"Pola ini menggunakan 有 untuk menyatakan dua hal yang mencapai tingkat yang sama; 這麼 merujuk pada sesuatu yang dekat, 那麼 pada sesuatu yang lebih jauh. Berbeda dengan 比 (yang menunjukkan keunggulan), pola ini menunjukkan tingkat yang setara, bukan \"lebih dari\".","This classroom is as big as a basketball court.":"Ruang kelas ini sebesar lapangan basket.","This dog is as tall as a small child.":"Anjing ini setinggi anak kecil.","\"A is more ~ than B\" — a somewhat formal/literary comparative":"\"A lebih ~ daripada B\" — bentuk perbandingan yang agak formal/sastra","A + bǐ + B + láide + adjective":"A + bǐ + B + láide + kata sifat","\"來得\" follows a 比 comparison to state the result in a formal/literary tone, close to 比...更/還. Note it precedes only adjectives/stative verbs, not action verbs.":"\"來得\" mengikuti perbandingan 比 untuk menyatakan hasil dengan nada formal/sastra, mirip dengan 比...更/還. Perhatikan bahwa ia hanya mendahului kata sifat/verba statif, bukan verba tindakan.","My younger brother is taller than kids his age.":"Adik laki-laki saya lebih tinggi daripada anak-anak seusianya.","Taking the MRT is more convenient than driving.":"Naik MRT lebih praktis daripada menyetir.","so (good) that there's nothing to say":"(bagus) sampai tidak ada yang bisa dikatakan lagi","V/Adj ＋ 得沒話說":"V/Kata sifat ＋ 得沒話說","Adding 沒話說 after 得 shows a degree so extreme there's nothing to criticize — a strong compliment, stronger than 得很. Never used for negative traits.":"Menambahkan 沒話說 setelah 得 menunjukkan tingkat yang begitu ekstrem sehingga tidak ada yang bisa dikritik — pujian yang kuat, lebih kuat daripada 得很. Tidak pernah digunakan untuk sifat negatif.","The sisters in that family get along so well there's nothing to complain about — they've almost never fought.":"Kakak-beradik perempuan di keluarga itu akur banget sampai tidak ada yang bisa dikomentari — mereka hampir tidak pernah bertengkar.","This shop's service is so good there's nothing to complain about — everyone wants to come back.":"Layanan toko ini bagus sampai tidak ada yang bisa dikomentari — semua orang ingin kembali lagi.","toward/from (someone), for borrowing or asking":"kepada/dari (seseorang), untuk meminjam atau bertanya","A ＋ 向 ＋ B ＋ V":"A ＋ 向 ＋ B ＋ V","向 marks the person an action is directed toward or drawn from (e.g. borrowing, asking, learning) — more formal than 跟. Don't confuse it with 對, which marks the target of an attitude or opinion.":"向 menandai orang yang menjadi arah atau sumber suatu tindakan (misalnya meminjam, bertanya, belajar) — lebih formal daripada 跟. Jangan disamakan dengan 對, yang menandai sasaran suatu sikap atau pendapat.","I borrowed a thousand dollars from Dad.":"Saya meminjam seribu dolar dari Ayah.","The students asked the teacher questions.":"Para siswa bertanya kepada guru.","for (the benefit of)":"untuk (kepentingan)","為 ＋ N ＋ V（帶來/做…）":"為 ＋ N ＋ V（帶來/做…）","為 introduces the beneficiary or target of an action (like 給, but more formal/written), often with verbs like 帶來/做/爭取. Don't confuse it with 因為, which means 'because.'":"為 memperkenalkan penerima manfaat atau sasaran suatu tindakan (seperti 給, tetapi lebih formal/tertulis), sering digunakan dengan kata kerja seperti 帶來/做/爭取. Jangan disamakan dengan 因為, yang berarti 'karena.'","Changing jobs can sometimes bring you new opportunities.":"Berganti pekerjaan terkadang bisa membawa peluang baru bagi Anda.","The teacher prepared a lot of materials for the students.":"Guru telah menyiapkan banyak materi untuk para siswa.","since / given that... then...":"karena / mengingat... maka...","既然 ＋ A，就 ＋ B":"既然 ＋ A，就 ＋ B","既然 presents an already-established fact, and 就 draws a conclusion or suggestion from it — implying 'given that this is so.' Unlike plain cause-effect 因為...所以..., it often carries a tone of advice.":"既然 menyampaikan fakta yang sudah pasti, dan 就 menarik kesimpulan atau saran darinya — menyiratkan 'mengingat hal ini sudah demikian.' Berbeda dengan hubungan sebab-akibat biasa 因為...所以..., ungkapan ini sering membawa nada saran.","Since you're already attending classes at school, you might as well make good use of the time to take advantage of the school's resources.":"Karena kamu sudah mengikuti kelas di sekolah, sebaiknya manfaatkan waktu itu sebaik-baiknya untuk memanfaatkan sumber daya sekolah.","Since you've already decided, don't hesitate anymore.":"Karena kamu sudah memutuskan, jangan ragu-ragu lagi.","if not... then...":"jika tidak... maka...","不/沒（有）＋ A，就 ＋ B":"不/沒（有）＋ A，就 ＋ B","不/沒(有) negates the condition, and 就 states the resulting consequence. Use 不 for habitual/future situations and 沒(有) for completed/past ones. Common in written rules and notices.":"不/沒(有) menegasikan syarat, sedangkan 就 menyatakan akibat yang timbul. Gunakan 不 untuk situasi kebiasaan/masa depan dan 沒(有) untuk situasi yang sudah selesai/masa lampau. Sering muncul dalam peraturan dan pengumuman tertulis.","If you don't fill in your email address, the application won't succeed.":"Jika Anda tidak mengisi alamat email, pendaftaran tidak akan berhasil.","If you don't leave early, you'll be late.":"Jika kamu tidak berangkat lebih awal, kamu akan terlambat.","if you don't... right now, then... soon (warning)":"jika sekarang tidak... maka sebentar lagi... (peringatan)","zài bù + Verb + jiù + (yào) + Result + le":"zài bù + Verb + jiù + (yào) + Result + le","Expresses an urgent warning: \"if you don't act right now, a bad result will follow soon.\" Carries more urgency than a plain \"如果不\" conditional, and the second clause often pairs with \"就要...了\".":"Mengungkapkan peringatan yang mendesak: 'jika tidak segera bertindak sekarang, akibat buruk akan segera menyusul.' Bernada lebih mendesak daripada kalimat kondisional biasa dengan '如果不', dan klausa kedua sering dipasangkan dengan '就要...了'.","I have to leave now — if I don't go right away, I'll be late.":"Saya harus pergi sekarang — kalau tidak segera berangkat, saya akan terlambat.","If you don't eat now, it'll get cold soon.":"Kalau sekarang tidak dimakan, nanti akan cepat dingin.","absolutely must...":"harus mutlak...","fēi + Verb(Phrase) + bùkě / bù":"fēi + Verb(Phrase) + bùkě / bù","A double-negative construction expressing strong necessity or obligation. \"不可\" can be dropped, leaving just \"非...不\", but \"非...不可\" is more natural in speech. More formal and emphatic than \"一定要\".":"Ini adalah konstruksi negasi ganda yang menyatakan keharusan atau kewajiban yang kuat. '不可' dapat dihilangkan sehingga tersisa '非...不' saja, tetapi '非...不可' lebih alami dalam percakapan. Lebih formal dan tegas daripada '一定要'.","I'm about to be late for the meeting, so I absolutely have to leave now.":"Saya hampir terlambat rapat, jadi saya harus berangkat sekarang juga.","This matter is very important, so I must do it.":"Hal ini sangat penting, jadi saya harus melakukannya.","even if... (hypothetical concession)":"meskipun... (konsesi hipotetis)","jíshǐ + Clause A (hypothetical/extreme) + (Subject) + yě + Clause B":"jíshǐ + Klausa A (hipotetis/ekstrem) + (Subjek) + yě + Klausa B","A concessive construction usable for hypothetical or even counterfactual situations. Unlike \"雖然...但是\", which describes an already-true fact, \"即使\" sets up a hypothetical or extreme scenario.":"Struktur konsesif yang dapat digunakan untuk situasi hipotetis atau bahkan kontrafaktual. Berbeda dengan \"雖然...但是\" yang menggambarkan fakta yang sudah terjadi, \"即使\" menyiapkan skenario hipotetis atau ekstrem.","Even after graduating from university, you should still keep learning new knowledge on your own.":"Bahkan setelah lulus kuliah, kamu tetap harus terus belajar pengetahuan baru secara mandiri.","Even if the weather is bad, we still go outside to exercise.":"Meskipun cuaca buruk, kami tetap keluar untuk berolahraga.","even if... (an extreme hypothetical concession)":"meskipun... (konsesi hipotetis ekstrem)","jiùshì + Clause A (extreme case), yě + Clause B":"jiùshì + Klausa A (kasus ekstrem), yě + Klausa B","Nearly synonymous with \"即使\", but more colloquial, and typically used when citing an extreme example as the concession. Here \"就是\" is interchangeable with \"就算\".":"Hampir sama artinya dengan \"即使\", tetapi lebih bersifat sehari-hari, dan biasanya digunakan saat mengutip contoh ekstrem sebagai konsesi. Di sini \"就是\" dapat saling dipertukarkan dengan \"就算\".","If exercise is good for your health, then even spending a bit more time on it is worthwhile.":"Jika olahraga baik untuk kesehatan, maka meskipun harus meluangkan sedikit lebih banyak waktu untuknya pun sepadan.","Even if it rains, I'll still go.":"Meskipun hujan, saya tetap akan pergi.","no matter how... still...":"sekalipun..., tetap saja...","zài + Adjective/Verb + yě + unchanged result":"zài + Kata sifat/Kata kerja + yě + hasil yang tidak berubah","Expresses that no matter how extreme the degree, the result stays the same. \"再\" precedes an adjective or stative verb to emphasize degree, unlike \"即使\", which frames a hypothetical clause.":"Menyatakan bahwa betapa pun ekstremnya suatu tingkatan, hasilnya tetap sama. \"再\" diletakkan sebelum kata sifat atau kata kerja statif untuk menekankan tingkatan, berbeda dengan \"即使\" yang membentuk klausa hipotetis.","He loves playing the piano, so no matter how hard practicing is, he doesn't mind.":"Dia sangat suka bermain piano, jadi seberapa pun sulitnya berlatih, dia tidak keberatan.","No matter how cold the weather is, he still goes jogging.":"Seberapa pun dinginnya cuaca, dia tetap pergi joging.","Even if... still...":"Meskipun... tetap...","就算 + A (hypothesis) + 也 + B (result)":"就算 + A (hipotesis) + 也 + B (hasil)","Concedes a hypothetical condition while stressing the result stays the same. Unlike 雖然 (a real fact), 就算 introduces a hypothesis. Near-synonym of 即使, but more colloquial.":"Mengonsesi suatu kondisi hipotetis sambil menekankan bahwa hasilnya tetap sama. Berbeda dengan 雖然 (fakta yang nyata), 就算 memperkenalkan sebuah hipotesis. Hampir sinonim dengan 即使, tetapi lebih bersifat sehari-hari.","Even without a camera, you can still take photos with your phone.":"Bahkan tanpa kamera, kamu tetap bisa memotret dengan ponsel.","Even if you don't agree, I'm still going.":"Meskipun kamu tidak setuju, saya tetap akan pergi.","Unless...":"Kecuali...","除非 + A (the only condition), 否則/才 + B":"除非 + A (satu-satunya syarat), 否則/才 + B","Names the one condition that avoids the outcome, often paired with 否則 or 才. Unlike plain 如果不 (if not), 除非 stresses that this is the only way.":"Menyebutkan satu-satunya syarat yang dapat menghindari hasil tersebut, sering dipasangkan dengan 否則 atau 才. Berbeda dengan 如果不 (jika tidak) yang biasa, 除非 menekankan bahwa inilah satu-satunya cara.","Unless you're very interested in teaching, you'll easily lose your patience.":"Kecuali kamu sangat tertarik dengan mengajar, kamu akan mudah kehilangan kesabaran.","Unless it doesn't rain tomorrow, we won't go hiking.":"Kecuali besok tidak hujan, kami tidak akan pergi mendaki.","Otherwise":"Kalau tidak","A, 否則 + B (negative consequence)":"A, 否則 + B (konsekuensi negatif)","Introduces the negative consequence if the preceding statement doesn't hold. Nearly interchangeable with the more colloquial 不然, but 否則 leans more formal/written.":"Memperkenalkan konsekuensi negatif jika pernyataan sebelumnya tidak terpenuhi. Hampir dapat dipertukarkan dengan 不然 yang lebih sehari-hari, tetapi 否則 lebih condong ke bahasa formal/tulisan.","Go wake up Dad quickly, otherwise he'll be late for work.":"Cepat bangunkan Ayah, kalau tidak dia akan terlambat kerja.","Remember to bring an umbrella, otherwise you'll get soaked.":"Ingat bawa payung, kalau tidak kamu akan basah kuyup.","If... then...":"Jika... maka...","假如 + A (hypothesis), (就) + B (result)":"假如 + A (hipotesis), (就) + B (hasil)","Introduces a hypothetical premise; an optional 就 in the result clause strengthens the sense of immediate consequence. Near-synonym of 如果, though 假如 leans more literary/formal.":"Memperkenalkan premis hipotetis; 就 opsional dalam klausa hasil memperkuat kesan akibat langsung. Nyaris sinonim dengan 如果, meski 假如 lebih condong ke gaya sastra/formal.","If you can't finish it, just save it as an afternoon snack!":"Kalau tidak bisa menghabiskannya, simpan saja sebagai camilan sore!","If you have any problems, just call me.":"Kalau kamu punya masalah apa pun, telepon saja saya.","Actually/on the contrary":"Sebenarnya/justru sebaliknya","Subject + 倒(是) + predicate (unexpected contrast)":"Subjek + 倒(是) + predikat (kontras tak terduga)","Highlights a fact that contrasts with expectation, placed right after the subject and before the verb. Similar to 卻, but 倒(是) often carries a lighter, more reassuring or mildly surprising nuance.":"Menyoroti fakta yang berlawanan dengan ekspektasi, diletakkan tepat setelah subjek dan sebelum kata kerja. Mirip dengan 卻, tetapi 倒(是) sering membawa nuansa yang lebih ringan, lebih menenangkan atau sedikit mengejutkan.","This company is worth investing in; as for how much to invest, that can actually be discussed further.":"Perusahaan ini layak untuk diinvestasikan; soal berapa jumlah investasinya, itu sebenarnya masih bisa dibicarakan lebih lanjut.","This matter is quite troublesome, but he's actually not worried at all.":"Urusan ini cukup merepotkan, tetapi dia sebenarnya sama sekali tidak khawatir.","would rather... than...":"lebih baik... daripada...","寧願 + A (the lesser cost accepted) + 也（不）要 + B (the desired outcome)":"寧願 + A (biaya lebih kecil yang diterima) + 也（不）要 + B (hasil yang diinginkan)","\"寧願\" expresses a personal willingness to choose one option over another, often implying reluctance about the alternative — slightly more emotional in tone than \"寧可\".":"\"寧願\" mengungkapkan kesediaan pribadi untuk memilih satu opsi dibanding yang lain, sering menyiratkan keengganan terhadap alternatifnya — nadanya sedikit lebih emosional daripada \"寧可\".","He would rather earn a little less money than spend all his time on work.":"Dia lebih memilih menghasilkan uang sedikit lebih sedikit daripada menghabiskan seluruh waktunya untuk bekerja.","She would rather walk home alone than ride in the car with him.":"Dia lebih memilih berjalan kaki pulang sendirian daripada naik mobil bersamanya.","would rather (choose)... than...":"lebih memilih (memilih)... daripada...","寧可 + A (the option chosen after weighing) + 也（不）要 + B":"寧可 + A (opsi yang dipilih setelah dipertimbangkan) + 也（不）要 + B","\"寧可\" expresses a deliberate choice made after weighing two options; it is more neutral and slightly more formal than \"寧願\", and combines naturally with either \"也要\" or \"也不要\".":"\"寧可\" mengungkapkan pilihan yang diambil dengan sengaja setelah mempertimbangkan dua opsi; sifatnya lebih netral dan sedikit lebih formal daripada \"寧願\", serta secara alami dapat dipasangkan dengan \"也要\" maupun \"也不要\".","I would rather earn a little less money than have no leisure time of my own.":"Saya lebih memilih menghasilkan uang sedikit lebih sedikit daripada tidak punya waktu luang sama sekali untuk diri sendiri.","He would rather go hungry than not save up money to buy that camera.":"Dia lebih memilih kelaparan daripada tidak menabung untuk membeli kamera itu.","unexpectedly, surprisingly":"tak terduga, mengejutkan","(Subject) + 居然 + VP (unexpected but actual result)":"(Subjek) + 居然 + VP (hasil tak terduga tetapi nyata)","\"居然\" shows surprise at something that actually happened contrary to expectation — it marks a real fact, not exaggeration, so don't confuse it with \"簡直\".":"\"居然\" menunjukkan keterkejutan atas sesuatu yang benar-benar terjadi berlawanan dengan ekspektasi — ini menandai fakta nyata, bukan melebih-lebihkan, jadi jangan disamakan dengan \"簡直\".","He's usually very busy with work, but surprisingly he still has time to write novels.":"Dia biasanya sangat sibuk dengan pekerjaan, tetapi mengejutkannya dia masih sempat menulis novel.","She's only been studying Chinese for half a year, but she can surprisingly understand newspapers already.":"Dia baru belajar bahasa Mandarin selama setengah tahun, tetapi mengejutkannya sudah bisa memahami koran.","simply, practically (exaggeration)":"sungguh, benar-benar (melebih-lebihkan)","簡直 + 是/像 + an exaggerated statement":"簡直 + 是/像 + pernyataan yang dilebih-lebihkan","\"簡直\" is used for exaggerated emphasis, meaning \"practically/simply\" rather than a literal fact — different from \"居然\", which marks genuine surprise at something real.":"\"簡直\" digunakan untuk penekanan yang dilebih-lebihkan, berarti \"sungguh/benar-benar\" alih-alih fakta harfiah — berbeda dengan \"居然\", yang menandai keterkejutan tulus atas sesuatu yang nyata.","Finishing a paper in one day is simply impossible.":"Menyelesaikan makalah dalam satu hari sungguh mustahil.","The scenery here is so beautiful it's simply like a painting.":"Pemandangan di sini begitu indah, sungguh seperti lukisan.","anyway, in any case":"bagaimanapun juga, dalam hal apa pun","(A yěhǎo, B yěhǎo,) 反正 + conclusion (true regardless of circumstances)":"(A yěhǎo, B yěhǎo,) 反正 + kesimpulan (benar terlepas dari keadaan)","\"反正\" indicates that the conclusion stays the same no matter the circumstances; it's often paired with \"〜也好、〜也好\" or \"不管〜\".":"\"反正\" menunjukkan bahwa kesimpulan tetap sama apa pun keadaannya; sering dipasangkan dengan \"〜也好、〜也好\" atau \"不管〜\".","Whether by borrowing money or by earning money first and studying later, he's determined to finish university no matter what.":"Entah dengan meminjam uang atau dengan mencari uang dulu baru kemudian belajar, dia bertekad untuk menyelesaikan kuliah apa pun yang terjadi.","Since we don't have to go to work tomorrow anyway, it's fine if we go to bed a bit later.":"Karena bagaimanapun juga besok tidak perlu masuk kerja, tidak apa-apa kalau kita tidur agak larut.","fortunately (avoided something bad)":"untungnya (berhasil menghindari sesuatu yang buruk)","幸虧 + reason, (不然) + bad outcome that was avoided":"幸虧 + alasan, (不然) + akibat buruk yang berhasil dihindari","Use 幸虧 to describe a lucky factor that prevented a bad outcome; a clause with 不然/要不然 ('otherwise') often follows. It is very close in meaning to 幸好, both used in everyday speech, so don't overthink the difference.":"Gunakan 幸虧 untuk menggambarkan faktor keberuntungan yang mencegah hasil buruk; klausa dengan 不然/要不然 ('kalau tidak') sering mengikutinya. Maknanya sangat dekat dengan 幸好, keduanya dipakai dalam percakapan sehari-hari, jadi tidak perlu terlalu memikirkan perbedaannya.","He almost took the wrong way, but fortunately he stopped to check the map.":"Dia hampir salah jalan, tetapi untungnya dia berhenti untuk memeriksa peta.","Before I left, I luckily brought an extra umbrella, otherwise I would have gotten soaked.":"Sebelum berangkat, untungnya saya membawa payung cadangan, kalau tidak saya pasti sudah basah kuyup.","surely... isn't it? (rhetorical question)":"masak iya...? (pertanyaan retoris)","難道 + subject + predicate + (嗎)?":"難道 + subjek + predikat + (嗎)?","難道 turns a sentence into a rhetorical question, showing the speaker is already confident of the (opposite) answer. The final 嗎 can sometimes be dropped, but keeping it sounds natural for learners. Unlike a real question, no answer is actually expected.":"難道 mengubah sebuah kalimat menjadi pertanyaan retoris, menunjukkan bahwa pembicara sudah yakin akan jawaban (yang sebaliknya). 嗎 di akhir kalimat terkadang bisa dihilangkan, tetapi mempertahankannya terdengar lebih alami bagi pembelajar. Berbeda dari pertanyaan sungguhan, sebenarnya tidak ada jawaban yang diharapkan.","We've been close friends for twenty years — how could I possibly not understand you?":"Kita sudah bersahabat selama dua puluh tahun — masak saya tidak mengerti kamu?","He's late every single day — surely he knows he'll get scolded for being late, doesn't he?":"Setiap hari dia terlambat — masak dia tidak tahu akan dimarahi karena terlambat?","count as / be considered (a judgment or evaluation)":"dianggap sebagai / dihitung sebagai (suatu penilaian atau evaluasi)","Subject + 算（是） + noun/adjective":"Subjek + 算（是） + kata benda/kata sifat","算 expresses the speaker's subjective judgment, meaning something reaches or fits a certain level/category. Adding 是 (算是) barely changes the meaning. It's a softer, less definite way of stating something than a plain 是 sentence.":"算 mengungkapkan penilaian subjektif pembicara, yang berarti sesuatu mencapai atau sesuai dengan tingkat/kategori tertentu. Menambahkan 是 (算是) hampir tidak mengubah artinya. Ini adalah cara menyatakan sesuatu yang lebih lembut dan kurang pasti dibandingkan kalimat 是 biasa.","This typhoon counts as a strong one, so you really need to prepare water and food in advance.":"Topan ini bisa dianggap kuat, jadi kamu benar-benar perlu menyiapkan air dan makanan terlebih dahulu.","This shop's beef noodles are considered cheap — only a hundred dollars.":"Mi sapi di toko ini terhitung murah — hanya seratus dolar.","no wonder... (realizing the reason)":"pantas saja... (menyadari alasannya)","難怪/怪不得 + clause (realization after learning the reason)":"難怪/怪不得 + klausa (menyadari sesuatu setelah mengetahui alasannya)","Both 難怪 and 怪不得 mean 'no wonder,' used when learning a reason clears up something puzzling; they're nearly interchangeable, with 怪不得 slightly more colloquial. The reason is often stated first, followed by the clause expressing realization.":"Baik 難怪 maupun 怪不得 berarti 'pantas saja', digunakan ketika mengetahui suatu alasan menjelaskan sesuatu yang membingungkan; keduanya hampir bisa saling menggantikan, dengan 怪不得 sedikit lebih kolokial. Alasannya biasanya disebutkan lebih dulu, diikuti oleh klausa yang menyatakan kesadaran tersebut.","It really was you — no wonder the voice sounded so familiar to me.":"Ternyata benar kamu — pantas saja suaranya terdengar familiar bagi saya.","He caught a cold — no wonder he looks so unwell today.":"Dia sedang masuk angin — pantas saja dia terlihat tidak sehat hari ini.","sure enough, as expected (prediction confirmed)":"benar saja, seperti yang diperkirakan (prediksi terbukti benar)","(prediction), 果然 + result (that matches it)":"(prediksi), 果然 + hasil (yang sesuai dengannya)","果然 states that an earlier prediction or guess actually came true; it can appear at the start of a sentence or right before the predicate. Unlike 難怪 (realizing a reason), 果然 is about a prediction matching reality.":"果然 menyatakan bahwa prediksi atau dugaan sebelumnya ternyata benar-benar terjadi; kata ini bisa muncul di awal kalimat atau tepat sebelum predikat. Berbeda dengan 難怪 (menyadari suatu alasan), 果然 berkaitan dengan prediksi yang sesuai dengan kenyataan.","Dad forgot to wear a hat when he went out, and sure enough, he got sunburned when he came back.":"Ayah lupa memakai topi saat keluar, dan benar saja, dia terbakar matahari ketika pulang.","The weather forecast said it would rain today, and sure enough, it rained when I went out.":"Ramalan cuaca mengatakan hari ini akan hujan, dan benar saja, saat saya keluar hujan pun turun.","surprisingly, actually":"tidak disangka, ternyata","Subject + jìng(rán) + unexpected result":"Subjek + jìng(rán) + hasil yang tidak terduga","\"Jìngrán\" expresses surprise at an unexpected outcome. It's close in meaning to \"jūrán\" but slightly more formal; the bare form \"jìng\" alone is common in writing.":"\"Jìngrán\" mengungkapkan keterkejutan atas hasil yang tidak terduga. Maknanya mirip dengan \"jūrán\" tetapi sedikit lebih formal; bentuk singkat \"jìng\" saja sering digunakan dalam tulisan.","A child not even ten years old actually has such a mature way of thinking.":"Seorang anak yang belum genap sepuluh tahun ternyata memiliki cara berpikir yang begitu dewasa.","He doesn't usually study much, but this time he actually got first place on the test.":"Dia biasanya tidak banyak belajar, tetapi kali ini ternyata mendapat peringkat pertama dalam ujian.","do (V) as usual / as scheduled":"melakukan (V) seperti biasa / sesuai rencana","zhào + V (+ Noun)":"zhào + V (+ Kata benda)","\"Zhào\" before a verb means carrying it out according to the original rule or plan, regardless of a change in circumstances — it emphasizes an unchanged standard more than \"háishì\" alone.":"\"Zhào\" sebelum kata kerja berarti melaksanakan sesuatu sesuai aturan atau rencana awal, terlepas dari adanya perubahan keadaan — ini lebih menekankan standar yang tidak berubah dibandingkan sekadar menggunakan \"háishì\".","Although he only moved in at the end of the month, he still pays this month's rent in full as usual.":"Meskipun dia baru pindah pada akhir bulan, dia tetap membayar penuh sewa bulan ini seperti biasa.","Even if the boss doesn't agree, the meeting will still be held as scheduled.":"Meskipun bos tidak setuju, rapat tetap akan diadakan sesuai rencana.","just (emphatic) — an unchanging trait":"memang (penegasan) — sifat yang tidak berubah","(Bùguǎn...) + Subject + jiùshì + Adj/Verb":"(Bùguǎn...) + Subjek + jiùshì + Adj/Verb","Here \"jiùshì\" is not the copula \"is\" but an emphatic adverb stressing a trait or stance that stays fixed no matter the circumstances; it often pairs with \"bùguǎn\" or \"zěnme.\"":"Di sini \"jiùshì\" bukan kata kopula \"adalah\", melainkan kata keterangan penegasan yang menekankan sifat atau sikap yang tetap tidak berubah apa pun keadaannya; sering dipasangkan dengan \"bùguǎn\" atau \"zěnme\".","No matter what problem he runs into, he's just always confident.":"Tidak peduli masalah apa yang dia hadapi, dia memang selalu percaya diri.","No matter how I persuade him, it's no use — he just won't apologize.":"Bagaimanapun aku membujuknya, tetap tidak ada gunanya — dia memang tidak mau minta maaf.","just N/V(O) alone is enough to...":"hanya dengan N/V(O) saja sudah cukup untuk...","Guāng + N/V(O) + jiù + Result":"Guāng + N/V(O) + jiù + Hasil","\"Guāng\" limits the scope to \"just this alone,\" and \"jiù\" introduces the sufficient result that follows. It's more colloquial and emphatic than using \"zhǐ\" by itself.":"\"Guāng\" membatasi cakupannya menjadi \"hanya ini saja,\" dan \"jiù\" memperkenalkan hasil yang cukup terjadi setelahnya. Ini lebih bersifat lisan dan lebih menegaskan dibandingkan hanya menggunakan \"zhǐ\" saja.","Just from the title alone, you can tell this is a very creative book.":"Hanya dari judulnya saja, kamu bisa tahu bahwa ini adalah buku yang sangat kreatif.","Just by looking at the photos, you can feel how beautiful the scenery there is.":"Hanya dengan melihat fotonya saja, kamu bisa merasakan betapa indahnya pemandangan di sana.","(not) at all, simply not":"(tidak) sama sekali, sepenuhnya tidak","Subject + gēnběn + (bù/méi) + V/Adj":"Subjek + gēnběn + (bù/méi) + V/Adj","\"Gēnběn\" strengthens a negative statement, adding a sense of \"simply/at all\" — stronger than plain \"bù/méi,\" often implying the situation is more extreme than expected.":"\"Gēnběn\" memperkuat pernyataan negatif, menambahkan makna \"sama sekali/sepenuhnya\" — lebih kuat daripada sekadar \"bù/méi,\" sering menyiratkan bahwa situasinya lebih ekstrem dari yang diperkirakan.","He's very busy with work every day, so he has basically no time at all to spend with his children.":"Dia sangat sibuk dengan pekerjaan setiap hari, sehingga hampir sama sekali tidak punya waktu untuk anak-anaknya.","He doesn't even know where the MRT station is — he's simply never been to Taipei at all.":"Dia bahkan tidak tahu di mana stasiun MRT itu — dia sama sekali belum pernah ke Taipei.","rely on / by means of":"mengandalkan / dengan cara","Subject + 靠 + means/support + verb phrase":"Subjek + 靠 + sarana/dukungan + frasa verba","\"靠\" means \"to rely on / by means of,\" introducing the means or support one depends on. \"靠著\" often marks an ongoing state. Don't confuse it with \"根據,\" which cites objective evidence.":"\"靠\" berarti \"mengandalkan / dengan cara,\" memperkenalkan sarana atau dukungan yang diandalkan seseorang. \"靠著\" biasanya menandai keadaan yang sedang berlangsung. Jangan disamakan dengan \"根據,\" yang mengutip bukti objektif.","Whatever problems arise in life, we must try hard to solve them by relying on our own strength.":"Apa pun masalah yang muncul dalam hidup, kita harus berusaha keras menyelesaikannya dengan mengandalkan kekuatan diri sendiri.","He got into university through his own effort.":"Dia berhasil masuk universitas dengan usahanya sendiri.","according to / based on":"menurut / berdasarkan","根據 + source/evidence + clause":"根據 + sumber/bukti + klausa","\"根據\" cites an objective source (a report, data, law) as the basis for a statement. Unlike \"靠,\" which names something one relies on for support, it backs up a judgment or conclusion, and is common in formal writing.":"\"根據\" mengutip sumber objektif (laporan, data, hukum) sebagai dasar suatu pernyataan. Berbeda dengan \"靠\" yang menyebutkan sesuatu yang diandalkan seseorang untuk mendapat dukungan, \"根據\" digunakan untuk mendukung suatu penilaian atau kesimpulan, dan umum digunakan dalam tulisan formal.","According to the weather report, it will rain tomorrow afternoon.":"Menurut laporan cuaca, besok sore akan turun hujan.","According to the survey, many young people like to drink handmade tea-stand beverages.":"Menurut survei, banyak anak muda suka minum minuman racikan tangan dari kedai teh.","so that / in order to":"agar / supaya","Clause 1, 好 + Clause 2 (purpose)":"Klausa 1, 好 + Klausa 2 (tujuan)","\"好\" precedes a verb phrase to show that the preceding action is done in order to achieve that purpose. It resembles \"以便\" but is more colloquial and concise.":"\"好\" diletakkan sebelum frasa verba untuk menunjukkan bahwa tindakan sebelumnya dilakukan demi mencapai tujuan tersebut. Mirip dengan \"以便\", tetapi lebih sehari-hari dan ringkas.","If you're living abroad alone, remember to call home often when you have time, so that your family can feel at ease.":"Jika kamu tinggal sendirian di luar negeri, ingatlah untuk sering menelepon pulang saat ada waktu, agar keluarga bisa merasa tenang.","I'll leave home early so as to avoid the rush-hour traffic jam.":"Saya akan berangkat dari rumah lebih awal agar terhindar dari kemacetan jam sibuk.","ever since ... (afterward)":"sejak ... (setelah itu)","自從 + event/time point + 後, + result":"自從 + peristiwa/titik waktu + 後, + hasil","\"自從......後\" marks a specific event or point in time as the starting point for an ongoing situation or change afterward, emphasizing the moment right after that point more than \"自從\" alone.":"\"自從......後\" menandai suatu peristiwa atau titik waktu tertentu sebagai titik awal dari suatu keadaan atau perubahan yang berlanjut setelahnya, dengan penekanan lebih pada momen tepat setelah titik itu dibandingkan hanya \"自從\" saja.","Since his research was published, it has received a great deal of recognition.":"Sejak penelitiannya dipublikasikan, penelitian itu telah mendapat banyak pengakuan.","Since moving to Taipei, he has made many new friends.":"Sejak pindah ke Taipei, dia telah mendapatkan banyak teman baru.","ever since ...":"sejak ...","自從 + event/time point + 以來, + (ongoing) result":"自從 + peristiwa/titik waktu + 以來, + hasil (yang berlangsung)","\"自從......以來\" emphasizes a state or change that has continued from a point in time up to now, stressing ongoing duration more strongly than \"自從......後.\"":"\"自從......以來\" menekankan suatu keadaan atau perubahan yang terus berlangsung sejak suatu titik waktu hingga sekarang, dengan penekanan pada durasi yang berkelanjutan lebih kuat daripada \"自從......後\".","Ever since he started learning tennis, his performance has consistently been outstanding.":"Sejak dia mulai belajar tenis, penampilannya selalu luar biasa.","Ever since I moved here, I've gotten to know many new friends.":"Sejak saya pindah ke sini, saya telah mengenal banyak teman baru.","up until now":"sampai sekarang","(past event), zhìjīn + (réng/hái/dōu) + verb":"(peristiwa masa lalu), zhìjīn + (réng/hái/dōu) + verba","\"Zhìjīn\" marks that a state or effect starting in the past continues up to now; it often pairs with \"仍/還/都\" after it. It is more formal/written than the spoken \"到現在\".":"\"Zhìjīn\" menandai bahwa suatu keadaan atau efek yang dimulai di masa lalu masih berlanjut hingga sekarang; sering diikuti oleh \"仍/還/都\" setelahnya. Kata ini lebih formal/tertulis dibandingkan \"到現在\" yang bersifat lisan.","He said a sentence that, to this day, still leaves a deep impression on me.":"Dia mengucapkan sebuah kalimat yang sampai sekarang masih meninggalkan kesan mendalam bagi saya.","This happened ten years ago, and people still often bring it up to this day.":"Hal ini terjadi sepuluh tahun yang lalu, dan sampai sekarang orang-orang masih sering membicarakannya.","used to be A, now B":"dulu A, sekarang B","Yuánlái + A, rújīn + B":"Yuánlái + A, rújīn + B","This pattern pairs a past state (\"原來\") with the present, changed state (\"如今\") to highlight contrast/change. Similar to \"以前...現在...\", but \"如今\" carries a slightly more literary, dramatic-change nuance.":"Pola ini memasangkan keadaan masa lalu (\"原來\") dengan keadaan sekarang yang telah berubah (\"如今\") untuk menonjolkan kontras/perubahan. Mirip dengan \"以前...現在...\", tetapi \"如今\" membawa nuansa sastra dan perubahan yang sedikit lebih dramatis.","This plot of land used to grow bananas; now it has been replanted with mangoes.":"Sebidang tanah ini dulunya ditanami pisang; sekarang telah ditanami ulang dengan mangga.","He used to be a teacher; now he has become the principal.":"Dulu dia adalah seorang guru; sekarang dia telah menjadi kepala sekolah.","on one hand... on the other hand...":"di satu sisi... di sisi lain...","Yì fāngmiàn + A, yì fāngmiàn + B":"Yì fāngmiàn + A, yì fāngmiàn + B","Used to present two aspects or actions that hold true at the same time; somewhat formal. Similar to \"一面...一面...\", but \"一方面\" is mainly for contrasting two aspects/reasons, while \"一面...一面...\" more often describes two actions done simultaneously.":"Digunakan untuk menyampaikan dua aspek atau tindakan yang berlaku pada saat yang sama; agak formal. Mirip dengan \"一面...一面...\", tetapi \"一方面\" terutama digunakan untuk mengontraskan dua aspek/alasan, sedangkan \"一面...一面...\" lebih sering menggambarkan dua tindakan yang dilakukan secara bersamaan.","When performing, on the one hand you have to pay attention to your movements, and on the other hand you also have to coordinate with others.":"Saat tampil, di satu sisi kamu harus memperhatikan gerakanmu, di sisi lain kamu juga harus berkoordinasi dengan orang lain.","On one hand she wants to save more money, and on the other hand she also wants to travel abroad.":"Di satu sisi dia ingin menabung lebih banyak uang, di sisi lain dia juga ingin bepergian ke luar negeri.","while doing A, doing B":"sambil melakukan A, melakukan B","Yímiàn + action A, yímiàn + action B":"Yímiàn + tindakan A, yímiàn + tindakan B","Describes the same subject doing two actions at the same time; fairly colloquial and largely interchangeable with \"一邊...一邊...\". Unlike \"一方面\" (which contrasts aspects/reasons), \"一面\" is used for concrete actions happening simultaneously.":"Menggambarkan subjek yang sama melakukan dua tindakan pada saat yang sama; cukup informal dan sebagian besar dapat dipertukarkan dengan \"一邊...一邊...\". Berbeda dengan \"一方面\" (yang mengontraskan aspek/alasan), \"一面\" digunakan untuk tindakan konkret yang terjadi secara bersamaan.","The audience below the stage clapped while singing along.":"Penonton di bawah panggung bertepuk tangan sambil ikut bernyanyi.","He was riding his bike while talking on the phone, which is very dangerous.":"Dia mengendarai sepeda sambil menelepon, yang sangat berbahaya.","absolutely, whatever you do":"mutlak, apa pun yang terjadi","Qiānwàn + (bié/bùyào) + verb":"Qiānwàn + (bié/bùyào) + kata kerja","An adverb expressing the speaker's strong warning or plea, typically used in imperative or prohibitive sentences. Especially common as \"千萬別/千萬不要\" (\"whatever you do, don't...\"). Carries more urgency/pleading than \"一定\".":"Kata keterangan yang mengungkapkan peringatan atau permohonan kuat dari pembicara, biasanya digunakan dalam kalimat perintah atau larangan. Terutama umum dalam bentuk \"千萬別/千萬不要\" (\"apa pun yang terjadi, jangan...\"). Memiliki nuansa mendesak/memohon yang lebih kuat daripada \"一定\".","When going abroad, you must absolutely remember to bring your passport.":"Saat pergi ke luar negeri, apa pun yang terjadi kamu harus ingat membawa paspor.","When crossing the street, whatever you do, don't look at your phone.":"Saat menyeberang jalan, apa pun yang terjadi, jangan melihat ponsel.","in the process of / ongoing":"sedang berlangsung / sedang dalam proses","V + 中":"V + 中","\"V+中\" marks an action as currently ongoing, often in formal or written contexts such as notices and reports. Unlike \"正在V\", \"V中\" can stand alone as a label (e.g. 施工中, 營業中) without needing a subject.":"\"V+中\" menandai suatu tindakan yang sedang berlangsung, sering digunakan dalam konteks formal atau tulisan seperti pengumuman dan laporan. Berbeda dengan \"正在V\", \"V中\" dapat berdiri sendiri sebagai label (misalnya 施工中, 營業中) tanpa memerlukan subjek.","The cause of the accident is still under investigation.":"Penyebab kecelakaan tersebut masih dalam penyelidikan.","This case is still under discussion, and there's no result yet.":"Kasus ini masih dalam pembahasan, dan belum ada hasilnya.","as a result, it turned out that...":"akibatnya, ternyata...","Clause 1, 結果 + Clause 2":"Klausa 1, 結果 + Klausa 2","\"結果\" introduces the final outcome that followed from what was said before, and can be used for both good and bad results. Unlike \"因此\", which signals a logical cause-to-conclusion link, \"結果\" emphasizes how a situation actually turned out.":"\"結果\" memperkenalkan hasil akhir yang terjadi setelah apa yang disebutkan sebelumnya, dan dapat digunakan untuk hasil baik maupun buruk. Berbeda dengan \"因此\", yang menandakan hubungan logis dari sebab ke kesimpulan, \"結果\" menekankan bagaimana suatu keadaan sebenarnya berakhir.","He interviewed at many companies, but in the end only one company notified him to start work.":"Dia wawancara di banyak perusahaan, tetapi hasilnya hanya satu perusahaan yang memberitahunya untuk mulai bekerja.","He stayed up late studying every night, and as a result he had such a bad headache during the exam that he couldn't write.":"Dia begadang belajar setiap malam, dan akibatnya saat ujian dia sakit kepala begitu parah sampai tidak bisa menulis.","due to / owing to":"karena / disebabkan oleh","由於 + reason, (就/因此) + result":"由於 + alasan, (就/因此) + hasil","\"由於\" introduces a cause or reason and is more formal/written than \"因為\". It often pairs with \"因此/所以/就\" in the result clause, and like \"因為\" it can appear at the start of a sentence or mid-sentence.":"\"由於\" memperkenalkan sebab atau alasan dan lebih formal/tertulis dibandingkan \"因為\". Kata ini sering berpasangan dengan \"因此/所以/就\" pada klausa hasil, dan seperti \"因為\", dapat muncul di awal kalimat atau di tengah kalimat.","Poor expressive ability was exactly my weakness, but by speaking and writing a lot, I managed to overcome these weaknesses.":"Kemampuan berekspresi yang buruk memang kelemahan saya, tetapi dengan banyak berbicara dan menulis, saya berhasil mengatasi kelemahan-kelemahan ini.","Due to the approaching typhoon, all of tomorrow's flights have been cancelled.":"Karena topan yang akan segera tiba, semua penerbangan besok telah dibatalkan.","therefore, as a result":"oleh karena itu, akibatnya","Reason clause, 因此 + result clause":"Klausa alasan, 因此 + klausa akibat","\"因此\" links a cause to its logical result and is more formal/written than \"所以\". Unlike \"所以\", it can begin a brand-new sentence on its own, not just join clauses within one sentence.":"\"因此\" menghubungkan sebab dengan akibat logisnya dan lebih formal/bersifat tulisan dibandingkan \"所以\". Berbeda dengan \"所以\", kata ini bisa mengawali kalimat baru secara mandiri, bukan hanya menghubungkan klausa dalam satu kalimat.","This noodle shop won first place in a beef noodle competition, and as a result attracted more customers.":"Kedai mi ini memenangkan juara pertama dalam kompetisi mi sapi, dan akibatnya menarik lebih banyak pelanggan.","He is late for class every time, so the teacher doesn't have a very good impression of him.":"Dia selalu terlambat masuk kelas, sehingga gurunya tidak memiliki kesan yang sangat baik terhadapnya.","even (to an extreme degree)":"bahkan (hingga tingkat ekstrem)","A, 甚至(於) + B":"A, 甚至(於) + B","\"甚至(於)\" highlights the most extreme or surprising item among a series, often paired with \"連…都/也\". \"甚至於\" is the more formal written variant. It carries stronger emphasis than \"連\" alone.":"\"甚至(於)\" menonjolkan hal paling ekstrem atau mengejutkan dalam suatu rangkaian, sering dipasangkan dengan \"連…都/也\". \"甚至於\" adalah varian yang lebih formal dalam bahasa tulisan. Penekanannya lebih kuat dibandingkan hanya menggunakan \"連\".","My little sister is very afraid of the dark — she even needs to keep the light on when sleeping at night.":"Adik perempuan saya sangat takut gelap — bahkan saat tidur malam pun harus tetap menyalakan lampu.","Transportation in this city is very convenient — there are even buses you can take in the middle of the night.":"Transportasi di kota ini sangat nyaman — bahkan tengah malam pun masih ada bus yang bisa dinaiki.","any":"apa pun","任何 + N (+ 都/也) + V":"任何 + N (+ 都/也) + V","\"任何\" means \"any/whatever,\" typically paired with \"都\" or \"也\" to express totality. Unlike \"什麼\", it doesn't ask about identity but asserts inclusiveness across all cases—a common mistake is omitting 都/也.":"\"任何\" berarti \"apa pun/sembarang\", biasanya dipasangkan dengan \"都\" atau \"也\" untuk menyatakan keseluruhan. Berbeda dengan \"什麼\", kata ini tidak digunakan untuk menanyakan identitas, melainkan menegaskan cakupan menyeluruh pada semua kasus — kesalahan umum adalah menghilangkan 都/也.","Before making any major decision, one should think carefully.":"Sebelum membuat keputusan penting apa pun, seseorang harus berpikir dengan hati-hati.","This matter is very important; no one can be careless about it.":"Hal ini sangat penting; siapa pun tidak boleh menganggapnya remeh.","the above":"yang di atas","由以上 + [content], ... / 以上是 + [content]":"由以上 + [content], ... / 以上是 + [content]","\"以上\" refers back to everything stated previously, often opening a summary as \"由以上...\" or \"以上是...\". Don't confuse it with the \"以上\" after numbers meaning \"or more,\" which is a different usage.":"\"以上\" merujuk kembali pada semua hal yang telah disebutkan sebelumnya, sering digunakan untuk membuka ringkasan dengan \"由以上...\" atau \"以上是...\". Jangan disamakan dengan \"以上\" setelah angka yang berarti \"atau lebih\", karena itu penggunaan yang berbeda.","From the above report, we can see that students in different regions learn differently.":"Dari laporan di atas, kita dapat melihat bahwa siswa di berbagai daerah belajar dengan cara yang berbeda.","The above is the key points of today's meeting. Does anyone have questions?":"Yang di atas adalah poin-poin penting rapat hari ini. Apakah ada yang punya pertanyaan?","in terms of / regarding":"dalam hal / mengenai","(在) + N + 方面":"(在) + N + 方面","\"（在）...方面\" narrows the topic to a specific area or aspect, often more neutral/objective than \"關於\". \"在\" can be omitted, but including it at the start of the clause sounds more natural.":"\"（在）...方面\" mempersempit topik ke bidang atau aspek tertentu, biasanya lebih netral/objektif dibandingkan \"關於\". \"在\" boleh dihilangkan, tetapi jika diletakkan di awal klausa akan terdengar lebih alami.","Besides exercise, Dad is also very careful about his diet.":"Selain berolahraga, Ayah juga sangat memperhatikan pola makannya.","When it comes to studying, my older sister has always worked hard.":"Dalam hal belajar, kakak perempuan saya selalu bekerja keras.","about / regarding":"tentang / mengenai","關於 + N, ... / N1 + 關於 + N2 + 的 + N3":"關於 + N, ... / N1 + 關於 + N2 + 的 + N3","\"關於\" introduces a topic and often opens the sentence to set the theme; it can also modify a noun as \"關於...的+N\". It covers a broader scope than \"（在）...方面\", which narrows to a specific aspect.":"\"關於\" memperkenalkan suatu topik dan sering mengawali kalimat untuk menetapkan tema; kata ini juga bisa memodifikasi kata benda dalam bentuk \"關於...的+N\". Cakupannya lebih luas dibandingkan \"（在）...方面\", yang mempersempit ke aspek tertentu.","Teacher Zhang wrote an article about appreciating Van Gogh's works.":"Guru Zhang menulis sebuah artikel tentang mengapresiasi karya-karya Van Gogh.","This is a book about Taiwan's history.":"Ini adalah buku tentang sejarah Taiwan.","judging from / looking at ...":"dilihat dari / berdasarkan ...","以/從 + N + 來看, ...":"以/從 + N + 來看, ...","\"以/從...來看\" means \"judging from/from the perspective of...\", followed by an evaluation or conclusion. \"以\" tends to mark a standard or criterion while \"從\" marks a starting angle, but in practice the two are largely interchangeable.":"\"以/從...來看\" berarti \"dilihat dari/dari sudut pandang...\", diikuti oleh sebuah penilaian atau kesimpulan. \"以\" cenderung menandai suatu standar atau kriteria, sedangkan \"從\" menandai sudut pandang awal, tetapi dalam praktiknya kedua kata ini sebagian besar dapat saling dipertukarkan.","When I got this job, I felt that, judging from the salary, it was quite good.":"Ketika mendapatkan pekerjaan ini, saya merasa, dilihat dari gajinya, itu cukup bagus.","Judging from its stability, this company is worth investing in.":"Dilihat dari stabilitasnya, perusahaan ini layak untuk diinvestasikan.","get along (or not) with":"cocok (atau tidak cocok) dengan","V + 得/不 + 來":"V + 得/不 + 來","\"V得來\" expresses that something/someone is compatible or works out well, while \"V不來\" expresses incompatibility. As a potential complement, it judges compatibility rather than physical ability, unlike complements such as \"V得動\".":"\"V得來\" mengungkapkan bahwa sesuatu/seseorang cocok atau berjalan lancar, sedangkan \"V不來\" mengungkapkan ketidakcocokan. Sebagai pelengkap potensial, ia menilai kecocokan, bukan kemampuan fisik, berbeda dengan pelengkap seperti \"V得動\".","The summer interns are about the same age as us, so everyone gets along really well.":"Para peserta magang musim panas seusia dengan kami, jadi semua orang sangat cocok satu sama lain.","He has a bad temper, so he doesn't get along with anyone.":"Dia bertemperamen buruk, jadi dia tidak cocok dengan siapa pun.","complete/fix an action (result)":"menyelesaikan/menetapkan suatu tindakan (hasil)","Adding \"下\" after a verb shows the result of the action becomes fixed or settled (e.g., ownership, an agreement). Unlike the directional complements \"下來/下去\", a bare \"下\" here marks a settled result rather than physical direction.":"Menambahkan \"下\" setelah kata kerja menunjukkan bahwa hasil dari tindakan tersebut menjadi tetap atau mantap (misalnya, kepemilikan, sebuah kesepakatan). Berbeda dengan pelengkap arah \"下來/下去\", \"下\" saja di sini menandai hasil yang sudah tetap, bukan arah fisik.","He bought this house for a very low price.":"Dia membeli rumah ini dengan harga yang sangat murah.","They signed a three-year contract.":"Mereka menandatangani kontrak tiga tahun.","inevitably, unavoidably":"tak terhindarkan, pasti","(Situation) + 不免 + V":"(Situasi) + 不免 + V","\"不免\" is a somewhat formal/written adverb meaning something naturally, unavoidably happens given the circumstances. It is close in meaning to the more spoken \"難免\" but \"不免\" reads slightly more literary.":"\"不免\" adalah kata keterangan yang agak formal/tertulis, yang berarti sesuatu terjadi secara alami dan tidak dapat dihindari mengingat keadaannya. Maknanya dekat dengan \"難免\" yang lebih lazim digunakan dalam bahasa lisan, tetapi \"不免\" terdengar sedikit lebih sastrawi.","In life, one inevitably encounters many problems and challenges.":"Dalam hidup, seseorang tak terhindarkan menghadapi banyak masalah dan tantangan.","Having just moved to a new environment, one can't help but feel a bit nervous.":"Baru saja pindah ke lingkungan baru, seseorang tak bisa tidak merasa sedikit gugup.","not necessarily":"belum tentu","A + 不見得 + B":"A + 不見得 + B","\"不見得\" means \"not necessarily,\" used to partially deny a common assumption. It's nearly interchangeable with \"不一定,\" but \"不見得\" is a bit more colloquial and often carries a nuance of gently correcting someone's assumption.":"\"不見得\" berarti \"belum tentu\", digunakan untuk menyangkal sebagian suatu asumsi umum. Kata ini hampir dapat dipertukarkan dengan \"不一定\", tetapi \"不見得\" sedikit lebih bersifat percakapan dan sering membawa nuansa mengoreksi asumsi seseorang secara halus.","Students with poor grades won't necessarily be unable to get a chance to succeed.":"Siswa dengan nilai buruk belum tentu tidak akan mendapat kesempatan untuk sukses.","Cheap things aren't necessarily of poor quality.":"Barang murah belum tentu berkualitas buruk.","actually not at all (contrary to expectation)":"sama sekali tidak (bertentangan dengan dugaan)","並 + 不/沒 + VP":"並 + 不/沒 + VP","\"並\" placed before \"不/沒\" strengthens the negation, correcting an assumption by emphasizing \"that's actually not the case.\" It carries a stronger, more argumentative tone than a plain \"不/沒\" and often appears when refuting or clarifying something.":"\"並\" yang diletakkan sebelum \"不/沒\" memperkuat penyangkalan, mengoreksi suatu asumsi dengan menekankan bahwa \"sebenarnya bukan begitu\". Nada bicaranya lebih kuat dan argumentatif dibandingkan dengan \"不/沒\" biasa, dan sering muncul saat membantah atau memperjelas sesuatu.","Although their religions are different, it doesn't affect their cooperative relationship at all.":"Meskipun agama mereka berbeda, hal itu sama sekali tidak memengaruhi hubungan kerja sama mereka.","Although he didn't say anything, he wasn't angry at all inside.":"Meskipun dia tidak mengatakan apa-apa, di dalam hatinya dia sama sekali tidak marah.","never again":"tidak akan pernah lagi","zài yě + bù/méi + V (+ le)":"zài yě + bù/méi + V (+ le)","\"再也不/沒\" emphasizes a strong, often emotional sense of \"never again.\" Use 沒 (+過) for past experience and 不 for future intent or habits. It's stronger in tone than the basic \"不再\" and usually ends with 了.":"“再也不/沒” menekankan makna kuat, sering kali emosional, dari “tidak akan pernah lagi”. Gunakan 沒 (+過) untuk pengalaman masa lalu dan 不 untuk niat di masa depan atau kebiasaan. Ungkapan ini memiliki nada yang lebih kuat dibandingkan “不再” yang dasar, dan biasanya diakhiri dengan 了.","Since I ran into Wang Ming on the bus that day, I've never seen him again.":"Sejak bertemu Wang Ming di bus hari itu, saya tidak pernah bertemu dengannya lagi.","After that argument, they never spoke to each other again.":"Setelah pertengkaran itu, mereka tidak pernah lagi bicara satu sama lain.","there isn't a single one who doesn't...":"tidak ada satu pun yang tidak...","méiyǒu yī + M (+ N) + bù/méi + ... + de":"méiyǒu yī + M (+ N) + bù/méi + ... + de","A double-negative structure meaning \"every single one is...\" The classifier changes with the noun, and the sentence ends with 的. Similar in meaning to 每個人都, but carries stronger emphasis or surprise.":"Ini adalah struktur negasi ganda yang berarti “setiap satu pun...”. Kata penggolong (M) berubah sesuai dengan kata bendanya, dan kalimat diakhiri dengan 的. Maknanya mirip dengan 每個人都, tetapi memiliki penekanan atau kesan terkejut yang lebih kuat.","Not a single customer who has eaten at this restaurant has failed to say it's good.":"Tidak ada satu pun pelanggan yang pernah makan di restoran ini yang tidak bilang enak.","There isn't a single student in this class who doesn't like the teacher.":"Tidak ada satu pun siswa di kelas ini yang tidak menyukai gurunya.","designate/name X as Y":"menetapkan/menamai X sebagai Y","bǎ + N1 + V + wéi + N2":"bǎ + N1 + V + wéi + N2","This \"把\" structure shows that N1 is officially designated, named, or turned into N2. The verb is limited to words like 定, 稱, 列, 訂, 視, and 為 cannot be dropped. It's often confused with 當作 (\"regard as\"), which doesn't imply an official decision.":"Struktur “把” ini menunjukkan bahwa N1 secara resmi ditetapkan, dinamai, atau diubah menjadi N2. Kata kerjanya terbatas pada kata-kata seperti 定, 稱, 列, 訂, 視, dan 為 tidak boleh dihilangkan. Struktur ini sering tertukar dengan 當作 (“menganggap sebagai”), yang tidak menyiratkan sebuah keputusan resmi.","The professor set the topic of the lecture as \"Team Spirit.\"":"Profesor menetapkan topik kuliah tersebut sebagai “Semangat Tim”.","We named this road \"Happiness Road.\"":"Kami menamai jalan ini “Jalan Kebahagiaan”.","honestly / to be honest":"sejujurnya / terus terang","Lǎoshí shuō, + sentence":"Lǎoshí shuō, + sentence","Placed at the start of a sentence to preface an honest opinion. Nearly interchangeable with 說實話. It's usually followed by the speaker's frank opinion, sometimes something slightly awkward to say.":"Diletakkan di awal kalimat untuk mengawali sebuah pendapat yang jujur. Hampir dapat dipertukarkan dengan 說實話. Biasanya diikuti oleh pendapat terus terang dari pembicara, kadang berupa hal yang agak canggung untuk diucapkan.","Honestly, this joke isn't funny.":"Sejujurnya, lelucon ini tidak lucu.","Honestly, I don't think this movie is very good.":"Sejujurnya, saya rasa film ini tidak terlalu bagus.","it is said that / reportedly":"konon / dikabarkan","jùshuō + sentence":"jùshuō + sentence","Used at the start of a sentence to convey hearsay or secondhand information the speaker hasn't personally verified. Nearly synonymous with 聽說, but 據說 leans slightly more formal/written.":"Digunakan di awal kalimat untuk menyampaikan informasi yang didengar atau informasi dari pihak kedua yang belum diverifikasi sendiri oleh pembicara. Hampir sama artinya dengan 聽說, tetapi 據說 sedikit lebih formal/bersifat tulisan.","It's said that this place originally had no lake, and it only appeared after a major earthquake.":"Konon tempat ini awalnya tidak memiliki danau, dan danau itu baru muncul setelah gempa bumi besar.","It's said that this shop's beef noodle soup is the best in all of Taipei.":"Konon mi kuah daging sapi di toko ini adalah yang terenak di seluruh Taipei.","I think / In my opinion":"menurut saya / pendapat saya","Wǒ kàn + judgment/suggestion":"Wǒ kàn + judgment/suggestion","'Wǒ kàn' softly gives the speaker's judgment/suggestion, close to 'I think/guess'; often paired with 還是 to soften advice, more tentative than flat 我覺得.":"“Wǒ kàn” menyampaikan penilaian/saran pembicara secara halus, mendekati arti “saya rasa/saya kira”; sering dipasangkan dengan 還是 untuk memperhalus saran, terkesan lebih ragu-ragu dibandingkan 我覺得 yang polos.","I think we'd better leave early, or we'll be late.":"Menurut saya sebaiknya kita berangkat lebih awal, kalau tidak kita akan terlambat.","I think you'd better call and ask clearly.":"Menurut saya sebaiknya kamu menelepon dan menanyakan dengan jelas.","Look / You see":"Lihat / Begini","Nǐ kàn + sentence":"Nǐ kàn + kalimat","'Nǐ kàn' draws the listener's attention to something or invites their opinion, like 'look' or 'see?'; placed at the start of a casual sentence.":"'Nǐ kàn' digunakan untuk menarik perhatian pendengar pada sesuatu atau meminta pendapat mereka, seperti 'lihat' atau 'coba lihat?'; diletakkan di awal kalimat santai.","Look, what's really going on with this?":"Coba lihat, sebenarnya ada apa dengan ini?","Look, it's raining outside — we need to bring an umbrella.":"Coba lihat, di luar sedang hujan — kita perlu membawa payung.","So you're saying... / In that case...":"Jadi maksudmu... / Kalau begitu...","Zhème shuō, + conclusion":"Zhème shuō, + kesimpulan","'Zhème shuō' introduces a conclusion drawn from what was just said, like 'so you're saying...'; it signals the speaker's own inference from the prior statement.":"'Zhème shuō' digunakan untuk memperkenalkan kesimpulan yang ditarik dari apa yang baru saja dikatakan, seperti 'jadi maksudmu...'; ini menandakan kesimpulan pribadi pembicara dari pernyataan sebelumnya.","So you're saying I have to go see him before three o'clock.":"Jadi maksudmu aku harus pergi menemuinya sebelum jam tiga.","So you're saying you didn't go to work at all yesterday?":"Jadi maksudmu kemarin kamu sama sekali tidak pergi bekerja?","On the contrary / Conversely":"Sebaliknya","Clause A; xiāngfǎn de, Clause B (contrast)":"Klausa A; xiāngfǎn de, Klausa B (kontras)","'Xiāngfǎn de' is a written connector introducing the opposite of what was just stated, like 'on the contrary'; more formal and logically contrastive than casual 但是.":"'Xiāngfǎn de' adalah kata penghubung dalam bahasa tulis yang memperkenalkan kebalikan dari apa yang baru saja dinyatakan, seperti 'sebaliknya'; lebih formal dan bersifat kontras logis dibandingkan 但是 yang lebih santai.","I don't think parents should tell children the answer directly; on the contrary, they should let them have more chances to try.":"Saya rasa orang tua tidak seharusnya langsung memberi tahu jawabannya kepada anak; sebaliknya, mereka harus memberi anak lebih banyak kesempatan untuk mencoba.","This movie got great reviews; on the contrary, the sequel disappointed people.":"Film ini mendapat ulasan yang sangat bagus; sebaliknya, sekuelnya mengecewakan banyak orang.","Besides / Moreover":"Selain itu / Lagipula","Reason A, zàishuō + Reason B":"Alasan A, zàishuō + Alasan B","'Zàishuō' adds another supporting reason on top of one already given, close to 'besides/moreover'; more casual than 而且 and often frames the added reason as secondary.":"'Zàishuō' digunakan untuk menambahkan alasan pendukung lain selain yang sudah disebutkan, mendekati makna 'selain itu/lagipula'; lebih santai daripada 而且 dan sering menempatkan alasan tambahan itu sebagai alasan sekunder.","He's not interested in watching movies, besides, business is so busy that he has no time either.":"Dia tidak tertarik menonton film, lagipula, urusan bisnisnya begitu sibuk sehingga dia juga tidak punya waktu.","This piece of clothing is too expensive, besides, I don't like the color either.":"Baju ini terlalu mahal, lagipula, saya juga tidak suka warnanya.","that is to say":"dengan kata lain","A, 也/那/這就是說, B":"A, 也/那/這就是說, B","Used to rephrase or summarize what was just said: \"A, that is to say, B.\" 也/那/這 are largely interchangeable here; 也就是說 is the most common colloquial form.":"Digunakan untuk menyatakan ulang atau merangkum apa yang baru saja dikatakan: \"A, dengan kata lain, B.\" 也/那/這 di sini sebagian besar dapat saling menggantikan; 也就是說 adalah bentuk lisan yang paling umum digunakan.","The weather forecast says there'll be a typhoon this weekend. In other words, we can't go to the beach.":"Ramalan cuaca mengatakan akan ada topan akhir pekan ini. Dengan kata lain, kita tidak bisa pergi ke pantai.","He's late every time — in other words, he doesn't care about this appointment at all.":"Dia selalu terlambat setiap kali — dengan kata lain, dia sama sekali tidak peduli dengan janji ini.","how should I put it":"bagaimana ya mengatakannya","exactly!/isn't that so!":"benar sekali!/bukankah begitu!","可不是！":"Benar sekali! / Bukankah begitu!","An agreement interjection meaning \"Isn't that so!/Exactly!\" — despite containing 不, it expresses strong agreement, not negation. Often stands alone or is followed by a short elaboration.":"Sebuah seruan persetujuan yang berarti \"Bukankah begitu!/Benar sekali!\" — meskipun mengandung karakter 不, ungkapan ini menyatakan persetujuan yang kuat, bukan penyangkalan. Sering berdiri sendiri atau diikuti oleh penjelasan singkat.","Isn't that so! / Exactly!":"Bukankah begitu! / Benar sekali!","\"It's really hot today!\" \"Isn't that so! It's already over 35 degrees.\"":"\"Hari ini benar-benar panas!\" \"Benar sekali! Sudah lebih dari 35 derajat.\"","怎麼說呢, ...":"怎麼說呢, ...","A hesitation filler used when it's hard to answer right away or one is choosing words carefully — \"how should I put it...\" Common when the speaker wants to soften or avoid a blunt answer.":"Kata pengisi jeda yang digunakan ketika sulit menjawab segera atau sedang memilih kata dengan hati-hati — \"bagaimana ya bilangnya...\". Biasa digunakan ketika penutur ingin memperhalus jawaban atau menghindari jawaban yang terlalu blak-blakan.","How should I put it... I just feel we don't get along.":"Bagaimana ya bilangnya... aku hanya merasa kami tidak cocok.","Was the movie good? How should I put it... the plot was so-so, but the actors did a good job.":"Filmnya bagus tidak? Bagaimana ya bilangnya... alur ceritanya biasa saja, tapi para aktornya berakting dengan baik.","this way/as a result":"dengan begitu/akibatnya","A, 這樣一來, B":"A, 這樣一來, B","Introduces the result or consequence of what was just said: \"this way / as a result.\" Often used when a prior action leads to a positive outcome.":"Memperkenalkan hasil atau akibat dari apa yang baru saja dikatakan: \"dengan begitu / akibatnya\". Sering digunakan ketika suatu tindakan sebelumnya membawa hasil yang positif.","I already bought the tickets. This way, we can go buy souvenirs later with peace of mind.":"Aku sudah membeli tiketnya. Dengan begitu, nanti kita bisa membeli oleh-oleh dengan tenang.","The boss decided to raise salaries. As a result, employees' motivation to work increased quite a bit.":"Bos memutuskan untuk menaikkan gaji. Akibatnya, motivasi kerja karyawan meningkat cukup banyak.","forget it/never mind":"sudahlah/tidak apa-apa","算了, ... (giving up/compromise)":"算了, ... (menyerah/berkompromi)","Expresses giving up or dropping a matter — \"forget it, let's not bother.\" Often implies mild resignation or compromise, unlike 可不是 which expresses agreement.":"Mengungkapkan sikap menyerah atau melepaskan suatu masalah — \"sudahlah, tidak usah repot-repot\". Sering menyiratkan kepasrahan ringan atau kompromi, berbeda dengan 可不是 yang mengungkapkan persetujuan.","Never mind, it's so late — you go home first, I'll take care of the rest.":"Sudahlah, sudah larut malam — kamu pulang duluan saja, sisanya biar aku yang urus.","I called several times and no one answered. Forget it, let's deal with it tomorrow.":"Aku sudah menelepon beberapa kali dan tidak ada yang menjawab. Sudahlah, kita urus besok saja.","by means of / using":"dengan cara/menggunakan","A + yǐ + means + V":"A + yǐ + cara/sarana + V","\"以\" is a formal written equivalent of \"用\", introducing a means or method. In speech, \"用\" is far more common; \"以\" appears mainly in official or written contexts.":"\"以\" adalah padanan formal dalam tulisan untuk \"用\", yang memperkenalkan sarana atau metode. Dalam percakapan, \"用\" jauh lebih umum digunakan; \"以\" terutama muncul dalam konteks resmi atau tulisan.","Regarding what was discussed today, if you have any suggestions, please feel free to submit them by email.":"Mengenai apa yang dibahas hari ini, jika Anda memiliki saran, silakan kirimkan melalui email.","If you have any issues, please contact customer service by phone.":"Jika Anda memiliki masalah, silakan hubungi layanan pelanggan melalui telepon.","in order to":"agar/supaya","VP1, yǐ + VP2 (purpose)":"VP1, yǐ + VP2 (tujuan)","Here \"以\" introduces a purpose clause, close in meaning to \"以便\" (\"in order to\"). Don't confuse it with \"以1\", which marks means/instrument instead of purpose.":"Di sini \"以\" memperkenalkan klausa tujuan, maknanya dekat dengan \"以便\" (\"agar/supaya\"). Jangan disamakan dengan \"以1\", yang menandai sarana/alat, bukan tujuan.","Students should strengthen their own abilities in order to increase their chances of entering their ideal industry.":"Mahasiswa sebaiknya memperkuat kemampuan diri agar dapat meningkatkan peluang untuk masuk ke bidang industri yang diidamkan.","He practices Chinese hard every day in order to improve his own speaking ability.":"Dia berlatih bahasa Mandarin dengan giat setiap hari agar dapat meningkatkan kemampuan berbicaranya.","at [time] (formal)":"pada [waktu] (formal)","S + (already/will) + yú + time + VP":"S + (sudah/akan) + yú + waktu + VP","\"於\" functions like \"在\" for time in formal writing, often appearing as \"已於\" or \"將於\" in news and official documents. In everyday speech, \"在\" is used instead.":"\"於\" berfungsi seperti \"在\" untuk menunjukkan waktu dalam tulisan formal, sering muncul sebagai \"已於\" atau \"將於\" dalam berita dan dokumen resmi. Dalam percakapan sehari-hari, \"在\" digunakan sebagai gantinya.","The general manager already departed for Vietnam at 2 p.m. to visit clients.":"Direktur utama sudah berangkat ke Vietnam pukul 2 siang untuk mengunjungi klien.","The meeting will start at 9 a.m. tomorrow.":"Rapat akan dimulai pukul 9 pagi besok.","at [place] (formal)":"di [tempat] (formal)","S + will + yú + place + VP":"S + akan + yú + tempat + VP","Here \"於\" is the formal written equivalent of \"在\" for location, commonly used to announce where an event will take place. Compare with \"於1\", which marks time rather than place.":"Di sini, \"於\" adalah padanan formal dalam bahasa tulis untuk \"在\" yang menunjukkan lokasi, biasa digunakan untuk mengumumkan tempat berlangsungnya suatu acara. Bandingkan dengan \"於1\", yang menandai waktu, bukan tempat.","This event will be held at the International Convention Center.":"Acara ini akan diadakan di Pusat Konvensi Internasional.","The graduation ceremony will be held in the auditorium.":"Upacara wisuda akan diadakan di aula.","by (agent of the action)":"oleh (pelaku tindakan)","A + yóu + B + V":"A + yóu + B + V","\"由\" introduces who performs or is responsible for an action (\"A由B+V\" = \"B does A\"). Don't confuse this with \"由1\", which marks a starting point (\"from\") rather than an agent.":"\"由\" memperkenalkan siapa yang melakukan atau bertanggung jawab atas suatu tindakan (\"A由B+V\" = \"B melakukan A\"). Jangan disamakan dengan \"由1\", yang menandai titik awal (\"dari\"), bukan pelaku.","The prize drawing will have its winners selected by computer.":"Pemenang undian akan dipilih oleh komputer.","This performance was planned by the students themselves.":"Pertunjukan ini direncanakan oleh para siswa sendiri.","emphasizing a reason in a rhetorical question":"menekankan alasan dalam pertanyaan retoris","A + yòu + méi/bù + VP, ...? (rhetorical)":"A + yòu + méi/bù + VP, ...? (retoris)","Here 又 reinforces a negated reason in a rhetorical question, meaning 'you didn't even...', not the usual 'again' sense of 又. Don't confuse with 又...又... (both...and).":"Di sini 又 memperkuat alasan yang dinegasikan dalam pertanyaan retoris, berarti 'bahkan tidak...', bukan makna 'lagi' yang biasa pada 又. Jangan disamakan dengan 又...又... (baik...maupun...).","You didn't even do anything wrong—what is there to be afraid of?":"Kamu bahkan tidak melakukan kesalahan apa pun—apa yang perlu ditakuti?","He's not even unaware of it—why pretend not to know?":"Dia bahkan bukannya tidak tahu—kenapa berpura-pura tidak tahu?","highlighting a specific example (in particular)":"menyoroti contoh tertentu (khususnya)","Búshì měi ge N dōu VP, A jiù VP.":"Búshì měi ge N dōu VP, A jiù VP.","就 here singles out a specific instance that contrasts with a preceding general negative statement ('not every X...'), meaning 'X in particular does...'. Distinct from 就 meaning 'then/right away'.":"就 di sini menunjuk pada satu contoh tertentu yang bertentangan dengan pernyataan negatif umum sebelumnya ('tidak setiap X...'), berarti 'X tertentu justru...'. Berbeda dengan 就 yang berarti 'lalu/segera'.","Not every foreigner refuses to eat stinky tofu—my Japanese friend, for one, loves eating it.":"Tidak setiap orang asing menolak makan tahu busuk—teman saya yang orang Jepang, misalnya, justru sangat suka memakannya.","Not every kid is afraid of shots—my little brother, in particular, isn't scared at all.":"Tidak setiap anak takut disuntik—adik laki-laki saya, khususnya, sama sekali tidak takut.","Tòuguò + N, ...":"Tòuguò + N, ...","透過 introduces the means or medium through which something is achieved; it's more formal/written. Don't confuse with 經過 (to pass through a place/process) or 通過 (to pass/get approval).":"透過 memperkenalkan sarana atau media untuk mencapai sesuatu; sifatnya lebih formal/tertulis. Jangan disamakan dengan 經過 (melewati suatu tempat/proses) atau 通過 (lolos/disetujui).","Through this book, we learn about his process of continuous learning and growth.":"Melalui buku ini, kita belajar tentang proses pembelajaran dan pertumbuhannya yang berkelanjutan.","Through the internet, we can chat with people all over the world.":"Melalui internet, kita bisa mengobrol dengan orang-orang di seluruh dunia.","along / following (a direction, flow)":"sepanjang / mengikuti (suatu arah, aliran)","Shùn(zhe) + N + VP":"Shùn(zhe) + N + VP","順(著) means to move along or follow a direction/flow (sound, trend, road). It overlaps with 沿著 but emphasizes following a flow or cue, not just a physical line.":"順(著) berarti bergerak mengikuti atau menuruti suatu arah/aliran (suara, tren, jalan). Maknanya tumpang tindih dengan 沿著, tetapi lebih menekankan mengikuti aliran atau petunjuk, bukan sekadar garis fisik.","Follow the sound of the music, and you'll see a group of people exercising.":"Ikuti saja suara musiknya, kamu akan melihat sekelompok orang sedang berolahraga.","Follow this road straight ahead, and you'll reach the train station.":"Ikuti jalan ini terus ke depan, kamu akan sampai di stasiun kereta.","along (a physical place or line)":"sepanjang (suatu tempat atau garis fisik)","Yán(zhe) + N + VP":"Yán(zhe) + N + VP","沿(著) describes moving along a physical, linear place (a river, road, coast) — a geographic sense. Contrast with 順(著), which more often follows an abstract flow or cue.":"沿(著) menggambarkan pergerakan di sepanjang suatu tempat fisik yang memanjang (sungai, jalan, pantai) — bermakna geografis. Berbeda dengan 順(著), yang lebih sering mengikuti suatu alur atau isyarat abstrak.","In the evening, I often take a walk along the river.":"Pada malam hari, saya sering berjalan-jalan di sepanjang sungai.","We rode our bikes along the coast—the scenery was beautiful.":"Kami bersepeda di sepanjang pantai—pemandangannya indah.","take A as B":"menjadikan A sebagai B","A + 以 + X + 為 + Y":"A + 以 + X + 為 + Y","\"Yǐ A wéi B\" means \"take A as B,\" common in formal/written Chinese to state a goal, standard, or means. Note 為 here is read wéi (to serve as), not wèi (for the sake of) — a common tone mistake.":"\"Yǐ A wéi B\" berarti \"menjadikan A sebagai B\", umum digunakan dalam bahasa Tionghoa formal/tulisan untuk menyatakan tujuan, standar, atau cara. Perhatikan bahwa 為 di sini dibaca wéi (menjadi/berperan sebagai), bukan wèi (demi) — kesalahan nada yang sering terjadi.","His goal is to obtain a lawyer's qualification.":"Tujuannya adalah untuk memperoleh kualifikasi sebagai pengacara.","Her goal is to become a doctor.":"Tujuannya adalah untuk menjadi dokter.","by means of / relying on":"dengan cara / mengandalkan","Subject + 憑 + ability/effort/document + verb phrase":"Subjek + 憑 + kemampuan/usaha/dokumen + frasa kata kerja","\"Píng\" means \"by means of / relying on,\" introducing the basis (ability, effort, evidence, or a document) for an action. It's slightly more formal than \"靠,\" though both mean \"to rely on.\"":"\"Píng\" berarti \"dengan cara / mengandalkan\", digunakan untuk memperkenalkan dasar (kemampuan, usaha, bukti, atau dokumen) bagi suatu tindakan. Kata ini sedikit lebih formal daripada \"靠\", meskipun keduanya berarti \"mengandalkan\".","He got into the best design college in the country through his own effort.":"Dia berhasil masuk ke sekolah desain terbaik di negeri ini berkat usahanya sendiri.","She got this job on her own merit.":"Dia mendapatkan pekerjaan ini berkat kemampuannya sendiri.","depends on":"tergantung pada","(Subject) + 視 + condition/factor + 而定":"(Subjek) + 視 + kondisi/faktor + 而定","\"Shì A ér dìng\" means \"it depends on A\" — a set written-style phrase that closes the sentence on its own, with no extra clause needed after 定.":"\"Shì A ér dìng\" berarti \"tergantung pada A\" — sebuah frasa tetap bergaya tulisan yang mengakhiri kalimat dengan sendirinya, tanpa perlu klausa tambahan setelah 定.","The price of a house mainly depends on its location and size.":"Harga sebuah rumah terutama tergantung pada lokasi dan ukurannya.","Whether we can go out and play depends on the weather.":"Bisa tidaknya kita keluar bermain tergantung pada cuaca.","come about via / derived through":"terjadi melalui / diperoleh melalui","A + 是 + 經由 + B + 而來 + 的":"A + 是 + 經由 + B + 而來 + 的","\"Jīngyóu A ér lái (de)\" explains that something came about via process A — a formal way to describe the origin behind a result, stronger than plain \"經過\" (to pass through).":"\"Jīngyóu A ér lái (de)\" menjelaskan bahwa sesuatu terjadi melalui proses A — cara formal untuk menggambarkan asal-usul di balik suatu hasil, lebih kuat daripada \"經過\" (melalui/melewati) yang biasa.","These data were derived through statistics.":"Data ini diperoleh melalui statistik.","This conclusion was reached through many experiments.":"Kesimpulan ini dicapai melalui banyak eksperimen.","A is about equal to / comparable with B":"A kurang lebih setara / dapat dibandingkan dengan B","A + 跟 + B + (在...方面) + 相當":"A + 跟 + B + (在...方面) + 相當","\"A gēn B xiāngdāng\" means \"A is roughly equal to / comparable with B\" — vaguer than \"一樣\" (exactly the same), used to compare degree, quantity, or ability.":"\"A gēn B xiāngdāng\" berarti \"A kurang lebih setara / dapat dibandingkan dengan B\" — lebih samar daripada \"一樣\" (persis sama), digunakan untuk membandingkan tingkat, jumlah, atau kemampuan.","The boy sitting in front looks to be about the same age as me.":"Anak laki-laki yang duduk di depan tampak seusia denganku.","My younger brother's height is about the same as mine.":"Tinggi badan adik laki-lakiku kira-kira sama dengan punyaku.","not as good as; can't compare to":"tidak sebaik; tidak dapat dibandingkan dengan","A + 比不上 + B":"A + 比不上 + B","The negative form of 比得上, meaning A cannot match B. Word order is fixed as A+比不上+B — don't reverse it. Close in meaning to 不如, but more colloquial.":"Bentuk negatif dari 比得上, yang berarti A tidak dapat menandingi B. Urutan katanya tetap A+比不上+B — jangan dibalik. Maknanya mirip dengan 不如, tetapi lebih bersifat percakapan sehari-hari.","Although the toy you bought is exquisite, it doesn't compare to the value of something made by hand.":"Meskipun mainan yang kamu beli itu indah, nilainya tetap tidak bisa menandingi barang buatan tangan.","This restaurant's flavor doesn't compare to what my grandma cooks.":"Rasa masakan restoran ini tidak bisa menandingi masakan buatan nenek saya.","compared with B":"dibandingkan dengan B","(A) + 與 + B + 相比":"(A) + 與 + B + 相比","\"與 + comparison target + 相比\" means \"compared with...\". Subject A is often omitted since it's already stated; the result/change follows afterward. More formal/written than the colloquial 跟...比起來.":"\"與 + objek perbandingan + 相比\" berarti \"dibandingkan dengan...\". Subjek A sering dihilangkan karena sudah disebutkan sebelumnya; hasil/perubahan disebutkan setelahnya. Lebih formal/tertulis dibandingkan bentuk percakapan 跟...比起來.","Compared to five years ago, this city has become much more prosperous now.":"Dibandingkan dengan lima tahun yang lalu, kota ini sekarang menjadi jauh lebih makmur.","Compared to the previous one, this article has improved a lot.":"Dibandingkan dengan yang sebelumnya, artikel ini sudah banyak meningkat.","so; thereupon (introduces a resulting action)":"maka; lalu (mengantarkan tindakan yang menjadi akibat)","cause/situation + 於是 + resulting action":"sebab/situasi + 於是 + tindakan akibat","A connector introducing the resulting action that followed from the preceding situation. Similar to 所以, but 於是 leans toward a sequential action that happened next, while 所以 fits a plain logical conclusion better.":"Kata penghubung yang mengantarkan tindakan akibat yang terjadi setelah situasi yang disebutkan sebelumnya. Mirip dengan 所以, tetapi 於是 lebih condong pada tindakan berurutan yang terjadi selanjutnya, sedangkan 所以 lebih cocok untuk kesimpulan logis biasa.","Smoking is harmful to health, so Dad decided to quit smoking.":"Merokok berbahaya bagi kesehatan, maka Ayah memutuskan untuk berhenti merokok.","He realized his phone was missing, so he hurried back to look for it.":"Dia menyadari ponselnya hilang, lalu buru-buru kembali untuk mencarinya.","the reason...is because...":"alasan...adalah karena...","(subject) + (之)所以 + result, 是因為 + reason":"(subjek) + (之)所以 + hasil, 是因為 + alasan","States the result first with 之所以, then emphasizes the reason afterward with 是因為 — the reverse order of 因為...所以... (reason→result). 之 is optional and can be dropped.":"Menyatakan hasil terlebih dahulu dengan 之所以, kemudian menekankan alasan setelahnya dengan 是因為 — kebalikan dari urutan 因為...所以... (alasan→hasil). 之 bersifat opsional dan dapat dihilangkan.","The reason he succeeded is because of his persistence and effort.":"Alasan dia berhasil adalah karena ketekunan dan usahanya.","The reason she was late is because there was a traffic jam.":"Alasan dia terlambat adalah karena terjebak macet.","along with; as...changes":"seiring dengan; sejalan dengan perubahan...","隨著 + noun/clause, subject + action":"隨著 + kata benda/klausa, subjek + tindakan","Expresses that the result in the second clause occurs alongside a preceding change or trend. Words like 開始/逐漸 (indicating gradual change) often co-occur. Unlike 因為 (simple causation), it marks a parallel, ongoing relationship of change.":"Menyatakan bahwa hasil pada klausa kedua terjadi bersamaan dengan perubahan atau tren yang telah disebutkan sebelumnya. Kata-kata seperti 開始/逐漸 (menunjukkan perubahan bertahap) sering muncul bersamaan. Berbeda dengan 因為 (hubungan sebab-akibat sederhana), ini menandai hubungan perubahan yang paralel dan sedang berlangsung.","With the changes of the times, many values have begun to be challenged.":"Seiring dengan perubahan zaman, banyak nilai mulai dipertanyakan.","With the opening of the MRT, this area has become more and more lively.":"Seiring dibukanya jalur MRT, kawasan ini menjadi semakin ramai.","because of A, B (formal, one-clause cause-result)":"karena A, maka B (formal, sebab-akibat dalam satu klausa)","因（為）+ A (cause) + 而 + B (action)":"因（為）+ A (sebab) + 而 + B (tindakan)","\"因(為)...而...\" links a cause (A) directly to a resulting action (B) within one clause, more formal/written than \"因為...所以...\", which joins two full clauses. The part after 而 must be a verb phrase, not a full sentence.":"\"因(為)...而...\" menghubungkan langsung suatu sebab (A) dengan tindakan akibat (B) dalam satu klausa, lebih formal/tertulis dibandingkan \"因為...所以...\", yang menggabungkan dua klausa lengkap. Bagian setelah 而 harus berupa frasa verba, bukan kalimat lengkap.","The government changed this policy because of the people's protests.":"Pemerintah mengubah kebijakan ini karena protes dari rakyat.","He gave up this job because his health wasn't good.":"Dia meninggalkan pekerjaan ini karena kesehatannya tidak baik.","as a result, thus (formal result connector)":"akibatnya, oleh karena itu (kata penghubung hasil yang formal)","[Cause clause], 因而 + [Result clause]":"[Klausa sebab], 因而 + [Klausa hasil]","\"因而\" is a formal written connector meaning \"as a result,\" placed after the cause clause. More literary than \"所以.\" Unlike \"因為...而...,\" it links two separate clauses, not a single clause.":"\"因而\" adalah kata penghubung formal dalam bahasa tulis yang berarti \"akibatnya,\" diletakkan setelah klausa penyebab. Lebih sastrawi daripada \"所以.\" Berbeda dengan \"因為...而...,\" kata ini menghubungkan dua klausa terpisah, bukan satu klausa tunggal.","Affected by the typhoon, flights were consequently grounded.":"Terkena dampak topan, penerbangan akibatnya dilarang terbang.","This road is often congested, so many people choose to commute by MRT.":"Jalan ini sering macet, sehingga banyak orang memilih naik MRT untuk bepergian ke tempat kerja.","in order to A, B (purpose connector)":"untuk A, B (kata penghubung tujuan)","為了 + A (purpose) + 而 + B (action)":"為了 + A (tujuan) + 而 + B (tindakan)","\"為了A而B\" expresses doing B for the purpose of achieving A. It looks similar to \"因為A而B\" but differs in meaning: 為了 marks purpose/goal, while 因為 marks cause/reason.":"\"為了A而B\" mengungkapkan melakukan B demi mencapai tujuan A. Bentuknya mirip dengan \"因為A而B\" tetapi berbeda maknanya: 為了 menandai tujuan/sasaran, sedangkan 因為 menandai sebab/alasan.","He followed the doctor's advice and started controlling his diet for the sake of his health.":"Dia mengikuti saran dokter dan mulai mengontrol pola makannya demi kesehatannya.","She studies until late at night every day in order to get into her dream university.":"Setiap hari dia belajar hingga larut malam agar bisa masuk ke universitas impiannya.","need not, there's no need to (formal)":"tidak perlu, tidak usah (formal)","無須 + Verb (phrase)":"無須 + Kata kerja (frasa)","\"無須\" is a formal, written equivalent of \"不必/不需要,\" meaning \"there's no need to.\" It must be followed by a verb (phrase), not directly by a noun.":"\"無須\" adalah bentuk formal dalam bahasa tulis yang setara dengan \"不必/不需要,\" berarti \"tidak perlu.\" Kata ini harus diikuti oleh kata kerja (frasa), bukan langsung oleh kata benda.","After the government built a new road, residents no longer need to take a detour.":"Setelah pemerintah membangun jalan baru, warga tidak perlu lagi memutar jalan.","Nowadays online shopping is so convenient that you can buy daily necessities without even leaving home.":"Saat ini belanja daring sangat praktis sehingga Anda bisa membeli kebutuhan sehari-hari tanpa perlu keluar rumah.","not to the extent of, won't go so far as to":"tidak sampai pada tingkat, tidak akan sampai","(雖然...) 但 + 不至於 + Verb (phrase)":"(雖然...) 但 + 不至於 + Kata kerja (frasa)","\"不至於\" means the situation won't reach a serious extreme, emphasizing degree more than a simple negation like \"不會.\" It's often paired with \"雖然...但...\".":"\"不至於\" berarti keadaan tidak akan mencapai tingkat yang sangat parah, lebih menekankan pada tingkat/derajat dibandingkan sekadar negasi sederhana seperti \"不會.\" Kata ini sering dipasangkan dengan \"雖然...但...\".","Taipei's winter is damp and cold, but not to the point of snowing.":"Musim dingin di Taipei lembap dan dingin, tetapi tidak sampai turun salju.","He's angry, but he probably won't go so far as to resign.":"Dia sedang marah, tetapi kemungkinan tidak akan sampai mengundurkan diri.","never, absolutely not":"tidak pernah, sama sekali tidak","Subject + 絕不 + Verb":"Subjek + 絕不 + Kata kerja","\"絕不\" is a strong negative adverb expressing firm resolve or certainty — stronger than plain \"不.\" Unlike \"從不\" (never, as a habit), \"絕不\" expresses will and determination, not routine.":"\"絕不\" adalah kata keterangan negasi yang kuat, mengungkapkan tekad atau kepastian yang teguh — lebih kuat daripada \"不\" biasa. Berbeda dengan \"從不\" (tidak pernah, bersifat kebiasaan), \"絕不\" mengungkapkan kemauan dan tekad, bukan rutinitas.","He is cautious by nature and will never say things without basis.":"Dia memang berhati-hati dan tidak akan pernah mengatakan sesuatu tanpa dasar.","I will never tell anyone your secret.":"Saya tidak akan pernah memberitahu rahasiamu kepada siapa pun.","have never (yet); literary":"belum pernah; bahasa sastra/tulis","Subject + 未曾 + Verb (+ 過)":"Subjek + 未曾 + Kata kerja (+ 過)","\"未曾\" is a literary way of saying \"have never (done something) before,\" equivalent to spoken \"從來沒有…過.\" It's more formal than casual speech and is often followed by \"過.\"":"\"未曾\" adalah cara ungkap dalam bahasa tulis untuk \"belum pernah (melakukan sesuatu) sebelumnya,\" setara dengan \"從來沒有…過\" dalam bahasa lisan. Kata ini lebih formal daripada bahasa percakapan biasa dan sering diikuti oleh \"過.\"","This article has never been published before.":"Artikel ini belum pernah dipublikasikan sebelumnya.","He has never been abroad before.":"Dia belum pernah pergi ke luar negeri sebelumnya.","must not, not allowed to (rules/law)":"tidak boleh, dilarang (peraturan/hukum)","Subject + 不得 + Verb":"Subjek + 不得 + Kata kerja","\"不得\" is a formal, written way to express prohibition (\"must not\"), used in rules, laws, and contracts. It is more formal than spoken \"不可以.\"":"\"不得\" adalah cara formal dan tertulis untuk menyatakan larangan (\"tidak boleh\"), digunakan dalam peraturan, undang-undang, dan kontrak. Ungkapan ini lebih formal daripada \"不可以\" dalam bahasa lisan.","This company's rules state that employees' daily working hours must not exceed eight hours.":"Peraturan perusahaan ini menyatakan bahwa jam kerja harian karyawan tidak boleh melebihi delapan jam.","The library rule states that borrowed books must not exceed ten.":"Peraturan perpustakaan menyatakan bahwa buku yang dipinjam tidak boleh melebihi sepuluh buku.","unable to, have no way to":"tidak dapat, tidak ada cara untuk","Subject + 無法 + Verb":"Subjek + 無法 + Verba","\"無法\" expresses that there is objectively no way to do something, due to circumstances or lack of ability. It is slightly more formal than \"不能\" and often emphasizes an external cause or constraint.":"\"無法\" menyatakan bahwa secara objektif tidak ada cara untuk melakukan sesuatu, karena keadaan atau kurangnya kemampuan. Kata ini sedikit lebih formal daripada \"不能\" dan sering menekankan sebab atau kendala eksternal.","Wang Meimei loves cleanliness and cannot stand even a little mess.":"Wang Meimei sangat menyukai kebersihan dan tidak tahan bahkan dengan sedikit kekacauan.","Because of the heavy rain, the plane was unable to take off on time.":"Karena hujan lebat, pesawat tidak dapat lepas landas tepat waktu.","and, as well as (connecting nouns, formal)":"dan, serta (menghubungkan kata benda, formal)","A, B, as well as C":"A, B, serta C","\"以及\" is a formal written conjunction that connects nouns, typically placed before the last item in a list. It is more literary than \"和\" or \"跟\" and suits formal writing or enumerations.":"\"以及\" adalah kata sambung formal dalam bahasa tulis yang menghubungkan kata benda, biasanya diletakkan sebelum item terakhir dalam sebuah daftar. Kata ini lebih sastrawi daripada \"和\" atau \"跟\" dan cocok untuk tulisan formal atau penyebutan berurutan.","I told everyone about the people I met during the trip, the interesting things that happened, as well as the beautiful scenery I saw.":"Saya menceritakan kepada semua orang tentang orang-orang yang saya temui selama perjalanan, hal-hal menarik yang terjadi, serta pemandangan indah yang saya lihat.","This meeting invited teachers, parents, as well as student representatives to attend together.":"Pertemuan ini mengundang guru, orang tua, serta perwakilan siswa untuk hadir bersama.","listing two reasons (for one thing... for another)":"menyebutkan dua alasan (pertama... kedua...)","yìlái + reason 1, èrlái + reason 2":"yìlái + alasan 1, èrlái + alasan 2","A somewhat formal way to list two parallel reasons or causes. In casual speech, 一方面...一方面... is more common than 一來...二來.":"Ini adalah cara yang agak formal untuk menyebutkan dua alasan atau sebab yang sejajar. Dalam bahasa lisan sehari-hari, 一方面...一方面... lebih umum digunakan daripada 一來...二來.","This place has no phone for one thing, and no internet for another, so it's very inconvenient to get in touch.":"Tempat ini pertama tidak ada telepon, kedua tidak ada internet, jadi sangat tidak nyaman untuk menghubungi.","Learning Chinese lets you make friends for one thing, and understand Taiwanese culture for another.":"Belajar bahasa Mandarin pertama membuat Anda bisa berteman, kedua membuat Anda memahami budaya Taiwan.","both A and B are true":"baik A maupun B keduanya benar","jì + A, yě + B":"jì + A, yě + B","Shows that A and B are both true at the same time; somewhat formal. Similar to 不但...而且..., but 既...也... treats A and B as equal, without implying B is stronger than A.":"Menunjukkan bahwa A dan B sama-sama benar pada saat yang sama; agak formal. Mirip dengan 不但...而且..., tetapi 既...也... memperlakukan A dan B secara setara, tanpa menyiratkan bahwa B lebih kuat daripada A.","Coming to Taiwan lets you both learn Chinese and enjoy great food.":"Datang ke Taiwan membuat Anda bisa belajar bahasa Mandarin sekaligus menikmati makanan lezat.","This job is both relaxed and very meaningful.":"Pekerjaan ini santai sekaligus sangat bermakna.","please do not (signs/notices)":"mohon jangan (tanda/pengumuman)","(qǐng) + wù + verb":"(qǐng) + wù + verba","A formal, written prohibition used on public signs and notices, not in everyday speech (use 不要/別 there instead). The set phrase 請勿 is the most common form.":"Ini adalah larangan formal dan tertulis yang digunakan pada tanda dan pengumuman publik, bukan dalam percakapan sehari-hari (gunakan 不要/別 sebagai gantinya). Frasa tetap 請勿 adalah bentuk yang paling umum.","Please do not smoke in the public area!":"Mohon tidak merokok di area umum!","Please do not talk loudly inside the library.":"Mohon tidak berbicara dengan suara keras di dalam perpustakaan.","cause/result in (introduces a resulting state)":"menyebabkan/mengakibatkan (memperkenalkan keadaan hasil)","cause clause + shǐde + result clause":"klausa sebab + shǐde + klausa akibat","A formal, written expression showing that a preceding cause leads to a following result or state. More clause-connecting than 使, and cannot be followed by a command or request.":"Ungkapan formal dan bergaya tulisan yang menunjukkan bahwa sebab yang disebutkan sebelumnya menyebabkan hasil atau keadaan yang mengikutinya. Lebih bersifat menghubungkan klausa dibandingkan 使, dan tidak boleh diikuti oleh perintah atau permintaan.","This writer spent two years revising it, making the novel even more complete.":"Penulis ini menghabiskan waktu dua tahun untuk merevisinya, membuat novel tersebut menjadi lebih sempurna.","His long-term effort finally led him to success.":"Usahanya yang panjang akhirnya membawanya menuju kesuksesan.","to make/cause (someone to do something)":"membuat/menyebabkan (seseorang melakukan sesuatu)","subject + shǐ + object + verb/adjective":"subjek + shǐ + objek + verba/adjektiva","A causative verb similar in meaning to 讓, but more formal/written. The subject is often something inanimate or abstract; in casual speech 讓 is more natural.":"Verba kausatif yang maknanya mirip dengan 讓, tetapi lebih formal/bergaya tulisan. Subjeknya sering berupa sesuatu yang tak bernyawa atau abstrak; dalam percakapan sehari-hari, 讓 terasa lebih alami.","Drinking a cup of coffee in the morning can make his mind clearer.":"Minum secangkir kopi di pagi hari dapat membuat pikirannya lebih jernih.","The teacher's encouragement made me more confident.":"Dorongan semangat dari guru membuat saya lebih percaya diri.","to cause/make (someone feel or do something)":"menyebabkan/membuat (seseorang merasakan atau melakukan sesuatu)","A + 令 + B + feeling/action":"A + 令 + B + perasaan/tindakan","\"令\" is a formal, written causative verb similar to 讓/使, meaning \"to make someone feel/become.\" It must be followed by a person plus an emotional or resultant state. In casual speech, 讓 sounds more natural.":"\"令\" adalah verba kausatif formal dan bergaya tulisan yang mirip dengan 讓/使, berarti \"membuat seseorang merasakan/menjadi.\" Kata ini harus diikuti oleh seseorang ditambah keadaan emosional atau hasil tertentu. Dalam percakapan sehari-hari, 讓 terdengar lebih alami.","This restaurant's atmosphere and service leave a deep impression on people.":"Suasana dan pelayanan restoran ini meninggalkan kesan yang mendalam bagi orang-orang.","The ending of this movie left the audience utterly astonished.":"Akhir film ini membuat penonton benar-benar tercengang.","besides/in addition to (doing) ~, in the margin of ~":"selain/di samping (melakukan) ~, di sela-sela ~","(在) + VP1(main activity) + 之餘 + VP2(additional action)":"(在) + VP1(kegiatan utama) + 之餘 + VP2(tindakan tambahan)","\"之餘\" expresses doing something extra in the margin/spare time of a main activity. Unlike 之後 (after), it's not about time sequence but about doing something alongside the main action. The leading 在 is often omissible.":"\"之餘\" menyatakan melakukan sesuatu tambahan di sela-sela/waktu luang dari suatu kegiatan utama. Berbeda dengan 之後 (setelah), ini bukan tentang urutan waktu, melainkan tentang melakukan sesuatu bersamaan dengan tindakan utama. 在 di awal sering dapat dihilangkan.","Besides his work, he doesn't forget to enrich his professional knowledge.":"Selain bekerja, ia tidak lupa memperkaya pengetahuan profesionalnya.","Besides taking care of the children, she also keeps exercising every day.":"Selain mengurus anak-anak, ia juga tetap berolahraga setiap hari.","in one go, without stopping or pausing":"sekaligus, tanpa berhenti atau jeda","Subject + 一口氣 + Verb(+完/了) + (quantity)":"Subjek + 一口氣 + Verba(+完/了) + (jumlah)","\"一口氣\" is an adverbial placed before the verb, meaning an action is completed continuously without stopping. It's often used with strenuous or lengthy tasks (running, drinking, finishing work). A common mistake is placing it after the verb.":"\"一口氣\" adalah kata keterangan yang diletakkan sebelum verba, berarti suatu tindakan diselesaikan secara berkelanjutan tanpa berhenti. Kata ini sering digunakan untuk tugas yang melelahkan atau berlangsung lama (berlari, minum, menyelesaikan pekerjaan). Kesalahan umum adalah meletakkannya setelah verba.","He ran five thousand meters in one go.":"Ia berlari sejauh lima ribu meter sekaligus tanpa berhenti.","She drank an entire bottle of water in one gulp.":"Ia menghabiskan sebotol air dalam sekali teguk.","sooner or later, eventually":"cepat atau lambat, pada akhirnya","早晚 + 會 + VP":"早晚 + 會 + VP","Here \"早晚\" doesn't mean \"morning and evening\" but functions as an adverb meaning \"sooner or later, inevitably.\" It's typically paired with 會 before the verb, often ending with 的 for emphasis. It's interchangeable with the synonym 遲早.":"Di sini \"早晚\" tidak berarti \"pagi dan malam\", melainkan berfungsi sebagai kata keterangan yang berarti \"cepat atau lambat, pasti terjadi.\" Kata ini biasanya dipasangkan dengan 會 sebelum verba, dan sering diakhiri dengan 的 untuk penekanan. Kata ini dapat dipertukarkan dengan sinonimnya, 遲早.","Let's just tell Dad the car broke down—he'll find out sooner or later.":"Katakan saja pada Ayah kalau mobilnya rusak—cepat atau lambat dia akan tahu juga.","It's no use denying it now—everyone will find out sooner or later.":"Sekarang menyangkalnya pun percuma—cepat atau lambat semua orang akan mengetahuinya.","if (a more formal/written equivalent of 如果)":"jika (padanan yang lebih formal/bergaya tulisan dari 如果)","若 + condition clause, + result clause":"若 + klausa syarat, + klausa hasil","\"若\" is the written/formal counterpart of 如果, common in news reports and formal writing but rare in daily conversation (where 如果/要是 sound more natural). It's grammatically complete without 就 or 的話, though they may follow for emphasis.":"\"若\" adalah padanan formal/tulisan dari 如果, umum digunakan dalam berita dan tulisan resmi tetapi jarang dipakai dalam percakapan sehari-hari (di mana 如果/要是 terdengar lebih alami). Secara tata bahasa sudah lengkap tanpa 就 atau 的話, meskipun keduanya bisa mengikuti untuk penekanan.","If costs increase, prices will probably rise as well.":"Jika biaya meningkat, harga mungkin juga akan naik.","If it rains tomorrow, the sports day will be postponed.":"Jika besok hujan, hari olahraga akan ditunda.","if it weren't for...":"seandainya bukan karena...","要不是 + A, (就) + B":"要不是 + A, (就) + B","'要不是' expresses a counterfactual: 'if it weren't for X, Y would have happened.' Often paired with 就. Similar to 如果不是 but more colloquial, often implying relief or regret about what almost happened.":"'要不是' mengungkapkan pengandaian kontrafaktual: \"seandainya bukan karena X, Y akan terjadi.\" Sering dipasangkan dengan 就. Mirip dengan 如果不是 tetapi lebih santai/sehari-hari, sering menyiratkan rasa lega atau penyesalan atas sesuatu yang hampir terjadi.","If it weren't for your help, this might not have gone so smoothly.":"Seandainya bukan karena bantuanmu, ini mungkin tidak akan berjalan selancar ini.","If you hadn't reminded me, I would have already forgotten that there's a meeting today.":"Seandainya kamu tidak mengingatkanku, aku pasti sudah lupa bahwa hari ini ada rapat.","in case / what if (something unlikely happens)":"kalau-kalau / bagaimana jika (sesuatu yang tidak mungkin terjadi)","萬一 + A (undesirable event), (就) + B (response)":"萬一 + A (kejadian yang tidak diinginkan), (就) + B (respons)","'萬一' means 'in the unlikely case that (something undesirable) happens,' used to talk about precautions for a low-probability bad event. Compared to plain 如果, it stresses the event is unlikely and often unwanted.":"'萬一' berarti \"dalam kemungkinan kecil bahwa (sesuatu yang tidak diinginkan) terjadi,\" digunakan untuk membicarakan tindakan pencegahan terhadap kejadian buruk yang berpeluang kecil. Dibandingkan dengan 如果 biasa, kata ini menekankan bahwa kejadian tersebut jarang terjadi dan seringkali tidak diinginkan.","If there were a hospital on the island, in case a car accident happened, it could be dealt with immediately.":"Jika di pulau itu ada rumah sakit, kalau-kalau terjadi kecelakaan mobil, itu bisa segera ditangani.","Remember to bring an umbrella when you go out, in case it rains, so you won't get wet.":"Ingat membawa payung saat keluar rumah, kalau-kalau hujan, supaya kamu tidak basah.","once ... (then)":"begitu ... (maka)","一旦 + A (an action/change), (就) + B (a resulting, often hard-to-reverse outcome)":"一旦 + A (suatu tindakan/perubahan), (就) + B (hasil yang sering kali sulit diubah kembali)","'一旦' means 'once X happens, then...', usually followed by a consequence that is hard to reverse. Unlike 萬一, it doesn't imply the event is unlikely — it can be about something certain or common.":"'一旦' berarti \"begitu X terjadi, maka...\", biasanya diikuti oleh konsekuensi yang sulit diubah kembali. Berbeda dengan 萬一, kata ini tidak menyiratkan bahwa kejadian tersebut jarang terjadi — bisa saja tentang sesuatu yang pasti atau umum terjadi.","Once the environment is destroyed, it's very hard to restore it.":"Begitu lingkungan rusak, sangat sulit untuk memulihkannya.","Once this disease is discovered, it must be treated immediately.":"Begitu penyakit ini ditemukan, harus segera diobati.","without A, there would be no B":"tanpa A, tidak akan ada B","沒有 + A, 就沒有 + B (emphasizing A is essential for B)":"沒有 + A, 就沒有 + B (menekankan bahwa A penting bagi B)","'沒有A，就沒有B' emphasizes that A is a necessary condition for B, often used to praise someone's contribution or importance. It's not just two negative statements — it highlights a cause-and-contribution relationship.":"'沒有A，就沒有B' menekankan bahwa A adalah syarat yang diperlukan bagi B, sering digunakan untuk memuji kontribusi atau pentingnya seseorang. Ini bukan sekadar dua pernyataan negatif — ini menonjolkan hubungan sebab dan kontribusi.","Without his guidance, there wouldn't be such a creative idea.":"Tanpa bimbingannya, tidak akan ada ide sekreatif ini.","Without farmers working hard to grow crops, there would be no rice for us to eat every day.":"Tanpa petani yang bekerja keras menanam hasil panen, tidak akan ada nasi untuk kita makan setiap hari.","even though / despite ..., (still) ...":"meskipun / walaupun ..., (tetap) ...","儘管 + A (a concessive fact), 還是/但是 + B (a result unaffected by A)":"儘管 + A (fakta konsesif), 還是/但是 + B (hasil yang tidak terpengaruh oleh A)","'儘管' is similar to 雖然 in expressing concession, but pairs with 還是/但是 to stress that result B holds true regardless of fact A. It sounds slightly more formal/written than 雖然.":"'儘管' mirip dengan 雖然 dalam mengungkapkan konsesi, tetapi dipasangkan dengan 還是/但是 untuk menekankan bahwa hasil B tetap berlaku terlepas dari fakta A. Terdengar sedikit lebih formal/tulisan dibandingkan 雖然.","Even though we don't see each other often, we always have a great time chatting whenever we get together.":"Meskipun kami tidak sering bertemu, kami selalu senang mengobrol setiap kali berkumpul.","Even though it's pouring rain outside, he still got to the office on time.":"Meskipun hujan deras di luar, dia tetap tiba di kantor tepat waktu.","to move the object before the verb (formal equivalent of 把)":"memindahkan objek ke depan kata kerja (padanan formal dari 把)","Subject + 將 + Object + Verb (+ Complement)":"Subjek + 將 + Objek + Kata kerja (+ Pelengkap)","\"將\" functions like the more colloquial \"把,\" moving the object before the verb to emphasize what happens to it. It's typical of written or formal Chinese; in speech, 把 is far more common.":"\"將\" berfungsi seperti \"把\" yang lebih umum digunakan dalam bahasa lisan, memindahkan objek ke depan kata kerja untuk menekankan apa yang terjadi padanya. Ini adalah pola yang khas dalam bahasa Tionghoa tulisan atau formal; dalam percakapan, \"把\" jauh lebih umum digunakan.","Teachers must also keep learning constantly in order to pass new knowledge on to students.":"Guru juga harus terus belajar agar dapat menyampaikan pengetahuan baru kepada murid-muridnya.","The company decided to tell all the employees this news.":"Perusahaan memutuskan untuk memberitahukan kabar ini kepada seluruh karyawan.","\"Vs得要命\" expresses an extreme degree — \"incredibly/terribly ~\"":"\"Vs得要命\" mengungkapkan tingkat yang sangat ekstrem — \"sangat/luar biasa ~\"","Stative Verb/Adjective + 得要命":"Kata Kerja Statif/Kata Sifat + 得要命","\"得要命\" is a colloquial exaggeration much stronger than \"得很,\" close to \"to death\" in English. It attaches only to stative verbs/adjectives, not action verbs.":"\"得要命\" adalah ungkapan berlebihan yang bersifat lisan, jauh lebih kuat daripada \"得很,\" mendekati arti \"setengah mati\" dalam bahasa Indonesia. Kata ini hanya melekat pada kata kerja statif/kata sifat, bukan kata kerja tindakan.","Even if the sun comes out, the weather is still freezing cold.":"Meskipun matahari muncul, cuaca tetap sangat dingin.","Before the exam, everyone was incredibly nervous.":"Sebelum ujian, semua orang gugup luar biasa.","\"不料\" introduces an unexpected turn of events (\"unexpectedly\")":"\"不料\" memperkenalkan perkembangan yang tidak terduga (\"tanpa disangka\")","(Previous clause), 不料 + (unexpected event)":"(Klausa sebelumnya), 不料 + (peristiwa tak terduga)","\"不料\" sits at the start of a clause to signal that something unexpected happened, contrary to what the earlier situation would suggest. It's close in meaning to \"沒想到\" but reads as more formal/written.":"\"不料\" diletakkan di awal klausa untuk menandakan bahwa sesuatu yang tak terduga telah terjadi, berlawanan dengan apa yang diisyaratkan oleh situasi sebelumnya. Maknanya dekat dengan \"沒想到\" tetapi terkesan lebih formal/tertulis.","They had already left half an hour early, but unexpectedly there was a traffic jam, and they still ended up being late.":"Mereka sudah berangkat setengah jam lebih awal, tetapi tanpa disangka terjadi kemacetan, sehingga tetap terlambat.","He originally planned to take the MRT to work, but unexpectedly the MRT suddenly stopped running, making him late.":"Awalnya dia berencana naik MRT ke tempat kerja, tetapi tanpa disangka MRT tiba-tiba berhenti beroperasi, sehingga dia terlambat.","\"誰叫...\" expresses blame — \"it's your own fault for...\" / \"well, who told you to...\"":"\"誰叫...\" mengungkapkan sikap menyalahkan — \"salah sendiri, siapa suruh...\" / \"habis, siapa suruh...\"","誰叫 + Subject + (不) + Verb Phrase, (self-inflicted result follows)":"誰叫 + Subjek + (不) + Frasa Kata Kerja, (diikuti akibat yang ditanggung sendiri)","\"誰叫\" doesn't literally ask \"who made you...\" — it's a colloquial way of blaming someone, meaning \"well, that's what you get for...\". A negative consequence follows in the second clause.":"\"誰叫\" secara harfiah bukan berarti bertanya \"siapa yang membuatmu...\", melainkan cara lisan untuk menyalahkan seseorang, berarti \"salah sendiri, siapa suruh...\". Akibat negatif akan mengikuti di klausa kedua.","Well, that's what you get for not coming earlier — all the food's been eaten up.":"Salah sendiri, siapa suruh tidak datang lebih awal — makanannya sudah habis dimakan.","Well, that's what you get for not listening to me — it's no use regretting it now.":"Salah sendiri, siapa suruh tidak mendengarkan saya — sekarang menyesal pun percuma.","\"有什麼好V(O)/SV的\" rhetorically dismisses something as \"not worth ~ing\" / \"nothing to ~ about\"":"\"有什麼好V(O)/SV的\" digunakan secara retoris untuk menampik sesuatu, berarti \"tidak perlu ~\" / \"tidak ada yang perlu ~\"","(Subject) + 有什麼好 + Verb (+ Object) / Adjective + 的":"(Subjek) + 有什麼好 + Kata Kerja (+ Objek) / Kata Sifat + 的","This is a rhetorical question — grammatically a question, but it actually means a strong \"there's no need to ~ at all.\" A verb (+object) or adjective follows \"有什麼好,\" and the sentence always ends in 的.":"Ini adalah pertanyaan retoris — secara tata bahasa berbentuk pertanyaan, tetapi sebenarnya bermakna penegasan kuat \"sama sekali tidak perlu ~\". Setelah \"有什麼好\" diikuti kata kerja (+objek) atau kata sifat, dan kalimatnya selalu diakhiri dengan 的.","The result is already decided — what's there left to discuss!":"Hasilnya sudah diputuskan — apa lagi yang perlu dibicarakan!","Everything's already prepared — what is there to worry about?":"Semuanya sudah dipersiapkan — apa yang perlu dikhawatirkan lagi?","A + 畢竟 + B (states the underlying reason/fact)":"A + 畢竟 + B (menyatakan alasan/fakta yang mendasarinya)","\"Bìjìng\" points out an unchanging underlying fact or reason, often with a concessive nuance (\"no matter what, this fact must be considered\"), followed by a reasonable conclusion drawn from it. Don't confuse it with \"jiūjìng\" (used in questions, meaning \"actually/in the end\").":"\"Bìjìng\" menunjukkan suatu fakta atau alasan mendasar yang tidak berubah, sering kali membawa nuansa konsesif (\"bagaimanapun juga, fakta ini harus dipertimbangkan\"), diikuti oleh kesimpulan wajar yang ditarik darinya. Jangan disamakan dengan \"jiūjìng\" (digunakan dalam kalimat tanya, berarti \"sebenarnya/pada akhirnya\").","After all, he's just a child, so it's normal that he likes to play.":"Bagaimanapun juga dia hanya seorang anak kecil, jadi wajar saja jika dia suka bermain.","After all, he's getting older, so he climbs mountains more slowly.":"Bagaimanapun juga usianya sudah semakin tua, jadi wajar jika dia mendaki gunung lebih lambat.","(Even if) ..., 難免 + will/have ... (an undesirable result is unavoidable)":"(Meskipun) ..., 難免 + akan/memiliki ... (hasil yang tidak diinginkan tak terhindarkan)","\"Nánmiǎn\" means an undesirable outcome can't be avoided, usually followed by 會/有 + something negative. It's close to \"bùmiǎn\" but more commonly used in speech. It cannot stand alone as a predicate — a verb phrase must follow.":"\"Nánmiǎn\" berarti suatu hasil yang tidak diinginkan tidak dapat dihindari, biasanya diikuti oleh 會/有 + sesuatu yang negatif. Maknanya dekat dengan \"bùmiǎn\" tetapi lebih umum digunakan dalam bahasa lisan. Kata ini tidak dapat berdiri sendiri sebagai predikat — harus diikuti oleh frasa kata kerja.","Even a new car will inevitably have some minor problems.":"Bahkan mobil baru pun tidak terhindar dari beberapa masalah kecil.","When you've just started learning to drive, it's inevitable to feel nervous.":"Saat baru mulai belajar mengemudi, wajar jika merasa gugup.","don't judge by appearances; despite how it seems":"jangan menilai dari penampilan luar; meskipun kelihatannya begitu","別看 + A (apparent situation), (but actually/still) + B (the real situation)":"別看 + A (situasi yang tampak), (tetapi sebenarnya/tetap) + B (situasi yang sebenarnya)","\"Biékàn\" opens a sentence to contrast appearance with reality (\"it may look like X, but actually/still Y\"), often followed by 其實/還是/卻. Unlike \"雖然\" (a plain concessive fact), \"別看\" specifically highlights a gap between appearance/impression and reality, and is more colloquial.":"\"Biékàn\" mengawali kalimat untuk mengontraskan penampilan luar dengan kenyataan (\"kelihatannya X, tetapi sebenarnya/tetap Y\"), sering diikuti oleh 其實/還是/卻. Berbeda dengan \"雖然\" (yang hanya menyatakan fakta konsesif biasa), \"別看\" secara khusus menyoroti kesenjangan antara penampilan/kesan dan kenyataan, serta lebih bersifat percakapan sehari-hari.","Don't be fooled by how busy he looks with work — he still makes time to exercise.":"Jangan tertipu oleh betapa sibuknya dia terlihat dengan pekerjaan — dia tetap menyempatkan diri untuk berolahraga.","Don't be fooled by how small this shop looks — business is really booming.":"Jangan tertipu oleh betapa kecilnya toko ini terlihat — bisnisnya sebenarnya sangat ramai.","it doesn't matter; makes no difference":"tidak masalah; tidak ada bedanya","A + 無所謂 + B (for A, the distinction/concern of B doesn't exist)":"A + 無所謂 + B (bagi A, perbedaan/kepedulian terhadap B tidak ada)","\"Wúsuǒwèi\" means \"it doesn't matter / makes no difference,\" often followed by a noun phrase or 對/跟…(來說), indicating no real distinction or importance. As a standalone reply it means \"either is fine, I don't mind.\" Unlike \"沒關係\" (mainly a response to an apology), \"無所謂\" more broadly expresses an attitude of not caring.":"\"Wúsuǒwèi\" berarti \"tidak masalah / tidak ada bedanya\", sering diikuti oleh frasa nomina atau 對/跟…(來說), yang menunjukkan tidak adanya perbedaan atau kepentingan yang nyata. Sebagai jawaban berdiri sendiri, artinya \"yang mana saja boleh, saya tidak keberatan\". Berbeda dengan \"沒關係\" (yang terutama digunakan untuk menanggapi permintaan maaf), \"無所謂\" mengungkapkan sikap tidak peduli secara lebih luas.","There's no right or wrong answer to this question — everyone just sees it differently.":"Pertanyaan ini tidak memiliki jawaban benar atau salah — setiap orang hanya memandangnya secara berbeda.","I don't mind where we eat — you decide.":"Saya tidak masalah mau makan di mana — kamu yang putuskan.","at the drop of a hat; tends to easily (do something undesirable)":"hanya karena hal sepele langsung...; cenderung dengan mudah (melakukan sesuatu yang tidak diinginkan)","(A) + 動不動就 + B (easily and frequently does B, usually negative)":"(A) + 動不動就 + B (dengan mudah dan sering melakukan B, biasanya bernuansa negatif)","\"Dòngbúdòng jiù\" describes an action or state that happens frequently over trivial triggers, usually carrying the speaker's complaint or surprise, and must be followed by a verb phrase (not a noun). Unlike \"常常\" (just states frequency, neutral), \"動不動就\" carries a critical, \"over the slightest thing\" nuance.":"\"Dòngbúdòng jiù\" menggambarkan tindakan atau keadaan yang sering terjadi hanya karena pemicu sepele, biasanya membawa nada keluhan atau keheranan pembicara, dan harus diikuti oleh frasa verba (bukan nomina). Berbeda dengan \"常常\" (yang hanya menyatakan frekuensi secara netral), \"動不動就\" membawa nuansa kritis, seperti \"hanya karena hal sekecil apa pun\".","He's been emotionally unstable lately — he cries at the drop of a hat.":"Belakangan ini dia sedang tidak stabil secara emosional — hanya karena hal sepele langsung menangis.","This computer keeps crashing at the slightest thing, which is really annoying.":"Komputer ini hanya karena hal sepele langsung macet, benar-benar menyebalkan.","clearly...(yet); expressing contradiction":"jelas-jelas...(tetapi); mengungkapkan kontradiksi","Míngmíng + fact, (què/hái) + contradictory action":"Míngmíng + fakta, (què/hái) + tindakan yang bertentangan","\"Míngmíng\" emphasizes a fact the speaker is certain of, followed by a contrasting or contradictory result, often paired with \"卻/還\". Unlike neutral \"其實\", it always carries a tone of complaint or surprise.":"\"Míngmíng\" menekankan suatu fakta yang diyakini pembicara, diikuti oleh hasil yang bertentangan atau kontradiktif, sering dipasangkan dengan \"卻/還\". Berbeda dengan \"其實\" yang bersifat netral, kata ini selalu membawa nada keluhan atau keheranan.","It clearly says here that pets are prohibited, so why did you bring the puppy in?":"Di sini jelas-jelas tertulis dilarang membawa hewan peliharaan, kenapa kamu membawa masuk anak anjing itu?","He clearly knows I'm busy, but he keeps calling me.":"Dia jelas-jelas tahu saya sedang sibuk, tetapi tetap terus meneleponku.","fortunately, luckily":"untungnya, syukurlah","Hǎozài + fortunate circumstance, clause":"Hǎozài + keadaan yang beruntung, klausa","\"Hǎozài\" appears at the start of a clause to state a fortunate condition that averted a bad outcome, often followed by \"不然/否則\" for the hypothetical negative result. It's nearly synonymous with \"幸虧\" but more colloquial.":"\"Hǎozài\" muncul di awal klausa untuk menyatakan suatu kondisi yang beruntung yang mencegah terjadinya hasil buruk, sering diikuti oleh \"不然/否則\" untuk menyebutkan hasil negatif yang seandainya terjadi. Kata ini hampir sinonim dengan \"幸虧\" tetapi lebih bersifat percakapan sehari-hari.","Fortunately, this isn't the official performance yet, so everyone can practice once more.":"Untungnya ini belum pertunjukan resmi, jadi semua orang masih bisa berlatih sekali lagi.","Luckily I brought an umbrella, otherwise I would have gotten soaked.":"Untungnya saya membawa payung, kalau tidak saya pasti sudah basah kuyup.","nominalizes the object of a verb: \"what (subject) V-s\"":"menominakan objek dari sebuah verba: \"apa yang (subjek) lakukan/V\"","N1 + suǒ + V + de (+ N2)":"N1 + suǒ + V + de (+ N2)","\"Suǒ\" is a written-style marker placed before the verb (with \"的\" after) to nominalize the object of the action. Omitting \"所\" is still grammatical but sounds more colloquial; adding it gives a more formal, written register.":"\"Suǒ\" adalah penanda bergaya tulisan yang diletakkan sebelum verba (dengan \"的\" di belakangnya) untuk menominakan objek dari tindakan tersebut. Menghilangkan \"所\" tetap gramatikal tetapi terdengar lebih seperti bahasa lisan sehari-hari; menambahkannya memberikan register yang lebih formal dan bergaya tulisan.","Generally speaking, what linguists focus on is the issue of language rules.":"Secara umum, apa yang menjadi fokus para ahli bahasa adalah masalah aturan bahasa.","What this shop sells is all fruit produced locally in Taiwan.":"Yang dijual toko ini semuanya adalah buah-buahan yang diproduksi secara lokal di Taiwan.","no matter what, in any case":"apa pun yang terjadi, bagaimanapun juga","Wúlùn rúhé, subject + dōu + V":"Wúlùn rúhé, subjek + dōu + V","\"Wúlùn rúhé\" is a fixed phrase placed at the start of a sentence to stress that the conclusion holds regardless of any condition, typically followed by \"都\" in the next clause. Unlike \"無論 + question word\" patterns, it's a fixed idiom that can't be broken apart.":"\"Wúlùn rúhé\" adalah frasa tetap yang diletakkan di awal kalimat untuk menekankan bahwa kesimpulannya berlaku terlepas dari kondisi apa pun, biasanya diikuti oleh \"都\" pada klausa berikutnya. Berbeda dengan pola \"無論 + kata tanya\", ini adalah ungkapan tetap yang tidak dapat dipecah.","This meeting is very important, so no matter what, you must attend.":"Rapat ini sangat penting, jadi apa pun yang terjadi, kamu harus hadir.","No matter what, I will get to the airport on time to pick you up.":"Apa pun yang terjadi, saya akan tiba di bandara tepat waktu untuk menjemputmu.","generally speaking (stating a general tendency)":"secara umum (menyatakan kecenderungan umum)","Yìbān éryán, clause":"Yìbān éryán, klausa","\"Yìbān éryán\" opens a sentence to state a general tendency or principle, allowing for exceptions; it's a more formal, written-style synonym of \"一般來說\", common in reports and essays.":"\"Yìbān éryán\" digunakan di awal kalimat untuk menyatakan kecenderungan atau prinsip umum, dengan kemungkinan adanya pengecualian; ini adalah sinonim yang lebih formal dan bergaya tulisan dari \"一般來說\", yang umum digunakan dalam laporan dan esai.","Generally speaking, the higher the salary, the easier it is to attract talent.":"Secara umum, semakin tinggi gaji, semakin mudah untuk menarik talenta.","Generally speaking, it doesn't snow in winter in Taiwan.":"Secara umum, di Taiwan tidak turun salju pada musim dingin.","now, as a result of this":"sekarang, sebagai akibat dari hal ini","(cause clause), 這下子, (resulting clause)":"(klausa sebab), 這下子, (klausa akibat)","\"這下子\" marks a resulting change in situation, meaning \"now/this time (as a result)\". It's colloquial and placed after the cause clause to introduce the consequence.":"\"這下子\" menandai perubahan situasi sebagai akibat, berarti \"sekarang/kali ini (sebagai akibatnya)\". Ini adalah ungkapan sehari-hari yang diletakkan setelah klausa sebab untuk memperkenalkan akibatnya.","He found a good job — now he can finally finish paying off the loan.":"Dia menemukan pekerjaan yang bagus — sekarang akhirnya dia bisa melunasi pinjamannya.","He finally found his passport — now we can finally leave on time.":"Dia akhirnya menemukan paspornya — sekarang kita akhirnya bisa berangkat tepat waktu.","mainly, the main reason is":"terutama, alasan utamanya adalah","(topic) + 主要（的）是 + (the main reason/content)":"(topik) + 主要（的）是 + (alasan/isi utama)","\"主要（的）是\" highlights the main reason or point among several possible ones, roughly \"mainly / the main thing is\". The 的 is optional and doesn't change the meaning.":"\"主要（的）是\" menyoroti alasan atau poin utama di antara beberapa kemungkinan, kurang lebih berarti \"terutama / yang utama adalah\". \"的\" bersifat opsional dan tidak mengubah makna.","The main reason I invited everyone to this meeting today is that I want to understand everyone's views on this issue.":"Alasan utama saya mengundang semua orang ke rapat hari ini adalah karena saya ingin memahami pandangan semua orang tentang masalah ini.","This shop sells a lot of things, but mainly coffee and desserts.":"Toko ini menjual banyak barang, tetapi terutama kopi dan makanan penutup.","basically, in general":"pada dasarnya, secara umum","基本上, + (statement of the overall situation)":"基本上, + (pernyataan tentang situasi keseluruhan)","\"基本上\" means \"basically/in general,\" used to state an overall situation while implying minor exceptions may exist. It's usually placed at the start of a sentence.":"\"基本上\" berarti \"pada dasarnya/secara umum,\" digunakan untuk menyatakan situasi keseluruhan sambil menyiratkan bahwa mungkin ada sedikit pengecualian. Biasanya diletakkan di awal kalimat.","Basically, these apps are all free; you only need to pay if you want more features.":"Pada dasarnya, aplikasi-aplikasi ini semuanya gratis; kamu hanya perlu membayar jika ingin fitur tambahan.","Basically, this project is already finished; only the final check remains.":"Pada dasarnya, proyek ini sudah selesai; hanya tinggal pemeriksaan akhir.","it can be seen that, this shows":"dapat dilihat bahwa, ini menunjukkan","(fact/phenomenon), 可見 + (conclusion drawn from it)":"(fakta/fenomena), 可見 + (kesimpulan yang ditarik darinya)","\"可見\" introduces a logical conclusion drawn from a preceding fact, meaning \"this shows / it can be seen that\". It's more formal and written than colloquial equivalents like \"看起來\".":"\"可見\" memperkenalkan kesimpulan logis yang ditarik dari fakta sebelumnya, berarti \"ini menunjukkan / dapat dilihat bahwa\". Kata ini lebih formal dan bergaya tulisan dibandingkan padanan sehari-hari seperti \"看起來\".","This magazine sells over fifty thousand copies a month, which shows it's very popular in the market.":"Majalah ini terjual lebih dari lima puluh ribu eksemplar per bulan, yang menunjukkan bahwa majalah ini sangat populer di pasar.","He practices seriously every day, which shows he really wants to improve.":"Dia berlatih dengan serius setiap hari, yang menunjukkan bahwa dia benar-benar ingin meningkatkan diri.","but then again, having said that":"tapi kalau dipikir-pikir lagi, ngomong-ngomong","(previous statement), （可是）話說回來, + (a return to another perspective)":"(pernyataan sebelumnya), （可是）話說回來, + (kembali ke sudut pandang lain)","\"話說回來\" shifts back to another angle after a preceding statement, similar to \"but then again / having said that\". Adding \"可是\" before it strengthens the contrastive nuance. It's more colloquial than \"不過\".":"\"話說回來\" mengalihkan pembicaraan ke sudut pandang lain setelah pernyataan sebelumnya, mirip dengan \"tapi kalau dipikir-pikir lagi / ngomong-ngomong\". Menambahkan \"可是\" di depannya memperkuat nuansa kontrasnya. Ungkapan ini lebih bersifat lisan/santai dibandingkan \"不過\".","Getting along with people is indeed difficult. But then again, as long as you're sincere, you can make good friends.":"Bergaul dengan orang lain memang sulit. Tapi kalau dipikir-pikir lagi, selama kamu tulus, kamu bisa mendapatkan teman baik.","This exam didn't go very well. But then again, at least I learned how to manage my time.":"Ujian ini tidak berjalan dengan baik. Tapi kalau dipikir-pikir lagi, setidaknya aku belajar cara mengatur waktu.","on the contrary; conversely":"sebaliknya","Clause A, fǎnzhī, Clause B (B states the opposite of A)":"Klausa A, fǎnzhī, Klausa B (B menyatakan hal yang berlawanan dengan A)","\"Fǎnzhī\" introduces a statement opposite to what precedes it; it's a formal written connector placed at the start of a clause, followed by a comma. It's more formal than \"相反地,\" which is more common in speech.":"\"Fǎnzhī\" memperkenalkan pernyataan yang berlawanan dengan yang disebutkan sebelumnya; ini adalah kata penghubung formal dalam bahasa tulis, diletakkan di awal klausa, diikuti tanda koma. Kata ini lebih formal daripada \"相反地,\" yang lebih umum digunakan dalam bahasa lisan.","Exercising too intensely before bed makes it hard to sleep; conversely, listening to some music can help you sleep.":"Berolahraga terlalu berat sebelum tidur membuat sulit tidur; sebaliknya, mendengarkan musik bisa membantu kamu tidur.","When the weather is nice, everyone wants to go out; conversely, on rainy days people would rather stay home.":"Saat cuaca cerah, semua orang ingin keluar; sebaliknya, pada hari hujan orang lebih memilih tinggal di rumah.","Statement A, huàn jù huà shuō, Statement B (B rephrases A)":"Pernyataan A, huàn jù huà shuō, Pernyataan B (B mengungkapkan kembali A)","Used to restate the preceding idea in different, clearer words; it's a formal connector. Similar to \"也就是說,\" but \"換句話說\" emphasizes rephrasing while \"也就是說\" emphasizes drawing a conclusion.":"Digunakan untuk menyatakan kembali gagasan sebelumnya dengan kata-kata lain yang lebih jelas; ini adalah kata penghubung formal. Mirip dengan \"也就是說,\" tetapi \"換句話說\" menekankan pengungkapan ulang, sedangkan \"也就是說\" menekankan penarikan kesimpulan.","The birth rate has dropped; in other words, there are fewer and fewer children.":"Angka kelahiran telah menurun; dengan kata lain, jumlah anak-anak semakin sedikit.","He works overtime until very late every day; in other words, he has almost no time of his own.":"Dia lembur sampai sangat larut setiap hari; dengan kata lain, dia hampir tidak punya waktu untuk dirinya sendiri.","besides this; in addition":"selain itu; di samping itu","Statement A (and B), chúcǐzhīwài, additional point C":"Pernyataan A (dan B), chúcǐzhīwài, poin tambahan C","Adds one more point on top of what was already mentioned; more formal than \"而且,\" and typically used to add a final point after a list.":"Menambahkan satu poin lagi selain yang sudah disebutkan; lebih formal daripada \"而且,\" dan biasanya digunakan untuk menambahkan poin terakhir setelah suatu daftar.","He is not only a successful entrepreneur but also a scholar; besides that, he is a good father too.":"Dia bukan hanya seorang pengusaha sukses tetapi juga seorang cendekiawan; selain itu, dia juga seorang ayah yang baik.","The food at this restaurant is delicious and cheap; on top of that, the service is also very friendly.":"Makanan di restoran ini enak dan murah; di samping itu, pelayanannya juga sangat ramah.","correspondingly; relatively":"secara relatif; sesuai dengan itu","A changes, xiāngduì de, B changes correspondingly":"A berubah, xiāngduì de, B pun berubah secara sesuai","An adverb showing that one thing changes in proportion to a preceding change; unlike \"越來越\" (which emphasizes increasing degree), it highlights the correlation between two changes.":"Kata keterangan yang menunjukkan bahwa sesuatu berubah sebanding dengan perubahan sebelumnya; berbeda dengan \"越來越\" (yang menekankan tingkat yang semakin meningkat), kata ini menyoroti korelasi antara dua perubahan.","The company has grown larger and larger, and correspondingly, the space it needs has also increased.":"Perusahaan itu semakin besar, dan sesuai dengan itu, ruang yang dibutuhkan juga bertambah.","Income has increased, and correspondingly, the taxes owed have also increased.":"Pendapatan telah meningkat, dan sesuai dengan itu, pajak yang harus dibayar juga meningkat.","in fact; actually":"sebenarnya; pada kenyataannya","Common belief/appearance, shìshí shàng, actual fact B":"Anggapan umum/tampilan luar, shìshí shàng, fakta sebenarnya B","Used to state the actual fact, contrasting it with a common assumption or appearance; similar to \"其實\" but more formal, often used in essays with objective facts or data.":"Digunakan untuk menyatakan fakta sebenarnya, sebagai kontras terhadap asumsi umum atau tampilan luar; mirip dengan \"其實\" tetapi lebih formal, sering digunakan dalam esai dengan fakta atau data yang objektif.","Most people think exercise will definitely help you lose weight, but in fact, controlling your diet is the most important thing.":"Kebanyakan orang berpikir bahwa olahraga pasti akan membantu menurunkan berat badan, tetapi pada kenyataannya, mengontrol pola makan adalah hal yang paling penting.","Everyone thinks he's rich, but in fact, he saves money every month just to get by.":"Semua orang mengira dia kaya, tetapi sebenarnya, dia harus menabung setiap bulan hanya untuk bertahan hidup.","in short, anyway (to sum up)":"singkatnya, bagaimanapun (untuk meringkas)","[content], 總之, [conclusion]":"[isi], 總之, [kesimpulan]","\"總之\" wraps up a complex situation into one conclusion, similar to \"in short/anyway.\" Don't confuse it with \"反正\" (whatever happens, dismissive) — 總之 leads to a summary, not indifference.":"\"總之\" merangkum situasi yang rumit menjadi satu kesimpulan, mirip dengan \"singkatnya/bagaimanapun\". Jangan disamakan dengan \"反正\" (apa pun yang terjadi, bernada acuh tak acuh) — 總之 mengarah ke sebuah rangkuman, bukan sikap tidak peduli.","No matter what difficulties you run into or how it turns out, anyway, just take the first step first.":"Tidak peduli kesulitan apa pun yang kamu hadapi atau bagaimana hasilnya nanti, bagaimanapun, ambil saja langkah pertama dulu.","Whether you believe it or not, anyway, this is true.":"Percaya atau tidak, bagaimanapun, ini adalah kenyataan.","from this it can be known/seen that...":"dari sini dapat diketahui/dilihat bahwa...","[evidence], 由此可知/看來/可見, [inference]":"[bukti], 由此可知/看來/可見, [kesimpulan]","Used to draw a logical conclusion from evidence just given (\"from this we can see/know that...\"). 可知 is more definite, 看來 more tentative, 可見 stresses visible proof. Common in written/formal Chinese.":"Digunakan untuk menarik kesimpulan logis dari bukti yang baru saja disebutkan (\"dari sini dapat dilihat/diketahui bahwa...\"). 可知 lebih bersifat pasti, 看來 lebih bersifat perkiraan, 可見 menekankan bukti yang terlihat jelas. Umum digunakan dalam bahasa Tionghoa tulisan/formal.","Even when he's very busy, he still goes to volunteer — from this we can see that he's a warm-hearted person.":"Bahkan saat sangat sibuk, dia tetap pergi menjadi relawan — dari sini dapat dilihat bahwa dia adalah orang yang berhati hangat.","He arrives at the office early every day — from this we can tell he's a very diligent person.":"Dia selalu tiba di kantor lebih awal setiap hari — dari sini dapat diketahui bahwa dia adalah orang yang sangat rajin.","all in all, in conclusion":"secara keseluruhan, sebagai kesimpulan","[long explanation], 總而言之, [summary]":"[penjelasan panjang], 總而言之, [ringkasan]","A more formal version of 總之, used to close a lengthy explanation (\"all in all/in conclusion\"). Unlike 簡言之, which stresses brevity, 總而言之 focuses on wrapping up everything said.":"Merupakan versi yang lebih formal dari 總之, digunakan untuk menutup penjelasan yang panjang (\"secara keseluruhan/sebagai kesimpulan\"). Berbeda dengan 簡言之 yang menekankan keringkasan, 總而言之 berfokus pada merangkum semua yang telah dikatakan.","I've said a lot today, but all in all, it's just to help everyone build up their concept of wealth management.":"Hari ini saya sudah bicara banyak, tetapi secara keseluruhan, semua itu hanya untuk membantu semua orang membangun konsep pengelolaan keuangan.","This movie has funny parts and moving parts — all in all, it's well worth watching.":"Film ini punya bagian yang lucu dan bagian yang mengharukan — secara keseluruhan, sangat layak untuk ditonton.","in brief, simply put":"singkatnya, sederhananya","[detailed explanation], 簡言之, [short conclusion]":"[penjelasan rinci], 簡言之, [kesimpulan singkat]","Means \"in short/simply put\" — used to restate a detailed explanation in one short sentence. It must follow the detailed content; don't open with it before explaining anything.":"Berarti \"singkatnya/sederhananya\" — digunakan untuk menyatakan kembali penjelasan yang rinci dalam satu kalimat singkat. Ungkapan ini harus mengikuti isi yang rinci; jangan memulai dengan ungkapan ini sebelum menjelaskan apa pun.","Simply put, when you're in a good mood, your immunity gets stronger.":"Sederhananya, ketika suasana hati sedang baik, daya tahan tubuh Anda akan menjadi lebih kuat.","This plan has a lot of details, but simply put, it's meant to improve efficiency.":"Rencana ini memiliki banyak detail, tetapi sederhananya, tujuannya adalah untuk meningkatkan efisiensi.","this way, as a result":"dengan begitu, sebagai hasilnya","[action/change], 如此一來, [result]":"[tindakan/perubahan], 如此一來, [hasil]","Means \"this way/as a result,\" pointing back to a change or action just described and stating its consequence. Unlike the more neutral \"因此\" (therefore), it explicitly refers to \"this situation\" (如此), so it needs a concrete prior change to point to.":"Berarti \"dengan begitu/sebagai hasilnya\", merujuk kembali pada perubahan atau tindakan yang baru saja dijelaskan dan menyatakan akibatnya. Berbeda dengan \"因此\" (oleh karena itu) yang lebih netral, ungkapan ini secara eksplisit merujuk pada \"situasi ini\" (如此), sehingga memerlukan perubahan konkret sebelumnya untuk dirujuk.","The economy is gradually improving now — as a result, job opportunities will increase.":"Perekonomian sekarang berangsur-angsur membaik — sebagai hasilnya, kesempatan kerja akan meningkat.","The government lowered oil prices — as a result, transportation costs went down.":"Pemerintah menurunkan harga minyak — sebagai hasilnya, biaya transportasi pun menurun.","to do something from the perspective of...":"melakukan sesuatu dari sudut pandang...","從＋NP＋的角度來＋V":"從＋NP＋的角度來＋V","Marks the standpoint an action is taken from, with \"來\" linking to the verb. Learners often drop \"的角度\" and just say \"從NP來V\", which sounds incomplete or unnatural.":"Menandai sudut pandang tempat suatu tindakan dilakukan, dengan \"來\" menghubungkan ke kata kerja. Pembelajar sering menghilangkan \"的角度\" dan hanya mengatakan \"從NP來V\", yang terdengar tidak lengkap atau tidak alami.","Designing products from the user's perspective is not only practical but also increases the number of buyers.":"Merancang produk dari sudut pandang pengguna tidak hanya praktis tetapi juga meningkatkan jumlah pembeli.","From the teacher's perspective, this problem isn't difficult at all.":"Dari sudut pandang guru, masalah ini sama sekali tidak sulit.","as for / as to (shifting to a new topic)":"adapun / mengenai (beralih ke topik baru)","Clause, zhìyú + new/related topic (+ clause)":"Klausa, zhìyú + topik baru/terkait (+ klausa)","Shifts from the previous topic to a related but separate or undecided point. Unlike \"關於\", which simply introduces a topic, \"至於\" carries a sense of contrast with what was just said.":"Beralih dari topik sebelumnya ke poin yang berkaitan tetapi terpisah atau belum diputuskan. Berbeda dengan \"關於\" yang hanya memperkenalkan suatu topik, \"至於\" membawa nuansa kontras dengan apa yang baru saja disebutkan.","The meeting time has to be postponed; as for when it will be rescheduled to, we'll notify you again.":"Waktu rapat harus ditunda; adapun akan dijadwalkan ulang ke kapan, kami akan memberi tahu Anda lagi.","Everyone agreed to go to Japan for this trip; as for which city to visit, it hasn't been decided yet.":"Semua orang setuju untuk pergi ke Jepang dalam perjalanan ini; adapun kota mana yang akan dikunjungi, belum diputuskan.","\"so-called X\" is/refers to Y (giving a definition)":"\"yang disebut X\" adalah/merujuk pada Y (memberikan definisi)","Suǒwèi + X + shì zhǐ / jiùshì + Y":"Suǒwèi + X + shì zhǐ / jiùshì + Y","Used to define or explain a term or concept; somewhat formal in register. \"是指\" sounds more explanatory, while \"就是\" reads as a more direct equivalence.":"Digunakan untuk mendefinisikan atau menjelaskan suatu istilah atau konsep; gaya bahasanya agak formal. \"是指\" terdengar lebih bersifat penjelasan, sedangkan \"就是\" terbaca sebagai kesetaraan yang lebih langsung.","So-called fairness means that everyone has the same opportunity.":"Yang disebut keadilan berarti setiap orang memiliki kesempatan yang sama.","So-called success refers to achieving the goals you've set for yourself.":"Yang disebut kesuksesan merujuk pada tercapainya tujuan yang telah Anda tetapkan untuk diri sendiri.","under (a condition/influence of)...":"di bawah (kondisi/pengaruh)...","zài + NP (+ zhī) xià":"zài + NP (+ zhī) xià","Expresses that a result occurs under a certain condition, influence, or circumstance. \"之\" is optional and formal, and is usually dropped in everyday speech.":"Menyatakan bahwa suatu hasil terjadi di bawah kondisi, pengaruh, atau keadaan tertentu. \"之\" bersifat opsional dan formal, dan biasanya dihilangkan dalam percakapan sehari-hari.","Under the pressure of the competition, he didn't perform as well as expected.":"Di bawah tekanan kompetisi, dia tidak tampil sebaik yang diharapkan.","With the teacher's help, he finally got into his dream university.":"Dengan bantuan gurunya, dia akhirnya berhasil masuk ke universitas impiannya.","as far as ... is concerned / for...":"sejauh menyangkut... / bagi...","duì(yú) + NP + ér yán":"duì(yú) + NP + ér yán","Introduces an opinion or evaluation from a particular person's standpoint. Close in meaning to \"對...來說\", but \"而言\" is more formal and written in register.":"Memperkenalkan pendapat atau penilaian dari sudut pandang seseorang tertentu. Maknanya dekat dengan \"對...來說\", tetapi \"而言\" lebih formal dan bergaya bahasa tulis.","For the company's employees, a raise is a great encouragement.":"Bagi karyawan perusahaan, kenaikan gaji merupakan dorongan yang besar.","For students, health is more important than grades.":"Bagi siswa, kesehatan lebih penting daripada nilai.","among/within...":"di antara/di dalam...","(zài) + range + (zhī) zhōng":"(zài) + range + (zhī) zhōng","'(Zài)...(zhī)zhōng' marks a range within which a comparison or choice is made, often paired with 最 or 比較. 在/之 are optional. Unlike 其中 (a pronoun, cannot take a following noun), this pattern directly follows a noun phrase.":"'(Zài)...(zhī)zhōng' menandai suatu cakupan tempat perbandingan atau pilihan dibuat, sering dipasangkan dengan 最 atau 比較. 在/之 bersifat opsional. Berbeda dengan 其中 (sebuah kata ganti yang tidak dapat diikuti oleh kata benda), pola ini langsung mengikuti frasa kata benda.","Among the various foods in Taiwan, he likes xiaolongbao the most.":"Di antara berbagai makanan di Taiwan, dia paling menyukai xiaolongbao.","Among the students in the class, Xiaoming has the best grades.":"Di antara para siswa di kelas, Xiaoming memiliki nilai terbaik.","as for.../in terms of...":"adapun.../dari segi...","jiù + topic/standpoint + éryán":"jiù + topic/standpoint + éryán","'Jiù...éryán' introduces a topic or standpoint before giving a judgment from that angle; it's a more formal, written equivalent of 就……來說. The clause following 而言 must be a full comment, not just a noun.":"'Jiù...éryán' memperkenalkan suatu topik atau sudut pandang sebelum memberikan penilaian dari sudut tersebut; ini merupakan padanan yang lebih formal dan bergaya tulis dari 就……來說. Klausa yang mengikuti 而言 harus berupa komentar yang utuh, bukan sekadar kata benda.","In terms of economic development, this year's average salary increased by three percent compared to last year.":"Dari segi perkembangan ekonomi, gaji rata-rata tahun ini meningkat tiga persen dibandingkan tahun lalu.","From the students' perspective, exam pressure is really huge.":"Dari sudut pandang siswa, tekanan ujian benar-benar sangat besar.","in terms of/in the area of...":"dalam hal/di bidang...","zài + abstract domain + shàng":"zài + ranah abstrak + shàng","'Zài...shàng' marks an abstract domain or aspect (e.g., 國際上, 品質上), distinct from its literal spatial use meaning 'on top of' (在桌子上). Learners often confuse the abstract and literal senses.":"'Zài...shàng' menandai suatu ranah atau aspek abstrak (misalnya, 國際上, 品質上), berbeda dari makna spasial harfiahnya yang berarti 'di atas' (在桌子上). Pembelajar sering keliru antara makna abstrak dan makna harfiah.","This famous director made a film that received high acclaim internationally.":"Sutradara terkenal ini membuat sebuah film yang mendapat pujian tinggi di kancah internasional.","This product is very well guaranteed in terms of quality.":"Produk ini sangat terjamin dalam hal kualitas.","mainly consists of/is based on...":"terutama terdiri dari/didasarkan pada...","yǐ + object + wéi zhǔ":"yǐ + objek + wéi zhǔ","'Yǐ...wéi zhǔ' states that something is the main/central component, placing the object right after 以. Unlike the adjective/adverb 主要, this pattern is a fixed construction naming the primary element explicitly.":"'Yǐ...wéi zhǔ' menyatakan bahwa sesuatu adalah komponen utama/sentral, dengan menempatkan objek tepat setelah 以. Berbeda dengan kata sifat/kata keterangan 主要, pola ini adalah konstruksi tetap yang menyebutkan unsur utama secara eksplisit.","This country's economy is mainly based on agriculture.":"Perekonomian negara ini terutama didasarkan pada pertanian.","Our company's products are mainly phone accessories.":"Produk perusahaan kami terutama adalah aksesori ponsel.","whether or not...":"apakah... atau tidak...","shìfǒu + VP (used in indirect questions)":"shìfǒu + VP (digunakan dalam pertanyaan tidak langsung)","'Shìfǒu' is the formal written equivalent of 'whether or not,' used inside indirect questions (after verbs like 檢查, 知道). Unlike the colloquial 有沒有 or V-not-V forms, it never takes a sentence-final 嗎.":"'Shìfǒu' adalah padanan resmi dalam bahasa tulis untuk 'apakah... atau tidak', digunakan dalam pertanyaan tidak langsung (setelah kata kerja seperti 檢查, 知道). Berbeda dengan bentuk sehari-hari 有沒有 atau V-tidak-V, kata ini tidak pernah diikuti 嗎 di akhir kalimat.","Every time I go out, I always check whether I have my wallet and keys.":"Setiap kali keluar rumah, saya selalu memeriksa apakah saya membawa dompet dan kunci atau tidak.","The teacher wants to know whether all the students understood.":"Guru ingin tahu apakah semua murid sudah mengerti atau tidak.","How about ...? (making a suggestion)":"Bagaimana kalau...? (untuk mengajukan usulan)","Statement/proposal + rúhé?":"Pernyataan/usulan + rúhé?","Sentence-final 如何? asks for agreement on a suggestion, similar to 怎麼樣? but more formal/polite. Don't confuse with 如何 meaning 'how' (如何做 = how to do it).":"如何? di akhir kalimat digunakan untuk meminta persetujuan atas suatu usulan, mirip dengan 怎麼樣? tetapi lebih formal/sopan. Jangan disamakan dengan 如何 yang berarti 'bagaimana' (如何做 = bagaimana melakukannya).","How about we set the gathering time for tomorrow afternoon?":"Bagaimana kalau kita menetapkan waktu berkumpul besok siang?","How about we change the graduation trip location to Hualien?":"Bagaimana kalau kita mengubah lokasi acara wisata kelulusan ke Hualien?","let alone; not to mention":"apalagi; jangankan","A, gèng hékuàng B":"A, gèng hékuàng B","更何況 uses the prior statement as a basis to raise an even more extreme example ('all the more so'). Adding 更 makes the emphasis stronger than plain 何況. Close in meaning to 更別說...了, but 更何況 is usually followed by a full subject+predicate clause.":"更何況 menggunakan pernyataan sebelumnya sebagai dasar untuk mengajukan contoh yang lebih ekstrem lagi ('apalagi'). Penambahan 更 membuat penekanannya lebih kuat dibanding 何況 biasa. Maknanya dekat dengan 更別說...了, tetapi 更何況 biasanya diikuti oleh klausa lengkap subjek + predikat.","One is bound to feel nervous before a competition, let alone a contestant competing for the first time.":"Sebelum perlombaan, siapa pun pasti akan merasa gugup, apalagi seorang peserta yang baru pertama kali berkompetisi.","He gets out of breath just from walking normally, let alone running.":"Berjalan biasa saja dia sudah terengah-engah, apalagi berlari.","not only..., but also (even more so)...":"bukan hanya..., tetapi juga (bahkan lebih)...","A + bù shuō, hái + B":"A + bù shuō, hái + B","不說 here is a fixed phrase meaning 'not to mention,' not a negation of 'to speak.' The subject is shared across both clauses; 還 adds an even more impressive fact. Close to 不僅...還..., but 不說 sounds more colloquial.":"不說 di sini adalah frasa tetap yang berarti 'belum lagi', bukan bentuk negasi dari 'berbicara'. Subjeknya sama untuk kedua klausa; 還 menambahkan fakta yang bahkan lebih mengesankan. Maknanya dekat dengan 不僅...還..., tetapi 不說 terdengar lebih sehari-hari.","Not only is his writing ability good, he's even won first place in a speech contest.":"Kemampuan menulisnya bukan hanya bagus, dia bahkan pernah meraih juara pertama dalam lomba pidato.","This restaurant is not only conveniently located, it's also very cheap.":"Restoran ini bukan hanya berlokasi strategis, tetapi juga sangat murah.","let alone... (sentence ends with 了)":"apalagi... (kalimat diakhiri dengan 了)","A, gèng biéshuō B le":"A, gèng biéshuō B le","更別說 raises an even more extreme/obvious example and characteristically ends with sentence-final 了; it can be followed by just a noun (e.g. 更別說夜晚了). It differs from 更何況, which usually takes a full clause (subject+predicate) after it. Don't forget the final 了.":"更別說 mengajukan contoh yang lebih ekstrem/jelas lagi dan biasanya diakhiri dengan 了 di akhir kalimat; kata ini bisa diikuti hanya oleh sebuah kata benda (misalnya 更別說夜晚了). Ini berbeda dengan 更何況, yang biasanya diikuti oleh klausa lengkap (subjek+predikat) setelahnya. Jangan lupa 了 di akhir kalimat.","The weather in the mountains is extremely cold — even in the daytime it's only five degrees, let alone at night.":"Cuaca di gunung sangat dingin — siang hari saja hanya lima derajat, apalagi malam hari.","He can't even understand spoken Chinese, let alone read a Chinese newspaper.":"Dia mendengar bahasa Mandarin saja tidak mengerti, apalagi membaca koran berbahasa Mandarin.","not to mention..., even... too":"jangan sebut soal..., bahkan... juga...","Biéshuō A, (lián) B yě C":"Biéshuō A, (lián) B yě C","別說 A, (連) B 也 C compares two subjects A and B, stressing that if even A is obviously so, B — an even more surprising case — is the same. Unlike 更別說...了, no sentence-final 了 is needed. 連 is optional but 也 is required.":"別說 A, (連) B 也 C membandingkan dua subjek A dan B, menekankan bahwa jika A saja sudah jelas demikian, maka B — kasus yang bahkan lebih mengejutkan — juga sama. Berbeda dengan 更別說...了, tidak diperlukan 了 di akhir kalimat. 連 bersifat opsional tetapi 也 wajib digunakan.","Not to mention students not recognizing this character, even the teacher doesn't recognize it.":"Jangan sebut murid tidak mengenali karakter ini, bahkan guru pun tidak mengenalinya.","Not to mention foreigners not understanding Taiwanese, even many young people can't understand it either.":"Jangan sebut orang asing tidak mengerti bahasa Taiwan, bahkan banyak anak muda pun tidak mengerti.","in addition, besides":"selain itu, di samping itu","Sentence. + 此外, + additional sentence.":"Kalimat. + 此外, + kalimat tambahan.","此外 starts a new sentence to add supplementary information, common in formal/written Chinese. Similar to 另外 but more formal; don't confuse it with 除了...以外 which means 'except for'.":"此外 memulai kalimat baru untuk menambahkan informasi tambahan, umum digunakan dalam bahasa Mandarin formal/tulisan. Mirip dengan 另外 tetapi lebih formal; jangan disamakan dengan 除了...以外 yang berarti 'kecuali'.","Besides, there's also a gift on your birthday.":"Selain itu, pada hari ulang tahunmu juga ada hadiah.","This shop's coffee is delicious. Besides, the service is also very friendly.":"Kopi di toko ini enak. Selain itu, pelayanannya juga sangat ramah.","not only... but (even/instead)...":"bukan hanya... tetapi (bahkan/malah)...","Subject + 非但 + negative situation, 還 + a worse or unexpected outcome.":"Subjek + 非但 + situasi negatif, 還 + hasil yang lebih buruk atau tidak terduga.","非但...還... stresses an unexpected reversal, usually toward something worse, and is more formal than 不但...而且...; it commonly pairs with a negated first clause, so don't force it into a positive-accumulation context.":"非但...還... menekankan pembalikan yang tidak terduga, biasanya ke arah yang lebih buruk, dan lebih formal daripada 不但...而且...; pola ini biasanya berpasangan dengan klausa pertama yang negatif, jadi jangan memaksakannya dalam konteks akumulasi positif.","The new product's sales not only failed to increase, but even dropped by 30%.":"Penjualan produk baru bukan hanya gagal meningkat, bahkan malah turun 30%.","He not only didn't apologize, he even scolded the other person.":"Dia bukan hanya tidak minta maaf, bahkan malah memarahi lawan bicaranya.","ranging from (the smallest) to (the largest)":"mulai dari (yang terkecil) hingga (yang terbesar)","小自 + small item, 大至 + large item, 都/皆 + shared statement.":"小自 + hal kecil, 大至 + hal besar, 都/皆 + pernyataan yang berlaku untuk semuanya.","小自...大至... lists the smallest and largest ends of a scope to stress 'everything included'; it's a formal/written pattern. Keep the small-to-large order and avoid it in casual speech.":"小自...大至... menyebutkan ujung terkecil dan terbesar dari suatu cakupan untuk menekankan 'mencakup segalanya'; ini adalah pola formal/tulisan. Pertahankan urutan dari kecil ke besar dan hindari penggunaannya dalam percakapan santai.","In our company, everything from buying pens to investment plans is decided personally by the president.":"Di perusahaan kami, mulai dari membeli pulpen hingga rencana investasi, semuanya diputuskan langsung oleh presiden direktur.","For this event, everything from poster design to venue rental is handled by her alone.":"Untuk acara ini, mulai dari desain poster hingga penyewaan tempat, semuanya ditangani sendiri olehnya.","just as, exactly as":"persis seperti, sesuai dengan","正如 + clause (what was said/thought), followed by the result.":"正如 + klausa (apa yang dikatakan/dipikirkan), diikuti oleh hasilnya.","正如 confirms that reality matches an earlier statement or expectation; formal register, often followed by 所+V+的. It's more written than the colloquial 就像 — avoid it in casual chat.":"正如 menegaskan bahwa kenyataan sesuai dengan pernyataan atau harapan sebelumnya; bergaya formal, sering diikuti oleh 所+V+的. Kata ini lebih bersifat tulisan dibandingkan 就像 yang sehari-hari — hindari penggunaannya dalam obrolan santai.","Just as we had guessed, the merchandise completely sold out within one day.":"Persis seperti dugaan kami, barang dagangan benar-benar habis terjual hanya dalam satu hari.","Just as the teacher said, the questions on this exam really weren't difficult.":"Persis seperti yang dikatakan guru, soal-soal dalam ujian ini memang tidak sulit.","to originate from, to come from":"berasal dari, datang dari","V (出/源/來/取, etc.) + 自 + source.":"V (出/源/來/取, dll.) + 自 + sumber.","(V)自 attaches directly after verbs like 出/源/來/取 to mean 'from,' forming formal compounds such as 出自, 源自, 來自. Unlike the preposition 從, which precedes the source before the verb, so don't mix up the word order.":"(V)自 melekat langsung setelah kata kerja seperti 出/源/來/取 untuk berarti 'dari,' membentuk kata majemuk formal seperti 出自, 源自, 來自. Berbeda dengan kata depan 從, yang mendahului sumber sebelum kata kerja, jadi jangan sampai tertukar urutan katanya.","This movie's inspiration comes from Dream of the Red Chamber.":"Inspirasi film ini berasal dari Hong Lou Meng (Mimpi di Kamar Merah).","This idiom originates from an ancient story.":"Idiom ini berasal dari sebuah kisah kuno.","formal written 'V + 於' indicating origin, time, or place":"bentuk tulisan formal 'V + 於' yang menunjukkan asal, waktu, atau tempat","A + V + 於 + B (time/place/origin)":"A + V + 於 + B (waktu/tempat/asal)","\"於\" is a formal/written substitute for 在/從, fixed to specific verbs like 畢業於, 生於, 位於; it's not freely combinable with any verb. Spoken Chinese prefers 在/從 constructions instead.":"\"於\" adalah pengganti formal/tulisan untuk 在/從, yang terpaku pada kata kerja tertentu seperti 畢業於, 生於, 位於; kata ini tidak bisa digabungkan secara bebas dengan sembarang kata kerja. Bahasa Mandarin lisan lebih menyukai konstruksi 在/從.","Li Minghua graduated from the Chinese department.":"Li Minghua lulus dari jurusan Bahasa Mandarin.","He was born in 1990.":"Dia lahir pada tahun 1990.","formal written 'to/until' for ranges":"bentuk tulisan formal 'sampai' untuk rentang","A + 至 + B (endpoint of a range)":"A + 至 + B (titik akhir suatu rentang)","\"至\" is the written form of 到, marking the endpoint of a range (numbers, time, place), often in \"從...至...\". Unlike 到, it cannot take aspect markers like 了 after it.":"\"至\" adalah bentuk tulisan dari 到, yang menandai titik akhir suatu rentang (angka, waktu, tempat), sering muncul dalam \"從...至...\". Berbeda dengan 到, kata ini tidak bisa diikuti penanda aspek seperti 了 setelahnya.","Our company is recruiting marketing staff; the salary is from 35,000 to 40,000.":"Perusahaan kami sedang merekrut staf pemasaran; gajinya dari 35.000 hingga 40.000.","Business hours are from 9 a.m. to 9 p.m.":"Jam operasional adalah dari pukul 9 pagi hingga 9 malam.","\"taking ... as an example\"":"\"mengambil ... sebagai contoh\"","以 + N + 為例":"以 + N + 為例","Used to introduce a concrete example that illustrates a general statement made earlier; \"以A為例\" means \"taking A as an example,\" followed by specific details.":"Digunakan untuk memberikan contoh konkret yang mengilustrasikan pernyataan umum yang telah disebutkan sebelumnya; \"以A為例\" berarti \"mengambil A sebagai contoh,\" diikuti dengan detail spesifik.","Taipei's transportation is very convenient; taking the MRT as an example, you can reach all the nearby attractions.":"Transportasi di Taipei sangat nyaman; mengambil MRT sebagai contoh, Anda bisa mencapai semua tempat wisata terdekat.","Taiwan has a lot of fruit; taking mangoes as an example, you can buy them everywhere in summer.":"Taiwan memiliki banyak buah; mengambil mangga sebagai contoh, Anda bisa membelinya di mana-mana pada musim panas.","\"so as not to / to avoid\"":"\"agar tidak / untuk menghindari\"","Clause 1, 免得 + Clause 2 (undesired result)":"Klausa 1, 免得 + Klausa 2 (hasil yang tidak diinginkan)","Introduces an undesired outcome to be avoided by doing the action in the first clause. Similar to 以免, but 免得 is more colloquial and commonly used in speech, while 以免 is more formal/written.":"Memperkenalkan hasil yang tidak diinginkan yang harus dihindari dengan melakukan tindakan pada klausa pertama. Mirip dengan 以免, tetapi 免得 lebih kolokial dan umum digunakan dalam percakapan, sedangkan 以免 lebih formal/tulisan.","Dry your hair quickly, so you won't catch a cold.":"Cepat keringkan rambutmu, agar tidak masuk angin.","Remember to bring an umbrella before you go out, so you won't get soaked.":"Ingat bawa payung sebelum keluar rumah, agar tidak basah kuyup.","\"however\" — formal written contrastive conjunction":"\"namun\" — konjungsi kontras formal/tulisan","Clause 1, 然而 + Clause 2 (contrast)":"Klausa 1, 然而 + Klausa 2 (kontras)","\"然而\" is the formal/written equivalent of 但是/不過, introducing a contrast to what precedes; often paired with 雖然 in the first clause. In casual speech, 但是 is more common.":"\"然而\" adalah padanan formal/tulisan dari 但是/不過, yang memperkenalkan kontras terhadap apa yang disebutkan sebelumnya; sering dipasangkan dengan 雖然 pada klausa pertama. Dalam percakapan sehari-hari, 但是 lebih umum digunakan.","Economic development is important; however, environmental protection must not be neglected either.":"Pembangunan ekonomi itu penting; namun, perlindungan lingkungan juga tidak boleh diabaikan.","He studies hard every day; however, his grades are still not ideal.":"Dia belajar dengan tekun setiap hari; namun, nilainya masih belum ideal.","not A but B":"bukan A melainkan B","bùshì + A, ér shì + B":"bùshì + A, ér shì + B","Used to firmly correct a false assumption by naming the real cause or fact. Unlike plain negation (不是B), it always supplies the correct alternative after 而是. Don't confuse with plain 而, which just contrasts without correcting.":"Digunakan untuk mengoreksi secara tegas asumsi yang salah dengan menyebutkan penyebab atau fakta yang sebenarnya. Berbeda dengan negasi biasa (不是B), pola ini selalu memberikan alternatif yang benar setelah 而是. Jangan disamakan dengan 而 biasa, yang hanya menyatakan kontras tanpa koreksi.","The key to changing your destiny is not relying on fortune-telling, but relying on your own effort.":"Kunci untuk mengubah takdirmu bukanlah bergantung pada ramalan, melainkan bergantung pada usahamu sendiri.","It's not that he doesn't want to help, but that he doesn't have time.":"Bukannya dia tidak mau membantu, melainkan dia tidak punya waktu.","not only not..., but on the contrary...":"bukan hanya tidak..., tetapi sebaliknya justru...","(bùdàn) bù/méi + V, fǎn'ér + unexpected result":"(bùdàn) bù/méi + V, fǎn'ér + hasil tak terduga","Negates the expected outcome, then 反而 introduces the opposite, unexpected result. Always paired with a preceding negation (不/沒); unlike plain 而 (simple contrast), it specifically marks a reversal against expectation.":"Menegasikan hasil yang diharapkan, kemudian 反而 memperkenalkan hasil sebaliknya yang tak terduga. Selalu berpasangan dengan negasi sebelumnya (不/沒); berbeda dengan 而 biasa (kontras sederhana), pola ini secara khusus menandai pembalikan dari yang diharapkan.","Although they hiked all day long, they don't feel tired — on the contrary, they're full of energy.":"Meskipun mereka mendaki seharian penuh, mereka tidak merasa lelah — sebaliknya, mereka justru penuh energi.","He didn't sleep well last night, but at work he was even more energetic instead.":"Semalam dia tidur tidak nyenyak, tetapi saat bekerja dia justru malah lebih berenergi.","whereas / on the other hand (formal contrast)":"sedangkan / di sisi lain (kontras formal)","A, B zé + C (contrasts with A)":"A, B zé + C (berkontras dengan A)","A formal, written-style conjunction contrasting two items, more formal than spoken 可是/不過. Commonly used when comparing two different subjects side by side. Very close to 而, but 則 leans more toward listing or comparing parallel facts.":"Konjungsi bergaya formal dan tertulis yang mengontraskan dua hal, lebih formal daripada 可是/不過 dalam bahasa lisan. Biasa digunakan saat membandingkan dua subjek berbeda secara berdampingan. Sangat mirip dengan 而, tetapi 則 lebih condong pada penyebutan atau perbandingan fakta-fakta yang sejajar.","Electric cars don't pollute the air; the drawback, however, is that the price is on the high side.":"Mobil listrik tidak mencemari udara; sayangnya, kekurangannya adalah harganya agak tinggi.","I like hiking, whereas my older sister likes swimming.":"Saya suka mendaki, sedangkan kakak perempuan saya suka berenang.","and / whereas (literary connective)":"dan / sedangkan (konjungsi sastra)","A, ér + B (contrast or addition)":"A, ér + B (kontras atau penambahan)","A written-style connector linking two clauses to show contrast or addition; broader than 則, which is mainly for parallel contrast. Rarely used in casual speech — typical of formal writing and explanations.":"Konjungsi bergaya tulisan yang menghubungkan dua klausa untuk menunjukkan kontras atau penambahan; cakupannya lebih luas daripada 則, yang terutama untuk kontras yang sejajar. Jarang digunakan dalam percakapan sehari-hari — khas untuk tulisan formal dan penjelasan.","On weekend evenings everyone goes out to eat together, whereas I'd rather cook for myself at home.":"Pada malam akhir pekan semua orang keluar makan bersama, sedangkan saya lebih suka memasak sendiri di rumah.","My younger brother likes playing basketball, whereas my younger sister likes drawing.":"Adik laki-laki saya suka bermain basket, sedangkan adik perempuan saya suka menggambar.","unexpectedly / to one's surprise":"tak disangka / di luar dugaan","Subject + jìng + (verb/adjective phrase)":"Subjek + jìng + (frasa verba/adjektiva)","An adverb expressing the speaker's surprise that a result exceeded expectations. Nearly interchangeable with 竟然, but 竟 alone is more common in formal or written style, placed directly before the verb or adjective.":"Kata keterangan yang menyatakan keterkejutan pembicara bahwa suatu hasil melampaui dugaan. Hampir dapat dipertukarkan dengan 竟然, tetapi 竟 sendiri lebih umum digunakan dalam gaya formal atau tulisan, diletakkan tepat sebelum verba atau adjektiva.","In just under a few years, this company's capital unexpectedly reached several hundred million US dollars.":"Hanya dalam waktu kurang dari beberapa tahun, modal perusahaan ini tak disangka telah mencapai ratusan juta dolar AS.","He practiced for less than a month, and unexpectedly got into National Taiwan University.":"Dia berlatih kurang dari sebulan, dan tak disangka berhasil diterima di National Taiwan University.","literary equivalent of \"的\"":"padanan sastra dari \"的\"","A + 之 + B (formal written form of \"A 的 B\")":"A + 之 + B (bentuk tulisan formal dari \"A 的 B\")","\"之\" is the formal, written-language counterpart of \"的\", linking a modifier to a noun. It appears in idioms, proverbs, and formal writing but is rare in everyday speech; using it in casual conversation sounds stiff and unnatural.":"\"之\" adalah padanan formal dalam bahasa tulis dari \"的\", yang menghubungkan sebuah pewatas dengan kata benda. Kata ini muncul dalam idiom, peribahasa, dan tulisan formal, tetapi jarang digunakan dalam percakapan sehari-hari; menggunakannya dalam percakapan santai akan terdengar kaku dan tidak alami.","Parents accompany their children through the road of growth.":"Orang tua mendampingi anak-anak mereka menempuh jalan pertumbuhan.","Taipei is a city of gourmet food; tourists all love it.":"Taipei adalah kota kuliner; para wisatawan semuanya menyukainya."};
